{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall","id":518351,"title":"Ask Neall","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-18T12:02:08-07:00","id":518351,"title":"Ask Neall","content":"A thread for asking Scion 2E writer Neall Raemonn Price about the next edition.<br /> <br /> (<a href=\"http://www.ttrarchive.com/store/index.php?title=Scion_2E:_What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">Check here first</a> to see if your question's already been answered.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T15:00:03-07:00","id":518449,"title":"","content":"Nice Q&amp;A compilation; i'm very grateful to whoever did it, and to you, Marin, for linking it here.<br /> <br /> First and foremost, i have to ask one thing, though: Is Neall comfortable with you creating a specific thread to question him? Seems (to me) a little intrusive if he has not said something about it.<br /> <br /> And secondly, putting away any social niceties : Oh Neall, writer of the Gods! Tell us as much as you can about <b>Lugh of the Tuatha d\u00e9 Dannan</b> and how he is the pure essence of awesomeness!!! (what? are you implying my main character is a Scion of Lugh? ... Hell yeah <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) Can you share with us his Purviews? Maybe a little spoiler about his mantles? Any special moment while writing about him that you'd be happy to share?<br /> <br /> In truth, any little detail would do... and bigger chunks of information would be great!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T15:30:06-07:00","id":518515,"title":"","content":"The question was asked in the 'What Pantheons do you want to see', and permission was gained.<br /> <br /> If we are getting information on Lugh the long handed, I believe we can stretch the offering to cover information about <b>The Dagda</b> as well. Any information you can share?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T22:05:50-07:00","id":518923,"title":"","content":"Ohhh something I was wondering, in the Scion: Origins book...that's the mortal book right?...I'm assuming regular everyday people and pre-visitation scions will be covered in that book, are there any other &quot;types&quot; of mortals that will be covered by Origins? Like somebody whose grandfather was a faun, or comes from a linage of sorceresses?<br /> <br /> Edit: ok ignore this, it was the very first question on the what we know page oops<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">And, yes, pre-Visitation Scions, but also holy men and women of the pantheons, sorcerers who seek to steal the power of the gods, and those bound by Fate (your Oedipuses, your Cassandras, your Arjunas).</span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5622,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","user":"SpruceStripedGoose","date":". 05-19-2015, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T00:02:45-07:00","id":519034,"title":"","content":"Ok a proper question, is it still the plan to use the 1e hero, demi-god, and god covers for the 2e books? Those were the best White-Wolf covers ever so I would personally be happy to see them again...but on the other hand I can see how it could be confusing on drivethru to have two lines of very different books with identical covers. I'm imagining the confusion if the new edition of D&amp;D had the same covers as 3.5, especially when you can still find 3.5 on sale in some places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T07:19:57-07:00","id":519547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=518449#post518449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice Q&amp;A compilation; i'm very grateful to whoever did it, and to you, Marin, for linking it here.<br /> <br /> First and foremost, i have to ask one thing, though: Is Neall comfortable with you creating a specific thread to question him? Seems (to me) a little intrusive if he has not said something about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm good with it; said so in the thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And secondly, putting away any social niceties : Oh Neall, writer of the Gods! Tell us as much as you can about <b>Lugh of the Tuatha d\u00e9 Dannan</b> and how he is the pure essence of awesomeness!!! (what? are you implying my main character is a Scion of Lugh? ... Hell yeah <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) Can you share with us his Purviews? Maybe a little spoiler about his mantles? Any special moment while writing about him that you'd be happy to share?<br /> <br /> In truth, any little detail would do... and bigger chunks of information would be great! </div> </div> </div>Lugh L\u00e1mhfhada, a grand-Scion of Dian Cecht and god-born Scion of Cian and Ethniu, is definitely in the corebook, along with the rest of the Irish pantheon. The Origins signature character is actually a Scion of the Dagda, the Red Man of All Knowledge. Right now, the plan is for Lugh to have had a toe in the Gaulish pantheon before it was destroyed, and had especially good relationships with Taranis, Esus, and Toutatis. He may, or may not, be related to Lleu Llaw Gyffes, we haven't really decided yet - &quot;a God named Lou who is strong with a bright hand&quot; seems like a no-brainer, but a lot of their stories and relationships are completely different, so it may be more of a case of Taranis having a beard and thunderbolts. But, we're not even to first drafts yet.<br /> <br /> The Welsh/Britannian pantheon is something else entirely. I really hope we get to cover all of Celtic and Brythonic myth, I really do. You should see druids, bards and vates in Origins.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok a proper question, is it still the plan to use the 1e hero, demi-god, and god covers for the 2e books? </div> </div> </div>Yes, and Origins has a fourth cover to match.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 05-19-2015, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T07:56:36-07:00","id":519581,"title":"","content":"Good stuff!<br /> <br /> I like to hear that druids are finally getting a write up. I always saw that as an omission that sorely needed to be addressed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T11:03:29-07:00","id":519776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=518923#post518923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ohhh something I was wondering, in the Scion: Origins book...that's the mortal book right?...I'm assuming regular everyday people and pre-visitation scions will be covered in that book, are there any other &quot;types&quot; of mortals that will be covered by Origins? Like somebody whose grandfather was a faun, or comes from a linage of sorceresses?</div> </div> </div> </div>Descent from Legendary creatures is something I <i>really</i> want to have in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 05-20-2015, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T13:04:28-07:00","id":519934,"title":"","content":"We know that Gods will be able to belong to several pantheons, but what about Scions? Could gods from different pantheons have a god-born child and could that child belong to both pantheons?<br /> Also, could a mortal without divine blood become a Scion, by being adopted by a god, drinking amrita, eating a golden apple, or any other mean?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T14:09:54-07:00","id":519995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=519547#post519547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and Origins has a fourth cover to match.</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually reminds me of another question now that I think about it. Dr Aaron Tigrillo/Itztli Ocelotl is the signature character on the cover of Scion: God, and he always highlighted something weird to me, why do so many of the modern scions revert to ancient motifs when they become gods? In Scion becoming a god is the point where you are equal and independent from your parent, so it always struck me as strange that that was the point when many scions look far more like their ancient parents than their own modern interpretation of what a god should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T14:49:05-07:00","id":520025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=519995#post519995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This actually reminds me of another question now that I think about it. Dr Aaron Tigrillo/Itztli Ocelotl is the signature character on the cover of Scion: God, and he always highlighted something weird to me, why do so many of the modern scions revert to ancient motifs when they become gods? In Scion becoming a god is the point where you are equal and independent from your parent, so it always struck me as strange that that was the point when many scions look far more like their ancient parents than their own modern interpretation of what a god should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably for social reasons; after all a Scon reaching godhood is still a young, inexperienced and probably rather weak deity, without the raw power or influence of more ancient gods. As such they'll probably often want to fit in with the rest of the pantheon rather than try to stand out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T18:10:48-07:00","id":520273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=519995#post519995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This actually reminds me of another question now that I think about it. Dr Aaron Tigrillo/Itztli Ocelotl is the signature character on the cover of Scion: God, and he always highlighted something weird to me, why do so many of the modern scions revert to ancient motifs when they become gods? In Scion becoming a god is the point where you are equal and independent from your parent, so it always struck me as strange that that was the point when many scions look far more like their ancient parents than their own modern interpretation of what a god should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the Scions in 1e are doing what Anteros said - taking up a junior position within their parent's pantheon. In that case, you're dealing with hundreds - and often thousands - of years of cultural baggage and mores. Keep the &quot;desert ranger&quot; duster, Harshihar, but you better wear your Nemes headdress around the Ennead if you're going to deign to speak to them.<br /> <br /> I suspect that Scions creating their own pantheon can wear whatever they like, as long as it's sufficiently majestic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T20:15:43-07:00","id":520374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=519995#post519995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This actually reminds me of another question now that I think about it. Dr Aaron Tigrillo/Itztli Ocelotl is the signature character on the cover of Scion: God, and he always highlighted something weird to me, why do so many of the modern scions revert to ancient motifs when they become gods? In Scion becoming a god is the point where you are equal and independent from your parent, so it always struck me as strange that that was the point when many scions look far more like their ancient parents than their own modern interpretation of what a god should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>In alot of religions and cultures doing something so drastically individualistic would be somewhere between socially illegal (in their societies) and monumentously impious. It also raises the question of basic respect. Do you not respect the culture and traditions from whence you come? Its especially egregrious now that your an actual god to your people, your held to a much higher standard as a representation of both your family, pantheon and even your entire culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T08:45:43-07:00","id":521919,"title":"","content":"Will you be reaching out to members of the Scion community to assist with <b>Playtesting</b> and <b>Stress Testing</b> the mechanics (under an NDA possibly)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T09:02:40-07:00","id":521933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=520273#post520273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most of the Scions in 1e are doing what Anteros said - taking up a junior position within their parent's pantheon. In that case, you're dealing with hundreds - and often thousands - of years of cultural baggage and mores. Keep the &quot;desert ranger&quot; duster, Harshihar, but you better wear your Nemes headdress around the Ennead if you're going to deign to speak to them.<br /> <br /> I suspect that Scions creating their own pantheon can wear whatever they like, as long as it's sufficiently majestic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shouldn't it be the Ennead deigning to speak to Harishar? If he comes in with his headress on and then treats all the Great Gods as if they should be honored he showed up to spend his valuable time with them.... I think there would be some smiting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T10:07:17-07:00","id":521975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=521919#post521919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will you be reaching out to members of the Scion community to assist with <b>Playtesting</b> and <b>Stress Testing</b> the mechanics (under an NDA possibly)?</div> </div> </div> </div>The plan is to have a bit of Open Development, too, but we definitely want to have dedicated playtesting teams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T10:10:59-07:00","id":521983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=521933#post521933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shouldn't it be the Ennead deigning to speak to Harishar? If he comes in with his headress on and then treats all the Great Gods as if they should be honored he showed up to spend his valuable time with them.... I think there would be some smiting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I misspoke there. That's what I get for posting without coffee. They would deign to speak with him. <br /> <br /> But keep wearing the headdress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T10:33:47-07:00","id":522006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=521975#post521975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The plan is to have a bit of Open Development, too, but we definitely want to have dedicated playtesting teams.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome! Please let us know whenever we can start signing up for the dedicated playtesting teams! Thank you, sir.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T19:55:29-07:00","id":523867,"title":"","content":"Personally, I like the image of Doctor Tigrillo wearing a mix of something Atzlanti with a modern lab coat. The lab coat is a powerful modern symbol -- almost mythic -- and Fate might help him establish respect for it among the Gods. On formaql pantheon occasions, sure, go in full Atzlanti drag. But in his Overworld hospital, he wears the lab coat because that's what healers wear.<br /> <br /> (One episode of Radio Lab included a discussion of the symbolic power of the lab coat. &quot;Getting The Coat&quot; is an important part of graduating from medical student to doctor.)<br /> <br /> Neall: You mention characters descended from mythic creatures other than Gods. Will it be possible to play those mythic creatures themselves? IE play one of the Alfar, or a giant that's switched from Dark Virtues.<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T20:05:26-07:00","id":523880,"title":"","content":"I had misread it to mean you would be playing a minotaur, not the descendant of one... oh the possibilities... WANTS THE PRECIOUS!!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T07:08:30-07:00","id":524393,"title":"","content":"I've got a question, something that's been bugging me since Hero came out, actually. Will there be a full list of Merits/Backgrounds to help round out a character mechanically or will it still be left to the player to come up with narratively, and if so, will they be a separate thing from Birthrights or would Birthrights be a subset of Backgrounds/merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T08:30:06-07:00","id":524472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dean Shomshak</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neall: You mention characters descended from mythic creatures other than Gods. Will it be possible to play those mythic creatures themselves? IE play one of the Alfar, or a giant that's switched from Dark Virtues.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the hope - satyrs get brought up as a favorite - though I don't think it'll be <i>fully </i>covered in Origins and Hero. I know that Percy Jackson has raised a few eyebrows around here, but a character <i>like </i>Grover Underwood, albeit with a far more mythic and classical overtone, is a PC - one who progresses from Greek to Roman depictions by &quot;earning his horns and hooves&quot;. Alfar or sidhe descent should be possible, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=524393#post524393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got a question, something that's been bugging me since Hero came out, actually. Will there be a full list of Merits/Backgrounds to help round out a character mechanically or will it still be left to the player to come up with narratively, and if so, will they be a separate thing from Birthrights or would Birthrights be a subset of Backgrounds/merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the things I think Scion 1e did <i>well </i>mechanically was cutting out what didn't fundamentally matter to the world; a strict Resources Background, for example, didn't actually matter for a story about the divine. If you were a jet-setting celebrity, you just were; if you were a god of the homeless, you just were. That said, one of the things Sardonyx does is provide almost Merit-like hooks for individual organizations and the world, something you can buy into to increase your story purchase in the setting (though it can also be increased narratively). Birthrights are still a mostly separate thing, though they're very intertwined..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 05-22-2015, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T16:07:16-07:00","id":524865,"title":"","content":"Cool, thanks Neall! (And if anyone wants a depiction of Greco-Roman lesser immortals that's very much *not* Grover Underwood, I recommend the works of Thomas Burnett Swann. It's a creative misinterpretation of Greek material, but suggests interesting possibilities.)<br /> <br /> And mad props to Marin, too. I really have no further questions. Scion 2 is looking more exciting than anything WW/OP has done in, well, years, really.<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T23:49:23-07:00","id":525190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=524472#post524472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that Percy Jackson has raised a few eyebrows around here, but a character <i>like </i>Grover Underwood, albeit with a far more mythic and classical overtone, is a PC - one who progresses from Greek to Roman depictions by &quot;earning his horns and hooves&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Percy Jackson books are a series I have a love/hate relationship with, conceptually the world the characters live in is really cool and I would even say even on par with some of the best children's fantasy out there, but the series really talks down to its readers, the plots are transparent to the degree that more often than not you know exactly what is going to happen next in every scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Will we see any younger Scions in the new edition?</b> I'm trying to think if there have been any before but I am coming up blank. Scion highschool or summer camp could be pretty fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T10:51:01-07:00","id":525592,"title":"","content":"So aside from the Tuatha and the tenth pantheon, who're both getting new signature characters, what's happening with the sigs? Given the original covers are sticking around, that means the original Band will be coming back too, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T12:27:01-07:00","id":525780,"title":"","content":"What is the coolest purview power you feel has been written so far? What does it do?<br /> <br /> Are there any new purviews? Or any of the older ones being dropped?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T14:33:22-07:00","id":525940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=525190#post525190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Will we see any younger Scions in the new edition?</b> I'm trying to think if there have been any before but I am coming up blank. Scion highschool or summer camp could be pretty fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's entirely the tone we want to go, but the new core does involve the possibility of alternate settings and changes in tone using the core mechanics. I don't see why you couldn't use the mechanics to play a Camp Half-Blood game, even if the setting proper doesn't entirely support it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So aside from the Tuatha and the tenth pantheon, who're both getting new signature characters, what's happening with the sigs? Given the original covers are sticking around, that means the original Band will be coming back too, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>The three cover sigs, at least. They were probably the most interesting characters of the signature Band, though obviously that's my opinion. <br /> <br /> In terms of supplemental rules text and maybe a Ready-Made characters packet, sure. <br /> <br /> In terms of a 30-page fiction in the corebook, no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the coolest purview power you feel has been written so far? What does it do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Reply hazy! Ask writer again in a month or two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T16:43:19-07:00","id":526076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=525190#post525190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Will we see any younger Scions in the new edition?</b> I'm trying to think if there have been any before but I am coming up blank. Scion highschool or summer camp could be pretty fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;Ahem&gt; I know it's Neall's thread, but... Some years back, I ran a campaign called &quot;Scion High&quot; and it worked very well. I ran it as a teen supernatural action/soap opera, though, as seen on The CW, very much in the spirit of Buffy the Vampire Slayer, Smallville, or the Vampire Diaries. Scions in a modern high school, mixing their adventures with cars, dating, afterschool jobs, etc. The titanspawn all attended the rival high school.<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T21:43:02-07:00","id":526365,"title":"","content":"How hard will it be to push the war between the Gods and the Titans into the background and just run it as a game of pulp urban fantasy with mythic heroes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/91-wandering","name":"Wandering","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar91_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T22:41:28-07:00","id":526413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a bit of the Mage powerset that's really informing the development of Scion2e, and four members of Team Mage(s) are on Team Scion, so I think the concepts will translate well for your group</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm assuming that \u201cTeam Mage\u201d refers to <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>, as opposed to <b>Mage: the Ascension</b>? <br /> <br /> More generally, are there any spoilers you can provide about how Magic will work in Scion 2e? I know we're going to have sorcerers in Origin; and presumably magic will be tied to whatever mythology the practitioner subscribes to. But as I understand it, there are vast differences between the rune-based magic of the Norse people, Voodoo/Hoodoo/Santiera/etc., Egyptian mysticism, the Hermetic magic of Greek descent, Shinto priests, and Aztec blood magic, just to mention the most common magical practices associated with the original six Scion Pantheons \u2014 so much so that whole games can be (and have been) written about just one of them. How are you going to address this in <b>Scion</b> such that the magic rules only take up a portion of <b>Scion Origin</b> but still manage to capture the distinct flavors of these different belief systems?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T08:51:36-07:00","id":526724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wandering</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=526365#post526365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How hard will it be to push the war between the Gods and the Titans into the background and just run it as a game of pulp urban fantasy with mythic heroes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Very easy for <b>Origins</b> level games, more difficult for <b>Hero</b>. It helps that the Titanomachy is far more varied and &quot;cold&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm assuming that \u201cTeam Mage\u201d refers to <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>, as opposed to <b>Mage: the Ascension</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the most part, though two members of the latter are now on Team Scion as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More generally, are there any spoilers you can provide about how Magic will work in Scion 2e? I know we're going to have sorcerers in Origin; and presumably magic will be tied to whatever mythology the practitioner subscribes to. But as I understand it, there are vast differences between the rune-based magic of the Norse people, Voodoo/Hoodoo/Santiera/etc., Egyptian mysticism, the Hermetic magic of Greek descent, Shinto priests, and Aztec blood magic, just to mention the most common magical practices associated with the original six Scion Pantheons \u2014 so much so that whole games can be (and have been) written about just one of them. How are you going to address this in <b>Scion</b> such that the magic rules only take up a portion of <b>Scion Origin</b> but still manage to capture the distinct flavors of these different belief systems? </div> </div> </div>The answer leans more towards &quot;no&quot; to your question, but pantheon magic favors pretty heavily into the pantheon-specific Purviews.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T10:17:20-07:00","id":526813,"title":"","content":"How does gaining Legend work, is it bought with XP, given out by the GM, or something else? Because I remember that in 1e the power of higher level legend meant that anybody who didn't put every BP into it got left behind as the ones who did ascended to godhood very quickly, is this still the case or are different levels of Legend more balanced?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T11:49:52-07:00","id":526897,"title":"","content":"Is the new Edition planning on addressing the Elephant in the room that is Monotheism? Traditionally the forum has went the way of either making them servants of the Titans (Particularly Aten) or fidangleing them into the normal pantheon patterns.<br /> <br /> That segways into another question. Is the new Edition keeping the idea that belief does not empower or create deities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T14:01:58-07:00","id":527010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=526813#post526813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does gaining Legend work, is it bought with XP, given out by the GM, or something else? Because I remember that in 1e the power of higher level legend meant that anybody who didn't put every BP into it got left behind as the ones who did ascended to godhood very quickly, is this still the case or are different levels of Legend more balanced?</div> </div> </div> </div>Experience expenditure is linear, but right now - and this is pre-alpha - Legend dots are decoupled from direct experience expenditure anyways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the new Edition keeping the idea that belief does not empower or create deities?</div> </div> </div> </div>Create? No, belief doesn't create gods. Does it empower them? Probably not directly, or outside an alternate setting, though cults and followers will likely be playing a much bigger role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T14:41:53-07:00","id":527057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=527010#post527010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Experience expenditure is linear</b>, but right now - and this is pre-alpha - Legend dots are decoupled from direct experience expenditure anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the best thing I've heard so far, seeing as geometric XP was the first thing I houserule out of basically any game (never played nWoD 1e, but every other time I just gave out extra BP). It's good that Legend dots are decoupled from experience expenditure, as the only actual explanation I could find about it was 'it's basically your legend', which made it strange that it was upgraded with XP instead of going out there and doing legendary deeds or getting known.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T17:44:08-07:00","id":527210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=526897#post526897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That segways into another question. Is the new Edition keeping the idea that belief does not empower or create deities?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve wondered that myself\u2026 If mortal worship actually fueled the gods, then the gods could never have created man (repeatedly in some cases) as they\u2019d never had the power to begin with. Therefore there needs to be another mechanic for building up one\u2019s own legend, something that ties into all the \u201clegendary deeds\u201d the gods perform. One solution that comes to mind is that they absorb the legendary energies from the titans/minions they defeat, but that leaves more social and intellectual gods by the wayside, and really only serves as an excuse to spend EXP on Legend, which they have decoupled from EXP making the option invalid...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T20:24:46-07:00","id":527292,"title":"","content":"I've always considered it to be vague and nebulous cateloging of how important the being is to the metaphysics of the universe, however the Pantheon interprets it. I can justify it with Aesir Theology, and I imagine its probably easy enough to do with the vast majority of Pantheons as well.<br /> <br /> This solves the issue of &quot;Fighting&quot; scions getting all the important legendXPs from fallen foes. You simply have to do things that are &quot;Important and Mythic&quot; Which is nebulous enough to cover just about anything your table wants to handle, within reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T22:58:02-07:00","id":527366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=527210#post527210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve wondered that myself\u2026 If mortal worship actually fueled the gods, then the gods could never have created man (repeatedly in some cases) as they\u2019d never had the power to begin with. Therefore there needs to be another mechanic for building up one\u2019s own legend, something that ties into all the \u201clegendary deeds\u201d the gods perform. One solution that comes to mind is that they absorb the legendary energies from the titans/minions they defeat, but that leaves more social and intellectual gods by the wayside, and really only serves as an excuse to spend EXP on Legend, which they have decoupled from EXP making the option invalid...</div> </div> </div> </div>I have always liked how power derived from worship/recognition was handled in the comic Fables. For those characters, being a popular story gave you some supernatural oomph, but you could also draw power from other things, your homelands, your lineage, your training. Jack of Fables, who was all the Jacks from every story, was a terrible person and deserved to die ten times over but things always seemed uncannily go his way in the end. Frau Totenkinder drew her power increments from the world around her, her place of power, and was sparring and subtle in her expenditure of her great reserves. Bigby Wolf is the son of the North Wind, one of the most powerful beings in existence, and his changeable nature is a reflection of his bloodline. Bigby then in turn passes the power on to his children, along with the not insignificant power of his wife Snow's family as well<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T05:55:36-07:00","id":527575,"title":"","content":"Being a known deity should lend weight compared to hundreds of anonymous already out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T12:51:59-07:00","id":528017,"title":"","content":"What kind of effort does it take to destroy a pantheon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T15:03:23-07:00","id":528121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=528017#post528017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of effort does it take to destroy a pantheon?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gallic_Wars\" target=\"_blank\">a lot</a>, though obviously that depends on your definition of a lot. Divus Iulius certainly thought it took some doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T17:24:38-07:00","id":528276,"title":"","content":"If Gods do not depend on their worshippers for power, how does conquering the mortal culture associated with a Pantheon damage them? There aren't large numbers of people worshipping the pantheons of the Aztec, Inca, Maya, Toltec, Cherokee, Dine/Navajo, Zuni, Inuit, Algonquin, Seminole, Roman, Slavic, Greek, Norse, Egyptian, Sumerian, Irish, etc. Those Pantheons are doing fine. What's so special about the conquest of Gaul that not only the native worship but the <i>actual Gods</i> were &quot;destroyed&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T17:58:21-07:00","id":528304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=528276#post528276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Gods do not depend on their worshippers for power, how does conquering the mortal culture associated with a Pantheon damage them? There aren't large numbers of people worshipping the pantheons of the Aztec, Inca, Maya, Toltec, Cherokee, Dine/Navajo, Zuni, Inuit, Algonquin, Seminole, Roman, Slavic, Greek, Norse, Egyptian, Sumerian, Irish, etc. Those Pantheons are doing fine. What's so special about the conquest of Gaul that not only the native worship but the <i>actual Gods</i> were &quot;destroyed&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a a guess but I imagine the Greek/Roman pantheon was probably involved directly in that conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T18:21:19-07:00","id":528313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=528276#post528276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's so special about the conquest of Gaul that not only the native worship but the <i>actual Gods</i> were &quot;destroyed&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a lot that's changing in 2e, but the fate of the Nemetondevos isn't one of them - if anything, it's worse. The destruction of the Gaulish pantheon is one of those events where the history of the World in <b>Scion </b>diverges from our actual history, chiefly because I'm fairly certain Julius Caesar wasn't actually a Roman Scion. Their priests and druids were killed, their sacred shrines abandoned or torn down, their worshippers brought in chains back to Rome. If you kill off and enslave an entire population, so much that it's difficult to find <i>any </i>information on their gods, and the actual entities abandon their Overworld and allied Terra Incognitia, how does that <i>not</i> constitute destroying the pantheon? Gods don't die easily, but they <i>can </i>die, and so can pantheons. Even if the constituent gods are still alive (contrast &quot;still exist&quot;), sulking in their Underworld effectively means the pantheon's gone.<br /> <br /> This is <b>Scion</b> - lots of entities persist beyond death and can return to life, pantheons included.<br /> <br /> (Don't get up in arms about the Atlantean pantheon, though. I wouldn't count on them showing up for a long while, if ever.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T18:40:08-07:00","id":528367,"title":"","content":"Will fatebinding exist and, if so, will there be more specifics to the system?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T18:50:37-07:00","id":528370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=528367#post528367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will fatebinding exist and, if so, will there be more specifics to the system?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and in a far more specified version than before. Playability and connection to the overarching story being told at the table are what we're trying to look at when we put any system in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T18:55:01-07:00","id":528372,"title":"","content":"A question on the Loa: I know that the concept of Rada and Petwo is kinda hard to pin down, and while I had no problem with declaring the likes of Kalfu and Legba being separate deities and knowing that the Loa are getting a major overhaul is that something that's being introduced? (I am also aware that some view the Petwo as &quot;younger&quot; loa, birthed from the horrors of their people's enslavement... at which point the question is moot).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T19:18:54-07:00","id":528381,"title":"","content":"So, I have a question about the Fertility Purview (winner of the Griff Lifetime Achievement Award for Most Misleadingly Named Scion Purview). Namely, while the idea of being in charge of plants is cool in theory, and resonant with mythology, it never really translated into something worthwhile in Scion (for example: Unless you wanted to be nice to mortal farmers, all three Boons from Hero just don't have any use at all). Meanwhile, every pantheon has at least one deity in charge of plants, because they're responsible for giving you food and no one likes starving. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/74082-what-should-each-purview-do-in-2e\">I made a thread about this a while back</a>, but I'm curious as to how 2e might deal with the Fertility Purview","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T19:34:55-07:00","id":528386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=528313#post528313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a lot that's changing in 2e, but the fate of the Nemetondevos isn't one of them - if anything, it's worse. The destruction of the Gaulish pantheon is one of those events where the history of the World in <b>Scion </b>diverges from our actual history, chiefly because I'm fairly certain Julius Caesar wasn't actually a Roman Scion. Their priests and druids were killed, their sacred shrines abandoned or torn down, their worshippers brought in chains back to Rome. If you kill off and enslave an entire population, so much that it's difficult to find <i>any </i>information on their gods...</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but that happened to several civilizations. We know barely anything about a lot of societies. Scythians, Minoans, for example, are their Pantheons dead, too? Some of the Native American cultures aren't in much better condition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=528313#post528313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and the actual entities abandon their Overworld and allied Terra Incognitia, how does that <i>not</i> constitute destroying the pantheon?</div> </div> </div> </div>That totally does constitute it, but how did the one (mortal devastation) lead to the second (pantheon devastation)? That's my question. If all these other civilizations had their sacred sites destroyed, their stories lost to history, their priests and cults enslaved/murdered/killed, why did their Gods endure, but not the Gauls? I'm totally with you on the level of destruction that hit the <i>mortal</i> Gauls, but how did that affect their Gods? If the Gods don't need their human followers for food/prayer/sacrifice or whatever, then why would the Gods &quot;die&quot; just because their civilization was wiped out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T20:12:40-07:00","id":528433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>griffinguy24</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I have a question about the Fertility Purview</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, that thread was great, so thanks for that (in fact, I was just discussing Adonis earlier today, as an example of...nah, that'd be telling).<br /> <br /> I don't want to give any Purview spoilers right now, but I <i>will </i>say that besides the various excellent possibilities you mentioned in that thread, let me reiterate that cults are a <i>thing</i> in this edition. None of the three Fertility Boons in <b>Scion 1e</b> were worth a tinker's damn, I'll agree with you, but if there were a system for cults in place? Given a bit of committed Legend expenditures, you could greatly ease the lives of your followers or fellow worshippers of the pantheon - and that's just the prosaic application of a ton of fresh food and lessened grocery bills. Add the idea of Idunn-lite - giving your food certain blessings or encouraging traits - and suddenly a small core of your cult and specially-blessed followers are far more potent and effective than they were before.<br /> <br /> Purviews are going to be way bigger, more varied and unique, and interesting in ways gross and subtle, than the three powers per provided in 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T21:41:49-07:00","id":528517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=528433#post528433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, that thread was great, so thanks for that (in fact, I was just discussing Adonis earlier today, as an example of...nah, that'd be telling).<br /> <br /> I don't want to give any Purview spoilers right now, but I <i>will </i>say that besides the various excellent possibilities you mentioned in that thread, let me reiterate that cults are a <i>thing</i> in this edition. None of the three Fertility Boons in <b>Scion 1e</b> were worth a tinker's damn, I'll agree with you, but if there were a system for cults in place? Given a bit of committed Legend expenditures, you could greatly ease the lives of your followers or fellow worshippers of the pantheon - and that's just the prosaic application of a ton of fresh food and lessened grocery bills. Add the idea of Idunn-lite - giving your food certain blessings or encouraging traits - and suddenly a small core of your cult and specially-blessed followers are far more potent and effective than they were before.<br /> <br /> Purviews are going to be way bigger, more varied and unique, and interesting in ways gross and subtle, than the three powers per provided in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neat stuff.<br /> <br /> I know you don't want to give spoilers, and I'm sure there's still a lot of stuff to be hammered down yet, but can I ask which Purview is shaping up to be your favorite so far?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T23:20:42-07:00","id":528579,"title":"","content":"Also a question on purviews not so much a spoiler on purviews themselves more a scalability question. I've played scion 1st ed and also similar games now, an impression I got with the purviews from each of those games was that at the lowest tiers (2,3 legend in scion) they are as good as useless (sky 3 not but that is another thing entirely anyway, as flying is always cool ^^). Whereas what is useful you start to get at middle to high tiers (5+ in scion). <br /> <br /> My question there for the 2nd edition: Will this sort of problem be addressed? Aka will the purviews be quite useful and feeling godly even at low tiers already?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T10:05:13-07:00","id":528905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nervaqus987</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know you don't want to give spoilers, and I'm sure there's still a lot of stuff to be hammered down yet, but can I ask which Purview is shaping up to be your favorite so far?</div> </div> </div> </div>War, though even that's subject to change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=528579#post528579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question there for the 2nd edition: Will this sort of problem be addressed? Aka will the purviews be quite useful and feeling godly even at low tiers already?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was a writer on 2e <b>Exalted</b>, especially towards the end of the line. Without harping on it overly much, a lot of Exalted 1e - and even 2e - had what we call <i>speedbump </i>Charms. Power A is whack a guy, Power B is whack a guy real good. Once you'd bought Power B, which had Power A as a prerequisite, there was no real need to ever use Power A ever again. It was a bump into the road to the thing you actually wanted.<br /> <br /> <b>Infernals </b>was really the first <b>Exalted </b>book to explicitly repudiate that methodology; we approached the Infernal Charmset with the idea that powers should scale with you, and that Charms that upgraded your capabilities were treated as upgrades to the earlier Charm. Nobody should discard something they bought with hard-won XP, and powers should scale upward with the practitioner. I still believe in that approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T10:10:32-07:00","id":528910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=524472#post524472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alfar or sidhe descent should be possible, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aahhh. This, I really like. I mean, a band of Scions is one thing, but a Scion with a band of followers (all PCs) descended from elves is another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/173-morimaruvik","name":"Morimaruvik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar173_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T13:29:22-07:00","id":529195,"title":"","content":"I would hope the Alfar get more of an accurate treatment than the 1E Vain fashionista, which was painful in how it missed the mark.<br /> <br /> A game with a PC(s) descending from the Alfar would be excellent and fit rather easily into the canon. While the lesser Alfar are more akin to pantheistic spirits of objects, concepts and natural features, the &quot;Noble&quot; Alfar are almost entirely indistinguishable from the Gods. Whats the Difference between Dainn and Bragi? I have no idea, strange that they set you at the far end of the table and Freyr demands that you pour his Drink for him....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T04:07:31-07:00","id":530871,"title":"","content":"Purviews will be different from the 3 per tier. meaning more than 3 powers per tier or something entirely different to a 'power list'?<br /> <br /> Will Knacks and Epics still be a thing similar to their 1e form or something entirely different? Or removed entirely?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T06:48:13-07:00","id":530948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=530871#post530871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Purviews will be different from the 3 per tier. meaning more than 3 powers per tier or something entirely different to a 'power list'?</div> </div> </div> </div>More than three powers per tier/also entirely different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Will Knacks and Epics still be a thing similar to their 1e form or something entirely different? Or removed entirely? </div> </div> </div>Knacks are a thing, but a little more concentrated. They're attached to something other than Attributes.<br /> <br /> Epics are gone in their original form. Sardonyx has an innate scaling mechanic right now (in the pre-playtesting phase of Scion); &quot;Epics&quot; are more permission to scale upwards, and there are Knacks that relate to Might. You can still shotput a Volkswagon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 05-28-2015, 09:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T07:17:39-07:00","id":530959,"title":"","content":"But can you also recognize the army of the dead's tactics with nary a glance and prepare a successful counter offensive? (my point being are the mental knacks going to be a wee bit more useful this time around? gods of war that aren't actually tacticians until 6mo after the game comes out can be frustrating).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T07:20:06-07:00","id":530961,"title":"","content":"Yes, War will support tacticians and generals as well as Achilles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T07:48:25-07:00","id":531011,"title":"","content":"<i>Shotput a Volkswagon</i>...there's an image.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T10:02:57-07:00","id":531101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=531011#post531011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Shotput a Volkswagon</i>...there's an image.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ummmm.... why? That's meat and drink in elementary Scion. Trivial even.<br /> <br /> I've had Hero level characters who could run 140mph, easy. Across water and up the sides of buildings even. At low-level Demigod it was was more an exercise in orbital mechanics than in Scion math to put a football into LEO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T10:17:02-07:00","id":531111,"title":"","content":"I rather enjoyed Epic Strength at max and hitting someone with France. Cathartic even.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T10:31:08-07:00","id":531120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=531111#post531111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I rather enjoyed Epic Strength at max and hitting someone with France. Cathartic even.</div> </div> </div> </div>How <i>horrifying</i>. You would break the crust of the World like the bread France loves so much? You would silence the <i>chanson de geste</i> forever? Condemn the gods of Gaul once more to ignominy and death rather than glorious resurrection? Such a deed will color your Legend for all time!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 05-28-2015, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T11:41:43-07:00","id":531171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=531120#post531120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How <i>horrifying</i>. You would break the crust of the World like the bread France loves so much? You would silence the <i>chanson de geste</i> forever? Condemn the gods of Gaul once more to ignominy and death rather than glorious resurrection? Such a deed will color your Legend for all time!</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, there's much better ways of dealing with the French!<br /> <br /> I'm a bit upset Epics are gone, in my view the problem was more due to their scaling and always being a better investment than normal dots, they actually felt more mythological to me than some of the boons (although that may just be me having a slightly limited experience of mythology).<br /> <br /> Will we have Craftsmanship/Forgery purviews for Scions in 2e? Because the things that annoyed me the most about the 1e core were the lack of Frost, Illusion, and Craftsmanship powers. The first two were solved with Ragnarok, but the third never showed up, despite god of the forge being a decent archetype to aim for.<br /> <br /> On a related note, will there be guidelines for developing our own purviews?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T12:05:03-07:00","id":531188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=530961#post530961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, War will support tacticians and generals as well as Achilles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referring more to Mental Knacks as the original Hero book's mental knacks felt more like filler (You can taste better than anyone, ever; you can calculate the tip before you see the bill) neat stuff, but a bit <b>too</b> general for the players to actually make into something cool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=531011#post531011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Shotput a Volkswagon</i>...there's an image.</div> </div> </div> </div>Had a player do it in a Vampire game in which players were elders AND another do it in a Promethean game more recently... it tends to 'shut down' the game... people applauding and laughing giddily. Very, very cool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=531171#post531171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Will we have Craftsmanship/Forgery purviews for Scions in 2e? Because the things that annoyed me the most about the 1e core were the lack of Frost, Illusion, and Craftsmanship powers. The first two were solved with Ragnarok, but the third never showed up, despite god of the forge being a decent archetype to aim for.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It was more covered by God Level Intelligence knacks and some others that appeared in the Companion, which made sense as it made crafting/modifying relics and technology more 'free form' rather than dependent on which power was which (though &quot;the Forge&quot; avatar might have been stupid cool).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":256,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","user":"Gnomish American","date":".  Condesced three posts into one. 05-28-2015, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T12:14:25-07:00","id":531194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=531171#post531171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a bit upset Epics are gone, in my view the problem was more due to their scaling and always being a better investment than normal dots, they actually felt more mythological to me than some of the boons (although that may just be me having a slightly limited experience of mythology).</div> </div> </div> </div>They're still <i>there</i>, they're just not called Epics and you don't buy them as specific dot levels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Will we have Craftsmanship/Forgery purviews for Scions in 2e? Because the things that annoyed me the most about the 1e core were the lack of Frost, Illusion, and Craftsmanship powers. The first two were solved with Ragnarok, but the third never showed up, despite god of the forge being a decent archetype to aim for. </div> </div> </div>There's a whole crafting subsystem, for when you do a favor for dwarves. Crafter God should be a thing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T13:09:40-07:00","id":531219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=531120#post531120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How <i>horrifying</i>. You would break the crust of the World like the bread France loves so much? You would silence the <i>chanson de geste</i> forever? Condemn the gods of Gaul once more to ignominy and death rather than glorious resurrection? Such a deed will color your Legend for all time!</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention what it would do to the citizens of France.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T13:34:58-07:00","id":531234,"title":"","content":"Maybe they should have thought about that before deciding to be born there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T17:18:06-07:00","id":531405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=531011#post531011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Shotput a Volkswagon</i>...there's an image.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah.<br /> <img src=\"http://www.tuffgnarl.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/10/actioncomics.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T18:23:11-07:00","id":531477,"title":"","content":"That's a Studebaker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T23:17:32-07:00","id":531753,"title":"","content":"What is going to combat vs. social/world-building breakdown of the game? If D&amp;D is nearly 100% combat, and Exalted 2e is 75% combat 25% social, and WoD edges in closer to 50% combat 50% social, where do you see Scion falling?<br /> <br /> I know these values are kinda arbitrary because people can choose to focus in on just one element or the other, but I think they are pretty realistic representation of the coverage combat vs. social get in these systems as written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T00:25:22-07:00","id":531773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=531120#post531120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How <i>horrifying</i>. You would break the crust of the World like the bread France loves so much? You would silence the <i>chanson de geste</i> forever? Condemn the gods of Gaul once more to ignominy and death rather than glorious resurrection? Such a deed will color your Legend for all time!</div> </div> </div> </div>In my defence, the moon had been warped into a vast Egg that was birthing a Titan and I needed something suitably weighty to Hurl to the Moon to put a stop to that nonsense.<br /> <br /> I...uhhh...had to withdraw to the overworld for just a bit after that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T03:32:48-07:00","id":531830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=531111#post531111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I rather enjoyed Epic Strength at max and hitting someone with France. Cathartic even.</div> </div> </div> </div>Leave us alone. D:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T06:49:17-07:00","id":531931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=531830#post531830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Leave us alone. D:</div> </div> </div> </div>It hurt us more than it hurt you and, lets face it, you brought it on yourselves. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T12:16:21-07:00","id":532112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=531188#post531188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was more covered by God Level Intelligence knacks and some others that appeared in the Companion, which made sense as it made crafting/modifying relics and technology more 'free form' rather than dependent on which power was which (though &quot;the Forge&quot; avatar might have been stupid cool).</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mind pointing me towards them? I found the rules on creating Relics (which I like), but I didn't find any Knacks to support crafters in either God or Companion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T12:42:20-07:00","id":532123,"title":"","content":"<b>Concept to Execution </b>for one... aaand maybe that's all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T23:22:45-07:00","id":532956,"title":"","content":"That was, indeed, the only &quot;crafting&quot; power in Scion. It's also a poorly written power, since it's trying to cover... uh, everything, all at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T16:02:10-07:00","id":565822,"title":"","content":"Hey, Neall, congrats on the promotion.<br /> <br /> I know this thread has been quiet and you're likely busy, but I just have small queries to feed a mounting curiosity.<br /> <br /> Now that you are a developer in the line, is there anything you might feel like changing in setting or system that you might, uh... let slip for us? Even vagaries?<br /> <br /> Also: It's been a month since Scutarii wondered what you believe to be the coolest purview power so far written. Can you share, or is it still hazy?<br /> <br /> Thanks for indulging me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3708-amateur-hour","name":"Amateur Hour","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T16:20:00-07:00","id":565835,"title":"","content":"I seem to remember him saying that as of that question War was the coolest but that only because it was literally the one sitting in front of him at the time.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T10:05:32-07:00","id":566630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amateur Hour</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=565822#post565822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that you are a developer in the line, is there anything you might feel like changing in setting or system that you might, uh... let slip for us? Even vagaries?</div> </div> </div> </div>Scions aren't <i>just </i>made from one divine parent, one mortal parent, though that's by far the easiest and most common type of Scion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also: It's been a month since Scutarii wondered what you believe to be the coolest purview power so far written. Can you share, or is it still hazy? </div> </div> </div>It'll probably be hazy for months yet. It's my hope to take the safeties off Scion playtesting at the end of the year, but realistically it'll probably be early 2016.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T10:16:04-07:00","id":566636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=532956#post532956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was, indeed, the only &quot;crafting&quot; power in Scion. It's also a poorly written power, since it's trying to cover... uh, everything, all at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>Crafting is planned to be way more of a thing, and not just things Scions can do, either (they could commission an artifact from forge-gods or dwarves or something).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T12:43:02-07:00","id":566816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=566636#post566636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Crafting is planned to be way more of a thing, and not just things Scions can do, either (they could commission an artifact from forge-gods or dwarves or something).</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me wonder, how human sized are dwarves, and can a dwarf eventually become a god? Is dwarfiness a valid area to god around in? If not, could a dwarf theoretically become the Asier god of beards?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T13:23:36-07:00","id":566871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=566816#post566816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes me wonder, how human sized are dwarves</div> </div> </div> </div>Not very.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> can a dwarf eventually become a god </div> </div> </div>Not unless their parent is a god. At best, they could maybe achieve god-level crafting capabilities, but they certainly couldn't use those weapons in any grand capacity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is dwarfiness a valid area to god around in? If not, could a dwarf theoretically become the Asier god of beards? </div> </div> </div>I don't think so in either case!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T00:23:42-07:00","id":567497,"title":"","content":"Is there anything you can share about the Titans yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T13:13:07-07:00","id":591654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=567497#post567497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anything you can share about the Titans yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>A little. I'm changing up the way the Titan structure works, slightly. Titans are still different in cause and kind than the gods, though the main difference lies in politics.<br /> <br /> Not all Legendary Creatures are titanspawn, and that title doesn't automatically carry a stigma (at least not objectively; certain pantheons will feel differently. The Aesir won't particularly care, while the Theoi might care more).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T13:55:54-07:00","id":591740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=591654#post591654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all Legendary Creatures are titanspawn, and that title doesn't automatically carry a stigma (at least not objectively; certain pantheons will feel differently. The Aesir won't particularly care, while the Theoi might care more).</div> </div> </div> </div>So at the risk of covering ground already tread and forgotten, there won't be that element of &quot;Gods have a lot of possible virtues that are all--at least from their own perspective--some sort of benevolence, while Titans all espouse Dark Virtues about being a right bastard?&quot; anymore?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T14:40:30-07:00","id":591811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=591740#post591740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So at the risk of covering ground already tread and forgotten, there won't be that element of &quot;Gods have a lot of possible virtues that are all--at least from their own perspective--some sort of benevolence, while Titans all espouse Dark Virtues about being a right bastard?&quot; anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div>All Titans are dangerous and problematic (well, more problematic than gods) to let roam free, and many Titans are right bastards, but not all Titans are dangerous <i>because</i> they're right bastards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T15:36:02-07:00","id":591944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=591654#post591654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A little. I'm changing up the way the Titan structure works, slightly. Titans are still different in cause and kind than the gods, though the main difference lies in politics.<br /> <br /> Not all Legendary Creatures are titanspawn, and that title doesn't automatically carry a stigma (at least not objectively; certain pantheons will feel differently. The Aesir won't particularly care, while the Theoi might care more).</div> </div> </div> </div>Does the title &quot;Theoi&quot; as opposed to &quot;Dodekatheon&quot; indicate that you're introducing additional Greek gods beyond the main 12? If so, which ones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6592-mrbridger","name":"MrBridger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T19:23:51-07:00","id":592228,"title":"","content":"Since Demeter (who is pretty much ALWAYS considered a member) was deep-sixed for Hades (who is very seldom considered a member) in the first place, even the original Scion Dodekatheon... wasn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T19:51:26-07:00","id":592234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrBridger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=591944#post591944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the title &quot;Theoi&quot; as opposed to &quot;Dodekatheon&quot; indicate that you're introducing additional Greek gods beyond the main 12? If so, which ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>Theoi is the name for the general pantheon, though some purely Roman gods and an Etruscan god or two hang around in their own sub-pantheons. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Demeter (who is pretty much ALWAYS considered a member) was deep-sixed for Hades (who is very seldom considered a member) in the first place, even the original Scion Dodekatheon... wasn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rightfully so, in my opinion. Hear me out! Since Pluto (and Dis Pater, who's somewhat separate) was far more important to the Roman pantheon, and Hades/Pluto has a far greater significance and presence in modern, average knowledge of those pantheons. Scion's about modern myth just as much as the ancient myth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T21:30:18-07:00","id":592295,"title":"","content":"Demeter was always a bit too chthonic for a Scion style god anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T06:15:07-07:00","id":592553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=592295#post592295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demeter was always a bit too chthonic for a Scion style god anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>She'll definitely be in the core in 2e, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T10:19:10-07:00","id":592894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=592295#post592295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demeter was always a bit too chthonic for a Scion style god anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>More chthonic than (conservatively) Freya, Izanami, Tlazoteotl or Danu? Hardly. <br /> <br /> Seems more like the magic number was &quot;12&quot; and the authors thought that having Hades as a father just seemed cooler than having Demeter as a mom. After all, Hades gets TONS of press (even if it has pretty much nothing to do with how he was actually perceived) and Demeter doesn't even show up in most modern media productions of Greek Mythology. (Mystery cults be damned, I tell you!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T20:06:30-07:00","id":593478,"title":"","content":"Izanami is a good point, but I simply meant she was (among the greeks) pretty hard core and I understand why she was left out. She was the first goddess I wrote up for my own games and i'm glad to have her back in second.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T17:17:39-07:00","id":595153,"title":"","content":"Not sure how she was more hardcore than the other Greek gods... By condemning the world to winter because she was upset about her daughter's rape/kidnapping? By holding a baby in the fire to burn out his mortality? Getting raped in her own turn by her brother Poseidonand giving birth to an immortal horsie? Luring a guy away from a wedding for a tumble in a field then getting him killed because Zeus saw the mud on her ass? Those run from pretty ho-hum normal to relatively tame overall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T21:17:58-07:00","id":595348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=595153#post595153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By holding a baby in the fire to burn out his mortality?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not familiar with that story, who did she do that to?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T06:25:44-07:00","id":595574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=595348#post595348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not familiar with that story, who did she do that to?</div> </div> </div> </div> <b>Demeter at Eleusis[<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Demeter&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" target=\"_blank\">edit</a>]</b><br /><br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Eleusis2.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Eleusis2.jpg/170px-Eleusis2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eleusinian_mysteries\" target=\"_blank\">Eleusinian trio</a>: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Persephone\" target=\"_blank\">Persephone</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Triptolemos\" target=\"_blank\">Triptolemos</a>, and Demeter, on a marble <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bas-relief\" target=\"_blank\">bas-relief</a> from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eleusis\" target=\"_blank\">Eleusis</a>, 440\u2013430 BC<br /> <br /> <br /> Demeter's search for her daughter Persephone took her to the palace of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celeus\" target=\"_blank\">Celeus</a>, the King of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eleusis\" target=\"_blank\">Eleusis</a> in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Attica,_Greece\" target=\"_blank\">Attica</a>. She assumed the form of an old woman, and asked him for shelter. He took her in, to nurse <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demophon_of_Eleusis\" target=\"_blank\">Demophon</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Triptolemus\" target=\"_blank\">Triptolemus</a>, his sons by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metanira\" target=\"_blank\">Metanira</a>. To reward his kindness, she planned to make Demophon immortal; she secretly anointed the boy with <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ambrosia\" target=\"_blank\">ambrosia</a> and laid him in the flames of the hearth, to gradually burn away his mortal self. But Metanira walked in, saw her son in the fire and screamed in fright. Demeter abandoned the attempt. Instead, she taught Triptolemus the secrets of agriculture, and he in turn taught them to any who wished to learn them. Thus, humanity learned how to plant, grow and harvest grain. The myth has several versions; some are linked to figures such as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eleusis_(mythology)\" target=\"_blank\">Eleusis</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rarus\" target=\"_blank\">Rarus</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trochilus_(mythology)\" target=\"_blank\">Trochilus</a>. The Demophon element may be based on an earlier folk tale.<sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demeter#cite_note-39\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[39]</span></a></sup><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T08:06:12-07:00","id":595645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=595348#post595348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not familiar with that story, who did she do that to?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Basically, back when Demeter was searching for her daughter, she ended up in this one kingdom in the guise of an old woman.<br /> <br /> She ended up meeting the queen of the kingdom and told her that she was looking for her kidnapped daughter. In response, the queen invited Demeter into her home and her oldest son said he'd go out and look for her daughter.<br /> <br /> Demeter was so touched by their kindness that she said she'd nurse the queen's youngest child and decided on her own to make him immortal. Unfortunately, the queen happened in at the wrong time and whisked the kid out of the fire. Demeter instead taught them a ton about agriculture and later promoted the oldest son into a god of agriculture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T09:07:10-07:00","id":595694,"title":"","content":"It's effectively one of the most important parts of THE Demeter myth cycle and was an important part of the Eleusian Mysteries. Insofar as we know, since they were, well, Mysterious and not a lot got written down about them, particularly by insiders of the cult proper. And they didn't leave a ton of material evidence to go by. <br /> <br /> (Having said that, we know more about the elusive mysterious Eleusian Mysteries than we know about entire other pantheons - &quot;Gaulish&quot;, Hittite, a lot of Native American pantheons from tribes that were wiped out/suffered culture collapse pre-anthropologist, etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T09:46:15-07:00","id":595712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=595574#post595574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>Demeter at Eleusis[<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Demeter&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" target=\"_blank\">edit</a>]</b><br /><br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Eleusis2.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Eleusis2.jpg/170px-Eleusis2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eleusinian_mysteries\" target=\"_blank\">Eleusinian trio</a>: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Persephone\" target=\"_blank\">Persephone</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Triptolemos\" target=\"_blank\">Triptolemos</a>, and Demeter, on a marble <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bas-relief\" target=\"_blank\">bas-relief</a> from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eleusis\" target=\"_blank\">Eleusis</a>, 440\u2013430 BC<br /> <br /> <br /> Demeter's search for her daughter Persephone took her to the palace of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celeus\" target=\"_blank\">Celeus</a>, the King of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eleusis\" target=\"_blank\">Eleusis</a> in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Attica,_Greece\" target=\"_blank\">Attica</a>. She assumed the form of an old woman, and asked him for shelter. He took her in, to nurse <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demophon_of_Eleusis\" target=\"_blank\">Demophon</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Triptolemus\" target=\"_blank\">Triptolemus</a>, his sons by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metanira\" target=\"_blank\">Metanira</a>. To reward his kindness, she planned to make Demophon immortal; she secretly anointed the boy with <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ambrosia\" target=\"_blank\">ambrosia</a> and laid him in the flames of the hearth, to gradually burn away his mortal self. But Metanira walked in, saw her son in the fire and screamed in fright. Demeter abandoned the attempt. Instead, she taught Triptolemus the secrets of agriculture, and he in turn taught them to any who wished to learn them. Thus, humanity learned how to plant, grow and harvest grain. The myth has several versions; some are linked to figures such as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eleusis_(mythology)\" target=\"_blank\">Eleusis</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rarus\" target=\"_blank\">Rarus</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trochilus_(mythology)\" target=\"_blank\">Trochilus</a>. The Demophon element may be based on an earlier folk tale.<sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demeter#cite_note-39\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[39]</span></a></sup></div> </div> </div> </div>This whole section has been left out of every Greek Mythology book I've ever read!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T14:18:42-07:00","id":595970,"title":"","content":"Huh its one of the first I remember reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T01:10:19-07:00","id":596587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=592553#post592553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> She'll definitely be in the core in 2e, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I ended up dropping Hades after he was listed in the core and ruling that the &quot;Twelve&quot; of the Dodekatheon had by the modern day become Zeus, Hera, Poseidon, Athena, Ares, Aphrodite, Apollo, Artemis, Hermes, Hephaestus, Dionysus, and <i><b>PERSEPHONE</b></i>.<br /> <br /> With the idea being that Demeter was missing, and Hades was under seige by the breaking loose of Tartarus, and thus Persephone speaks for both on Olympus. Her Scions who received their Visitation in Spring, Summer, or early Autumn tend to favor her mother's divine aspects. Those Visited in late Autumn or Winter tend to favor her husband's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T01:23:48-07:00","id":596588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=591654#post591654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A little. I'm changing up the way the Titan structure works, slightly. Titans are still different in cause and kind than the gods, though the main difference lies in politics.</div> </div> </div> </div>My idea on this one was to drop the labels &quot;Greater Titan&quot; and &quot;Titan Avatar&quot; and just make the world-forms &quot;Primordials&quot;, and the avatars &quot;Titans&quot;. When Kronus castrated Ouranos (slew a previous governing Titan) he became the ruling Titan of the Primordial at the time. When the Gods bound the titans, the Primordial world-forms remain, making up most of the Overworld, but they're innert without governing Titans.<br /> <br /> I cannot stress enough that if Ra is a god, than his progeny Shu &amp; Tefnut, and their progeny Nut need to be gods as well. They're literally three of the nine who the &quot;Psedjet&quot; are named for.<br /> <br /> For Egyptian Titans I'd recommend using the Ogdoad. Amun/Amunet can be related to Kronus (perhaps Ra having usurped the title in their defeat). Huh/Hauhet to Rhea (who is a ruling Titan of Gaea, marked on vengeance for her children's betrayal, as she only wanted Kronus defeated not the Titans bound) and Coatlicue. Nun/Naunet to Tethys and Tiamat. Kuk/Kauket to Mikaboshi, Crius, and Ahriman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T01:33:33-07:00","id":596589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=566636#post566636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Crafting is planned to be way more of a thing, and not just things Scions can do, either (they could commission an artifact from forge-gods or dwarves or something).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I assume this is also something I can bug Cyclopes or other mythic crafter races over?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T03:58:04-07:00","id":596685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=596587#post596587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I ended up dropping Hades after he was listed in the core and ruling that the &quot;Twelve&quot; of the Dodekatheon had by the modern day become Zeus, Hera, Poseidon, Athena, Ares, Aphrodite, Apollo, Artemis, Hermes, Hephaestus, Dionysus, and <i><b>PERSEPHONE</b></i>.<br /> <br /> With the idea being that Demeter was missing, and Hades was under seige by the breaking loose of Tartarus, and thus Persephone speaks for both on Olympus. Her Scions who received their Visitation in Spring, Summer, or early Autumn tend to favor her mother's divine aspects. Those Visited in late Autumn or Winter tend to favor her husband's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Persephone was the Dodekatheon Parent I used the most in Scion. I like the contrast between the &quot;bucolic Kore herald of spring&quot; and the &quot;Dread Persephone, goddess of necromancy and curses&quot;, personas and since she's a relatively obscure goddess, people are less likely to stereotype an eventual scion.<br /> I as a bit disappointed to see her absent fom Scion: Hero since she's still a very important figure in myth.<br /> <br /> It wasn't as bad as the absence of Aida Wedo from the Loa for example, but it was up there with the lack of Sekhmet in the Pesedjet.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":1405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","user":"Anteros","date":". 07-20-2015, 07:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T07:05:12-07:00","id":596867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=596588#post596588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My idea on this one was to drop the labels &quot;Greater Titan&quot; and &quot;Titan Avatar&quot; and just make the world-forms &quot;Primordials&quot;, and the avatars &quot;Titans&quot;. When Kronus castrated Ouranos (slew a previous governing Titan) he became the ruling Titan of the Primordial at the time. When the Gods bound the titans, the Primordial world-forms remain, making up most of the Overworld, but they're innert without governing Titans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the cut of your jib, glamourweaver.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I assume this is also something I can bug Cyclopes or other mythic crafter races over? </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I mean, you can also ask for it by yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T09:25:10-07:00","id":597028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=596685#post596685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It wasn't as bad as the absence of Aida Wedo from the Loa for example, but it was up there with the lack of Sekhmet in the Pesedjet.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>How about HATHOR being missing... Sekhmet is important enough to get a write up, but Hathor is one of the most worshiped goddesses,of Ancient Egypt and has several good myths. It would be like having Hera missing. It would be like having Frigg or Freya meeting. Hathor beats out Persephone hands down as critical goddess missing. Like Demeter. <br /> <br /> And female Loa. At LEAST they could have included Ayida Wedo, Maman Brigitte and La Siren. It would have been easy to separate her out from Mama Wati (who is a problematic Titan at best, a culturally sensitivity boondoggle on the order of Yahweh-I-mean-Aten at worst). It's not like there are titan-like-divine-entities out there whose areas of influence overlap with a gods (Helios/Apollo, etc. etc.) There were only ELEVEN Loa listed... There was definitely room to have a few more. As for space constraints... Just edit out 1 page of the story or the adventure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T09:37:57-07:00","id":597037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=597028#post597028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How about HATHOR being missing... Sekhmet is important enough to get a write up, but Hathor is one of the most worshiped goddesses,of Ancient Egypt and has several good myths.</div> </div> </div> </div>*cough*same goddess*cough*nurturing vs. warrior aspects*cough*<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T10:17:51-07:00","id":597056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=597028#post597028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How about HATHOR being missing... Sekhmet is important enough to get a write up, but Hathor is one of the most worshiped goddesses,of Ancient Egypt and has several good myths. It would be like having Hera missing. It would be like having Frigg or Freya meeting. Hathor beats out Persephone hands down as critical goddess missing. Like Demeter.<br /> <br /> And female Loa. At LEAST they could have included Ayida Wedo, Maman Brigitte and La Siren. It would have been easy to separate her out from Mama Wati (who is a problematic Titan at best, a culturally sensitivity boondoggle on the order of Yahweh-I-mean-Aten at worst). It's not like there are titan-like-divine-entities out there whose areas of influence overlap with a gods (Helios/Apollo, etc. etc.) There were only ELEVEN Loa listed... There was definitely room to have a few more. As for space constraints... Just edit out 1 page of the story or the adventure.</div> </div> </div> </div>As glamourweaver mentioned, Hathor is the gentle, nurturing aspect of the Eye of Ra hile Sekhmet is the warrior aspect of the same divinity. There's this whole myth with the red beer.<br /> As for Aida Wedo, her absence was particulary egregious since she and Damballah are not only married but share the same veve, meaning you can't represent Damballah without representing his wife!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T10:49:55-07:00","id":597069,"title":"","content":"How many types of scions (divine/human parents, forged from clay, etc) do you have in mind? And will they be listed in Origins or Hero?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":461,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","user":"KingCarnival","date":". 07-20-2015, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T11:11:53-07:00","id":597079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=597069#post597069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many types of scions (divine/human parents, forged from clay, etc) do you have in mind? And will they be listed in Origins or Hero?</div> </div> </div> </div>Four; in <b>Hero</b>. They'll have different social ties, though I don't think they'll be so different mechanically.<br /> <br /> Technically God + Legendary Being = demigod, God + God = God will be options in later books, but I don't really consider them radical enough to merit their own pseudo-splats. I'm undecided though - it depends on how the social ties shake out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 07-20-2015, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T11:56:56-07:00","id":597123,"title":"","content":"Is being a Scion the only way to become a god? If so, where did the first gods come from? Is it possible for there to be a scion without a god being directly involved? Is it possible for someone who isn't a scion to become a scion.<br /> <br /> Also, thank you, you have successfully made me regret buying 1e and not waiting for 2e to come out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T12:41:22-07:00","id":597184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=597123#post597123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is being a Scion the only way to become a god? If so, where did the first gods come from?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not precisely...most of the gods were either Scions themselves, or issue of the Titans (Scions of another name). Every once in a while you've got an entity like Baba Yaga who really blurs the lines when it comes to what divinity actually means.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it possible for there to be a scion without a god being directly involved? </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it possible for someone who isn't a scion to become a scion. </div> </div> </div>Yes! There's even a way mentioned in this very thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T13:21:04-07:00","id":597199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=597184#post597184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not precisely...most of the gods were either Scions themselves, or issue of the Titans (Scions of another name). Every once in a while you've got an entity like Baba Yaga who really blurs the lines when it comes to what divinity actually means.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will the game smack me if I want to say that Baba Yaga is the same being the Norse call Angraboda? Not to mention even more primordial overlaps like Vritra &amp; Apep? Or that the Vanir (whose remaining self-identified members are now Aesir) were in fact the pan-poto-Celtic Pantheon, and if you scale Yggdrasil looking for Vanaheim, you may find the furthest outlands of Tir Na Nog?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T13:51:03-07:00","id":597246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=597199#post597199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will the game smack me if I want to say that Baba Yaga is the same being the Norse call Angraboda? Not to mention even more primordial overlaps like Vritra &amp; Apep? Or that the Vanir (whose remaining self-identified members are now Aesir) were in fact the pan-poto-Celtic Pantheon?</div> </div> </div> </div>It'll smack you more than a little. But it's your game, do what you want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and if you scale Yggdrasil looking for Vanaheim, you may find the furthest outlands of Tir Na Nog? </div> </div> </div>This might smack you a little bit more, because Terra Incognita are a far more important setting piece for the game in 2e, and the Overworlds and Incognita aren't always precisely compatible with one another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 07-20-2015, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T13:55:21-07:00","id":597255,"title":"","content":"Interesting... I wonder which one of those is Terra Incognita, since both Vanaheim and Tir Na Nog are homelands of Gods... and Yggdrasil is basically the most iconic Axis Mundi there is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T13:58:58-07:00","id":597282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=597255#post597255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting... I wonder which one of those is Terra Incognita, since both Vanaheim and Tir Na Nog are homelands of Gods... and Yggdrasil is basically the most iconic Axis Mundi there is.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a bit of a conceptual change happening to axis mundi, Terra Incognita, and Godrealms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T15:30:27-07:00","id":597380,"title":"","content":"Will we get Pan as a potential divine parent in 2nd edition? One of the things that always irked me about 1st edition was assigning the Marsyas myth to him and then using that as justification for him embracing the concept of the Christian devil and becoming an evil bastard. While it was an original idea (and one that I even could have gotten behind if they had left those things having happened to Marsyas and let Pan remain as he was in myth), it is one that I'd rather not have as canon in 2nd edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T16:22:33-07:00","id":597478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=597380#post597380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will we get Pan as a potential divine parent in 2nd edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, though I haven't decided if the Marsyas myth will be separate, or if Pan will be core. Pan won't be &quot;The Devil&quot;, though. Can't well have satyrs as a playable character type and not have Pan in there somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T16:27:41-07:00","id":597483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=597037#post597037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *cough*same goddess*cough*nurturing vs. warrior aspects*cough*</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;COUGH&gt; Kalfu and Legba being separate gods &lt;COUGH&gt;<br /> <br /> If you are going to separate two beings that are pretty clearly the exact same person, there is definitely some precedent to, oh, I don't know, two SEPARATE goddesses that are syncretized and conflated sometimes and.... NOT syncretized and conflated by the Egyptians through their 3000 years of myths morphing, changing, bleeding into each other... (like, say, conflating Amun and Ra, who are the same and separate) even though, ya know, they are also two separate gods. though they are clearly separate beings with separate origins, separate roles in other myth cycles. Since, ya know, Hathor is JUST Isis, right? Why even have Isis, let's just have Sekhmet.... Then we get a three in one! Oh wait, Bast and Sekhmet are also identified as being the same in some sources... Now we have Sekhmet as the ultimate incarnated aspect of Bast, Isis and Hathor! We've just reduced the number of goddess by three!<br /> <br /> In fact, in a game like Scion, why would you ever want to artificially REDUCE the number of divine parents avaiable. Hell, I'd love to play a scion of one of the four and ask about that... Probably right after I met one of the other ones. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T16:32:41-07:00","id":597487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=597199#post597199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or that the Vanir (whose remaining self-identified members are now Aesir) were in fact the pan-poto-Celtic Pantheon, and if you scale Yggdrasil looking for Vanaheim, you may find the furthest outlands of Tir Na Nog?</div> </div> </div> </div>I did that in my first Scion game! One of the players was a Scion of Odin and had Ratatosk as his Guide. It took them a long time to figure out what in Hel he was chattering on about &quot;beyond the forests of the Vanaheim and Alfheim, the raven that is not Odin's musters the warriors of the Vanir's kin. Etc.&quot; Especially after the scene at that character's mortal adopted father's wake involving Ratatosk and a pecan pie....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T21:16:04-07:00","id":597830,"title":"","content":"I'm looking forward to creating a megaman scion, sense constructed scions are in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T22:31:02-07:00","id":597887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=597380#post597380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will we get Pan as a potential divine parent in 2nd edition? One of the things that always irked me about 1st edition was assigning the Marsyas myth to him and then using that as justification for him embracing the concept of the Christian devil and becoming an evil bastard. While it was an original idea (and one that I even could have gotten behind if they had left those things having happened to Marsyas and let Pan remain as he was in myth), it is one that I'd rather not have as canon in 2nd edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, what about Pan embracing satanism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T23:45:19-07:00","id":597974,"title":"","content":"Embracing is fine.<br /> <br /> Just no tongue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T07:19:10-07:00","id":598336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=597830#post597830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm looking forward to creating a megaman scion, sense constructed scions are in.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can give Megaman the same mythic resonance as Pygmalion's Galatea or Enkidu, well, more power to you. Dr. Light isn't exactly who I'd go with as a divine progenitor, though.<br /> <br /> Being the direct creation of a god doesn't <i>necessarily</i> make you a Scion, and it takes a miraculous intervention on the part of the god. Such miracles aren't easy and they aren't free. By <i>far</i> the easiest of the four methods of making a Scion is the &quot;old-fashioned way&quot;. The other options exist for gods and goddesses such as Ninhursag (for whom it's easier), Artemis (who vastly prefers investing her power), Ausir (who finds it difficult to create unless he's working with the dead), or anyone else who desires or requires options other than breeding.<br /> <br /> (Weirdly enough, Aphrodite has Scions of all four methods.)<br /> <br /> Adopting a divine child from another god is still a character creation choice, and one that doesn't require an investiture of power, but there's some <i>issues</i> with doing it that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T08:01:54-07:00","id":598356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheGraySoul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=597887#post597887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, what about Pan embracing satanism?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In the Demigod book, it was revealed that the medieval Christian devil, with horns &amp; cloven hooves - was in fact what Pan had been up to after the rise of Christianity in Europe.<br /> <br /> On the subject of gods who an Abrahamic Pantheon are going to see as &quot;Adversaries&quot; (besides the obvious Phoenician cases), I'd point out that one of the titles of the Roman Mithras, whose cult was an early rival of Christianity, was &quot;Lightbringer&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T08:04:58-07:00","id":598360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=597487#post597487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did that in my first Scion game! One of the players was a Scion of Odin and had Ratatosk as his Guide. It took them a long time to figure out what in Hel he was chattering on about &quot;beyond the forests of the Vanaheim and Alfheim, the raven that is not Odin's musters the warriors of the Vanir's kin. Etc.&quot; Especially after the scene at that character's mortal adopted father's wake involving Ratatosk and a pecan pie....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I assume the &quot;raven that is not Odin's&quot; is a certain Irish goddess in black armor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T09:29:46-07:00","id":598439,"title":"","content":"<br /> I can't begin to say how delighted I am that satyrs will be a playable character type, and I am also glad to hear that Pan is not going to be the Devil this time around. Since you haven't decided whether or not the Marsyas myth would be separate from Pan's legends yet, might I argue in favor of leaving Marsyas as a separate being? It would give a good example of a satyr in the game that had managed to be remembered in mortal myth, even if he was remembered for a rather crappy event.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheGraySoul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=597887#post597887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, what about Pan embracing satanism?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Demigod book, they made Pan a middle-tier appropriate foe bent on the corruption of sexuality in the world. No longer a God, he had masqueraded as the Christian Devil in order to get vengeance for a wrong done to him by Apollo (an event that had actually happened to a satyr named Marsyas in mythology, which I believe they assigned to Pan in Scion in order to have a more recognizable figure in that role).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T09:50:52-07:00","id":598456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=598360#post598360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I assume the &quot;raven that is not Odin's&quot; is a certain Irish goddess in black armor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup!<br /> <br /> I think it was &quot;ravens are not Odin's&quot;. I was running the Morrigan as more of &quot;timesharing &quot;title for Babh, Macha and Nemain. One of the other PCs was a Scion of the Morrigan and ended up having to figure out which of them was her &quot;real&quot; mom, or if that was actually of any importance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T09:54:19-07:00","id":598461,"title":"","content":"Assuming the same relative power-scaling, I'd be fine with Pan being a God instead of a Demigod, but he shouldn't be Legend 12. That status for the Thieo should be reserved for the Olympian 12 + their siblings who don't hold those seats for political reasons (Hestia and Hades).<br /> <br /> Persephone may be a special case, but even there her power is kind of a marrying representation of others purviews (Demeter and Hades). Her worship in Ancient Greece was largely not in the context of her own power, but rather that she had Hades' ear and unlike him was sympathetic to prayer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T11:21:33-07:00","id":598562,"title":"","content":"That's about how Legend works in this edition, yes.<br /> <br /> Let me tell you, I'm <i>really </i>looking forward to the arguments as to why M\u00f3\u00f0i and Magni should be Legend 11 instead of 10, but \u00der\u00fa\u00f0r is fine at Legend 9.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T11:44:50-07:00","id":598583,"title":"","content":"I'd prefer to see Legend 12 be reserved for the heavy hitters of the pantheons when applicable. as it stands now, the Legend system is very vague and I think its prime space to represent your overall respect and importance in the pantheon, which would be great for giving a comparison for players who achieved Apotheosis, rather than assigning all the Gods as roughly equal among themselves. Let legend 12 be something that even other gods take serious notice of.<br /> <br /> Zeus, Poseidon and Hades are all able to be represented as Legend 12 among the Theoi. Zeus is the stronger of the three brothers but each of them is a step above the rest of the Dodekatheon. Poseidon has an ongoing threat to establish a coup if Zeus doesn't behave and rule fairly and each was a contender for King of the Gods at one point. Most of the other Olympians could probably be best represented by Legend 11, still enormously powerful but not at that comparable height. Many of the lesser deities could take Legend 10 or 9 (Prime space for Eros and the like, Gods in their own right but obviously lesser than the Olympians and not even comparable to Zeus)<br /> <br /> Odin, Thor and Freyr have to take a similar role among the Aesir, being the three most worshiped and forming a sort of triumvirate that many Indo-European religions have in common. The Rest of the common deities (Tyr, Heimdall, Baldr, Bragi, etc) could be represented as Legend 11: Njordr and Freya are explicitly referred to as lesser than Freyr and legend 11 makes sense in that context. Legend 10 and 9 could be reserved for the sons and daughters of these Gods and various named beings like Volundr and Dainn. Loki might be a crapshoot, I think a case can be made for Legend 12 or legend 11","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T12:02:40-07:00","id":598597,"title":"","content":"Way ahead of you, Ulf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T12:49:32-07:00","id":598628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=598583#post598583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the other Olympians could probably be best represented by Legend 11, still enormously powerful but not at that comparable height.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would definitely require a restructuring of how Legend works, as in First Edition, Gods without Legend 12 can't even pass on a favored Purview.<br /> <br /> That said, Zeus definitely needs the ability to somehow stand above other major deities of his own Pantheon, given that it's explicit in the myths he's supposed to be stronger than all of their strength combined (maybe something extra that comes explicitly from the POSITION of being King of Olympus, so that if he was somehow usurped, his usurper could assume the same power scale?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T13:55:59-07:00","id":598660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=598628#post598628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, Zeus definitely needs the ability to somehow stand above other major deities of his own Pantheon, given that it's explicit in the myths he's supposed to be <b>stronger than all of their strength combined</b> (maybe something extra that comes explicitly from the POSITION of being King of Olympus, so that if he was somehow usurped, his usurper could assume the same power scale?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, I think going that far makes some stories too un-gameable, as it makes it practically impossible to defy Zeus at all. For instance, telling the story of the continued cycle of usurpation from Ouranos to Kronos to Zeus to a player's Scion of Zeus gets ridiculous if he can fend off all the major gods by himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T14:47:43-07:00","id":598691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=598660#post598660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, I think going that far makes some stories too un-gameable, as it makes it practically impossible to defy Zeus at all. For instance, telling the story of the continued cycle of usurpation from Ouranos to Kronos to Zeus to a player's Scion of Zeus gets ridiculous if he can fend off all the major gods by himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, that, like his forefathers, Zeus is FATED to be overthrown by his son. So that's a pretty huge plus sitting in his corner. And Boy-Zeus wasn't a match for Kronos in a toe-to-toe slug it out match. He started the fight off with cleverness and guile, got him some allies, THEN started the Big Fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T14:54:32-07:00","id":598694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=598583#post598583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd prefer to see Legend 12 be reserved for the heavy hitters of the pantheons when applicable. as it stands now, the Legend system is very vague and I think its prime space to represent your overall respect and importance in the pantheon, which would be great for giving a comparison for players who achieved Apotheosis, rather than assigning all the Gods as roughly equal among themselves. Let legend 12 be something that even other gods take serious notice of.<br /> <br /> Zeus, Poseidon and Hades are all able to be represented as Legend 12 among the Theoi. Zeus is the stronger of the three brothers but each of them is a step above the rest of the Dodekatheon. Poseidon has an ongoing threat to establish a coup if Zeus doesn't behave and rule fairly and each was a contender for King of the Gods at one point. Most of the other Olympians could probably be best represented by Legend 11, still enormously powerful but not at that comparable height. Many of the lesser deities could take Legend 10 or 9 (Prime space for Eros and the like, Gods in their own right but obviously lesser than the Olympians and not even comparable to Zeus)<br /> <br /> Odin, Thor and Freyr have to take a similar role among the Aesir, being the three most worshiped and forming a sort of triumvirate that many Indo-European religions have in common. The Rest of the common deities (Tyr, Heimdall, Baldr, Bragi, etc) could be represented as Legend 11: Njordr and Freya are explicitly referred to as lesser than Freyr and legend 11 makes sense in that context. Legend 10 and 9 could be reserved for the sons and daughters of these Gods and various named beings like Volundr and Dainn. Loki might be a crapshoot, I think a case can be made for Legend 12 or legend 11</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the game needs to make it nearly impossible to get to Legend 12. The players should probably top out at Magni/Modi levels. Why on Earth should these newblood nobodies reach the exalted level of the All-Father, since, apparently, he's probably going to be the only one there. I mean, after all, Freyr and Thor still obeyed Odin's orders, right? So he MUST have the power advantage over them. I mean, Thor has huge anger management problems (just ask about any giant; they've all probably lost a cousin to him at some point), If he was equal in power (Legend) with the All-Father and, out of nowhere, swung a fist or a hammer, he would have knocked Odin flat on his narrow ass. And, if they are the same Legend, with Legend working the way it seems like it's going, then Thor, in any contest like this, should win and, yes, Odin is clever, but unless he's MORE clever than Thor is combat capable (which shouldn't be the case if they are of equal power), then Odin should have taken a few headers into the roof made out of shields of the valiant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T15:36:37-07:00","id":598724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=598694#post598694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then the game needs to make it nearly impossible to get to Legend 12. The players should probably top out at Magni/Modi levels. Why on Earth should these newblood nobodies reach the exalted level of the All-Father, since, apparently, he's probably going to be the only one there. I mean, after all, Freyr and Thor still obeyed Odin's orders, right? So he MUST have the power advantage over them. I mean, Thor has huge anger management problems (just ask about any giant; they've all probably lost a cousin to him at some point), If he was equal in power (Legend) with the All-Father and, out of nowhere, swung a fist or a hammer, he would have knocked Odin flat on his narrow ass. And, if they are the same Legend, with Legend working the way it seems like it's going, then Thor, in any contest like this, should win and, yes, Odin is clever, but unless he's MORE clever than Thor is combat capable (which shouldn't be the case if they are of equal power), then Odin should have taken a few headers into the roof made out of shields of the valiant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't that be the place for the pantheons that the players forge for themselves? That way they become the most powerful beings in their own Legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T19:58:35-07:00","id":598955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=598694#post598694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The players should probably top out at Magni/Modi levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>mmmmm... maybe top out as far as sheer xp can get you - but it should be possible to usurp Zeus, sacrifice yourself to yourself on Yggdrasil, steal the True Name of Ra, or otherwise narratively break that barrier and become a heavy hitter yourself by making the story of the Pantheon THE STORY OF YOU.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T23:45:00-07:00","id":599062,"title":"","content":"The complicated part about the existing gods is that most of them didn't have to work their way up from anything. Most of them were born/created/what ever as mind bendingly powerful as they are. In many ways it's kind of unfair on Scions in that they have to work their way up when, mystically, the gods kind of got handed what they are without having to earn it inch by inch by inch for the most part. Obviously there are some that did, or at least that started as lesser deities and advanced to be major players in the field, but whereas Scions have to advance through the ranks gods are already as powerful as they need to be.<br /> <br /> The advantage, as I see it, is that the players have a lot more self determination than gods do. Thor can be as mad at Odin as he wants to be but he's never going to challenge Odin and knock him off the throne. He just doesn't. It's not in his role. A player character god could, though. They're building their own role as they go.<br /> <br /> But yeah, you can't really compare how players come up and fit in to the way most gods did. They have a whole other system, for the most part.<br /> <br /> As for Zeus, I figure when Sonny Boy decides to take on the throne it'll be a lot like Baldr and the mistletoe dart. As all powerful as he is a window of Fate is opened. Something that shouldn't work does and bam, Zeus is on his almighty kiester wondering what just happened. Best part about Fate and legend, the way that it makes exceptions where they're needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T05:51:19-07:00","id":599271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=598691#post598691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except, that, like his forefathers, Zeus is FATED to be overthrown by his son. So that's a pretty huge plus sitting in his corner.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is this from? I know tthe myth of how a son by Metis would overthrow him, but Zeus solved that problem by eating her. There as also the myth that Thetis, then courted by Zeus, would bear a son greater than his father, which is why she was married off to Peleus. Other than that, I don't know of a myth specifically dooming Zeus to his father's and grandfather's fates, although it would be following a pattern.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T06:34:38-07:00","id":599293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Squee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=599062#post599062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The complicated part about the existing gods is that most of them didn't have to work their way up from anything. Most of them were born/created/what ever as mind bendingly powerful as they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Varies. I mean, most of them weren't born to mortals... in Greek Myth, Dionysus is the only top tier God who would have started out at the &quot;Hero&quot; level, and there are stories from the Gigantomachy that could imply his climb to full top tier status. Not to mention stealing Semele out of the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Odin certainly had to rip his metaphysically top tier status out of the universe. He was originally no different in power than Vili and Ve - who he slew Ymir and forged the cosmos with. But he became Allfather by sacrificing himself to himself on the branches of Yggdrasil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T06:59:50-07:00","id":599345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=598694#post598694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then the game needs to make it nearly impossible to get to Legend 12. The players should probably top out at Magni/Modi levels. Why on Earth should these newblood nobodies reach the exalted level of the All-Father, since, apparently, he's probably going to be the only one there. I mean, after all, Freyr and Thor still obeyed Odin's orders, right? So he MUST have the power advantage over them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd agree that getting to Odin or Zeus level power should probably be the culmination of a truly epic and long story, but i wouldn't make it impossible. I'd have to go with the suggestion that it requires narrative impact and in setting justifications rather than XP. In a game in which such things are likely to happen, i might mess with the passage of time as a god and give them hundreds of years or something to work themselves up.<br /> <br /> As for Odin being so dominant, its simply not true. Thor largely does whatever he wants, dresses like a bum and threatens all the other gods around him when he gets pissed. Of the two Existent stories specifically dealing with Freyr, one has him sitting on Odin's throne just because he wanted to and literally refusing to come down. Odin is forced to go to his Father Njordr and Sister Freya just for assistance in the matter, which also fails to sway him.<br /> <br /> The position of Germanic King should not be taken as the latter age absolute monarchy, it was largely a matter of being a warleader and respected enough to sway others to your opinions and was an elected position (although it tended to stay in families). Not to mention that a good chunk of the pantheon is really Odin's children or his children-in-law and they have some cultural expectations to adhere to for it. The pantheon is really an extended family and outright violence among them would be very frowned upon to say the least. Odin is just the combination of the best guy for the job and the beneficiary of some political issues among two branches of the family","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T08:53:23-07:00","id":599484,"title":"","content":"Nearly means nearly. Which is not the same as impossible without the nearly. The ability to go up in Legend should be exponentially or logarithmically more difficult that the scale in demigod with this idea in place. Becoming one of the head of a pantheon is becoming the &quot;ONE&quot; or one of a VERY small group (like the Trimurti) that has overall power. <br /> <br /> Your examples only back up my point with Odin. I didn't say he could kick Thor's ass or that he could out-Freyr Freyr, just that, in the end, he uses his divine abilities in such a way as to maintain his central position in the pantheon. Odin is all about cleverness. He's one of the few examples of what is essentially a trickster figure put in the position in his pantheon that he is. The same archetype usually ends up being the &quot;clever-est minion or buddy&quot; of the guy in charge. So Odin didn't &quot;outshine Freyr&quot;, he did the SMART thing and went and got the people that Freyr would listen to. His Mental stats beat Freyrs Social stats in an indirect contest with some proximate cause. In fact, Odin probably has plans B-X, with 0-x subplans within each one in case the Dad/Sister gambit didn't work. Odin won. He always does. Until he doesn't anymore and isn't in charge. Thor may act like a thug and bully and threaten people when he gets drunk, but Odin is usually able to point him at a giant needing killing or an impossible task needing doing for &quot;fun&quot;. Again, Odin's smarts win. Odin should be Legend 12 and Thor, Freyr, Loki, Freya Legend 11. The larger group of other gods Baldr, Hodr, Heimdallr, Frigga, Njord, etc. should be Legend 10. I doubt Magni, Modi, Vidar and the like should even BE gods. They seem very demi-god-y if that's a level of power and a not a description of parentage. <br /> <br /> A group of gods all being Legend 12 would have to be something like Brahma, Vishnu and Shiva. Or Damballa and Ayida Wedo. Perhaps all four Tezcatlipocas, but probably just Huitzilopochtli and the other 3 at Legend 11. <br /> <br /> I agree it should be one of the highest in PC goals and getting someone to Legend 12 would be the true expression of creating a new pantheon. Also, that there should be some mechanic for losing Legend in an appropriate context instead of just by being willully lazy. Like surviving the end of the world when the other guy doesn't. Like falling victim to the cycle of son vs. father. Like winning in a battle where leadership is explicitly on the line. Like being surpassed because your deal isn't as important as it seemed and some other deities got hooked into a more important fundamental aspect of the universe than, like say the cycle of creation and desctruction vs. being angry, causing storms and killing monsters with a big ass sword. In fact, it could even be by fiat of the god who is in charge of deciding who is in charge and gives them the nod. (Like El giving out palaces. Which Yam had to scare out of him and Ba'al had to essentially trick him out of, with Anat's help, of course).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T09:26:10-07:00","id":599500,"title":"","content":"I think we might be disagreeing on exactly what the legend difference means in terms of raw power. I totally agree that Odin's personality and suite of influence lends itself to playing the political game and functioning as a Germanic King, even If Thor might kick his ass in a white room brawl (Odin is more about leading troops than being personally a badass warrior) or that Freyr might out talk him and have more straight respect and admiration, Odin has the ability to beat them in different ways and the will to do so. Odin is basically the God of the Xanatos Gambit.<br /> <br /> My argument is that this is more a matter of characterization and attribute choices than it is a true measure of raw power. Thor, Freyr and Odin are each the most prominent and powerful examples of the things they each specialize in (Roughly Physical, Social and Mental). That's why all three should be legend 12, they are comparable to each other even if in the situation of &quot;Who gets to lead the pantheon&quot; Odin ends up winning. There is much more of a power differential between say, Freyr and Freya (Freyr is canonically more powerful even though they are basically divine twins and share almost entirely the same suite of powers and influence) or Thor and Tyr (Thor just wins). Putting the Triumvirate at legend 12 establishes them as roughly of equal levels of power and the others as being roughly less powerful overall. (Not to mention opening some very interesting possible stories and internal tension).<br /> <br /> Putting Thor and Freyr at Legend 11 puts them both at roughly the same power level as say Tyr or Heimdall, when both are quite superior and more comparable to Odin in what they actually do do.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T09:27:32-07:00","id":599501,"title":"","content":"...so! Any more questions for me? I'll answer pretty much anything, and the stuff I won't answer, I will at Gen Con.<br /> <br /> Seriously, ask me a straight question at Gen Con, I'll give you a straight answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T09:48:16-07:00","id":599571,"title":"","content":"My problem is that I'm just not sure WHAT has already been asked (aka could be these questions have shown up somewhere earlier already).<br /> <br /> a.) Will there be rules now for worshippers / worshipping and thus worship bringing something effectively? (1.0 had only a few indications and the fate rules to represent this a little bit)<br /> <br /> b.) As I know what gods and creatures one of my players would be after (he is........lets say it so he ALWAYS goes after playing the dragon).Playing a god of some mythical animal was a bit ackward in 1.0 when you tried to take on its form/shape. You used the animal purview for it to &quot;change&quot; form or at least partly change form.Will there be something that feels more natural in 2.0 to be able to portray this?<br /> <br /> c.) Human/mundane sorcerers: Will there be also mechanics for these?<br /> <br /> d.) Some special powers like devouring ones hearth to gain more powerful (fenris) or teh succubus / snow maidens life stealing powers. Will such powers get a more streamlined fealing? (in 1.0 there were a few powers that felt quite similar in terms of fluff and intended rules but had still different rules in how they worked if I remember correctly bakeneko and fenris being examples there). And also will scions also be able to acquire such powers?<br /> <br /> e.) Are there any plans to include rules for ursurping another scions (pre god lvl) or gods power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T09:52:16-07:00","id":599574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=599501#post599501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...so! Any more questions for me? I'll answer pretty much anything, and the stuff I won't answer, I will at Gen Con.<br /> <br /> Seriously, ask me a straight question at Gen Con, I'll give you a straight answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will any of the pantheons be getting a name change like the Theoi?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T09:56:54-07:00","id":599577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=599571#post599571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem is that I'm just not sure WHAT has already been asked (aka could be these questions have shown up somewhere earlier already).</div> </div> </div> </div>The <a href=\"http://www.ttrarchive.com/store/index.php?title=Scion_2E:_What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">What We Know Scion wiki</a> covers what Neall, and Joe before him, have answered so far. Human sorcerers look to be getting coverage in Origins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T10:04:21-07:00","id":599584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=599574#post599574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Will any of the pantheons be getting a name change like the Theoi?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Chinese, Egyptian, Aztec, the Loa (kinda-sorta), to name a few.<br /> <br /> I don't think anyone else is changing their name, and there are other names and groupings within there. The Dodekatheon, for example, is now more properly the twelve greatest gods of Olympus proper (which the book will detail, +1 for Hades, and maybe +another for Persephone, since those two never visit).<br /> <br /> <i>Lots</i> of pantheons have specifically-named groupings of three with mythical significance, or sub-pantheons and groupings contained within them. The Theoi up there contain two Triads, the (Greek names ahead) Olympioi, the Halioi, the Khthonioi, and associated sub-groupings. That's not accounting for allied Titans, where the politics get interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 07-22-2015, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T10:40:32-07:00","id":599617,"title":"","content":"Is the tone going to keep the 1E more light, humourous and cartoonish vibe or is it going to be taking a more dark and realistic mythological feel?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T10:51:05-07:00","id":599630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=599500#post599500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we might be disagreeing on exactly what the legend difference means in terms of raw power. I totally agree that Odin's personality and suite of influence lends itself to playing the political game and functioning as a Germanic King, even If Thor might kick his ass in a white room brawl (Odin is more about leading troops than being personally a badass warrior) or that Freyr might out talk him and have more straight respect and admiration, Odin has the ability to beat them in different ways and the will to do so. Odin is basically the God of the Xanatos Gambit.<br /> <br /> My argument is that this is more a matter of characterization and attribute choices than it is a true measure of raw power. Thor, Freyr and Odin are each the most prominent and powerful examples of the things they each specialize in (Roughly Physical, Social and Mental). That's why all three should be legend 12, they are comparable to each other even if in the situation of &quot;Who gets to lead the pantheon&quot; Odin ends up winning. There is much more of a power differential between say, Freyr and Freya (Freyr is canonically more powerful even though they are basically divine twins and share almost entirely the same suite of powers and influence) or Thor and Tyr (Thor just wins). Putting the Triumvirate at legend 12 establishes them as roughly of equal levels of power and the others as being roughly less powerful overall. (Not to mention opening some very interesting possible stories and internal tension).<br /> <br /> Putting Thor and Freyr at Legend 11 puts them both at roughly the same power level as say Tyr or Heimdall, when both are quite superior and more comparable to Odin in what they actually do do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disagreeing is fine if we are wrastling our way through a thought problem. (Since it's all academic anyways. I doubt it means anything to game of Scion as is or will be). <br /> <br /> I don't disagree with your reasoning on power levels, I think. I guess I think there should be an additional &quot;bump&quot; or &quot;perk&quot; from being the acknowledged leader of a pantheon that other gods of similar powers don't have. Essentially a &quot;card&quot; that they can play that doesn't necessarily trump everyone else, but it a meaningful and powerful expression of their current acknowldeged rulership. So, Thor and Freyr might share the same raw level of power as Odin, but, ya know, Odin is still the King and that does MEAN something when comparing him to Freyr and Thor. He isn't king of the gods at their sufferance and they do (mostly) respect his position and defer to him, except when they don't and then Odin has to figure some way to play that card or use his powers to reinforce his position.<br /> <br /> Usually it would be something one god has. (Most pantheons have some designated singular leader or leadership position.... the Celts definitely have one that transitions between different divinities) Sometimes it would be shared with another god, typically a divine marriage. And sometimes perhaps in a very tight group of deities who effectively share leadership. Then they would exercise the &quot;rulership&quot; collectively and probably individually when dealing with any other god who is not part of their clique. <br /> <br /> Meaning Odin, Thor, and Freyr may be the &quot;Big Three&quot; of the Aesir(Vanir), but Odin is still KING. Whereas Brahma, Vishnu and Shiva are the &quot;Big Three&quot; of the Devas, but they are all equally powerful and share the &quot;idea&quot; of being the ultimate divine power together as the Trimurti. Brahma doesn't rule over Vishnu and Shiva. He does different things than they do and each gives way to the others as is appropriate. And they are definitely in charge of the Devas now, even though Indra was once the King in a more typical rulership role. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T11:26:10-07:00","id":599650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=599617#post599617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the tone going to keep the 1E more light, humourous and cartoonish vibe or is it going to be taking a more dark and realistic mythological feel?</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter, though perfectly cognizant of the fact that there's a myth where Thor needs booze for a party and he and Tyr go harass Hymir, eat all his food, fuck up his whaling trip, and then smash goblets in the guy's face until he agrees to give them his cauldron o' limitless ale.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of myths where the gods act like shitfaced fratboys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T12:49:58-07:00","id":599702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=599650#post599650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The latter, though perfectly cognizant of the fact that there's a myth where Thor needs booze for a party and he and Tyr go harass Hymir, eat all his food, fuck up his whaling trip, and then smash goblets in the guy's face until he agrees to give them his cauldron o' limitless ale.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of myths where the gods act like shitfaced fratboys.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of Norse myths could be described in the style of It's Always Sunny episodes. <br /> <br /> &quot;Loki Bangs a Horse&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T13:01:40-07:00","id":599707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=599501#post599501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...so! Any more questions for me? I'll answer pretty much anything, and the stuff I won't answer, I will at Gen Con.<br /> <br /> Seriously, ask me a straight question at Gen Con, I'll give you a straight answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) You mentioned that there's four different kinds of Scion and that Aphrodite had Scions of all varieties. Would you mind telling what those are?<br /> <br /> 2) How possible is it to create something new? Like, there's a lot of myths about Gods creating new kinds of animals or things like that. For example, Poseidon creating horses or whatever. How doable is that and if so, what general ballpark would you have to be in to pull it off(Hero, Demigod, God)?<br /> <br /> 3) Revisiting an old question from a couple months ago, is War still your favorite Purview or has it been ousted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T13:20:51-07:00","id":599718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=599702#post599702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of Norse myths could be described in the style of It's Always Sunny episodes.<br /> <br /> &quot;Loki Bangs a Horse&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That is unfortunately one of the many myths that lose something in the modern age. While it appears comical to us today the Germanic peoples intended it to be something really dark and forbidden, like a Cthulu-esque &quot;Things that should not be&quot; type of thing.<br /> <br /> Of course, getting drunk and smashing shit up happens from time to time as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T13:55:29-07:00","id":599785,"title":"","content":"How closely are gods' and scion's powers going to mirror mythology?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T14:18:19-07:00","id":599816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nervaqus987</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=599707#post599707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">1) You mentioned that there's four different kinds of Scion and that Aphrodite had Scions of all varieties. Would you mind telling what those are?</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I'll tell you <i>three</i>,</span></span> and the fourth you can guess if you read every supplement in 1e. Ask me at Gen Con and I'll confirm it.<br /> <br /> 1) Be a Scion of god and mortal born, like 100 percent of the people on this planet (though I'm not sure in vitro would work, and I don't think it would, so knock a few decimal points off, I guess). Also works for adopted Scions, but you always retain some part of your parentage, even if Auntie Athena raised you and you really take after her.<br /> 2) Be a Scion created by a god from inanimate materials, brought to life by miraculous means. Enkidu is my go-to example. It takes a decent bit of work on the part of the god, even if you're Ninhursag (a top-tier creation deity), and it takes some association with mortality (thanks, Shamhat), but you're essentially custom-created by the god.<br /> 3) Be transformed in infancy by miraculous means. You must be the descendent of mortal nobility, or possibly have some sort of divine lineage far enough in your line to be suitably transformed. Triptolemus is my go-to example; Adonis would also be suitable, though it raises some questions from his inclusion in the Phoenician pantheon*. But I'm not about to limit character concepts, because clearly the vehicle towards Scionhood is <i>there</i>, so you can take his Greek origin as an acknowledgement of &quot;yeah, that's a way&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) How possible is it to create something new? Like, there's a lot of myths about Gods creating new kinds of animals or things like that. For example, Poseidon creating horses or whatever. How doable is that and if so, what general ballpark would you have to be in to pull it off(Hero, Demigod, God)? </div> </div> </div>Demigod to God. Ixion created the centaurs, both horse and biker variants. He still does, the jerk.<br /> <br /> Creating new subrealms and sub-pantheons is something you can do as a god. New Overworlds, pantheons, creation myths and altering the structure of the World is an appropriate end of a major, years-long epic campaign.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) Revisiting an old question from a couple months ago, is War still your favorite Purview or has it been ousted. </div> </div> </div>Actually, right now it's Fire, because we've been using it as a go-to example of how gods with a similar Purview have radically different expressions; the three characters we've been bandying about are Brigid, Loki and Agni. The first only has it because of syncretized Catholicism, and the metaphorical association with ritual purification and healing. Loki's expression is because his mother is lightning and his father is pine needles, but also because he (maybe) beat up a god with a similar name who was the literal expression of fire, stole that god's mantle, and threatened to burn the whole fucking place down**. Agni's expression of the Purview encompasses fires in virtually all forms metaphorical and literal, including inspiration and also blowing shit up.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*Maybe Adonis was originally Greek and joined the Phoenician pantheon in the Scion setting. I haven't really decided yet either way.<br /> **We also discussed expression through dogs as a joke, but talking Marvel raises a lot of hackles around these parts.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 07-22-2015, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T14:33:52-07:00","id":599832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=599785#post599785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How closely are gods' and scion's powers going to mirror mythology?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of a big question, wouldn't you say? Which mythology? Which gods? Which myths? Which competing myths within the same mythology?<br /> <br /> &quot;As close as we can, while still making new effects permissible and new niches, and making modern methods and uses viable&quot; is about the only answer I can give to an open-ended question like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T14:49:37-07:00","id":599845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=599718#post599718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is unfortunately one of the many myths that lose something in the modern age. While it appears comical to us today the Germanic peoples intended it to be something really dark and forbidden, like a Cthulu-esque &quot;Things that should not be&quot; type of thing.<br /> <br /> Of course, getting drunk and smashing shit up happens from time to time as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or we're just projecting our own cultural preconceptions backwards in time, where they aren't appropriate. Not that I'm saying the Norse were into sex with animals, though they very well COULD have been and it would have had no ick factor to them. They just didn't happen to feel that way.<br /> <br /> Myths were and could be funny. Worship wasn't always dark and deep and serious. Just because it would seem odd to blasphemous for there to be a Book of Jesus's Best Jokes today, doesn't mean that, to the Norse, having a wanker like Loki get screwed as a horse wasn't hellaciously funny and could very well have served as a cautionary tale in a culture where good planning and looking for the right angle was definitely considered a virtue. Loki, being Loki, thought he was so damn clever with the &quot;change into a mare&quot; plan that he didn't think ahead to natural conclusion of it AFTER providing the distraction. Moral of the story: Think your plans through before jumping off half-cocked.<br /> <br /> Additionally, our perception of self-identity may not square with those of other peoples. (It certainly doesn't from culture to culture in the modern world.) So, to us Loki is always a giant/god guy who happens to be in the shape of a horse, but he's still Loki-the-giant/god-guy. To other peoples (LOTS of other peoples) when Loki is a mare, he IS a mare. The identity &quot;Loki&quot; is more mutable than in our conceptions If Loki is a mare, doing things female horse would do isn't unnatural at all.<br /> <br /> What it certainly was not was the existential despair in the face of an uncaring universe in which humanity is less than a little part that can't even conceive of its own smallness and unimportance and the only sane reaction to true understanding is to go insane. That's Cthulhu-esque. Things aren't icky because fungus squicks people out. They're icky because we can't get outside our little heads to understand it so we viscerally HAVE to react against it so we reduce it to something we fear and hate and loathe because that's the closest thing that mere human brains can come to as a rational response. That doesn't really resonant with the Loki-as-a-mare story very much at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T15:39:11-07:00","id":599872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or we're just projecting our own cultural preconceptions backwards in time, where they aren't appropriate. Not that I'm saying the Norse were into sex with animals, though they very well COULD have been and it would have had no ick factor to them. They just didn't happen to feel that way. </div> </div> </div>I'm not including modern day values, but rather their own. The Norse and, to a lesser degree wider Germanic culture has been the he subject of extensive academic work over the years, probably the best having been the work of Wilhelm Gronbech, its not the same as say, the Gauls, we can reliably tell what they thought on <i>most</i> topics, especially considering that most of modern western society is a direct descendant of that culture. For instance, Sex with animals was considered horrendous that was routinely used as &quot;Fighting words&quot; against women. It was also considered a stain on his moral character, as the other gods insult him for it in Lokasenna.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Additionally, our perception of self-identity may not square with those of other peoples. (It certainly doesn't from culture to culture in the modern world.) So, to us Loki is always a giant/god guy who happens to be in the shape of a horse, but he's still Loki-the-giant/god-guy. To other peoples (LOTS of other peoples) when Loki is a mare, he IS a mare. The identity &quot;Loki&quot; is more mutable than in our conceptions If Loki is a mare, doing things female horse would do isn't unnatural at all. </div> </div> </div>The Norse had a soul system of 5 parts. The shape of a man (and god) was governed by the Hugr, which was different from the Munr which is closest to our modern conception of a mans soul (that is, a personality separate from the body, ones self). If loki changed shape, then he would have still been notably Loki as his other souls were totally unaffected. Its notable that he is insulted for this later, showing that he was expected to maintain the same expectations of behavior whatever his form. Though you are right, many aspects of the culture are different, they had a more &quot;Eastern&quot; concept of the self that was primarily built into a group such as a family or clan rather than strictly an individual.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> HAVE to react against it so we reduce it to something we fear and hate and loathe because that's the closest thing that mere human brains can come to as a rational response. </div> </div> </div>Thats exactly what it was. The Norse concept of Ergi and Hamingja was such that these things were literally <i>unthinkable</i> to good and noble men and that the natural repulsion to it was because ones soul pulled you into correct behavior. the implication is that Loki does such things as a matter of course and sees nothing wrong with it because he is an alien other, chaotic and unnatural and unlike Men and Gods alike. Its Cthulu-esqe because it conjures the image of the unspeakable, unnatural terror from beyond, something that violates the laws of reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T16:39:37-07:00","id":599969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=599832#post599832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kind of a big question, wouldn't you say? Which mythology? Which gods? Which myths? Which competing myths within the same mythology?<br /> <br /> &quot;As close as we can, while still making new effects permissible and new niches, and making modern methods and uses viable&quot; is about the only answer I can give to an open-ended question like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. As long as the new edition allows the Greek gods their trademark shapeshifting shenanigans, and the Devas can do their weird cosmic tricks I'll be happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T17:11:39-07:00","id":599994,"title":"","content":"Just some questions:<br /> <br /> Was Loki being a mare used against him in the flytting? He definitely had no issue using every event in Norse mythology against them. Flytting are two way streets, insult contests. (To which the Aesir were pretty poor losers since they were supposed to offer Loki a drink for beating them).<br /> <br /> Was screwing animals cited as a specific offense in legal codes? Germanic and Norse people were ridiculously litigious. If they had a problem with it, they would have a law against it, a prescribed punishment and a fee you could pay to get out of it.<br /> <br /> I don't know the answers<br /> <br /> The Norse weren't as self-effacing and face based as your are portraying them. Being a canny individualist who could take advantage of a situation was very well-thought of. And it wasn't to the just make one's family more prestigious. Self-aggrandizement and individual initiative was prized. Coming from a bilateral non-lineage kinship based on difficult acquisition of resources (common to Inuit and modern Western Culture), it is common to see cultures with strong lineage and clan collectivization mechanisms as being face based, but, they . ertainly don't have to be. People may be accountable to family, but family is not their measure. Lots of sagas about setting out and doing better on your own for yourself. And you get stories about that. Which means it's considered laudable. Also, even having bragging and flytting means you aren't looking at a culture where honor is specifically tied to a lineage based self-identity.<br /> <br /> And, no, it's still not Cthulhu-esque. It's obviously not unthinkable if people think badly of it. It's ENTIRELY thinkable. We can think about cannibalism and consider it awful Same with slavery and incest. People who do it are bad people. If you think people who do it are bad people, you've thought about it. None of that is Cthulhu-esque. It's not like the Norse would see said act and their minds would not be able to process it. It wouldn't be like suddenly there was a 5th lateral direction or an explosion of a new color that no one had ever seen before or both man and horse turned inside out, conjoin and then sprouted pustule/eyes and tentacles or simply that seeing such a thing would reveal to them that the world was so much less than they thought it was and they were less than nothing with consciousness just a delusion of dancing motes in the eyes of, not the unknown, but the unknowable. They would see it and have a very specific set of thoughts, like, say, &quot;Better kill that guy for doing something that is just wrong.&quot;<br /> <br /> Anyways, want to take this to separate thread, since this isn't really &quot;Ask(ing) Neal&quot; anything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T18:06:52-07:00","id":600040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=599969#post599969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair enough. As long as the new edition allows the Greek gods their trademark shapeshifting shenanigans</div> </div> </div> </div>That may or may not be their Pantheon-specific Purview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T19:50:05-07:00","id":600119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=600040#post600040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That may or may not be their Pantheon-specific Purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>That raises the odd question of why Loki has the Greek Pantheon Purview...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T19:51:58-07:00","id":600122,"title":"","content":"Does each character still have 4 virtues?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T20:16:25-07:00","id":600142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=600119#post600119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That raises the odd question of why Loki has the Greek Pantheon Purview...</div> </div> </div> </div>Loki can shapeshift, but always remains Loki. Man, woman, horse, they are all Loki. <br /> <br /> Lots of pantheons have shapeshifting powers, but the Theoi do it most often, and the best. Still, the PSPs are evolving in mechanical discussions, so this may not be the only element of what they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T20:17:12-07:00","id":600144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=600122#post600122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does each character still have 4 virtues?</div> </div> </div> </div>They still have Virtues, but we're looking at the best number.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T21:49:57-07:00","id":600174,"title":"","content":"Do the Titans not have objectively evil for their own sake &quot;virtues&quot; this time around?<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm fine with &quot;alien &amp; antithetical to human civilization&quot; virtues maybe (mine were Fecundity - creative capacity, Rapacity - destructive capacity, Submission - union with the greater Primordial, Dominance - command over oneself and others within that framework); but &quot;I'm evil for its own sake&quot; Virtues were really disappointing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T00:11:09-07:00","id":600249,"title":"","content":"Coming from New World of Darkness, what exactly <i>is </i>a Virtue in the system?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T00:35:46-07:00","id":600270,"title":"","content":"How do the gods handle alliance with Titans (aside from 'very carefully')? Are there any pantheons that haven't made such alliances?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":". 07-23-2015, 03:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T06:04:33-07:00","id":600473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=600249#post600249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coming from New World of Darkness, what exactly <i>is </i>a Virtue in the system?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They're stats based off Exalted (though Exalted 3E is moving away from making them so ingrained) that you can channel (add dice) by acting in certain ways, but have to resist (fail of roll of one) or suppress (spend a willpower point) to act against. Certain circumstances resulted in Virtues overload as the character takes the behavior to a destructive extreme (ala Tragic Flaws of Epic Myth). In 1E Scion, different Pantheons had different sets of Virtues to reflect their differing cultural outlooks. Like the Aesir had &quot;Courage, Endurance, Expression, and Loyalty&quot; while the Dodekatheon had &quot;Expresssion, Intellect, Valor, and Vengeance&quot;. <br /> <br /> Given the described ethos of those Pantheons - the communal Aesir should really have upheld Valor (bravery in defense of others, and honorable combat) and the almost-Randian-individualist Arete-obsessed, Hubris-prone Dodekatheon should have upheld Courage (proving oneself against the biggest deadliest foe possible).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T06:55:39-07:00","id":600542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the Titans not have objectively evil for their own sake &quot;virtues&quot; this time around?<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm fine with &quot;alien &amp; antithetical to human civilization&quot; virtues maybe (mine were Fecundity - creative capacity, Rapacity - destructive capacity, Submission - union with the greater Primordial, Dominance - command over oneself and others within that framework); but &quot;I'm evil for its own sake&quot; Virtues were really disappointing.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're far more alien and antithetical this time around (and I might well steal some of yours and add it to our master list, so thanks for those). They are not necessarily evil for evil's sake, but all titans are difficult to get along with, and tend to &quot;corrupt&quot;, in that they reformat the areas around them according to their essence. Some have adopted a few of the pantheon Virtues, rendering them more &quot;god-like&quot; than many Titans - enough to breed their own godly Scions. The distinction is political as much as it is metaphysical, inasmuch as they're largely the same thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=600270#post600270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do the gods handle alliance with Titans</div> </div> </div> </div>Very caref-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (aside from 'very carefully')? Are there any pantheons that haven't made such alliances? </div> </div> </div>Several, but of the core 10? The Chinese pantheon hates Hundun something fierce.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T09:44:19-07:00","id":600641,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing Titan-Scions find themselves in an &quot;interesting&quot; position when it comes to divine politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T10:39:43-07:00","id":600714,"title":"","content":"How would a Scion that gets afflicted with lycanthropy grow to use it as part of their Legend, would it just be animal purview of something different?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T11:01:22-07:00","id":600732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=600714#post600714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would a Scion that gets afflicted with lycanthropy grow to use it as part of their Legend, would it just be animal purview of something different?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eventually, it might get subsumed into the Animal Purview, but it'd be something afflicting the Scion (a Path, most likely) that just makes their life more interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T12:52:35-07:00","id":600856,"title":"","content":"How about titans that aren't 'alien and antithetical' but are still clearly titans. I'm thinking of Helios, Eos, Mnemosyne? They were titans that were trusted by the <br /> Theoi and interacted with them daily.<br /> <br /> Also where would you place people like Iris or the children of Styx on this scale of alien virtues and outlooks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T13:19:52-07:00","id":600916,"title":"","content":"Okay, what is a path?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T13:24:57-07:00","id":600921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=600856#post600856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about titans that aren't 'alien and antithetical' but are still clearly titans. I'm thinking of Helios, Eos, Mnemosyne? They were titans that were trusted by the Theoi and interacted with them daily.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>me</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some have adopted a few of the pantheon Virtues, rendering them more &quot;god-like&quot; than many Titans - enough to breed their own godly Scions. The distinction is political as much as it is metaphysical, inasmuch as they're largely the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also where would you place people like Iris or the children of Styx on this scale of alien virtues and outlooks? </div> </div> </div>Arke probably adopted Titanic Virtues, but Iris didn't, joining her sister out of Fatebinding or love or <i>amor fati</i>.<br /> <br /> Styx would be a goddess, I imagine. For the Greeks, the distinction is far more political. For other pantheons, the distinction is more metaphysical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T14:28:27-07:00","id":600972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=600040#post600040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That may or may not be their Pantheon-specific Purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh neat. I've been bouncing ideas around in my head for a Scion of Zeus who got the Shapeshifter stuff as opposed to the more usual Thunder and Lighting and/or Herakles Super Strength.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T16:33:54-07:00","id":601039,"title":"","content":"So Artemis forswearing the touch of man and then running off with nymphs.... She's only a &quot;virgin&quot; under a patriarchal Ancient Greek phallus-centric definition of sex and virginity, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T17:37:36-07:00","id":601168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=601039#post601039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Artemis forswearing the touch of man and then running off with nymphs.... She's only a &quot;virgin&quot; under a patriarchal Ancient Greek phallus-centric definition of sex and virginity, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>At least in Scion 1e, that was pretty much explicitly stated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T17:47:09-07:00","id":601171,"title":"