ts":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T18:31:00-07:00","id":601218,"title":"","content":"Can you please tell some more about the sorcerers who want to steal power from the gods?<br /> is still mechanically possibloe for a scion to become poerful enough to become a new addition in n pantheon?<br /> What atticus o'sullivan would think of thid game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 07-23-2015, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T20:24:07-07:00","id":601346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=601209#post601209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">gals being pals</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You know... given the origin of that meme was specifically how the tabloids described really invasive photos of a certain not-out celebrity and her roommate... that's kind of the perfect way to retell the Actaeon myth in the modern setting!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T23:47:33-07:00","id":601441,"title":"","content":"Any big things you can share about the Aztec pantheon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T02:34:27-07:00","id":601541,"title":"","content":"Judging from the myths I've read, I would call Artemis asexual. I think she just loathes sex. She becomes enraged at one of her nymphs who becomes pregnant, and one man she does favor, Hippolytus, has no interest in romance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/140-samcwic","name":"samcwic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T06:37:40-07:00","id":601757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=601218#post601218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you please tell some more about the sorcerers who want to steal power from the gods?<br /> What atticus o'sullivan would think of thid game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Baba Yaga isn't a goddess in <b>Scion 2e</b>. Her riders, though, can go toe-to-toe with demigods.<br /> <br /> Atticus is a viable character concept, although he's probably going to be a bit lower-powered than the books portray; the name of the game is <b>Scion</b>, not <b>Iron Druid</b>. Still, I adored the Iron Druid books, so take that for what you will.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any big things you can share about the Aztec pantheon?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Teotl are actually the Aztec pantheon this edition; the Inca and Mayan pantheons are slated for inclusion in later books, though they'll be mentioned (and the Aztecs and Maya share Quetzacoatl/Kukulkan). There are confederate pantheons in the game, but those aren't them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T06:44:45-07:00","id":601762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>samcwic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=601541#post601541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Judging from the myths I've read, I would call Artemis asexual. I think she just loathes sex. She becomes enraged at one of her nymphs who becomes pregnant, and one man she does favor, Hippolytus, has no interest in romance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Camilla, Atalanta; these are Scions of Artemis.<br /> <br /> I'm unsure of what to do with Artemis' sexuality (she does strike me in a majority of myths as largely asexual, but then there's the nymphs and Callisto), but I can promise you that she doesn't have any interest in men beyond a slight filial affection, and certainly not in being a dominatrix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T09:06:11-07:00","id":601903,"title":"","content":"What are the Chinese Pantheon called?<br /> Do the Chinese Pantheon have a standard language, or do they use all the Chinese languages?<br /> What's their Pantheon Specific Purview?<br /> Can you still play a 'child of the Pantheon', who has a caseworker instead of an identified parent?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T09:19:16-07:00","id":601912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=601903#post601903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the Chinese Pantheon called?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Shen. The Celestial Bureaucracy is a thing, but not the name of the pantheon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do the Chinese Pantheon have a standard language, or do they use all the Chinese languages? </div> </div> </div>Old Chinese, I'd imagine, though the proper answer is &quot;both&quot;. Many Scions have the ability to communicate regardless of language.<br /> <br /> While there's a lot of games I consider it fascinating to play around with language use and different dialects - Dark Ages Vampire, for one - and there's an element of linguistics in there borrowed from Percy Jackson (Pre-Visitation Scions within a pantheon are &quot;hardwired&quot; to pick up on the pantheon's distinct language, and rapidly become omnilingual), I generally don't consider quibbling over spoken communication to be a fruitful avenue of pathos in a game that's inherently cross-cultural. That said, the idea that the Shen debate which variety of Chinese to speak amongst themselves and their followers is probably correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What's their Pantheon Specific Purview? </div> </div> </div>It currently has a lot to do with order and fortune.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you still play a 'child of the Pantheon', who has a caseworker instead of an identified parent? </div> </div> </div>It doesn't precisely fit with how the four types of Scions operate, though there might be a generic template we can attribute to a Scion's parentage, and they take after their &quot;adopted&quot; parent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 07-24-2015, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T10:12:27-07:00","id":601954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>samcwic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=601541#post601541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Judging from the myths I've read, I would call Artemis asexual. I think she just loathes sex. She becomes enraged at one of her nymphs who becomes pregnant, and one man she does favor, Hippolytus, has no interest in romance.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I read Athena - but those examples with Artemis just show her attitude toward sex with men. Remember the Ancient Greeks, like most patriarchal cultures, did not conceive of &quot;lesbian sex&quot; as sex - sex and the loss of virginity by definition required penetration with a penis.<br /> <br /> I need a whole scene of a bisexual character arguing to Artemis that &quot;Gold Star&quot; lesbian elitism is just repackaged Right Wing purity myth - the idea that sex with a man can ruin a woman's nature, is a fundamentally phallus-centric worldview.<br /> <br /> If this character is a Scion it would help to have the favor of Aphrodite and Dionysus with them at the time, or they're likely to be turned into a prey animal and hunted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-24-2015, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T10:23:55-07:00","id":601961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=601757#post601757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(and the Aztecs and Maya share Quetzacoatl/Kukulkan).</div> </div> </div> </div>Do the Deva and the Shen share Yama/Yanluo?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T12:12:26-07:00","id":602069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=601961#post601961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the Deva and the Shen share Yama/Yanluo?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> The Deva, Shen, and Kami all share Yama, though he'll only be written up once for space concerns and the Deva pantheon is sort of primary. For a redeemed god of death who got his ass kicked, he's shockingly popular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T12:35:09-07:00","id":602091,"title":"","content":"What determines the primary pantheon of gods that are in multiple ones","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[