ns":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T16:35:23-07:00","id":616879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=616782#post616782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well the movies haven't - but the comics have, yes.<br /> <br /> *insert angry rant about the new straight-washed Hercules comics*</div> </div> </div> </div>My 2 cents on this: While I'm no fan of changing an established character to pander to ANY group, Herc being Bi didn't upset me in the least, it fit with his Legend/history. Retconing that is a dumb move.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T17:53:39-07:00","id":616982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=616879#post616879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My 2 cents on this: While I'm no fan of changing an established character to pander to ANY group, Herc being Bi didn't upset me in the least, it fit with his Legend/history. Retconing that is a dumb move.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As to &quot;changing established characters to pander&quot; - I just see it as correcting for the political bias toward white &amp; straight that was in play when they were created. If the &quot;now&quot; of the stories is endlessly being retconned into the present, with the characters background being adjusted all the time to fit that - I don't see why the white straight predominance that reflects the past era of their creation should ever be considered sacrosanct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T20:18:07-07:00","id":617100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=605402#post605402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe the answer is 'while dual wielding ten foot poles'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm far more concerned about the difficulty of walking carefully with the Loa and the Deva than freely playing around with the predominant religious cultural framework we're raised within in the West (regardless of our personal faiths).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T21:11:56-07:00","id":618427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=616982#post616982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As to &quot;changing established characters to pander&quot; - I just see it as correcting for the political bias toward white &amp; straight that was in play when they were created. If the &quot;now&quot; of the stories is endlessly being retconned into the present, with the characters background being adjusted all the time to fit that - I don't see why the white straight predominance that reflects the past era of their creation should ever be considered sacrosanct.</div> </div> </div> </div> It also has to make sense. I have no issue with SOME of the race changes that have happened in movies, for example, but (and I say this as a man of multiple ethnicity) black Hiemdall (SP?) bothers me. A character with few if any previous romantic interests demonstrates a new orientation? Fine. Breaking up an iconic relationship (Peter/MJ, Reed/Sue, Bruce/Selina) in the name of &quot;equality&quot;? Not so much. If you are wondering why the &quot;&quot; around equality, let me point out that more often than not, political movements <u>start off</u> wanting to be equal, but slowly move toward wanting to be <u>dominant</u>. Look at the Black Panthers. It's human nature to want to be the one in charge. LGBTQ individuals make up less than 1% of the population. So would Superheroes/Villains. It seems improbable that there would be more than 1 or 2 LGBTQ individuals per 1000 super people. I can name at least half a dozen in DC comics without breaking a sweat. (Admittedly, not all of them are high profile) &lt;/end rant&gt;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T22:23:58-07:00","id":618507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=618427#post618427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">black Hiemdall (SP?) bothers me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? They're aliens, not Nordic people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A character with few if any previous romantic interests demonstrates a new orientation? Fine. Breaking up an iconic relationship (Peter/MJ, Reed/Sue, Bruce/Selina) in the name of &quot;equality&quot;? Not so much. </div> </div> </div>When has any of this ever happened? Peter and MJ were broken up because hack writers ran out of story ideas with a married couple. Bruce and Selina have never had a stable relationship and Bruce has always had other love interests - Selina having the same doesn't change anything other than treating her as much as a fleshed out character as Bruce.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you are wondering why the &quot;&quot; around equality, let me point out that more often than not, political movements <u>start off</u> wanting to be equal, but slowly move toward wanting to be <u>dominant</u>. Look at the Black Panthers. </div> </div> </div>A black self defense organization formed to combat systemic racial brutality and create self-sufficency in the black community, in contrast with the integrationist cause of Southern black leadership? The guys who haven't existed in decades because of an illegal campaign to destroy and discredit them (COINTELPRO) by the FBI? What about them? What white institutions did they try and &quot;dominate&quot;?<br /> <br /> I mean I suppose there was the typical revolutionary socialist anti-US-government rhetoric you'd expect from a militant group in the 60s and 70s - but nothing out of the ordinary there or potentially actually threatening to white political establishment.<br /> <br /> We're talking about a group who's most notable accomplishments were things like creating their own volunteer ambulance service because many cities' ambulances wouldn't come into black neighborhoods. But they also advocated armed self-defense against institutional white violence, instead of passive nonviolence against violence, so they became a government target. But the equivalency to the Klan that gets thrown around so often (not saying you did so) is insane when you consider not a single &quot;lynching&quot; of anyone for their race can be lain at the Black Panthers' feet. There are some police officers who were killed in disputed circumstances, but even if the worst versions of those events are correct, it's a specific individual being a violent drunk rather than a systemic reign of terror ala the Klan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> LGBTQ individuals make up less than 1% of the population. </div> </div> </div>Bullshit. It's around 4 counting only self-identifying labels people use (which before you dismiss 3% as an insignificant difference - that's four times as many people than you were claiming - a difference of 9 million people in the US alone). If you base your count on sexual behavior rather than identifying labels, the number SKYROCKETS (how high is heavily debated).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It seems improbable that there would be more than 1 or 2 LGBTQ individuals per 1000 super people. I can name at least half a dozen in DC comics without breaking a sweat. (Admittedly, not all of them are high profile) &lt;/end rant&gt; </div> </div> </div>Why did you just change from 1% to .1%? Also supers being supers, they're going to have a lower percentage of &quot;being in the closet&quot; than the general public - as you can see makes a difference with the &quot;disproportionately high&quot; percentage of LGBT people in communities where it's relatively accepted and &quot;disproportionately low&quot; percentages where it isn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-07-2015, 02:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T23:28:42-07:00","id":618592,"title":"","content":"anyways to get it back to scion. Has it been asked how scions would interact with the religions that deal with their gods and goddesses? be it hinduism, hellenismos, asatru, shinto and so on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T04:42:43-07:00","id":618683,"title":"","content":"What happens to the setting when (not if...) a glowing Scion of Ra clad in raiments of gold and turquoise rides their chariot of fire shooting arrows of desire from their bow of burning gold at rampaging ice giants down the Thames?<br /> <br /> Do we then get the world going crazy trying to justify it, people converting as believers, wide spread panic and confusion etc.? Or is there some form of supernatural forgetfulness thing like the Sleeper curse in Mage and so on? Is there some attempt at a 'Masquerade' or are the pantheons fairly laissez faire with the whole thing only worried about Fatebinding rather than letting people know about them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T05:21:00-07:00","id":618693,"title":"","content":"I don't want to derail this thread, so I'll just say that the angriest voices in a crowd are often the loudest, and leave it at that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T06:38:00-07:00","id":618764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=618592#post618592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">anyways to get it back to scion. Has it been asked how scions would interact with the religions that deal with their gods and goddesses? be it hinduism, hellenismos, asatru, shinto and so on?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cult mechanics will be present within the game, and Scions will likely integrate with those religions. <i>It's worth noting</i>, and worth <i>stressing</i>, that those religions are not the same as the real-world living religions, but fictional portrayals within the <b>Scion</b> gameline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens to the setting when (not if...) a glowing Scion of Ra clad in raiments of gold and turquoise rides their chariot of fire shooting arrows of desire from their bow of burning gold at rampaging ice giants down the Thames?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no Sleeper Curse or Paradox. There's no Masquerade. People who literally saw the event will probably question their beliefs, people who saw it on TV might accept or dismiss it, and Fatebinding hits you like a hammer. Hope it was worth it. Your personal cult would probably get a boost, though.<br /> <br /> <b>Scion</b> is a World of Modern Myth. If you try to pull the scientifically-verifiable miracles on international TV, you'll <i>still</i> have people denying it, or - more likely - increasing their fervent worship to their own gods. While this can be good, it's really just rocked the boat quite a bit, and every god will think you're an asshole (as opposed to something necessary, like putting down a rampaging ice giant).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T07:35:44-07:00","id":618855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=616782#post616782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well the movies haven't - but the comics have, yes.<br /> <br /> *insert angry rant about the new straight-washed Hercules comics*</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll always have that glorious X-treme X-Men run with Hercules x Wolverine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T07:49:14-07:00","id":618864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=616824#post616824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine they can't hate it half as much as... well Persephone... hates how Hollywood treats Hades (Hades does his big stoic &quot;not caring about how anyone thinks of him performance).<br /> <br /> The real question is what pisses of Hera worse: her vilification (Hercules the Legendary Journeys) or being presented as Herc's loving mother (Disney's Hercules).</div> </div> </div> </div>Would Persephone be that concerned about Hades' bad image? After all she at least is treated sympatethically, and Hades <b>did</b> kidnap her, then tricked her into being bound to the Underworld. Mythology doesn't describe them as a particularly happy couple (although not a particularly unhappy one either), and even her jealousy at Hades' one dalliance with a nymph could e more a matter of pride, than hurt feelings, especially in light of her own affair with Adonis.<br /> ...Anybody else think the Greek gods should be on E! ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T10:45:58-07:00","id":619153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=618864#post618864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would Persephone be that concerned about Hades' bad image? After all she at least is treated sympatethically, and Hades <b>did</b> kidnap her</div> </div> </div> </div>The Orphic hymns portray her as deeply loving him and actually pleeding with her mother to stay - so it's a question of which source you want to listen to on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T11:39:52-07:00","id":619198,"title":"","content":"Why is Hera still married to Zeus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T11:40:21-07:00","id":619199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=618864#post618864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anybody else think the Greek gods should be on E! ?</div> </div> </div> </div>More like Jerry Springer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T11:54:14-07:00","id":619214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=619198#post619198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is Hera still married to Zeus?</div> </div> </div> </div>The goddess of marriage can't exactly be divorced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T13:01:50-07:00","id":619295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=619214#post619214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The goddess of marriage can't exactly be divorced.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is also the fact that at the end of the day, Zeus and Hera do love each other despite his sleeping around and her wrath. Within Hellenismos there is the festival of Theogamia; a day to celebrate the marriage between Zeus and Hera, as well as love and marriage in general.<br /> <br /> I do have a slight issue of the whole flanderization that particularly the greek gods and goddesses get; Zeus and Hera are the more noticable examples of it. While Zeus does sleep around, he is more than that. After all he is the god of law, authority, order, civilization, the weather, among many many other things. While Hera is the Goddess of Marriage, she was also the patron of the city of Argo, not surprising that the Argonauts stories have her as helping them. Along with her husband Zeus, she is associated with air and the sky as well as as demonstrated by this Orphic hymn. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;O royal Hera, of majestic mien, aerial-formed, divine, Zeus' blessed queen, throned in the bosom of cerulean air, the race of mortals is thy constant care. The cooling gales they power alone inspires, which nourish life, which every life desires. Mother of showers and winds, from thee alone, producing all things, mortal life is known: all natures share thy temperament divine, and universal sway alone is thine, with sounding blasts of wind, the swelling sea and rolling rivers roar when shook by thee. Come, blessed Goddess, famed almighty queen, with aspect kind, rejoicing and serene.&quot; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T13:23:09-07:00","id":619336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=619214#post619214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The goddess of marriage can't exactly be divorced.</div> </div> </div> </div> Interesting idea for a plot though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T14:18:02-07:00","id":619406,"title":"","content":"Reminds me of my idea of surprising modern American Scions by revealing that Hera is totally 100% for same-sex marriage recognition, while Dionysus is against it - because it's the strengthening of her domain and the weakening of his via assimilation of what was once &quot;Other&quot; as mainstream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T18:29:11-07:00","id":619616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=619406#post619406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reminds me of my idea of surprising modern American Scions by revealing that Hera is totally 100% for same-sex marriage recognition, while Dionysus is against it - because it's the strengthening of her domain and the weakening of his via assimilation of what was once &quot;Other&quot; as mainstream.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I just passed this on to my housemate (who I run a solo game for) and his jaw hit the floor. I can only imagine what your players must have looked like, glamourweaver <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T00:53:10-07:00","id":619864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=618764#post618764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cult mechanics will be present within the game, and Scions will likely integrate with those religions. <i>It's worth noting</i>, and worth <i>stressing</i>, that those religions are not the same as the real-world living religions, but fictional portrayals within the <b>Scion</b> gameline.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There's no Sleeper Curse or Paradox. There's no Masquerade. People who literally saw the event will probably question their beliefs, people who saw it on TV might accept or dismiss it, and Fatebinding hits you like a hammer. Hope it was worth it. Your personal cult would probably get a boost, though.<br /> <br /> <b>Scion</b> is a World of Modern Myth. If you try to pull the scientifically-verifiable miracles on international TV, you'll <i>still</i> have people denying it, or - more likely - increasing their fervent worship to their own gods. While this can be good, it's really just rocked the boat quite a bit, and every god will think you're an asshole (as opposed to something necessary, like putting down a rampaging ice giant).</div> </div> </div> </div>There was mention at some point of 'alternate' settings, will there be any chance of one of those looking at a world in which belief in the Pantheons is returning enmasse or, even more fun, has been consumed by the celebrity media? You know, articles in fashion magazines with titles like 'Konstantin reveals all: top 10 beauty tips from a Scion of Aphrodite!' or rather than doctrine/scripture/etc. you get 'Hera's top 10 tips for a healthy marriage!'<br /> <br /> I am...easily amused apparently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T08:15:10-07:00","id":620046,"title":"","content":"that makes me wonder, what is the default setting of scion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T18:57:43-07:00","id":620788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=605256#post605256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the mention of saints (on the one hand) and the potentially syncretic nature of the West African Pantheon(s), I find myself wanting to know: how will <b>Scion</b> address the Abrahamic faiths?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=605512#post605512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very caref-</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=605256#post605256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(And please don't say \u201cvery carefully\u201d; I\u2019m taking that as a given.)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=605512#post605512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know, but it's worth reiterating. Still, I'll talk more about this at Gen Con, so hold your horses for a few days.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just noting that we're a few days past Gen Con. For anyone who attended, what was said? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=605512#post605512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will note, though, that a primary source of inspiration for the new edition is <i>The Wicked + The Divine</i>, where the scientifically- and historically-verified Pantheon exists alongside Abrahamic faiths (to which monotheism, evolving from henotheism as a concept, came somewhat late) with no problem. Another source of inspiration is the NBC series <i>Kings</i>; yet another is Ishmael Reed's <i>Mumbo Jumbo</i>, whose monotheist Wallflower Order is very similar to the Order of the Divine Glory, except rather cooler. Make of that what you will for the moment, but I will say that I don't intend to include the Order of the Divine Glory in its past incarnation at the moment, and if I do, it'll be more like the Templars of Assassin's Creed than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Noted. As well:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=617100#post617100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm far more concerned about the difficulty of walking carefully with the Loa and the Deva than freely playing around with the predominant religious cultural framework we're raised within in the West (regardless of our personal faiths).</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Part of my question had to do with how <b>Scion</b> will be addressing followers of Abrahamic faiths; but another significant factor I\u2019m curious about is if and/or how matters pertaining to Abrahamic faith will factor into the 2e take on the Orisha/Loa, given the fact that Voudoun syncretized African faiths with the likes of Catholicism and the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T22:56:11-07:00","id":620931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=619864#post619864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There was mention at some point of 'alternate' settings, will there be any chance of one of those looking at a world in which belief in the Pantheons is returning enmasse or, even more fun, has been consumed by the celebrity media? You know, articles in fashion magazines with titles like 'Konstantin reveals all: top 10 beauty tips from a Scion of Aphrodite!' or rather than doctrine/scripture/etc. you get 'Hera's top 10 tips for a healthy marriage!'<br /> <br /> I am...easily amused apparently.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would love to see this too, though it definitely only works as a side setting. I'm not saying there is anything wrong with it, just if you introduce this as a possibility in the core setting it's the sort of concept that consumes a gameline by virtue of it's strong and self fulfilling nature. Fatebinding almost seems to exist purely to stop this sort of game happening, the nature of most Scions isn't necessarily subtle, for many of them without some pretty strong disincentives against doing so the endgame for them would pretty much be them becoming public superheroes...or maybe the stars of Jersey Shore Scion Edition...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T23:20:47-07:00","id":620935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=619153#post619153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Orphic hymns portray her as deeply loving him and actually pleeding with her mother to stay - so it's a question of which source you want to listen to on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The <a href=\"http://olympiansrule.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Olympians</a> graphic novels by George O'Connor have a neat take on this idea, he tells the stories pretty close to the historical &quot;facts&quot;, but he will add a layer of subtext beneath that myth to give the players a bit more personality. If I remember correctly, in his telling of the legend of Persephone she actually plays along with a plan put in motion by Hermes on the other God's behalf to let her stay with Hades for part of the year. When they ask if she has eaten any of the dead's food Persephone tells a little fib and says she ate a pomegranate seed so &quot;oops I guess I have to stay&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T07:17:47-07:00","id":621225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=619295#post619295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is also the fact that at the end of the day, Zeus and Hera do love each other despite his sleeping around and her wrath. Within Hellenismos there is the festival of Theogamia; a day to celebrate the marriage between Zeus and Hera, as well as love and marriage in general.<br /> <br /> I do have a slight issue of the whole flanderization that particularly the greek gods and goddesses get; Zeus and Hera are the more noticable examples of it. While Zeus does sleep around, he is more than that. After all he is the god of law, authority, order, civilization, the weather, among many many other things. While Hera is the Goddess of Marriage, she was also the patron of the city of Argo, not surprising that the Argonauts stories have her as helping them. Along with her husband Zeus, she is associated with air and the sky as well as as demonstrated by this Orphic hymn.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's petty well established they aren't in love in any modern meaning of the word. Zeus is depicted as cheating on, deceiving, humiliating and beating Hera qite often, while Hera has led the gods in rebellion against her husband twice that I know of.<br /> That people celebrate ther marriage doesn't mean it is a happy one, it means that disciples of a religion are unlikely to be big critics of its supreme deities.<br /> <br /> I always thought Hera making hail and clouds into weapons (in that text about Dionysus' invasion of India if I remember correctly) was really cool, since it clearly showed her attributes went beyond the merely social aspect people usually focus on.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T07:49:46-07:00","id":621254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=619864#post619864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was mention at some point of 'alternate' settings, will there be any chance of one of those looking at a world in which belief in the Pantheons is returning enmasse or, even more fun, has been consumed by the celebrity media? You know, articles in fashion magazines with titles like 'Konstantin reveals all: top 10 beauty tips from a Scion of Aphrodite!' or rather than doctrine/scripture/etc. you get 'Hera's top 10 tips for a healthy marriage!'<br /> <br /> I am...easily amused apparently.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can easily see Scions of crafter gods becoming the new Bill Gtaes's of the world (as well as the new Steve Jobs's [if I get to make a Caanite pantheon at some point I am so using the name Steve Job for a crafter]). Miner's strikes being run by Mead instead of tea, and low-level Scions being in really good jobs because nobody wants to piss off their mum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T13:10:56-07:00","id":621574,"title":"","content":"Will there be a 'normal' playtest, or at least another rules infodump?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T11:23:16-07:00","id":622457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=621225#post621225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's petty well established they aren't in love in any modern meaning of the word. Zeus is depicted as cheating on, deceiving, humiliating and beating Hera qite often, while Hera has led the gods in rebellion against her husband twice that I know of.<br /> That people celebrate ther marriage doesn't mean it is a happy one, it means that disciples of a religion are unlikely to be big critics of its supreme deities.<br /> <br /> I always thought Hera making hail and clouds into weapons (in that text about Dionysus' invasion of India if I remember correctly) was really cool, since it clearly showed her attributes went beyond the merely social aspect people usually focus on.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I disagree with your assessment of Zeus and Hera not being in love. Their marriage may be strained (and perhaps unhealthy by modern standards), but it doesn't mean that there isn't love there. The problem mainly seems to come from Zeus's extramarital affairs, but nothing says that monogamy is the necessary result of love. Hera tends towards monogamy, while Zeus tends towards polyamory, and this brings strife between them. If Hera did not love him, she might not care so much about his affairs, rather than becoming wrathfully jealous every time Zeus dallied with a mortal or a nymph. If Zeus did not wish to be with Hera, he could have divorced her.<br /> <br /> Also, there is a lot more meaning to the Thaeogamia. We are not just celebrating their marriage because we don't want the Gods to think that we are criticizing them. Of course, it helps that many Hellenic Polytheists don't interpret the myths literally.<br /> <br /> I agree wholeheartedly that it is nice to see Hera depicted as more than just &quot;The Goddess of Marriage&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T11:31:13-07:00","id":622464,"title":"","content":"Please don't equate infidelity with polyamory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T11:50:38-07:00","id":622484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=622464#post622464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please don't equate infidelity with polyamory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. One can cheat within a polyamorous relationship, or otherwise break the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T11:51:10-07:00","id":622485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=621574#post621574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will there be a 'normal' playtest, or at least another rules infodump?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm trying to build a vertical or alpha slice, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T13:59:10-07:00","id":622622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=622457#post622457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree with your assessment of Zeus and Hera not being in love. Their marriage may be strained (and perhaps unhealthy by modern standards), but it doesn't mean that there isn't love there. The problem mainly seems to come from Zeus's extramarital affairs, but nothing says that monogamy is the necessary result of love. Hera tends towards monogamy, while Zeus tends towards polyamory, and this brings strife between them. If Hera did not love him, she might not care so much about his affairs, rather than becoming wrathfully jealous every time Zeus dallied with a mortal or a nymph. If Zeus did not wish to be with Hera, he could have divorced her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, Hera and Zeus may not have the greatest marriage, but I never got the impersion it was an abusive one. But then again to use one of the most notably examples, Herakles' own name means Hera's Glory, not Zeus' glory but Hera, and some of the myths have it where once Herakles achieves godhood, he is welcomed with open arms by Hera. Hera would grant Herakles her daughter Hebe's hand in marriage after he became a god.<br /> <br /> Hesiod's theogny IIRC has a line about the two being in love, sure they quarelled after words. Also in regards to zeus and Polyamory, Hera was not his only wife. Hesoid's Theogony has Metis and Themis as wives of Zeus. Though IIRC only Hera is the one he truly loves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=622457#post622457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, there is a lot more meaning to the Thaeogamia. We are not just celebrating their marriage because we don't want the Gods to think that we are criticizing them. Of course, it helps that many Hellenic Polytheists don't interpret the myths literally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, the thing is even during the Classical and Hellenistic age, people kept making the myths more their own. Then add into the fact that nearly every city and every kingdom had their own different myths. Part of the problem is that a good number come from Athens, who was rivals with a lot of cities, including Argos. Argos' patron goddess was Hera, hence why the stories about the Argonauts have Hera as the deity that helps them a long. Society changes and with it people often like to look at their stories and find meaning in them for the Modern day. It doesn't matter if the Modern day means 2015 CE or the 15 BCE.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=622457#post622457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree wholeheartedly that it is nice to see Hera depicted as more than just &quot;The Goddess of Marriage&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1381,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","user":"herkles","date":". 08-10-2015, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T18:09:33-07:00","id":622950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=622464#post622464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please don't equate infidelity with polyamory.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair enough. I apologize for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T22:07:13-07:00","id":623115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=622457#post622457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I disagree with your assessment of Zeus and Hera not being in love. Their marriage may be strained (and perhaps unhealthy by modern standards), but it doesn't mean that there isn't love there. The problem mainly seems to come from Zeus's extramarital affairs, but nothing says that monogamy is the necessary result of love. Hera tends towards monogamy, while Zeus tends towards polyamory, and this brings strife between them. If Hera did not love him, she might not care so much about his affairs, rather than becoming wrathfully jealous every time Zeus dallied with a mortal or a nymph. If Zeus did not wish to be with Hera, he could have divorced her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hanging your wife upside down from a mountain go waaaay beyond the merely unhealthy. And not not wanting to be cheated on, is in no way a proof of love, especially when the status given by your marriage define most of who you are.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T06:50:41-07:00","id":625406,"title":"","content":"Neall,<br /> <br /> If it's not too spoiler-y...<br /> <br /> 1) Besides the Theoi and the Loa/Yoruba-gods (not sure of their collective noun off-hand), are their any other of the 1e pantheons that are getting major conceptual overhauls on their PSPs? (On a related note, please tell me Geasa are still in for the Tuatha)<br /> <br /> 2) Related but distinct: What is your general approach or design philosophy for PSPs?<br /> <br /> EDIT: As a side note, thank you in advance for actually balancing and playtesting this edition. I say this as someone that tried to ST it and failed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","name":"Lokisenna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T07:49:57-07:00","id":625495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokisenna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=625406#post625406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neall,1) Besides the Theoi and the Loa/Yoruba-gods (not sure of their collective noun off-hand), are their any other of the 1e pantheons that are getting major conceptual overhauls on their PSPs? (On a related note, please tell me Geasa are still in for the Tuatha)</div> </div> </div> </div>Virtually all of them. <i>Geasa </i>are still important for the Tuatha.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Related but distinct: What is your general approach or design philosophy for PSPs? </div> </div> </div>If there are cultural magics wielded by the gods, and/or if the mythologies have distinct powers their gods frequently use, those go into a Pantheon-specific Purview. Ideally, this is under a unifying theme that relates to the pantheons. This is why the Greeks are superior shapeshifters to even the Knacks of various Trickster Callings - they embody <i>concepts</i>, and thus their shape is often irrelevant. PSPs also tie into other Purviews and Knacks, to produce culturally-specific effects.<br /> <br /> That said, PSPs are one of the things we need to kick the tires the hardest and longest on, to make sure the fucking things <i>work</i>. Sei\u00f0r and runic magic are both distinct but would, under this paradigm, be under the \u00c6sir PSP; does this work for characters? Can we tie the two together somehow? It's slow going, but I think it'll work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT: As a side note, thank you in advance for actually balancing and playtesting this edition. I say this as someone that tried to ST it and failed. </div> </div> </div>Don't thank me yet; that's what the money is for!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 08-13-2015, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T08:03:16-07:00","id":625508,"title":"","content":"Now I know you have stated that the Gods aren't birthed from mortal belief nor fueled by it. But can you elaborate then why the player character would bother with them? It just doesn't seem to offer any benefit to play a God that gifts humans with something to better themselves. Like a new food. Or calming a raging typhoon. Also thanks for putting effort into this version. I struggle to use 1st Edition due to lack of polish and options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7272-ratet","name":"Ratet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T08:28:01-07:00","id":625520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;But can you elaborate then why the player character would bother with them? It just doesn't seem to offer any benefit to play a God that gifts humans with something to better themselves.&quot; </div> </div> </div>You probably shouldin't rely on mechanical incentives for why your character does something unless they are basically psychopaths. There are people who love, worship and adore you and rely on you for blessings and protection. Why wouldin't you want to help them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T08:33:04-07:00","id":625529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ratet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=625508#post625508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I know you have stated that the Gods aren't birthed from mortal belief</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, that is correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> nor fueled by it. </div> </div> </div>Did <i>not</i> say that. Gods aren't reliant on worship for power, it's true, the same way a car isn't precisely reliant on high-quality gasoline or a tank of nitrous oxide strapped under the frame. But those certainly make driving easier and give a massive boost, if you're not afraid of taking a little wear on the engine.<br /> <br /> There's a degree of symbiosis going on. Gods needs humanity as much as humanity needs the Gods, if for nothing else than to provide meaning for one another. They can exist apart from one another, but they're lesser for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But can you elaborate then why the player character would bother with them? It just doesn't seem to offer any benefit to play a God that gifts humans with something to better themselves. Like a new food. Or calming a raging typhoon. Also thanks for putting effort into this version. I struggle to use 1st Edition due to lack of polish and options. </div> </div> </div>Lots of reasons. Simple companionship, wanting to reaffirm their mantle and divinity in Fate through recognition, wanting a cult to do their works and do shit in the world in their name without getting their hands dirty. Some might even invoke worship so they stay away; prayer to the Morrigan, not for victory in war, but so that war doesn't touch your loved ones and homestead. Having a cult fuels certain miracles and effects, allows you to touch your followers in an organized way, and helps to codify and cement your divine role and Callings against negative Fatebindings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T08:38:39-07:00","id":625535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=625495#post625495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why the Greeks are superior shapeshifters to even the Knacks of various Trickster Callings - they embody <i>concepts</i>, and thus their shape is often irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any particular reason that this is more true of the Theoi than of other pantheons? For that matter, is it true of the non-Greek members?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, PSPs are one of the things we need to kick the tires the hardest and longest on, to make sure the fucking things <i>work</i>. Sei\u00f0r and runic magic are both distinct but would, under this paradigm, be under the \u00c6sir PSP; does this work for characters? Can we tie the two together somehow? It's slow going, but I think it'll work. </div> </div> </div>Things like this, I like to hear. Excellent.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","name":"Lokisenna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T08:42:22-07:00","id":625541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=625495#post625495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That said, PSPs are one of the things we need to kick the tires the hardest and longest on, to make sure the fucking things <i>work</i>. Sei\u00f0r and runic magic are both distinct but would, under this paradigm, be under the \u00c6sir PSP; does this work for characters? Can we tie the two together somehow? It's slow going, but I think it'll work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose the Germanic cultural mistrust of Magic is just going to vanish then? Because Practicing Sei\u00f0r was not only a specifically female practice but was actually highly illegal and a cause for ridicule, scorn, fear and distrust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T09:11:42-07:00","id":625588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokisenna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=625535#post625535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any particular reason that this is more true of the Theoi than of other pantheons? For that matter, is it true of the non-Greek members?</div> </div> </div> </div>Greco-Roman Gods tend to be gods embodying abstract concepts a lot more often than other types of divinity, or the Spirtual Beings of Native mythologies, or what have you. The Morrigan has War as her Purview, it's true; Deimos, though, is God of Dread. Dread! It's to a degree you don't often see in other pantheons.<br /> <br /> Loki is spectacularly good at turning gender, or into a horse, or into lots of other things. The Theoi as a whole can do stuff like turn into clouds and rain on people. Specifically Etruscan (like Leinth, who mostly hangs out in the Underworld or in hospice care) and specifically Roman (like Divis Julius, who's still sour about Brutus) Gods are <i>less</i> good at this sort of thing, but still <i>pretty good</i>, they just tend to focus their power in other arenas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T09:20:33-07:00","id":625598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=625541#post625541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose the Germanic cultural mistrust of Magic is just going to vanish then? Because Practicing Sei\u00f0r was not only a specifically female practice but was actually highly illegal and a cause for ridicule, scorn, fear and distrust.</div> </div> </div> </div>Give me a <i>little</i> credit for actually <i>reading</i> the Lokisenna. I'm aware of the mistrust. Loki gives Odin shit for knowing sei\u00f0r. Runic magic like what Egil does and the shamanic seid are two different practices that would fit into the same PSP - one is culturally cool, the other isn't. Maybe it's because of the hybrid, confederate pantheon the \u00c6sir are, having absorbed the Vanir, that their PSP is like that. We're still kicking the tires. But yes, practicing sei\u00f0r would probably be a cause for all of the above.<br /> <br /> This actually ties into an interesting element of <b>Scion</b>, though - you're modern characters, and modern people, interacting with ancient mores and divinities and social codes. In much of the modern day, who gives a shit if it's a womanly act or a specifically feminine practice? (Besides all the \u00c6sir.)<br /> <br /> If you're a male Scion, is your masculinity defined by the magics you perform? Do you bow to social pressure, or do you tell Thor to choke on his hammer, you'll wear a dress if you feel like it and magic all day? And this goes way beyond the Norse. Lots of gods are colossal assholes. The Greeks do all kinds of inappropriate shit, and still do. The Aztecs are expecting their blood or the sun don't rise. What's it <i>mean</i> to confront this sort of thing head-on, these belief systems?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 08-13-2015, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T10:50:14-07:00","id":625680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=625598#post625598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Give me a <i>little</i> credit for actually <i>reading</i> the Lokisenna. I'm aware of the mistrust. Loki gives Odin shit for knowing sei\u00f0r. Runic magic like what Egil does and the shamanic seid are two different practices that would fit into the same PSP - one is culturally cool, the other isn't. Maybe it's because of the hybrid, confederate pantheon the \u00c6sir are, having absorbed the Vanir, that their PSP is like that. We're still kicking the tires. But yes, practicing sei\u00f0r would probably be a cause for all of the above.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok I'll give you a <i>little</i> credit, just don't go wild and spend it all at once <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. To be serious though, I appreciate actually doing some of the research to know what your talking about, in 1E i got the distinct impression that someone did a wikipedia scan or read a children book o' myths.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This actually ties into an interesting element of <b>Scion</b>, though - you're modern characters, and modern people, interacting with ancient mores and divinities and social codes. In much of the modern day, who gives a shit if it's a womanly act or a specifically feminine practice? (Besides all the \u00c6sir.)<br /> <br /> If you're a male Scion, is your masculinity defined by the magics you perform? Do you bow to social pressure, or do you tell Thor to choke on his hammer, you'll wear a dress if you feel like it and magic all day? And this goes way beyond the Norse. Lots of gods are colossal assholes. The Greeks do all kinds of inappropriate shit, and still do. The Aztecs are expecting their blood or the sun don't rise. What's it <i>mean</i> to confront this sort of thing head-on, these belief systems? </div> </div> </div>Indeed it does, my third scion before last played that concept to the hilt complete with Rightful Heir of the Throne shticks. My worry is that if these types of cultural traits and ancient beliefs are white washed over to conform with modern expectations, then it completely destroys the possibility of those very interesting storylines when different ages and mores and values conform.<br /> <br /> Interestingly enough for people who want to go that route, the idea that Seidr is womanly is putting the cart before the horse. Seidr is cowardly and improper and thus only suitable for women in the Germanic mindset. Its far more likely that a Gender Egalitarian Scion of the Aesir is going to come to the conclusion that Seidr is improper for everyone, not just men.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T11:27:46-07:00","id":625700,"title":"","content":"Honestly, assuming magic is still a Purview, I'd just be inclined to treat seidr as the culturally specific form the rituals take. I'm not aware of any really specific-to-the-Norse EFFECTS of their magic in legend, and its practiced by so few of the gods (pretty much just Odin and Freyja [&amp;/or Frigg; it's hard to tell sometimes because of how often conflated Freyja and Frigg are]).<br /> <br /> I agree that Seidr should be Vanir in origin (introduced to the Aesir by either Frigg [who is widely assumed to have been Vanir before marrying Odin] or Freyja [who is without a doubt Vanir]. Rune magic is the magic that Odin gained from sacrificing himself to himself on Yggdrasil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T11:37:12-07:00","id":625707,"title":"","content":"There is a bit of vagueness about what exactly constitutes Seidr. Personally I prefer the definition that its sorcery involving curses and charms of that sort. This is quite different from the Oracular abilities of a Seer of the self help and nifty tricks of Rune magic or Galdr and explains why it was unlawful. I'd have to recommend putting it into magic as well, 1E magic actually contains just about anything Seidr wise you might want to accomplish. Odin learned Seidr by the instruction of Freya, who doubtless practiced it before the merging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T11:43:16-07:00","id":625708,"title":"","content":"How much can we expect to see reference to gods throwing their support behind modern cultural phenomena (Loki and trans* &amp; genderqueer rights, etc.)? What about culture-specific things like the modern attempts at reviving the Gaelic languages? I would imagine the Tuatha would at least support such, if not actively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","name":"Lokisenna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T11:51:38-07:00","id":625712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokisenna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=625708#post625708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much can we expect to see reference to gods throwing their support behind modern cultural phenomena (Loki and trans* &amp; genderqueer rights, etc.)? What about culture-specific things like the modern attempts at reviving the Gaelic languages? I would imagine the Tuatha would at least support such, if not actively.</div> </div> </div> </div>A <i>bit</i>, and this extends into the level of fictionality I referenced earlier: the Gods of <b>Scion</b> are not the actual gods of these religions, but the gods through the chosen lens of mythology and fiction for game purposes. Loki uses the singular they. I'd be much happier saying Caeneus is a trans* Scion of Poseidon. On the other hand, there's the danger of, as Ulfhednar said, effectively whitewashing the myths and de-fanging the pathos you get from these radically different ancient mores in the modern era. It's a balancing act, one that needs to actually be taken on a case-by-case basis.<br /> <br /> And yes, the Tuatha would support those things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 08-13-2015, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T12:38:05-07:00","id":625747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=625712#post625712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, the Tuatha would support those things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, more questions on language things gods might have opinions on, out of curiosity!<br /> <br /> 1) The Theoi's opinion on the modern state of Greece going with Modern Greek as its official language instead of Ancient Greek?<br /> 2) Their thoughts on (Classical) Latin revivalism? Sure, it's a small movement, but it's there!<br /> 3) Any gods with opinions on constructed languages? Intended auxiliary languages, like Esperanto or Lojban?<br /> 4) What do the Polynesian gods that are still around think of Tok Pisin?<br /> <br /> Non-language, but related, question:<br /> <br /> 5) How much active effort do the pantheons put toward trying to save the scrapes of their original associated cultures that are still around? Let's be honest, no modern culture is going to feel at home to gods as old as those in Scion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","name":"Lokisenna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T13:08:06-07:00","id":625782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokisenna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=625747#post625747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) How much active effort do the pantheons put toward trying to save the scrapes of their original associated cultures that are still around? Let's be honest, no modern culture is going to feel at home to gods as old as those in Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>This made me think about two questions relating to scion.<br /> <br /> Question 1.) is Scion going with the idea the values and ideas of the gods and their religion don't ever change and have never changed?<br /> Question 2.)Relatedly How do the various indian gods view modern india, same with the Japanese. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T13:35:26-07:00","id":625811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokisenna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=625747#post625747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, more questions on language things gods might have opinions on, out of curiosity!<br /> <br /> 1) The Theoi's opinion on the modern state of Greece going with Modern Greek as its official language instead of Ancient Greek?</div> </div> </div> </div>Their bred Scions are still hardwired to speak Ancient Greek or Latin, depending on mantled entity. They're not thrilled, but they probably don't muchly care. They'd speak Modern when it suits them.<br /> <br /> [quote]2) Their thoughts on (Classical) Latin revivalism? Sure, it's a small movement, but it's there!<br /> <br /> Probably happy about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) Any gods with opinions on constructed languages? Intended auxiliary languages, like Esperanto or Lojban? </div> </div> </div>Probably not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) What do the Polynesian gods that are still around think of Tok Pisin? </div> </div> </div>I'll probably cover that when we do the Atua in Demigod.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Non-language, but related, question:<br /> 5) How much active effort do the pantheons put toward trying to save the scrapes of their original associated cultures that are still around? Let's be honest, no modern culture is going to feel at home to gods as old as those in Scion. </div> </div> </div>There's a good deal of ancient cults still active, more so than in the modern day here. Our world is not the World in <b>Scion</b>, though it's close. The old gods never went away; they still exist in the teeming mass of humanity. The old religions are still there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T13:36:28-07:00","id":625812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=625782#post625782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This made me think about two questions relating to scion.<br /> <br /> Question 1.) is Scion going with the idea the values and ideas of the gods and their religion don't ever change and have never changed?<br /> Question 2.)Relatedly How do the various indian gods view modern india, same with the Japanese.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are questions the book itself will have a <i>lot </i>to say on, more so than I can cover here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T01:34:28-07:00","id":626429,"title":"","content":"This set of questions came to me;<br /> <br /> Going under the assumption that the modern collection of monotheistic religions are incorrect as far as Scion goes, where do all the uncounted billions of dead souls from the last few centuries end up when they die? Do they simply wander the earth cluttering up the place with traffic that only those with the Death purview can see? Do they all become specters as they have no death god to look after them? And can an aspiring death god of one pantheon or another lay claim to these essentially homeless souls? Most importantly, was this concept addressed in the new edition?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T05:22:00-07:00","id":626505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=626429#post626429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This set of questions came to me;<br /> <br /> Going under the assumption that the modern collection of monotheistic religions are incorrect as far as Scion goes, where do all the uncounted billions of dead souls from the last few centuries end up when they die? Do they simply wander the earth cluttering up the place with traffic that only those with the Death purview can see? Do they all become specters as they have no death god to look after them? And can an aspiring death god of one pantheon or another lay claim to these essentially homeless souls? Most importantly, was this concept addressed in the new edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some simply reincarnate on death (most probably do, actually, since the World's population is growing). Others might linger in the World itself, until a wandering psychopomp stops to help them (which is the kind of thing that heroes and demigods of Death do during their downtime). If they're not claimed by related pantheons, such as the Arabic or Caananite ones, there are &quot;unaffiliated&quot; realms within the Underworld. The Underworld has some <i>really</i> prime pieces of real estate, but there are still wild, untamed elements, and there are neutral underworlds where cities grow upwards towards the muted, cold sun of the dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T06:06:35-07:00","id":626533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=626505#post626505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Caananite</div> </div> </div> </div>!<br /> <br /> Am I to interpret this to mean, more or less, that in the context of the setting, the modern monotheistic faiths are incorrect because they've abandoned most of their gods, rather than the stupid thing with Aten from 1e? You've mentioned the latter is out anyway.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","name":"Lokisenna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T07:00:27-07:00","id":626576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokisenna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=626533#post626533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> !<br /> <br /> Am I to interpret this to mean, more or less, that in the context of the setting, the modern monotheistic faiths are incorrect because they've abandoned most of their gods, rather than the stupid thing with Aten from 1e? You've mentioned the latter is out anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Monotheism's place in the setting is something I don't want to comment much more on, because I want the wording to be <i>exactly</i> what I mean, and if I give an off-the-cuff answer it'll either piss off or turn off a whole lot of people.<br /> <br /> Aten is something that's going to be in the book, just different. The Caananite pantheon is something I'd like to cover in Scion anyways, warily circling the Egyptian and Mesopotamian pantheons in a Levantine standoff. They're slated for the Demigod book.<br /> <br /> Besides, we've got some precedent for Baal in our inspirational material:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://41.media.tumblr.com/6f558157b14b10666d1d5355d58aba8c/tumblr_ng3qynHQRb1u4a1aso1_500.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 08-14-2015, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T07:05:30-07:00","id":626578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=626576#post626576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Monotheism's place in the setting is something I don't want to comment much more on, because I want the wording to be <i>exactly</i> what I mean, and if I give an off-the-cuff answer it'll either piss off or turn off a whole lot of people</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, understandable. Sorry if it seemed like I was trying to corner you on the topic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Aten is something that's going to be in the book, just different. The Caananite pantheon is something I'd like to cover in Scion anyways, warily circling the Egyptian and Mesopotamian pantheons in a Levantine standoff. They're slated for the Demigod book.<br /> <br /> Besides, we've got some precedent for Baal in our inspirational material:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://41.media.tumblr.com/6f558157b14b10666d1d5355d58aba8c/tumblr_ng3qynHQRb1u4a1aso1_500.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> </div> </div> </div>Aw yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","name":"Lokisenna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T07:31:04-07:00","id":626620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=626505#post626505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some simply reincarnate on death (most probably do, actually, since the World's population is growing).</div> </div> </div> </div>Branching off this (and because I don't remember if 1e addressed this): Where do new souls for come from? What's the usual time between death and reincarnation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","name":"Lokisenna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T07:51:46-07:00","id":626638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokisenna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=626620#post626620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Branching off this (and because I don't remember if 1e addressed this): Where do new souls for come from? What's the usual time between death and reincarnation?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll just note that in most Hindu and Mahayana thought on the subject I'm aware of (I haven't read a lot of Theravada writing), most &quot;new souls&quot; are just first time HUMANS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T07:52:55-07:00","id":626640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokisenna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=626620#post626620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Branching off this (and because I don't remember if 1e addressed this): Where do new souls for come from? What's the usual time between death and reincarnation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody really knows where new souls come from, though most don't care, and theories revolve around the depleting biomass of the planet fueling new souls for humanity. As in so much else, myth defies scientific analysis.<br /> <br /> Different pantheons regard reincarnation differently. Some have afterlives and Underworlds that are specifically geared towards engineering reincarnation as quickly as possible; others have permanent residences for souls and shades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T07:55:31-07:00","id":626642,"title":"","content":"who is that guy in that art peice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T07:59:14-07:00","id":626643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=626642#post626642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">who is that guy in that art peice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Baal, from <i>The Wicked + The Divine</i>. Make sure to get your Baals right around him, though. He gets annoyed if you haven't done your homework.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://multiversitystatic.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/2014/09/wicdiv4-2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T08:03:54-07:00","id":626648,"title":"","content":"So does Inari also use singular-They?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T08:07:24-07:00","id":626651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=626648#post626648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So does Inari also use singular-They?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not always; Inari would be genderfluid on the binary sexual continuum for the most part, unless they're being androgynous that day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T08:27:09-07:00","id":626665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=626643#post626643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Baal, from <i>The Wicked + The Divine</i>. Make sure to get your Baals right around him, though. He gets annoyed if you haven't done your homework.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://multiversitystatic.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/2014/09/wicdiv4-2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Cool, I am not really familar with the Wicked and the divine. So feel free to tell me about it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T08:45:16-07:00","id":626694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=626665#post626665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool, I am not really familar with the Wicked and the divine. So feel free to tell me about it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It is <a href=\"https://imagecomics.com/content/view/gods-are-the-ultimate-pop-stars-in-the-wicked-the-divine\" target=\"_blank\">sufficiently cool</a> that it has dethroned <i>American Gods </i>as the top inspiration for this edition of the game, or at least shouldered that book to the side aesthetic-wise. Also worth noting is Gillen's run on Journey into Mystery, which is also excellent, and provided the inspiration for the fourth type of Scion for the second edition (though WicDiv and <i>Mage: the Hero Defined </i>also contributed heavily).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T10:39:03-07:00","id":626733,"title":"","content":"I am not very much into graphic novels, but I may decide to check that out in the future. <br /> <br /> Some questions:<br /> <br /> 1.) How might some of the 'minor' deities be in Scion. By this I mean deities that are not the big ones. to use the Greeks, ones that are not the 12 Olympians + Hades and Persephone. The Greek religion has a deity for about everything, so I am curious how they might be around in Scion 2nd.<br /> 2.) How will scion be addressing the non-deity creatures that were worshiped and part of the myths and stories. Things like nature spirits weather they be Nymphs, Faun, Elves or dwarves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T10:43:53-07:00","id":626735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=626694#post626694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is <a href=\"https://imagecomics.com/content/view/gods-are-the-ultimate-pop-stars-in-the-wicked-the-divine\" target=\"_blank\">sufficiently cool</a> that it has dethroned <i>American Gods </i>as the top inspiration for this edition of the game, or at least shouldered that book to the side aesthetic-wise. Also worth noting is Gillen's run on Journey into Mystery, which is also excellent, and provided the inspiration for the fourth type of Scion for the second edition (though WicDiv and <i>Mage: the Hero Defined </i>also contributed heavily).</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking at those inspirations... is the fourth type a god who's died and been reincarnated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T11:54:52-07:00","id":626764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=626735#post626735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at those inspirations... is the fourth type a god who's died and been reincarnated?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. That's what happens when you make the Devata and Tuatha into core pantheons (with Nemetondevos as a stretch goal).<br /> <br /> Gods, demigods, and even heroes <i>can</i> be reincarnated and weave their Legend to take advantage of their prior incarnation's power. It's hard to kill a god (unless they're Fated somehow to completely perish, and even then it's nearly impossible to keep a good life-death-rebirth deity down, so long as they don't get killed by mistletoe or something), but it can be done, and they'll hang out in the Underworld until they resurrect somehow, choose to reincarnate as mortals, or just sort of dissipate into a shade. Their divine mantles don't disappear when they die - the archetypes and power they embody still exist within Fate, so a successor could potentially seize that mantle and adopt it themselves.<br /> <br /> Minor gods, perished demigods, or cultural heroes chosen to do the will of divinity are the ones we suggest in the game (a few from every pantheon), or gods from a now-defunct part of the pantheon, but if your <b>Scion</b> game has that Thor took one to the face about twenty years back and now you've got to fight off Magni and Modi to wield Mjolnir once more, more power to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T12:10:00-07:00","id":626781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=626764#post626764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep. That's what happens when you make the Devata and Tuatha into core pantheons (with Nemetondevos as a stretch goal).<br /> <br /> Gods, demigods, and even heroes <i>can</i> be reincarnated and weave their Legend to take advantage of their prior incarnation's power. It's hard to kill a god (unless they're Fated somehow to completely perish, and even then it's nearly impossible to keep a good life-death-rebirth deity down, so long as they don't get killed by mistletoe or something), but it can be done, and they'll hang out in the Underworld until they resurrect somehow, choose to reincarnate as mortals, or just sort of dissipate into a shade. Their divine mantles don't disappear when they die - the archetypes and power they embody still exist within Fate, so a successor could potentially seize that mantle and adopt it themselves.<br /> <br /> Minor gods, perished demigods, or cultural heroes chosen to do the will of divinity are the ones we suggest in the game (a few from every pantheon), or gods from a now-defunct part of the pantheon, but if your <b>Scion</b> game has that Thor took one to the face about twenty years back and now you've got to fight off Magni and Modi to wield Mjolnir once more, more power to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is Baldur still around by default, or is he on the table for this? His primary remembered story is about him dying, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":58,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","user":"Lokisenna","date":". 08-14-2015, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","name":"Lokisenna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T12:15:42-07:00","id":626782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokisenna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=626781#post626781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Baldur still around by default, or is on the table for this? His primary remembered story is about him dying, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>By default, he's not - the Edda prophecies are in the future, rather than the past, much like in 1e - but if you decide they're <i>not</i>, he surely is. Though claiming his mantle prior to Ragnarok might be problematic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T12:18:21-07:00","id":626785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=626782#post626782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By default, he's not - the Edda prophecies are in the future, rather than the past, much like in 1e - but if you decide they're <i>not</i>, he surely is. Though claiming his mantle prior to Ragnarok might be problematic.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does sound like a good way for a character to end up dead themselves, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","name":"Lokisenna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T12:38:48-07:00","id":626825,"title":"","content":"At my own table, Baldur was slain at the end of the Viking age, while Scandenavia was finishing being converted to Christianity - it's been Fimbulwinter ever since as far as Asgarde is concerned. Loki is bound, but escapes regularly to make mischief and has to be tracked down and rebound (and Odin's been known to be behind some of his excursions when necessary to address some problem... often a problem Loki was responsible for previously setting in motion). <i><b>Forseti</b></i> acts as patron to Scions in his late father's name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T15:05:56-07:00","id":627008,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone,<br /> this is the first time I write on this forum even though I have been reading it quite regularly for a while now.<br /> My question to Neall - and to the whole community - is the following:<br /> <br /> What are the next deadlines for the Scion project?<br /> <br /> If the answer to this question is clearly stated somewhere, I must have missed it, and I apologize for the repetition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7302-darknailo","name":"darknailo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T18:40:30-07:00","id":627161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=626764#post626764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep. That's what happens when you make the Devata and Tuatha into core pantheons (with Nemetondevos as a stretch goal).<br /> <br /> Gods, demigods, and even heroes <i>can</i> be reincarnated and weave their Legend to take advantage of their prior incarnation's power. It's hard to kill a god (unless they're Fated somehow to completely perish, and even then it's nearly impossible to keep a good life-death-rebirth deity down, so long as they don't get killed by mistletoe or something), but it can be done, and they'll hang out in the Underworld until they resurrect somehow, choose to reincarnate as mortals, or just sort of dissipate into a shade. Their divine mantles don't disappear when they die - the archetypes and power they embody still exist within Fate, so a successor could potentially seize that mantle and adopt it themselves.<br /> <br /> Minor gods, perished demigods, or cultural heroes chosen to do the will of divinity are the ones we suggest in the game (a few from every pantheon), or gods from a now-defunct part of the pantheon, but if your <b>Scion</b> game has that Thor took one to the face about twenty years back and now you've got to fight off Magni and Modi to wield Mjolnir once more, more power to you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> First This is awesome.<br /> <br /> Second Does this mean that becoming associated with purviews/knacks require less that it did in 1e?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T20:08:32-07:00","id":627184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class