:"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T22:38:33-07:00","id":627278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=626764#post626764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep. That's what happens when you make the Devata and Tuatha into core pantheons (with Nemetondevos as a stretch goal).<br /> <br /> Gods, demigods, and even heroes <i>can</i> be reincarnated and weave their Legend to take advantage of their prior incarnation's power. It's hard to kill a god (unless they're Fated somehow to completely perish, and even then it's nearly impossible to keep a good life-death-rebirth deity down, so long as they don't get killed by mistletoe or something), but it can be done, and they'll hang out in the Underworld until they resurrect somehow, choose to reincarnate as mortals, or just sort of dissipate into a shade. Their divine mantles don't disappear when they die - the archetypes and power they embody still exist within Fate, so a successor could potentially seize that mantle and adopt it themselves.<br /> <br /> Minor gods, perished demigods, or cultural heroes chosen to do the will of divinity are the ones we suggest in the game (a few from every pantheon), or gods from a now-defunct part of the pantheon, but if your <b>Scion</b> game has that Thor took one to the face about twenty years back and now you've got to fight off Magni and Modi to wield Mjolnir once more, more power to you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I really curious to see who you chose for some of the of the Pantheons (especially the Theoi since they have some of the most explicitly unkillable and eternal gods in world mythology), especially wondering whether you decided to put any &quot;big names&quot; in that stack rather than include them as canonically viable active parents.<br /> <br /> So is this cycle of death and reincarnation how the Avatars of the Devata work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T13:21:48-07:00","id":627821,"title":"","content":"The gods were eternal, sure, but the demigods were a totally different story. Orpheus, Achilles, Bellerophon, Pollux, Endymion","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T13:34:24-07:00","id":629041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=626764#post626764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minor gods, perished demigods, or cultural heroes</div> </div> </div> </div>So... I could be the reincarnation of Achilles or a deified Roman emperor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T21:28:01-07:00","id":629545,"title":"","content":"That's how I understood it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T06:43:21-07:00","id":629856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=629041#post629041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So... I could be the reincarnation of Achilles or a deified Roman emperor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Those are actually pretty good examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T14:18:56-07:00","id":630249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=626764#post626764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gods, demigods, and even heroes <i>can</i> be reincarnated and weave their Legend to take advantage of their prior incarnation's power. It's hard to kill a god (unless they're Fated somehow to completely perish, and even then it's nearly impossible to keep a good life-death-rebirth deity down, so long as they don't get killed by mistletoe or something), but it can be done, and they'll hang out in the Underworld until they resurrect somehow, choose to reincarnate as mortals, or just sort of dissipate into a shade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes more than just hangout - Izanami gives at least one precedent of a god using their death to establish their permanent purview and domain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T21:10:02-07:00","id":630621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=629856#post629856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. Those are actually pretty good examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shudder.<br /> Deified roman emperors can be quite brutal...........<br /> Nero, Calligula, Caesar (and his Brutus)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T04:44:17-07:00","id":631018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=630621#post630621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shudder.<br /> Deified roman emperors can be quite brutal...........<br /> Nero, Calligula, Caesar (and his Brutus)</div> </div> </div> </div>Julius Caesar has actually already been mentioned as part of the Theoi:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=625588#post625588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Divis Julius, who's still sour about Brutus</div> </div> </div> </div>As for Caligula...didn't he hijack the pantheon by impersonating Zeus/Jupiter during WW2, in 1E? A lot of the WW2 material from Companion was iffy, but always had more positive feelings about that idea. EDIT: I -don't- want this single off-hand comment to drag the whole damn thread off-topic, so...<br /> <br /> Neall, is Gaius/Caius Caligula sticking around, and if so, is this footnote doing so, too? I'm going to hazard a guess that you're not interested in re-hashing the WW2 stuff anytime soon, if ever, I was just curious about this small point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":58,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","user":"Lokisenna","date":". 08-18-2015, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","name":"Lokisenna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T05:32:34-07:00","id":631057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokisenna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=631018#post631018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Julius Caesar has actually already been mentioned as part of the Theoi:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for Caligula...didn't he hijack the pantheon by impersonating Zeus/Jupiter during WW2, in 1E? A lot of the WW2 material from Companion was iffy, but always had more positive feelings about that idea. EDIT: I -don't- want this single off-hand comment to drag the whole damn thread off-topic, so...<br /> <br /> Neall, is Gaius/Caius Caligula sticking around, and if so, is this footnote doing so, too? I'm going to hazard a guess that you're not interested in re-hashing the WW2 stuff anytime soon, if ever, I was just curious about this small point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know about Julius that is why _I mentioned him there^^ <br /> <br /> And for Caligula.....he tried to put himself up as a deity in real rome...........about the time he was murdered. That is why I mentioned him in that comment <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T08:28:55-07:00","id":631211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokisenna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=631018#post631018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for Caligula...didn't he hijack the pantheon by impersonating Zeus/Jupiter during WW2, in 1E?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can we please not do that again?<br /> <br /> If they do a WW2 era, my strong pitch with the Theoi is to go Trojan War with it and have the Pantheon divided. Zeus and Hades play neutral as always. Using <a href=\"http://www.aoc.gov/sites/default/files/styles/artwork-node/public/images/artwork/6082318543_90e9752777_o.jpg?itok=k_RTkncH\" target=\"_blank\">this artwork</a> as inspiration, invested with Western Democracy are Athena and Poseidon (the patrons of Athens, also of course Poseidon backs the strongest navy in the world), Demeter, Hermes, Hephaestus, and Dionysus.<br /> <br /> On the other side (i'll stick with Greek names for clarity despite the culture in question) backing a new Roman Empire in Italy are Ares and Aphrodite (strongest backers of Imperial Rome by way of their Scions Romulus and Aeneus respectively), Apollo, Artemis, Hestia, and Hera.<br /> <br /> There have been some side shifts since Troy (note Hera), but it's a lot of the same old wounds for Olympus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T08:53:37-07:00","id":631241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=631211#post631211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can we please not do that again?<br /> <br /> If they do a WW2 era, my strong pitch with the Theoi is to go Trojan War with it and have the Pantheon divided. Zeus and Hades play neutral as always. Using <a href=\"http://www.aoc.gov/sites/default/files/styles/artwork-node/public/images/artwork/6082318543_90e9752777_o.jpg?itok=k_RTkncH\" target=\"_blank\">this artwork</a> as inspiration, invested with Western Democracy are Athena and Poseidon (the patrons of Athens, also of course Poseidon backs the strongest navy in the world), Demeter, Hermes, Hephaestus, and Dionysus.<br /> <br /> On the other side (i'll stick with Greek names for clarity despite the culture in question) backing a new Roman Empire in Italy are Ares and Aphrodite (strongest backers of Imperial Rome by way of their Scions Romulus and Aeneus respectively), Apollo, Artemis, Hestia, and Hera.<br /> <br /> There have been some side shifts since Troy (note Hera), but it's a lot of the same old wounds for Olympus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am actually new to the Scion forum here, so my apologies for treading on a touchy subject - it's why I put a note about -not- wanting a derail.<br /> <br /> Your ideas are very good. Consistently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","name":"Lokisenna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T09:14:04-07:00","id":631252,"title":"","content":"personally I don't care much for a ww2 era. If there were to be historical eras, I would want to see something else for scion beyond ww2; like say napoelonic or the thirty years war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T10:29:15-07:00","id":631292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokisenna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=631241#post631241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am actually new to the Scion forum here, so my apologies for treading on a touchy subject - it's why I put a note about -not- wanting a derail.<br /> <br /> Your ideas are very good. Consistently.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, sorry, I didn't mean to suggest you were doing anything wrong by bringing it up! I was just expressing my thoughts on resurrecting that topic in the books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T10:40:36-07:00","id":631302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=631292#post631292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh, sorry, I didn't mean to suggest you were doing anything wrong by bringing it up! I was just expressing my thoughts on resurrecting that topic in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems we've had a miscommunication. No problem <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","name":"Lokisenna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T11:04:47-07:00","id":631315,"title":"","content":"If we were to do a historical era involving the Theoi, it'd be the reign of Julian the Apostate. Hands-down.<br /> <br /> Julian is also my top choice to play a reincarnated Scion, by the by. &quot;Haven't won <i>yet</i>, Galilean.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T11:13:51-07:00","id":631322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=631315#post631315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we were to do a historical era involving the Theoi, it'd be the reign of Julian the Apostate. Hands-down.<br /> <br /> Julian is also my top choice to play a reincarnated Scion, by the by. &quot;Haven't won <i>yet</i>, Galilean.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Iiiiii feel stupid for not thinking of this. Fuck. Yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","name":"Lokisenna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T11:41:09-07:00","id":631349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=631315#post631315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we were to do a historical era involving the Theoi, it'd be the reign of Julian the Philospher. Hands-down.<br /> <br /> Julian is also my top choice to play a reincarnated Scion, by the by. &quot;Haven't won <i>yet</i>, Galilean.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I much prefer to call him the philospher over apostate, but hey I practice Hellenismos, which IIRC he actually coined. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T12:03:59-07:00","id":631385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=631315#post631315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we were to do a historical era involving the Theoi, it'd be the reign of Julian the Apostate. Hands-down.<br /> <br /> Julian is also my top choice to play a reincarnated Scion, by the by. &quot;Haven't won <i>yet</i>, Galilean.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>What'd you nominate for other pantheons' historical eras? (say for a Scion equivalent of Dark Eras)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T12:29:03-07:00","id":631403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=631349#post631349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I much prefer to call him the philospher over apostate, but hey I practice Hellenismos, which IIRC he actually coined. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I like what my own forbearers called him: Julian the Hellene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T12:31:23-07:00","id":631405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=631385#post631385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What'd you nominate for other pantheons' historical eras? (say for a Scion equivalent of Dark Eras)</div> </div> </div> </div>Aesir and Mabinogion pitch: Saxon invasion/Arthurian Britain","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T13:13:37-07:00","id":631456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=631385#post631385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What'd you nominate for other pantheons' historical eras? (say for a Scion equivalent of Dark Eras)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we're not doing a Dark Eras book.<br /> <br /> (though we might be <i>now</i>)<br /> <br /> Let's see...going by the core pantheons?<br /> <br /> The Haitian Revolution, the Tuscarora War, Viking raids on Ireland...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T15:04:29-07:00","id":631601,"title":"","content":"One possibility for the Shen would be the Investiture War (fall of the Shang, rise of the Zhou) which drawing on Fengshen Yanyi you have a lot of divine rivalries and conflict running through. BUT, for crossover purposes, I really like idea of either Han Dynasty when Buddhism is introduced to China, or the Tang Dynasty when it reaches its ascendancy, and having the integration of Yanlou (Yama) into the Bureaucracy, relations with the Devata, and the conversion of several major Shen to Buddhism be central to the setting.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, go Qin and have the formatting of the Shen under the Celestial Bureaucracy be the central narrative.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Reign of Akhenaten is the most obvious answer for the Netjer, but one could easily go 19th early 20th Century and explore the stirring of the Netjer with Western Egyptology, tomb desecration, Rosetta Stone, etc etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> Kami has to be Edo Period, and include the ascent of Inari to full top-tier divinity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T16:40:49-07:00","id":631717,"title":"","content":"What would be good for the Hindu pantheon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T18:22:34-07:00","id":631800,"title":"","content":"The obvious answer would be the era of British dominance and the coming of the Tuatha","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T21:23:39-07:00","id":631892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=631800#post631800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The obvious answer would be the era of British dominance and the coming of the Tuatha</div> </div> </div> </div>I very much doubt the Tuatha are fans of the British Empire themselves.<br /> <br /> As I mentioned with my crossover pitch before, if you go with Buddhism spreading to China, and spreading deities like Yama, you have the chance for crossover politics right there.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the Greco-Bactrian period is rich ground for unexpected cross pantheon mingling!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T05:18:52-07:00","id":632160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=631456#post631456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, we're not doing a Dark Eras book.<br /> <br /> (though we might be <i>now</i>)</div> </div> </div> </div>*salivates* I would back this <i>so</i> hard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=631892#post631892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I very much doubt the Tuatha are fans of the British Empire themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>IRL, though, they were mostly displaced <i>long</i> before the British Empire was even considered a possibility, by Catholicism. Far less familiar with Irish religious history, and Irish history in general, than I would like, though. #dumbassAmerican","signature":"","edited":{"userid":58,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","user":"Lokisenna","date":". 08-19-2015, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","name":"Lokisenna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T06:25:29-07:00","id":632192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokisenna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=632160#post632160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IRL, though, they were mostly displaced <i>long</i> before the British Empire was even considered a possibility, by Catholicism. Far less familiar with Irish religious history, and Irish history in general, than I would like, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect the Tuatha's issues with the British Empire would be over how it treated the Irish as nothing more than barbarians and savages - and the material effects of that, such as famine - rather than their own displacement.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway. It wouldn't be original, since Dark Eras has a post-Alexandrian Era, but an Era set during Alexander's life would be interesting, as the Theoi, the Netjer, the Yazata, the Annunaki and the Devatas all have reason to get involved, and it kicks off a long-standing relationship between the Netjer and the Theoi (that is, the Greek/Roman rule of Egypt).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T08:02:06-07:00","id":632301,"title":"","content":"Not to mention, Irish Catholicism integrated elements of Irish Paganism (&quot;Saint Bridget&quot; anyone?) that British Protestantism was less kindly toward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T11:15:45-07:00","id":632544,"title":"","content":"I just realized that the ability for culture heroes to reincarnate give perfect representions for Fate/Stay Night Servants","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":461,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","user":"KingCarnival","date":". 08-19-2015, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T01:31:10-07:00","id":633289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=632544#post632544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just realized that the ability for culture heroes to reincarnate give perfect representions for Fate/Stay Night Servants</div> </div> </div> </div>And I wondered how long until someone sees that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Although with a later reveal in the series there is a question though.....those heroes are not necessarily reincarnated from the past but can be reincarnations of FUTURE heroes.<br /> Not sure if withoug houserule that is supported by the new scion (one can houserule it anyway <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). But I guess it would be cool^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T07:17:28-07:00","id":633407,"title":"","content":"Are Callings paths that are used to measure a scion's growth along a mythic archetype?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T08:58:11-07:00","id":633505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=633407#post633407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Callings paths that are used to measure a scion's growth along a mythic archetype?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Scions can further define the Calling to suit their particular expression of divine nature, providing additional motifs and themes for Knacks and Purviews.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T09:12:13-07:00","id":633513,"title":"","content":"Any thoughts on how to address Olodumare/Olorun/Olofi, Ometeotl, Ahura Mazda, Gitchi Manitou, Mungu, Unkulunkulu, and other &quot;Great Spirit&quot; type distant creator gods, often honored by the respective Pantheons as the highest divinity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T09:32:11-07:00","id":633523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=633513#post633513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any thoughts on how to address Olodumare/Olorun/Olofi, Ometeotl, Ahura Mazda, Gitchi Manitou, Mungu, Unkulunkulu, and other &quot;Great Spirit&quot; type distant creator gods, often honored by the respective Pantheons as the highest divinity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, a few, but none I'm really willing to detail out yet.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T13:11:27-07:00","id":633731,"title":"","content":"Well since it's &quot;Ask Neall&quot;, I'd like to ask Neall, what sources do you use for mythology? Even Irish mythology which I grew up with is sometimes too complex with all its layers, but you seem to have a good control over several mythologies. Is there any series of books you use, any particularly good sources?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T15:34:34-07:00","id":633879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=626694#post626694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also worth noting is Gillen's run on Journey into Mystery, which is also excellent, and provided the inspiration for the fourth type of Scion for the second edition (though WicDiv and <i>Mage: the Hero Defined </i>also contributed heavily).</div> </div> </div> </div>I just have to note that hearing Matt Wagner's Mage series as an inspiration at all makes me all kinds of happy. I've been thinking it was excellent Scion material for <i>years--</i>almost since Hero was released--if in feel more than actual content.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T17:38:40-07:00","id":634043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=633523#post633523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, a few, but none I'm really willing to detail out yet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How far are you willing to detail? How about instead of a <i>Creator of the Universe</i> type of god..would you be willing to address someone more minor, like say...Deimos and his god of Dreadness? When I made a stab at him before, it worked out to RAW: a bunch of Social knacks or the social knacks and the well done homebrew Emotion Purview from Brent Not Broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T16:53:28-07:00","id":635145,"title":"","content":"I know you mentioned Fatebinding has a bit more bite, what are your ideas on implementing that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T15:42:14-07:00","id":636334,"title":"","content":"I've been wondering how relationships between pantheons are going to be treated in this edition. In 1st edition it was all based on rivalry. Pantheons all seemed a bit racist and isolationist towards one another and it just boggles my mind. I mean what do you think is going to happen when you put scions into teams where they face life and death together fighting a war? Strong bonds and emotions are going to form when someone saves your life in most cases. But if scions of different pantheons want to carry their eventual relationships to the point of having children\u2026then most discussions got to 'you can't have dual heritage' or &quot;There is no way the head of your pantheon would let that happen..huge political mess.&quot; <br /> <br /> I mean is it just me or does it seem strange that beings that epic mental stats and literal eons of experience can't learn to work with each other except in cases where the titans are about kill everyone and everything...and then its as allies of the moment...ONLY!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T14:24:52-07:00","id":640646,"title":"","content":"We do know it will be somewhat more nuanced this time because Gods do actually cross pantheons, rather than those always being different gods (Yama is the big case we know of in the core, as he is also Yanluo to the Shen and Emma-O to the Kami).<br /> <br /> So that gives more wiggle room for the Pantheons to actual influence each other in myth rather than them having completely isolated histories before super recently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T21:40:18-07:00","id":646349,"title":"","content":"What all can you share about the reincarnation-type Scions?<br /> <br /> Do they get a Visitation? Birthrights? Is there some recommended minimum level of fame and Legend they should have achieved. Not gonna lie, my first thought was using this type of Scion for Romance of the Three Kingdoms characters. I figure at least Lu Bu, Cao Cao and Zhuge Liang would have sufficient Legend. So would Guan Yu, but he's already a God.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T05:33:00-07:00","id":646563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=634043#post634043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How far are you willing to detail? How about instead of a <i>Creator of the Universe</i> type of god..would you be willing to address someone more minor, like say...Deimos and his god of Dreadness? When I made a stab at him before, it worked out to RAW: a bunch of Social knacks or the social knacks and the well done homebrew Emotion Purview from Brent Not Broken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gods still go along a Legend 8-12 scale, but not every Scion's parent is a 12. There's a way for gods to act with a degree of omnipotence they don't usually possess, hearkening back to a Mythic Era. And yeah, I liked the Emotion Purview, and there should be something similar for Scions and Gods who embody concepts and emotions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been wondering how relationships between pantheons are going to be treated in this edition. In 1st edition it was all based on rivalry. Pantheons all seemed a bit racist and isolationist towards one another and it just boggles my mind. I mean what do you think is going to happen when you put scions into teams where they face life and death together fighting a war? Strong bonds and emotions are going to form when someone saves your life in most cases. But if scions of different pantheons want to carry their eventual relationships to the point of having children\u2026then most discussions got to 'you can't have dual heritage' or &quot;There is no way the head of your pantheon would let that happen..huge political mess.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still a huge political mess, but I'm of the opinion that such stories are more fun to play through than to outright forbid.<br /> <br /> Pantheons are less divine bloodlines and more socio-magical constructs within Fate, tied to a culture and the gods. However, gods themselves can belong to multiple cultures and multiple pantheons. Later, in Demigod and God, we'll detail how Scions can form their own pantheons - which is somewhat related to those Mythic acts I was talking about earlier (and that's why Crow's feathers are black).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean is it just me or does it seem strange that beings that epic mental stats and literal eons of experience can't learn to work with each other except in cases where the titans are about kill everyone and everything...and then its as allies of the moment...ONLY!!! </div> </div> </div>There's other reasons they can't learn to work together. Being a god doesn't make you superhuman, or even a super-human. To bring back the Hera example, the goddess of marriage is always going to dislike illegitimate children, even if they're pledged to her glory after the fact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T05:47:59-07:00","id":646575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GhanjRho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=646349#post646349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What all can you share about the reincarnation-type Scions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dead Gods, dead heroes. It's really more about the playstyle you want to have than anything specific. The process has to be catalyzed by a shade, or it has to be helped along by various death gods if the deceased wasn't a divinity to begin with. Dead-dead gods might fall into this incarnation by default, but heroes have to undertake a process before they're reborn.<br /> <br /> (Reborn as babies, with no memories of what happened.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do they get a Visitation? Birthrights? Is there some recommended minimum level of fame and Legend they should have achieved. Not gonna lie, my first thought was using this type of Scion for Romance of the Three Kingdoms characters. I figure at least Lu Bu, Cao Cao and Zhuge Liang would have sufficient Legend. So would Guan Yu, but he's already a God. </div> </div> </div>They do get a Visitation (potentially from themselves), but they don't usually start with Birthrights, having to make do on loaned pieces of power. Old Birthrights of their previous life resonate with their divine souls, though.<br /> <br /> Zhuge Liang would've been a sorcerer, though yeah, he's a good target for reincarnation as a Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T07:56:20-07:00","id":646690,"title":"","content":"Now I have an image of Heracles going to see Hades to get a few souls released from the Underworld; a few decades later, a reincarnated Jason and his new Argonauts sail again\u2026<br /> <br /> (I'm really liking the notion of playing a reborn hero of legend.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T08:06:45-07:00","id":646722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=646690#post646690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I have an image of Heracles going to see Hades to get a few souls released from the Underworld; a few decades later, a reincarnated Jason and his new Argonauts sail again\u2026<br /> <br /> (I'm really liking the notion of playing a reborn hero of legend.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. It also fills in a gap from the prior edition - a lot of things made sense as sources for heroes, but did not make any sense as actual gods. Arthur (of Wales/England/France) comes to mind, here, as do the likes of Siegfried, Beowulf, etc. Jason's Argonauts returned sounds like an awesome campaign seed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","name":"Lokisenna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T10:33:28-07:00","id":646934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokisenna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=646722#post646722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed. It also fills in a gap from the prior edition - a lot of things made sense as sources for heroes, but did not make any sense as actual gods. Arthur (of Wales/England/France) comes to mind, here, as do the likes of Siegfried, Beowulf, etc. Jason's Argonauts returned sounds like an awesome campaign seed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell it makes the game even easier to pitch in some places. I mean look at the list of Fate/Stay <a href=\"http://typemoon.wikia.com/wiki/Servant#Known_Servants\" target=\"_blank\">Servants</a>. Are plenty of heroes right there.<br /> <br /> Oh is Legend a thing that can be bought with XP or more of a GM assigned level-up?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":461,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","user":"KingCarnival","date":". 08-31-2015, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T11:45:35-07:00","id":647022,"title":"","content":"Question , which has been nagging me for some time. Will Legend/Fate stay tied to the story first, or will it change into something else?<br /> edit: By which mean. Story told by people in the setting about the PC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6491,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","user":"zorb42","date":". 08-31-2015, 02:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T11:56:53-07:00","id":647024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=646934#post646934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh is Legend a thing that can be bought with XP or more of a GM assigned level-up?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Story told by people in the setting about the PC.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not purchased with XP, but it's fulfilled by hitting story milestones and (very loosely) tied to XP expenditures. Fate is both a game mechanic and an in-universe thing, but Legend is representative of a thing in the setting - i.e. nobody crushes their scouter and goes HE'S OVER LEGEND 9!!!!!!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T12:43:03-07:00","id":647103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pantheons are less divine bloodlines and more socio-magical constructs within Fate, tied to a culture and the gods. However, gods themselves can belong to multiple cultures and multiple pantheons. Later, in Demigod and God, we'll detail how Scions can form their own pantheons - which is somewhat related to those Mythic acts I was talking about earlier (and that's why Crow's feathers are black). </div> </div> </div>That post raised a question for me.<br /> IS it possible that a god is married in one pantheon to another god and in another pantheon the same god is married to a different god?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T13:53:34-07:00","id":647159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=647103#post647103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That post raised a question for me.<br /> IS it possible that a god is married in one pantheon to another god and in another pantheon the same god is married to a different god?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you think of a case in mythology?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T09:10:36-07:00","id":648078,"title":"","content":"Mithras comes to mind. The Greeks identified him with Helios (spouces: Perse &amp; Clymene). Mitra the Vedic god (who was in my readings conflated/indestinguisable from Varuna) had a spouce of Varuni. I know the Romans identified him with Sol Invictus..not sure who he was married to though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T09:32:47-07:00","id":648093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=648078#post648078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mithras comes to mind. The Greeks identified him with Helios (spouces: Perse &amp; Clymene). Mitra the Vedic god (who was in my readings conflated/indestinguisable from Varuna) had a spouce of Varuni. I know the Romans identified him with Sol Invictus..not sure who he was married to though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's a regular Mithraic mystery, isn't it?<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> In all seriousness, I haven't given it a ton of thought, but I might have to now. I'd suspect that it'd be treated like any mantle difference, in that the god is that thing when he's got that hat on and different when he doesn't, so the spouse is treated as estranged sometimes and sometimes not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T10:31:05-07:00","id":648130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=647159#post647159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you think of a case in mythology?</div> </div> </div> </div>I THINK I heard something like it with a few asiatic gods but not 100% on it (I know more about the norse and the greek and and japanese than the chinese ones)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T15:13:42-07:00","id":648402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=648078#post648078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mithras comes to mind. The Greeks identified him with Helios (spouces: Perse &amp; Clymene). Mitra the Vedic god (who was in my readings conflated/indestinguisable from Varuna) had a spouce of Varuni. I know the Romans identified him with Sol Invictus..not sure who he was married to though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Some of that could be false conflation though rather than a god existing in multiple Pantheons, like Hermes/Mercury being identified with Odin and Thoth.<br /> <br /> I am curious to see how the Roman Mithras is treated. Did the Yazata Mithra pick up a Roman following? And is he the same deity that amongst the Devata is Mitra?<br /> <br /> Which in turn raises the question if the Daeva Indra is a distinct being loyal to Ahirman, or if that's just Yazata slander against the Deva Indra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-01-2015, 06:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T18:18:26-07:00","id":648494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=648130#post648130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I THINK I heard something like it with a few asiatic gods but not 100% on it (I know more about the norse and the greek and and japanese than the chinese ones)</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's one example:<br /> <br /> According to the Canaanites, Astarte is married to Baal, while Anat may or may not have been married to Baal as well. According to the Egyptians, Astarte and Anat were married off to Set by their father, Ra, as a sort of consolation prize after he lost the trial against Horus.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T23:31:58-07:00","id":648599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=648402#post648402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am curious to see how the Roman Mithras is treated. Did the Yazata Mithra pick up a Roman following? And is he the same deity that amongst the Devata is Mitra?<br /> <br /> Which in turn raises the question if the Daeva Indra is a distinct being loyal to Ahirman, or if that's just Yazata slander against the Deva Indra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neall's previously said that Mithra belongs both to the Persian and Roman pantheons. No word yet on whether he's a member of the Devata.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T11:58:46-07:00","id":649157,"title":"","content":"The Yoruba/Voodoo pantheons come to my mind for this Who's Married to Whom question, especially when it comes to Ogoun / Ogun.<br /> <br /> In Haitian Vodou, Ogoun Feray is married to Erzulie Freda. In Yoruba, Ogun was married to Oya (but she left him for Chango), and in some stories I've read he is still married to Oshun (who is stepping out on him to see Chango too)<br /> <br /> I look forward to seeing how THAT mess gets handled. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2789-laume78","name":"laume78","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T06:41:47-07:00","id":651097,"title":"","content":"One thing I just remembered. Is there also a plan to handle kami that came into existence becaues of objects?<br /> Like for example common myths about a teacup becoming one/getting a kami?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T19:35:59-07:00","id":651983,"title":"","content":"In a battle between a hero and a demigod or a demigod vs a god or a hero vs a god, is it possible for the weaker side to win or at least to have a proper figth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T21:59:28-07:00","id":653501,"title":"","content":"I don't remember if it's been asked, but will a focused Animal purview return?<br /> ...<br /> I really want to make a Son of Tyr with Animal (platypus)...what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7395,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7395-meribson","user":"Meribson","date":". 09-06-2015, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7395-meribson","name":"Meribson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7395_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T17:46:59-07:00","id":654597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meribson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=653501#post653501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't remember if it's been asked, but will a focused Animal purview return?<br /> ...<br /> I really want to make a Son of Tyr with Animal (platypus)...what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I think Animal (something) is way too narrow to be a good purview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T18:37:57-07:00","id":655769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=654597#post654597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I think Animal (something) is way too narrow to be a good purview.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I completely agree with you. I think that instead of Animal [Species] Animal should be Animal [Genus]. I mean really is it so much more powerful if you can talk to a yorkie, a jackal and a dingo? They all have about the same stats...and they are all about Int 1-2 creatures. If you had purview over a genus you may actually get some use out of your ability if you do any kind of travelling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T23:40:48-07:00","id":656127,"title":"","content":"I think it makes more sense to focus on Either taking on the aspects of a single animal (internal power) or the ability to influence animals in general. I'm hard pressed to find a Deity who's use of Animal Purview wouldn't fall into one or the other and it makes it actually useful regardless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T00:48:52-07:00","id":656195,"title":"","content":"In gameplay we use a houserule for Animal. For those uses where extra dice or use are awarded (such as Animal Aspect) a Scion who specialises in a given animal (like Ravens) gets the full bonus. Scions who specialise in a broad category (such as Birds) get half (round up) and those who don't specialise and can operate with all animals get a quarter (rounded up). It's not seen as a punishment for the broader users but as a reward for specialisers who know their chosen animal in and out. Seems to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T06:52:34-07:00","id":656472,"title":"","content":"Pantheons. Do they happen organically or is there a specific type of work that goes into the founding of one? Are there requirements for being a member of a pantheon; i.e. knowledge of a secret handshake, annual dues, etc... Or can anyone join? like-minded individuals, those with similar virtues and/or goals. If it is one way over the other, what is the universe's grand-design in making it that way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2692-captain-morganism","name":"Captain Morganism","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2692_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T13:48:58-07:00","id":656872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=655769#post655769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I completely agree with you. I think that instead of Animal [Species] Animal should be Animal [Genus]. I mean really is it so much more powerful if you can talk to a yorkie, a jackal and a dingo? They all have about the same stats...and they are all about Int 1-2 creatures. If you had purview over a genus you may actually get some use out of your ability if you do any kind of travelling.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That does raise some interesting questions. I guess it makes sense Athena gets to trump Artemis when the Animal both are exerting domain over is an owl - or Poseidon trump her when its a horse - but Artemis still has more pull in both cases than... say.... Hermes would.<br /> <br /> An Animal generalist should also be able to have specific favored animals of course - like Artemis has the &quot;specific&quot; bonuses with hinds and canines - but has the &quot;general&quot; level with all other animals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T16:08:24-07:00","id":657124,"title":"","content":"I can see that I'm apparently in a minority in that I like the way that the Animal purview was set up. It made me think of a god's totem animal. And I couldn't think of a single god that I knew of that had that kind of power over all forms of animal life. I saw the limitation as something that you chose to work with when you took the power.<br /> <br /> Like all of the characters I built (but didn't get to play) that had extinct animals as the focus of their Animal purview. It was intended to be something that paid off further down the road, but I recognized that I wasn't going to get any use out of it until Legend 4. It'd be the same basic thing with the Australian son of Tyr. Sure platypi are somewhat...rare everywhere else in the world but it was a part of the character that I'd be building.<br /> <br /> It's the same thing when I build D&amp;D/Pathfinder characters and built them with below optimum abilities, I don't care if their utility suffers if it fits the character that I am working with.<br /> <br /> (In case you hadn't noticed, I am most assuredly NOT a munchkin.)<br /> <br /> *EDIT*: There's a blog post over on JSR that explains it better than I can: <a href=\"http://johnsscionresources.blogspot.com/2012/05/meet-my-better-half.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://johnsscionresources.blogspot....tter-half.html</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7395,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7395-meribson","user":"Meribson","date":".  adding blog post 09-08-2015, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7395-meribson","name":"Meribson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7395_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T21:12:59-07:00","id":657361,"title":"","content":"The problem is Meribson, as the power hierarchy worked out, that's not how it ended up playing out. The Purview became universal at the higher levels, but it was only the gods with SPECIFIC animal associations who favored the Purview and thus had the Purview at said levels. Meanwhile Artemis, a deity more tied to animals than any other Olympian, didn't favor the purview in the first place.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T08:35:57-07:00","id":657918,"title":"","content":"Animal left out things that gods could do in myths or made them really really hard to do and required intense investment. Not allowing PCs' to do things gods could do in myths is the cardinal sin of the Purview. Oh, and being COMPLETELY unbalanced in both directions (uselessness and omni-powerful) depending on the choices made. <br /> <br /> Loki (who also doesn't have Animal) changed into a mare and gadfly. So he had to have Animal (Flies) and Animal (Horses) or one or the other at extremely high levels to accomplish that. <br /> <br /> Zeus could be just about anything he wanted, so long as it ended up getting him into someone's pants. Did Zeus have Animal (Eagle) at mega-high levels? Or does the Animal Purview once again fall flat on it's face once again.<br /> <br /> Odin doesn't pass on Animal (Raven) or Animal (Wolf), so, does he have them? (Dear gods, I knoe If not, can he talk to Freki and Geri? Can he talk to Hugin and Munin? (I know literature has his ravens mouthing off like they were Heckle and Jeckle, but are there myths that state they are smart-asses?). Sure they (along with Sleipner) could be just Creatures that tag along with him and he has no more way of communicating with them than a being with really really high stats could communicate with his horse, his doggies and his pet birds. Or part of their powers as being Creatures could be that they can talk (animals can talk in Norse mythology after all, if you have the wherewithal to understand them) or communicate with Odin with some kind of D&amp;D Ranger-like animal empathy, but how does that fare as you start applying it outwards. Is it the same for Freya and her cats? How about Freyr and his horses? How about the Morrigan and her ravens? <br /> <br /> And all that is staying with the friendly/familiar European pantheons. Is it meaningful that Thoth has an ibis or baboon head or is that just a investment in off-kilter Appearance Knacks? Okay, I might buy that, but what about Bastet? Jumping all the way around the world and out of the pantheons &quot;cool&quot; enough to get a write up, What about Tangaroa and his kids from Aotearoa (New Zealand). He has all sea life and some connections to a bunch of land-living creatures, which his kids parse up into sub-groups. What animal is his &quot;totem&quot;? (We went for a Cthulhu feel and had it be octopi, based on twisting around some myths and the general coolness of being the son of the octopus/squid god of the abyssal deeps). And why can't he affect any of the animals that belong to the other Maori gods? Is he just being polite? <br /> <br /> The Animal Purview really only works conceptually (not mind you from a crunch standpoint) for completely totemic deities, like the various raven or coyote gods scattered across the North American pantheons. Which leaves a lot of the &quot;gods associated with animals who turn into them, talk to them, rule over them, but AREN'T actually them&quot; out of the picture","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T08:53:16-07:00","id":657934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=651097#post651097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I just remembered. Is there also a plan to handle kami that came into existence becaues of objects?<br /> Like for example common myths about a teacup becoming one/getting a kami?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tsukumogami are probably more along the lines of mythical creatures like satyrs and centaurs than gods proper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T21:14:12-07:00","id":658875,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this has been answered or not, or if you will, but I searched through the linked website for keywords I thought might ping it, didn't find anything. Will the powers like Animal and War work like Mage Spheres, be closer to Scion 1 or something else entirely?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2448-dante","name":"Dante","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T22:58:54-07:00","id":658978,"title":"","content":"Just curious Neall (and forgive me if this has already been asked) but who is your favorite god/who would you want to be a scion of, and why?<br /> <br /> Edit: In fact, I'd be interested to hear other people's answer to this question as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T04:11:24-07:00","id":659224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheGraySoul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=658978#post658978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just curious Neall (and forgive me if this has already been asked) but who is your favorite god/who would you want to be a scion of, and why?<br /> <br /> Edit: In fact, I'd be interested to hear other people's answer to this question as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm my personal case: Lugh of the Tuatha D\u00e9 Dannan, hands down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T09:41:49-07:00","id":659456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheGraySoul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=658978#post658978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just curious Neall (and forgive me if this has already been asked) but who is your favorite god/who would you want to be a scion of, and why?<br /> <br /> Edit: In fact, I'd be interested to hear other people's answer to this question as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are these scions that function in the universe defined by the current Scion rules? Because that matters a lot in my choice. Some gods that might be very fun to be the kind of are bad choices because game doesn't really support their Purview. Like, say, any crafter deity....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 09-10-2015, 09:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T16:03:02-07:00","id":659990,"title":"","content":"Not sure it\u2019s been asked of you Neal, although I think it has been mentioned before. Is there going to be any rules, boons for vampire style combination boons (e.g. she who has Earth and Fire could become a volcano goddess and control magma?)<br /> <br /> As to my favourite god...completely depends on the pantheon and even then I can\u2019t always narrow it down. [Greeks: Favourite/Scion of: Nike/Zeus, Japanese: Favourite/Scion of: Hachiman, Susano, Norse: Favourite/Scion of: Thor/Thor, Egyptians: Favourite/Scion of: Set/Set..it keeps going on and on]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T18:55:27-07:00","id":662506,"title":"","content":"This goes to Neall as well as anyone else working on the project.<br /> <br /> What is your diet? Is it true that Chinese food is one of your main food groups or is it pizza?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T03:24:54-07:00","id":664076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=662506#post662506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This goes to Neall as well as anyone else working on the project.<br /> <br /> What is your diet? Is it true that Chinese food is one of your main food groups or is it pizza?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ... Should we take this as maybe an inside joke which i don't understand at all, or directly into troll territory and ignore subsequently?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T07:45:25-07:00","id":664301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=658875#post658875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if this has been answered or not, or if you will, but I searched through the linked website for keywords I thought might ping it, didn't find anything. Will the powers like Animal and War work like Mage Spheres, be closer to Scion 1 or something else entirely?</div> </div> </div> </div>Current models are closer to Blood Sorcery in Requiem, but you're actually on the right track, or at least following our months-old tracks. If all goes well, they should interface cleanly with Fatebinding and Paths.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheGraySoul</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just curious Neall (and forgive me if this has already been asked) but who is your favorite god/who would you want to be a scion of, and why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Either Lugh, like Phersus, or the Dagda, mantled as the Red Man of All Knowledge. In fact, while I've mentioned it before, the Origins signature character is a Scion of the Dagda.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are these scions that function in the universe defined by the current Scion rules? Because that matters a lot in my choice. Some gods that might be very fun to be the kind of are bad choices because game doesn't really support their Purview. Like, say, any crafter deity....</div> </div> </div> </div>Crafter and Creation deities are tough in oScion, it's true. I asked one of the Sardonyx authors to prototype out a Scion-style crafting subsystem and she went absolutely bananas and did a fabulous job above and beyond the expectations and mandate I set for her. I expect that fertility, creation, and crafter deities will have a lot more to do as an integral part of a band.<br /> <br /> Oh, and to reinforce someone above - yeah, emotional deities can be a thing, though it's filtered through Callings and Legend. Brigid's association with fire as inspiration and poetic elegance is such.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure it\u2019s been asked of you Neal, although I think it has been mentioned before. Is there going to be any rules, boons for vampire style combination boons (e.g. she who has Earth and Fire could become a volcano goddess and control magma?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you can combine otherwise distinct Purview expressions like that, expressed through motifs granted via Birthrights, Knacks, Callings, Paths and Legend. I know that seems like a lot, but you can affect how you do things a lot of ways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is your diet? Is it true that Chinese food is one of your main food groups or is it pizza?</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally try to get a good amount of greens in my diet, though I'm more of a lean red meat fan than perhaps is good for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T09:16:47-07:00","id":664450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=664301#post664301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Current models are closer to Blood Sorcery in Requiem, but you're actually on the right track, or at least following our months-old tracks. If all goes well, they should interface cleanly with Fatebinding and Paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if the tiers will factor in. I've always thought that an appropriate model would be for heroes to have mythic tools that let them channel the Purviews in specific ways suitable to the relic in question; for demigods to internalize aspects of the Purviews as discrete internal powers, and for gods to be able to command the Purviews in a manner not unlike Mage's Spheres. That is, the higher you go, the fewer restrictions you have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T10:27:11-07:00","id":664533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=664450#post664450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if the tiers will factor in. I've always thought that an appropriate model would be for heroes to have mythic tools that let them channel the Purviews in specific ways suitable to the relic in question; for demigods to internalize aspects of the Purviews as discrete internal powers, and for gods to be able to command the Purviews in a manner not unlike Mage's Spheres. That is, the higher you go, the fewer restrictions you have.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a bad supposition!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T01:59:22-07:00","id":668006,"title":"","content":"I wanted to ask something regarding goddesses. A friend of mine was rather annoyed with Scion 1e due to its tendency to be short on granting physical Epic Attributes (aside, occasionally, from Epic Dexterity) to the purviews of female deities, even when those goddesses were explicitly war goddesses storied for battle prowess.<br /> <br /> Now, I know that the StoryPath system is going to be doing away with Epic Attributes in favor of its own method of representing capabilities of that magnitude, but even so--will we get to see the ladies kick a little bit more ass directly in this edition than last time? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T08:17:45-07:00","id":668273,"title":"","content":"Oh, yes. Women of all types will kick ass in the new edition. Moreover, even if your divine mother really doesn't support a lot of fighting - like, say, Hera, who got Athena to do her spear-throwing for her - that doesn't mean a Scion of Hera wouldn't herself have significant battle prowess. Ancestry in this edition gives you a bonus and a boost during your early years, but doesn't influence or constrain development over the course of the character's life, like Favored Purviews and Attributes did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T10:23:37-07:00","id":668437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=668273#post668273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, yes. Women of all types will kick ass in the new edition. Moreover, even if your divine mother really doesn't support a lot of fighting - like, say, Hera, who got Athena to do her spear-throwing for her - that doesn't mean a Scion of Hera wouldn't herself have significant battle prowess. Ancestry in this edition gives you a bonus and a boost during your early years, but doesn't influence or constrain development over the course of the character's life, like Favored Purviews and Attributes did.</div> </div> </div> </div>First? This sounds awesome.<br /> <br /> Second? Minor nitpick? Hera has two myths where she lays some smack down all by herself. Trojan War: literally smacked Artemis down with her own bow. Indian War: actually demonstrated command over the Sky/Thunder Purview to smack down Artemis AGAIN.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T11:49:48-07:00","id":668550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=668437#post668437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second? Minor nitpick? Hera has two myths where she lays some smack down all by herself. Trojan War: literally smacked Artemis down with her own bow. Indian War: actually demonstrated command over the Sky/Thunder Purview to smack down Artemis AGAIN.</div> </div> </div> </div>What am I, some kind of developer of all the gods and goddesses? I can't keep track of every single myth all of the time!<br /> <br /> That's why I employ people to do it for me!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T13:08:44-07:00","id":668729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=668273#post668273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, yes. Women of all types will kick ass in the new edition. Moreover, even if your divine mother really doesn't support a lot of fighting - like, say, Hera, who got Athena to do her spear-throwing for her - that doesn't mean a Scion of Hera wouldn't herself have significant battle prowess. Ancestry in this edition gives you a bonus and a boost during your early years, but doesn't influence or constrain development over the course of the character's life, like Favored Purviews and Attributes did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely metal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T05:14:56-07:00","id":669558,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if this has been asked...<br /> <br /> Is any consideration being given to historical setting books? Or to a book on games in the mythological periods of the source material?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","name":"Lokisenna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T06:26:59-07:00","id":669600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokisenna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=669558#post669558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is any consideration being given to historical setting books? Or to a book on games in the mythological periods of the source material?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at the moment. It's something I've considered for later books and further down the line - a &quot;Dark Eras&quot; style book for Scion, with the Aesir in the Viking Age, or the Theoi during the reign of Julian. But that's 3+ years down the line, after all the cores are out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T15:41:31-07:00","id":670240,"title":"","content":"Is &quot;Theoi&quot; what we're calling the Greek Gods now? I hope so, as &quot;Dodekatheon&quot; was a bit of a mouthful. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T15:49:02-07:00","id":670244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CycloneJoker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=670240#post670240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is &quot;Theoi&quot; what we're calling the Greek Gods now? I hope so, as &quot;Dodekatheon&quot; was a bit of a mouthful. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>well it is the name of the greek gods. I use Theoi when ever I am refering to them in the general in my own rituals and prayers. Besides Dodekatheon mainly refers to just the 12 olympions, and the greek religion has far more then 12 gods and goddesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T16:19:52-07:00","id":670274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CycloneJoker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=670240#post670240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is &quot;Theoi&quot; what we're calling the Greek Gods now? I hope so, as &quot;Dodekatheon&quot; was a bit of a mouthful. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Also the Etruscan and Roman gods, but that's really more by default than anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T17:54:34-07:00","id":670348,"title":"","content":"Will the Kamuy get a mention anywhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T05:48:50-07:00","id":676326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=670348#post670348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will the Kamuy get a mention anywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most likely. I'm instructing the writers to feel free to name-drop pantheons in relation to the core that aren't necessarily detailed yet; the instructions on how to build a pantheon in Origin and Demigod should give folks all the tools they need to write up whatever pantheons they like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T16:34:46-07:00","id":679430,"title":"","content":"I saw in the previous questions thread questions mentioning of having purely roman gods and even Etruscan ones in the Theoi. Will you look at other pop culture works dealing with the differences in how the gods were portrayed in greek and roman myths respectively like the Heroes of Olympus book series? Second question will nation gods like Britannia, Roma and those introduced in the 1e companion book. While not a lot of people liked it that is what mythological gods were after all a representation of the societal values of the culture they spawned from. The last question or more of a plea really.....can you please have The Citizen in there? He is wonderful","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8100,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","user":"Caedus","date":".  forgot to phrase it as a question 09-26-2015, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T07:27:42-07:00","id":683093,"title":"","content":"I'm not actually beyond putting in gods like Brittannia, Columbia, Marianne, or Rodina Mat; but in this case, they'd be part of Scion's universe (the former three as Goddesses of Liberty and Scions of Athena).<br /> <br /> In this case, these goddesses get a pass because of imagery they evoke. Even then, it's mostly my own attraction to the concept and imagery, and a desire to enrich <b>Scion</b>'s own universe and show the progression of Scions outside the pantheon structure, rather than any actual attempt to adhere to mythology.<br /> <br /> In other words, those creations, while fictional, get a pass in my book because they <i>at least</i> evoke divine imagery, Greco-Roman concepts, and make a functional point within the setting. There's a strong likelihood of them appearing in a stretch goal or Companion book, so you can use or not use them to your heart's content. But no, sadly, The Citizen doesn't count for any of these things, so he's in the prior edition. He could still, however, be an archetypal god you create in a past setting or decide to move your character towards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T07:58:00-07:00","id":683116,"title":"","content":"Where would Uncle Sam fall? (I guess I'm asking this thanks to the Uncle Sam graphic novel, which leaves me wondering if he could be brought in.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T08:07:00-07:00","id":683130,"title":"","content":"I strongly suspect that he'd be in the same camp as the Citizen. Maybe we could get a Shards-like book somewhere down the road that covers these guys and others like them (such as Santa Claus and Superman); but I'd be surprised to see them in anything more mainstream than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T08:43:16-07:00","id":683210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=683093#post683093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIn other words, those creations, while fictional, get a pass in my book because they <i>at least</i> evoke divine imagery, Greco-Roman concepts, and make a functional point within the setting. There's a strong likelihood of them appearing in a stretch goal or Companion book, so you can use or not use them to your heart's content. But no, sadly, The Citizen doesn't count for any of these things, so he's in the prior edition. He could still, however, be an archetypal god you create in a past setting or decide to move your character towards.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know this point and its points of view has spawn cruel and bloody forum wars previously, so i won't elaborate, but i wanted to thank you. Very much. For the explanation and for the decision. <br /> <br /> Anyway, my question is about the game progress. How are we, in development terms? The rules (and develpment grade in general) spoilers went silent some time ago, and i'd appreciate a little update. ^^<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T17:37:47-07:00","id":683655,"title":"","content":"Since I am a stickler for both antagonists and redeemable antagonists (I find those who can seek peaceful existence and choose not to are a meaningful form of despicable), can I ask what the Titanic Virtues are?<br /> <br /> I get they're not ones that really involve being nice to humans, but there's a lot of variation between &quot;doesn't care either way&quot; and &quot;is actively malevolent&quot;, which the Dark Virtues...really didn't do that. I think they wanted to (they were always couched as simply animal-like behavior, but Malice isn't exactly a normal behaviour among animals), but they didn't.<br /> <br /> Since I am a therianthrope fan, would a Benandanti (good walker; an Italian sect of peasant mystics that would astrally project themselves as riding on or as beasts to fight wicked spirits of famine-often held to be a strange form of true werewolf) be possible to play as, and under which line (Origins, Hero, Demigod)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T10:35:54-07:00","id":685913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=683655#post683655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since I am a stickler for both antagonists and redeemable antagonists (I find those who can seek peaceful existence and choose not to are a meaningful form of despicable), can I ask what the Titanic Virtues are?</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually <i>really</i> liked glamourweaver's list from above the thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since I am a therianthrope fan, would a Benandanti (good walker; an Italian sect of peasant mystics that would astrally project themselves as riding on or as beasts to fight wicked spirits of famine-often held to be a strange form of true werewolf) be possible to play as, and under which line (Origins, Hero, Demigod)? </div> </div> </div>Origins, though they could make appearances at the Hero level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T16:01:07-07:00","id":686246,"title":"","content":"Lots of pages to try and go through and a massive list of things that have been answered. Maybe my search-fu is weak but I noticed that you have announced that 10 pantheons are in the core (Hero?) game. Could you list/name them please? <br /> I realise this question has possibly been answered but I cannot find it. <br /> <br /> And on a second thing, when are the kickstarters for this likely to be going up? I want to throw money at you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7117-smythetech","name":"SmytheTech","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T23:48:30-07:00","id":686623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SmytheTech</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=686246#post686246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lots of pages to try and go through and a massive list of things that have been answered. Maybe my search-fu is weak but I noticed that you have announced that 10 pantheons are in the core (Hero?) game. Could you list/name them please?<br /> I realise this question has possibly been answered but I cannot find it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Egyptian, Greek/Roman, Norse, Aztec, Yoruba/Voodoo, Japanese, Chinese, Hindu, Irish, Algonquin.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.ttrarchive.com/store/index.php?title=Scion_2E:_What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">I've got a wiki</a> collecting all the Scion questions Neall (and Joe Carriker before him) answered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T22:19:06-07:00","id":687942,"title":"","content":"1. Will there be rules for making firearms useful past Hero level?<br /> 2. Can we get more sample relics per Pantheon? \u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T08:13:54-07:00","id":688339,"title":"","content":"Will the Relics Rules Change? <br /> will there still be flaxible enought so you can make anything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4856-alfanumerico","name":"alfanumerico","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T11:54:36-07:00","id":688567,"title":"","content":"We just played through eternal lies from pelgrane Press, converting it to scion and using scion as our background setting. Any change we Will see Big, chunky, and large scion campaigns ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8286-plotinus","name":"Plotinus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T08:57:04-07:00","id":691321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=687942#post687942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Will there be rules for making firearms useful past Hero level?<br /> 2. Can we get more sample relics per Pantheon? \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Yes. Something like Eric's Giantsbane would be putting out the equivalent of tank rounds, fired from (and with the speed of) a revolver at demigod level.<br /> 2. Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>alfanumerico</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will the Relics Rules Change?<br /> will there still be flaxible enought so you can make anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and kinda. They're actually way more integral to how you use your Purviews and express them than previously. In the prior edition, my Scion of Lugh had a pierced ear and an earring made of a drop of molten gold cooled with purified water that gave him access to Sun, Fire, and Water.<br /> <br /> It's a neat piece of fiction, if I do say so myself, but it was purely to enable access to those Purviews. In this edition, his relic would probably cost a little less than standard, because it doesn't actually provide a method by which to express your Purviews except via very subtle effects. Eric's Giantsbane, by contrast, shoots lightning and drowns out sound with thunder, and could - as Eric grows in power - make really broad, destructive changes to weather conditions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Plotinus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We just played through eternal lies from pelgrane Press, converting it to scion and using scion as our background setting. Any change we Will see Big, chunky, and large scion campaigns ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's my hope to do so, yes, as books subsequent to the cores. Something like Eternal Lies or the Dracula Dossier from Pelgrane are two good examples of what I'd like to do; probably something to do with the Keepers of the World, who are my very favorite antagonist group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T13:59:21-07:00","id":691691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=691321#post691321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Yes. Something like Eric's Giantsbane would be putting out the equivalent of tank rounds, fired from (and with the speed of) a revolver at demigod level.<br /> <br /> Eric's Giantsbane, by contrast, shoots lightning and drowns out sound with thunder, and could - as Eric grows in power - make really broad, destructive changes to weather conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is awesome to hear. Never really cared for guns myself but I'm sure that will make many happy. <br /> <br /> Does this ideology also apply to the other Birthrights? Most Followers/Creatures became obsolete around Demigod. Guide was just meh in my opinion and Sanctum/Avatar were window dressing at best. I'm hoping that the other Birthrights remain viable throughout your scion's life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T14:51:24-07:00","id":691732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=691691#post691691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does this ideology also apply to the other Birthrights? Most Followers/Creatures became obsolete around Demigod. Guide was just meh in my opinion and Sanctum/Avatar were window dressing at best. I'm hoping that the other Birthrights remain viable throughout your scion's life.</div> </div> </div> </div>In theory, yes, though only Relics are used to actually channel Purviews.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BltLUwY92kk\" target=\"_blank\">I've got some ideas for Sanctum, though.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar (which is renamed in this edition) is still only available to gods, and has some really interesting applications for play considering the mantles I've been talking about. I've been talking a lot to the writers of <b>Imperial Mysteries </b>for <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T15:42:33-07:00","id":691756,"title":"","content":"I'm going to nod approvingly to that video reference and go directly to the part that has made my heart jump<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=691732#post691732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Avatar (which is renamed in this edition) is still only available to gods, and has some really interesting applications for play considering the mantles I've been talking about. I've been talking a lot to the writers of <b>Imperial Mysteries </b>for <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stop making me love you, Neall. &lt;3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T06:06:30-07:00","id":693799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> 