Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T17:30:06-07:00","id":694381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=693799#post693799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll probably like Purviews a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Can you elaborate a little bit about that? Come on, just a little bit. You know you want to! xD I was holding myself (as again it has been quite a sensible point in the Forums, the develope and presentation of the Purviews and God abilities), but Imperial Mysteries is one of the best supplements ever made in my honest opinion (so having any of its stuff re-interpreted in Scion are GREAT news for me) and now that little tease over the Purviews was the proverbial last drop to my self-control.<br /> <br /> Also, a Scion Kickstarter was a thing already, am i right here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T01:06:17-07:00","id":694644,"title":"","content":"Hello. Just signed up. Thank you for taking the time to answer all these questions.<br /> <br /> Now I know you can't answer with exact numbers but, assuming an above average amount of delays, roughly how long can we expect to wait between each of the four main books? A year? more less?<br /> <br /> Also, will it be possible to start a character at hero? I love the idea of origins but am having some trouble thinking of interesting ways of having a band of pre visitation scions form when they are probably only at oWOD hunter levels of knowing what the heck is going on. (Complete assumption on that part.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T07:02:44-07:00","id":694860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=694381#post694381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you elaborate a little bit about that? Come on, just a little bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want Purviews to be far more flexible than they were previously, yet still intuitive for new players to use. We're trying to do this by (ironically) constraining them a little. Callings and relics tie into your Purview expression, and into the Knacks and Boons that stem from said Purviews.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, a Scion Kickstarter was a thing already, am i right here? </div> </div> </div>Not yet. Probably next year, assuming nothing changes (which it always could).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now I know you can't answer with exact numbers but, assuming an above average amount of delays, roughly how long can we expect to wait between each of the four main books? A year? more less? </div> </div> </div>Assuming an above average amount of delays, I'd like there to be 9 months between core releases.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, will it be possible to start a character at hero? I love the idea of origins but am having some trouble thinking of interesting ways of having a band of pre visitation scions form when they are probably only at oWOD hunter levels of knowing what the heck is going on. (Complete assumption on that part.) </div> </div> </div>Yes, you can start at Hero level.<br /> <br /> Pre-Visitation Scions can be anything from having no knowledge of mythology and no outside knowledge other than coping with parental abandonment issues to a Scion raised within a cult who knows full well who and what their parents are to a Scion raised on nothing <i>but </i>mythology - like growing up in a settlement within a Terra Incognita, like the Nonecy of Avalon or Paititi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T09:31:49-07:00","id":695018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=694860#post694860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pre-Visitation Scions can be anything from having no knowledge of mythology and no outside knowledge other than coping with parental abandonment issues to a Scion raised within a cult who knows full well who and what their parents are to a Scion raised on nothing <i>but </i>mythology - like growing up in a settlement within a Terra Incognita, like the Nonecy of Avalon or Paititi.</div> </div> </div> </div>*salivates* This edition is going to live up the game's premise -so- much better than 1E. Thank you, Neall.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","name":"Lokisenna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T09:46:27-07:00","id":695043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=694860#post694860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pre-Visitation Scions can be anything from having no knowledge of mythology and no outside knowledge other than coping with parental abandonment issues to a Scion raised within a cult who knows full well who and what their parents are to a Scion raised on nothing <i>but </i>mythology - like growing up in a settlement within a Terra Incognita, like the Nonecy of Avalon or Paititi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone up for Marvel's Iron Fist in Scion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T10:37:23-07:00","id":695104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=694860#post694860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pre-Visitation Scions can be anything from having no knowledge of mythology and no outside knowledge other than coping with parental abandonment issues to a Scion raised within a cult who knows full well who and what their parents are to a Scion raised on nothing <i>but </i>mythology - like growing up in a settlement within a Terra Incognita, like the Nonecy of Avalon or Paititi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of, are most-to-all Scions going to be half-divine? I know a few are going to be part-Titanborn (which makes sense-so are the Theoi and Aesir) and some are sorcerers who seek to take the powers of the gods/titans, but is it possible for different origins?<br /> <br /> (I say this primarily because of my own biases-I love heroes unchosen by destiny but possess such <i>aerte </i>and the good fortune to become as important as any of those of royal/divine blood and/or spirit. And the divine right of kings makes me inherently suspicious of that ideology, only slightly quelled by the gods being right there to ask about their choice in leaders-if they are perfectly capable of giving that mantle to someone whose competence outweighs traditional inheritance and will do so, I'm fine with the idea).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T10:48:26-07:00","id":695107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=695104#post695104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking of, are most-to-all Scions going to be half-divine? I know a few are going to be part-Titanborn (which makes sense-so are the Theoi and Aesir) and some are sorcerers who seek to take the powers of the gods/titans, but is it possible for different origins?<br /> <br /> (I say this primarily because of my own biases-I love heroes unchosen by destiny but possess such <i>aerte </i>and the good fortune to become as important as any of those of royal/divine blood and/or spirit. And the divine right of kings makes me inherently suspicious of that ideology, only slightly quelled by the gods being right there to ask about their choice in leaders-if they are perfectly capable of giving that mantle to someone whose competence outweighs traditional inheritance and will do so, I'm fine with the idea).</div> </div> </div> </div>There are four types of Scions. From the Scion 2e What We Know wiki:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>me</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Be a Scion of god and mortal born, like 100 percent of the people on this planet (though I'm not sure in vitro would work, and I don't think it would, so knock a few decimal points off, I guess). Also works for adopted Scions, but you always retain some part of your parentage, even if Auntie Athena raised you and you really take after her. 2) Be a Scion created by a god from inanimate materials, brought to life by miraculous means. Enkidu is my go-to example. It takes a decent bit of work on the part of the god, even if you're Ninhursag (a top-tier creation deity), and it takes some association with mortality (thanks, Shamhat), but you're essentially custom-created by the god. 3) Be transformed in infancy by miraculous means. You must be the descendent of mortal nobility, or possibly have some sort of divine lineage far enough in your line to be suitably transformed. Triptolemus is my go-to example; Adonis would also be suitable, though it raises some questions from his inclusion in the Phoenician pantheon*. But I'm not about to limit character concepts, because clearly the vehicle towards Scionhood is <i>there</i>, so you can take his Greek origin as an acknowledgement of &quot;yeah, that's a way&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><br /> <br /> </b><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Q: Looking at those inspirations... is the fourth type a god who's died and been reincarnated? <b>(marin)</b></i> A: Yep. That's what happens when you make the Devata and Tuatha into core pantheons (with Nemetondevos as a stretch goal).<br /> Gods, demigods, and even heroes can be reincarnated and weave their Legend to take advantage of their prior incarnation's power. It's hard to kill a god (unless they're Fated somehow to completely perish, and even then it's nearly impossible to keep a good life-death-rebirth deity down, so long as they don't get killed by mistletoe or something), but it can be done, and they'll hang out in the Underworld until they resurrect somehow, choose to reincarnate as mortals, or just sort of dissipate into a shade. Their divine mantles don't disappear when they die - the archetypes and power they embody still exist within Fate, so a successor could potentially seize that mantle and adopt it themselves. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T13:13:54-07:00","id":695279,"title":"","content":"So no Titanborn or Acendant Sorcerers as Scions... but they are gona be playable at Origins Right? i supouse thats why was <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel\">Leliel</a></b> misguided ...<br /> <br /> Speaking of wich... earlier you claim Aphrodite as having all 4 types of Scions... I supouse Eneas is the Good old Fashion born and Galatea is the Hand Crafted one, you already mention Adonis as a Noble Acendant, so who is Aphrodite Back from the dead Scion?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4856-alfanumerico","name":"alfanumerico","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T13:29:58-07:00","id":695317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>alfanumerico</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=695279#post695279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So no Titanborn or Acendant Sorcerers as Scions... but they are gona be playable at Origins Right? i supouse thats why was <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel\">Leliel</a></b> misguided ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Neall's counting Titanborn as being created by the same methods as god-born Scions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T14:27:23-07:00","id":695390,"title":"","content":"Hello. Thanks a lot for answering all those questions. Could you elaborate a litle on sorcery. Is it gonna be flexible like mage ? More spell list like ? What kind of power Can a sorcerer pool, Will a mixed group of sorcerers and scions be able to fit together on the powerscale, or will the sorcerers be left behind, when the scions reach hero or demigod level in legend ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8286-plotinus","name":"Plotinus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T14:44:46-07:00","id":695395,"title":"","content":"I know I may get attacked for this but will Atlantis be mentioned at all in 2E or avoided completely?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/601-dioscuri","name":"Dioscuri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T16:28:38-07:00","id":695442,"title":"","content":"Since I finished Magnus Chase and the Gods of Asgard yesterday, I figure why not:<br /> <br /> If you could take a second crack at a Ragnarok book, what would you do differently?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-09-2015, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T16:43:16-07:00","id":695449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dioscuri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=695395#post695395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know I may get attacked for this but will Atlantis be mentioned at all in 2E or avoided completely?</div> </div> </div> </div>No attacks here!<br /> <br /> The Atlantis of 1e will not be returning, no. There may be a more classical variant.<br /> <br /> The Atlantean gods might return as a stretch goal some day in the future, but not anytime soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T00:26:09-07:00","id":696838,"title":"","content":"A question that always lingered on my mind: What about Apotheosis? Not for Scions but for mere mortals who one way or another managed to be regarded as gods? Would it be possible for them to gain legend and, given enough time, ressources and probably luck, ascend to actual gods?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T16:57:23-07:00","id":698098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=696838#post696838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question that always lingered on my mind: What about Apotheosis? Not for Scions but for mere mortals who one way or another managed to be regarded as gods? Would it be possible for them to gain legend and, given enough time, ressources and probably luck, ascend to actual gods?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Such a mortal might become a Scion through means, but mere mortal apotheosis isn't possible in the game. Mortals have options, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T22:15:06-07:00","id":698401,"title":"","content":"Instead of redoing Ragnarok, is there consideration for other books along that scope of fleshing out other pantheons? I've already done my own for the Greeks but would love to see one for pantheons that receive less love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":333,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","user":"Achilles","date":". 10-12-2015, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T08:56:19-07:00","id":698640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=698401#post698401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of redoing Ragnarok, is there consideration for other books along that scope of fleshing out other pantheons? I've already done my own for the Greeks but would love to see one for pantheons that receive less love.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly in the future. We've got a lot of pantheons to go through, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T11:41:57-07:00","id":698825,"title":"","content":"A bit of an oddball question: What is Scion's stance toward the mythic past vs. the historic past? How true is our own anthropologically reconstructed early history (for example, the work that's been done to reconstruct the Proto-Indo-European religion) in the context of the setting? Obviously, it's only conjecture in real life, but the evidence is still well-considered. Scion, though, is in a place to make statements for the purpose of its own history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","name":"Lokisenna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T12:42:21-07:00","id":698893,"title":"","content":"Any idea when we can hope for more updates? We got a few a while ago, but nothing recent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T09:36:38-07:00","id":699893,"title":"","content":"Are poisons going to be reworked and made a viable threat. A few people in our group investing in both plant and animal purviews have tried going down this path with a number of character concepts but in the end poisons basically only hurt regular humans and animals. There was no real way to eventually attempt something like J\u00f6rmungandr/Titanspawn venom level of effect and the other damage/effects listed on Hero pg 182 were weak/unusable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T19:29:06-07:00","id":700399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokisenna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=698825#post698825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bit of an oddball question: What is Scion's stance toward the mythic past vs. the historic past? How true is our own anthropologically reconstructed early history (for example, the work that's been done to reconstruct the Proto-Indo-European religion) in the context of the setting? Obviously, it's only conjecture in real life, but the evidence is still well-considered. Scion, though, is in a place to make statements for the purpose of its own history.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to give this a far more considered answer in Scion's setting chapters. However, in short? Scion prioritizes the mythic past over the historic past. Aeneas, son of Aphrodite and last son of Troy, founded the family that led to Romulus-who-became-Quirinus. The Kurukshetra War of the Mahabharata was an epic struggle of demigods in the Kuru Kingdom. The Proto-Indo-European religion, as we knew it, largely didn't exist. While the pantheons are living, growing, changing and - occasionally - dying entities, they are not the same as our own anthropologically reconstructed history. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are poisons going to be reworked and made a viable threat. A few people in our group investing in both plant and animal purviews have tried going down this path with a number of character concepts but in the end poisons basically only hurt regular humans and animals. There was no real way to eventually attempt something like J\u00f6rmungandr/Titanspawn venom level of effect and the other damage/effects listed on Hero pg 182 were weak/unusable</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't I know it. Yeah, I want poisons to be threatening, and those Purviews to be effective.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any idea when we can hope for more updates? We got a few a while ago, but nothing recent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should be blogging about the Storypath living doc, the Scion alpha, and a few other things before Thanksgiving.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T04:39:24-07:00","id":700680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=700399#post700399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to give this a far more considered answer in Scion's setting chapters. However, in short? Scion prioritizes the mythic past over the historic past. Aeneas, son of Aphrodite and last son of Troy, founded the family that led to Romulus-who-became-Quirinus. The Kurukshetra War of the Mahabharata was an epic struggle of demigods in the Kuru Kingdom. The Proto-Indo-European religion, as we knew it, largely didn't exist. While the pantheons are living, growing, changing and - occasionally - dying entities, they are not the same as our own anthropologically reconstructed history.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I expect, and of course, is appropriate. It has given me an idea for homebrew Indo-European gods arriving and declaring the &quot;subsequent&quot; pantheons to be imposters, though. Might be a decent campaign seed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","name":"Lokisenna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T06:20:59-07:00","id":700733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokisenna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=700680#post700680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is what I expect, and of course, is appropriate. It has given me an idea for homebrew Indo-European gods arriving and declaring the &quot;subsequent&quot; pantheons to be imposters, though. Might be a decent campaign seed.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's some rough edges to sand down in that approach, but if we went the other way, I think it'd be a very different game. While the mantle provides some warping of identity due to long-term Fatebinding, and while some aspects of a god's memory and history might also be altered by this effect, we've got to draw the line. &quot;A myth is a true story that may or may not have happened.&quot; And while Zeus could plausibly be Tinia and Jupiter and still be three different phases of the same entity, I feel less certain about Dy\u0113us or Dis Pater or Dyau\u1e63 Pit\u0101r. (Well, probably not Dy\u0113us.)<br /> <br /> However.<br /> <br /> The idea of the Proto religions being the original concepts of less-polished gods is really a difference in mechanical and conceptual degree than baseline <b>Scion</b>, not in kind. Turning that dial up to 11 is something I might want to explore in a later supplement for players who prefer a game like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 10-14-2015, 09:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T16:28:43-07:00","id":703940,"title":"","content":"I have a few questions about shape shifting. I remember reading that Greeks did this the best but beyond that before you could look like someone, even change height and weight, add rows of teeth and basically look like a very strange humanoid. Animal allows you to turn into your totem. Say you want to turn into Godzilla as an extreme example or another creature of myth like a dragon or a roc. <br /> <br /> Right now I suppose you could turn into a whale with Animal but there are no rules for how drastically you can affect your height and weight and from how it reads in the appearance knacks I'd be prone to say something like maybe twice as big as a human tops but after looking at Colossus armour I'd really feel the need to scale that back since Unusual Alteration costs you 1 Legend and the investment of two knacks for prerequisites (which means it is doable at Legend 2) whereas Colossus Armour is a Legend 8 minimum. I guess I'm basically asking for some structure/rules around shifting height, weight, mass and possible power gains outside of flying because that can be done with wings alone. (e.g. shifting into a dragon -strength, armour, flight, breath weapon, ect.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T20:01:10-07:00","id":704191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=599484#post599484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nearly means nearly. Which is not the same as impossible without the nearly. The ability to go up in Legend should be exponentially or logarithmically more difficult that the scale in demigod with this idea in place. Becoming one of the head of a pantheon is becoming the &quot;ONE&quot; or one of a VERY small group (like the Trimurti) that has overall power.<br /> <br /> Your examples only back up my point with Odin. I didn't say he could kick Thor's ass or that he could out-Freyr Freyr, just that, in the end, he uses his divine abilities in such a way as to maintain his central position in the pantheon. Odin is all about cleverness.</div> </div> </div> </div>While Odin is indeed clever, remember he engages in riddling contests in which the loser loses his head, he is also a God of Shamans and Skalds AND a DEATH god.<br /> After all what did you sleipner(an 8 legged horse) was a reference to? A coffin carried by four men.<br /> Doubt it? He does get half of the heroic dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T20:38:34-07:00","id":704243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=604921#post604921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Christopher Lee was a direct descendent of Charlemagne and nobility, so maybe he was a Scion himself, albeit one who never seized his power and chose Fame over Legend. As for Babe the Blue Ox, we can argue all day about fictional figures who clothe themselves in the tropes of divinity, and that's worthy of some wordcount to me - not Paul Bunyan, but Columbia, or Marianne, or Brittannia.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm an old fan of myths who has played a few Super hero games and god myth games. I been watching this and this reminds of something I had brewing .<br /> Part based on Godsend, Gestalt hero, and a little Jung. A setting not unlike comico's Elementals series where all superheros a mystic based.<br /> Where Athena asks Wonder Woman to go America to be the champion of a sister goddess Columbia. Maybe Athena is Columbia.<br /> Just ideas percolating as I read about your work.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T07:57:14-07:00","id":705066,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Neall;n664301]<br /> <br /> Current models are closer to Blood Sorcery in Requiem, but you're actually on the right track, or at least following our months-old tracks. If all goes well, they should interface cleanly with Fatebinding and Paths.[Quote}<br /> <br /> <br /> Static or Dynamic from S&amp;B?<br /> <br /> On the subject of Uncle Sam I read something about a Civic based Mars in Roman mythology almost an general city god or god of civilization and civic virtues.<br /> I figure Uncle same may be something like with a rivalry with Columbia.<br /> <br /> On the Canaanite/Elohim pantheon, As much as I would like to see something on this done I don't see how you can thread the needle without touching the ugaritic texts, Assyrian influences , Babylonian, Chaldean, Manichean, &amp; Zoroastrian influences. Then you have touch on Mystery cult influences of area on christianity. <br /> And that will piss some people off. <br /> <br /> Good luck if you can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T10:21:34-07:00","id":705369,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Chattnos;n705066]<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=664301#post664301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> On the Canaanite/Elohim pantheon, As much as I would like to see something on this done I don't see how you can thread the needle without touching the ugaritic texts, Assyrian influences , Babylonian, Chaldean, Manichean, &amp; Zoroastrian influences. Then you have touch on Mystery cult influences of area on christianity.<br /> And that will piss some people off.<br /> <br /> Good luck if you can.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been done several times with good to excellent levels of playibility and basing it fairly soundly on what myths are extant. It's not like entire pantheons haven't been published with much, much, much, much, much, much less to work with. Say, the Nemetondevos, for which there is effectively NO extant mythology at all, besides some pretty images on preserved artifacts with a whole LOT of interpolation. <br /> <br /> I don't see why you need to play around with Manichaeism, unless you just are begging to get into the issues that piss people off. It's very late in the game compared to the myths in and of themselves. If you want to play with Zoorastrianism, you need to take it over to the Yazatas where it belongs. You can separate out the Babylonian (&amp; Chaldean, though I don't know how you are dividing those two in a meaningful way) pretty effectively. There is some syncretism going on, but there's also a lot with Greek mythology as well. Just don't pay attention to it for purposes of generating a solid pantheon for Scion purposes. Focus on the myths, not on the religion. I'd say you have a lot more problems with Hittite and Hurrian mythological &quot;bleed&quot; as the temples were often used interchangeably and there is a fair bit of story crossover for deities like Hittite like Tarhun/Teshub and Baal'Hadad. The Assyrian pantheon could be distinguished from Canaanite fairly easily. There might be more problems for the Assyrian in separation from the Sumerian/Akkadian/Chaldean Mesopotamian pantheon. <br /> <br /> One big question would be figuring out how to distinguish or integrate the Phoenician. I would probably fall on the side of saying the Canaanite/Phoenician dichotomy parallel the Greek/Roman one. (Besides the fact that &quot;Canaanite&quot; and &quot;Phoenician&quot; both mean the same thing &quot;The Purple People&quot; in different languages, demonstrating a continuity of identity)<br /> <br /> Just like there are &quot;core&quot; texts that can focus/ground the mythology of the other pantheons in Scion as a whole, e.g. the Iliad/Odyssey/Annead, Hesiod's Theogeny, the Homeric Hymns, Ovid's Metamorphosis for the Theoi, the Popul Vuh for a Mayan Pantheon, the Eddas for the Aesir, the Tale of Gilgamesh (with the 20 new lines!) and the Inanna cycles for a Mesopotamian pantheon, the Lebor Gabala Erenn for the Tuatha De, the Mabinogion for a Welsh pantheon, etc., you probably wouldn't go wrong for Canaanite by starting with the Ba'al Cycle and working out from there, but only so far as you need to for game purposes. Sure you CAN try to deal with the recently discovered graffit in the Sinai waystation where Ba'al (Hadad), Yahweh and Astarte are all depicted together, with Yahweh being depicted as a vassal/lieutenant of Ba'al's, but, unless that's something you WANT to take that on for purposes of your own game. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T19:08:41-07:00","id":706040,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Ajax;n705369]<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=705066#post705066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's been done several times with good to excellent levels of playibility and basing it fairly soundly on what myths are extant. It's not like entire pantheons haven't been published with much, much, much, much, much, much less to work with. Say, the Nemetondevos, for which there is effectively NO extant mythology at all, besides some pretty images on preserved artifacts with a whole LOT of interpolation.<br /> <br /> I don't see why you need to play around with Manichaeism, unless you just are begging to get into the issues that piss people off. It's very late in the game compared to the myths in and of themselves. If you want to play with Zoorastrianism, you need to take it over to the Yazatas where it belongs. You can separate out the Babylonian (&amp; Chaldean, though I don't know how you are dividing those two in a meaningful way) pretty effectively. There is some syncretism going on, but there's also a lot with Greek mythology as well. Just don't pay attention to it for purposes of generating a solid pantheon for Scion purposes. Focus on the myths, not on the religion. I'd say you have a lot more problems with Hittite and Hurrian mythological &quot;bleed&quot; as the temples were often used interchangeably and there is a fair bit of story crossover for deities like Hittite like Tarhun/Teshub and Baal'Hadad. The Assyrian pantheon could be distinguished from Canaanite fairly easily. There might be more problems for the Assyrian in separation from the Sumerian/Akkadian/Chaldean Mesopotamian pantheon.<br /> <br /> One big question would be figuring out how to distinguish or integrate the Phoenician. I would probably fall on the side of saying the Canaanite/Phoenician dichotomy parallel the Greek/Roman one. (Besides the fact that &quot;Canaanite&quot; and &quot;Phoenician&quot; both mean the same thing &quot;The Purple People&quot; in different languages, demonstrating a continuity of identity)<br /> <br /> Just like there are &quot;core&quot; texts that can focus/ground the mythology of the other pantheons in Scion as a whole, e.g. the Iliad/Odyssey/Annead, Hesiod's Theogeny, the Homeric Hymns, Ovid's Metamorphosis for the Theoi, the Popul Vuh for a Mayan Pantheon, the Eddas for the Aesir, the Tale of Gilgamesh (with the 20 new lines!) and the Inanna cycles for a Mesopotamian pantheon, the Lebor Gabala Erenn for the Tuatha De, the Mabinogion for a Welsh pantheon, etc., you probably wouldn't go wrong for Canaanite by starting with the Ba'al Cycle and working out from there, but only so far as you need to for game purposes. Sure you CAN try to deal with the recently discovered graffit in the Sinai waystation where Ba'al (Hadad), Yahweh and Astarte are all depicted together, with Yahweh being depicted as a vassal/lieutenant of Ba'al's, but, unless that's something you WANT to take that on for purposes of your own game.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You have bigger problem. Just reading the old testament (a good translation) it is obvious the hebrew pantheon started out as a pantheon with a henotheistic tradition.<br /> Not everyone is ready to accept that. And how do you deal with the fact in Job's time the Adversary was working for yahweh yet by latter times the fall happen before Eden?<br /> And who the hell was the serpent BTW? Any connection to the brass serpent Idol Moses was instructed to make by god?<br /> <br /> Addendum:<br /> FYI I found this with might of interest to those on this thread.<br /> <img src=\"https://believervsnonbelievers.files.wordpress.com/2014/01/246da14db63537a20f5cdc6e50e38e86.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","user":"Chattnos","date":". 10-17-2015, 11:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T00:50:27-07:00","id":706442,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://twitter.com/TheOnyxPath/status/655398930054692864\" target=\"_blank\">Congratulations to Neall on his marriage.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T04:14:30-07:00","id":706615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=706040#post706040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have bigger problem. Just reading the old testament (a good translation) it is obvious the hebrew pantheon started out as a pantheon with a henotheistic tradition.<br /> Not everyone is ready to accept that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering Scion as a whole is much more inclusive than hebrew henotheism, I don't understand why this would be a problem for anyone willing to stomach or enjoy the base concept, so long as it was done well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T08:01:54-07:00","id":706880,"title":"","content":"Query. I've heard that the system won't use a traditional 'hit point' style damage system. How will the new damage system work? I noticed in the second teaser that using Medicine can remove Bleeding or Impairments - is it based on Conditions? Do successful hits impose hindering Conditions? Also curious how Vitality would weigh into a system like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/820-gyre","name":"gyre","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T13:16:20-07:00","id":707352,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> I like your graphic for certain values. It obviousy oversimplifies, but it has too. It does present some things that are merely guessed at as bald-faced fact and it's positioning and attributions are definitely questionable. But as far as &quot;big ideas&quot; it's a good card toss into the hat.<br /> <br /> However, don't confuse mythology with religion. They're not 100% the same thing. Scion is a game of mythology, not religion. Religion can be good somestimes to enhance and embellish, but it makes a hard fit as it's practice, not narrative. So that whole chart is beside the point. Who cares about the Old Testament except insofar as it will make your Canaanite pantheon bad-ass and cool? You have to pick and chose which versions of which myths as it is when you are trying to come up with some intersection of several Venn diagrams. In the end, you just have to choose something that will make sense and work in the context of the game. Trying to make a pantheon out of that chart is just hurting yourself for no reason whatsoever.<br /> <br /> There's nothing hard about making a workable version of the Elohim:<br /> <br /> Virtues: Duty, Order, Piety, Vengeance<br /> <br /> Gods:<br /> Baal (Hadad)<br /> Anat<br /> Astarte<br /> Asherah<br /> Dagon<br /> El<br /> Kothar (na-Hawis)<br /> Mot<br /> Nikkal<br /> Reshef<br /> Shapash<br /> <br /> PSP: Umer (the Word based on Baals promises to Anat)<br /> <br /> Underworld: Mirey (The throne of Mot, a city)<br /> <br /> Overworld: Lel (where El and only El can call the Assembly of the Gods)<br /> <br /> Titan: Go wild with it. If you want to make a point about mono vs. polytheism this might be a fine place for something like a modern conceptualization of a supreme singular deity. Otherwise, these guys like to fight dragons or dragon-like beasties, so Yam or Lotan.<br /> <br /> There, that took like 15 minutes. Filling out the gods descriptions would take about an hour or so and getting the first three dots of Umer done would probably take another. You could make it ready for a PC parent choice during a typical game prep and then start busting out the rest later. Sure you can make different choices and the ones I made were just off the cuff. There are definitely other workable ways to make things fall out (conflating or remixing the three A's, whether or not Moloch should play a part, should El be a god or a titan)?) and still not paralyze oneself with indecision.<br /> <br /> Or just use the one created by Gotham By Night. That one is really good (and all the fleshing out has been done), but the PSP is displaced into an externalized person and place (kinda like Jotunblut), and I wanted something intrinsic to the character (since I, like many others, don't like Jotunblut).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":".  Took out the chart to keept the post from being too large. 10-18-2015, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T22:16:15-07:00","id":708151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=705066#post705066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Canaanite/Elohim pantheon, As much as I would like to see something on this done I don't see how you can thread the needle without touching the ugaritic texts, Assyrian influences , Babylonian, Chaldean, Manichean, &amp; Zoroastrian influences. Then you have touch on Mystery cult influences of area on christianity.<br /> And that will piss some people off.<br /> <br /> Good luck if you can.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't think we should care about people who would be &quot;pissed off&quot; by a writer drawing on their own cultural-religious background (which in this case applies to anyone raised in a Western country) as inspiration for fiction. I'm much more concerned about treading carefully with the Deva, Loa/Orisha, and North Amerindian pantheons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T09:11:58-07:00","id":708802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=708151#post708151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really don't think we should care about people who would be &quot;pissed off&quot; <u>by a writer drawing on their own cultural-religious background (which in this case applies to anyone raised in a Western country)</u> as inspiration for fiction. I'm much more concerned about treading carefully with the Deva, Loa/Orisha, and North Amerindian pantheons.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the problem. The majority of the people who think they know the background of that religion are woefully uneducated on it's history.<br /> Just being from western background doesn't qualify you to speak on the topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T11:05:57-07:00","id":709043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://twitter.com/TheOnyxPath/status/655398930054692864\" target=\"_blank\">Congratulations to Neall on his marriage.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=708802#post708802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is the problem. The majority of the people who think they know the background of that religion are woefully uneducated on it's history.<br /> Just being from western background doesn't qualify you to speak on the topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll just respond with Ajax's comment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, don't confuse mythology with religion. They're not 100% the same thing. Scion is a game of mythology, not religion.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gyre</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Query. I've heard that the system won't use a traditional 'hit point' style damage system. How will the new damage system work? I noticed in the second teaser that using Medicine can remove Bleeding or Impairments - is it based on Conditions? Do successful hits impose hindering Conditions? Also curious how Vitality would weigh into a system like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The system is indeed similar to hindering Conditions caused by successful hits; Vitality, in this case, would allow you to shake off some of the more damaging hits, convert them to a lesser form, or push through despite damage (walking on broken legs, etc.).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T22:44:37-07:00","id":709971,"title":"","content":"Sorry if this has been asked and answered already.<br /> <br /> What is the order in which the content of a Scion book is written. I would assume that Scion: Origin is a little different as the Storypath system it will be based on is still in production/testing. But for future books does it start with writing fluff and lore then move on to mechanics and crunch based on that fluff? or is it the other way around with crunch and mechanics being the starting place and fluff and lore later written to match the mechanics? or a combination of both?<br /> <br /> Also I guess where is Scion sitting right now in the context of these possible arrangements?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T05:31:17-07:00","id":710420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>However, don't confuse mythology with religion. They're not 100% the same thing. Scion is a game of mythology, not religion.</i> </div> </div> </div><i><br /> This nonbeliever doesn't see a distinction. Neither most believers I know except when talking about other faiths.<br /> Otherwise I'll be interesting to see what you come up with.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T07:40:18-07:00","id":710529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=709971#post709971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the order in which the content of a Scion book is written. I would assume that Scion: Origin is a little different as the Storypath system it will be based on is still in production/testing. But for future books does it start with writing fluff and lore then move on to mechanics and crunch based on that fluff? or is it the other way around with crunch and mechanics being the starting place and fluff and lore later written to match the mechanics? or a combination of both?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, man, that's a long answer. The short answer is that &quot;fluff&quot; and &quot;crunch&quot; are generally intermixed and will coexist within a chapter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This nonbeliever doesn't see a distinction. Neither most believers I know except when talking about other faiths.</div> </div> </div> </div>A religion is a culture that preserves a faith; a mythology directly addresses the subjects of that faith. <b>Scion</b> deals with the direct subjects of that faith, although the cults and religions that grow up around those subjects are also addressed and a focus of the game (in a change from 1e, because though it's not something your characters <i>necessarily </i>have to interact with, I find it hard to believe that Thor doesn't care for his followers, and how your characters deal with their place in established religions is a <i>thing</i>).<br /> <br /> In the real world, and speaking as a believer myself, religions have a lot of cultural influences going into them and influencing the way they see their subjects. In <b>Scion</b>, while that's still true, it's more proactive because you're able to affect that cultural change yourself, and the religious change is a reaction to what you're doing. Not only are the subjects of the religions actual actors and have a direct hand in their fate, but just as the gods of Scion aren't the true gods of religions, the religions of Scion aren't <i>quite</i> true versions of themselves (inasmuch as such a thing could be created and represented).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T16:10:14-07:00","id":711395,"title":"","content":"I'm still waiting for Neall to give his full explanation of how things like Christianity's mythology fit into <b>Scion 2e</b> \u2014 which I'm mentioning <i>not</i> to pressure Neall to get around to doing so (I'm glad he's taking his time to get it right), but rather to admonish others not to jump to conclusions. For instance, it is not, at this point, a given that \u201cJudeo-Christian mythology\u201d can only exist to the extent that you can fit it within the context of a Canaanite Pantheon. That's an unfounded assumption until we know more; and I will not be surprised if, e.g., <b>Scion: Origins</b> includes saints and prophets empowered by Christian beliefs. Or not. The point is, let's not get ahead of ourselves here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T17:14:58-07:00","id":711464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=711395#post711395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still waiting for Neall to give his full explanation of how things like Christianity's mythology fit into <b>Scion 2e</b></div> </div> </div> </div>You probably won't get a full explanation until the book itself. <b>Scion</b>'s World is based on our world, albeit with subtle differences (like the small matter of all mythologies being true). The Abrahamic religions might be relatively unchanged, but the mythologies behind them would be significantly altered.<br /> <br /> If the Abrahamic faiths can still be in <i>The Wicked + the Divine</i>, I don't see any reason why they can't be in <b>Scion</b>, though I'll go into it more at length in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T20:37:37-07:00","id":711710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=708802#post708802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is the problem. The majority of the people who think they know the background of that religion are woefully uneducated on it's history.<br /> Just being from western background doesn't qualify you to speak on the topic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> All the Pantheons demand in-depth research to do well certainly. What I'm saying is I don't care about the people who would be offended by someone who shares their cultural background presenting the myths of their religion in a way they disagree with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T09:21:51-07:00","id":712569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=710420#post710420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This nonbeliever doesn't see a distinction. Neither most believers I know except when talking about other faiths.<br /> Otherwise I'll be interesting to see what you come up with.[/I]</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not so sure about that. Lots of people know the story about Noah's Ark and the Flood. It's not often re-enacted, even symbolically. Same with Samson &amp; Delilah, Daniel in the Lion's Den, Jonah and the Whale (Leviathan), Cain &amp; Abel (unless you think Vampire the Masquerade counts...), the Tower of Babel, Abraham and Isaac, the tribulations of Job, etc. etc. etc. etc. <br /> <br /> Arguably, most of those are legends, not myths, but then, so is the Iliad. Creating the world (whichever of the two pleases you), etc. may get some symbolic nods as religious acts, but, most people have a very clear, if not explicit division between religion (which is all about practice, parse the word and it literally means &quot;the way of doing things/stuff&quot;) and mythology whether or not they are believers or not. People may celebrate the matter of a myth (or legend) but they know the difference between the story and an act, unless that's the point of the exercise a la ecstatic trances, et al. , which leads into other realms that start moving further and further away from providing the material useful for the game, such as the Popul Vuh, the Labor Gabal Erenn, the Baal Cycle, the Theogeny, the Elder Eddas, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T10:15:39-07:00","id":712626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=707352#post707352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, don't confuse mythology with religion. They're not 100% the same thing. Scion is a game of mythology, not religion</div> </div> </div> </div>By definition they are two different things, but that's not something you can use in a practical sense. The moment you tell someone their religious beliefs are merely mythology you are opening yourself to an enormous shitstorm. So outside of an academic setting, the two are effectively the same thing.<br /> <br /> Like telling someone they are a re constructionist neo-pagan. It might be <i>true</i>, but it's also <i>really insulting</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T12:31:12-07:00","id":712859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=712626#post712626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By definition they are two different things, but that's not something you can use in a practical sense. The moment you tell someone their religious beliefs are merely mythology you are opening yourself to an enormous shitstorm. So outside of an academic setting, the two are effectively the same thing.<br /> <br /> Like telling someone they are a re constructionist neo-pagan. It might be <i>true</i>, but it's also <i>really insulting</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats not quite the same and is a bit wrong on both counts. Firstly, Mythology has an unfair assumption that the myths it refers to are inherently fanciful and untrue. That's mostly colloquial ignorance, all religions contain mythology (With the possible exception of some eastern faiths which are debatably a religion to begin with). All it means is the stories of the faith rather than the Rituals and Theology. At best, Theology can inform the motivations and thoughts of mythological figures and events, but its not particularly useful for a game, movie or book.<br /> <br /> Also, a Reconstructionist Pagan isin't an insult, its basically an admission that the persons practices have a historical pedigree. I think your meaning an Eclectic or Syncretic Neopagan like Wiccanism, which the former has a tendency to look down upon for various reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T12:52:07-07:00","id":712914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=712859#post712859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, a Reconstructionist Pagan isin't an insult, its basically an admission that the persons practices have a historical pedigree. I think your meaning an Eclectic or Syncretic Neopagan like Wiccanism, which the former has a tendency to look down upon for various reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it is definitely an insult. Part of the problem is that the average person does not know the difference between a reconstructionist pagan and a syncretic neopagan so they are both wielded in ignorance like a weapon and it all becomes considerably negative. You also have individuals who are unaware of the difference and will strongly object to being called anything but their adopted title, regardless of the academic accuracy of that title.<br /> <br /> Just the word pagan by itself is deeply insulting to some (and others happily embrace it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T13:08:13-07:00","id":712932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=712914#post712914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it is definitely an insult. Part of the problem is that the average person does not know the difference between a reconstructionist pagan and a syncretic neopagan so they are both wielded in ignorance like a weapon and it all becomes considerably negative. You also have individuals who are unaware of the difference and will strongly object to being called anything but their adopted title, regardless of the academic accuracy of that title.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I've come across some people on Tumblr who describe themselves as reconstructionist. They don't seem to see it as an insult.<br /> <br /> It can be used negatively (hello pagan infighting), but I've never ever got the idea that simply using the word reconstructionist was an insult.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T13:37:12-07:00","id":712967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=712932#post712932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can be used negatively (hello pagan infighting), but I've never ever got the idea that simply using the word reconstructionist was an insult.</div> </div> </div> </div>You haven't met the same people I've met =D<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T15:08:15-07:00","id":713072,"title":"","content":"In that sense Atheist, Muslim or whatever can be an insult. Professional competitive videogame players might say &quot;I hope your mother is in good health&quot; as an insult to other players in order to skirt competition regulations regarding &quot;true&quot; insults.<br /> <br /> So, considering that pretty much anything can be made insulting or given an insulting connotation by how one uses it (and sure, some topics are more sensitive than others), it is certainly not impossible to include the mythology of someone's religion as part of a game or other source of entertainment without being insulting about it - most people can realize when fidelity to matters of faith can be put aside for entertainment purposes to some degree. Simply including the subject is not inherently insulting. For instance, as far as I know the movie Bruce Almighty did not cause a huge outcry from religious people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T16:02:13-07:00","id":713140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=713072#post713072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that sense Atheist, Muslim or whatever can be an insult.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why you call them whatever <i>they</i> want to be called.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T11:13:14-07:00","id":714805,"title":"","content":"Insofar as it matters for the purposes of a GAME that is intended for idle amusement, if you are going to be offended by the matter and substance of the game, you probably need to make your concerns known to your fellow players and your ST and see how they feel about it. If they don't want to cater (because that is exactly what it is, though a very respectful sort of catering) to your personal belief structure, you need to either find a group that will do so, or not play. If the matter and substance of the game offends you intrinsically, you need to avoid playing it. <br /> <br /> If you feel you can't deal with the Canaanite Pantheon without addressing issues that will be offensive, then don't do so.... I, and others, don't agree. I dunno what Neal et al. will do about it. I honestly anticipate one at some point. Probably with a little boxed off bit of texted altercasting. The Ba'al Cycle is a really good/fun myth. There is a fair bit of other stuff to support a robust pantheon. Other mythologies with a whole lot less have been published in the past. The mythology of other more directly extant world-level faiths is being put forward (respectfully) as gaming material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T22:34:31-07:00","id":717391,"title":"","content":"Disregarding the issue of the Abrahamic religions, Neall has mentioned that Faith/Belief will act as a basically useful but not necessary kind of turbocharging for Gods. With that said, how is that going to be balanced with the fact that the Devas are basically sitting there with more active worshippers at this very moment than some other pantheons may have had in their entire history?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T22:38:08-07:00","id":717401,"title":"","content":"I agree and thing a Canaanite pantheon might be pretty nifty BUT I can also see people being wary of the addition coming off as too &quot;take that&quot; (the Titan being THE WORD or the mountain god YHWH getting a kick out of a practical joke his scion pulled 2k years ago or something obnoxious like that). As a Christian I have no problem differentiating my beliefs from interesting fiction (and had no problem with playing Demon the Fallen)... gosh I hope I made a point with this post... its late, if the post is useless tell me and i'll delete it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T02:46:57-07:00","id":722443,"title":"","content":"Ey there mates!<br /> <br /> So, some more questions to Neall. I've been thinking about it some time now, and i cannot find any references. *<b>What*</b> is a God <b>Mantle</b> and how do you steal it? <i>[I have the idea of the Mantle being something like an abstract representation/aura/fate implications of the God nature, but i'd appreciate a clean definition of it]</i> Does it manifests as a relic, that can be stolen physically? Or is it something like a metaphor, that is won after some kind of clash or competition? What would be the effects of stealing it, both to the God that lost it and the one who took it? Can a mortal steal it and achieve the state of a Scion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T02:54:37-07:00","id":722449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=717401#post717401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a Christian I have no problem differentiating my beliefs from interesting fiction (and had no problem with playing Demon the Fallen)...</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to me that we all could use a little more of this good common sense of yours, Ray. Unfortunatedly, the threads and fights over this point are always coming back, so as much as i'd like to see an Abrahamic pantheon, i think is not doable. Let's not linger on this point much more <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T03:03:24-07:00","id":722460,"title":"","content":"Eh; I've noticed that the people who say that Christians will be offended are almost invariably not Christians themselves; and whenever a Christian states his or her opinion on the matter, it's usually more along the lines of Gnomish American's perspective that gets expressed.<br /> <br /> And Neall has indicated that some sort of Abrahamic faiths are likely to make an appearance in Scion 2e \u2014 and not in the manners they appeared in 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T14:15:55-07:00","id":724129,"title":"","content":"I agree with Dataweaver but I do remember a lot of 'us' (we're really diverse) feeling like the Order (and to a lesser extant Aten though I don't get that one) from the companion was a slap in the face. Most of the animosity from 1st edition was more the fan community and some of the fan takes on he &quot;Elohim Pantheon&quot; that were... less than good. That being said, I agree that we should move on, lest we awaken the God of Flame Wars (totally writing that asshole up... maybe a modern version of Loki (if its still fire aspected) or Hephaestus.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T20:58:54-07:00","id":725086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=664301#post664301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Current models are closer to Blood Sorcery in Requiem, but you're actually on the right track, or at least following our months-old tracks. If all goes well, they should interface cleanly with Fatebinding and Paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again static or dynamic version?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T14:21:04-07:00","id":727047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=724129#post724129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with Dataweaver but I do remember a lot of 'us' (we're really diverse) feeling like the Order (and to a lesser extant Aten though I don't get that one) from the companion was a slap in the face. Most of the animosity from 1st edition was more the fan community and some of the fan takes on he &quot;Elohim Pantheon&quot; that were... less than good. That being said, I agree that we should move on, lest we awaken the God of Flame Wars (totally writing that asshole up... maybe a modern version of Loki (if its still fire aspected) or Hephaestus.</div> </div> </div> </div>There seems to be some cultural freight with the term &quot;Elohim&quot; proper, &quot;Children/Tribe of El&quot;. Though it did get repurposed to represent the hierarchy of angels in later Abrahamic religions and mystic traditions, that's what the deities of the Canaanites were called by the Canaanites. The term is used in that fashion in Ba'al Cycle. &quot;Children/Tribe of El&quot; In Scion terms, it would be what the Canaanite gods would call themselves, like Norse gods calling themselves the Aesir or Vanir. <br /> <br /> As to any negative weight to said cultural freight.... well, it seems sort of particularistic to single &quot;Elohim&quot; out when &quot;Theoi&quot; will replace &quot;Dodekatheon&quot; for the Romano-Greek pantheon and &quot;Theos&quot; is the currently used Greek word for the Abrahamic deity (aka Yahweh, El, etc. etc. etc.). Likewise if &quot;Teotl&quot; is replacing the out of effing nowhere weirdness of &quot;Azlanti&quot;, guess what? When Christian Nahuatl speakers speak about their God, they use the term &quot;Teotl&quot; as well. And so, and so on. Of course, people can get offended about whatever they wish to be offended about, but it will take a LOT of tiptoeing, in fact, probably an impossible amount, to cater to individualized proclivities to outrage. If Theoi and Yazata and Devas and Amatsukami (and Teotl?) are going to be okay, and all of them are in use by major religions followed by significant numbers of people, then Elohim should probably past muster as well. <br /> <br /> It might be a lot of fun to play a Nephilim version of Scion. (It would even be liturgically sound if set before the Flood...) Perhaps, some Abrahamic angels have been behaving very badly indeed in the recent past. But it seems like it would be a great take for a &quot;Mirrors&quot; book, with some discussion on having it be a &quot;Nephilim-only&quot; world and having a &quot;how to integrate Nephilim into Scion&quot;. Maybe Nephilim would be somewhat different than (other) Scions? Maybe not? Who knows.... Other than that, it might be easier to focus on the same core concept of RPing mythology in a modern setting that the original edition focused on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T16:10:18-07:00","id":727260,"title":"","content":"I'm not asking for an \u201cElohim\u201d Pantheon that represents the mythology of the Abrahamic faiths; I'm fine with \u201cElohim\u201d being used to represent the Canaanite deities. I'm also not (necessarily) asking for an Abrahamic \u201cPantheon\u201d, per se (if, by \u201cPantheon\u201d, you mean \u201ca Mythology that serves as a rich source for new Scions\u201d) \u2014 though, as you say, that <i>could</i> be done with the Abrahamic concept of Nephilim. But remember that in Scion 2e, we're no longer limited <i>just</i> to Scions as player characters: <i>Origins</i> will include a number of character options besides pre-Visitation Scions (notably prophets and priests) that could be tied to the Judaic, Christian, or Islamic Mythologies, and I won't be surprised if <b>Demigod</b> and <b>God</b> provide options for protagonists who operate on their respective levels but are not Scions. If the latter speculation holds true, then Islamic djinn, Abrahamic angels, and the like could be valid protagonist characters in sufficiently high-tier chronicles. <br /> <br /> As well, remember that Zeus, Jupiter, and T___ (sorry; I blanked on the name) are the same god in 2e, just seen through different mythological lenses. I don't see why you couldn't have something similar going on with the Abrahamic faiths and the various mythologies (such as the Canaanites, for the Judaic Mythology) that they have some overlap with. <br /> <br /> Finally, I'm not asking for the Abrahamic faiths to get full Pantheon write-ups in <b>Origin</b>, <b>Hero</b>, <b>Demigod</b>, or <b>God</b>; but I <i>would</i> at least like to see a text box in <b>Origin</b> explaining how the Abrahamic faiths fit into the world of <b>Scion</b>, including some ideas of what you can do with them both as protagonists and antagonists (though unless and until their mythological constructions get officially detailed, actually <i>implementing</i> these options \u2014 the protagonist ones at least \u2014 would ultimately be left in the gaming group's hands).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T16:16:12-07:00","id":727308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=725086#post725086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again static or dynamic version?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes? what I was understanding Neall to say is that Heroes have access to something akin to what Mage would call &quot;static&quot;, whereas Gods have access to what Mage would characterize as &quot;dynamic&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T06:49:07-07:00","id":728674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=727308#post727308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes? what I was understanding Neall to say is that Heroes have access to something akin to what Mage would call &quot;static&quot;, whereas Gods have access to what Mage would characterize as &quot;dynamic&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of both, but yes, this is on the right track.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T08:25:27-07:00","id":729015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=727260#post727260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not asking for an \u201cElohim\u201d Pantheon that represents the mythology of the Abrahamic faiths; I'm fine with \u201cElohim\u201d being used to represent the Canaanite deities. I'm also not (necessarily) asking for an Abrahamic \u201cPantheon\u201d, per se (if, by \u201cPantheon\u201d, you mean \u201ca Mythology that serves as a rich source for new Scions\u201d) \u2014 though, as you say, that <i>could</i> be done with the Abrahamic concept of Nephilim. But remember that in Scion 2e, we're no longer limited <i>just</i> to Scions as player characters: <i>Origins</i> will include a number of character options besides pre-Visitation Scions (notably prophets and priests) that could be tied to the Judaic, Christian, or Islamic Mythologies, and I won't be surprised if <b>Demigod</b> and <b>God</b> provide options for protagonists who operate on their respective levels but are not Scions. If the latter speculation holds true, then Islamic djinn, Abrahamic angels, and the like could be valid protagonist characters in sufficiently high-tier chronicles.<br /> <br /> As well, remember that Zeus, Jupiter, and T___ (sorry; I blanked on the name) are the same god in 2e, just seen through different mythological lenses. I don't see why you couldn't have something similar going on with the Abrahamic faiths and the various mythologies (such as the Canaanites, for the Judaic Mythology) that they have some overlap with.<br /> <br /> Finally, I'm not asking for the Abrahamic faiths to get full Pantheon write-ups in <b>Origin</b>, <b>Hero</b>, <b>Demigod</b>, or <b>God</b>; but I <i>would</i> at least like to see a text box in <b>Origin</b> explaining how the Abrahamic faiths fit into the world of <b>Scion</b>, including some ideas of what you can do with them both as protagonists and antagonists (though unless and until their mythological constructions get officially detailed, actually <i>implementing</i> these options \u2014 the protagonist ones at least \u2014 would ultimately be left in the gaming group's hands).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not disagreeing with you in particular on any point at all. I just quoted you to keep track of what sub-thread was the matter of my post (as opposed to, say, making gods more like mages). <br /> <br /> My point is that the term &quot;Elohim&quot; gets hooked to two completely different things and then the two are often conflated. The Canaanite(/Phoenician?) pantheon should be called &quot;the Elohim&quot; as much as, say, the Norse patheon is called the &quot;Aesir&quot;. The fact that the Elohim also came to mean something else is somewhat unfortunate from a Scion point of view. You can handle the the Canaanite Elohim with a very light touch vis-a-vis the Abrahamic divine, but said conflation causes the concerns at issue here. I guess you could try to dig up some other word in Canaanite (or Phoenician) that means &quot;gods&quot; and use that instead. Just like you could stop calling the Norse gods the Aesir and call them the &quot;Tivar&quot; which has some merit, as the term explicitly includes both the Aesir and Vanir. <br /> <br /> I think there has been specific discussion about what sorts of beastie are going to be available at each tier. I don't remember whether you can scale up all of them, though I think the gist was &quot;not&quot; at the time. I don't know if that has changed. IMHO, they probably should be able to.... What is Pan if not a god-level satyr? And, if the work-around on that is that Hermes was his dad, then Silenus could take the slot in that argument effortlessly. And that can play out over various mythologies pretty effortlessly as well. Garuda seems like he could be Vishnu's companion animal that reached godhood. And so on.<br /> <br /> Tinia is the Etruscan god that the Romans identified with the Greek Zeus, which is who they explicitly worshiped... Jupiter is a conflation of &quot;Zeus Pater&quot; from Greek, which has a /z/ sound and the Latin /j/ is close phonetic analogue. Tinia, on the other hand, is probably a completely different god who make or may not have anything to do with Zeus beyond the superficial similarity of them both being sky gods who liked lightning. There is still debate on whether the Etruscans were even Indo-European in origin (the consensus is leaning to &quot;they were&quot;, but the debate is still open). In which case, Tinia has less in common with Zeus than Zeus does with Thor. Etruscans didn't write down their myths for the most part. The Jupiter = Tinia equation has a lot to do with art painted on the walls of Etruscan tombs. BUT absent any real mythology, smooshing them all together into one guy is pretty much all you can do if you want to use Tinia without going all Nemetondevos (e.g. taking an ounce of some names from inscriptions, another of some archaeological evidence of ritual practices and a dram or two of interpolation from extant art, mixing them all up and adding to about a gallon of pure speculation, baking at 350 degrees for 60 minutes and coming up with a Gaulish pantheon). From what we've got, Zeus and Tinia are superficially a <i><b>lot</b></i> more alike than, say, Lugh and Llew are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T11:14:31-07:00","id":729412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=727047#post727047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There seems to be some cultural freight with the term &quot;Elohim&quot; proper, &quot;Children/Tribe of El&quot;. Though it did get repurposed to represent the hierarchy of angels in later Abrahamic religions and mystic traditions, that's what the deities of the Canaanites were called by the Canaanites. The term is used in that fashion in Ba'al Cycle. &quot;Children/Tribe of El&quot; In Scion terms, it would be what the Canaanite gods would call themselves, like Norse gods calling themselves the Aesir or Vanir.<br /> <br /> As to any negative weight to said cultural freight.... well, it seems sort of particularistic to single &quot;Elohim&quot; out when &quot;Theoi&quot; will replace &quot;Dodekatheon&quot; for the Romano-Greek pantheon and &quot;Theos&quot; is the currently used Greek word for the Abrahamic deity (aka Yahweh, El, etc. etc. etc.). Likewise if &quot;Teotl&quot; is replacing the out of effing nowhere weirdness of &quot;Azlanti&quot;, guess what? When Christian Nahuatl speakers speak about their God, they use the term &quot;Teotl&quot; as well. And so, and so on. Of course, people can get offended about whatever they wish to be offended about, but it will take a LOT of tiptoeing, in fact, probably an impossible amount, to cater to individualized proclivities to outrage. If Theoi and Yazata and Devas and Amatsukami (and Teotl?) are going to be okay, and all of them are in use by major religions followed by significant numbers of people, then Elohim should probably past muster as well.<br /> <br /> It might be a lot of fun to play a Nephilim version of Scion. (It would even be liturgically sound if set before the Flood...) Perhaps, some Abrahamic angels have been behaving very badly indeed in the recent past. But it seems like it would be a great take for a &quot;Mirrors&quot; book, with some discussion on having it be a &quot;Nephilim-only&quot; world and having a &quot;how to integrate Nephilim into Scion&quot;. Maybe Nephilim would be somewhat different than (other) Scions? Maybe not? Who knows.... Other than that, it might be easier to focus on the same core concept of RPing mythology in a modern setting that the original edition focused on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's not what I was saying. That's why I put &quot;Elohim&quot; in quotes. I was talking about the pantheons that just grabbed biblical figures and slapped godhood on them or wrote up Jesus (not particularly hard) and gave him Melee(!), . I have no problem with the Canaanite deities being referred to as Elohim, that's what they are. as for the Nephilim idea... I've had a similar one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T08:56:39-07:00","id":732362,"title":"","content":"From earlier comments about relics it sounds like they grow in power with the hero. is this 1) a representation of the Hero (e.g. Eric goes from Hero to Demigod and therefore can use his relic to greater effect because he himself is capable of more), 2) the relic growing with the character and just being able to do more (sort of like a limited npc) or 3) Eric put more points into Gianttsbane and therefore it can do more? Or some combination?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T13:19:42-07:00","id":732941,"title":"","content":"Are the cults that develop around characters decided more by IC actions or OOC mechanics?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T19:02:07-08:00","id":752779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=729412#post729412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...wrote up Jesus (not particularly hard) and gave him Melee(!)...</div> </div> </div> </div>If he had a Specialty in &quot;Home-made whips&quot;, I'd let it go. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T20:53:03-08:00","id":752947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=605512#post605512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I will note, though, that a primary source of inspiration for the new edition is <i>The Wicked + The Divine</i>,</div> </div> </div> </div>Neall,<br /> This quote has pretty much given you my full faith. I kinda really love this comic and as such, im really pleased about this development.<br /> I was already waiting for this with much anticipation, now im absolutely trembling with it.<br /> <br /> like, i cant wait to see what you have in store for Scion 2e!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","name":"Grimangel53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T21:48:51-08:00","id":753024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=619864#post619864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There was mention at some point of 'alternate' settings, will there be any chance of one of those looking at a world in which belief in the Pantheons is returning enmasse or, even more fun, has been consumed by the celebrity media? You know, articles in fashion magazines with titles like 'Konstantin reveals all: top 10 beauty tips from a Scion of Aphrodite!' or rather than doctrine/scripture/etc. you get 'Hera's top 10 tips for a healthy marriage!'<br /> <br /> I am...easily amused apparently.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> note: The Wicked + The Divine.<br /> This is what that setting might look like, and what my first campaign might look like for a small portion of it. <br /> gods i love this comic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","name":"Grimangel53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T22:18:31-08:00","id":753056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=633879#post633879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just have to note that hearing Matt Wagner's Mage series as an inspiration at all makes me all kinds of happy. I've been thinking it was excellent Scion material for <i>years--</i>almost since Hero was released--if in feel more than actual content.</div> </div> </div> </div>im right there with you, especially on the facts of WicDiv and American Gods being primary sources of inspiration. I'm really freaking excited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","name":"Grimangel53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T23:16:14-08:00","id":753095,"title":"","content":"Question for Neall<br /> <br /> the possiblity of Baal being a thing, because im a WicDiv junkie and want to see a Baal-Scion, is...?<br /> Could we possibly get something of an Angelic Pantheon? Like with the Archangels, some other named ones, and maybe Lucifer and a couple other fallen? once again, because im a WicDiv junkie and would love to have to a Lucifer-Scion, <br /> <br /> also, to everyone else, sorry for taking up a few...sections of posting! i'm a little late to the party!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","name":"Grimangel53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T08:10:56-08:00","id":761515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=732362#post732362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From earlier comments about relics it sounds like they grow in power with the hero. is this 1) a representation of the Hero (e.g. Eric goes from Hero to Demigod and therefore can use his relic to greater effect because he himself is capable of more), 2) the relic growing with the character and just being able to do more (sort of like a limited npc) or 3) Eric put more points into Gianttsbane and therefore it can do more? Or some combination?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a combination of all 3. Giantsbane will never be able to cause a soft and gentle rain, but it can probably cause tornadoes and hurricanes with enough ammo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T08:15:24-08:00","id":761518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimangel53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=752947#post752947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This quote has pretty much given you my full faith. I kinda really love this comic and as such, im really pleased about this development.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm also a huge fan of Gillen's run on <i>Journey into Mystery </i>and Pak's run on <i>The Incredible Hercules</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the possiblity of Baal being a thing, because im a WicDiv junkie and want to see a Baal-Scion, is...? </div> </div> </div>Extremely high. I <i>really</i> want to do a Caananite pantheon. And angelic pantheon, not so much...but I will, at some future Scion panel, wear my &quot;Lucifer Died For Our Sins&quot; t-shirt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T16:14:57-08:00","id":761807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=761515#post761515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a combination of all 3. Giantsbane will never be able to cause a soft and gentle rain, but it can probably cause tornadoes and hurricanes with enough ammo.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't seem to make any sense. Or are you saying that if there is a god of gentle rain, no one else can make it rain gently?<br /> <br /> Scion 1E already limited you from creating any weather until Legend 12... so this isn't raising my hopes that characters will have better 'real' flexibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T16:33:32-08:00","id":761821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=761807#post761807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't seem to make any sense. Or are you saying that if there is a god of gentle rain, no one else can make it rain gently?<br /> <br /> Scion 1E already limited you from creating any weather until Legend 12... so this isn't raising my hopes that characters will have better 'real' flexibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it means Giantsbane, the Relic, is exclusively made for causing storms. It can do anything under that purview, including control the storm Eric made.<br /> <br /> It doesn't seem that hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T05:06:50-08:00","id":762205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=761807#post761807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't seem to make any sense. Or are you saying that if there is a god of gentle rain, no one else can make it rain gently?<br /> <br /> Scion 1E already limited you from creating any weather until Legend 12... so this isn't raising my hopes that characters will have better 'real' flexibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>You also have to take into account the personality of the one using the relic.<br /> <br /> Eric Donner tends to be a blunt force of nature like his father... so when pushed to use Giantbane to create a storm... he is more likely to go all out (and maybe a little overboard) by making a torrential rain or even a tornado than he is to create a nice gentle rain. He is many things... but subtle isn't one of them. Could he make a gentle rain? Probably not... Eric usually doesn't usually pull his punches.<br /> <br /> Now another character with a similar relic (power wise) and a more gentle disposition is likely to be able to create that gentle rain... but by the same token probably can't create the forceful and destructive storms that Eric and his father are known for (and likely prefer). It is more about the story of the character that determines the limits of ones power... straying outside of that narrative is likely difficult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":2243,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","user":"Shadowstripe","date":". 11-10-2015, 08:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T06:45:11-08:00","id":762265,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Shadowstripe has the right of it. The Legend, motifs of the individual relic, and Calling/personality of the God is what alters the expression of the Purview, not anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T11:56:50-08:00","id":762475,"title":"","content":"How easy it will be to hack it for other settings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5975-odrysian","name":"Odrysian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5975_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T14:56:20-08:00","id":762623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=762205#post762205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You also have to take into account the personality of the one using the relic.<br /> <br /> Eric Donner tends to be a blunt force of nature like his father... so when pushed to use Giantbane to create a storm... he is more likely to go all out (and maybe a little overboard) by making a torrential rain or even a tornado than he is to create a nice gentle rain. He is many things... but subtle isn't one of them. Could he make a gentle rain? Probably not... Eric usually doesn't usually pull his punches.<br /> <br /> Now another character with a similar relic (power wise) and a more gentle disposition is likely to be able to create that gentle rain... but by the same token probably can't create the forceful and destructive storms that Eric and his father are known for (and likely prefer). It is more about the story of the character that determines the limits of ones power... straying outside of that narrative is likely difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, that's going back to the individual relics for purview powers that we saw in some of the rules mechanics that weren't cleaned up totally.<br /> <br /> I have say... that's silly and limiting in an RPG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T15:15:59-08:00","id":762640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=762623#post762623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, that's going back to the individual relics for purview powers that we saw in some of the rules mechanics that weren't cleaned up totally.<br /> <br /> I have say... that's silly and limiting in an RPG.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the very fact that the Giantsbane <i>changes power based on who's wielding it, as a function of said individual's own desires </i>is somehow a limitation on their versatility?<br /> <br /> I don't think you're having the same conversation the rest of us are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T20:55:35-08:00","id":762811,"title":"","content":"Since I don't want my perhaps unwarranted exasperation to be my main contribution to the thread:<br /> <br /> I've been on a Titan kick lately, particularly given how one of the characters in this fanfic I'm writing is the daughter of one <span style=\"font-size:12px\">(<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Itzpapalotl, who I am taking to be the Titaness of astrophysical catastrophes-supernovae, gamma ray bursts and the like-to be precise), so I have a couple of questions relating to them:<br /> <br /> 1) Are the Aztec Pantheon (do they have a new name? I didn't catch it) getting a more fitting set of Titans, like </span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Itzpapalotl? She's a much better devouring mother figure, given how she's an actual villain/usually malignant figure of their myths, as opposed to Huehuecoyotl, who is actually Aztec Coyote rather than the god of blindness (and has cooler minions besides-her race of giant-equivalents are literally living stars who are fated to destroy the current world but regularly get impatient and attack the sun itself out of overeagerness).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> 2) Is Aten the <i>only </i>Avatar (or equivalent-I don't think the idea of Titan Avatars exist any more, just primal gods of a concept) of Akhenaten any more? I ask because there's actually a lot you can associate with the sun apart from solipsism and holiness, and more importantly for my immediate interests, I may have to change a few points (the idea is that Aten actually absorbed all of the other Avatars so he could rule alone-including Coeus, Avatar of Light As End of Ignorance, The main antagonist is actually the Greek Titan of Oracular Knowledge Phoebe, causing a lot of chaos in her attempt to force Aten to acknowledge he can't possibly rule Light alone and disgorge his peers, getting her husband back in the process).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T22:53:49-08:00","id":762861,"title":"","content":"I think the notion of a relic being largely responsible for what you can do with it is the perfect way to utilise it. It's thematic that you can use Giantbane for firing up tornados and lightning storms, but not for a gentle rain. If for no other reason than it looks absurd. Eric fires Giantbane and instead of bullets a howling tempest screams into being. Epic and thematic. Eric fires Giantbane and suddenly the clouds form cutesy animal shapes to entertain children looks rediculous and he'd probably balk at doing it even if he <i>could</i> do it.<br /> <br /> Yes, that does put a limit on relics but it's no more 'silly' than considering it silly that you can't use a car to fly across a city. Just because a car allows for transportation doesn't mean it handles <i>all kinds of</i> transportation.<br /> <br /> Scion is a <i>game</i> of themes, war against the Titans aside. That's why most gods don't do everything relating to their purview even if they, technically, have the ability to do so. Their limitations, if you want to look at them that way, add flavour, not mechanical gimping and silliness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T23:58:17-08:00","id":762878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=762811#post762811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Are the Aztec Pantheon (do they have a new name? I didn't catch it).</div> </div> </div> </div>They're known as the Teotl in 2e, according to Neall.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T22:22:27-08:00","id":763774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Squee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=762861#post762861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the notion of a relic being largely responsible for what you can do with it is the perfect way to utilise it. It's thematic that you can use Giantbane for firing up tornados and lightning storms, but not for a gentle rain. If for no other reason than it looks absurd. Eric fires Giantbane and instead of bullets a howling tempest screams into being. Epic and thematic. Eric fires Giantbane and suddenly the clouds form cutesy animal shapes to entertain children looks rediculous and he'd probably balk at doing it even if he <i>could</i> do it.<br /> <br /> Yes, that does put a limit on relics but it's no more 'silly' than considering it silly that you can't use a car to fly across a city. Just because a car allows for transportation doesn't mean it handles <i>all kinds of</i> transportation.<br /> <br /> Scion is a <i>game</i> of themes, war against the Titans aside. That's why most gods don't do everything relating to their purview even if they, technically, have the ability to do so. Their limitations, if you want to look at them that way, add flavour, not mechanical gimping and silliness.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a fairly <u><i>dramatic</i></u> change to how your PC's powers worked. I'm really trying not to be very negative, but the more I listen about this information, the less I hear about the Scion game system I love.<br /> <br /> Unless they are removing the purview powers effectively from Relics and they'll just be native, but that isn't the feeling I'm getting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T02:19:41-08:00","id":763880,"title":"","content":"Gods, like mortals tend to fall into patterns of behavior that is difficult for them to break. Thor is a warrior, so his first instinct is to charge into battle with an enemy and pound it into the dirt. Acting outside of this is difficult for him... such as when he had to dress up as Freya to get his hammer back from the Giants... and even then, the moment he got it back, he fell back into his typical &quot;Smash everything&quot; routine.<br /> <br /> For relics like Giantsbane, they are forged with a specific purpose in mind... and are even harder to use outside of that role. Even a gentle scion who uses a similar relic to call forth a gentle rain to water crops will find it difficult to get Giantsbane to summon anything less than a Torrential Rain... because that is more or less how it was meant to be used... as a warrior's weapon... not as a gardening tool. It was meant to channel the raw destructive power of the storm... not provide food or water to a nation. It is a weapon that fits the personality of the Scion it was meant for... since Eric tends to be as blunt as his father.<br /> <br /> Now that doesn't mean that all relics will be so limited. The drums made for Amelia Battelle (Scion of Shango, Demigod pg 303) would be a more versatile relic capable of both great storms and gentle rains. This is the nature of this particular relic, to control multiple aspects of the same Purview as Giantsbane... but in a more precise manner than Giantsbane's blunt uses.<br /> <br /> While Giantsbane may be somewhat limited in its use of abilities... it has more to do with the way its Scion chooses to use it than anything else. Could someone else use Giantsbane in a more gentle manner? Possibly, but unlikely as it isn't a tool of finesse (just how gentle do you think a hand cannon-like gun can be?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T06:49:28-08:00","id":764012,"title":"","content":"Once again, Shadowstripe has the right of it.<br /> <br /> I mentioned this before upthread, but the first relic I ever had was for a Scion of Lugh; it was two drops of molten and bronze cooled in pure water worn on a leather thong about the neck, to give Sun, Earth, Fire, and Water. I still think it's neat, but I never really <i>cared </i>about the thing, and it wasn't truly a symbol of my character's Legend, the way Apollo's plectrum, arrows, and kithara represented him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a fairly <u><i>dramatic</i></u> change to how your PC's powers worked. I'm really trying not to be very negative, but the more I listen about this information, the less I hear about the Scion game system I love.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'll be blunt: there's a lot about this edition that represents a dramatic change. I have to look at the game as building a really robust and diverse line of roleplaying in the World of Scion, and it can't be built on a house of sand.<br /> <br /> The most attractive element of <b>Scion 1e</b> was the concept, and in my opinion the mechanics of the prior edition sometimes didn't enable or express that concept, in whole or in part because the system itself got in the way. Team Scion isn't so much addressing those mechanical issues as bypassing them altogether by using a new system. Everything has to be rebuilt from the ground up, so why not avoid the classic problems entirely? The way relics work - integrating with your Callings and Legend to provide a new motif for your Purviews - are another way of showing that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odrysian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=762475#post762475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How easy it will be to hack it for other settings?</div> </div> </div> </div>Should be fairly easy. &quot;Other settings&quot; is a design goal going into the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 11-12-2015, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T12:47:39-08:00","id":764314,"title":"","content":"So... I'm getting that anything I actually liked in the mechanics, I should just forget.<br /> <br /> I'm finding very little reason to actually buy a full new edition when it's only the concept that's the same.<br /> <br /> You are really pushing to alienate your previous buyers with this attitude, Neall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T13:44:00-08:00","id":764357,"title":"","content":"Neall actually explained quite reasonably why there will be changes, IMHO. There are only so many times he can attempt to talk you out of being pissed off, Arthur, when just about every post you post here comes at 2nd Edition from a predominantly negative viewpoint. We're going to base Scion 2nd on a new system. This is a fact. That system is designed to offer a play experience that we hope will be enjoyable and which we hope to build from for Scion 2nd's specific rules to both capture what we think worked in the first edition, and to fix those things we feel did not. The odds are you, or most people, will not agree with every decision. We hope folks will agree with most of them, though, and we hope that you will too once you see how they work in context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T14:40:35-08:00","id":764401,"title":"","content":"The way I see it, the problems with 1e Scion was that the mechanics of the system got in the way of the fun... especially at the highest levels when the mechanics prevented a lot of things (like being able to hit something with a high level of Epic Dex without having a high level of Epic Dex to counter it).<br /> <br /> Rather than try to fix a broken mechanic, the new system is trying to deal with the problem my having a system in place that can handle everything from mortals beating on each other to Gods throwing planets at Titans (probably more figuratively than literally... but in Scion... who knows?).<br /> <br /> In Scion 1e, you had to adjust the concept of characters to what the mechanics could allow... Scion 2e hopes that the mechanics will adaptable to whatever concept a player can imagine for their character. You want a brute of a Storm God like Thor who basically uses storms and such as a blunt weapon... BAMM! Done. You want a more thoughtful Weather God who uses her power more as a fine tool (to give her worshipers a bountiful crop as well as to defend them with powerful storms)... that can be done too.<br /> <br /> Just as one can't use a Gun to heal a person of the wounds it creates, so too will the abilities of Relics be somewhat limited in what they allow others to do with them. Yes, if you take Giantsbane from Eric, you will be able to summon powerful storms... but a gentle rain is unlikely simply because Giantsbane was never intended to be that subtle (it is a weapon of war... not a gardening tool). If you want a Relic that can create a gentle rain... why would you try stealing Giantsbane in the first place? It isn't exactly known for doing such a miracle. It would be like stealing a nuclear weapon so that you can give people a suntan. Overkill at best... but much more likely to be a disaster.<br /> <br /> Does Giantsbane's inability to function in this way constitute a fatal limitation? Not really since Eric is not the kind of Character who would even think of using it in such a manner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T21:27:01-08:00","id":764711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=764357#post764357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neall actually explained quite reasonably why there will be changes, IMHO. There are only so many times he can attempt to talk you out of being pissed off, Arthur, when just about every post you post here comes at 2nd Edition from a predominantly negative viewpoint. We're going to base Scion 2nd on a new system. This is a fact. That system is designed to offer a play experience that we hope will be enjoyable and which we hope to build from for Scion 2nd's specific rules to both capture what we think worked in the first edition, and to fix those things we feel did not. The odds are you, or most people, will not agree with every decision. We hope folks will agree with most of them, though, and we hope that you will too once you see how they work in context.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realize I haven't even talked about this in ages before this last week or so, right?<br /> <br /> My real problem is they are about to duplicate changing something so severely that it is only sorta close to the previous edition. They got rid of appearance, removed epics entirely without even trying to fix them, powers and relics look like they are going to be so different that they are unrecognizable and have changed the background setting so heavily and theme that I don't think it will even feel like the same game.<br /> <br /> This is even more drastic as a change than New World of Darkness from oWoD, which ended up being not as successful or replacing said Old World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> I am not against fixes, updates and even new ideas. <b><u><i>This</i></u></b>, though, is changing things so much that it might as well be a new game, which will probably have its own issues.<br /> <br /> Why am I supposed to just shut up and ignore things that I think are throwing everything good about Scion 1E? Or is this forum only good as a hug box? No one can disagree with the creator?<br /> <br /> Alienating any portion of your existing fan base is almost always a terrible idea. <br /> <br /> But like I said, at this point I don't think I'll be likely to move on from 1st Edition even to just use as a reference or to support the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T02:13:53-08:00","id":764791,"title":"","content":"There was very little of the first edition that was truly worth saving. I played for years because the setting was interesting, but the rules were complete garbage. You had to have stacks of paper with house rules on them to make the game playable at all, and after about the middle of the demigod tier even that didn't help. We eventually started using the fate system to play Scion because the first editions rules were so wonky.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T02:44:56-08:00","id":764800,"title":"","content":"The problem with epics was that they more or less couldn't be fixed without changing the system... any attempt to do so would probably be temporary at best (sooner or later, the underlying problems with them would resurface). Working with a new system from the ground up allows for the fixing of this problem (or more precisely, making sure the problem doesn't happen)... and to deal with other issues that the old system also had.<br /> <br /> Of course with this change, other things that used a similar system as Epics (namely Purviews that also used the 12 tier system) would need to be reworked to fit within the new system. In doing so, it could allow for a much more diverse and robust method of defining the powers of the gods... so that two gods of the same level of power and area of influence aren't mirror images of each other in what they can do. This hopefully allows a Scion of Thor to be a Storm God focusing exclusively on storms while a Scion of Quetzalcoatl can be a Goddess of Rains in general and can do much more than cause destruction with her powers. Before, the two would more or less have identical powers with the only difference between them being their fathers... at least in regards to the Sky Purview.<br /> <br /> The simple fact is, the flaws in 1e was that the system was never intended to define such characters and the more they tried, the more problems doing so caused. The fact that virtually everyone who plays the game has had to make extensive house rules at some point to make the game playable means that the game is inherently flawed on some level and needs to be rebuilt. Will doing so alienate some players? Maybe... at least until the try the new system and see for themselves if it is better or not. Yes, there will be some changes that many might not be happy about, but that happens in every new edition of any game. If you aren't game to try the new system... that is your choice.<br /> <br /> The end result is that the decision has been made. You can either deal with it and try to find something in the new system that gets your imagination fired up... or get left behind with your memory of the way things were while the game moves on without you. You are right about one thing... the new system may indeed have its own issues... but will they be as bad and as unplayable as 1e's were? Only time will tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":2243,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","user":"Shadowstripe","date":". 11-13-2015, 05:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T05:32:29-08:00","id":764875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=764711#post764711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do realize I haven't even talked about this in ages before this last week or so, right?<br /> <br /> My real problem is they are about to duplicate changing something so severely that it is only sorta close to the previous edition. They got rid of appearance, removed epics entirely without even trying to fix them, powers and relics look like they are going to be so different that they are unrecognizable and have changed the background setting so heavily and theme that I don't think it will even feel like the same game.<br /> <br /> This is even more drastic as a change than New World of Darkness from oWoD, which ended up being not as successful or replacing said Old World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> I am not against fixes, updates and even new ideas. <b><u><i>This</i></u></b>, though, is changing things so much that it might as well be a new game, which will probably have its own issues.<br /> <br /> Why am I supposed to just shut up and ignore things that I think are throwing everything good about Scion 1E? Or is this forum only good as a hug box? No one can disagree with the creator?<br /> <br /> Alienating any portion of your existing fan base is almost always a terrible idea.<br /> <br /> But like I said, at this point I don't think I'll be likely to move on from 1st Edition even to just use as a reference or to support the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are going to be significant changes to the system, yes. We need to have those changes, as well as changes to how relics work, etc. in order to make a game that is playable AND has a cool setting and theme. And as for that setting and theme, I am not seeing where Scion 2 is anything but more in-depth and richer than before.<br /> <br /> If Change in and of itself is going to alienate previous players, then I don't think we have a choice but to alienate those folks. Really, not much else we can do as the game could not simply be &quot;tweaked&quot; and called a fixed game. If folks see what we've done as a whole and don't like it, then that would be a bad thing, certainly, but I don't think that will be the case for most fans of Scion 1.<br /> <br /> And Arthur, your posting pattern isn't a discussion of disagreements in an attempt to communicate clearly your concerns, which I think would be awesome for Neall and the rest of our Scion community. If you could enhance our understanding of Scion with your posts, I think that would be great. (You don't need to hug anybody here, but the hyperbolic and accusatory way you have been posting is a road-block to having a real discussion with you). Please try that for a change. Thanks!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T08:42:44-08:00","id":764986,"title":"","content":"As far as I see it. Scion 2 tries to address the problems scion 1 had (and it had a lot sadly on the mechanical base). I'm curious where scion 2 ends up going in the end so far I'm curious about how good it will be at representing things that shall be represented.<br /> <br /> Scion 1 on the other hand had mechanics that broke at demigod level earliest.....1 epic difference made sure you were never able to do anything against the other one (except if you were VERY inventive......and belive me in all rounds I had only 1 player was inventive enough so that he managed to overcome this....and he even overcame it with EASE). But even at hero you had broken knacks that needed houserules and the heroes just felt......weak. Compared to how I had imagined things at least.<br /> <br /> For me myself I had to use relics and trick the system with them to be able to do what I thought a hero should be able to do,..... . And that started like I said already at hero level.<br /> <br /> <br /> I found scion 1 a very interesting and good idea. Sadly the rules couldn't achieve what they wanted and should. But it was a good try for a 1st version non the less.<br /> <br /> That far rulewise.<br /> Background wise I have to admit........it was not dark enough for me. At least the feeling I got was that I looked for a horror film and only got a 12+ horror (not slasher but horror). So I had to darken things considerably and also put in dark pantheons so that there is also something that leads to ppl seeing what gods can end up becoming, .... . Or dead gods rising again, ....<br /> From what I read so far from teh background changes it seems like that this time around I won't have to come up with things myself completely (including the houserules for doing so) but instead can use and tweak what is there now (dark pantheons, reborn gods, scions not from human origins, ....).<br /> <br /> <br /> One thing of note though. One thing that really got me in almost every scion round I had in 1st edition: There was just no reason for the death gods (Hel aside thanks to norse fate) to NOT allow the other gods to get back to the battlefield when they died during an attack by the titans. Also what if the death god himself/herself was killed........did he/she just have to release himself/herself from TArtarus and get back to killing titans?<br /> Ingame it was only a topic once but preparationwise I had that problem a few times and I REALLY hope that scion 2nd comes up with something adequate there.<br /> <br /> (and yepp one can call me a perfectionist when it comes to such tiny details......they just tend to riffle me^^)<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> I even had to come up with a merit system where every god that was weaker than odin got +2 merit points for each purview he/she had less.<br /> Before that I had the problem that EVERYONE wanted to play a scion of odin............","signature":"","edited":{"userid":914,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","user":"Ryu","date":". 11-13-2015, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T08:45:35-08:00","id":764987,"title":"","content":"Speaking strictly for myself? I don't feel the slightest bit alienated by the changes to Scion thus far. I loved Scion as a setting and a concept, but I fully accept that the system needs to be revised, and thus far I like what I'm seeing.<br /> <br /> Obviously, I won't have a full opinion until I've seen the finished product, but right now my impression is that Team Scion is working diligently to give us a version of Scion that keeps the stuff I loved about Scion, while fixing the rather serious problems that hindered my full enjoyment of it. Frankly, that's all I can ask of them.<br /> <br /> And making relics more mythologically weighty would definitely be an important change, in my book. Neall's example is a great one, if you ask me: a little necklace you wear strictly because you needed something to channel your Purviews is nothing like Thor's mythic hammer, without which he has to resort to subterfuge and &quot;womanly tactics&quot; in order to accomplish his goals.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T09:34:14-08:00","id":765010,"title":"","content":"What can you tell us about the combat system? Is it based on opposed attack and dodge rolls or are you rolling to hit a fixed defensive number?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9296-zeldafan42","name":"Zeldafan42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9296_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T15:34:06-08:00","id":765185,"title":"","content":"I too am super curious about the combat system. If players spend successes on Effects, can a player decide to spend all of their successes on inflicting a particularly serious injury, or split it between a lesser injury AND disarming his foe? Do they have to announce the Effects before rolling, or is it more cinematic in that they can decide after rolling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/820-gyre","name":"gyre","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T18:29:40-08:00","id":765270,"title":"","content":"Dear Mr. Neall,<br /> <br /> While not hard in 1e, will playing a titan scion be something mention in the starting books and will it have special rules? And not just a corrupted, but an actual scion of a titan.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T09:48:34-08:00","id":765617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gyre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=765185#post765185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I too am super curious about the combat system. If players spend successes on Effects, can a player decide to spend all of their successes on inflicting a particularly serious injury, or split it between a lesser injury AND disarming his foe? Do they have to announce the Effects before rolling, or is it more cinematic in that they can decide after rolling?</div> </div> </div> </div>Right now - and this might change after more playtesting - successes are spent after rolling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">While not hard in 1e, will playing a titan scion be something mention in the starting books and will it have special rules? And not just a corrupted, but an actual scion of a titan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only certain Titans, like Helios. The division between God and Titan is more political than metaphysical, but there <i>are </i>metaphysical differences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T11:00:02-08:00","id":765656,"title":"","content":"I have two questions (maybe duplicating earlier ones, if so, i apologize) :<br /> <br /> 1) will there be an open beta test of the finished rules? If so, any estimation when that will happen?<br /> 2) Is there a possibility to see who works on the Scion 2e line? Not only the head developer but all contributers to the line?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance. Very much looking forward to what is to come for Scion 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/153-ebon-wolf","name":"Ebon Wolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T12:22:14-08:00","id":765707,"title":"","content":"Would a born scion of Mikaboshi be possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T12:30:17-08:00","id":765711,"title":"","content":"System/Mechanics questions.<br /> <br /> One thing I've found in games that are meant to be high action is that players need to be both confident that what they do will pan out - so fixed ways of spending resources for specific effects or guaranteed success in certain things like 'can always land on their feet' or 'will always have a weapon to hand' so they can make sure they can do the cool thing (i.e.: not playing mother may I with th eGM) and also that they need to keep engaged; meaning time between declaring what you do and the resolution of that thing not having lots of steps with time consuming stuff going on and also fairly rapid turns so that they don't do their thing and then sit down waiting for 45 minutes for their next chance to do something cool.<br /> <br /> So, on to the question.<br /> <br /> What things can a player who is waiting for their next turn do to influence the game, either helping their allies or hindering enemies? E.g.: I spend a [name] point to [hurl a chair at the charging axeman], giving them a +1 difficulty modifier on their attack against my friend!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","user":"Scutarii","date":". 11-14-2015, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T15:58:09-08:00","id":765850,"title":"","content":"I'm curious if you intend to do anything with native Australian mythology?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T07:35:47-08:00","id":766242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ebon Wolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=765656#post765656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have two questions (maybe duplicating earlier ones, if so, i apologize) :<br /> <br /> 1) will there be an open beta test of the finished rules? If so, any estimation when that will happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>After January.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Is there a possibility to see who works on the Scion 2e line? Not only the head developer but all contributers to the line? </div> </div> </div>Not yet! But if they want to announce themselves, they can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would a born scion of Mikaboshi be possible? </div> </div> </div>Only if the August Star of Heaven deems it dignified to manifest as a human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T07:37:15-08:00","id":766245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horngeek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=765850#post765850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious if you intend to do anything with native Australian mythology?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they're slated for God's pantheons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T14:04:38-08:00","id":766518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=766242#post766242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only if the August Star of Heaven deems it dignified to manifest as a human.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Zues doesn't have to take a human form I don't see Mikaboshi having to lower himself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T22:56:05-08:00","id":766859,"title":"","content":"Zeus to Hera: &quot;Baby, I was a swan! It doesn't count if I'm a swan!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T23:12:06-08:00","id":766867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=764711#post764711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why am I supposed to just shut up and ignore things that I think are throwing everything good about Scion 1E?</div> </div> </div> </div>No they're keeping the concepts (though not cramming everything else cool about mythology out with the single plot of Titanomachy), and just replacing the unworkable mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alienating any portion of your existing fan base is almost always a terrible idea. </div> </div> </div>If it's an either/or, putting out a game that actually works and mechanically reflects the rich concepts of its setting is a great idea over trying to appease the tiny tiny tiny minority of people that liked 1E Scion's mechanics.... like, I've seriously never even heard of someone who felt that way until now.... is definitely a good idea. Please alienate away. You will attract vast multitudes more fans who actually care about gameplay, which has always been Scion's roadblock to building a bigger following.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T23:23:26-08:00","id":766873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=763774#post763774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a fairly <u><i>dramatic</i></u> change to how your PC's powers worked. I'm really trying not to be very negative, but the more I listen about this information, the less I hear about the Scion game system I love.<br /> <br /> Unless they are removing the purview powers effectively from Relics and they'll just be native, but that isn't the feeling I'm getting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's basing divine tools primarily on the thematic narrative they're associated rather than &quot;purview&quot; being everything - purview being an abstraction that isn't strongly founded in mythology. They're a tool to express a mythic narrative, not the all-encompassing definition of divine powers.<br /> <br /> It's already been said multiple times that you're going to be LESS hammered in by your divine parent's purview than before, so it's completely plausible to play the gentle-rain-divinity son of Thor and make that the expression of your purview. But Thor tools in and of themselves doing Thor-things, rather than being all-encompassing weather-control, is definitely thematically fitting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T23:36:47-08:00","id":766876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=766873#post766873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's basing divine tools primarily on the thematic narrative they're associated rather than &quot;purview&quot; being everything - purview being an abstraction that isn't strongly founded in mythology. They're a tool to express a mythic narrative, not the all-encompassing definition of divine powers.<br /> <br /> It's already been said multiple times that you're going to be LESS hammered in by your divine parent's purview than before, so it's completely plausible to play the gentle-rain-divinity son of Thor and make that the expression of your purview. But Thor tools in and of themselves doing Thor-things, rather than being all-encompassing weather-control, is definitely thematically fitting.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Thiiiiiiiiiiis! This is why I'm so excited for what's to come!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T23:56:13-08:00","id":766886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=764711#post764711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why am I supposed to just shut up and ignore things that I think are throwing everything good about Scion 1E? Or is this forum only good as a hug box? No one can disagree with the creator?</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you explain what features you think are being thrown away as you see them?<br /> <br /> I'm wondering what Neall thinks he is saying compared to what you (or anyone else for that matter) is hearing.<br /> <br /> Thanks!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T15:09:21-08:00","id":767366,"title":"","content":"Are Avatar expressions of a purview still a thing in any way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T15:22:16-08:00","id":767375,"title":"","content":"Was wondering if weapon simplification was a goal in 2nd edition? I recently read about exalted 3rd edition's system of simply having a few weapon stats for light medium and heavy weapons. Scion is fairly abstract in it's combat so it would seem an abstract weapon classification system would fit rather well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T18:59:54-08:00","id":767512,"title":"","content":"Oh cool Scion's development status moved up to &quot;alpha&quot; this week in the Monday Meeting notes!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T19:14:40-08:00","id":768860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=766886#post766886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you explain what features you think are being thrown away as you see them?<br /> <br /> I'm wondering what Neall thinks he is saying compared to what you (or anyone else for that matter) is hearing.<br /> <br /> Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as noted they totally gutted the Epic System to put in 'tier changes' that are supposed to put differences between a normal mortal and gods, etc. Weirdly, if you just left Epics but only let them go up to 5, you get an almost identical spread (0-12 vs. 0-11 autos). Oh, and the Tiers only apply &quot;sometimes&quot;. So you can have a skilled mortal beat a god at their best skill. And the tiers apply (sometimes) to all attributes, even something you aren't necessarily known for but have decent stats.<br /> <br /> Then they decided that Appearance is no longer an actual attribute, pushing New WoD's trinity type of balanced attributes (that you attack and defend with) for 'social combat'. While socials needed something of a fix, I'm not for totally re-doing attributes as the actual attribute of appearance was one of the most defining traits for a couple of my player's characters.<br /> <br /> Then in this latest explanation of how Relics work, Donar's gun 'calls storms', but <i>that is all it can do</i>. If he wanted a gentle rain or to shape clouds, he can't. Compared to the different types of actions you could take with the Sky purview previously from his relic, that's very much a limiting change. (Purview 'powers' could be totally unrelated from your Relics, but that isn't what I got from that discussion.)<br /> <br /> Then there is the removing the Titan War shades from the godly political situation because of how things are being re-organized. That kind of reminds me of removing the Camarilla and Sabbat from World of Darkness. Yeah, there's still political things that can be done, but there is no longer that strong dynamic. (This is one of the major points that people I know did not like in New WoD.)<br /> <br /> So there'll be d10, attributes and stats, powers and demigods. But it almost an entirely different game because almost everything is changed to some degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T04:41:26-08:00","id":769109,"title":"","content":"It needs to be a different game because the original game <i>didn't work</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T07:51:47-08:00","id":769241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=768860#post768860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, as noted they totally gutted the Epic System to put in 'tier changes' that are supposed to put differences between a normal mortal and gods, etc. Weirdly, if you just left Epics but only let them go up to 5, you get an almost identical spread (0-12 vs. 0-11 autos). Oh, and the Tiers only apply &quot;sometimes&quot;. So you can have a skilled mortal beat a god at their best skill. And the tiers apply (sometimes) to all attributes, even something you aren't necessarily known for but have decent stats.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pushing more 'general hypercompetence' rather than the extremes of the old Epics. Are the specifics of the old Epic system important to you or is it more the ability to make a statement about your character through their hypercompetence in a chosen area? As in, would tweaking Epics be the only acceptable solution to you or would a new system that leads to similar results in a more elegant way be fine?<br /> <br /> Worth noting that skilled mortals do occasionally defeat gods/powerful creatures/etc. often in games of wits where a mortal comes up with a cunning solution<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then they decided that Appearance is no longer an actual attribute, pushing New WoD's trinity type of balanced attributes (that you attack and defend with) for 'social combat'. While socials needed something of a fix, I'm not for totally re-doing attributes as the actual attribute of appearance was one of the most defining traits for a couple of my player's characters. </div> </div> </div>I dislike Appearance as a stat and prefer the nWoD attribute spread as much more generally useful, so many times I've seen Appearance be relegated to near irrelevance. There are often (in fact almost always) other ways of representing the mechanical effects of how someone looks in game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then in this latest explanation of how Relics work, Donar's gun 'calls storms', but <i>that is all it can do</i>. If he wanted a gentle rain or to shape clouds, he can't. Compared to the different types of actions you could take with the Sky purview previously from his relic, that's very much a limiting change. (Purview 'powers' could be totally unrelated from your Relics, but that isn't what I got from that discussion.) </div> </div> </div>Are you concerned about Donar specifically? The way I understood it is that your character has a theme and the kinds of powers they get from a purview will fit their theme. So a 'Weather' purview combined with your PCs overall theme of violence and aggression means you'd not be using the gentle rains and breeze powers from 'Weather'.<br /> <br /> However. because your PCs decide on their themes if the players want to be able to do everything from summoning mighty storms and riding tsunami to sending a single drop of rain to make a statue appear to be crying with their 'Weather' purview then they can by deciding that their character's overall theme includes that.<br /> <br /> I.e.: the use of a purview is limited by your PCs themes. You choose your PCs themes and can make them as broad or specific as you like. Therefore your use of a purview is limited by your PCs deciding what their limits are.<br /> <br /> I could be wrong though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T07:58:01-08:00","id":769245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=768860#post768860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, as noted they totally gutted the Epic System to put in 'tier changes' that are supposed to put differences between a normal mortal and gods, etc. Weirdly, if you just left Epics but only let them go up to 5, you get an almost identical spread (0-12 vs. 0-11 autos). Oh, and the Tiers only apply \u201csometimes\u201d. So you can have a skilled mortal beat a god at their best skill. And the tiers apply (sometimes) to all attributes, even something you aren't necessarily known for but have decent stats.</div> </div> </div> </div>They didn't \u201cgut\u201d the Epic Attributes system; that implies that remnants of it are still dangling around. They <i>replaced</i> the Epic Attributes system with a scaling system, of which we haven't yet seen enough to pass judgment. For example, nothing we've seen indicates that this scaling applies to all Attributes evenly; that's just an assumption that you're making. Likewise, you're making it sound like the \u201csometimes\u201d nature of this new scaling is random, leading to arbitrary cases where a mortal can best a god. I find it more likely that the conditions where scaling doesn't apply will be such that it <i>makes sense</i> for the mortal to stand a chance \u2014 <i>under those circumstances</i>. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=768860#post768860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then they decided that Appearance is no longer an actual attribute, pushing New WoD's trinity type of balanced attributes (that you attack and defend with) for 'social combat'. While socials needed something of a fix, I'm not for totally re-doing attributes as the actual attribute of appearance was one of the most defining traits for a couple of my player's characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>With all due respect, I can't say that this bothers me in the slightest. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=768860#post768860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then in this latest explanation of how Relics work, Donar's gun 'calls storms', but <i>that is all it can do</i>. If he wanted a gentle rain or to shape clouds, he can't. Compared to the different types of actions you could take with the Sky purview previously from his relic, that's very much a limiting change. (Purview 'powers' could be totally unrelated from your Relics, but that isn't what I got from that discussion.)</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll have to see how limiting it actually turns out to be. I suspect that it won't so much be \u201cmore limited\u201d as \u201cdifferently limited\u201d. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=768860#post768860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then there is the removing the Titan War shades from the godly political situation because of how things are being re-organized. That kind of reminds me of removing the Camarilla and Sabbat from World of Darkness. Yeah, there's still political things that can be done, but there is no longer that strong dynamic. (This is one of the major points that people I know did not like in New WoD.)</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand it, they're not being removed; they're just not being portrayed in the same absolute \u201cGods good; Titans bad\u201d black-and-white morality that 1e presented. That leads to a <i>richer</i> set of possibilities, not a poorer one. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=768860#post768860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there'll be d10, attributes and stats, powers and demigods. But it almost an entirely different game because almost everything is changed to some degree.</div> </div> </div> </div>You forgot to say \u201cYMMV\u201d. You're entitled to your opinion; but it's exactly that: <i>your opinion</i>, not objective truth. And please don't claim to speak for fans of Scion 1e; I'd wager than most of us are fans of Scion 1e. In terms of concept, at least; as Resplendent Fire pointed out, the mechanics of 1e were\u2026 problematic. <br /> <br /> And finally: please bear in mind that 2e is not, <i>and cannot be</i>, the Storyteller System. That's owned by White Wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T10:57:46-08:00","id":769403,"title":"","content":"I have a question for Neall. Can you purchase Birthrights with experience points? Right now there are only three times you can really purchase Birthrights (I suppose you can claim someone's relics if you kill them) But say you're Legend 10 and decide that you have found your true love and want to get your own Sanctum with them or maybe even your own Terra Incognita (if that is possible)...is this a possibility in game?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m guessing if you are having the ability to create relics with some kind of forging rules there are mechanics to get extra relic dots so I\u2019m hoping this applies to the other birthrights available.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T12:00:37-08:00","id":769443,"title":"","content":"That question reminded me of something I don;t think was ever asked; Do titanspawn and monsters and such still have trophies which grant various effects, and do we need to shell out exp to keep them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T13:17:09-08:00","id":769486,"title":"","content":"I'm sort of wondering if they intend to allow guns to compete in 2nd edition as well. I allow my players to apply a 1 dot birthright property on their firearms to make em scale to Str or Per based on how the firearm is made. This keeps it exclusively with relic firearms and allows mundane firearms to fade away like they should.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T13:36:12-08:00","id":769505,"title":"","content":"As someone who owns all the original Scion hardcovers [and the GBN expansions/rewrites], I can say that I absolutely look forward to a new edition of the rules, because the old one just didn't work. There were problems through pretty much the whole system [which have been discussed many times already], problems with the Pantheons [Aztlanti and Loa, especially], and problems with the inclusion of Aten and the Angels - not to mention railroading and wasted page count in the pre-gen story line, unbalanced NPCs, and useless skills [socials] and items [firearms]. If someone was able to make it work, my hat is off to them, but I am looking forward to a new system that works without house-ruling the hell out of it. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T15:44:37-08:00","id":769602,"title":"","content":"Me, I'm hoping they don't remove the Hands of Aten, but I do hope they make it clear they aren't actually Angels, just his riff on the idea to manipulate people who confuse him for a monotheistic God. I like him in there as the embodiment of faith used as a justification for violence and domination, but I'd be more at peace with him if he was explicitly a false God (in terms of image, he actually is close enough to the Gods to be actually divine).<br /> <br /> Also, that they get more angelic, as in the wheels-of-fire, four-faced cherub sense. Seriously, people with wings is just...generic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T16:51:20-08:00","id":769635,"title":"","content":"Aten has the virtue of being an actual part of Egyptian mythology; I wouldn't mind him being reworked to more closely resemble the actual myths. If that means losing Aten-the-Titan and his faux Angels, so be it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T18:59:11-08:00","id":769714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=769635#post769635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aten has the virtue of being an actual part of Egyptian mythology; I wouldn't mind him being reworked to more closely resemble the actual myths. If that means losing Aten-the-Titan and his faux Angels, so be it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That works too. <br /> <br /> ...Except that if we're doing that, he's still pretty similar to a monotheistic god. Just from reading Wikipedia, Akhenaten is the originator of the idea of &quot;the mind of God is creation&quot;. Assuming he isn't an aspect of Ra and thus, not really his own character. We're probably going to have to take some liberties.<br /> <br /> The part about the inherent elitism of Aten-worship is something we should probably import from Aten-the-actual-god, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T00:08:06-08:00","id":769797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=768860#post768860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, as noted they totally gutted the Epic System to put in 'tier changes' that are supposed to put differences between a normal mortal and gods, etc. Weirdly, if you just left Epics but only let them go up to 5, you get an almost identical spread (0-12 vs. 0-11 autos). Oh, and the Tiers only apply &quot;sometimes&quot;. So you can have a skilled mortal beat a god at their best skill. And the tiers apply (sometimes) to all attributes, even something you aren't necessarily known for but have decent stats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you see, I'd feel like this would be a much more persuasive argument if Tier was going to be literally the only difference between Gods and Mortals and there wouldn't be any sort of supernatural powers at all.<br /> <br /> Given the game line, it's themes, etc, I feel like it's <i>pretty damn likely</i> that there's gonna be a number of other supernatural powers that tilt things just a wee bit further in towards the gods than the basic benefits of Tier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T01:58:32-08:00","id":769820,"title":"","content":"True. 2e Tier (are you a mortal, a pre-Visitation Scion, a Hero, a Demigod, a God, or a Greater Titan?) is a different thing than 2e Scale, though I'm pretty sure the former limits the latter. And Scale, not Tier, is what's replacing Epic Attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T02:09:41-08:00","id":769824,"title":"","content":"There are actually a number of games out there where, while dice pools remain the same, scale is changed and matters. The old d6 Star Wars game comes to mind. It's why you can't shoot a TIE fighter out of the air with a rifle. Dice pools and difficulty are one thing but scale is the big changer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T02:33:39-08:00","id":769830,"title":"","content":"Last thought before I go to work: Scale is taken directly from \u201cWhite Wolf Comics presents the Cabal\u201d in <b>Mage Chronicler's Guide</b>, where everything is handled either through Impact (which grants from one to sixteen successes) or through SFX (which multiplies successes by a factor ranging from two to a hundred or more). <i>That's</i> something I'm hoping will change during development and playtesting: I'm hoping that the Impact will scale more or less linearly (a big problem with Scion 1e was that eventually a difference of a single dot of Epic Attribute was essentially an \u201cI win\u201d button), and that instead of multiplying successes, SFX will be built into what a success does for you: someone with low-Scale Strength should spend a success to pick up a barrel, while someone with moderate-Scale Strength should be spending a success to pick up a pickup, and someone with top-Scale Strength should be spending a success to lift a building or larger object. That is, the higher a trait's Scale, the more each Success means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-20-2015, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T07:31:08-08:00","id":769965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=769602#post769602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Me, I'm hoping they don't remove the Hands of Aten, but I do hope they make it clear they aren't actually Angels, just his riff on the idea to manipulate people who confuse him for a monotheistic God. I like him in there as the embodiment of faith used as a justification for violence and domination, but I'd be more at peace with him if he was explicitly a false God (in terms of image, he actually is close enough to the Gods to be actually divine).<br /> <br /> Also, that they get more angelic, as in the wheels-of-fire, four-faced cherub sense. Seriously, people with wings is just...generic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternately, and in accordance with inspirational material such as Wicked+Divine, present <i>actual Hebrew angels</i> in the game, mainly as Guides. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=769714#post769714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That works too. <br /> <br /> ...Except that if we're doing that, he's still pretty similar to a monotheistic god. Just from reading Wikipedia, Akhenaten is the originator of the idea of \u201cthe mind of God is creation\u201d. Assuming he isn't an aspect of Ra and thus, not really his own character. We're probably going to have to take some liberties.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't mind him being an aspect of Ra and thus not really his own character. But that's just an off-the-cuff thought by a amateur mythologist. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=769714#post769714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The part about the inherent elitism of Aten-worship is something we should probably import from Aten-the-actual-god, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, certainly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T22:53:38-08:00","id":770548,"title":"","content":"A question for Neil, what counts as a god? I'd like to see a fairy tale version of Scion, with the catch that we're not just the children of say, Alice in Wonderland or Robinson Crusoe, to pull names out of my hat at random. But we're next in-line (or maybe competing?) to become the next Alice or Robinson, superhero legacy style. Except more so, because it's more than just a title or mantle, it's a change of existence - we become the myth for good and for bad, and in doing so, perpetuate it. Because society needs myths/narratives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1411-wingnut2292","name":"wingnut2292","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1411_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T09:41:12-08:00","id":770799,"title":"","content":"More questions for the thread! (Or, well, a repost of these questions! xD As i said preivously, i don't think they have been answered, if so, would be anyone so kind as to point me where?)<br /> <br /> - *<b>What*</b> is a God <b>Mantle</b> and how do you steal it? <i>[I have the idea of the Mantle being something like an abstract representation/aura/fate implications of the God nature, but i'd appreciate a clear definition of it]</i> Does it manifests as a relic, that can be stolen physically? Or is it something like a metaphor, that is won after some kind of clash or competition?<br /> <br /> - What would be the effects of stealing it, both to the God that lost it and the one who took it?<br /> <br /> - Can a mortal steal it and achieve the state of a Scion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T01:02:18-08:00","id":775854,"title":"","content":"Has anyone gotten to the point of becoming a god and siring scions, say as an ending to one game and beginning to another? My question to Neall and the board is what does it cost the parent to Visit/bring up to Demigod and then Apotheosis?<br /> <br /> You are essentially giving someone 10 dots knack/boons, more attributes, birthrights and freebies each time. Ok Birthrights you may get the smith god to help with or pull something out of your adventuring vault. What does it cost the god mechanically? Are they weakened/drained of most their legend after doing this?<br /> <br /> Another question is beyond having someone doing your bidding do the gods get something when their scions graduate to Demigod/Godhood (maybe that is why Zeus and Odin keep having so many children..outside of just not being able to keep it in their pants).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":333,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","user":"Achilles","date":". 11-28-2015, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T15:08:45-08:00","id":777386,"title":"","content":"can you tell something about the Teotl pantheon purview?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T07:15:29-08:00","id":785949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wingnut2292</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=770548#post770548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question for Neil, what counts as a god? I'd like to see a fairy tale version of Scion, with the catch that we're not just the children of say, Alice in Wonderland or Robinson Crusoe, to pull names out of my hat at random. But we're next in-line (or maybe competing?) to become the next Alice or Robinson, superhero legacy style. Except more so, because it's more than just a title or mantle, it's a change of existence - we become the myth for good and for bad, and in doing so, perpetuate it. Because society needs myths/narratives.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know it's circular, but right now a god is god, with certain traits. Though taking on a mantle like that is certainly possible, and you could re-skin Scion to do that with some doing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">- *<b>What*</b> is a God <b>Mantle</b> and how do you steal it? <i>[I have the idea of the Mantle being something like an abstract representation/aura/fate implications of the God nature, but i'd appreciate a clear definition of it]</i> Does it manifests as a relic, that can be stolen physically? Or is it something like a metaphor, that is won after some kind of clash or competition?</div> </div> </div> </div>A mantle is your divine identity, the ur-identity existing within Fate from which you draw your divine power. To a certain extent, you are your mantle, and <i>it</i> is <i>you</i>, even when you can separate them. Incarnations spin out of the Mantle. Gods are far more intimately tied to their mantles than demigods and heroes; that which binds their mantle in Fate, binds them as well, and they have to be extraordinarily careful about what they do outside the identity they've made for themselves. Of course, you can have multiple mantles...<br /> <br /> Relics can be part of a mantle. A good example is Mjolnir being part of Thor's Legend. It can be metaphorical as well, and often is, which is how Loki became associated with fire.<br /> <br /> <b>Scion 2e</b> can perhaps be most fairly said to be a game about how <i>you </i>are defined in whole and in part by the <i>you </i>other people see. It's in the very name of the game - the word <i>scion </i>means you're descended from someone or something extremely notable, immediately casting the relationship as inferior, junior, and familial. The game is about relationships and presentation, destiny and culture, and the mantle is the final mechanical expression of that core theme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone gotten to the point of becoming a god and siring scions, say as an ending to one game and beginning to another? My question to Neall and the board is what does it cost the parent to Visit/bring up to Demigod and then Apotheosis?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, not in <b>2e</b>...<br /> <br /> This brings up a little point I wanted to make: one of my quieter goals in 2e is to make each tier a sort of distinct style of play within the wider framework of Scion. You might not <i>want </i>to graduate to demigodhood or even godhood, as the bit about the mantle above indicates. The process of apotheosis isn't pretty often: as Divus Iulius, who had to die stabbed by his best friend to complete the ascension.<br /> <br /> Godhood is a little different in 2e. Anyone past Legend 9 is a god, capable of siring Scions (provided they are capable of old-fashioned reproduction and not, I dunno, a serpent or a dog or a dickless corpse or something). Creating Scions via another method takes a tad more juice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicholas Milioni</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">can you tell something about the Teotl pantheon purview?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sacrificing to the gods is part of the core cult mechanics and subsystems; I suspect most of the Teotl PSP will be about maximizing and getting more out of that particular subsystem.<br /> <br /> PSPs typically involve things other pantheons <i>can </i>kinda-sorta do, but that one particular pantheon absolutely excels at. Lots of gods can shapeshift, but the Greeks turn themselves and others into clouds and animals and stars and abstract emotions like dread all the freaking time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T08:48:21-08:00","id":786002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=785949#post785949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Godhood is a little different in 2e. Anyone past Legend 9 is a god, capable of siring Scions (provided they are capable of old-fashioned reproduction and not, I dunno, a serpent or a dog or a dickless corpse or something). Creating Scions via another method takes a tad more juice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bah. Just get your sister to make you a golden penis and you'll be fine.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T21:18:30-08:00","id":786488,"title":"","content":"Osiris: Can we <i>please</i> stop referring to me as a dickless corpse? Come on, man. That's just not cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T18:43:15-08:00","id":787073,"title":"","content":"if a god wanted to change his lifestyle,say,if a god of water and the sea eventuslly gets boring of water and sea and to do the opposite,could she find a god of the earth and become an god of Both sea and Eearth somehow?<br /> i really would like to play a charater with that quest,changing your role,becoming something else<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 12-15-2015, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T20:45:54-08:00","id":787130,"title":"","content":"Poseidon: Come on Hades, let me be the god of riches, dammit! How 'bout another round of rock papers scissors. Best 4 out of 7.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T23:33:44-08:00","id":787174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=787073#post787073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if a god wanted to change his lifestyle,say,if a god of water and the sea eventuslly gets boring of water and sea and to do the opposite,could she find a god of the earth and become an god of Both sea and Eearth somehow?<br /> i really would like to play a charater with that quest,changing your role,becoming something else</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reminded of recent events in Marvel comics, in which Loki has been trying to escape his Fate at Ragnarok, by shedding his role as &quot;God of Evil&quot;, and once more becoming simply &quot;God of Mischief&quot;...\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T03:18:16-08:00","id":787251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=787174#post787174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm reminded of recent events in Marvel comics, in which Loki has been trying to escape his Fate at Ragnarok, by shedding his role as &quot;God of Evil&quot;, and once more becoming simply &quot;God of Mischief&quot;...\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I dindt read his comics in A loong time thats story sounds really cool,in which comic loki does that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T05:34:23-08:00","id":787290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=787251#post787251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dindt read his comics in A loong time thats story sounds really cool,in which comic loki does that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Mangle is referring to this comic. Directly from Wikipedia (go to <b>Other Versions; Loki triumphant</b>):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loki_(comics)\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loki_(comics)\" target=\"_blank\"> Loki (disambiguation) - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loki_(comics)\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loki_(comics) </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/dc/Loki1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> &quot;A 4 issue series simply titled &quot;Loki&quot; where Loki has now claimed leadership of Asgard, and all must recognize that fact, even Thor. Finally winning the throne after a long sought out fight is not as sweet as he thought it would be.&quot; </span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T05:34:49-08:00","id":787291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=787251#post787251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dindt read his comics in A loong time thats story sounds really cool,in which comic loki does that?</div> </div> </div> </div>A story arc running through Kieron Gillen's <i>Journey into Mystery</i> run, Gillen's <i>Young Avengers</i>, and Al Ewing's <i>Loki: Agent of Asgard.</i> Fortunately, they've all been collected as graphic novels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T07:09:07-08:00","id":787337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=787073#post787073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if a god wanted to change his lifestyle,say,if a god of water and the sea eventuslly gets boring of water and sea and to do the opposite,could she find a god of the earth and become an god of Both sea and Eearth somehow?<br /> i really would like to play a charater with that quest,changing your role,becoming something else</div> </div> </div> </div>Changing your mantle's associations is pretty epic, yeah. It is akin to Loki becoming God of Story rather than God of Lies; how do you do that when everyone knows you as a liar? And like as not, you'll never lose your prior association totally. You might become a divinity of a coastal city or the shore along with the deep ocean, but it's difficult.<br /> <br /> More often, you'll have to live with the god you've become. Doing otherwise takes time and careful effort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T07:52:06-08:00","id":787369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=787337#post787337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Changing your mantle's associations is pretty epic, yeah. It is akin to Loki becoming God of Story rather than God of Lies; how do you do that when everyone knows you as a liar? And like as not, you'll never lose your prior association totally. You might become a divinity of a coastal city or the shore along with the deep ocean, but it's difficult.<br /> <br /> More often, you'll have to live with the god you've become. Doing otherwise takes time and careful effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>i also always saw kid loki as an awesome example of a reincanated scion (althought he started as a full blown god,albeit a infant one).<br /> That must have happned once or twice in the scionverse,a reicarnation of a trickest god,or a blood thirsty war deity,or one of those gods that wnated blood sacrifices every sunday,and trying to find his legacy by becoming a more pacific version of the being they were reicarnated as.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T08:41:29-08:00","id":787392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=787369#post787369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i also always saw kid loki as an awesome example of a reincanated scion (althought he started as a full blown god,albeit a infant one).<br /> That must have happned once or twice in the scionverse,a reicarnation of a trickest god,or a blood thirsty war deity,or one of those gods that wnated blood sacrifices every sunday,and trying to find his legacy by becoming a more pacific version of the being they were reicarnated as.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reincarnation is one of the ways you can do it, since you're partially rebuilding your mantle from the ground up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T09:45:16-08:00","id":787453,"title":"","content":"Am I missing some kind implication here? So if water god wants to turn into water and earth god...doesn't she/he save up xp, buy up earth boons...do something Earth like... cause an earthquake or maybe raise a mountain in front of a bunch of people and voila...people start to associate you with this kind of stuff. Or do it like the Theoi... head off to Italy/another culture and just start off displaying those powers so in your introduction to them its always been there.<br /> <br /> Or is it something wierder than that and after becoming a god you can't buy up purviews/gain new associateds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T10:31:59-08:00","id":787480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=787337#post787337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Changing your mantle's associations is pretty epic, yeah. It is akin to Loki becoming God of Story rather than God of Lies; how do you do that when everyone knows you as a liar? And like as not, you'll never lose your prior association totally. You might become a divinity of a coastal city or the shore along with the deep ocean, but it's difficult.<br /> <br /> More often, you'll have to live with the god you've become. Doing otherwise takes time and careful effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>is stealing part of someone else mantle strictly necessary? the water god who wanted to be also an earth god you and i just talked about,what would happen if he founded a coastal city? became the patron of the coastal city and helped everyone in the city in his own way,including taking care of the city land,and be worshipped by 96% percent by the city inhabitants,would that be enough to become part earth deity? or it would be 100% necessary to stole something from a previous earth deity mantle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T11:39:14-08:00","id":787527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=787453#post787453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or is it something wierder than that and after becoming a god you can't buy up purviews/gain new associateds?</div> </div> </div> </div>Something weirder. You can broaden existing Purview associations with XP, but it's very hard to make new ones except as the story allows. This is something we'll go into a lot more depth in with the actual books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicholas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">is stealing part of someone else mantle strictly necessary?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. It's usually pretty hard to steal something from another god, rather than picking up a similar association.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b