ng with the deep ocean, but it's difficult.<br /> <br /> More often, you'll have to live with the god you've become. Doing otherwise takes time and careful effort.</div> </div> </div> </div> Loki has died at least twice \u200balready in his pursuit of this goal, and yet<i> still </i>Evil Loki seems to be his destiny...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T00:39:51-08:00","id":787890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=787800#post787800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Loki has died at least twice \u200balready in his pursuit of this goal, and yet<i> still </i>Evil Loki seems to be his destiny...</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm...<br /> <br /> In Agent of Asgard, he averts the evil future Loki of that series, turns it into a &quot;could have been&quot; instead of &quot;what will be&quot;. He still has the weight of expectations hanging on him, pulling at him, but he intends basically not to let it stop him doing what he's doing, stop him being a god of stories and mischief.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T02:29:15-08:00","id":787937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=787890#post787890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mm...<br /> <br /> In Agent of Asgard, he averts the evil future Loki of that series, turns it into a &quot;could have been&quot; instead of &quot;what will be&quot;. He still has the weight of expectations hanging on him, pulling at him, but he intends basically not to let it stop him doing what he's doing, stop him being a god of stories and mischief.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should mention, I'm a bit behind, using trades to (sort of) catch up. I kind of wish Marvel would make use of the fact there are <b><i><u>two</u></i></b> Lokis in Norse myth; Loki of Asgard, and Loki of Utgard.<br /> <br /> BTW, will my scion of Loki by able to troll people...with actual <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gvYfRiJQIX8\" target=\"_blank\">trolls?</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T08:40:48-08:00","id":788785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=787752#post787752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can you name one or more gods who used to be part of an pantheon,but their original pantheon died and the becane part of a new one? i know there are gods like that in the sciion books i can't seem to identify them!</div> </div> </div> </div>Not <i>really</i>. Cernunnos might qualify, with the resurrection of the Horned Man in neopaganism, but this depends on how destroyed you consider the Nemetondevos to be (their godrealms and Overworlds are gone, their terra incognita have been destroyed or colonized by other pantheons, their followers, Scions and a chunk of their gods are dead - some in the cycle of reincarnation, some just really upset and sitting in the Celtic Underworld).<br /> <br /> Quetzacoatl hangs out a lot more with the Teotl than he does the K'uh (which is still around). Much of the Caananite pantheon (also still around) will be city and culture gods who banded together under a single banner. Some gods like Mikola Mozhaiski might've been a Scion of the Bogovi (who are, you guessed it, still extant) but he still mostly does his own thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 12-18-2015, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T11:31:11-08:00","id":788881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=787752#post787752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can you name one or more gods who used to be part of an pantheon,but their original pantheon died and the becane part of a new one? i know there are gods like that in the sciion books i can't seem to identify them!</div> </div> </div> </div>Manaanan mac Lir is apparently this in Scion: Companion, having come to the Tuatha from an older pantheon whose name is lost to history, but I don't know if that was based on anything real-world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T17:41:28-08:00","id":789041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=788881#post788881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Manaanan mac Lir is apparently this in Scion: Companion, having come to the Tuatha from an older pantheon whose name is lost to history, but I don't know if that was based on anything real-world.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=788785#post788785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not <i>really</i>. Cernunnos might qualify, with the resurrection of the Horned Man in neopaganism, but this depends on how destroyed you consider the Nemetondevos to be (their godrealms and Overworlds are gone, their terra incognita have been destroyed or colonized by other pantheons, their followers, Scions and a chunk of their gods are dead - some in the cycle of reincarnation, some just really upset and sitting in the Celtic Underworld).<br /> <br /> Quetzacoatl hangs out a lot more with the Teotl than he does the K'uh (which is still around). Much of the Caananite pantheon (also still around) will be city and culture gods who banded together under a single banner. Some gods like Mikola Mozhaiski might've been a Scion of the Bogovi (who are, you guessed it, still extant) but he still mostly does his own thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks guys. oh,i never heard of the K'uh before,they were the gods of which people? Are the Nine Lords Of the Night a important part of any pantheon?<br /> And about the relationship between gods and titans,were the first gods created by the titans?if they were,how did that happen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 12-18-2015, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T22:41:06-08:00","id":789119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=789041#post789041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks guys. oh,i never heard of the K'uh before,they were the gods of which people?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're the Maya gods.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T14:56:54-08:00","id":789438,"title":"","content":"A question about Knacks. There are a bunch of Gun knacks, any chance of this edition either generalizing these to a more Ranged Weapon knacks or adding things like Bow &amp; Arrow Knacks to the mix (of which I would figure there would be like ten times the number over the gun knacks).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T18:42:50-08:00","id":790026,"title":"","content":"is magic related to true names,especially stealing someone's name to be able to control the named, still a thing?<br /> About sorcerers,since you mentioned they can start as rincewind and go all the way to baba yaga,do you already have a idea about how they would escalate in power,or ,mechanically speaking, can sorceres reach legend 9?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 12-20-2015, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T11:10:16-08:00","id":790358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=789438#post789438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question about Knacks. There are a bunch of Gun knacks, any chance of this edition either generalizing these to a more Ranged Weapon knacks or adding things like Bow &amp; Arrow Knacks to the mix (of which I would figure there would be like ten times the number over the gun knacks).</div> </div> </div> </div>Current Knacks don't actually tie them to specific Skills (or Attributes), but Storypath doesn't actually have Gun or Bow as separate Skills; it's all Aim. So, no matter how it shakes out, you're good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicholas Milioni</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">is magic related to true names,especially stealing someone's name to be able to control the named, still a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>In some pantheons, such as Egyptian, sure.<br /> <br /> I should note that the Magic Purview is probably going to largely go away in favor of a more holistic focus on cultural magics facilitated by the Pantheon-Specific Purview. Magics in the core of Origins will be handled differently, not always in regard to Fate-only, and will be something that can be expanded upon in later books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> About sorcerers,since you mentioned they can start as rincewind and go all the way to baba yaga,do you already have a idea about how they would escalate in power,or ,mechanically speaking, can sorceres reach legend 9? </div> </div> </div>Yeah, we've got a few ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T12:54:49-08:00","id":790437,"title":"","content":"are there plans for the keepers of the world to be brought back? did quetzcoatl started as part of the K'uh and then he become a Teotl? if so,how did that happen ? was it something he made happen or was it outside of his control?<br /> oh,and i was thinking about something you could use,just a suggestion if i may be so bold: you know the power of Reshape Shen? the one wen the chinese pantheon used to transform foreign gods in new versions? i think it'd be cool if at least some gods of <i>all </i>pantheons could do the same thing ,but just the most powerful gods of each pantheon though,Deities like Zeus,Ra,Danu,Odin,it just feels <i>right </i>that those guys could turn other immortals in something that is part of their pantheon. do you think that'd be cool?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 12-21-2015, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T13:32:07-08:00","id":790453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=790437#post790437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">are there plans for the keepers of the world to be brought back? did quetzcoatl started as part of the K'uh and then he become a Teotl? if so,how did that happen ? was it something he made happen or was it outside of his control?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can belong to multiple pantheons in the second edition.<br /> <br /> I <i>love </i>the Keepers of the World, and if anything they'll be a bigger part of 2e. There's even going to be a mechanic to sort of explain their big evil plan...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> oh,and i was thinking about something you could use,just a suggestion if i may be so bold: you know the power of Reshape Shen? the one wen the chinese pantheon used to transform foreign gods in new versions? i think it'd be cool if at least some gods of <i>all </i>pantheons could do the same thing ,but just the most powerful gods of each pantheon though,Deities like Zeus,Ra,Danu,Odin,it just feels <i>right </i>that those guys could turn other immortals in something that is part of their pantheon. do you think that'd be cool? </div> </div> </div>A lot of All-Mother or All-Father-class gods have the ability to invite someone into their pantheon, yeah. Since that's the level you're operating at, it's largely restricted to Legend 12.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T13:39:55-08:00","id":790457,"title":"","content":"what would happen to a god if ssuch a god did something completely anthetical to their mantle,or mantles? there are consequences for when the gods do that right?<br /> And the Keepers,so, if they are six gods who banded together for a common cause and htye plan to do something with the power of Legend that will shake the world. would that be neough fot the six of them to become a brand new pantheon? or at least a <i>SUB</i>-pantheon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 12-21-2015, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T10:12:10-08:00","id":790903,"title":"","content":"How many Callings are intended to be introduced in the core book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T11:44:57-08:00","id":790946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=790358#post790358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should note that the Magic Purview is probably going to largely go away in favor of a more holistic focus on cultural magics facilitated by the Pantheon-Specific Purview. Magics in the core of Origins will be handled differently, not always in regard to Fate-only, and will be something that can be expanded upon in later books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Splendid! The Magic Purview always seemed kind of weird to me. I really like exploring how each different culture handled magic, and a single one-size-fits-all Purview never seemed a good way to sum that up. Plus, several of my players would completely fuck up my night by casting &quot;Deus ex Machina&quot; every five minutes and expecting me to just pull easy outs for them out of my ass! <br /> <br /> This is some of the best news I've seen about Scion 2e yet. And so far MOST of what I've heard has been good news.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, we've got a few ideas. </div> </div> </div>Can't wait to learn more about these ideas. I'm really looking forward to more information about sorcerers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T11:48:57-08:00","id":790949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=790903#post790903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many Callings are intended to be introduced in the core book?</div> </div> </div> </div> <i>At least</i> ten. Creator, Guardian, Herald*, Hunter, Judge, Leader, Lover, Sage, Trickster, Warrior.<br /> <br /> There might be an eleventh, if design moots it so. You can have more than one Calling.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">*I keep wanting to use &quot;Psychopomp&quot;</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T12:14:26-08:00","id":790981,"title":"","content":"something silly tha'ts been bugging me. why is mikaboshi called the &quot;august star of heaven&quot; if he's a titan of darkness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T12:17:22-08:00","id":790984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=790981#post790981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">something silly tha'ts been bugging me. why is mikaboshi called the &quot;august star of heaven&quot; if he's a titan of darkness?</div> </div> </div> </div>He'