e specific?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T19:41:56-08:00","id":793903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=793294#post793294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">does the netjer have any kind of central leader? like zeus is the king of the theoi?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Netjer are a good pantheon for Political Intrigue, <br /> <br /> Their Nominal Leader is Horus, who got the position after defeating Set, who got the position after Castrating Osiris, who got the position after Isis (his wife) Learned the True name of Ra and downgraded from this all powerfull Status to somewere more on par whit every one else (in a way Ra is more like a Titan who is been bound and slaved by the Netjer)<br /> <br /> So you have a lot of Political Players out there<br /> <br /> Horus: the Oficial Leader but also one of the youngest of his Pantheon, (and many other pantheons, i can see Odin and Zeus looking down to him and leaving him out of the Grand Politics) <br /> <br /> Set: the Deposed Dictator who is just waiting for a Chance to do another Coup and go back to the top<br /> <br /> Osiris: the Kings Father who loose the Trone on a Tecnicality (Eunucs can not be Kings)<br /> <br /> Ra: the Reveared Elder who every body else more or less serve him but his days of actual political powers are way behind <br /> <br /> Isis: the Manipulative one, the one that steal Ra true name and The Power Behind the Trone of both Osiris and Horus<br /> <br /> so while Cronus and Uranus are more or less out of the picture of Olimpus Politics and the only real treat to Zeus trone is his Prophesiced Scion (how may or may not already exist) Horus has to deal whit all this other guys all older than him and half of who are actualy his Parents","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4856-alfanumerico","name":"alfanumerico","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T21:09:30-08:00","id":793933,"title":"","content":"I always saw thoth as a the one guy who could totally destroy all the others and become the king/pharaoh/the big dog if he wanted,but he prefers to mind his own bussines than being a leader","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T06:12:11-08:00","id":794126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=793754#post793754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there going to be anything on gods and plants? Many gods don't only have certain Animals linked close to them in legend, but plants as well. Will that simply be something along the lines of fertility or something a bit more specific?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gods have associations of all sorts, yeah. Doing something with the association can give you the ability to get the attention of the god (or your attention, when you are the god).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T07:13:01-08:00","id":794154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=792416#post792416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">can you explain how interpretatio romana happens and what it is?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interpretatio Romana - &quot;The Roman Translation&quot; - is what happens when two cultures meet and one of them decides the gods of the other are a mislabelling of the ones they already have. For instance, the Romans saw Oghma as how the barbaric, misinformed Celts perceived Hercules, and see also how Hermes and Thoth were equated. I can't say for sure if this phenomenon is how the Greek gods were equated to the Roman ones(Zeus to Jupiter et al)--Wikipedia certainly seems to think so, but, you know, Wikipedia--but it would be a good example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T07:20:28-08:00","id":794162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=794154#post794154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interpretatio Romana - &quot;The Roman Translation&quot; - is what happens when two cultures meet and one of them decides the gods of the other are a mislabelling of the ones they already have. For instance, the Romans saw Oghma as how the barbaric, misinformed Celts perceived Hercules, and see also how Hermes and Thoth were equated. I can't say for sure if this phenomenon is how the Greek gods were equated to the Roman ones(Zeus to Jupiter et al)--Wikipedia certainly seems to think so, but, you know, Wikipedia--but it would be a good example.</div> </div> </div> </div>In <b>Scion 2e</b>, it's sort of two distinct metaphysical processes that are labelled as one thing - two gods being tied together by Fate as rivals, and a god becoming recognized by another culture as a pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T08:12:15-08:00","id":794194,"title":"","content":"*facepalm* You know, I was going to add, &quot;at least in the real world, but I don't know how it's going to work in Scion.&quot; And then I completely forgot.<br /> <br /> But that part of the question was answered for me; thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T10:24:06-08:00","id":794257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>alfanumerico</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=793903#post793903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Netjer are a good pantheon for Political Intrigue, <br /> <br /> Their Nominal Leader is Horus, who got the position after defeating Set, who got the position after Castrating Osiris, who got the position after Isis (his wife) Learned the True name of Ra and downgraded from this all powerfull Status to somewere more on par whit every one else (in a way Ra is more like a Titan who is been bound and slaved by the Netjer)<br /> <br /> So you have a lot of Political Players out there<br /> <br /> Horus: the Oficial Leader but also one of the youngest of his Pantheon, (and many other pantheons, i can see Odin and Zeus looking down to him and leaving him out of the Grand Politics) <br /> <br /> Set: the Deposed Dictator who is just waiting for a Chance to do another Coup and go back to the top<br /> <br /> Osiris: the Kings Father who loose the Trone on a Tecnicality (Eunucs can not be Kings)<br /> <br /> Ra: the Reveared Elder who every body else more or less serve him but his days of actual political powers are way behind <br /> <br /> Isis: the Manipulative one, the one that steal Ra true name and The Power Behind the Trone of both Osiris and Horus<br /> <br /> so while Cronus and Uranus are more or less out of the picture of Olimpus Politics and the only real treat to Zeus trone is his Prophesiced Scion (how may or may not already exist) Horus has to deal whit all this other guys all older than him and half of who are actualy his Parents</div> </div> </div> </div>Really nice summary, alfanumerico! I'd want to ask Neall if they are gping to follow that general direction with the Egyptian Gods (as they are so old, their roles change from Nomo to Nomo and from period to period, but i like this version best of all ^^)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":1349,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","user":"Phersus","date":"12-28-2015, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T03:47:32-08:00","id":796761,"title":"","content":"I had another question regarding Mantles, if a god is acting within there mantle will they have a distinct advantage. for example a sea god fight another god under the sea. (In one of my favorite scion inspirations, the almighty Johnsons the personification of Ullr often tricks the other gods to engage him in a game, where he always wins as one of his mantles is the god of games).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2943-blured","name":"Blured","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T10:30:54-08:00","id":797861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Creating new subrealms and sub-pantheons is something you can do as a god. New Overworlds, pantheons, creation myths and altering the structure of the World is an appropriate end of a major, years-long epic campaign. </div> </div> </div>would you mind explaining how creating a a new creation myth would work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T08:38:19-08:00","id":798273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=797861#post797861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">would you mind explaining how creating a a new creation myth would work?</div> </div> </div> </div>A number of myths involve successive ages of humanity. The Greeks had different ages undone by the king of the gods being butchered. The Aztecs had different ages undone by the sun getting knocked out of the sky. The Navajo had different ages that were made through the people emerging from successive worlds. Hell, even Ragnarok is supposed to end with a new creation. Basically, there's a decent chance you'll have to rebuild everything. Which could be a whole lot of fun, come to think of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T14:43:57-08:00","id":798403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>griffinguy24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=798273#post798273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A number of myths involve successive ages of humanity. The Greeks had different ages undone by the king of the gods being butchered. The Aztecs had different ages undone by the sun getting knocked out of the sky. The Navajo had different ages that were made through the people emerging from successive worlds. Hell, even Ragnarok is supposed to end with a new creation. Basically, there's a decent chance you'll have to rebuild everything. Which could be a whole lot of fun, come to think of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>and then after the scion jack bauer finished throin zeus into the sun he said &quot;let there be <i>light.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T13:23:01-08:00","id":802305,"title":"","content":"Question on presentation style. In D&amp;D4e powers and abilities have a little bit of fluff and a very mechanical, defined, consistent presentation. Maybe not the most engaging to read but clear and consistent to use in game. Vampire has flowery often quite florid powers but any given character probably only has a handful of them so it's fair enough to use them. Exalted tends to have a lot of distinct (often fairly fiddly) powers and any given player is likely to have a lot of them and to be using several of them simultaneously but it uses laguage in a similar way to Vampire.<br /> <br /> I find this a detriment to running games of Exalted. Is there a style guide on how powers and abilities in Scion should be written? Does that guide favour having a mechanical, concise and consistent language (even if it loses some of that mythic feel) or does it favour the Vampire/Exalted style? Or does it do both? Or some other third way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T14:28:27-08:00","id":802346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=802305#post802305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find this a detriment to running games of Exalted. Is there a style guide on how powers and abilities in Scion should be written? Does that guide favour having a mechanical, concise and consistent language (even if it loses some of that mythic feel) or does it favour the Vampire/Exalted style? Or does it do both? Or some other third way?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the goals of the alpha is to essentially create a style guide by discovering what works and what doesn't on the micro scale before we go macro. However, in general, the base Weaving of a Purview into the World has florid language and feel, since it's partially based on the dramatic editing; currently, Knacks are written a bit more simply and directly, while Boons take a cross between the two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T08:45:57-08:00","id":803123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=802346#post802346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the goals of the alpha is to essentially create a style guide by discovering what works and what doesn't on the micro scale before we go macro. However, in general, the base Weaving of a Purview into the World has florid language and feel, since it's partially based on the dramatic editing; currently, Knacks are written a bit more simply and directly, while Boons take a cross between the two.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad to see it's been a consideration and something you'll be keeping an eye out for in your alpha testing, bodes well that you're thinking about this kind of thing nice and early on <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T13:21:08-08:00","id":807253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>griffinguy24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=798273#post798273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A number of myths involve successive ages of humanity. The Greeks had different ages undone by the king of the gods being butchered. The Aztecs had different ages undone by the sun getting knocked out of the sky. The Navajo had different ages that were made through the people emerging from successive worlds.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a mechanic in the game, though after the last design discussion I think we're knocking it back to Director advice.<br /> <br /> The actual Creation Myth mechanics are something in <b>God</b>, for when you make a new pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T16:16:38-08:00","id":807399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=802305#post802305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question on presentation style. In D&amp;D4e powers and abilities have a little bit of fluff and a very mechanical, defined, consistent presentation. Maybe not the most engaging to read but clear and consistent to use in game. Vampire has flowery often quite florid powers but any given character probably only has a handful of them so it's fair enough to use them. Exalted tends to have a lot of distinct (often fairly fiddly) powers and any given player is likely to have a lot of them and to be using several of them simultaneously but it uses language in a similar way to Vampire.<br /> <br /> I find this a detriment to running games of Exalted. Is there a style guide on how powers and abilities in Scion should be written? Does that guide favor having a mechanical, concise and consistent language (even if it loses some of that mythic feel) or does it favor the Vampire/Exalted style? Or does it do both? Or some other third way?</div> </div> </div> </div>I find you can have an agreeable compromise between the two. In general, it's good to call out things that the player will be looking up often directly: Range, Cost, Duration, Damage, Activation Roll, Resistance Roll, Action Type, etcetera. &quot;Florid&quot; language though can paint a more vivid picture of how the power is supposed to work in the narrative, and can make it easier to rule in the matter of edge cases or off-label uses. It also can make the power feel less like a purely mechanical construct, which I think helps the fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:41:59-08:00","id":808896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=793754#post793754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there going to be anything on gods and plants? Many gods don't only have certain Animals linked close to them in legend, but plants as well. Will that simply be something along the lines of fertility or something a bit more specific?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to represent rootwork in one or more of the African-American pantheons, depending on where we decide to focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:49:05-08:00","id":808905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=808896#post808896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to represent rootwork in one or more of the African-American pantheons, depending on where we decide to focus.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's... not really what I was asking. Neall already answered to what I was referring to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","