o?</div> </div> </div> </div>Im really interested to hear how it went too, often these first unveilings come with some really good stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T04:34:12-08:00","id":811676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=810410#post810410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Earlier I think he gave a very rough estimate of 6 or 7 months between releases once the first book was done. So if the stars are right we maybe, might, almost, get Hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Mortal core book and Hero will be coming out at the same time, but i could be wrong about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T05:54:14-08:00","id":811726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=811548#post811548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Im really interested to hear how it went too, often these first unveilings come with some really good stories.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot;Loki? Oh, that asshole.&quot;</i>*<br /> <br /> The two games were really well. The player characters fought and investigated their way through Washington, D.C., to the towers in the suburb of Rosslyn. One group managed to break the ensorclement around the giant Eggth\u00e9r by pointing out that Fjalar had not crowed, nor had the horn of Heimdall sounded, so this <i>couldn't</i> be Fimbulwinter. The other group decided to stop the myth-fueled snowstorm that the giant was inadvertently causing by melting and refreezing the snowdrift atop the skyscraper and then pushing him off the building (try explaining a three-ton corpse in the middle of a street). The Egyptian Scion NPC only died a horrible death in one of the sessions.<br /> <br /> Storypath is rock-solid as an engine, but the Scion-specific systems like freeform Purviews, regaining Legend, and implementing Virtues need a lot of work. Still, I think all the ideas are there.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">* The god writeup for Loki for the two PC Scions of Loki starts with, &quot;This asshole.&quot; The phrase cropped up in both sessions.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T05:57:16-08:00","id":811729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=811676#post811676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the Mortal core book and Hero will be coming out at the same time, but i could be wrong about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are. The term &quot;mortal&quot; is perhaps a misnomer. Changelings, kitsune-spawn, pre-Visitation Scions...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T07:25:04-08:00","id":811781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=811729#post811729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are. The term &quot;mortal&quot; is perhaps a misnomer. Changelings, kitsune-spawn, pre-Visitation Scions...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's changelings as in the original meaning, right? Switching a faerie for a human baby? Is that limited to the British &amp; Irish faerie races?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T08:12:53-08:00","id":811813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=811781#post811781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's changelings as in the original meaning, right? Switching a faerie for a human baby? Is that limited to the British &amp; Irish faerie races?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and probably not - it's a thing in Scandinavian and Nigerian cultures (though I'd want to avoid the ogbanje for other reasons).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T09:38:18-08:00","id":811873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=811813#post811813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, and probably not - it's a thing in Scandinavian and Nigerian cultures (though I'd want to avoid the ogbanje for other reasons).</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as im aware, there is no tradition of the Scandinavian Alfar performing changeling behavior. Certainly dangerous and at times malicious towards mankind, and also seductive and sexual (there are many half elfs scattered about, but these tend to be heroes and a source of prestige) but not any baby swapping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T13:20:08-08:00","id":812054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=811873#post811873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as im aware, there is no tradition of the Scandinavian Alfar performing changeling behavior. Certainly dangerous and at times malicious towards mankind, and also seductive and sexual (there are many half elfs scattered about, but these tend to be heroes and a source of prestige) but not any baby swapping.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bI seem to recall something about dwarves, trolls, or Svartalfar swapping, or at least abducting, human children.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T14:05:27-08:00","id":812097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=812054#post812054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI seem to recall something about dwarves, trolls, or Svartalfar swapping, or at least abducting, human children.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing comes to mind immediately, which isn't to say that there definitely are not any. It sounds more like something from a later era, more of a folkloric Huldufolk sort of image of them from post-christian times, probably with some significant cultural admixture from Continental fairy tales.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T14:46:55-08:00","id":812136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=812097#post812097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing comes to mind immediately, which isn't to say that there definitely are not any. It sounds more like something from a later era, more of a folkloric Huldufolk sort of image of them from post-christian times, probably with some significant cultural admixture from Continental fairy tales.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a few mentions on Wikipedia and other places. But even if it's just immigrant stories or a relic of Christianization, I'm actually mostly fine with that; consider the idea that cultural admixture, like interpretatio Romana, has a cause-and-effect relationship in <b>Scion</b>'s World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T19:33:05-08:00","id":812308,"title":"","content":"Will the playtest adventure reach the general public","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T05:35:18-08:00","id":812514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=812308#post812308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will the playtest adventure reach the general public</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! I will be cleaning it up myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T16:39:53-08:00","id":813009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=812514#post812514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes! I will be cleaning it up myself.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> YAY!! I'd like to have at least a glimpse of these newfangled rules. And it's good to hear you say they're rock-solid. Gives me hope, it does! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T07:39:14-08:00","id":815436,"title":"","content":"what are the plans for the K'uh pantheon purview?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T13:51:52-08:00","id":817924,"title":"","content":"I've been rereading the Scion previews and comments and I've been wondering how accessible Terra Incognita (and for that matter, Overworld and Underworld) are going to be. From my <i>vague and distant memories</i> of first edition, Terra Incognita were only really accessible if you had a psychopomp Demigod on your team. I know they're going to be more prominent in second edition, but I'd like to know more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T06:38:17-08:00","id":818384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=815436#post815436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what are the plans for the K'uh pantheon purview?</div> </div> </div> </div>None yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been rereading the Scion previews and comments and I've been wondering how accessible Terra Incognita (and for that matter, Overworld and Underworld) are going to be. From my <i>vague and distant memories</i> of first edition, Terra Incognita were only really accessible if you had a psychopomp Demigod on your team. I know they're going to be more prominent in second edition, but I'd like to know more.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can be accessed by anyone who's aware of how to get there and has a Legend score, although gods (often, though not necessarily Heralds) can enable access and traversal by mere mortals. Mortals can, and do, emigrate and immigrate back and forth between the World and Terra Incognita; one of the alpha characters spent much of her formative years hiding from Loki in empty Vanaheim, while another was raised in a village dedicated to Agni (called &quot;Potemkin World&quot;, though that's not culturally apropos).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T19:50:07-08:00","id":819647,"title":"","content":"I have come begging for more wisdom! <br /> <br /> I'm a big fan of gods who have eclectic sets of purviews that aren't obviously connected, but that make sense when you squint a little and look at them sideways. For instance, part of Cuchulainn's legend inspired me to come up with a Scion who's the patron of night sentries and the guardian of sleeping soldiers, and whose purviews would include night, war, protection, recuperative rest, faithful lovers, households, dreams, winter and (hibernating) bears. This leads me to two questions:<br /> <br /> 1- What's the narrative or thematic difference between Scions who pick up a large number of purviews and those who specialize?<br /> 2- How would Demigods and Gods who want to dip their toe into peripheral purviews make use of low-level purview effects that are designed to work at the Hero level?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T20:23:56-08:00","id":821401,"title":"","content":"I know it might be hard not to spoil in answering this, but do you have any idea of how the characterization of Athena has changed between editions? What's she like in Scion 2e?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T20:38:17-08:00","id":821408,"title":"","content":"What about the depiction of Artemis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T05:52:35-08:00","id":822298,"title":"","content":"Really looking forward to playtesting Scion. Any idea when the Alpha Slice will be released?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/820-gyre","name":"gyre","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T06:05:47-08:00","id":822306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=821401#post821401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know it might be hard not to spoil in answering this, but do you have any idea of how the characterization of Athena has changed between editions? What's she like in Scion 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Athena and Minerva is the Greco-Roman goddess of war (strategy), crafts, wisdom, courage, civilization, mathematics, the city of Athens, and olive oil. In terms of Callings, she <i>heavily </i>favors Sage and Warrior.<br /> <br /> Athena presents a challenge for the designers, in that we don't have Epic Intelligence anymore (though the Physical Epics have been subsumed into Purviews) but that &quot;wisdom&quot; and &quot;mathematics&quot; is difficult to adequately interpolate in our design schema. Gods, over a very broad and reductive view of mythology, tend to be a lot more physically powerful than humanity, yet while they're often <i>wiser </i>or more far-seeing they're not always much smarter. Athena, though, does tend to be really damn smart.<br /> <br /> Ultimately I'm going for a brute-force and low-powered solution - she's &quot;only&quot; got superhuman Attributes, specialties, and Knacks to help her with knowledge-based rolls - and she works that through various Purviews like Passion to kindle clear thought and reason in others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 02-03-2016, 09:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T06:06:21-08:00","id":822307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=821408#post821408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the depiction of Artemis?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, she's not a dominatrix, I'll tell you <i>that </i>much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T06:07:24-08:00","id":822308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gyre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=822298#post822298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really looking forward to playtesting Scion. Any idea when the Alpha Slice will be released?</div> </div> </div> </div>Got a few more drafts coming in, but I'll see if I can't get a more solid due date.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T06:11:22-08:00","id":822311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=819647#post819647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have come begging for more wisdom!<br /> <br /> 1- What's the narrative or thematic difference between Scions who pick up a large number of purviews and those who specialize?<br /> 2- How would Demigods and Gods who want to dip their toe into peripheral purviews make use of low-level purview effects that are designed to work at the Hero level?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're much better at broad, weak effects over a big list than specialized and powerful effects. There's a freeform aspect to using Purviews besides using them like Boons (formerly called weaving, now called miracles) that allows you to burn Legend for, well, free-form effects. Boons are more specialized and powerful expressions of the Purview.<br /> <br /> So, at Demigod and God, you've got way more Legend to burn and can use your free-form effects in more variable ways, but you're basically locked to dipping your toe in and burning a ton of Legend rather than refining your process and deepening your competence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T07:58:55-08:00","id":822390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=822311#post822311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're much better at broad, weak effects over a big list than specialized and powerful effects. There's a freeform aspect to using Purviews besides using them like Boons (formerly called weaving, now called miracles) that allows you to burn Legend for, well, free-form effects. Boons are more specialized and powerful expressions of the Purview.<br /> <br /> So, at Demigod and God, you've got way more Legend to burn and can use your free-form effects in more variable ways, but you're basically locked to dipping your toe in and burning a ton of Legend rather than refining your process and deepening your competence.</div> </div> </div> </div>So would it be accurate to compare the new Purview system to Mage: The Awakening? With Miracles resembling more &quot;on the fly&quot; spells and Boons resembling rotes?<br /> <br /> I mean I'm sure there are differences, but that sounds pretty similar to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T08:57:24-08:00","id":822439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=822390#post822390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So would it be accurate to compare the new Purview system to Mage: The Awakening? With Miracles resembling more &quot;on the fly&quot; spells and Boons resembling rotes?<br /> <br /> I mean I'm sure there are differences, but that sounds pretty similar to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not <i>quite </i>as freeform, but there are similarities in the current alpha build. I might compare it more to Dark Ages Mage. The Purviews are more heavily weighted towards Boons (there's more flexibility and raw power to them, and more <i>of </i>them, than previously), but the freeform is for effects not covered by Boons but make sense to perform (&quot;I have absolute command of Frost, so can I just snuff out the fireplace?&quot;) or if a Scion wants to replicate a Boon they haven't selected (in which case it generally costs more Legend).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T09:00:02-08:00","id":822441,"title":"","content":"How are you guys planning to work with Pantheons who don't necessarily fit into Scion's outlines? For example, the Tuatha who went off and died in a majority of their Major Gods, and who did not have any real 'Overworld' equivalent instead retiring to something more like a host of Terra Incognita?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T09:37:28-08:00","id":822460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=822306#post822306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Athena and Minerva is the Greco-Roman goddess of war (strategy), crafts, wisdom, courage, civilization, mathematics, the city of Athens, and olive oil. In terms of Callings, she <i>heavily </i>favors Sage and Warrior.<br /> <br /> Athena presents a challenge for the designers, in that we don't have Epic Intelligence anymore (though the Physical Epics have been subsumed into Purviews) but that &quot;wisdom&quot; and &quot;mathematics&quot; is difficult to adequately interpolate in our design schema. Gods, over a very broad and reductive view of mythology, tend to be a lot more physically powerful than humanity, yet while they're often <i>wiser </i>or more far-seeing they're not always much smarter. Athena, though, does tend to be really damn smart.<br /> <br /> Ultimately I'm going for a brute-force and low-powered solution - she's &quot;only&quot; got superhuman Attributes, specialties, and Knacks to help her with knowledge-based rolls - and she works that through various Purviews like Passion to kindle clear thought and reason in others.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Awesome! Cool to hear about how she was modeled, though I will admit I was more asking about her personality/behavior. Like how does Scion 2e portray her, or what notes are there on that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T10:25:01-08:00","id":822487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=822441#post822441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are you guys planning to work with Pantheons who don't necessarily fit into Scion's outlines? For example, the Tuatha who went off and died in a majority of their Major Gods, and who did not have any real 'Overworld' equivalent instead retiring to something more like a host of Terra Incognita?</div> </div> </div> </div>Death isn't always a stumbling block for a lot of gods in 2e. It sucks, but there's a few ways to get over it.<br /> <br /> While we're still in the process of outlines and writing, right now, Terra Incognita are really the <i>only </i>difference in terms of planes or dimensions in Scion 2e (well, the Underworld, though even that's up for debate in terms of something like Mag Mell or Elysia). The Overworld and the Underworld are more like <i>frequencies </i>Terra Incognita tune to. Most Underworlds, Overworlds, and connected Godrealms could fairly be described as Terra Incognita that have been colonized by, aspected to, or linked to the World via association with a respective Pantheon. It's <i>possible</i> to stick to various Overworlds and traverse them without crossing back into the World via the axes mundi, though this is much easier in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> The Manitouk are a little unique in that they really don't <i>have </i>a lot of proper Terra Incognita, only a few Godrealms connected to Strange Sites like Manitoulin Island.<br /> <br /> (also, you'll show up in the Underworld if you die, so)<br /> <br /> Strange Sites and Touchstones remain relatively unchanged, though Touchstones don't lead to the ideal of a place and Scions can themselves be Touchstones. Strange Sites are maybe a proto-Terra Incognita.<br /> <br /> And yes, this does change the shape of the Second Titanomachy, in terms of Primordials assaulting the Overworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 02-03-2016, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T10:26:06-08:00","id":822489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=822460#post822460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awesome! Cool to hear about how she was modeled, though I will admit I was more asking about her personality/behavior. Like how does Scion 2e portray her, or what notes are there on that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Athena is one of the best models for a high-rating Guide. She's friendly, in the same sense a helpful aunt is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T10:45:14-08:00","id":822501,"title":"","content":"While we're talking gods, anything you could share on Legba?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T11:04:20-08:00","id":822521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=822439#post822439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not <i>quite </i>as freeform, but there are similarities in the current alpha build. I might compare it more to Dark Ages Mage. The Purviews are more heavily weighted towards Boons (there's more flexibility and raw power to them, and more <i>of </i>them, than previously), but the freeform is for effects not covered by Boons but make sense to perform (&quot;I have absolute command of Frost, so can I just snuff out the fireplace?&quot;) or if a Scion wants to replicate a Boon they haven't selected (in which case it generally costs more Legend).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sweet! Sounds like the new Purview system is going to be almost exactly like I always thought it should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T11:19:14-08:00","id":822534,"title":"","content":"Gotta say, I really like that explanation Neall. I really like the explanation of Godrealms / Overworlds being Terra Incognita that have been more 'developed', I'd expect sometimes literally in the case of Olympus where it has a bunch of buildings on it.<br /> <br /> You mentioned the Primordials assaulting the Overworld, which is on the topic of another question I had but thought it was a bit out there until you said that. Are you guys going to break Primordial entities (Ouranos, Gaia, Danu, Ymir, Ame-no-Minakanushi, for example) up from Titans? Or is Primordial a new less-Greek focused term for what was called 'Titan'? I've got a terrible suspicion you've mentioned this before and it may have just totally slipped my mind.<br /> <br /> On the topic of the Second Titanomachy, are you guys continuing with Titans being always antagonistic forces?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T11:36:54-08:00","id":822553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=822534#post822534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotta say, I really like that explanation Neall. I really like the explanation of Godrealms / Overworlds being Terra Incognita that have been more 'developed', I'd expect sometimes literally in the case of Olympus where it has a bunch of buildings on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Four Cities of Ireland are another example, though the Tuatha are really crappy at tuning Terra Incognita to the Overworld. Still holdin' out for Ireland!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You mentioned the Primordials assaulting the Overworld, which is on the topic of another question I had but thought it was a bit out there until you said that. Are you guys going to break Primordial entities (Ouranos, Gaia, Danu, Ymir, Ame-no-Minakanushi, for example) up from Titans? </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or is Primordial a new less-Greek focused term for what was called 'Titan'? I've got a terrible suspicion you've mentioned this before and it may have just totally slipped my mind. </div> </div> </div>While Titans are more strongly tied to Primordials, the difference is largely more political than it is metaphysical. (Though it is still very metaphysical.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the topic of the Second Titanomachy, are you guys continuing with Titans being always antagonistic forces? </div> </div> </div>No. The thing about Titans in 2e is that they're generally not tied to thoughts of humanity or human ways of thinking (which is why they tend to be large in stature in some myths) as they are expanding their Purview (which most of them are singularly focused to), and they tend to just sort of <i>gently sandblast </i>the area they're in with theurgic energy. Take Helios - generally pretty tight with the Olympinas, but he <i>literally </i>has the aureole of the Sun around his head, which is really crappy for a whole host of reasons. Helios can't really understand what the big deal is, even if mortals cry when he wanders into view, shield their eyes and cry some more, and then slowly get sunburnt to death. For that reason, a lot of Titans stick around Terra Incognita, of which there are limited supplies.<br /> <br /> Titanspawn are generally either direct creations of a Titan or Titanic servant, or a Legendary Race adapted to living within the magic of a Titan. It, too, is really more of a political designation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T12:07:19-08:00","id":822579,"title":"","content":"Gotta say, I quite like all of that Neall. The Tuatha <i>really</i> are bad at actually settling anywhere, you're bang on with them still holding out for Ireland.<br /> <br /> I really like breaking the Primordials and Titans up. I've been trying to think of ways to do it myself, so I'm really looking forward to seeing what you guys end up doing with it. Also moving Titans away from being antagonistic even when it's out of character. The description of Helios you gave there is wicked.<br /> <br /> I've got to say, with those little tidbits, I'm really looking forward to seeing what you guys produce. Been a bit hesitant, but seeing how you guys plan to change some of those building blocks has really won me over. You also mentioned taking a hatchet to Magic I believe, which I'm really looking forward to as well.<br /> <br /> Since I'm desperately trying to procrastinate away a reading I've got to do, I've got one last question. You've been asked before what your favorite Purview is, my question is what Purview are you feel has shaped up / is shaping up the best? Not necessarily your favorite, but the one you feel that has just hit all of the nails on the head in terms of function and mythic connection? I only ask since my favorite Purview from the revision my friends and myself have made is nowhere close to the one I'm most 'pleased' with in actual design. For us, Darkness just turned out spectacularly, despite it barely ever being used in our games in the almost half-decade of playing together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T12:19:28-08:00","id":822594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=822579#post822579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since I'm desperately trying to procrastinate away a reading I've got to do, I've got one last question. You've been asked before what your favorite Purview is, my question is what Purview are you feel has shaped up / is shaping up the best? Not necessarily your favorite, but the one you feel that has just hit all of the nails on the head in terms of function and mythic connection? I only ask since my favorite Purview from the revision my friends and myself have made is nowhere close to the one I'm most 'pleased' with in actual design. For us, Darkness just turned out spectacularly, despite it barely ever being used in our games in the almost half-decade of playing together.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't decide whether Darkness should incorporate Moon too.<br /> <br /> I really like what Vance is doing with the new Aesir PSP (Wyrd). Fire was coming along well, but now that we've decided to incorporate Passion, I'm wondering if a number of Fire Boons wouldn't be more appropriate there. But I think Stars is my favorite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T13:13:43-08:00","id":822671,"title":"","content":"Darkness and Moon are one of those really tricky things. Sun includes the theoretical &quot;Day&quot; powers, which has it opposing both Darkness and Moon at the same time. The way I look at it is that there are many figures who are linked to one, but not the other, which makes the two Purviews distinct from each other. For example, in the 'Primarily Moon' camp we have Selene, Artemis (though that one is just sort of tenuous sometimes), Sin, Mani, Coyolxauhqui, Bast (though I will admit the Egyptians are not my forte), and Chors. That host is directly representative of very specifically the Moon lacking direct connections to the 'Night' short of it being when they are around. For figures who are primarily 'Night', we have Nix, Apep (sort of), Nott, and Tezcat. For a Deity that unifies both Purviews, there is Tsukuyomi.<br /> <br /> So, cultures are dividing these concepts up pretty heavily. Why, I'm not particularly sure. it might be because you can occasionally see the Moon during the day, or because the Moon is a very obvious 'entity' in the night sky. On top of this, there are some pretty divergent 'subsections' that can exist within Darkness and Moon (just like how you've mentioned Fire incorporates Passion). Moon can have the obvious Lunacy, but also things for illuminating hidden things, and changing. Compared to this, Darkness can draw a connection on fear, and obscuring things (for example, hiding things from Mystery). Due to this, I feel that Darkness and Moon should probably remain disparate Purviews, cultures were viewing them as separate entities, and the both evoke rather divergent ideas.<br /> <br /> Wyrd is a <i>really</i> great basis in concept for the Norse. Our revised Norse PsP is probably similar. Jotunblut was neat, but it really required a lot of dancing around why Njord, Freya, and Freyr had it when they were not descended from Giants. Compared to that, the inexorable style of Norse Fate connects them all (with Freyr doomed to die, and Njord, well, doomed to live and return to his sister-wife without his beloved children) and is a divergent enough idea that it can make a really neat PsP.<br /> <br /> Stars was my personal nemesis for about sixteen months while I threw ideas at it until it finally started to work. I'm really looking forward to seeing what you lot have done to Stars to make it, well, sensible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T13:21:04-08:00","id":822676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=822671#post822671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stars was my personal nemesis for about sixteen months while I threw ideas at it until it finally started to work. I'm really looking forward to seeing what you lot have done to Stars to make it, well, sensible.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://40.media.tumblr.com/a16fc39f1328d34187453ae1bbe55951/tumblr_ngufwhx8yA1r3tui4o1_500.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T13:47:23-08:00","id":822703,"title":"","content":"That sort of thing's a lot like I ended up going with, I think. I've not had the chance to read The Wicked + The Divine yet, but Ishtar was one of the big points I drew on. Lots of being... not antagonistic, but divergent or separate from the Pantheon. Ishtar holding reality hostage (threatening to tear the gates off the Underworld) if her demands are not met, Radegast clearly being very important, being one of the Four Kings, but only interfacing with others when someone else drags him into the story (Stribog stealing his Cloak of Stars). Quetzalcoatl violating social norms and breaking into the Underworld to steal things. Aether being the Titan that is so distant it exists beyond Ouranos, more withdrawn than even the other Titans, Ame-no-Minakanushi popping into existence and then almost instantly leaving. All powerful beings, all important, and wondrous, but... far away, literally, or not. Also capable of making constellations and physically doing things with the Stars, but you can only make so many Boons out of 'fiddle with the night sky'.<br /> <br /> Either way if you guys did similarly or not, I look forward to seeing to how you vanquished that beast of a Purview. So important yet so poorly or inconsistently defined.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 02-03-2016, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T13:49:14-08:00","id":822705,"title":"","content":"Yeah.<br /> <br /> I'm also a big fan of how Forge is turning out, if only because our alpha crafting rules are suitable for making all kinds of stuff (like planning situations rather than actually constructing an artifact).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T14:15:27-08:00","id":822746,"title":"","content":"Oh that sounds neat. Planning is a very tricky thing to represent well using the toolkit from Scion, especially because a lot of the time you end up trying to play someone who is more intelligent than yourself if you're playing someone who is bothering to invest time and energy into planning. It becomes one of those situations where the character is limited by the player's own capacity. Manipulation and Wits both also end up having that problem sometimes, where if a player doesn't have the natural capacity for those things, it can be tricky for the character to really wield them.<br /> <br /> Is Forge going to be able to do any work with... I guess non-physical works of art? Poetry, music, oral-storytelling, that sort of thing? Those things can be exceptionally tricky to represent in a Deity's repertoire. Especially when it is something that is obviously important to the culture (Susano-O inventing poetry [localized cult center myth, so that's one of the 'grain of salt' myths], Cairbre inventing Satire, Apollo serenading others with his music, Dionysus being a patron of acting) but not particularly mechanics friendly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T14:44:04-08:00","id":822784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=822746#post822746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Forge going to be able to do any work with... I guess non-physical works of art? Poetry, music, oral-storytelling, that sort of thing? Those things can be exceptionally tricky to represent in a Deity's repertoire. Especially when it is something that is obviously important to the culture (Susano-O inventing poetry [localized cult center myth, so that's one of the 'grain of salt' myths], Cairbre inventing Satire, Apollo serenading others with his music, Dionysus being a patron of acting) but not particularly mechanics friendly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect poetry, music, skaldin', and the like are going to be a weird intersection of Forge and Passion Purviews and Sage and Lover Knacks. I may have to make a few Edges for that sort of thing specifically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T15:19:23-08:00","id":822819,"title":"","content":"That would be very cool to see. The oral storytelling is something that I've always wanted to be able to represent in the system, since it's pretty important across a wide range of cultures. Especially when you get that interesting 'Immortality' that the Indo-Europeans occasionally have kicking around with the stories that will be told forever. Not actually living forever, but having the tales of your glory lasting for an eternity being almost better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T03:09:38-08:00","id":823195,"title":"","content":"So how many purviews are there in total at the moment?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T06:25:56-08:00","id":823284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=823195#post823195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how many purviews are there in total at the moment?</div> </div> </div> </div>23 General Purviews and 10 PSPs, though 4 GPs probably won't be in <b>Hero</b>, or will be stretch goal content. This differs from pantheon stretch goals in that they will, eventually, be published, just possibly not in <b>Hero</b>. Although, one of them is the GP for city gods, so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T10:55:02-08:00","id":823505,"title":"","content":"Well that's alot. Awesome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T12:22:39-08:00","id":823596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=822594#post822594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fire was coming along well, but now that we've decided to incorporate Passion, I'm wondering if a number of Fire Boons wouldn't be more appropriate there. But I think Stars is my favorite.</div> </div> </div> </div>*shakes fist* damn you, capricious dev!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T12:35:23-08:00","id":823616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=823596#post823596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*shakes fist* damn you, capricious dev!</div> </div> </div> </div>Poor Vance had to go through a lot of my, &quot;But let's try it <i>this </i>way...&quot; before we hit on something I really liked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T14:02:40-08:00","id":823691,"title":"","content":"So I take it then that Boons this time will have levels that make sense rather then each boon having arbitrary levels all willy nilly? I have faith in you! And is there a system with the purviews to have more freeform powers at each level to go along with the specific powers?<br /> <br /> How much are Gods going to have Attributes inferred, like the old Dodekatheon had a bunch of Charisma, Stamina, and Manipulation foisted on the gods because I guess it was assumed they were political.<br /> <br /> Will Herakles be a patron from the Start?<br /> <br /> <br /> Pleeeeease don't be afraid to have things be asymetrical! In the 1st ed it felt soooo forced when everyone was balanced having equal numbers yada yada. Like it felt ham fisted that a lot of things were said to be demigod level just because the Underworld was in the Demigod book, like Valhalla and Nidhoggr. And not all Mighty Gods should be the same strength. Tyr and Thor both had Epic Strength but in their adventure together Thor had to lift a giant Cauldron Tyr was not strong enough to carry.<br /> <br /> Though I believe you guys said epics are way different now, more like Purviews?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T00:03:16-08:00","id":824067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=822307#post822307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, she's not a dominatrix, I'll tell you <i>that </i>much.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bThank you very much.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T08:55:45-08:00","id":824356,"title":"","content":"Well, arriving late has its perks sometimes. For example, you get to read that whole conversation between Watcher and Neall completely instead of hitting F5 each 30 minutes. I mean, with that back and forth i had the feeling i should be grabbing some popcorn at some point. Welcome to the hype train (also, those focused/broad mechanics about the Boons/Purviews? Oh, yes.).<br /> <br /> Keep up the good work! <br /> <br /> I'd like to volunteer also to the playtest when is finally open.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T16:18:41-08:00","id":824654,"title":"","content":"Phersus: Right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T10:37:11-08:00","id":824997,"title":"","content":"Absolutely xD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T10:44:44-08:00","id":825468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=822306#post822306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Athena and Minerva is the Greco-Roman goddess of war (strategy), crafts, wisdom, courage, civilization, mathematics, the city of Athens, and olive oil. In terms of Callings, she <i>heavily </i>favors Sage and Warrior.<br /> <br /> Athena presents a challenge for the designers, in that we don't have Epic Intelligence anymore (though the Physical Epics have been subsumed into Purviews) but that &quot;wisdom&quot; and &quot;mathematics&quot; is difficult to adequately interpolate in our design schema. Gods, over a very broad and reductive view of mythology, tend to be a lot more physically powerful than humanity, yet while they're often <i>wiser </i>or more far-seeing they're not always much smarter. Athena, though, does tend to be really damn smart.<br /> <br /> Ultimately I'm going for a brute-force and low-powered solution - she's &quot;only&quot; got superhuman Attributes, specialties, and Knacks to help her with knowledge-based rolls - and she works that through various Purviews like Passion to kindle clear thought and reason in others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if there's anything that just un-sold this version for me, this is it. I'm not a fan of systems that basically make physical powers the only viable thing. The Dresden Files RPG had this exact problem and the GM and players said 'well the system and world setting don't allow for super-intelligence like abilities.'<br /> <br /> Except the setting actually did 'super-intelligence' with local omniscience for some characters and I cribbed a fairly basic skillset out for that system, but that basically got me to the point of quitting the campaign because of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T11:06:39-08:00","id":825478,"title":"","content":"Any thoughts on how to handle.. let's call them &quot;Father Figure Gods&quot;? I.e. gods that are mentioned once (or maybe twice, but rarely more) within canonical texts or legends, but usually never do much except for maybe creating the world? Damballah of the Loa would come to mind as he created the world, but rarely intervenes and usually doesn't interact with other gods in any well-known stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T12:45:00-08:00","id":825539,"title":"","content":"Izanagi is another example there, I kinda thought he was more like a titan since his role seems to be restricted to create Japan with Izanami; create various element gods (kagatsuchi being the only one whose name I can recall); and create Amaterasu, Susanno-O, and Tsukuyomi; then leave the stage entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T15:25:31-08:00","id":825624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=825468#post825468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if there's anything that just un-sold this version for me, this is it. I'm not a fan of systems that basically make physical powers the only viable thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arthur, man, I feel like there's literally nothing I can write that you won't take out of context and in the worst possible manner.<br /> <br /> There's other ways of doing omniscience, far sight, and cunning in the game than Epic Intelligence, and those mostly belong in the Sage Calling. There are powers of prophecy and divination, and wisdom and cunning, will be represented. But, no, sorry, unless they're gods of genius or they were geniuses before apotheosis - like Zhuge Liang or Imhotep - you're not going to see many powers of super-intelligence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T16:01:54-08:00","id":825634,"title":"","content":"As a curiosity, if the game system going to be so heavily defensive oriented? Specificially is bashing damage going to be such a bad idea? As stands a weapon like a bo staff or a shortstick is going to be a really bad idea unless you have a phenomenal amount of Epic Strength to force damage through, or you invest in the weapon being able to do Lethal damage.<br /> <br /> There are a range of cool 'bashing' weapons that really don't get a lot of play because they're functionally useless. Any chance they're going to be any more useful this time around? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T20:43:57-08:00","id":825743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=825624#post825624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Arthur, man, I feel like there's literally nothing I can write that you won't take out of context and in the worst possible manner.<br /> <br /> There's other ways of doing omniscience, far sight, and cunning in the game than Epic Intelligence, and those mostly belong in the Sage Calling. There are powers of prophecy and divination, and wisdom and cunning, will be represented. But, no, sorry, unless they're gods of genius or they were geniuses before apotheosis - like Zhuge Liang or Imhotep - you're not going to see many powers of super-intelligence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet you described that you could not (or did not) make a replacement purview for Epic Intelligence, even though you said you did for the Epic Strength abilities.<br /> <br /> That sounds to me like they are not getting a fair change over treatment. Losing Epic Appearance might be able to be worked around, but losing Epic Intelligence with no clear replacement is a bit of a slap in the face. Only gods of strength need be modeled, ignore the gods of knowledge and wisdom.<br /> <br /> So no, everything I'm hearing now is 'this is only sorta related to Scion 1E, but we are going to call it 2E.' Change for change's sake, etc. It very well could be fun, but at this point it's so different you might as well rename it. I was really looking forward to 2E originally, but the more I hear the less invested I'm in.<br /> <br /> (sorry for the snippiness, but my headache isn't helping me convey how disappointed I am in more polite terms.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1246,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","user":"ArthurHansen","date":". 02-07-2016, 11:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T22:02:19-08:00","id":825768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arthur, man, I feel like there's literally nothing I can write that you won't take out of context and in the worst possible manner.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoa; prescient.<br /> <br /> Arthur, a nitpick: intelligence isn't wisdom; and Neall specifically mentioned that he <i>is</i> tackling the latter. As for the former, I suspect that TC: Aberrant will have plenty to say on that topic; and given the co-development of the two gamelines, I won't be surprised if there's a relatively easy way to port that into Scion if you actually find that you need it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-08-2016, 01:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T01:45:15-08:00","id":825843,"title":"","content":"Everybody should just ignore everything that Arthur ever posts. It has no real meaning and it is never constructive. He is quite simply a troll.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T04:05:57-08:00","id":825908,"title":"","content":"Instead of Epic Intelligence in sounds like you use specific powers to narrow your competence. You will have the tools for instance to be a Divine Inventor. But you don't have something that just makes SMRT.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T06:00:34-08:00","id":825948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Squee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=825634#post825634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a curiosity, if the game system going to be so heavily defensive oriented? Specificially is bashing damage going to be such a bad idea? As stands a weapon like a bo staff or a shortstick is going to be a really bad idea unless you have a phenomenal amount of Epic Strength to force damage through, or you invest in the weapon being able to do Lethal damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't have bashing damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T06:14:06-08:00","id":825957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=825743#post825743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So no, everything I'm hearing now is 'this is only sorta related to Scion 1E, but we are going to call it 2E.' Change for change's sake, etc. It very well could be fun, but at this point it's so different you might as well rename it. I was really looking forward to 2E originally, but the more I hear the less invested I'm in.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there's <i>any </i>accusation I hate more than &quot;change for change's sake&quot; I'd really love to hear it, so I can hate it more.<br /> <br /> Scion's going to be nine years old as of April, and - to be totally blunt - it has some deep-seated structural issues. I can't fix the issues in it without ripping the entire engine out, which we were doing anyways for a whole host of other reasons. While rebuilding it, I decided to take Knacks off Attributes and focus them on divine archetypes and the archetypal image, while broadening out the list of Purviews. The way we're doing the divide means that transhuman physical potential isn't tied to any specific archetype or personage, while gods of wisdom and intelligence have a very specific archetype (the Sage). Add to that I also wanted to largely avoid Reed Richards-as-God outside of specific Shards, and the old way of doing Epic Intelligence was gone.<br /> <br /> Arthur, we'll be putting up parts of the system for free in the Alpha. There will be backer drafts when this goes to KS. You don't like it, don't buy it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T06:47:06-08:00","id":825970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=825948#post825948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We don't have bashing damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two things:<br /> <br /> Firstly I read that in the voice of Siegfried from the original Get Smart: &quot;Schtocker. We don't have bashing damage here!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Secondly, yay! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Looking really forward to this Neall. Thanks for the quick turn-around answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T16:05:20-08:00","id":826360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=825957#post825957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If there's <i>any </i>accusation I hate more than &quot;change for change's sake&quot; I'd really love to hear it, so I can hate it more.<br /> <br /> Scion's going to be nine years old as of April, and - to be totally blunt - it has some deep-seated structural issues. I can't fix the issues in it without ripping the entire engine out, which we were doing anyways for a whole host of other reasons. While rebuilding it, I decided to take Knacks off Attributes and focus them on divine archetypes and the archetypal image, while broadening out the list of Purviews. The way we're doing the divide means that transhuman physical potential isn't tied to any specific archetype or personage, while gods of wisdom and intelligence have a very specific archetype (the Sage). Add to that I also wanted to largely avoid Reed Richards-as-God outside of specific Shards, and the old way of doing Epic Intelligence was gone.<br /> <br /> Arthur, we'll be putting up parts of the system for free in the Alpha. There will be backer drafts when this goes to KS. You don't like it, don't buy it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn this is all sounding juicy and good changes! You have my faith my good Sir! I mean you are a Famous Boat known to Fortitude after all...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T16:56:29-08:00","id":826391,"title":"","content":"Yeah, seems like I will not be buying anything more from Obsidian Path at this point. So it's just time for me to bow out, because who cares about people that liked the original Scion, flaws and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T17:00:46-08:00","id":826397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=826391#post826391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, seems like I will not be buying anything more from Obsidian Path at this point. So it's just time for me to bow out, because who cares about people that liked the original Scion, flaws and all.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you have all the tools of the Original Scion still at your disposal. Nothing stopping you from continuing with 1st ed fan stuff. But it needed to go in this direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T17:11:29-08:00","id":826406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=826391#post826391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, seems like I will not be buying anything more from Obsidian Path at this point. So it's just time for me to bow out, because who cares about people that liked the original Scion, flaws and all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hear you. I haven't bought anything from Obsidian Path in\u2026 well, I can't remember the last time. That said, I have my copy of Scion 1e should I ever want to use it, and I'm looking forward to Onyx Path's second edition of Scion when it comes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T19:40:43-08:00","id":826482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=826391#post826391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, seems like I will not be buying anything more from Obsidian Path at this point. So it's just time for me to bow out, because who cares about people that liked the original Scion, flaws and all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you enjoyed Scion 1ed, then I would recommend sticking with Scion 1ed with all the acknowledgement that you won't have much support outside of the fan supplements, people willing to debate old rules. I'm looking at the changes, and without context, they're making me incredibly wary - so I can see why you're concerned; but at the same time, there is a game still there for you: and fan supplements that still support the 1ed game. There's still a huge following for OWoD before the 20th anniversaries, after all.<br /> <br /> At the same time, while this all sounds incredibly like Hero's Journey (or does Hero's Journey sound like this?) you should wait until a playtest comes out, or the first kickstarter comes up before you make any definitive judgements.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T20:10:12-08:00","id":826498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=825743#post825743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds to me like they are not getting a fair change over treatment. Losing Epic Appearance might be able to be worked around, but losing Epic Intelligence with no clear replacement is a bit of a slap in the face. Only gods of strength need be modeled, ignore the gods of knowledge and wisdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are very few gods (any?) in most mythologies that are literally superhumanly intelligent though. They are wise and knowledgeable yes, but not trans-Einstein hyper intellects, so the absence of epic Intelligence makes sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T20:11:31-08:00","id":826500,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Squee;n825970]<br /> <br /> Firstly I read that in the voice of Siegfried from the original Get Smart: &quot;Schtocker. We don't have bashing damage here!&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> I will never be able to NOT hear Siegfried from get smart now... thank you for that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T20:29:54-08:00","id":826505,"title":"","content":"With your mention of gutting the system and building from the ground up again Neall, I thought of a few more questions prompted from more of the finicky ideas I've toyed with but mostly been limited by 1E's core system. They <i>really</i> are finicky however, most of them are the mechanical / balancing messes that it's totally reasonable to handwave around to make the game fun and balanced. Others of them are honestly a bit stupid, trying to model things in a system which probably should just be ignored for the sanity of everyone involved.<br /> <br /> It's totally justified to say, &quot;No Watcher, that's insane.&quot; to all of these. I'm just wondering if you guys have tried to work with these ideas, or, like myself, looked at them with a great deal of trepidation and looked around for a large rug to hide them under until an epiphany comes. Just idol curiosity if you guys have anything in store in these crazy tricky areas.<br /> <br /> 'Gods' can be wildly different in 'power' across Pantheons, and different Pantheons can have entirely different ideas of what makes a 'God' compared to others. The biggest example that springs to mind is how the Tuatha are <i>very</i> mortal, while the Theoi are supposed to be totally and utterly immortal (With strange exceptions in Aesculapius and Pan) which necessitates why they are imprisoning everything that is Divine rather than just killing things. In displays of power, the Tuatha and the Theoi also exist on wildly different ends of the spectrum, with Greek Deities hurling mountains but not being noted for being particularly strong, where the Tuatha's strongest figures show this by throwing flagstones the length of a hall or or hauling an impressively large club. Will these sorts of disparities be represented mechanically? Or for everyone's sanity will the large mechanical differences be limited to the PsPs?<br /> <br /> Then we have Fate. In Scion 1E, the Fate represented was very much the Grecian idea of Fate, or the Norse idea of Fate / Wyrd, an unstoppable and insurmountable force even for the Deities that can doom even them (Ragnarok, The Son of Zeus). However, this idea of Fate is inconsistent with other cultures. The Deva noted in internal theology to be 'beyond' their concept of Fate which grips only lesser beings. The Mesopotamians didn't seem to have 'Fate' anything like we see in Scion 1E, with their closest concept being a bit more like, 'The Will of the Gods'. The Orisha who have Fate that one <i>must</i> uphold, bit are not compelled to do so, with the mandate left to an individual to fulfill least bad things happen if they fail or refuse. Then I'm sure there is a Pantheon somewhere that entirely lacks the concept, but it's a bit late here and my memory is not coming particularly quite forthcoming. Are you guys going to have different 'versions' of Fate? I feel like you may have hinted to this with the Norse specifically having Wyrd as a PsP, but I just wanted to ask if it went beyond the doom 'n gloom Aesir.<br /> <br /> There is also the really tricky Pan-Pantheon Deities like Manannan (Irish) - Manawydan (Welsh), Quetzalcoatl (Aztec) - Kukulkan (Mayan), Kannon (Japanese Buddhism) - Guanyin (Chinese Buddhism). Do you have any idea how they will be handled in Scion 2E? Treat them all as individual Deities or try to work out a way to have Pan-Pantheon figures without being a balance mess running around with multiple PsPs. EDIT: This question has totally already been asked and answered, entirely slipped my mind, sorry!<br /> <br /> The Deities who annoyingly went and changed over the course of their depiction are also a pain to represent. For example, Aphrodite and Venus are so drastically different in attitude it's shocking. Aphrodite running around being cruel, vapid, and self centered, where as Venus suddenly becomes a bit benevolent with her helping her son Aeneas. Ares who went from being an incontinent, a bit mad, most-despised of Zeus' children, to Mars, a familial and state protector who is painted much more as an upstanding and not incoherently screaming warrior. Or, Set being quickly demonized with the rise of the Cult of Isis/Osiris/Horus. Do you guys have anything to try to explain or way to represent mechanically those strange abnormalities of personality, or just leave that for individual Storytellers to sort out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 02-09-2016, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T21:55:53-08:00","id":826558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=826498#post826498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are very few gods (any?) in most mythologies that are literally superhumanly intelligent though. They are wise and knowledgeable yes, but not trans-Einstein hyper intellects, so the absence of epic Intelligence makes sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it seems more like we don't have much instances of Super Intelligence as often we have specific talents, like super counting, and omnipresence. The potential is there but the point is it is not something the stories exist to tell. I mean Super Wisdom and Super Intelligence are both ambiguous concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T00:21:45-08:00","id":826623,"title":"","content":"I've been watching this for a while, and had a couple of thoughts. The problem with Super Intelligence is that we mere mortals have a harder time using it in games than, say Super Strength. How do you simulate Isis' supreme knowledge in a game? Have her know what the mortal players are going to do before they do it? Give her scads of dice and make it impossible to outwit her? As long as there is a system to represent Gods/Goddesses of Wisdom and Intelligence, so that they can aid their faithful, it doesn't really matter how it's done. At this point, it's not really possible to comment on how this is all going to come together. Scion 1st Edition was broken. A new game, call it what you will, is definitely needed. This all sounds like a serious attempt is being made to put together something that will be a lot more balanced, play-tested, and true to Mythological tales than the first game. Those who don't like it don't have to buy it. I'm certainly interested to hear more as this is developed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T00:54:06-08:00","id":826634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=826505#post826505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is also the really tricky Pan-Pantheon Deities like Manannan (Irish) - Manawydan (Welsh), Quetzalcoatl (Aztec) - Kukulkan (Mayan), Kannon (Japanese Buddhism) - Guanyin (Chinese Buddhism). Do you have any idea how they will be handled in Scion 2E? Treat them all as individual Deities or try to work out a way to have Pan-Pantheon figures without being a balance mess running around with multiple PsPs.<br /> <br /> The Deities who annoyingly went and changed over the course of their depiction are also a pain to represent. For example, Aphrodite and Venus are so drastically different in attitude it's shocking. Aphrodite running around being cruel, vapid, and self centered, where as Venus suddenly becomes a bit benevolent with her helping her son Aeneas. Ares who went from being an incontinent, a bit mad, most-despised of Zeus' children, to Mars, a familial and state protector who is painted much more as an upstanding and not incoherently screaming warrior. Or, Set being quickly demonized with the rise of the Cult of Isis/Osiris/Horus. Do you guys have anything to try to explain or way to represent mechanically those strange abnormalities of personality, or just leave that for individual Storytellers to sort out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Neall's mentioned the concept of divine mantles, which are tied to a god's Legend rating; Zeus, Jupiter, and Tinia are all the same god, but mantling different dots of Legend. Similarly with Quetzalcoatl and Kulkulkan - same god, but different mantles for different cultures and pantheons.<br /> <br /> Last Neall mentioned, gods who belong to multiple pantheons can learn their respective PSPs.<br /> <br /> (Set's an interesting case - not sure whether he'd be a case of Fatebinding or mantling.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T04:54:36-08:00","id":826702,"title":"","content":"Ah yes of course! I remember reading about that previously, sorry that totally slipped my mind!<br /> <br /> Set is always just very weird. He's my favorite example how religions change over time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T10:59:06-08:00","id":826946,"title":"","content":"I'm getting the impression that as time passes and a hero ascends towards godhood they kind of calcify in their roles and what they're capable of, or at least what they have influence over.<br /> <br /> Is this correct?<br /> <br /> (Also, if this is retreading old ground and I missed where this was discussed earlier could someone point it out to me? Thanks!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T14:19:48-08:00","id":827088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=790453#post790453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can belong to multiple pantheons in the second edition.<br /> <br /> I <i>love </i>the Keepers of the World, and if anything they'll be a bigger part of 2e. There's even going to be a mechanic to sort of explain their big evil plan...<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div> I didnt really understood their plan in 1e. what were they trying to achieve exactly? Were they trying to become the only gods or similar beings im the World?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T14:22:54-08:00","id":827089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=827088#post827088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didnt really understood their plan in 1e. what were they trying to achieve exactly? Were they trying to become the only gods or similar beings im the World?</div> </div> </div> </div>If memory serves, the Keepers of the World tried to sever the connection between the Overworlds and the Mortal World, as well as basically incapacitating the Titans by lobotomizing Gaia through Proxy. This was intended to make it so that mankind was finally free of both Gods and Titans to pursue its own destinity. Although both Imhothep and Weyland had pretty much their own idea on how this &quot;freedom&quot; should look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T14:54:26-08:00","id":827112,"title":"","content":"Wouldnt lobotomizyng Gaea help other Titans,for thered be less competition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T17:57:23-08:00","id":827214,"title":"","content":"I forgot about the whole Lobotomy thing. I feel Heracles reaaaally should be in the Core Dodekatheon Gods first presented. His popularity is comparable to Thor and Loki. And if he was actually in the core I feel a lot more players would be a Scion of Herakles. That Said didn't he have all three Physicals favored? Seemed a bit much also giving him Dex...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T19:17:52-08:00","id":827268,"title":"","content":"I understand some of the reasoning for it. He literally created the Olympic games and set the standard for the ancient events. He was also really good with a bow. I suppose they could have left it at having completely blown a lot of xp on Arete but it would be plain old cheaper to just have a good Dex to cover all of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T23:20:36-08:00","id":827336,"title":"","content":"Any info you can give us on how fast you think players will be moving up in legend and tiers of play? Like exalted is currently running on the assumption you go from essence 1 to 5 in 60 sessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T07:09:33-08:00","id":827487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm getting the impression that as time passes and a hero ascends towards godhood they kind of calcify in their roles and what they're capable of, or at least what they have influence over.<br /> <br /> Is this correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>More or less. It becomes much more involved to change, due to Fatebindings and the fact that your power flows from the divine archetypal image you've created. Changing means getting your hands dirty with mortals, and that could lead to much bigger unintended consequences.<br /> <br /> There's a reset button, but most Gods don't care for it, and there's no guarantee (and a lot stacked against) things happening differently the second time around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=827336#post827336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any info you can give us on how fast you think players will be moving up in legend and tiers of play? Like exalted is currently running on the assumption you go from essence 1 to 5 in 60 sessions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like players to hit divinity after about a year of solid weekly play of 4-5 hour sessions, and &quot;cap out&quot; at Legend 12 about six months later. Once you're a God, though, you can jockey for position in a pantheon and potentially lose Legend (<i>especially </i>if you're Tuatha), so there's what the MMOs refer to as &quot;endgame content&quot;. There's a few capstone arcs to God, especially with making your own pantheon and Creation Myth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand some of the reasoning for it. He literally created the Olympic games and set the standard for the ancient events. He was also really good with a bow. I suppose they could have left it at having completely blown a lot of xp on Arete but it would be plain old cheaper to just have a good Dex to cover all of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>He most likely would have all three Physical Epics favored, yeah - and honestly, that's about it. He might also have Stars associated with him, but I doubt he has any Boons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T07:32:08-08:00","id":827501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=827487#post827487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once you're a God, though, you can jockey for position in a pantheon and potentially lose Legend (<b><i>especially </i>if you're Tuatha</b>)</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn it, Neall! You can't drop something like that on us and not explain! It's immoral!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T08:08:25-08:00","id":827516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=827501#post827501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn it, Neall! You can't drop something like that on us and not explain! It's immoral!</div> </div> </div> </div>They're a restless bunch. You see how many kings they go through? Questing and wanderlust is in their DNA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T08:30:41-08:00","id":827538,"title":"","content":"Hey neall,in your opinion which titan would be the scariest to face in battle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T09:41:02-08:00","id":827580,"title":"","content":"Mike Martin? ...I'll see myself out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T13:14:52-08:00","id":827734,"title":"","content":"Hello Neall, thanks for answering so many questions. I read through the topics during the last couple of days and it made me so freaking excited for Scion 2.0. Can't wait to actually read it. It would be so nice to have a system that doesn't need hundreds of tweeks and house rules to be playable. Here is my question though: Can you tell us what purviews will be included in the core rules as of now. That would be fantastic. Thank you very much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11209-blackfyre","name":"Blackfyre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11209_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T14:41:42-08:00","id":827802,"title":"","content":"Or to build on that, how the Alpha slice is shaping up? Do we have any kind of broad estimate of when we'll see that?<br /> <br /> Should we hope for before GenCon, or set expectations accordingly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T18:13:55-08:00","id":827898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackfryre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=827734#post827734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is my question though: Can you tell us what purviews will be included in the core rules as of now. That would be fantastic. Thank you very much.</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Beasts, Darkness, Death, Earth, Epic Dexterity, Epic Might, Epic Stamina, Fertility, Fire, Forge, Fortune, <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Frost, </span></span>Health, Illusion, Moon, Sky, Sun, War, Water. There's four more I've got planned as potential stretch goals or Companion material.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should we hope for before GenCon, or set expectations accordingly?</div> </div> </div> </div>It'll be out well before Gen Con, but it's <i>just </i>an Alpha slice - a basic Purview or two, the basic rules, and some pre-gen characters. Nothing huge!</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T19:53:34-08:00","id":827936,"title":"","content":"So question is Scion Origin or Scion Hero going to be the Corebook? Its Hero right? Then does that Mean Origin will come after Hero?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T20:01:21-08:00","id":827940,"title":"","content":"Do some pantheons share gods because of fatebinding?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T20:25:21-08:00","id":827951,"title":"","content":"Will you achieve Godhood even if you are not specifically trying? I mean can you play extended time at one of the lower levels without bending the rules? I've never been toooo keen on rushing through all the stages, yet I can see why we don't want it taking tooooo long to reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T20:46:46-08:00","id":827961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=827936#post827936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So question is Scion Origin or Scion Hero going to be the Corebook? Its Hero right? Then does that Mean Origin will come after Hero?</div> </div> </div> </div>Origin is going to be the core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T20:49:15-08:00","id":827963,"title":"","content":"Do gods still can become avatars of their purview?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T23:39:12-08:00","id":828039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=827961#post827961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Origin is going to be the core book.</div> </div> </div> </div>And current plans are for Origin and Hero to be released together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T08:28:46-08:00","id":828230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=827898#post827898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Beasts, Darkness, Death, Earth, Epic Dexterity, Epic Might, Epic Stamina, Fertility, Fire, Forge, Fortune, <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Frost, </span></span>Health, Illusion, Moon, Sky, Sun, War, Water. There's four more I've got planned as potential stretch goals or Companion material.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>No Stars? I remember you mentioning it several times. Or is it one of the four potential stretch goals? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_b