/span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Health, Illusion, Moon, Sky, Sun, War, Water. There's four more I've got planned as potential stretch goals or Companion material.</span></span>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm interested in how you would model someone like Aphrodite. Out of the list above I can see her having some strong ties to Water, Beasts and Health..not sure how I'd manage the positive and negative aspects of Love/Lust/Passion though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T12:26:15-08:00","id":828917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=828899#post828899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm interested in how you would model someone like Aphrodite. Out of the list above I can see her having some strong ties to Water, Beasts and Health..not sure how I'd manage the positive and negative aspects of Love/Lust/Passion though.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're talking Aphrodite Ourania, then she could plausibly have Earth, Sky, or even Moon or Stars.<br /> <br /> Aphrodite is representative of the big overlap of the Lover Calling and the Passion Purview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T15:01:40-08:00","id":828969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=828917#post828917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're talking Aphrodite Ourania, then she could plausibly have Earth, Sky, or even Moon or Stars</div> </div> </div> </div>What citations are you using for these?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T21:04:38-08:00","id":829095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=828917#post828917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If we're talking Aphrodite Ourania, then she could plausibly have Earth, Sky, or even Moon or Stars.<br /> <br /> Aphrodite is representative of the big overlap of the Lover Calling and the Passion Purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>The second part, totally understandable.<br /> <br /> But... the only way I can see Aphrodite Ourania is if someone's going by her description as &quot;Celestial&quot; which ... is very confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T00:50:32-08:00","id":829165,"title":"","content":"What citations are you using for these?<br /> <br /> Any good source of Greek Mythology - online, there is Theoi, which covers the original source material for the Classical Mythology. Aphrodite is represented as either a Titan [daughter of Uranus], or a Goddess of Love [daughter of Zeus], depending on the original source used.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T06:58:14-08:00","id":829228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=829095#post829095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But... the only way I can see Aphrodite Ourania is if someone's going by her description as &quot;Celestial&quot; which ... is very confusing.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What citations are you using for these?</div> </div> </div> </div>Britannica, though as Purple Snit notes, nearly every online resource notes the varying terminology of what &quot;celestial&quot; means to a Titan. And it makes sense if you're looking at it in the Titanic or Mesopotamian sense, where celestial import means control over the world entire. But Aphrodite probably isn't going to have Earth, Sky, Moon, or Stars. I was mostly being flippant.<br /> <br /> (mmmmmaybe Stars or Sky, but probably not.)<br /> <br /> The idea that Aphrodite's parentage and by extension metaphysical character is of some ambiguity, even to herself, relates to another part of Scion's Gods and how they work in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 02-13-2016, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T12:12:50-08:00","id":829362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=829228#post829228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The idea that Aphrodite's parentage and by extension metaphysical character is of some ambiguity, even to herself, relates to another part of Scion's Gods and how they work in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are God's who are issues of titans stronger than God's that are sons of other gods ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T13:39:57-08:00","id":829393,"title":"","content":"I always felt Titan and God is a more a semantics argument, as in mythology they were just one tribe of God, so I like the idea of them being flexible in game. Because I wasn't a fan of many gods, like Mami Watu who has a sizeable number of worshipers, being shoehorned into roles as evil titans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T13:51:07-08:00","id":829396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=829393#post829393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always felt Titan and God is a more a semantics argument, as in mythology they were just one tribe of God, so I like the idea of them being flexible in game. Because I wasn't a fan of many gods, like Mami Watu who has a sizeable number of worshipers, being shoehorned into roles as evil titans.</div> </div> </div> </div> There is a pretty big difference God's are refined and sophisticated and complex,Titans are more simple,titans are not beings that control the elements or emotions like the God's do,titans don't need to control anything for they aee embodiments of concepts;like Zeus might be the master of sky and lighting;but ouraonos literaly is the sky;Loki can do anything with fire but surtur simply is fire. In the end the difference of god and titans is not of good and evil is a difference of scale","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T13:55:08-08:00","id":829399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=829396#post829396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a pretty big difference God's are refined and sophisticated and complex,Titans are more simple,titans are not beings that control the elements or emotions like the God's do,titans don't need to control anything for they aee embodiments of concepts;like Zeus might be the master of sky and lighting;but ouraonos literaly is the sky;Loki can do anything with fire but surtur simply is fire. In the end the difference of god and titans is not of good and evil is a difference of scale</div> </div> </div> </div>But that doesn't seem to always hold true, particularly with the Trimurti. And what is the difference between Zeus and Cronus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T14:01:35-08:00","id":829403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=829399#post829399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that doesn't seem to always hold true, particularly with the Trimurti. And what is the difference between Zeus and Cronus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Same thing between Zeus and Ouranos really,Zeus is a exttremely powerful dude that controls lightinh;but zeusvis a physical being zeus's true shape is of a man. Chronos in the other hand is not a giant man who controls Time;chronos is time itself he only looks like a giant cause he wants to have physical shape. Zeus is a person that manipulates a force of nature Chronos is a force of nature that mayblook like a person but isnt","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T14:03:51-08:00","id":829405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=829403#post829403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Same thing between Zeus and Ouranos really,Zeus is a exttremely powerful dude that controls lightinh;but zeusvis a physical being zeus's true shape is of a man. Chronos in the other hand is not a giant man who controls Time;chronos is time itself he only looks like a giant cause he wants to have physical shape. Zeus is a person that manipulates a force of nature Chronos is a force of nature that mayblook like a person but isnt</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is though Cronus and Chronos are two different entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T14:05:33-08:00","id":829407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=829405#post829405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is though Cronus and Chronos are two different entities.</div> </div> </div> </div> really? i thought it was just two spelling of the same name?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T14:09:39-08:00","id":829408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=829407#post829407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">really? i thought it was just two spelling of the same name?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cronus was the King of the Generations of the Gods Before Zeus, the Titans, Chronos was time personified and an Idea that came later. Some have suggested conflating both beings due to Fatebinding. But we don't really have much on what Cronus was the personification of, besides he was the leader of the Titans so I made him represent Rulership. But in legends Him and Zeus aren't really fundamentally different, except maybe Zeus had a more robust Childhood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T14:14:11-08:00","id":829410,"title":"","content":"Hmmm you probably right not this then, but can fatebinding literary combine two beings into one? How does that happen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T14:27:32-08:00","id":829414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=829410#post829410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm you probably right not this then, but can fatebinding literary combine two beings into one? How does that happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was just a random theory I saw posted before. But I guess a reasoning is Fatebinding can retroactively change history, so they may reveal they were the same person.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Neall what is the role Folklore will play in 2nd ed? Will they be tied to Mythology they are likely closest to, like Erlkoennig becoming a Troll? I thought that was rather cool, as well as Hamleth being a Scion of Vidar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T15:06:18-08:00","id":829426,"title":"","content":"I still think 2pac was Yahew Scion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T18:21:24-08:00","id":829497,"title":"","content":"I always felt that &quot;Titans&quot; were the personification of elemental concepts such as darkness, time, sky, sun, etc., but &quot;Gods&quot; were their more human-centric offspring, worshipped by and involved with the humans around them. At any rate, since Cronus is definitely father to Zeus, he can't be the same being; the Olympians are children of Titans, and fought against them - this is the whole inspiration for the Titanomachy that defines 1st edition Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T20:33:32-08:00","id":830009,"title":"","content":"Few questions after combing through the &quot;What We Know&quot; with a broad toothed comb...<br /> <br /> If you can't answer them for any reason feel free to affirm with a scratch on the nose or reply in the negative with a grandiose wink<br /> <br /> 1) Is Raven going to be a parent for the Manitouk Pantheon? <br /> 2) How will Divine Parentage work re: ethnicity? (IE, if I wanted to play a very dark skinned son of Odin (traditionally Nordic depicted))<br /> 3) Has there been any discussion on an Abrahamic Pantheon aside from hotly debated that I may have missed in the thread?<br /> <br /> \u200bThanks yo","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T08:15:19-08:00","id":830235,"title":"","content":"In Re 1: Unless it's just outright pandering to cultural stereotyping, it would be pretty hard to shoehorn in such a god, assuming you mean the post-Contact mish-mash of many different deities into one &quot;Raven&quot;, despite the fact that those mythologies referring to divine ravens come from many different groups and are irreconcilable. Like &quot;Coyote&quot;. In fact, in the materials I have to hand, I can't find anything like a raven figure in the core mythology, legends or folk tales of the people in question. Admittedly, the majority of what I have is Haudenosaunee. There might be something from the other Algonquian groups. Or something outside the easily accessible myths. There are people out there that have done a fair bit of close-in work on this and I'll defer to them to see if they can dig up something vaguely Raven-like from the relevant materials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T11:21:35-08:00","id":830352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=830009#post830009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Few questions after combing through the &quot;What We Know&quot; with a broad toothed comb...<br /> <br /> If you can't answer them for any reason feel free to affirm with a scratch on the nose or reply in the negative with a grandiose wink<br /> <br /> 1) Is Raven going to be a parent for the Manitouk Pantheon?<br /> 2) How will Divine Parentage work re: ethnicity? (IE, if I wanted to play a very dark skinned son of Odin (traditionally Nordic depicted))<br /> 3) Has there been any discussion on an Abrahamic Pantheon aside from hotly debated that I may have missed in the thread?<br /> <br /> \u200bThanks yo</div> </div> </div> </div>,<br /> <br /> Regarding 2, one of the better ways ways to handwavea lack of caring for ethnic considerations in terms of the gods (and as this directly applies to your question) look no further than the Varangian Guard; an elite sect of personal bodyguards normally of Nordic descent that served the Byzantine Empire. It was a highly considered honor and many men went there to make a name for themselves. There are Greeks who still prefer to their heritage as Varangian even though the order was long assimilated after the 14th century.<br /> <br /> Racism as we know it is not going to be something the Gods really bother with except maybe the Kami. I'm pretty certain Odin would be a-ok with a ethnic outsider as a son provided that said son is perfectly happy to play a part in Odin's schemes. Odin is also The Wanderer. Why would he care if his kid's dark-skinned?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T17:17:55-08:00","id":830623,"title":"","content":"Also the Aesir have jumped all kinds of 'outsiders' into the gang. Giants, mortals, the whole shebag. I really don't think he's going to worry about it. You're a bit out of luck if your daddy is Raiden (in more ways than one, there) or the Jade Emperor but Odin's a pretty good choice <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T00:16:02-08:00","id":830882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=830352#post830352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">,<br /> <br /> Regarding 2, one of the better ways ways to handwavea lack of caring for ethnic considerations in terms of the gods (and as this directly applies to your question) look no further than the Varangian Guard; an elite sect of personal bodyguards normally of Nordic descent that served the Byzantine Empire. It was a highly considered honor and many men went there to make a name for themselves. There are Greeks who still prefer to their heritage as Varangian even though the order was long assimilated after the 14th century.<br /> <br /> Racism as we know it is not going to be something the Gods really bother with except maybe the Kami. I'm pretty certain Odin would be a-ok with a ethnic outsider as a son provided that said son is perfectly happy to play a part in Odin's schemes. Odin is also The Wanderer. Why would he care if his kid's dark-skinned?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that question was in regards to how a pantheon would view scions from outside their &quot;traditional&quot; culture and more how it would work genetically.<br /> <br /> And I'd say probably very little, outside of certain standard rules (Odin is always missing an eye, Hephaestus always has a limp, and so on) I imagine the gods can look any way they want otherwise it would be pretty hard for the animal headed Egyptian gods or distinctly non human Aztec ones from siring any children.<br /> Not that anything from first edition is necessarily canon anymore but didn\u2019t demi-god have a write up for a novice band with a black son of Tyr, a white son of Isis, and a blonde daughter of Poseidon(The least odd but Greeks and Italians tend to have darker colorations in a general sense)?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T04:33:29-08:00","id":830954,"title":"","content":"A Scion does, in fact, have <i>two</i> parents most of the time; and hereditary features can come from either. So unless both mommy and daddy are norse, I don't see why daddy being Odin <i>requires</i> you to have nordic features.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T06:28:53-08:00","id":830983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=830954#post830954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Scion does, in fact, have <i>two</i> parents most of the time; and hereditary features can come from either. So unless both mommy and daddy are norse, I don't see why daddy being Odin <i>requires</i> you to have nordic features.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep!<br /> <br /> That's not even including Scions who were carved from a living ash tree or had life breathed into them from on high.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T08:08:04-08:00","id":831036,"title":"","content":"i think i may have asked this one before but just to be sure,are purview avatars still present?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 02-16-2016, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T09:12:59-08:00","id":831068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m