le=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absolutely, it is. <b>Origins</b> has several &quot;mortal level&quot; supernatural templates. The Xian, though, would likely be akin to demigods.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there's any way to get the White Eyebrow into this game as an evil scion of L\u01ceoz\u01d0 \u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T17:47:08-08:00","id":841029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=840968#post840968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there's any way to get the White Eyebrow into this game as an evil scion of L\u01ceoz\u01d0 \u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>laozi was a god?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T18:59:04-08:00","id":841058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=841029#post841029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">laozi was a god?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, he was worshiped as one. Depending on the tradition, he's sometimes considered to have been a manifestation of one of the Three Pure Ones. That said, having him serve as patron to Bai Mei seems rather strange to me, particularly since Bai Mei was supposed to have been an ex-Buddhist monk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T19:56:52-08:00","id":841071,"title":"","content":"He started out as a Buddhist monk, but his involvement with &quot;evil Daoist sorcery&quot; established him as a villain and/or got him thrown out of Sh\u00e0ol\u00edn depending on which apocryphal legend you like best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T21:05:48-08:00","id":841103,"title":"","content":"You can be Buddhist and Daoist, they are not mutually exclusive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T12:39:12-08:00","id":841435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=841071#post841071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He started out as a Buddhist monk, but his involvement with &quot;evil Daoist sorcery&quot; established him as a villain and/or got him thrown out of Sh\u00e0ol\u00edn depending on which apocryphal legend you like best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but I'm not sure I can see one of the Three Pure Ones being willing to tolerate heretical Daoist practices on the part of their students. Save them from the consequences of their bad decisions as in the case of Gold Horn and Silver Horn, sure, but letting them continue on that road?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=841103#post841103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can be Buddhist and Daoist, they are not mutually exclusive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of Chinese folk religion's syncretistic nature, but I appreciate the intent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T13:03:06-08:00","id":841457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Creticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=841435#post841435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but I'm not sure I can see one of the Three Pure Ones being willing to tolerate heretical Daoist practices on the part of their students. Save them from the consequences of their bad decisions as in the case of Gold Horn and Silver Horn, sure, but letting them continue on that road?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a story hook to me!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T11:27:59-08:00","id":842017,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">are there any plans for having books that go really deep into the details of each individual pantheon like ragnarok did with the norse?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T18:32:38-08:00","id":842319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=841457#post841457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like a story hook to me!</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha ha, true enough, no xianxia story would be complete without some intra-school shenanigans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T18:44:49-08:00","id":842326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=842017#post842017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">are there any plans for having books that go really deep into the details of each individual pantheon like ragnarok did with the norse?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Not on the level of full books. We might break them down into supplements, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T19:27:38-08:00","id":842345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=664301#post664301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> the Dagda, mantled as the Red Man of All Knowledge.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div> i was curious about that really,do all god's mantles have tiles names like the Red Man of All Knowledge? if so,can yo give one or two examples","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 03-04-2016, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T09:35:29-08:00","id":844009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=599816#post599816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I'll tell you <i>three</i>,</span></span> and the fourth you can guess if you read every supplement in 1e. Ask me at Gen Con and I'll confirm it.<br /> <br /> 1) Be a Scion of god and mortal born, like 100 percent of the people on this planet (though I'm not sure in vitro would work, and I don't think it would, so knock a few decimal points off, I guess). Also works for adopted Scions, but you always retain some part of your parentage, even if Auntie Athena raised you and you really take after her.<br /> 2) Be a Scion created by a god from inanimate materials, brought to life by miraculous means. Enkidu is my go-to example. It takes a decent bit of work on the part of the god, even if you're Ninhursag (a top-tier creation deity), and it takes some association with mortality (thanks, Shamhat), but you're essentially custom-created by the god.<br /> 3) Be transformed in infancy by miraculous means. You must be the descendent of mortal nobility, or possibly have some sort of divine lineage far enough in your line to be suitably transformed. Triptolemus is my go-to example; Adonis would also be suitable, though it raises some questions from his inclusion in the Phoenician pantheon*. But I'm not about to limit character concepts, because clearly the vehicle towards Scionhood is <i>there</i>, so you can take his Greek origin as an acknowledgement of &quot;yeah, that's a way&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Demigod to God. Ixion created the centaurs, both horse and biker variants. He still does, the jerk.<br /> <br /> Creating new subrealms and sub-pantheons is something you can do as a god. New Overworlds, pantheons, creation myths and altering the structure of the World is an appropriate end of a major, years-long epic campaign.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, right now it's Fire, because we've been using it as a go-to example of how gods with a similar Purview have radically different expressions; the three characters we've been bandying about are Brigid, Loki and Agni. The first only has it because of syncretized Catholicism, and the metaphorical association with ritual purification and healing. Loki's expression is because his mother is lightning and his father is pine needles, but also because he (maybe) beat up a god with a similar name who was the literal expression of fire, stole that god's mantle, and threatened to burn the whole fucking place down**. Agni's expression of the Purview encompasses fires in virtually all forms metaphorical and literal, including inspiration and also blowing shit up.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*Maybe Adonis was originally Greek and joined the Phoenician pantheon in the Scion setting. I haven't really decided yet either way.<br /> **We also discussed expression through dogs as a joke, but talking Marvel raises a lot of hackles around these parts.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>whos agni?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T10:01:00-08:00","id":844022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=844009#post844009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">whos agni?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hindu god of fire and inspiration. As god of the sacrificial fire, he is the one who conveys sacrifices to the gods.<br /> <br /> Interestingly for a god of fire, he's also associated with water.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T10:01:14-08:00","id":844023,"title":"","content":"Agni is the Hindu God of Fire and Messengers<br /> <br /> Ninja'd","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T11:04:53-08:00","id":844057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=844022#post844022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hindu god of fire and inspiration. As god of the sacrificial fire, he is the one who conveys sacrifices to the gods.<br /> <br /> Interestingly for a god of fire, he's also associated with water.</div> </div> </div> </div> i thoght it was a Hawaiin god,dont know why. Maybe he was also associated with the water because of the duality theme we see in some myths","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T20:25:55-08:00","id":844312,"title":"","content":"Agni is associated with Water mostly in the Vedas because he's the conduit for Vedic sacrifice and the primary purpose of sacrifice is to bring the rains. In addition, he is variously called the father, the son, and the grandson of Water. As the Fire of the Sun, he causes the oceans to evaporate and form the clouds, hence he is their father...as the Fire of Lightning, he is born of the Water of the clouds, hence he is their son, and as the Fire of, well, Fire, he is born of the fuel of wood, which is born of rains, hence he is the grandson of Water. The 35th hymn of the 2nd Mandala of the Rig Veda is specifically dedicated to Agni as Apam Napat (Grandson of the Waters) and calls him the supreme creator and all other Gods are referred to as branches of him.<br /> <br /> Arguably, the entirety of Vedic religion is primarily concerned with two topics, Light and Water, and how the three supreme lights, the Flame of Agni, the Lightning of Indra, and the Sun of the Adityas, give Water in the form of rains to mankind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T00:44:16-08:00","id":844382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=844022#post844022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hindu god of fire and inspiration. As god of the sacrificial fire, he is the one who conveys sacrifices to the gods.<br /> <br /> Interestingly for a god of fire, he's also associated with water.</div> </div> </div> </div>Brighid does both also.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T07:41:40-08:00","id":844502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=844382#post844382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Brighid does both also.</div> </div> </div> </div>i thoguht she was a sex goddess?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T08:00:26-08:00","id":844508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=842326#post842326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not on the level of full books. We might break them down into supplements, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>what are the current supplements plans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T08:27:21-08:00","id":844523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=844508#post844508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what are the current supplements plans?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not defined yet. My preference would be for smaller supplements and a full-court press into Demigod.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T20:48:18-08:00","id":844893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=844502#post844502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i thoguht she was a sex goddess?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only in the broader sense of spring and fertility. She's not an equivalent of Aphrodite or Ishtar.<br /> <br /> Primarily she's the triple-goddess of the hearth, the forge, and poetry (fire of the soul), but also has an association with freshwater springs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T06:39:37-08:00","id":845043,"title":"","content":"Has there been any updates on the new birthright/relic creation rules? A few questions I have...<br /> <br /> 1. Are relics going to still be a fairly vague system where anything can be created? While I loved the 1st edition rules with relics being so open I realize it was an absolute pain to balance them for each character. Is the new system going to be a bit more streamlined or easier to work with?<br /> <br /> 2. Are creatures and summons going to be more viable overall? I recall a player of mine who had a Raiden scion with 15 lightning elemental archers (reskinned and tweaked police). Eventually we got to a Minotaur (essentially one of the first high soak enemies) and even with all 15 of them attacking in conjunction with her it seemed they just couldn't even scratch it. In general it seemed summons and creatures just didn't scale well.<br /> <br /> 3. Any plans on making relic firearms a thing that actually works? I'm all for mundane firearms being crap against demigods and gods but I'd really like the idea that a relic firearm can be used effectively just as long as any other weapon.<br /> <br /> (Random question)<br /> 4. Bows vs Thrown popped into my head as I was asking that last question. Bows in general seemed to lack identity in the end game. Scions could throw weapons around the world, guns didn't work at all, and bows (while scaling off str) still had this pipsqeak range that really held them back. Just hoping that if Relic Firearms make a comeback that atleast bows will have a unique niche within the game.<br /> <br /> (Final Random Question)<br /> 5. Any hope we can see weapons reduced to a more simplified system like exalted 3rd edition? The weapon list was sort of a mess in 1st edition. Not only were they all semi obscure ancient weapon names the stats seemed to be all over the place. Hard to justify certain weapons over others except for flavor reason.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance! Hope the above questions don't come off as nitpicky or negative, I just really want to see Scion 2nd edition blow the 1st edition out of the water. Hopeing to help make it as solid of a system as it can be so people can play it with minimal need for big homebrew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T07:11:35-08:00","id":845052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=845043#post845043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has there been any updates on the new birthright/relic creation rules? A few questions I have...<br /> <br /> 1. Are relics going to still be a fairly vague system where anything can be created? While I loved the 1st edition rules with relics being so open I realize it was an absolute pain to balance them for each character. Is the new system going to be a bit more streamlined or easier to work with?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not anything, but there's support for crafting characters (and a Forge Purview), as well as a system where you just append dots at character creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Are creatures and summons going to be more viable overall? I recall a player of mine who had a Raiden scion with 15 lightning elemental archers (reskinned and tweaked police). Eventually we got to a Minotaur (essentially one of the first high soak enemies) and even with all 15 of them attacking in conjunction with her it seemed they just couldn't even scratch it. In general it seemed summons and creatures just didn't scale well. </div> </div> </div>The whole system is built to do scaling well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Any plans on making relic firearms a thing that actually works? I'm all for mundane firearms being crap against demigods and gods but I'd really like the idea that a relic firearm can be used effectively just as long as any other weapon. </div> </div> </div>Yes, relic firearms will be as effective as other relic ranged weapons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. Bows vs Thrown popped into my head as I was asking that last question. Bows in general seemed to lack identity in the end game. Scions could throw weapons around the world, guns didn't work at all, and bows (while scaling off str) still had this pipsqeak range that really held them back. Just hoping that if Relic Firearms make a comeback that atleast bows will have a unique niche within the game. </div> </div> </div>I don't know about unique, but it'll work. I toyed with bows being the top ranged weapon, guns being the best at providing Evocation Boons, and spears and thrown weapons being somewhere in between.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5. Any hope we can see weapons reduced to a more simplified system like exalted 3rd edition? The weapon list was sort of a mess in 1st edition. Not only were they all semi obscure ancient weapon names the stats seemed to be all over the place. Hard to justify certain weapons over others except for flavor reason. </div> </div> </div>Yes, they're simplified. They should mostly scale with the character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thanks in advance! </div> </div> </div>You're welcome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T07:29:03-08:00","id":845062,"title":"","content":"Awesome stuff! All good news so far. Clarification on the first question though. I was actually referring to character creation. When you chose your birthright options and built your custom starting relics (by spending points) you could create some pretty interesting stuff. The system got a extra chart in the companion guide (I think that was the one) that helped with assigning point values to certain benefits. Overall it seemed like the intention was that you could easily make up stuff from scratch. Long story short, one guy in my party had a ironman like suit with alot of logistics to it so he could summon it to him alongside his weapon and my other buddy had a amulet that let him be a sort of D&amp;D wizard. Awesome stuff in the end but overall I had a hard time balancing it all to work smoothly. Sure, my bad for trying to do full on custom relics but it did seem like that was the hinted intent.<br /> <br /> I guess long question short, are we going to get another chart with point costs for certain benefits that will make unique birthright/relic creation easier? A bigger or more encompassing list? I think back to Mutants and Masterminds and how they allowed you to essentially build everything from a list of components.<br /> <br /> In the end, id rather see it (a) just become less open but more refined and balanced or (b) completely open easyish to create about anything akin to Mutants and Masterminds or other point based system.<br /> <br /> In all honesty, id probably learn more towards wanting A personally. Sure, tons of open options are great... but ultimately that tends to create power disparity when some people want flavorful items and others want nuclear warheads attached to weapons essentially. There is always going to be power disparity in a open progress dot based game but any way we could lessen that would be great.<br /> <br /> Which leads me into what should be my final random question.<br /> <br /> - Any easier magic blasty options? Seemed like purviews didn't have many direct elemental blasts (atleast early) that someone could build a character off of. Part of the reason I had to design an entire mana/magic blasting relic.<br /> <br /> Thanks alot Neall! Really love the level of interaction you are having with the fans during development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 03-10-2016, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T09:10:32-08:00","id":845114,"title":"","content":"1)Do you think Hercules should have the purvie Stars? after all he became an constellation<br /> 2) So if Fate and Fatebinding power over the Gods will change is it still possible to use Fatebending to force gods to become willing servants of Another god,or A titan? like they did in Scion:Companion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T09:22:37-08:00","id":845124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=845114#post845114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1)Do you think Hercules should have the purvie Stars? after all he became an constellation</div> </div> </div> </div>An interesting question. I would give it to him. Then I thought about it further. Would Phobos and his dread brother get Moon since they have Moons named after them? Or any of the planets with their corresponding deities like Aphordite/Venus","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T09:27:57-08:00","id":845126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=845124#post845124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An interesting question. I would give it to him. Then I thought about it further. Would Phobos and his dread brother get Moon since they have Moons named after them? Or any of the planets with their corresponding deities like Aphordite/Venus</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm,i think yes,because when you throw fatebinding into the mix,that changes everything about them gods. so if thousands of people start to call a moon Phobos,maybe fate will decide phobos will have a deep connectiont to that moon and thus he gains the moon purview,cause the moon is part of who phobos is now. same thing with hercules,millions of people named a group of starts Hercules,fate will follow suit and make those stars are part of hercules is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T12:02:52-08:00","id":845201,"title":"","content":"Hmm...I guess it depends a bit on exactly what these purviews represent. For instance, do the moons Phobos and Deimos have any mythical associations to them that are similar to the ones given to our own moon? Where they even recognized as other moons? Or where Phobos and Deimos the moons just sharing the characterization already present in Phobos and Deimos, with nothing of significant being added from being represented by celestial bodies?<br /> <br /> Personally, I probably would not give Herakles a Stars Purview. Too broad of a powerset* for someone who is just represented in a constellation and with, as far as I know, no mythical associations with powers from or over the stars in general. In the same way, I don't think, say, Mars, should have some sort of planetary purview just because he is represented by a Planet.<br /> <br /> <br /> It probably makes sense that such Fate Bindings might occur, but I think in many cases a Purview might not be the best way to represent it. Gods have some sort of &quot;seat/place of power&quot; mechanic this time around, right? A place where they are stronger? Maybe such bindings can give rise to such a place in some form? Like, Ares has his place in Olympus, and a lesser seat of power on the red planet?<br /> <br /> Maybe specific Mantles? I'm still not sure exactly what those do and how far a god changes in different Mantles, but there might be something there to allow for the less common interpretations of a given divinity to be expressed.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Of course, that can change depending on how far one can personalize and specialize Purviews in second edition. But it still seems far fetched to me to present Hercules with any sort of broad Stars associations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T13:30:32-08:00","id":845238,"title":"","content":"Will things like Pandora's Box most likely being a Jar and the Golden Apples of the Hesperides likely not being apples be a thing or will Fatebinding result in them being their most commonly known modern state?<br /> <br /> Will there be a different rules for the Children of Demigods or Hero Level Scions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T16:41:48-08:00","id":845877,"title":"","content":"Or will it just be possible to make it so that those things (and any others) are represented in whatever way works best for your campaign?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T21:11:04-07:00","id":848597,"title":"","content":"Weird question incoming.<br /> <br /> Is it all possible in 2nd edition to clone a Scion or make a bioborg replicant of one a la Thor's robo-clone Ragnorak from Marvel's Civil War comic? If so, would that clone/android/whatever still need a Visitation? IIRC a God can create artificially create a Scion, but I wonder if human ingenuity and comic book superscience can pull it off too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T05:45:36-07:00","id":848732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=848597#post848597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weird question incoming.<br /> <br /> Is it all possible in 2nd edition to clone a Scion or make a bioborg replicant of one a la Thor's robo-clone Ragnorak from Marvel's Civil War comic? If so, would that clone/android/whatever still need a Visitation? IIRC a God can create artificially create a Scion, but I wonder if human ingenuity and comic book superscience can pull it off too.</div> </div> </div> </div>That <i>is </i>a weird question. I'd say no - <b>Scion</b> takes lengths to stop gods from feeling like comic book superheroes, and while humans can attain a sort of folk deification, actual apotheosis or Visitation isn't possible without a divine spark.<br /> <br /> That said, I'd <i>love </i>to do a techno-data Shard later, where gods are Big Data, pantheons are proprietary software engines on quantum platforms, and Scions are their analog interfaces. In that case, yeah, a god or Scion could be remade through human ingenuity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T08:15:10-07:00","id":848805,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">A few earlier discussions on how some nymphs/other divine beings are perceived with a lesser importance even though by rights they shouldn't be. (e.g. Nymphs are the daughters of titans but are thought of as low legend beings, Kheiron is another example. He is the son of Kronos and an Nymph Philyra (the daughter of Okeanos) but pretty much relegated to the mentor of heroes role and was considered around Legend 6 in his write-up).</span><br /> \u200b<br /> My question is how does Scion currently view this. Before I would have said the following:<br /> -child of two gods/titans equals a god/titan (starting at Legend 9 who may or may not rise in importance). <br /> -child of a god and another being of legend (nymph/elf) (starting at demigod level Legend 5)<br /> -child of a god and a mortal = basic scion starting at Legend 2 to 4 depending on the power of the god","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T08:21:13-07:00","id":848813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=848732#post848732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That <i>is </i>a weird question. I'd say no - <b>Scion</b> takes lengths to stop gods from feeling like comic book superheroes, and while humans can attain a sort of folk deification, actual apotheosis or Visitation isn't possible without a divine spark.<br /> <br /> That said, I'd <i>love </i>to do a techno-data Shard later, where gods are Big Data, pantheons are proprietary software engines on quantum platforms, and Scions are their analog interfaces. In that case, yeah, a god or Scion could be remade through human ingenuity.</div> </div> </div> </div>whats the first shard you're planning to do after the main scion books are done?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T04:02:10-07:00","id":852882,"title":"","content":"I tried to look for the answer but could not find it and maybe it's not finalized but will the new combat system and general system be as complex as the exalted 3rd ed ones ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2799-astoril","name":"Astoril","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T04:57:17-07:00","id":852896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astoril</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=852882#post852882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tried to look for the answer but could not find it and maybe it's not finalized but will the new combat system and general system be as complex as the exalted 3rd ed ones ?</div> </div> </div> </div>This was last year, so things have probably had some changes, but take a look at these system teasers for some idea:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/codename-sardonyx-teaser-the-first/\" target=\"_blank\">Core mechanic, Consolation and Momentum</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/codename-sardonyx-teaser-the-second/\" target=\"_blank\">Attributes and Abilities</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/codename-sardonyx-schemas-and-scales/\" target=\"_blank\">Schemas and Scales</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T06:49:30-07:00","id":852939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=848813#post848813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">whats the first shard you're planning to do after the main scion books are done?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Twilight Age, after the apocalypse, where humanity collapses back into the Dark Ages. Mood and setting is like Into the Badlands, if the Badlands are next to Mad Max: Fury Road, with a heavy dose of A Canticle for Leibowitz.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 03-25-2016, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T07:05:32-07:00","id":852945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=848805#post848805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">A few earlier discussions on how some nymphs/other divine beings are perceived with a lesser importance even though by rights they shouldn't be. (e.g. Nymphs are the daughters of titans but are thought of as low legend beings, Kheiron is another example. He is the son of Kronos and an Nymph Philyra (the daughter of Okeanos) but pretty much relegated to the mentor of heroes role and was considered around Legend 6 in his write-up).</span><br /> \u200b<br /> My question is how does Scion currently view this. Before I would have said the following:<br /> -child of two gods/titans equals a god/titan (starting at Legend 9 who may or may not rise in importance).<br /> -child of a god and another being of legend (nymph/elf) (starting at demigod level Legend 5)<br /> -child of a god and a mortal = basic scion starting at Legend 2 to 4 depending on the power of the god</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not entirely sure yet, though children of gods and mortals always start at Legend 0; their Visitation raises them to Legend 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T07:06:52-07:00","id":852946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astoril</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=852882#post852882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tried to look for the answer but could not find it and maybe it's not finalized but will the new combat system and general system be as complex as the exalted 3rd ed ones ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The system aims to be less compex though still deep, and the power analogues are planned to be far simpler, broad, and expansive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T14:33:09-07:00","id":854216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=852946#post852946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The system aims to be less compex though still deep, and the power analogues are planned to be far simpler, broad, and expansive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh,speaking of power...<br /> <br /> What exactly a god would have to do,to steal's another mantle? i'm assuming it involves more than winning a battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T10:32:17-07:00","id":854543,"title":"","content":"Not sure if you noticed this question buried in my overly long and complicated post a page back.<br /> <br /> Will there be easier access to more blasty options if someone wanted to play a character that resembled something closer to a sorcerer or mage?<br /> <br /> With 1st edition there seemed to be only a few attacks within the purviews and all of them were around demigod tier and didn't seem to scale all that well. Is a early Hero tier blasty character just not something that fits the theme of scion overall? I admit that I can't really think of many hero tier like figures in mythology that were slinging spells. They tended to use tools/relics and natural/divine prowess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 03-28-2016, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T11:38:22-07:00","id":854568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=854543#post854543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will there be easier access to more blasty options if someone wanted to play a character that resembled something closer to a sorcerer or mage?<br /> <br /> With 1st edition there seemed to be only a few attacks within the purviews and all of them were around demigod tier and didn't seem to scale all that well. Is a early Hero tier blasty character just not something that fits the theme of scion overall? I admit that I can't really think of many hero tier like figures in mythology that were slinging spells. They tended to use tools/relics and natural/divine prowess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. Divine prowess is still focused around that; spells are done through cultural magics. But there will be sorcerous options later down the road.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T12:13:19-07:00","id":854590,"title":"","content":"This may be another sort of strange question Neall, but it is a topic that I can remember being brought up on the old forums occasionally, and frequently within our own groups. At what point do Mortals become irrelevant non-actors in a Scion's story? Not necessarily <i>all</i> Mortals, Megara, Fergus mac Roich, Conall Cernach, and others play important roles, but more like Mortals in abstract. What point (Legend rating) can a Social Scion just enthrall mortals with no effort? At what point can mortals not physically hurt a Scion who has Epic Stamina at the highest value their Legend rating allows?<br /> <br /> Obviously the importance of Mortals varies Pantheon to Pantheon. To the Anunna they are a slave race capable of little greatness compared to the Great Gods, while to the Tuatha they are dangerous conquerors entirely capable of Deicide. But, I assume for the sanity of the Storytellers, players, and developers, Mortals are just standardized across Pantheons in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T13:07:43-07:00","id":854622,"title":"","content":"So when you say later down the road do you mean in future side supplements or do you mean similar to 1st edition in the fact that throwing around lightning bolts or fire balls will show up in Demigod rather than Hero.<br /> <br /> Random Question. Will sling's be a weapon choice? I only ask because that may fit my friend's character as a weapon type before he grows into energy slinging capabilities. I assume we could always use throwing rules if there isn't a particular writeup for a sling.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the info, Neall. Great stuff!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 03-28-2016, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T14:54:20-07:00","id":854689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=854590#post854590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may be another sort of strange question Neall, but it is a topic that I can remember being brought up on the old forums occasionally, and frequently within our own groups. At what point do Mortals become irrelevant non-actors in a Scion's story? Not necessarily <i>all</i> Mortals, Megara, Fergus mac Roich, Conall Cernach, and others play important roles, but more like Mortals in abstract.</div> </div> </div> </div>At no point, really, though they're probably at their lowest point of relevance at Demigod.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What point (Legend rating) can a Social Scion just enthrall mortals with no effort? </div> </div> </div>None. It always takes committed effort.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At what point can mortals not physically hurt a Scion who has Epic Stamina at the highest value their Legend rating allows? </div> </div> </div>Who has Epic Stamina Boons, you mean? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Probably Legend 2, although no Scion is completely safe. A God caught without Legend can probably survive a .50 cal round to the head, but they're not really going to be getting up for a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T14:55:27-07:00","id":854690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=854622#post854622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So when you say later down the road do you mean in future side supplements or do you mean similar to 1st edition in the fact that throwing around lightning bolts or fire balls will show up in Demigod rather than Hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>Future supplements will detail mortal sorcerers who can challenge the pantheons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Random Question. Will sling's be a weapon choice? I only ask because that may fit my friend's character as a weapon type before he grows into energy slinging capabilities. I assume we could always use throwing rules if there isn't a particular writeup for a sling. </div> </div> </div>I think they should be mentioned under throwing rules, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T15:54:46-07:00","id":854704,"title":"","content":"I was actually referring to Scions rather than Mortals. More specifically, would it be possible to make a scion of Zeus who at character creation (or within hero tier) chooses to throw lightning bolts as his/her combat tactic of choice rather than using weapons. When I said sorcerer and mage I was more so referencing to archetype. My friend's wants his character to be a Scion of Freya who flys around and uses blasts of elemental energy as his means of fighting rather than a weapon. It's a flavor choice rather than a power choice. He wouldn't expect to be any stronger than anyone else in the group.<br /> <br /> Sorry for any confusion in how I originally phrased it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 03-28-2016, 07:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T18:03:02-07:00","id":854766,"title":"","content":"How would the game handle something like a non divine priest/human sorcerer? I mean by default they have no legend or really really low legend. So they'd end up having like first or second level scion abilities or would they get to channel their god's power and be capable of greater feats?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T19:18:39-07:00","id":854813,"title":"","content":"Do you know of any titans that'll be part of the Aztec pantheon or the Egyptian one?<br /> What is the relationship between relics and purivews now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T12:51:38-07:00","id":855191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=854766#post854766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would the game handle something like a non divine priest/human sorcerer? I mean by default they have no legend or really really low legend. So they'd end up having like first or second level scion abilities or would they get to channel their god's power and be capable of greater feats?</div> </div> </div> </div>They have to pull Legend from other sources, be it devotion to Virtues or spellcasting abilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicholas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the relationship between relics and purivews now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Relics add additional motifs, Evocation Boons, and allow you to channel a Purview outside that of your Callings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T14:50:29-07:00","id":855263,"title":"","content":"The Sage callin has which purviews?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T15:46:22-07:00","id":855295,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Callings, will it be possible for a starting (Hero) character to have more than one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T18:21:14-07:00","id":855403,"title":"","content":"Curiously Neall, if you had to compile a listening list of Scion as you have it now and you'd like it to be, what songs would you put on the 'Making of Scion' playlist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T19:20:18-07:00","id":855430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Squee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=855403#post855403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curiously Neall, if you had to compile a listening list of Scion as you have it now and you'd like it to be, what songs would you put on the 'Making of Scion' playlist?</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd pretty much be a bunch of Queens of the Stone Age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T22:42:57-07:00","id":855506,"title":"","content":"I was wondering which book you planned on including things like playing fauns, nymphs, huldras, kitsunes, etc. Pretty much, which book would have the rules in place for playing supernatural races(cause plenty of myth still have things like nymphs and shit be the children of gods and goddesses). Also, if I was to make a Prometheus Scion, what kind of stuff would you say Prometheus would have in their Purview(that's the right term, right?) <br /> <br /> Also, what's the difference between Purview and Calling, like when making a character what sort of thing does each inform? Finally, how much is Origins laying down in terms of options and things you may do(like sorcery stuff)? <br /> <br /> Though the idea of sorcerers being able to take on pantheons sounds cool as hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2042-madxhatter0","name":"MadxHatter0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:27:55-07:00","id":856010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=598691#post598691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except, that, like his forefathers, Zeus is FATED to be overthrown by his son. So that's a pretty huge plus sitting in his corner. And Boy-Zeus wasn't a match for Kronos in a toe-to-toe slug it out match. He started the fight off with cleverness and guile, got him some allies, THEN started the Big Fight.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=599271#post599271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is this from? I know tthe myth of how a son by Metis would overthrow him, but Zeus solved that problem by eating her. There as also the myth that Thetis, then courted by Zeus, would bear a son greater than his father, which is why she was married off to Peleus. Other than that, I don't know of a myth specifically dooming Zeus to his father's and grandfather's fates, although it would be following a pattern.</div> </div> </div> </div>I realize I'm like a year late, but I just read this entire thread last night and wanted to give you an answer.<br /> <br /> In Aeschylus's &quot;Prometheus Bound&quot;, Prometheus prophesizes that Zeus will be overthrown by a son, as is the curse of his line, and that no one can prevent it but Prometheus. Fortunately, the next two plays of the trilogy have some patches extant, so know what he was talking about<b></b>: <br /> <br /> In the second play, Prometheus Unbound, Heracles breaks him loose. In the third play, Prometheus the Fire-Bringer, he warns Zeus about Thetis, who will bear a child greater than his father. Thetis is married to Peleus, births Achilles, and Zeus breaks his family curse and forgives Prometheus. They hug it out.<br /> <br /> (Funny, a lot of Greek Tragedy has a happy ending if you can actually find the entire trilogy. You'd think Star Wars was a tragedy if you could only watch Empire.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://twitter.com/carykingdom\" target=\"_blank\">@CaryKingdom </a>- Writer and Ne'er-do-well<br /> Deititian at <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/worlds/scion/\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Second Edition</a><br /> Storyguide of <a href=\"https://scabbyrooster.fandom.com/wiki/The_Demi_Dozen\" target=\"_blank\">The Demi Dozen</a>, a Hero-level, live-streamed Scion Campaign<br /> Everything is subject to change; all opinions expressed are solely my own or those of my houseplants.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1093-arlecchino","name":"Arlecchino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T18:57:54-07:00","id":858070,"title":"","content":"So, there's been Talk about playing a Werewolf and stuff(and mentioning that it would eventually be subsumed into the animal purview if you were a scion)<br /> <br /> Could I say, Playa Scion born of one of the aseir who does not get visited, but ends up getting bitten by a werewolf, still does't get visited, then gets attacked by a giant(I don't know, maybe the Giant smelled his godling blood and descided to take him out before he grew up), and something or other triggers the Werewolf-scion to change, and while changed the wolf self kills the giant, and rips out and consumes it's heart and the blood with in, and then the wolf half kind of gets addicted to the giant's blood, and becomes more docile when it's had some, so the werewolf scion gets really good at spotting and hunting giants, and eventually he's consumed enough giants' heartsblood to, essentially, Visit himself, and then the Aesir pick him up and point him at hostile giants or something.<br /> <br /> Is this a viable concept?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T12:07:48-07:00","id":859799,"title":"","content":"Do we know how long it may be until some public playtesting will occur? My group is frothing at the mouth to get a hold of Sion 2nd Edition as soon as possible. I know they would be up for being a dedicated group of testers if possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T14:21:59-07:00","id":859871,"title":"","content":"Does the 2ed corebook explains exactly the details of what would happen if the Gods kept showing up at the World ? the firsr corebook simply said that they'd be FateBound in Un-Recogzinable forms and or be FateBound in a war against each other,but the book never explains how that would happen. Does the new edition explains it more deeply?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T16:15:24-07:00","id":863957,"title":"","content":"whats the relationship between Avatars and Mantles?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T05:18:12-07:00","id":864219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=859799#post859799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we know how long it may be until some public playtesting will occur? My group is frothing at the mouth to get a hold of Sion 2nd Edition as soon as possible. I know they would be up for being a dedicated group of testers if possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the most recent Monday Update, I'm not even sure that we can call Scion 2.0 a &quot;back burner&quot; project. Onyx Path's focus seems to be completely on the Chronicles of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T06:15:55-07:00","id":864252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=864219#post864219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the most recent Monday Update, I'm not even sure that we can call Scion 2.0 a &quot;back burner&quot; project. Onyx Path's focus seems to be completely on the Chronicles of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about that; since the start of the year, Scion: Alpha has gone from First Draft through Second Draft and into Development. Plus, if I recall correctly, on the interview, Neall mentioned that the Alpha is progressing steadily. They hate giving dates (understandably), but the Alpha out by the end of the year seems likely, and Origin and Hero by next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T06:35:07-07:00","id":864259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=864219#post864219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the most recent Monday Update, I'm not even sure that we can call Scion 2.0 a &quot;back burner&quot; project. Onyx Path's focus seems to be completely on the Chronicles of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I'm sending out the first drafts outline to folks this week...? I wanted my focus to be on the book itself rather than what I regard as a teaser or beta project.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T08:07:43-07:00","id":864294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=864219#post864219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the most recent Monday Update, I'm not even sure that we can call Scion 2.0 a &quot;back burner&quot; project. Onyx Path's focus seems to be completely on the Chronicles of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you say that? Look at those books in progress, we have projects all over the place!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T08:17:40-07:00","id":864300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=864219#post864219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Onyx Path's focus seems to be completely on the Chronicles of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">and Cavaliers of Mars</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T20:10:54-07:00","id":864681,"title":"","content":"My problem seems to be that I no longer have a taste for Vampire/Werewolf/etc. The one series White Wolf put out that I enjoy is Scion. I am thrilled that Onyx Path now owns the property, having seen the quality of work they put forth.<br /> I have, however, seen the film equivalent of a beloved project go through multiple directors and miss every previously announced date. Each week as I read the Monday Update, hoping to see Scion in bold, I watch book after book go through the entire announced-to-publish life cycle. Heck, I don't even think Beast was discussed this time last year.<br /> <br /> I like what we have been shown of the new rules. I am intrigued at what Neall has shared on this thread. After having my third health scare since the announcement of Scion 2nd Edition, however, I am beginning to doubt that I will be able to run it by the time it is released.<br /> <br /> I know that Onyx Path has been very open and professional about their projects, but I can still feel frustrated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","user":"PHGraves","date":".  rescuing Neall's name from Autocorrect. 04-12-2016, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T05:50:45-07:00","id":864854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=864681#post864681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like what we have been shown of the new rules. I am intrigued at what Neall has shared on this thread. After having my third health scare since the announcement of Scion 2nd Edition, however, I am beginning to doubt that I will be able to run it by the time it is released.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really sorry to hear that. I think you'll be pleased after this week, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T11:03:36-07:00","id":865024,"title":"","content":"Podcast was good, your reaction to &quot;Breus&quot; was... it was funny listening to your typing come to a dead halt. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T11:54:25-07:00","id":865043,"title":"","content":"I made a joke to my friend about making a Chinese nail salon worker who was a scion of a Chinese god of fertility. Places curses on people with sigils on their nails and can poison people with her touch. After thinking about it for a while I kinda sorta love the idea. Not sure of a name but if fertility still has the ability to poison on touch or make people infertile on touch I think that's what im going to do. Thinking Scion of Nuwa if she still exists and is handled the same way. She would likely be a sort of anti-hero merc of sorts. Could be hired for assassination jobs or as a strategist/informant since she has high intelligence and wits. She wouldn't be the direct stealthy rogue type as much as the hide in plain sight type in terms of blending in and playing smart.<br /> <br /> Since Neal was baffled with Breus and was unable to answer how you would make him, maybe you could tell me how mine would be done? Might be informative to people. The main think I am unsure about it how I would accomplish the curses through sigils painted on their nails. Although I assume any cursing type purview could always be reskinned to be her drawing the sigils. Or the sigils could always just a be a signature thing she does even though the curses come from her purviews rather than directly from the sigils.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 04-13-2016, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T12:16:34-07:00","id":865051,"title":"","content":"...What Yig said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T12:22:01-07:00","id":865053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=865043#post865043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might be informative to people. Main thing I'm unsure if it would be possible is the curses through sigils on nails.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a small Marvel of Fertility, done through the Pantheon Specific Purview. Easily done. <i>Easily</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T12:33:19-07:00","id":865056,"title":"","content":"Sounds awesome, good to hear! I guess that answers the question of if im going to delve in deep and make the character come release. Just need to practice my nail salon worker voice... &gt;.&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T12:53:09-07:00","id":865064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=865056#post865056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds awesome, good to hear! I guess that answers the question of if im going to delve in deep and make the character come release. Just need to practice my nail salon worker voice... &gt;.&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>Just be sure to avoid stereotypes and play it respectfully if you do. A lot of those nail salons are actually run by Vietnamese-Americans, after the growth of the luxury beauty industry in postwar America. It's important not to reinforce stereotypes of &quot;otherness&quot; and embrace culture and community.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T13:01:47-07:00","id":865068,"title":"","content":"Yea, she would be a fairly boring (and ignorant) character to play if she was just a gimmick character playing purely off a stereotype. I suspect she will be the type of person to be willing to begrudgingly embrace said stereotype though to stay under the radar at times. That's the great thing about the character idea. She started off purely as a joke on the stereotype and then of course I couldn't help but layer in other details of her personality that made me want to actually play her. I suspect away from her cover identity she will be a strong personality woman who tends to take charge and not tolerate incompetence. She ends up being a morally grey highly intelligent assassin/spy/strategist type character who frequently uses disguises during reconnaissance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 04-13-2016, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T23:03:54-07:00","id":865341,"title":"","content":"Or, much like the woman that run the local Chinese take out, it could be both, she looks and sounds like the stereo type but like all PEOPLE is much much more. Our take out lady is the stereotypical angry old Chinese lady, except that when you get to know her she's just caustic because it amuses her and she's usually annoyed at her son (the cook) who she thinks is too lazy (he's not but you know moms) and very much enjoys her customers despite fighting through the language barrier (English is a tough nut to crack when you're raised speaking mandarin... or any other Asian language for that matter). <br /> <br /> My point is she can be a morally gray, highly intelligent assassin, spy and strategist and still be a gossipy old Vietnamese woman (seriously, many Vietnamese women fought in a pretty big international scuffle not so long ago and gossip is a GREAT way to get information) who takes great pride in her skill with an emery board (and a perverse joy out of insulting her daughter who's too busy going to college to be smart and find a man and settle down).<br /> <br /> \u200bsorry for being a bit ranty, but I enjoy playing older characters BECAUSE of that weird &quot;sweet old backward thinking&quot;. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T12:46:54-07:00","id":865659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=520273#post520273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect that Scions creating their own pantheon can wear whatever they like, as long as it's sufficiently majestic.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Are you really planning on ascending to divinity in <i>that</i> outfit?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T16:08:45-07:00","id":865736,"title":"","content":"Loki looks down at the helmet Thor is going to wear for the ceremony. &quot;Nice feathers.&quot; [/sarcasm]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T14:09:05-07:00","id":866518,"title":"","content":"<i><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect that Scions creating their own pantheon can wear whatever they like, as long as it's sufficiently majestic.</div> </div> </div> </div></i>How do Scions creating their own pantheon get around their pantheons punishing them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T15:25:27-07:00","id":866540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=866518#post866518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do Scions cre