trong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=880943#post880943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh,sorry. english its not my first lnaguage,and i had forgotten what audacity means,its their PSP still related to Giants?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it's Wyrd, which UIfhednar talks about a bit up above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T07:38:04-07:00","id":880968,"title":"","content":"Essentially, the fact is, it's a game, not a mythology thesis. The Pantheons represent the larger-than-life manifestations of key concepts, in a manner that defines them, and gives the players a recognizable role-playing hook to hang their characters on. The Aesir are associated mythically with the end of the world known as Ragnarok. The Aztec are associated with sacrifice. For game purposes, they need to incorporate concepts that are recognizeable, even if not 100% accurate by current archeological and historical study. &quot;Ragnarok is coming, and we will die as the world is reborn&quot; is the basic tenet of Aesir mythology that pretry much any potential player wIll recognize. They struggle against it, but they also know it is inevitable in some form. Hence, I think, Fatalism (&quot;Ragnarok cannot be prevented&quot;), coupled with Audacity (&quot;but I may be able to alter my own fated role and change some little part of it&quot;). That's my interpretation, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T07:38:44-07:00","id":880969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=880966#post880966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, it's Wyrd, which UIfhednar talks about a bit up above.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neall,that lasst comment was you #665 post,the enxt one wiill the #666<br /> make it count,make Luci proud :&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T08:30:28-07:00","id":880998,"title":"","content":"Lucifer died for our sins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"use