 snapping her fingers...</div> </div> </div> </div>i felt sad the first time she did that,i cried the second time","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T16:17:10-07:00","id":881336,"title":"","content":"Hmmm,So Teotl are Hunger and Sacrifice and Aesir are Fatalism and Audacity. Are Pesedejt something along the lines of Renewal and Wisdom?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T17:09:43-07:00","id":881367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=880968#post880968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essentially, the fact is, it's a game, not a mythology thesis. The Pantheons represent the larger-than-life manifestations of key concepts, in a manner that defines them, and gives the players a recognizable role-playing hook to hang their characters on. The Aesir are associated mythically with the end of the world known as Ragnarok. The Aztec are associated with sacrifice. For game purposes, they need to incorporate concepts that are recognizeable, even if not 100% accurate by current archeological and historical study. &quot;Ragnarok is coming, and we will die as the world is reborn&quot; is the basic tenet of Aesir mythology that pretry much any potential player wIll recognize. They struggle against it, but they also know it is inevitable in some form. Hence, I think, Fatalism (&quot;Ragnarok cannot be prevented&quot;), coupled with Audacity (&quot;but I may be able to alter my own fated role and change some little part of it&quot;). That's my interpretation, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is a pretty fair assessment. Seeing the virtues as a range of ideas and issues at stake for a certain pantheon, rather than values which define a pantheon, might help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T17:24:06-07:00","id":881375,"title":"","content":"So far we also have Tradition versus 