seems to be specifically refering to mesoamerican legends but there are lots of other traditions where animal transformations hold a spiritual meaning above and beyond the utility of the power. That kinda sets them apart from say the greek gods who seemed to change shape more on a whim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5622,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","user":"SpruceStripedGoose","date":". 05-05-2016, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T17:00:16-07:00","id":883309,"title":"","content":"I think the difference between Greeks shape changing and Aztec shape changing is that it is a ability like any other for the Greeks,nothing special. But for the Aztec it is Sacred,not an ability or skill,but the ultimate, ate she of your soul. You are the Jaguar and Jaguar is you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T20:59:46-07:00","id":883450,"title":"","content":"Nagualism may or may not end up allowing the practitioner to turn into the animal in question, but it will definitely allow someone to take on the strengths and weaknesses of their associated creature. You might also be able to manifest it as a sort of companion animal\u2014not so much a pet or familiar as a His Dark Materials-style d\u00e6mon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T21:27:29-07:00","id":883469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=883450#post883450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nagualism may or may not end up allowing the practitioner to turn into the animal in question, but it will definitely allow someone to take on the strengths and weaknesses of their associated creature. You might also be able to manifest it as a sort of companion animal\u2014not so much a pet or familiar as a His Dark Materials-style d\u00e6mon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a dark side to a pantheons traits, or a path to corruption? Like say Ben Da