3:51-07:00","id":883840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=883835#post883835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to ask, because I know it's been answered somewhere, but I just can't locate the post - which pantheons are we getting for the starting books?</div> </div> </div> </div>Read the next blog post, judging from how the voting's going. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T09:27:00-07:00","id":883842,"title":"","content":"Hey neall,if titans are consumed by their purview. Does that means <u><i>everything </i></u> they do has to be related to the purview?<br /> Cano a god show up to their culture and interact with them with no fear of fatebinding? ^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 05-06-2016, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T11:50:50-07:00","id":883943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=883835#post883835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to ask, because I know it's been answered somewhere, but I just can't locate the post - which pantheons are we getting for the starting books?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aesir<br /> Deva<br /> Kami<br /> Manitou<br /> Netjer<br /> Orisha<br /> Shen<br /> Teotl<br /> Theoi<br /> Tuatha de Dannan<br /> <br /> That's before any stretch goal addition. Neall's mentioned he wants to do the a Hero-book addition of the Nemetondevos (Gaulish gods) as a dead Pantheon that is there to claim their mantles or for them to be reborn as new PCs.<br /> <br /> I think he's also confirmed the Mesopotamian, Canaan/Phoenician, Aboriginal Australian, Polynesian, and more Native American Pantheons for some of the later books. Also the expansion of the Orisha in coalition with the Loa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T12:07:19-07:00","id":883959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=883943#post883943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aesir<br /> Deva<br /> Kami<br /> Manitou<br /> Netjer<br /> Orisha<br /> Shen<br /> Teotl<br /> Theoi<br /> Tuatha de Dannan</div> </div> </div> </div>To expand a bit: some of 1e's pantheons have been renamed for 2e. The Egyptian pantheon are the Netjer, the Chinese pantheon are the Shen, the Mexica pantheon are the Teotl, and the Greco-Roman pantheon are the Theoi.<br /> <br /> The Orisha are the Yoruba pantheon, one of the progenitor pantheons of the Loa of Vodou, and the Manitouk are the Algonquin pantheon, brand new to 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T12:41:31-07:00","id":883995,"title":"","content":"*nods*. Dodekatheon or Olympians refer to the specific 12 gods who rule on Mount Olympus - but all Greco-Roman gods are Theoi. The Psedjet are the greatest gods of the Ennead cosmology, but all Egyptian gods are Netjer. The Kami divide into the Amatsukami in heaven and the Kunitsukami in the World. The Celestial Bureaucracy is a massive institution that employs many Shen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T14:00:27-07:00","id":884049,"title":"","content":"Cool. Hopefully, the Mayans won't get lumped in with the Aztecs this time. And it will be nice to have Orisha instead of a generic &quot;voodoo&quot; pantheon. I also wouldn't mind Russian/Polish/Wendish gods, and the Finnish pantheon as well.<br /> Another question: How will the Vanir be handled? Will there be any expansion of them, or just &quot;Frey &amp; Freyja were traded to the Aesir, and that's pretty much all we know about the Vanir&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T19:18:52-07:00","id":884255,"title":"","content":"Nice! Glad to hear about all the pantheons. In terms of possible Pacific Islander Pantheons, I have a friend who would lose her mind if she found out that the Tagalog were included. Any chance they may be on a list for a future book or in anyone's minds for a stretch goal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T20:36:28-07:00","id":884307,"title":"","content":"When you say...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">They hide in plain sight, when they bother to hide at all. Dwarves and elves are in towns in the Scandinavian countries, sometimes even plying their trade. Centaurs herd in the plains of Thessaly, where there are so few cameras. Tengu nests nestle among Japanese skyscrapers. Colonies of satyrs in the mountains of Greece, fighting for territory with the aforementioned centaurs who lope across the plains. In the American West, a different kind of centaur rides the highways on two wheels, chrome where human legs should be and oil pumping in their hearts.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>How well hidden, or perhaps well known are magical creatures and peoples in the World? If went on Snopes and searched &quot;Tengu sighting in Akihabara&quot;, or was on Etsy looking for &quot;authentic Dwarven crafts&quot; what would I find?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T23:38:36-07:00","id":884416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=884049#post884049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool. Hopefully, the Mayans won't get lumped in with the Aztecs this time. And it will be nice to have Orisha instead of a generic &quot;voodoo&quot; pantheon. I also wouldn't mind Russian/Polish/Wendish gods, and the Finnish pantheon as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Maya and Inca pantheons are slated for later books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T09:20:38-07:00","id":884680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheGraySoul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=884255#post884255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice! Glad to hear about all the pantheons. In terms of possible Pacific Islander Pantheons, I have a friend who would lose her mind if she found out that the Tagalog were included. Any chance they may be on a list for a future book or in anyone's minds for a stretch goal?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, for God, actually. Toss me a PM and I'll make sure she gets a playtest invite if she wants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T09:29:07-07:00","id":884684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=884049#post884049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question: How will the Vanir be handled? Will there be any expansion of them, or just &amp;quot;Frey &amp; Freyja were traded to the Aesir, and that's pretty much all we know about the Vanir&amp;quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>The \u00c6sir are the pantheon we're focusing on in Hero; in Scion, Vanaheim is an empty Terra Incognita, and the Vanir have mostly moved to Asgard. I'm not opposed to expanding them in a later book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T14:20:21-07:00","id":884899,"title":"","content":"Oh i may have asked this before or it may have been asked if so then i am sorry. Looking back at Scion: God first edition. Harrow or Harshiar or whatever his god name was...the egyptian pantheon signature character mentioned having the band create a new pantheon and a new god world for themselves. Would this be possible for player characters to do in second edition and could this new pantheon get it's own underworld as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T16:09:05-07:00","id":884977,"title":"","content":"Yes, it's possible in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T16:32:58-07:00","id":884992,"title":"","content":"What's the average number of gods per pantheon that you are shotting for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T16:33:33-07:00","id":884993,"title":"","content":"When it comes to Fate,does the gods worshippers some benefit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T11:37:01-07:00","id":885525,"title":"","content":"What's the impetus for earthly supernatural forces (take the Nordic elves and dwarves for example) to keep themselves concealed? Are they subject to Fatebinding too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T14:00:58-07:00","id":885672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=885525#post885525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the impetus for earthly supernatural forces (take the Nordic elves and dwarves for example) to keep themselves concealed? Are they subject to Fatebinding too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to warn you, Neall, if you let me decide then the answer will of course be &quot;racism.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T20:54:51-07:00","id":885937,"title":"","content":"Hi. I've been interested in Scion for a while now, and the stuff I'm seeing for 2E looks amazing so far. However, I have a question. Back when I first heard about Incarnates being a thing, I was thinking of making a set of twins who were Incarnates of Balder and Hodr. However, I checked the thread after learning that the Geneses were mentioned in here, and saw your ruling on the Balder being reincarnated (In that if it did happen, it would be rather problematic due to Balder not being fated to return until after Ragnarok), and with Hodr suffering a similar fate, I realized that there was no way that the idea was ever going to work. However, the idea of playing an Incarnate is still rather interesting to me, and so to prevent any more hiccups on that matter my question to you is: Is there any other deities from the Aesir -- or other pantheons, for that matter -- that are similarly off-limits for that particular Genesis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11755-aquatica1000","name":"Aquatica1000","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T02:15:26-07:00","id":886038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquatica1000</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=885937#post885937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi. I've been interested in Scion for a while now, and the stuff I'm seeing for 2E looks amazing so far. However, I have a question. Back when I first heard about Incarnates being a thing, I was thinking of making a set of twins who were Incarnates of Balder and Hodr. However, I checked the thread after learning that the Geneses were mentioned in here, and saw your ruling on the Balder being reincarnated (In that if it did happen, it would be rather problematic due to Balder not being fated to return until after Ragnarok), and with Hodr suffering a similar fate, I realized that there was no way that the idea was ever going to work. However, the idea of playing an Incarnate is still rather interesting to me, and so to prevent any more hiccups on that matter my question to you is: Is there any other deities from the Aesir -- or other pantheons, for that matter -- that are similarly off-limits for that particular Genesis?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How about Kvasir? He is in the story of the capture and binding of Loki, but his death is instrumental to the Mead of Poetry. So he needs to already be dead - but he's supposed to still do stuff that hasn't happened yet before Ragnarok. So, there you go.<br /> <br /> Or Bor! Man, imagine getting to tell Odin you're his dad!<br /> <br /> Also, I believe Neall has suggested that while it won't be canon, it will be very easy for a table to say &quot;so someone killed Thor 20 years ago, but obviously the Wyrd says Thor isn't supposed to die until Ragnarok, so he's coming back&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-09-2016, 05:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T05:58:03-07:00","id":886142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=885672#post885672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to warn you, Neall, if you let me decide then the answer will of course be &quot;racism.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I would expect nothing less.<br /> <br /> Racism actually probably does have a little bit to do with it, in the sense that a lot of real-world cultural traditions are derided as Ceremonies of the Other rather than legitimate or differing cultural practices. In the last days of the Roman Republic, the Romans didn't fuck with Egypt's gods even if they fucked with the Egyptians; but today if someone tells you her Italian grandmother is a witch and she comes from a long line of witches you're probably going to roll your eyes. Same deal with a Slavic woman keeping a bit of coarse salt on her mantle. <b>Scion</b>'s World is a lot more accepting of cultural and religious diversity than our world, but it's the same fundamental place (except for all the gods*) with the same fundamental problems.<br /> <br /> The gods don't interact with mortals because they're people first and not superheroes**, but also because their Callings and Fate lock them into roles and relationships and they get tired of it after a while. This is also why they spin off Incarnations - to interact with mortals while Fate is running in the background and on the meta scale, rather than binding them into a thousand dramas in microcosm.<br /> <br /> *says the monotheist<br /> **although when was the last time Reed Richards busted out some hypertech for the benefit of humanity<br /> answer me that<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquatica1000</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi. I've been interested in Scion for a while now, and the stuff I'm seeing for 2E looks amazing so far. However, I have a question. Back when I first heard about Incarnates being a thing, I was thinking of making a set of twins who were Incarnates of Balder and Hodr. However, I checked the thread after learning that the Geneses were mentioned in here, and saw your ruling on the Balder being reincarnated (In that if it did happen, it would be rather problematic due to Balder not being fated to return until after Ragnarok), and with Hodr suffering a similar fate, I realized that there was no way that the idea was ever going to work. However, the idea of playing an Incarnate is still rather interesting to me, and so to prevent any more hiccups on that matter my question to you is: Is there any other deities from the Aesir -- or other pantheons, for that matter -- that are similarly off-limits for that particular Genesis?</div> </div> </div> </div>Please, don't let me discourage you! Baldr being an Incarnate lends an air of seriousness to the whole thing. What happens if Baldr is &quot;offline&quot; when Ragnarok hits? Or is the new Incarnate of Baldr wondering whether he'll have to die and Incarnate <i>again </i>for Ragnarok to go off?<br /> <br /> There's probably some deities for whom it's more problematic than others, and Baldr is one of them. By contrast, the Teotl God in the alpha is implied to <i>constantly </i>Incarnate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T07:18:44-07:00","id":886210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=886142#post886142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would expect nothing less.<br /> <br /> Racism actually probably does have a little bit to do with it, in the sense that a lot of real-world cultural traditions are derided as Ceremonies of the Other rather than legitimate or differing cultural practices. In the last days of the Roman Republic, the Romans didn't fuck with Egypt's gods even if they fucked with the Egyptians; but today if someone tells you her Italian grandmother is a witch and she comes from a long line of witches you're probably going to roll your eyes. Same deal with a Slavic woman keeping a bit of coarse salt on her mantle. <b>Scion</b>'s World is a lot more accepting of cultural and religious diversity than our world, but it's the same fundamental place (except for all the gods*) with the same fundamental problems.<br /> <br /> The gods don't interact with mortals because they're people first and not superheroes**, but also because their Callings and Fate lock them into roles and relationships and they get tired of it after a while. This is also why they spin off Incarnations - to interact with mortals while Fate is running in the background and on the meta scale, rather than binding them into a thousand dramas in microcosm.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh gods above and below, Neall, you have no idea how happy this has just made me. I mean don't get me wrong, I really enjoy Scion 1e. It's hands down my favourite game, despite some of the holes in it, and despite needing some homebrewing and such to make it run the way my players and I like it to.<br /> <br /> But I am so very excited about the themes and ideas I'm seeing for Scion 2e. Very excited. Not that the same setting ideas can't apply for a 1e game, but if these are the concepts and ideas that you are having whilst <i>writing</i> Scion 2e I am so stoked and I look forward to buying up every product you can roll out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 20