t, for that matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T07:50:11-07:00","id":886243,"title":"","content":"Lol,son. We all know those silly &quot;gods&quot; are just sorcerers who think they're gods,doesn't matter if you can throw lightfireing,there's only One god<br /> *is swallowed by Poseidon Earthquake*<br /> *Burned by Agni Fire*<br /> *Morrisons crow eat my eyes*<br /> Well,<i>on a second thought</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T07:51:27-07:00","id":886245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=886233#post886233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this new edition a bit Darker?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark, but not dour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T07:54:23-07:00","id":886251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=886245#post886245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dark, but not dour.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats cool e :^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:30:00-07:00","id":886497,"title":"","content":"Is the fateful aura,the aura that forces heroes demigods and god's to be part of great events still present?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:35:32-07:00","id":886501,"title":"","content":"Is coatliclue still a Titan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 05-09-2016, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T14:07:30-07:00","id":886628,"title":"","content":"Could you have Thor's Hammer as a Relic, I know basic assumption is Thor hold Mjolnir but the books used to give high profile items as starting Relics all the time, like the Golden Fleece. So is there something stopping you from having the Nyoi Bo itself instead of just a fragment? Naturally this is a situation where I guess some or most of the Gods may have passed.<br /> <br /> So similarly any rules for being the next incarnation of the God like say Vishnu reborn, or even usually non reincarnating gods like Zeus?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=886245#post886245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dark, but not dour.</div> </div> </div> </div>??<br /> Does that mean its not aimed at a younger audience like the original?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T14:31:36-07:00","id":886639,"title":"","content":"I don't think the original was aimed at a &quot;younger audience&quot; at all - there was plenty of nudity and suggestive content in the various books, and nothing seemed less mature than, say, World of Darkness or Exalted. I'm looking forward to a serious, well-thought-out game system with a solid background to set campaigns in.<br /> As to having Mjollnir as a relic - that risks the old D&amp;D &quot;let's get Thor's hammer!&quot; mentality for games. It was made for him, and it isn't very likely that it would be given to anyone else. The Dwarves could make similar relics for Scions, if that fits with the story, but the original belongs with Thor, IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T14:59:43-07:00","id":886657,"title":"","content":"The hammer being stolen though is a Norse myth staple!<br /> <br /> Also I think Neall suggested a while ago a plausible plot where you're playing Thor Incarnate and trying to get the Hammer to reclaim your Destiny, while Magnitude and Modi are trying to wield it to rise in their father's place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T15:03:13-07:00","id":886659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=886639#post886639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the original was aimed at a &amp;quot;younger audience&amp;quot; at all - there was plenty of nudity and suggestive content in the various books, and nothing seemed less mature than, say, World of Darkness or Exalted. I'm looking forward to a serious, well-thought-out game system with a solid background to set campaigns in.<br /> As to having Mjollnir as a relic - that risks the old D&amp;D &amp;quot;let's get Thor's hammer!&amp;quot; mentality for games. It was made for him, and it isn't very likely that it would be given to anyone else. The Dwarves could make similar relics for Scions, if that fits with the story, but the original belongs with Thor, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was actually made for him, it was just he was the clear choice for it. But the armor of Achilles was made for him and Victor got it, same with the Dardalus device.<br /> <br /> But Scion 1st Ed was stated in an interview as aimed at a slightly younger audience. And it did tailor down the darkness. For instance the Horus preview origin included Seth Farrows attempting to rape Horus' mom, and by the time the book came out it was edited out. Also less grey areas as far as whitewolf is normally concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T15:04:12-07:00","id":886661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=886628#post886628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">??<br /> Does that mean its not aimed at a younger audience like the original?</div> </div> </div> </div>The original wasn't intentionally aimed at a younger audience. Or if it was they did a bad job of it. I am being struck by the memory of a particular scene in the Demigod book's fiction with minotaurs and that Scion of Aphrodite.<br /> <br /> The new edition is aimed at accurately capturing mythology, and has a more complex world than the previous edition with its' simple amythic fight-evil-titanspawn centric narrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-09-2016, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T08:51:21-07:00","id":887219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=886628#post886628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you have Thor's Hammer as a Relic,</div> </div> </div> </div>You could have it, but you aren't going to be able to use it at Thor levels without the belt and gauntlets that even Thor needed. So that's 3-4 Relics including the hammer proper. (Magni may or may not be the exception to that.)<br /> <br /> Thor's hammer would get stolen, but you don't hear about the thieves using it Thor-style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T09:20:01-07:00","id":887239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=887219#post887219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thor's hammer would get stolen, but you don't hear about the thieves using it Thor-style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oppa Thor style?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T09:41:32-07:00","id":887249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=886661#post886661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original wasn't intentionally aimed at a younger audience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Story time!<br /> <br /> The <i>original</i> pitch for <b>Scion </b>in 2004 was for a pre-OSR Storyteller game that took place in a post-apocalyptic North America and was aimed at newer roleplayers, including but not limited to a younger audience. By &quot;pre-OSR&quot; I mean that it specifically set out to capture elements of 1e D&amp;D - loose narration, randomly generated story elements, stripped down mechanical play, but still based on the Storyteller engine.<br /> <br /> This was before <i>Castles &amp; Crusades</i>, mind.<br /> <br /> The actual setting was after an unspecified apocalypse had wiped out much of the population and technological infrastructure, regressing humanity to an effective Dark Age. In response, the Old Gods decided to choose new mortal champions, and also activated the children they'd been having all along. The old Scions weren't meant to progress beyond hero level as part of their narrative arc - it was about working the will of your parent in this shattered world, working to restore the old faiths and knit society back together once more. The Western US was basically a variant of <i>Mad Max: Fury Road</i>, while the Eastern US was a lot like <i>Into the Badlands</i>. The details of the setting were highly nonspecific, both because it was meant to be generated on tables and because it was deliberately designed to not have a lot of setting details to actually recall. <b>Exalted</b> was hitting a fever pitch at this point, and the vast setting was starting to fill out; <b>Scion</b>, being based on our world (but post-apocalypse), was already filled-out to some degree, so it was never going to get more than a few specific instances of setting-building in order to keep things free for the Storyteller. Again, the operative word is &quot;New Dark Ages&quot;, in terms of feeling rather than actuality, so while you've got trade going on you've still got these big populations who have no true idea the other one exists.<br /> <br /> Anyways, long story short, some elements of that original pitch - the nonspecific setting, the stripped-down mechanics - actually did last into <b>Scion</b> proper. This made it appealing to new roleplayers, even if the subject matter wasn't precisely meant for young players.<br /> <br /> If you think I'm not going to have that setting come up in a Shard, you've got another think coming, because it's awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 05-10-2016, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T09:45:47-07:00","id":887252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=887239#post887239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oppa Thor style?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what that means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T10:00:04-07:00","id":887260,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure its a humorous reference to Psy's song Gungam Style.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9bZkp7q19f0\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9bZkp7q19f0\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9bZkp7q19f0\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9bZkp7q19f0 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T10:03:23-07:00","id":887262,"title":"","content":"&quot;Oppa Gungnir Style&quot; works a little better","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T10:17:59-07:00","id":887275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=887262#post887262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Oppa Gungnir Style&quot; works a little better</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, yes it does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T13:24:11-07:00","id":887446,"title":"","content":"Oh! Yeah &quot;for new players&quot; I can definitely see. It was the idea of the game as being notably kid-friendly (compared to then-WW, now-OP norm) that I definitely think didn't land.<br /> <br /> Really excited about the different Shards!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T13:26:27-07:00","id":887448,"title":"","content":"I can't remember if this has been addressed in the past 70 pages, but is Mithras (as in the God of the Roman cult) in the game? If so, is he duel-pantheon, a Yazata who gained a following elsewhere without ever being Theos, Theos just using a Yazata name (as most modern historians would suggest), or something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-10-2016, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T14:55:35-07:00","id":887518,"title":"","content":"What (if anything) will be done about the Roman tradition of god-stealing? I'm referring to how gods in conquered territories became aspects of their own gods; Camulus becoming part of Mars, for example. Which becomes especially interesting when said god is part of another major pantheon, Mars Nodens has to be an interesting topic to bring up with Nuada Airgetlam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T16:53:03-07:00","id":887626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GhanjRho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=887518#post887518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What (if anything) will be done about the Roman tradition of god-stealing? I'm referring to how gods in conquered territories became aspects of their own gods; Camulus becoming part of Mars, for example. Which becomes especially interesting when said god is part of another major pantheon, Mars Nodens has to be an interesting topic to bring up with Nuada Airgetlam.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;God-stealing&quot; has a lot of really negative implications that simply aren't true. Syncretism isn't appropriation. It's &quot;extending the metaphors&quot;. If you're Roman, there are many many many many many MANY many different aspects of Mars available to you from the get go. You can have different versions of the same deity in the same temple complex, worshiped separately inasmuch as they are worshiped together. So, when you head out from home, it's not too hard to see the gods of other pantheons as being much the same. Which, some of the time, they are. The many different version of Ares and Artemis have a lot to do with regional variation, but they also have a lot to do with the agglutination of various different deities into the larger conceptualizaion of &quot;Ares&quot; and &quot;Artemis&quot; as a part of the larger cultural context. On a larger stage, this led to some gods getting mushed together, or even new gods being created from such mushing. (Can we say &quot;Serapis&quot;?) It's not even a Roman thing. It's common in polytheistic religions. There is plenty of it between the Greeks and Phoencians. The whole Mithras/Mitra issue is another example. It's everywhere. There's a lot of Cha'ac in Tlaloc. Guanyin and Avalokiesvara and Chenrezik. <br /> <br /> The Romans aren't saying &quot;Oh, Nodens? There is no Nodens, there is only Mars. There has only ever been Mars and you ignorant savages have simply not known that Nodens was actually Mars. Aren't you happy we Romans came along to conquer you and clear that up? Of course you are....&quot; They didn't go around carving the stories off the walls of temples because &quot;They got it wrong, Hercules never did THAT!&quot;<br /> <br /> In any case, this is definitely more of an &quot;ancient religion&quot; issue than a &quot;mythology&quot; question. And the latter is more of the matter of Scion. No one is tacking the (no-longer-extant-in-any-meaningful-way or, alternatively, pretty much completely made up) mythology of Nodens onto Mars. They certainly aren't saying the Mars was King of Ireland and got his arm cut off, replaced by a silver arm and then replaced again by one of flesh (but didn't go back to being King even though he was once again without blemish). Nor are they saying Mars has a son named Gwyn who lives in Glatsonbury Tor and has a pack of magic hunting hounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T19:07:36-07:00","id":887749,"title":"","content":"Will there be rules for players to create their own signature boons? You mentioned the ability to make a frost purview attack ability using the marvel system but what about a player who wants to build his character into something like the God of Winter with a focus on it's destructive capabilities. Would that Hero eventually be able to turn that frequently used marvel into a full fledged boon to make it something he doesn't have to spend legend points on every time he wants to cast it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T22:35:10-07:00","id":887900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=887448#post887448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't remember if this has been addressed in the past 70 pages, but is Mithras (as in the God of the Roman cult) in the game? If so, is he duel-pantheon, a Yazata who gained a following elsewhere without ever being Theos, Theos just using a Yazata name (as most modern historians would suggest), or something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Initially, Neall said Mithras could be dual-pantheon, but later moved to Mithras and Mitra being separate gods, culturally very different while having potentially very similar origins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T22:59:36-07:00","id":887911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=887900#post887900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Initially, Neall said Mithras could be dual-pantheon, but later moved to Mithras and Mitra being separate gods, culturally very different while having potentially very similar origins.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd also be inclined to see Mithras as a Roman Centurion Scion of Mitra who achieved his own Godhood, and chose to align himself with the Theoi rather than his father's Pantheon.<br /> <br /> Edit: oh, born from a rock... So I guess the Galatea/Kvasir/etc Genesis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-11-2016, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T20:06:39-07:00","id":888791,"title":"","content":"how many legend dots a scion would need to built his own relic from scratch?,which purviews would she need?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T22:48:52-07:00","id":888858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=887626#post887626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &amp;quot;God-stealing&amp;quot; has a lot of really negative implications that simply aren't true. Syncretism isn't appropriation. It's &amp;quot;extending the metaphors&amp;quot;. If you're Roman, there are many many many many many MANY many different aspects of Mars available to you from the get go. You can have different versions of the same deity in the same temple complex, worshiped separately inasmuch as they are worshiped together. So, when you head out from home, it's not too hard to see the gods of other pantheons as being much the same. Which, some of the time, they are. The many different version of Ares and Artemis have a lot to do with regional variation, but they also have a lot to do with the agglutination of various different deities into the larger conceptualizaion of &amp;quot;Ares&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;Artemis&amp;quot; as a part of the larger cultural context. On a larger stage, this led to some gods getting mushed together, or even new gods being created from such mushing. (Can we say &amp;quot;Serapis&amp;quot;?) It's not even a Roman thing. It's common in polytheistic religions. There is plenty of it between the Greeks and Phoencians. The whole Mithras/Mitra issue is another example. It's everywhere. There's a lot of Cha'ac in Tlaloc. Guanyin and Avalokiesvara and Chenrezik. <br /> <br /> The Romans aren't saying &amp;quot;Oh, Nodens? There is no Nodens, there is only Mars. There has only ever been Mars and you ignorant savages have simply not known that Nodens was actually Mars. Aren't you happy we Romans came along to conquer you and clear that up? Of course you are....&amp;quot; They didn't go around carving the stories off the walls of temples because &amp;quot;They got it wrong, Hercules never did THAT!&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> In any case, this is definitely more of an &amp;quot;ancient religion&amp;quot; issue than a &amp;quot;mythology&amp;quot; question. And the latter is more of the matter of Scion. No one is tacking the (no-longer-extant-in-any-meaningful-way or, alternatively, pretty much completely made up) mythology of Nodens onto Mars. They certainly aren't saying the Mars was King of Ireland and got his arm cut off, replaced by a silver arm and then replaced again by one of flesh (but didn't go back to being King even though he was once again without blemish). Nor are they saying Mars has a son named Gwyn who lives in Glatsonbury Tor and has a pack of magic hunting hounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider me educated. Have a like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T15:44:42-07:00","id":889402,"title":"","content":"The mention of how pantheons can overlap, be made new, and broken has me thinking. Have any of the gods formed new pantheons in modern times/recent memory? Like could a handful of gods from different pantheons who worked together to aide the Allies in WWII have formed a new overlapping pantheon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5622,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","user":"SpruceStripedGoose","date":". 05-12-2016, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T07:25:34-07:00","id":889867,"title":"","content":"Are gods aware of Callings in-character, or are they just a mechanical concept?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T07:50:42-07:00","id":889887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=889867#post889867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are gods aware of Callings in-character, or are they just a mechanical concept?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're mostly a mechanical concept, although there's some tongue-in-cheek mortal work on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T09:33:07-07:00","id":889978,"title":"","content":"are there any gods who change a lot mentally and phiscally with different mantles,or is are they essentialy the same?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T10:33:30-07:00","id":890005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noneofyourbusiness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Into the Badlands</i> the 1991 Western horror film, or <i>Into the Badlands</i> the 2015 AMC TV series loosely based on <i>Journey to the West</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicholas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">are there any gods who change a lot mentally and phiscally with different mantles,or is are they essentialy the same?</div> </div> </div> </div>No God can mantle an Incarnation without it changing them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T10:48:17-07:00","id":890017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=890005#post890005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The latter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No God can mantle an Incarnation without it changing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>can the God spawn the incarnation at anytime or does He need specific cirscuntances?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T11:19:59-07:00","id":890032,"title":"","content":"Will the Netjer be using their popular Greek names (Osiris, Anubis, Isis) or their classic Egyptian/Kemetic ones (Azar, Anpu, Aset)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T12:01:14-07:00","id":890059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=890032#post890032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will the Netjer be using their popular Greek names (Osiris, Anubis, Isis) or their classic Egyptian/Kemetic ones (Azar, Anpu, Aset)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both! Although I prefer the Kemetic, with the Greek to be the first in the AKA column.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 05-13-2016, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T12:25:31-07:00","id":890074,"title":"","content":"Will there be any more information on Virtues given to us any time soon? I am looking forward to seeing how they function for the new edition. I'm also curious to see which are associated with each pantheon, especially the Theoi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T16:05:01-07:00","id":890215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=890059#post890059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Both! Although I prefer the Kemetic, with the Greek to be the first in the AKA column.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't the Greek names the more recognizable ones to most people? I guess the kemetic ones are historically accurate, but maybe a bit obscure no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T16:11:39-07:00","id":890219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=890215#post890215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aren't the Greek names the more recognizable ones to most people? I guess the kemetic ones are historically accurate, but maybe a bit obscure no?</div> </div> </div> </div>Which ones do you think the gods prefer? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T17:56:34-07:00","id":890298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=890219#post890219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which ones do you think the gods prefer? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly they might not have a problem with the greek ones, the Ptolemaic period made up the last three centuries they were actively worshipped. From their point of view they are their most current names.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T18:58:22-07:00","id":890332,"title":"","content":"is Prometheus going to be mentioned?<br /> if so,is he still a Titan like in 1e or a god?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T20:30:58-07:00","id":890373,"title":"","content":"Can we get more about the history? Particularly in how much is different. It says it isn't an alternative history, though i am curious how does it avoid getting into alternative history when the gods have scions. How did Christianity and Islam win out in the World of Legend*, were their saints basically scions? The case could be made for the Christian Saints being scions when you read some of their lives which are rather out there at times. Or did the gods stop making scions for what ever reason? I am not even sure if the Abarahmic God is even in Scion.<br /> <br /> Speaking of things being different from our world in the Scion Setting. What of the Greek and Roman Ruins. Are they still largely ruins, or are they restored or rebuilt, perhaps even compactly restored; of course in some cases that isn't much as they are rather remarkably preserved. Would they be used by the worshipers of the Theoi or be allowed to use them for religious purposes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T21:27:15-07:00","id":890400,"title":"","content":"Is an incarnate Scion capable of becoming something other than their divine identity? I'm thinking specifically of the Journey to the North, wherein a soul of the Jade Emperor becomes a potent deity in their own right, IIRC.<br /> <br /> Could an incarnate God form a new pantheon rather than rejoining the next one from whence they came?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T23:10:25-07:00","id":890451,"title":"","content":"So if I'm a brand spanking newbie to Scion but am also a huge mythology and history nerd, what should I read first to get the gist of things?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T00:20:53-07:00","id":890474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=890451#post890451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if I'm a brand spanking newbie to Scion but am also a huge mythology and history nerd, what should I read first to get the gist of things?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly in your position I wouldn't bother with 1st Edition at all, and just stick with Neall's blog posts.<br /> <br /> Inspiration wise, Neall's mentioned American Gods* and Wicked &amp; Divine as highly influential modern sources.<br /> <br /> * which is not to say we'll see &quot;modern gods&quot; like Media, the Technical Boy, or the Intangibles. Gaiman's cosmology runs on faith. Scion's runs on narrative. Abstractions don't become Gods just because people prioritize them in their lives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-14-2016, 03:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T00:22:32-07:00","id":890475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=890332#post890332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is Prometheus going to be mentioned?<br /> if so,is he still a Titan like in 1e or a god?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well he's explicitly a Titan in Greek Myth so...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","ed