":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T14:51:32-07:00","id":908634,"title":"","content":"right, I forgot","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T15:24:06-07:00","id":908660,"title":"","content":"...I've got another question. I've heard that Epic Perception was being replaced by/shuffled into one of the callings (as opposed to being a set of epic attributes/knacks like in 1E). What I'm wondering is which Calling is it? I keep thinking it's either Hunter, Judge, or Sage, but I'm not sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11755-aquatica1000","name":"Aquatica1000","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T15:33:57-07:00","id":908664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquatica1000</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=908660#post908660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I've got another question. I've heard that Epic Perception was being replaced by/shuffled into one of the callings (as opposed to being a set of epic attributes/knacks like in 1E). What I'm wondering is which Calling is it? I keep thinking it's either Hunter, Judge, or Sage, but I'm not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's been said that Epic Attributes have gone the way of the dodo, replaced with Knacks and Paths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T15:43:31-07:00","id":908669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=908664#post908664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's been said that Epic Attributes have gone the way of the dodo, replaced with Knacks and Paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>The three Physical Epics are now Purviews, though you can be potent in combat without them. At God level, you are - to a certain point of view - a force of nature with a face. Though, to quote part of the ST chapter of Origins: <br /> <br /> &quot;Myths are not the product of attempts to explain why the sun rises or what lightning is. They are expressions of people's response to those events and how to find meaning\u2014material, social, historical, or psychological\u2014in them. They help people orient themselves in their lives, provide structure and purpose.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T15:47:22-07:00","id":908672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=908454#post908454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Neall, the blog post looks brilliant. I was hesitant about archtype-esque ideas, but this looks to qualm my worries about them. What instantly stood out to me (asides from the funny Lugh blurb) was the mention of &amp;quot;Liminal&amp;quot; as one of the Paths. Instantaneously you had my attention with this, totally unexpected, and yet from the name I can see that it is something absolutely core to myth that was unfortunately left out of Scion 1E.<br /> <br /> Could you let us know more about the &amp;quot;Liminal&amp;quot; Path and some Gods or Goddesses who embody it? My immediate thought was Loki, Tezcat, Ishtar, and Radegast as the outside-insiders, but I wouldn't want to assume anything at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I've decided to put outsider-insider status more on tricksters, but a large part of &quot;divided deities&quot; or ones who are clearly of two worlds are Liminal. Ishtar, but also Hermes or Janus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T16:06:41-07:00","id":908683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=908672#post908672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I've decided to put outsider-insider status more on tricksters, but a large part of &amp;quot;divided deities&amp;quot; or ones who are clearly of two worlds are Liminal. Ishtar, but also Hermes or Janus.</div> </div> </div> </div>So is Sutek/Set Liminal, Trickster, or both?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T16:46:09-07:00","id":908710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=908683#post908683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is Sutek/Set Liminal, Trickster, or both?</div> </div> </div> </div>Likely both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T16:50:23-07:00","id":908714,"title":"","content":"Just how hard pit is for Full Fledged God to change one of their calling or add one more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T17:00:29-07:00","id":908722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=908710#post908710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Likely both.</div> </div> </div> </div>So gods can have multiple Callings. Stellar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T20:23:55-07:00","id":908844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=908664#post908664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's been said that Epic Attributes have gone the way of the dodo, replaced with Knacks and Paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Okay, I seem to have misworded my question. Not the first time I've done it, I guess. I was already aware that the remaining Epics are the physicals, which are now Purviews. My question was more like &quot;Are some of the Perception knacks going to be incorporated in the game in some way, shape or form?&quot; Sorry if I seem stubborn, I just liked several of them...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11755-aquatica1000","name":"Aquatica1000","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T20:38:14-07:00","id":908852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquatica1000</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=908844#post908844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Okay, I seem to have misworded my question. Not the first time I've done it, I guess. I was already aware that the remaining Epics are the physicals, which are now Purviews. My question was more like &quot;Are some of the Perception knacks going to be incorporated in the game in some way, shape or form?&quot; Sorry if I seem stubborn, I just liked several of them...</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be difficult to do Heimdallr, Horus and Helios without having something that boosted your senses. They were all supposed to be all seeing and not in the prophetic sense with Heimdallr having keen hearing as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T21:36:40-07:00","id":908881,"title":"","content":"On further reflection I've found something extremely important about the Callings system that makes me love it: it's an elegant solution to 1e's problem of less powerful or complex gods having less to offer to their Scions. This way, a Scion can inherit power and some character elements from their parent without feeling left out by picking, say, Aphrodite instead of Odin.<br /> <br /> Good choice, devs. Playing field = leveled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T03:21:13-07:00","id":909011,"title":"","content":"I was more concerned about the Associated Powers: Since callings give you associated powers, are the Gods still associated with Powers? If so, are the powers &quot;transmitted&quot; to their Scions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T03:26:41-07:00","id":909014,"title":"","content":"Gotta say, Neall, the more I read of Scion 2E the more excited I'm getting. I can't wait to see the full thing.<br /> <br /> Also, when I looked at the Alpha Slice (yeah yeah I only found it within the last couple weeks or so, at best) I was amused by the note on the Scale examples. &quot;Kaiju-hunting Robot&quot; is Scale 6.<br /> <br /> THANKS A LOT, now all I can imagine is a Scion of Hephestus or something building a Jaeger from Pacific Rim to fight a Titan.<br /> <br /> <i>And I have never realized how much I needed that until now</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=909011#post909011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was more concerned about the Associated Powers: Since callings give you associated powers, are the Gods still associated with Powers? If so, are the powers &quot;transmitted&quot; to their Scions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the post DOES mention that Gods are associated with Callings... And that at first, Heroes inherit a Calling from their parent. So my understanding is that a Scion would inherit some Favored/Associated Purviews via a Calling?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T08:52:15-07:00","id":909200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=909014#post909014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the post DOES mention that Gods are associated with Callings... And that at first, Heroes inherit a Calling from their parent. So my understanding is that a Scion would inherit some Favored/Associated Purviews via a Calling?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be weird, wouldn't it? I mean If Leader is associated with Sky, that means every God Leader is associated with Sky, let's say Odin or Huitzilopochtli, which is not really right. Need to see the full stuff ^^<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T09:07:48-07:00","id":909208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=909014#post909014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotta say, Neall, the more I read of Scion 2E the more excited I'm getting. I can't wait to see the full thing.<br /> <br /> Also, when I looked at the Alpha Slice (yeah yeah I only found it within the last couple weeks or so, at best) I was amused by the note on the Scale examples. &quot;Kaiju-hunting Robot&quot; is Scale 6.<br /> <br /> THANKS A LOT, now all I can imagine is a Scion of Hephestus or something building a Jaeger from Pacific Rim to fight a Titan.<br /> <br /> <i>And I have never realized how much I needed that until now</i></div> </div> </div> </div>This..sounds like a great idea to use in something I'm planning. An incarnation of Hephestus making this and using it.<br /> <i>This is going to be so much fun.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","name":"Grimangel53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T10:27:52-07:00","id":909258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=909200#post909200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would be weird, wouldn't it? I mean If Leader is associated with Sky, that means every God Leader is associated with Sky, let's say Odin or Huitzilopochtli, which is not really right. Need to see the full stuff ^^<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like each Calling has <i>multiple</i> associated Purviews, so Leaders may be associated with Sky, Sun, and... I'unno, maybe has a smattering of Leadership-based Knacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T11:59:18-07:00","id":909347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=909258#post909258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds like each Calling has <i>multiple</i> associated Purviews, so Leaders may be associated with Sky, Sun, and... I'unno, maybe has a smattering of Leadership-based Knacks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Let's say Leader includes Sky, Sun, Water, Fertility. How do you know what suits Zeus better? Of course Sky is the only one here. So does it mean we get to choose the Purviews associated with our character among the Purviews suggested?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T12:34:31-07:00","id":909371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=909347#post909347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Let's say Leader includes Sky, Sun, Water, Fertility. How do you know what suits Zeus better? Of course Sky is the only one here. So does it mean we get to choose the Purviews associated with our character among the Purviews suggested?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose so. You may have Zeus's Leadership skill, but you might express it differently than Pops did. My read (and this may be ENTIRELY inaccurate) is that Knacks and Purviews associated with your Calling count as Favored for you, to use the 1E mechanics as a comparison. Since the post confirms that yes, you can get Knacks from outside your Calling, just not easily.<br /> <br /> And if sounds like you can go through an arc where you denounce your divine heritage and can replace your Calling with another Calling, which leads to more Fun Times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T21:01:56-07:00","id":909803,"title":"","content":"Will there be any &quot;generic&quot; stunts with a prescribed cost and mechanical benefit similar to the gambits in EX3, at least in concept if not execution. Or will the scope of the stunt your extra sucesses allow and the mechanical/narrative benefit just be made up on the fly every time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T22:37:28-07:00","id":909858,"title":"","content":"Forgive me if this is silly (never played 1e), but is the expectation in play that all Pantheons are in the table, or just one? If the former, would sticking to a single Pantheon damage the game at all or terribly limit the amount of player options (beyond the obvious)?<br /> <br /> Also, is there any chance of us seeing what the complete listing for a single deity looks like once all the competent parts have been spoiled? I imagine having an example will make guessing all the more fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T22:47:59-07:00","id":909861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=909858#post909858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive me if this is silly (never played 1e), but is the expectation in play that all Pantheons are in the table, or just one? If the former, would sticking to a single Pantheon damage the game at all or terribly limit the amount of player options (beyond the obvious)?<br /> <br /> Also, is there any chance of us seeing what the complete listing for a single deity looks like once all the competent parts have been spoiled? I imagine having an example will make guessing all the more fun.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The usual expectation is that people will play characters tied to multiple Pantheons. The sample-characters Band in first edition included a Scion of Horus, a Scion of Thor, a Scion of Baron Samedi, a Scion of Aphrodite, etc - and the villain Band was equally diverse.<br /> <br /> Sticking to a single Pantheon was absolutely possible though, and one supplement was released that assumed an entirely Norse Cosmology. So that is definitely doable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T07:04:26-07:00","id":910046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=909803#post909803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will there be any &quot;generic&quot; stunts with a prescribed cost and mechanical benefit similar to the gambits in EX3, at least in concept if not execution. Or will the scope of the stunt your extra sucesses allow and the mechanical/narrative benefit just be made up on the fly every time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, we've got generic stunts like Create Complication, etc.<br /> <br /> Doing what Ex3 calls both stunts and Gambits is basically in the scope of the Stunt system. Part of the reason we went this direction is due to a criticism I've had of all three editions, which is that stunts are narrated <i>before </i>you roll, so it's still possible to completely fuck them up. &quot;With a cry of vengeance on my lips and murder in my heart, I sprint up the mast, leap onto the rigging, and springboard into the air, flipping down to slam my daiklave into the Lintha pirate!&quot; &quot;...well, that's a botch, you miss the rigging and fall into the briny deep.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T08:38:41-07:00","id":910106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=910046#post910046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, we've got generic stunts like Create Complication, etc.<br /> <br /> Doing what Ex3 calls both stunts and Gambits is basically in the scope of the Stunt system. Part of the reason we went this direction is due to a criticism I've had of all three editions, which is that stunts are narrated <i>before </i>you roll, so it's still possible to completely fuck them up. &amp;quot;With a cry of vengeance on my lips and murder in my heart, I sprint up the mast, leap onto the rigging, and springboard into the air, flipping down to slam my daiklave into the Lintha pirate!&amp;quot; &amp;quot;...well, that's a botch, you miss the rigging and fall into the briny deep.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds great, that moment when I saw that you had flipped stunts, as silly as it may sound, was when I was first like &quot;they get it, they really get it!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T15:00:56-07:00","id":910341,"title":"","content":"Is there some kind of mechanicn for Demigods and Gods to create Incarnations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T23:42:26-07:00","id":911493,"title":"","content":"I got the impression in reading through this thread that monotheism isn't overwhelmingly dominant in the World like it is in our world. Is that correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T23:55:08-07:00","id":911502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oriares</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=911493#post911493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got the impression in reading through this thread that monotheism isn't overwhelmingly dominant in the World like it is in our world. Is that correct?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From the The World blog post:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cults and temples take a far smaller place alongside prayer groups and churches, but they\u2019re there, in greater numbers and more acceptance than our world. Where you might see a gold cross around a young woman\u2019s neck, it might instead be a hammer amulet on a leather thong, or even a small raven\u2019s claw. The statue of Christ the Redeemer standing tall over in Rio de Janiero isn\u2019t replaced by Zeus on his throne, but signs of the lightning god of ruling are throughout the city. Ob-gyns with silk shirts occasionally charge their patients a premium for the taurobolinium, a phrase most don\u2019t quite grasp smuggled as it is within most overpriced American prenatal tests. It\u2019s a fashion among a very few soldiers in the know to carve the T\u00eewaz rune into their rifles to ensure the weapon won\u2019t jam on them. Other soldiers secretly into Mars to look here as they prepare for battle. Listen closely to the weather report over Caribbean radios, and you\u2019ll hear a drumbeat reminiscent of Shango\u2019s. In San Francisco, there\u2019s a few more Shinto-Buddhist temples to compete with those of what Western pantheons call the Celestial Bureaucracy. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T05:12:22-07:00","id":911581,"title":"","content":"There will be saints in Origins right? can you tell a bit more about them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T05:14:04-07:00","id":911582,"title":"","content":"sorry;I double posted","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 06-10-2016, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T01:03:23-07:00","id":912141,"title":"","content":"How central is the war against the Titans going to be in 2e? As a newcomer to the game, it's certainly one of the aspects that appeals to me the least, especially because it doesn't readily map to all of the Pantheons (the Kemetic gods chief among them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T02:00:57-07:00","id":912158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=912141#post912141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How central is the war against the Titans going to be in 2e? As a newcomer to the game, it's certainly one of the aspects that appeals to me the least, especially because it doesn't readily map to all of the Pantheons (the Kemetic gods chief among them).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been mentioned it will be less central, and may not feature at all depending on the Shard.<br /> <br /> If you're curious, the Titan that first edition plays the Egyptian gods off of is Aten, the Titan of Light (who the Greeks call Hyperion), who megalomaniacly originated monotheism in his effort to consume the gods of Egypt.<br /> <br /> Apophis (Apep) got name dropped as a Titan as well, but didn't get the coverage Aten got.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T00:37:09-07:00","id":912681,"title":"","content":"Will there be some overlap in how Callings and Purviews are linked together? Such as both Guardians and Warriors having access to the War Purview as a possible example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T13:02:33-07:00","id":912958,"title":"","content":"Any idea how long it'll take until we get a kickstarter for Scion?<br /> <br /> Edit: Late 2016, missed the already answered questions page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","user":"notanautomaton","date":". 06-12-2016, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"htt