ctions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T21:56:50-07:00","id":913229,"title":"","content":"Do we have any information on what will the Gods of the Manitouk Pantheon be?<br /> <br /> Basically, I want to know if Raven will be there","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T03:07:19-07:00","id":913329,"title":"","content":"Do we know anything about how Magic will be handled?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T03:29:03-07:00","id":913330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=913229#post913229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we have any information on what will the Gods of the Manitouk Pantheon be?<br /> <br /> Basically, I want to know if Raven will be there</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can tell you right now that Raven isn't an Algonquin figure, and is Northwestern in origin. My money's on him being introduced via an Inuit Pantheon under the name Tulugak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T06:54:18-07:00","id":913363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oriares</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=912681#post912681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will there be some overlap in how Callings and Purviews are linked together? Such as both Guardians and Warriors having access to the War Purview as a possible example?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm definitely hollering at neall for there to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","user":"Robert Vance","date":". 06-13-2016, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T09:29:52-07:00","id":913449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=913330#post913330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I can tell you right now that Raven isn't an Algonquin figure, and is Northwestern in origin. My money's on him being introduced via an Inuit Pantheon under the name Tulugak.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks bruv. Is the Northwest regional group the one that has the myth about that female figure that had her fingers cut off that turned in to all marine life?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T11:07:09-07:00","id":913524,"title":"","content":"I've asked a ton of terribly long winded questions... so I'm going to keep this one simple.<br /> <br /> <b>Can frequently used wonders eventually be turned into boons?</b><br /> <br /> As I understand it, wonders require you to spend legend every time you use it and boons simply reserve a point of legend. Spending every time or allocating in advance and having unlimited usages. I think it would be great to allow characters to really feel unique compared to one another. I mean sure, the DM could always homebrew new boons for em but it would be cool if the system sort of encouraged it in game as to create new and original god concepts rather than just sticking to the normal script of expectations. I think this is almost mandatory to truly to sell the idea of new gods for a new era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 06-13-2016, 02:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T12:33:21-07:00","id":913584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=913449#post913449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thanks bruv. Is the Northwest regional group the one that has the myth about that female figure that had her fingers cut off that turned in to all marine life?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sedna is an Inuit goddess, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T13:05:34-07:00","id":913611,"title":"","content":"I'm getting confused about something,Neall and other developers went out of their way to explain that mortal belief doesnt affect the gods,but everything i'm seeing contardicts that,we know that the gods rarelys how up on earth because interacitng with mortals cause Fatebindings that lock them in certain behaviors,and we know that gods mosty interact with Mortals using their Incarnations because Fate and the God's Callings has locked them int acting in certain ways. Gods have to create Incarnations to eb able to talk to mortals without being bound into a drama. And all of these things Fate does to Gods happens because of mortals,in the end its the <i>Mortals </i>that end up deciding what the god can or can't do,Or who the god is or isn't. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar137_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"137\" data-vbnamecard=\"137\">Neall</a>,would you mnd explaining? because i'm getting sort of confused","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T15:06:56-07:00","id":913680,"title":"","content":"I think there is a difference between Mortal beliefs doesn't affect gods and Gods don't require mortal belief. Mortals affect gods plenty via Fatebinding. It locks them into various modes of actions and limits their choices.<br /> <br /> Gods don't require mortals is more along the lines of an independence of power separate from mortal prayer/faith. Just because no one has prayed to [god of your choice] in two thousand years doesn't mean that their power has waned to any point or become close to mortal like some modern stories are trying to conflate. Zeus is Zeus. He's was a Legend 12 (or whatever he works out to be in 2nd Ed) powerful god in Ancient Greece seven thousand years ago and remains so today. He doesn't require the belief or worship of mortals to sustain his power...although if he had worshipers it would do something for him (if I remember the conversations correctly he may get extra temporary Legend points/other beneficial effects).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T15:40:15-07:00","id":913693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=913680#post913680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there is a difference between Mortal beliefs doesn't affect gods and Gods don't require mortal belief. Mortals affect gods plenty via Fatebinding. It locks them into various modes of actions and limits their choices.<br /> <br /> Gods don't require mortals is more along the lines of an independence of power separate from mortal prayer/faith. Just because no one has prayed to [god of your choice] in two thousand years doesn't mean that their power has waned to any point or become close to mortal like some modern stories are trying to conflate. Zeus is Zeus. He's was a Legend 12 (or whatever he works out to be in 2nd Ed) powerful god in Ancient Greece seven thousand years ago and remains so today. He doesn't require the belief or worship of mortals to sustain his power...although if he had worshipers it would do something for him (if I remember the conversations correctly he may get extra temporary Legend points/other beneficial effects).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh that makes more sense,I was starting to get a &quot;normal humans are not important vibe&quot; from the Neallspice answers and I got a bit worried?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T20:52:29-07:00","id":913842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=913229#post913229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we have any information on what will the Gods of the Manitouk Pantheon be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some tentative research let me put together this list of likely candidates<br /> <br /> Nanabozho (who is also Michabo, the Great Hare - Wisakedjak, and Gluscap)<br /> <br /> Chibiabos (Wolf, god of the dead, possibly also Malsum to Gluscap, though that villainous legend is disputed)<br /> <br /> Nokomis (Grandmother Woodchuck)<br /> <br /> Kichi-Odjig (the Great Fisher)<br /> <br /> Biboon (the North Wind)<br /> <br /> First Mother (the Corn Maiden found in many native american legends even beyond the Algonquin groups; alternatively could be male to the Ojibwa and be Mandaamin - both cases sacrifices self to become corn)<br /> <br /> Tshakapesh (Man in the Moon)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You've also got, particularly among the western Algonquin groups like the Ojibwe, Thunderbird (Animikii/Binesi) and Horned Serpent (Misingenbig). I don't know how Neall's planning to handle them other than he has plans. They're even more prominent among the legends of the Plains Indians, but obviously overlap through cultural exchange.<br /> <br /> <br /> And then there's Gitchi Manitou Him/Itself. My guess is that He/It will be left a distant unmanifest divinity referred to by different names by different Pantheons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 06-14-2016, 02:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T21:33:17-07:00","id":913859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=913842#post913842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thunderbird (Animikii/Binesi)</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Man, my dad's a giant bird.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Mine's a monkey, and he's kind of a blowhard.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;... Do you ever wonder <i>how</i> that happened? Like, how he met your mom and-&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I spend a good portion of my waking time pointedly trying NOT to think about that very subject.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T23:24:48-07:00","id":913901,"title":"","content":"Would you ever consider adding extra deities to the Pantheons in Hero after release?<br /> <br /> I would love to see my buddy Sobek make it in, but doubt he's popular enough to make the cut (I see Ra, Heru, Sutek, Aset, Hathor, Anpu, Ptah, Azar, Bast, and Sekhmet all making it in before him, and that's a lot of gods for a book with nine other Pantheons to fit).<br /> <br /> Also, will you merge Bast and Sekhmet, or are they distinct goddesses in Scion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T23:31:26-07:00","id":913908,"title":"","content":"Sobek was in the spread last edition IIRC. The big ones not included last edition that I hope will be are Nephthys and Sekhmet/Hathor.<br /> <br /> It will be interesting to see how Tefnut, Shu, Keb, and Nut are handled. If they're titans from a metaphysical standpoint (because Keb should really be the same type of being as Nut. Either both gods or both titans) are they Pantheon-allied ones whose Scions are as playable as the Scions of gods?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T23:56:39-07:00","id":913922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=913908#post913908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sobek was in the spread last edition IIRC. The big ones not included last edition that I hope will be are Nephthys and Sekhmet/Hathor.<br /> <br /> It will be interesting to see how Tefnut, Shu, Keb, and Nut are handled. If they're titans from a metaphysical standpoint (because Keb should really be the same type of being as Nut. Either both gods or both titans) are they Pantheon-allied ones whose Scions are as playable as the Scions of gods?</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope that the God/Pantheon divide is deemphasized or done away with entirely, as it doesn't really fit most Pantheons. Were Keb and Nut really worshipped at all? I always thought they were treated as incarnate forces or facets of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T00:41:29-07:00","id":913940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=913922#post913922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hope that the God/Pantheon divide is deemphasized or done away with entirely, as it doesn't really fit most Pantheons. Were Keb and Nut really worshipped at all? I always thought they were treated as incarnate forces or facets of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>That incarnate forces role is exactly what &quot;Titans&quot; in the broader sense are in the setting. Gods are defined primarily by their narrative (which I guess means &quot;Calling&quot; in Second Edition) while Titans are defined primarily by their Purview. Poseidon is god of the sea, Okeanus is the ocean incarnate, for example. Re is a sun-god, Aten is the literal sun-disc. Etc. We are going to see inherent automatic conflict between Gods and Titans not be the center of the game this edition though.<br /> <br /> In any regard, the nine gods of the Ennead of Heliopolis were Re, <b>Tefnut, Shu, Keb, Nut,</b> Azar, Aset, Nephthys, and Sutekh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T18:34:48-07:00","id":914529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=913940#post913940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That incarnate forces role is exactly what &quot;Titans&quot; in the broader sense are in the setting. Gods are defined primarily by their narrative (which I guess means &quot;Calling&quot; in Second Edition) while Titans are defined primarily by their Purview. Poseidon is god of the sea, Okeanus is the ocean incarnate, for example. Re is a sun-god, Aten is the literal sun-disc. Etc. We are going to see inherent automatic conflict between Gods and Titans not be the center of the game this edition though.<br /> <br /> In any regard, the nine gods of the Ennead of Heliopolis were Re, <b>Tefnut, Shu, Keb, Nut,</b> Azar, Aset, Nephthys, and Sutekh.</div> </div> </div> </div>correct me if'm rong,was the Ennead preced by another group Called the Ogdaed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T18:39:59-07:00","id":914537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=914529#post914529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">correct me if'm rong,was the Ennead preced by another group Called the Ogdaed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Different cities. The Ennead is Heliopolis. The Ogdoad is Hermopolis. The Ogdoad would probably be Titans in Scion cosmology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T18:44:04-07:00","id":914543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=914537#post914537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Different cities. The Ennead is Heliopolis. The Ogdoad is Hermopolis. The Ogdoad would probably be Titans in Scion cosmology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm,neall mentioned that sometimes <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">a god becomes recognized by another culture as a pantheon. could the ennead and the ogdaed have merged?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T18:54:28-07:00","id":914552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=914543#post914543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm,neall mentioned that sometimes <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">a god becomes recognized by another culture as a pantheon. could the ennead and the ogdaed have merged?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, the chthonic &quot;infinities&quot; the Ogdoad represent really seem like they fit Titans in setting more than gods. In Hermopolis cosmology, the Ogdoad created Ra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T19:00:27-07:00","id":914557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=914552#post914552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like I said, the chthonic &quot;infinities&quot; the Ogdoad represent really seem like they fit Titans in setting more than gods. In Hermopolis cosmology, the Ogdoad created Ra.</div> </div> </div> </div>that makes more sense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T20:01:45-07:00","id":915988,"title":"","content":"Does Santa Claus exist in the World - and if so, what Pantheon sired him?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 06-17-2016, 02:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T20:12:23-07:00","id":915993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=915988#post915988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Santa Clause</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the Tim Allen movie? I hope so, it's one of my favorites! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Seriously though, I got no idea)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T20:40:05-07:00","id":916004,"title":"","content":"I believe Claus is a German name...so I'm going with Norse. He'd be a Vanir trying to spread cheer compared to the dour nature of the Aesir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T23:26:26-07:00","id":916049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=916004#post916004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe Claus is a German name...so I'm going with Norse. He'd be a Vanir trying to spread cheer compared to the dour nature of the Aesir.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vanir works for the Germanic roots of the tradition observed in the English speaking world. St. Nicholas was Greek though and associate with various traditions in the Mediterranean that were adopted from earlier Poseidon-associated stories/traditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T23:34:16-07:00","id":916053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=915988#post915988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Santa Claus exist in the World - and if so, what Pantheon sired him?</div> </div> </div> </div>I asked Neall what Santa would be in Scion terms earlier. His response:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Probably a mantle shared between the Norse and Slavic pantheons. I'd like Mikola Mozhaiski to be in the game, at the very least. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T00:31:27-07:00","id":916064,"title":"","content":"I'm definitely leaning toward using him as one of the figures to help fill out the Vanir. &quot;Jolnir&quot;, is the seasonal god of Yule, of similar status to his fellow Vanir deity Eostre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T00:49:19-07:00","id":916070,"title":"","content":"My current list of the gods of Vanaheim:<br /> <br /> -Delling (king)<br /> <br /> -Nott (queen)<br /> <br /> -Dagr<br /> <br /> -Hoenir (aka Vili, Odin's brother and their hostage chief in assuring the peace between Vanaheim and Asgard)<br /> <br /> -Jolnir<br /> <br /> -Eostre<br /> <br /> -Nerthus (original sister-wife of Njord, thus mother to Freyr and Freyja)<br /> <br /> -Jord (titantess of the world, and benevolent mother-goddess to the Vanir, though less easy peace with Aesir)<br /> <br /> -Meili (Jord's other son by Odin, the Vanir god of lightning)<br /> <br /> Aegir and Ran's domain laps the shores of Vanaheim, and these titans are much closer by blood to the Vanir nature gods than they are to the Aesir.<br /> <br /> Odr, the long lost husband of Freyja, was of the Vanir, but he's gone a Vikining beyond the known cosmos","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 06-17-2016, 04:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T05:23:18-07:00","id":916134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=916070#post916070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My current list of the gods of Vanaheim:<br /> <br /> -Delling (king)<br /> <br /> -Nott (queen)<br /> <br /> -Dagr<br /> <br /> -Hoenir (aka Vili, Odin's brother and their hostage chief in assuring the peace between Vanaheim and Asgard)<br /> <br /> -Jolnir<br /> <br /> -Eostre<br /> <br /> -Nerthus (original sister-wife of Njord, thus mother to Freyr and Freyja)<br /> <br /> -Jord (titantess of the world, and benevolent mother-goddess to the Vanir, though less easy peace with Aesir)<br /> <br /> -Meili (Jord's other son by Odin, the Vanir god of lightning)<br /> <br /> Aegir and Ran's domain laps the shores of Vanaheim, and these titans are much closer by blood to the Vanir nature gods than they are to the Aesir.<br /> <br /> Odr, the long lost husband of Freyja, was of the Vanir, but he's gone a Vikining beyond the known cosmos</div> </div> </div> </div>wait,Nott is or is <i>nott </i>the queen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 06-17-2016, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T08:29:58-07:00","id":917363,"title":"","content":"Hey Neall, I have a question. I'm not sure if it's been asked befoer, but will we possibly get goddesses like Tyche/Fortuna and Hesta/Vesta in the Theoi?I know there's already going to be alot of them, but seeing as those two are ones I'd love to see a scion play from, i was just wondering. <br /> Cant wait for the announcement for Scion's kickstarter, when it comes. I want the books to be on their way already!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","name":"Grimangel53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T23:58:54-07:00","id":917832,"title":"","content":"Even if they aren't in the core (I would be SHOCKED if a minor goddess like Tyche was in the core list, I'd be surprised if Hestia was in the core, but I'd expect her to come up later), but going off first edition, pulling on them to play a Scion of one is just a matter of choosing the right associated Purviews (and now presumably Callings), so shouldn't be a hard addition at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T07:57:11-07:00","id":918038,"title":"","content":"You can't have Thyche if you don't have Nemesis as well. Thyche would wander the world spreading her gifts of Fortune/Fate/Chance and Providence and then Nemesis would find the 'jerk' who got anything too extravagant and punish them for it. They are like a package deal or since I consider Nemesis a greater Goddess than Thyche, Thyche would be in her Retinue. It's a god level background I made up to describe people like Apollo, Aphrodite, Frigg and most King/Queens of the gods who had Legend 9+ Followers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T08:49:27-07:00","id":919117,"title":"","content":"Something I was curious about incarnates. I know they are a type of scion and we are now allowed to branch off majorly from our parent's concept, but where does that leave the incarnates? Is it truly possible to become completely a different person to who you were incarnated from? A goddess of luck and marriage becoming a god of, I don't know, Hate. And what does this mean for pantheons who do this fairly regularly like the Deva?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T21:21:29-07:00","id":919497,"title":"","content":"Can you tell us anything about the Relics in the Hero book? I'd like to get a pretty broad selection, if possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T00:44:56-07:00","id":919572,"title":"","content":"Is it possible for a lesser... god-like... aspect of a Titan to be free even while the Titan is imprisoned? I'm just wondering about the very different status of Saturn compared to Kronus. It could work if most of Kronus is bound, but an agricultural aspect of him escaped to flee to Italy, where the Sabine gods led by Janus welcomed him (things becoming complicated later when Aeneas shows up with the Olympians in tow).<br /> <br /> Wow... Aeneas &amp; the Sabine gods, Divus Julius &amp; the Nemetondevos.... look out for those Scions of Venus!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T11:29:10-07:00","id":919835,"title":"","content":"Sort of gives the phrase 'Love conquers all' a new meaning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T16:22:17-07:00","id":919991,"title":"","content":"Do the gods largely draw their Scions from the cultures and ethnic groups with historic ties to them, or is anyone fair game? Would it be odd to see an African-American chosen by the Aesir, or a white man chosen by the Devas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 06-23-2016, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T16:48:25-07:00","id":920004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=919991#post919991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the gods largely draw their Scions from the cultures and ethnic groups with historic ties to them, or is anyon fair game? Would it be odd to see an African-American chosen by the Aesir, or a white man chosen by the Devas?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know for sure but i think it matters what kind of scion it is.<br /> 1) For birth scion, I think it matters more if the mortal they sleep with vibes with what they are associated with, although they still probably met them where their cultural ties are strong. (Daddy may have been a tourist for example)<br /> 2) Scions from long lines are more likely to be a particular culture or ethnicity simply by what they are, but the Romans spread wide and the next Divus Julius could be anybody, while perhaps other pantheons are less likely to branch, also more years makes it more likely.<br /> 3)The scions made of whole cloth? Definitely their own culture. It's what they are familiar with and might even make the act easier, but don't forget many of those cultures were much more racially diverse than we believe them to be, today. <br /> 4) Incarnates? I don't really know, but I believe at least somewhat tied to their own culture and themes. <br /> <br /> But once again, this can cover multiple areas. Cultures weren't entirely homogeneous back in the old days, depending who they were, and today many cultures have spread far and wide, so it's not absurd to say scions can almost be anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T17:30:22-07:00","id":920030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=919991#post919991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the gods largely draw their Scions from the cultures and ethnic groups with historic ties to them, or is anyon fair game?</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T18:02:04-07:00","id":920041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=917832#post917832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if they aren't in the core (I would be SHOCKED if a minor goddess like Tyche was in the core list, I'd be surprised if Hestia was in the core, but I'd expect her to come up later), but going off first edition, pulling on them to play a Scion of one is just a matter of choosing the right associated Purviews (and now presumably Callings), so shouldn't be a hard addition at all.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'll probably figure it out then. (i'd love to see nemesis as well, though i wouldn't call tyche a lesser god, especially in her roman form, but cest la vie) I can hope for Hestia, as she is an Olympian, and pray for a chance that tyche/fortuna and nemesis both get their day, via supplement, billing in the book, or even if i just have to figure out the goddesses myself (which i will totally do for those two because they're fantastic.) i can dream cant i?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","name":"Grimangel53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T22:10:50-07:00","id":920165,"title":"","content":"Any chance of us seeing another blog post soon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T22:16:05-07:00","id":920169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=917832#post917832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if they aren't in the core (I would be SHOCKED if a minor goddess like Tyche was in the core list, I'd be surprised if Hestia was in the core, but I'd expect her to come up later), but going off first edition, pulling on them to play a Scion of one is just a matter of choosing the right associated Purviews (and now presumably Callings), so shouldn't be a hard addition at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know Hestia and Demeter aren't as interesting as some of the other Dodekatheon gods, but I always felt like their exclusion was kinda unfair. They were first generation gods, equals to Zeus, Hera, Poseidon, and Hades, but their purviews weren't as sexy as say Ares, Aphrodite, or Hermes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T22:31:31-07:00","id":920176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=920169#post920169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know Hestia and Demeter aren't as interesting as some of the other Dodekatheon gods, but I always felt like their exclusion was kinda unfair. They were first generation gods, equals to Zeus, Hera, Poseidon, and Hades, but their purviews weren't as sexy as say Ares, Aphrodite, or Hermes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the bigger question is prominence in myth rather than how sexy a purview is or technical rank. Hestia is almost guaranteed to be back burner because she doesn't have prominent stories in which she's the central actor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T23:34:34-07:00","id":920209,"title":"","content":"Agreed, I mean Hera probably has the least amount of Sexy Purviews except perhaps Hestia, but her prominence in myth demands she has a place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T23:13:52-07:00","id":921367,"title":"","content":"How are the odds of us seeing a Sumerian/Babylonian Pantheon in Demigod or elsewhere?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T05:38:23-07:00","id":921448,"title":"","content":"The Mesopotamian pantheon's slated for later books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T11:38:12-07:00","id":922755,"title":"","content":"I gotta say, the blog post that Neall made about Pantheons made me imagine him acting like a kid in a candy store, picking up books of myths and legends and going &quot;Oh, oh, can I do a writeup for this one?!&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: To clarify, this is meant as a complement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T14:22:41-07:00","id":922843,"title":"","content":"Hey Neall, Quick question. I'm not sure if this one has been asked already, but where are you getting resources for the Manitouk Pantheon? I'm interested, one in learning more about it and two, if people from that culture are being consulted about it.<br /> This comes mostly because I've seen some backlash rise around some like J.K.R. using Native American myth and symbology as part of their narrative world, without looking for consultation on how to use it with respect to the culture and faith of those people. I'm wondering if there has been any thought about this around the office, and what your take on it is. Especially given the nature of this game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","name":"Grimangel53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T19:31:25-07:00","id":922994,"title":"","content":"The fact that they're doing a distinctly Algonquin Pantheon, as opposed to some generic Native American catchall, puts most of my fears to rest about making the same mistakes as Rowling's oblivious b.s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T20:14:25-07:00","id":923025,"title":"","content":"I wonder - with the &quot;old religions&quot; having continuously existed into modern day, will positions like the Pythia still be filled in the World? Will the Pythia be a public figure handing out prophesies from Delphi, respected as a religious leader not unlike the Pope or the Dalai Lama, even if without the same number of followers?<br /> <br /> Similarly will the Temple at Uppsala still stand and be a site of global pilgrimage for believers in the Aesir?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T20:18:10-07:00","id":923027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=923025#post923025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder - with the &quot;old religions&quot; having continuously existed into modern day, will positions like the Pythia still be filled in the World? Will the Pythia be a public figure handing out prophesies from Delphi, respected as a religious leader not unlike the Pope or the Dalai Lama, even if without the same number of followers?<br /> <br /> Similarly will the Temple at Uppsala still stand and be a site of global pilgrimage for believers in the Aesir?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the book doesn't specifically confirm this, then it will be considered so at my games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T20:20:11-07:00","id":923029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=923025#post923025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder - with the &amp;quot;old religions&amp;quot; having continuously existed into modern day, will positions like the Pythia still be filled in the World? Will the Pythia be a public figure handing out prophesies from Delphi, respected as a religious leader not unlike the Pope or the Dalai Lama, even if without the same number of followers?<br /> <br /> Similarly will the Temple at Uppsala still stand and be a site of global pilgrimage for believers in the Aesir?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I party entirely too hard at a reconstructed Bubastis?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T20:39:59-07:00","id":923032,"title":"","content":"Of course even if the Pythia is one of the most well known leaders of faith in the Theoi, there are going to be other denominations. The Orphics, the Eleusinians, the Mithraists - to say nothing of those in general who worship the gods in their Roman incarnations and put their faith in the revelations of numerous &quot;Sibyls&quot;, and the Sibylline Books, rather than putting special stake in the Pythia (which ironically puts those faithful speaking Latin in the role of the Protestants in this religious dynamic).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T20:48:54-07:00","id":923036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=923032#post923032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course even if the Pythia is one of the most well known leaders of faith in the Theoi, there are going to be other denominations. The Orphics, the Eleusinians, the Mithraists - to say nothing of those in general who worship the gods in their Roman incarnations and put their faith in the revelations of numerous &amp;quot;Sibyls&amp;quot;, and the Sibylline Books, rather than putting special stake in the Pythia (which ironically puts those faithful speaking Latin in the role of the Protestants in this religious dynamic).</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that it seems like The World is going to be left largely vague and we're likely to see lots of Shards rather than a deep drill into one setting, these comments are really bumming me out. I'd kill to see more of this setting in that kind of detail. <br /> <br /> Is there a minority among Kemetics who revere the Ogdoad, rather than the Ennead or wider pantheon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T20:54:11-07:00","id":923041,"title":"","content":"...Sorry if I seem insensitive/like I'm derailing the conversation, but... why do people think that Rowling messed up here? I've read the stuff myself and haven't really seen anything wrong with it. In addition, I haven't seen anyone upset at the Morrigan being a mortal witch in the Harry Potter Universe, nor have I seen any Asatru go up in arms over the Norse gods being portrayed as aliens in the MCU. What makes this instance different/bad?<br /> <br /> (I want to clarify, by the way, that I'm not saying anyone is wrong here. I'm just kinda clueless about all this, and it's bothering me because I also consider myself a Harry Potter fan and I still don't understand the problem. Then again, I do like the Fate series, which is infamous for taking liberties with source materials, so maybe it's just that I'm less sensitive to stuff like this.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11755-aquatica1000","name":"Aquatica1000","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T21:15:41-07:00","id":923051,"title":"","content":"The difference is Native American religions have been continuously practiced, they aren't reconstructed, and they aren't open for outsiders like neo-paganism or major Monotheist faiths - they are tied to native identity; and more importantly as a white European her disregard for representing them fairly ties in with a long AND CONTINUOUS history of cultural imperialism. Western Europeans and their descendants have been trying to obliterate Native American spirituality for over half a millennium. If she's going to delve into the subject matter she needs to display some sensitivity and respect toward that reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 06-29-2016, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T22:50:36-07:00","id":923089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquatica1000</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=923041#post923041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Sorry if I seem insensitive/like I'm derailing the conversation, but... why do people think that Rowling messed up here? I've read the stuff myself and haven't really seen anything wrong with it. In addition, I haven't seen anyone upset at the Morrigan being a mortal witch in the Harry Potter Universe, nor have I seen any Asatru go up in arms over the Norse gods being portrayed as aliens in the MCU. What makes this instance different/bad?<br /> <br /> (I want to clarify, by the way, that I'm not saying anyone is wrong here. I'm just kinda clueless about all this, and it's bothering me because I also consider myself a Harry Potter fan and I still don't understand the problem. Then again, I do like the Fate series, which is infamous for taking liberties with source materials, so maybe it's just that I'm less sensitive to stuff like this.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Barring a few neopagans, very few people still practice the faiths of the Norse gods. There are still plenty of Native Americans, and a rich white lady from overseas folding theor actual beliefs into her world of pretend is pretty obviously harmful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T23:10:39-07:00","id":923104,"title":"","content":"Neall, will there be any Shards in Origin/Hero/etc, or will they be in other books/standalone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T02:02:56-07:00","id":923143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=923089#post923089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Barring a few neopagans, very few people still practice the faiths of the Norse gods. There are still plenty of Native Americans, and a rich white lady from overseas folding theor actual beliefs into her world of pretend is pretty obviously harmful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Particularly when it's done saying &quot;their beliefs are silly misunderstandings of the magic already established in the setting&quot; something she notably does not explicitly do with Christian miracles. A lot of us might be fine with it if she did, but obviously that would anger huge portions of her market, and if she isn't willing to treat Christianity that way, there's a problem treating other continuous living belief systems that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T23:29:00-07:00","id":923730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=923143#post923143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Particularly when it's done saying &amp;quot;their beliefs are silly misunderstandings of the magic already established in the setting&amp;quot; something she notably does not explicitly do with Christian miracles. A lot of us might be fine with it if she did, but obviously that would anger huge portions of her market, and if she isn't willing to treat Christianity that way, there's a problem treating other continuous living belief systems that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Am I the only one who has no idea what we're talking about here? Did Rowling put some kind of Native stuff in HP that I missed entirely?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T00:36:37-07:00","id":923748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=923730#post923730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Am I the only one who has no idea what we're talking about here? Did Rowling put some kind of Native stuff in HP that I missed entirely?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> She's been doing &quot;Magical History of North America&quot; reveals on Pottermore, in lead up to the new movie out later this year (set in a strikingly white version of 1920s New York... you know... during the Harlem Renaissance). Some of the stuff is kind of oblivious about the US*, but the first entry, the one on Native Wizardry was basically a &quot;What Not to Do&quot; on the subject and set off an online storm via the voiced complaints of Native peoples.<br /> <br /> She just posted the history of the founding of Ilvermorney (the US counterpart to Hogwarts), which is a good read (it was founded by a runaway Irish Heir of Slytherin, who married a Muggle back in the 18th Century), along with a new test on the site to determine your Ilvermorney House (named for indigenous magical creatures: Thunderbird, Horned Serpent, Wampus, or Pukwudgie).<br /> <br /> <br /> *It's weird that Salem is as big a deal as it is defining American Wizarding World's extreme culture of secrecy compared to Britain, when Britain had far more witch hunts. Also, I'm not sure if the policies of complete separation between the Magical Community and the Muggle World are meant to be a stand-in for racial segregation (i don't think so, I think it's supposed to fill the role of prohibition in the movie's 1920s setting), but if it's not, she needs to realize how loaded the word &quot;segregation&quot; is in a US context. If it IS meant to be a racial politics allegory, it's a really bad one, because her narrative presented both sides as baring guilt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 06-30-2016, 03:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T15:49:47-07:00","id":924144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=923748#post923748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*It's weird that Salem is as big a deal as it is defining American Wizarding World's extreme culture of secrecy compared to Britain, when Britain had far more witch hunts. Also, I'm not sure if the policies of complete separation between the Magical Community and the Muggle World are meant to be a stand-in for racial segregation (i don't think so, I think it's supposed to fill the role of prohibition in the movie's 1920s setting), but if it's not, she needs to realize how loaded the word &quot;segregation&quot; is in a US context. If it IS meant to be a racial politics allegory, it's a really bad one, because her narrative presented both sides as baring guilt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking from a strictly meta perspective, Salem and the Witch Trials are kinda super famous. Pretty much <i>everyone's</i> heard of them at one point or another so it makes for a decent spot to put a &quot;And this is why magic and mundane don't mix&quot; and have most people go &quot;Yeah, that makes sense&quot; and not put any more thought on the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T13:08:29-07:00","id":924578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquatica1000</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=923041#post923041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (I want to clarify, by the way, that I'm not saying anyone is wrong here. I'm just kinda clueless about all this, and it's bothering me because I also consider myself a Harry Potter fan and I still don't understand the problem. Then again, I do like the Fate series, which is infamous for taking liberties with source materials, so maybe it's just that I'm less sensitive to stuff like this.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I consider myself a harry potter fan as well, and as i've been a bit desensitized to issues like these, i'd rather be made aware, and understand. dont worry. wanting to understand is well.. understandable.<br /> <br /> I'd personally like to learn more about their mythos, legends, and stories, because from the little i do understand, i would actually like to learn about it and really get the myths. i love mythologies, legends, and stories, so I'd like to learn more, as always.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","name":"Grimangel53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T16:18:56-07:00","id":924665,"title":"","content":"I feel we are getting a bit off base; so...<br /> <br /> I noticed that magic will mostly be counted under pantheon specific purviews; but in the first book, mortal magicians will exist. Will these guys not be connected to any pantheon? And regardless, how will it deal with pantheons who widely accept mortal practitioners in their myth but who operate in specific ways? I mean an ancient Egyptian magician is very different from the woman practicing seidr, and even further from religious agents like mambos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T20:16:30-07:00","id":924747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=924665#post924665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel we are getting a bit off base; so...<br /> <br /> I noticed that magic will mostly be counted under pantheon specific purviews; but in the first book, mortal magicians will exist. Will these guys not be connected to any pantheon? And regardless, how will it deal with pantheons who widely accept mortal practitioners in their myth but who operate in specific ways? I mean an ancient Egyptian magician is very different from the woman practicing seidr, and even further from religious agents like mambos.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect that (as part of making Scion feel distinct from both the WoD/CofD and other urban fantasy universes) there may be the ruling that all supernatural forces stem from the Pantheons. You might have Kahunas and Seidr-witches, but Hermetic wizards are probably not a thing (unless you get generous with your interpretation of Hermes-Trismegustus).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T06:09:00-07:00","id":924859,"title":"","content":"I suspected as much, but Neall has talked about wizards in general on several occasions so wasn't sure, especially with PSPs being shown (I presume) until later. I know PSPs will detail how each pantheon uses magic, so I was curious if mortal magicians would be separated or it would just list magic types. Aka: Prophets, Religions agents, witches, and then I guess the heavy hitters of myth, like the Egyptian sorcerers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T13:23:35-07:00","id":926594,"title":"","content":"Mortal magicians who explicitly derive their power from non-pantheon sources are a pretty integral part of many mythologies. Evil witches in West African folklore are a good example. You also don't have to be a scion of L\u01ceoz\u01d0 to practice D\u00e0oist sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T13:52:49-07:00","id":926613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=926594#post926594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortal magicians who explicitly derive their power from non-pantheon sources are a pretty integral part of many mythologies. Evil witches in West African folklore are a good example. You also don't have to be a scion of L\u01ceoz\u01d0 to practice D\u00e0oist sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think in the Last GenCon it was mentioned that sorcererrs could <i>steal </i>power from the gods,is that like,they suck out Purviews and Knacks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T15:00:29-07:00","id":926661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=926594#post926594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortal magicians who explicitly derive their power from non-pantheon sources are a pretty integral part of many mythologies. Evil witches in West African folklore are a good example. You also don't have to be a scion of L\u01ceoz\u01d0 to practice D\u00e0oist sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Both of your examples get their power from at least pantheon inspired sources. The Daoist sorceror doesn't need to be a scion, but he does need power that is connected to Doaist principles. The same with the witch whose power and it's capabilities are defined by what folklore she's from.<br /> <br /> I'm curious if<br /> 1) The sorceror and the witch will work the exact same way<br /> 2) Be put in different groups so all witches or all sorcerors work the same way <br /> 3) Or finally will they be defined by the pantheons they are part, aka Does the Daoist sorcerer have particular abilities the Egyptian sorceror does not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T19:16:24-07:00","id":927401,"title":"","content":"Are