":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T21:57:20-07:00","id":945288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=945232#post945232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The gen con brochure said that theriantropes will be playable, so would that mean I could have an NPC pack of werewolf scions (one the son of Anubis (since they determined that eygptian jackals are actually wolves) one a daughter of Fenrir, one a child of Marinette of the dry arms (who is heavily associated with werewolves in voodoo theology), a pup of Zeus' Zeus <i>Lykaios</i> aspect and a scion of the Turkic/Mongolian wolf mother figure Asena? because if so, I just had a great story idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want Egyptian werewolves, look to Wepawet before Anubis; he's a hunter, scout, and war god, plus a wolf rather than a jackal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T22:39:03-07:00","id":945298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=945288#post945288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you want Egyptian werewolves, look to Wepawet before Anubis; he's a hunter, scout, and war god, plus a wolf rather than a jackal.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, Wepawet is often portrayed as either Anubis' son or father, so add that to the wolf/jackal mix-up and I can't help but consider anubis a wolf. But yeah, Wepawet is cool too. I actually have a story set in a universe of my own creation where the canine version of saint Christoper was originally a werewolf priest of Wepawet, then he (allegedly) had that encounter with kid Jesus at the river, changed his name to Christoper and wound up converting European's werewolves to Christianity, thus why they exist openly in my book's world. Several of the main characters in my novel are members of the church he founded<br /> <br /> Also, one of my Scion plot ideas for the Asena scion is that they have a weird relationship with the Slavic gods due to the fact that several of the ethnic groups that Asena appears in the mythology of both have messed up relationships with Russia, but also consider her a nationalistic figure (including Turkey and possibly Chechnya) but also is important to the Mongolians who are allies with Russia. All it would take is a international incident that forces them to choose sides to put her in danger. Also, one thing I discovered that the cWod got right is that Russian folklore considers wolves to be the aristocrats of the forest, so maybe a smexy silver fang knockoff could tempt her to side with Mongolia and Russia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 08-07-2016, 01:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T15:28:03-07:00","id":945705,"title":"","content":"Can we hope to see the Storypath Preview once everyone recovers from Gen Con?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T18:37:54-07:00","id":945792,"title":"","content":"On this brief tangent, a cool thing about Wepwawet vs Anup is that technically where Wepwawet is always depicted as masculine, Anup is a bit more wibbly wobbly with being rendered masculine, feminine and sometimes just neutral across multiple texts. Which kind of fits as old school Anup was a more liminal deity, going hard on being a psychopomp, almost shamanistic in how they cross back and forth between our world and the Duat(said to actually know the ways in and out), etc. etc. Did I mention I am all the hype about getting to play a Scion of the Netjeru(and the Yoruba, oh so much the Yoruba).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2042-madxhatter0","name":"MadxHatter0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:44:33-07:00","id":947025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=940138#post940138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neall,can you please tell more about Mantle Stealing?</div> </div> </div> </div>You walk like the gods until they walk like you. And then you walk somewhere else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions"