class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=948314#post948314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait,can scions become something beyond a god?</div> </div> </div> </div>Making your own pantheon and crafting your Creation and Constituent Myths is what I consider to be a viable ending for a <b>Scion </b>campaign.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Other way of reading it: Can you go from a God to a </i><i>Demigod</i><i> and then back down to </i><i>Hero</i><i>?</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well, here's the thing. If a dead God's Incarnates become fragments of that God who can claim said God's mantle, the Incarnation who claims it is very similar, but different in a lot of ways.<br /> <br /> I mean, did you ever read the end of Sandman, where Morpheus learns he needs to change or die and makes his choice? Morpheus and Daniel are both Dream, but they're very different.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T07:13:40-07:00","id":948581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=948572#post948572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making your own pantheon and crafting your Creation and Constituent Myths is what I consider to be a viable ending for a <b>Scion </b>campaign.<br /> <br /> [/I]<br /> <br /> Well, here's the thing. If a dead God's Incarnates become fragments of that God who can claim said God's mantle, the Incarnation who claims it is very similar, but different in a lot of ways.<br /> <br /> I mean, did you ever read the end of Sandman, where Morpheus learns he needs to change or die and makes his choice? Morpheus and Daniel are both Dream, but they're very different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once a Creation is crafted does it literrally becomes real? Does the World change to match the myth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T11:35:32-07:00","id":948718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <st