e and pledge service to get a loan of a relic, Knack, or Boon; and <i>Eyes of Knowledge</i>, which lets you ask a question of a divine being and receive the answer in the form of a poetic monologue. Devotion's Reward could probably temporarily purify your spiritual essence, the result of which is blue skin and sprouting extra arms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very, very cool. Any chance you could spoil the name of the Netjer equivalent?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T20:52:35-07:00","id":956129,"title":"","content":"Let's just take this to its logical conclusion. <br /> <br /> Neall, can we know about all the PSPs, pwease?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T03:43:26-07:00","id":956246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=955636#post955636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can only attack once per turn.<br /> <br /> This initiative system is basically designed to encourage those sorts of chain reactions by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is as I see in the rules, one player character acts on alternative turn with the director characters. How to create those chain reactions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T06:14:51-07:00","id":956283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=956246#post956246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is as I see in the rules, one player character acts on alternative turn with the director characters. How to create those chain reactions?</div> </div> </div> </div>That might be how things shake up in the roster, but often I've found that two players act one after another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T06:20:33-07:00","id":956286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=956129#post956129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's just take this to its logical conclusion.<br /> <br /> Neall, can we know about all the PSPs, pwease?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll take it a step further and give you the playtest motifs, or how other Purviews' free-form magic is worked through the cultural lens of the PSP.<br /> <br /> <b>\u00c6sir: Wyrd</b><br /> <i>The destinies spun by the Nornir can be changed through drawing runes or magical weaving.</i><br /> <b>Kami: Yaoyorozu-no-Kamigami</b><br /> <i>The kami are all things, and can be bidden to work wonders.</i><br /> <b>Dev\u00e1: Yoga</b><br /> <i>By chanting spells and undergoing austerities, one may create or become a miracle.</i><br /> <b>Manitou: Dodaem</b><br /> <i>An offering of tobacco, prayers, dance and song convinces the myriad, unseen manitous to work their magic in your favor.</i><br /> <b>Netjer: Heku</b><br /> <i>Speaking the sacred ritual words releases sekhem, lending power to the soul.</i><br /> <b>Orisha: Posession*</b><br /> <i>Those who understand plants can use them in magic and medicine.</i><br /> <b>Sh\u00e9n: Tianming*</b><br /> <i>Alchemy manipulates the energies both within and without the body through exercises and concoctions associated with the five elements.</i><br /> <b>Teotl: Nextlahualli</b><br /> <i>Offerings of flowers, food, effigies, and blood empower the gods to sustain the World with miracles.</i><br /> <b>Theoi: Metamorphosis*</b><br /> <i>The most high may grant their favor to those who beseech them.</i><br /> <b>Tuatha de Danann: Geasa*</b><br /> <i>Magic flows from verse and satire.</i><br /> <br /> *This Purview's motif doesn't have a ton to do with the Boons it's got.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 08-23-2016, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T06:43:42-07:00","id":956296,"title":"","content":"Interesting. I didn't expect the PSPs to be so geared towards each Pantheon's culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T06:58:50-07:00","id":956302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=956296#post956296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. I didn't expect the PSPs to be so geared towards each Pantheon's culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>The motifs are, because all freeform magic must be worked through a motif (whether you get it from a relic or a PSP). The PSPs themselves are comprised of magic we see gods using in stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T09:18:35-07:00","id":956369,"title":"","content":"Neall, I got super hype seeing Heku on there(though from most readings I've seen it spelled out as heka, but that's a minor nitpick if anything, and you probably have better sources than me). Though, I was wondering if you could say why the Orisha got Possession? Cause, getting ridden is a thing, but you see that more in vodoun. While, if you asked me, one of the major forms of &quot;magic&quot; involving the Orisha and Yoruba culture at large is the concept of ashe, and I was wondering if you could talk about about why you went for possession instead of something like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2042-madxhatter0","name":"MadxHatter0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T11:28:41-07:00","id":956447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=956286#post956286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll take it a step further and give you the playtest motifs, or how other Purviews' free-form magic is worked through the cultural lens of the PSP.<br /> <br /> <b>\u00c6sir: Wyrd</b><br /> <i>The destinies spun by the Nornir can be changed through drawing runes or magical weaving.</i><br /> <b>Kami: Yaoyorozu-no-Kamigami</b><br /> <i>The kami are all things, and can be bidden to work wonders.</i><br /> <b>Dev\u00e1: Yoga</b><br /> <i>By chanting spells and undergoing austerities, one may create or become a miracle.</i><br /> <b>Manitou: Dodaem</b><br /> <i>An offering of tobacco, prayers, dance and song convinces the myriad, unseen manitous to work their magic in your favor.</i><br /> <b>Netjer: Heku</b><br /> <i>Speaking the sacred ritual words releases sekhem, lending power to the soul.</i><br /> <b>Orisha: Posession*</b><br /> <i>Those who understand plants can use them in magic and medicine.</i><br /> <b>Sh\u00e9n: Tianming*</b><br /> <i>Alchemy manipulates the energies both within and without the body through exercises and concoctions associated with the five elements.</i><br /> <b>Teotl: Nextlahualli</b><br /> <i>Offerings of flowers, food, effigies, and blood empower the gods to sustain the World with miracles.</i><br /> <b>Theoi: Metamorphosis*</b><br /> <i>The most high may grant their favor to those who beseech them.</i><br /> <b>Tuatha de Danann: Geasa*</b><br /> <i>Magic flows from verse and satire.</i><br /> <br /> *This Purview's motif doesn't have a ton to do with the Boons it's got.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bMy God!<br /> <br /> It's like you guys reached inside my head, pulled out my entire list of things I'd like to see done to improve PSPs, and just said &quot;Yeah, let's do all of this.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm so thrilled to see how this gets tied into the cultures and beliefs of the people who actually worshipped these gods. This really will make playing a Scion of one Pantheon or another feel like a genuinely unique experience.<br /> <br /> This is what Scion should've been from Day One! Can't wait to get my hands on this book.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T11:59:51-07:00","id":956472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=956286#post956286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>\u00c6sir: Wyrd</b><br /> <i>The destinies spun by the Nornir can be changed through drawing runes or magical weaving.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! Weaving and drawing runes? Fuck, I'll probably be MUCH more eager to use that than the old Jotunblut Purview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T20:31:16-07:00","id":956745,"title":"","content":"You know what? I'm in the mood for basic questions. <br /> <br /> Character Creation. How many dots do you start with for Attributes and Skills? Edges? Specialties? How many skills are there in total? <br /> <br /> Stunts. I know they're tied to extra successes, but are they standardized? If I want to hit someone with a &quot;You Are Tied Up&quot; Complication, do I need fewer dice than if I hit someone with &quot;You Are Covered In White Phosphorous&quot; Complication? Can I divide extra successes to cause different Complications and Enhancements?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T23:01:18-07:00","id":956801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=956472#post956472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh! Weaving and drawing runes? Fuck, I'll probably be MUCH more eager to use that than the old Jotunblut Purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026though I expect that Odin's sacrifice for knowledge still factors in somehow. He's not one-eyed because of an <i>accident</i>, you know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T00:11:58-07:00","id":956827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=956801#post956801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026though I expect that Odin's sacrifice for knowledge still factors in somehow. He's not one-eyed because of an <i>accident</i>, you know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I've no doubt. I don't know if Odin's missing eye even factored into the 1E Jotunblut.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T01:04:22-07:00","id":956846,"title":"","content":"Very glad to see all that stuff about utterances make its way into proper Kemetic magic. Quick question though: I've always seen it as heka or hekau, never heku. Any reason why?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T02:28:04-07:00","id":956858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=956827#post956827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh I've no doubt. I don't know if Odin's missing eye even factored into the 1E Jotunblut.</div> </div> </div> </div>It didn't. Ragnarok explained Odin sacrificing his eye as basically his equivalent of a Relic for channeling Purviews.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T03:20:14-07:00","id":956869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=956858#post956858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It didn't. Ragnarok explained Odin sacrificing his eye as basically his equivalent of a Relic for channeling Purviews.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I read the book. Which is why I was surprised that Dataweaver brought it up.<br /> <br /> Me: Wow, this new Purview looks better than Jotunblut!<br /> <br /> Data: Yeah, bet Odin still lost his eye.<br /> <br /> Me: ... I believe so, don't think that has much to do with Jotunblut...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T04:30:01-07:00","id":956881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MadxHatter0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=956369#post956369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, I was wondering if you could say why the Orisha got Possession? Cause, getting ridden is a thing, but you see that more in vodoun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possession is important in Yor\u00f9b\u00e1 religion as well, especially in diaspora. I can recommend some sources if you're interested in reading more about it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MadxHatter0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=956369#post956369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> While, if you asked me, one of the major forms of &quot;magic&quot; involving the Orisha and Yoruba culture at large is the concept of ashe, and I was wondering if you could talk about about why you went for possession instead of something like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u00c0\u1e63\u1eb9 is so universal a force that Vance and I would have a difficult time boiling it down to two Boons and an innate power that represent the concept as a whole. Still, if you have ideas about how to accomplish such a thing, I'm interested!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":8310,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","user":"Lula","date":". 08-24-2016, 07:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T06:54:23-07:00","id":956922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Theoi: Metamorphosis*</b><br /> <i>The most high may grant their favor to those who beseech them.</i><br /> <br /> *This Purview's motif doesn't have a ton to do with the Boons it's got.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does this motif work if Zeus is the one using it? I can see how the other Theoi might be able to do so, but I can't think of a God that Zeus would consider higher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T07:07:53-07:00","id":956929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=956922#post956922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How does this motif work if Zeus is the one using it? I can see how the other Theoi might be able to do so, but I can't think of a God that Zeus would consider higher.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dodekatheon (as opposed to the rest of the Theoi), while Incarnate, sort of eyerollingly mutter and ask themselves for aid or otherwise acknowledge that they're helping themselves. They can also make a straightforward appeal to the Goddess Arete or Virtus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 08-24-2016, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T07:18:39-07:00","id":956944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=956929#post956929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Dodekatheon (as opposed to the rest of the Theoi), while Incarnate, sort of eyerollingly mutter and ask themselves for aid or otherwise acknowledge that they're helping themselves. They can also make a straightforward appeal to the Goddess Arete or Virtus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, okay. Less &quot;Are you there God? It's me, Zeus&quot; and more &quot;Tremble before me mortals, for I am Zeus, King of the Gods, (etc.)&quot;. I can get behind that. The idea that He might call upon himself for aid hadn't even occurred to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T07:19:01-07:00","id":956945,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I wouldn't want to like, be dismissive of possession, it's just I see it more in talks of Umbanda and Vodoun then native Yoruba traditions where it still happens but it's much more limited to those specifically initiated as opposed to Umbanda where anyone can become possessed, and Vodoun which kind of lies between the two. It's still totally culturally appropriate, so uhh, not trying to be a downer or something <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> As for Ase, and making it as a concept, well I guess to come up with one would largely depend on what separates an Innate power from a Boon. Cause with ashe it's in many ways absolute but limited. In that, since it's in many ways the &quot;ability to make things happen&quot; in combination with &quot;command and authority&quot;. Yet, to make use of certain ashe you have to be initiated. Yet, it's also transferrable to some extent. One interesting boon could maybe be the ability to transfer your ashe to someone. Which mechanically could look like, you taking some sort of object and spending Legend(or whatever you do to activate a Knack or Boon or what have you) and then make your roll. The result becomes how much ashe you placed into it, and then you could give that to someone, and they could unleash that singular use of it. While another Boon could maybe be like, the ability to take the ashe from another thing, and by doing so you can assume one trait from it or at an equal expenditure of Legend a certain amount of dice that thing has. Or you could find a way to send out your ashe to possess someone.<br /> <br /> While, for an Innate power, I don't know, I'd have to think longer on that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2042-madxhatter0","name":"MadxHatter0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T07:22:07-07:00","id":956947,"title":"","content":"Neall, for a few of those, like the Orisha and Dodekathon PSP stuff, what does it mean that the motif doesn't have a lot to do with the Boons it gets?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2042-madxhatter0","name":"MadxHatter0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T07:34:06-07:00","id":956956,"title":"","content":"So PSPs are still one Boon per legend level then","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":461,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","user":"KingCarnival","date":". 08-24-2016, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T07:48:12-07:00","id":956965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MadxHatter0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=956947#post956947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neall, for a few of those, like the Orisha and Dodekathon PSP stuff, what does it mean that the motif doesn't have a lot to do with the Boons it gets?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Orisha motif involves rootwork, but their Boons revolve around spirtual possession (though I suppose, in theory, it's all related to a concept of invoking towards a spiritual balance. Mendez is the expert, though). The Theoi PSP involves invocation of a deity or self for aid, but their Boons are about shapeshifting into clouds or turning people into pigs because they're being sexist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T07:59:20-07:00","id":956968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=956956#post956956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So PSPs are still one Boon per legend level then</div> </div> </div> </div>Every Purview has three sample Boons; every PSP has two sample Boons. They're not the only possible Boons, though. As of playtest, you only get a limited number of Boons at your level of Legend, 5 Boons total at Legend 4 (so they can max out one Purview and their PSP, or potentially have 5 different Purviews. Better have relics for all those Purviews.)<br /> <br /> PSPs and relics give <i>motifs</i>, or methods of using the power of Purviews.<br /> <br /> A Scion may channel one Purview of their divine parent without need of a relic. Someone mentioned that Eric Donner is often fixing up his car with Forge while he uses Giantsbane to channel Sky, and I think that's a good example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T09:28:59-07:00","id":957013,"title":"","content":"I think I've read 'you better have a relic to channel that' like four times now. How hard is it to gain a relic after say character creation? Can you forge one of your own before you achieve Godhood? Is it some insanely difficult process for the smith gods or can they churn them out like Hephaestus used to do for all the gods and the heroes with his team of Cyclops working in Mount Aetna?<br /> <br /> What kind of time frame are we looking at if you suddenly discover you\u2019ve been invited to a wedding between a child of Amaterasu and a child Nike and want to make a good impression?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T10:17:18-07:00","id":957032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957013#post957013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I've read 'you better have a relic to channel that' like four times now. How hard is it to gain a relic after say character creation? Can you forge one of your own before you achieve Godhood? Is it some insanely difficult process for the smith gods or can they churn them out like Hephaestus used to do for all the gods and the heroes with his team of Cyclops working in Mount Aetna?</div> </div> </div> </div>Haephestus has like all of his Boons tied up into Forge and all of his Knacks in Creator. Churning out relics is what the man <i>does</i>.<br /> <br /> For other gods, even Creators or Forgers, it's more difficult and time consuming process. It's not insanely difficult to get a relic after character creation, but it's not an easy or inexpensive process either. The more relics you have, or the more eggs are in one relic basket, the more vulnerable you become. Also, to be able to channel a Purview with marvels, you have to buy at least one Boon in it - and you only get a limited number of those at any one time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What kind of time frame are we looking at if you suddenly discover you\u2019ve been invited to a wedding between a child of Amaterasu and a child Nike and want to make a good impression? </div> </div> </div>You're probably better off giving cash, but questing to find a suitable relic is a good option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T10:28:14-07:00","id":957037,"title":"","content":"So to use any Purview as a Hero you need to <br /> 1- Choose it as the Purview you can channel for free. <br /> OR<br /> 2- Possess an appropriate Relic so you can channel that Purview as a motif<br /> OR <br /> 3- Know one Boon from that Purview so you can channel it as a marvel. <br /> <br /> Is that correct? Or am I misunderstanding what motifs and marvels are?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T10:40:42-07:00","id":957040,"title":"","content":"As someone getting into Scion with 2e, could someone briefly explain what Purviews, Boons, and Knacks are?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T10:51:26-07:00","id":957041,"title":"","content":"From the Storypath preview:<br /> <br /> Purviews and Boons: Discrete elemental miracles tied into the powers of the World, granting Scions influence over their powers of their parents: fire, the sea, the forge, thunder and the sky, and many others.<br /> <br /> Knacks: An upgrade to the Skill Tricks of Mortals, these allow Scions truly superhuman action hero moves or suave dramatic powers that defy belief.<br /> <br /> And from the Scion Alpha slice:<br /> <br /> Fire Purview<br /> The Purview of Fire is held by gods who wield mastery over flame, magma, or forge, from Hephaestus to Agni to Pele. It holds sway both over literal flames, which hold power to destroy and create and the metaphorical flames that may burn in the mortal heart, from the fires of sultry passion to the illumination of enlightenment.<br /> Marvels: Marvels of Fire often cause fortuitous events to happen as a result of a chance fire or a false fire alarm, or through the coincidental action of mortals who are strongly associated with fire, such as smokers, firefighters, or arsonists. Destinies woven from flame may alternatively manifest because of a sudden outburst of inspiration from a mortal.<br /> <br /> Heaven\u2019s Fire (Boon)<br /> The Scion calls divine fire up from the depths of her soul, her ichor running hot with the fury of her Purview.<br /> Cost: Imbue 1 Legend<br /> Action: Simple<br /> The Scion sends a blast of flame into the World, whether it emanates from her eyes or simply blazes a fiery path through whatever she snaps her fingers at. Dexterity + Athletics as an attack. Her fireblasts have Enhancement 3, clash/near/far range, and the Autofire, Deadly, Piercing, and Ranged tags.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T11:18:30-07:00","id":957059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957037#post957037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So to use any Purview as a Hero you need to<br /> 1- Choose it as the Purview you can channel for free.<br /> OR<br /> 2- Possess an appropriate Relic so you can channel that Purview as a motif<br /> OR<br /> 3- Know one Boon from that Purview so you can channel it as a marvel.<br /> <br /> Is that correct? Or am I misunderstanding what motifs and marvels are?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're misunderstanding a little.<br /> <br /> A marvel is a free-form use of a Purview. It can be used for a lot of effects, including replicating a Boon you don't know with drastically reduced efficiency and greater cost <i>and </i>the marvel's use most conform to a motif - you can't wave your arms and use Fire to set off every fire alarm in the skyscraper, you have to wave your arms and invoke Hestia's anger at fire burning outside a proper hearth, or wave your arms to toss a herbal potion of smoke and fear into the control room, or wave your arms while reciting a satirical poem about the responsiveness of the city's fire department and daring them to respond. If you can channel the Purview, you can use a marvel. But to channel a Purview:<br /> 1) It must be one of your parent's Purviews, chosen at character creation.<br /> or<br /> 2) You must possess an appropriate relic or Guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 08-24-2016, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T11:37:38-07:00","id":957075,"title":"","content":"Seems complicated to use Marvels... but interesting.<br /> <br /> Oh channeling a Purview became more restrictive. Hope Purviews would be distributed more or less equally.. or is it balanced?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T11:53:10-07:00","id":957083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=956968#post956968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Every Purview has three sample Boons; every PSP has two sample Boons. They're not the only possible Boons, though. As of playtest, you only get a limited number of Boons at your level of Legend, 5 Boons total at Legend 4 (so they can max out one Purview and their PSP, or potentially have 5 different Purviews. Better have relics for all those Purviews.)<br /> <br /> PSPs and relics give <i>motifs</i>, or methods of using the power of Purviews.<br /> <br /> A Scion may channel one Purview of their divine parent without need of a relic. Someone mentioned that Eric Donner is often fixing up his car with Forge while he uses Giantsbane to channel Sky, and I think that's a good example.</div> </div> </div> </div>In true mythic fashion, the great god Donner would be the lord of thunder, protection from evil... and vintage muscle cars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T12:38:02-07:00","id":957110,"title":"","content":"Forgive me if this is blatantly obvious, but is the upcoming Kickstarter just for Origins and Hero or the entire Scion 2e line?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T12:53:34-07:00","id":957126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957110#post957110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive me if this is blatantly obvious, but is the upcoming Kickstarter just for Origins and Hero or the entire Scion 2e line?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just the first two books, though if it explodes it'll probably fund a few more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T12:59:36-07:00","id":957135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957126#post957126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just the first two books, though if it explodes it'll probably fund a few more.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Demigod and Hero don't depend on this Kickstarter in order to exist?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T13:05:43-07:00","id":957140,"title":"","content":"No, they do. But Onyx Path has yet to do a Kickstarter that doesn't exceed the minimum \u2013 frequently within the first day, and sometimes within the first few hours. If Scion breaks that pattern and fails to achieve funding (not gonna happen), Rich would almost certainly take it as a sign that Scion doesn't have the legs he thought it had, and the whole thing would be called into question. But again, the truth of the matter is that it's never yet been a question of <i>if</i> the project will be funded; only <i>when</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T13:40:26-07:00","id":957164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957140#post957140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they do. But Onyx Path has yet to do a Kickstarter that doesn't exceed the minimum \u2013 frequently within the first day, and sometimes within the first few hours. If Scion breaks that pattern and fails to achieve funding (not gonna happen), Rich would almost certainly take it as a sign that Scion doesn't have the legs he thought it had, and the whole thing would be called into question. But again, the truth of the matter is that it's never yet been a question of <i>if</i> the project will be funded; only <i>when</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm, I dunno. Assuming it's along the lines of most Onyx Path Kickstarters, which have been for special editions, if the KS failed I think we'd see the four corebooks out, completing the set, but expanding the line would probably get some rethinking. If it's closer to Pugmire, which was for a complete edition of the book, then your point holds.<br /> <br /> There was one KS that was iffy on whether it'd be funded, V20's Children of the Revolution Deluxe Edition, which only funded on the penultimate day, but it's an outlier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T13:40:32-07:00","id":957165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=956968#post956968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Every Purview has three sample Boons; every PSP has two sample Boons. They're not the only possible Boons, though. As of playtest, you only get a limited number of Boons at your level of Legend, 5 Boons total at Legend 4 (so they can max out one Purview and their PSP, or potentially have 5 different Purviews. Better have relics for all those Purviews.)</div> </div> </div> </div>if a scion uses the same relic through all his Legend,does the relic achieves godhood with the scion becoming a divine relic?<br /> so a legend 4 scion could possess all the boons from his PSP and one of his Parents or patrons purviews?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T13:42:19-07:00","id":957166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=956968#post956968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Every Purview has three sample Boons; every PSP has two sample Boons. They're not the only possible Boons, though. As of playtest, you only get a limited number of Boons at your level of Legend, 5 Boons total at Legend 4 (so they can max out one Purview and their PSP, or potentially have 5 different Purviews. Better have relics for all those Purviews.)<br /> <br /> PSPs and relics give <i>motifs</i>, or methods of using the power of Purviews.<br /> <br /> A Scion may channel one Purview of their divine parent without need of a relic. Someone mentioned that Eric Donner is often fixing up his car with Forge while he uses Giantsbane to channel Sky, and I think that's a good example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure I'm 100% getting it so asking:<br /> <br /> 1.) So does that mean you can gain UP TO 5 boons at legend 4 or automatically gain a total of 5 boons at legend 4? Thus if you want more powers you need either relics or use marvels of your existing boons in order to do diffent things than those 5 boons normally allow?<br /> <br /> 2.) How high does legend go this incarnation (aka 2nd edition) max.? And what is the highest for origin tier and hero tier?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T14:02:31-07:00","id":957176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957166#post957166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure I'm 100% getting it so asking:<br /> <br /> 1.) So does that mean you can gain UP TO 5 boons at legend 4 or automatically gain a total of 5 boons at legend 4? Thus if you want more powers you need either relics or use marvels of your existing boons in order to do diffent things than those 5 boons normally allow?</div> </div> </div> </div>As of playtest, the latter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2.) How high does legend go this incarnation (aka 2nd edition) max.? And what is the highest for origin tier and hero tier? </div> </div> </div>Legend 4 for Hero, Legend 12 for God, same as 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T19:33:49-07:00","id":957336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=953777#post953777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What it specifically requires is a Path that indicates you're a satyr, which gives access to a suite of Satyr-only powers. You buy them like you would Knacks, and there's an upgrade tree with more Knacks in Hero. It's incredibly easy to play a Scion satyr. If you really wanted to, you could play <i>just </i>a satyr, though you'd top out at Hero-level.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry to go back a few pages, but I'm quite curious about this subject. Are there other mythological creatures that are 'well supported' to be made scions as player characters, in the new edition? And on the same subject, if one wanted to have a character that bridged between two cultures (like say, a Scion of the Aesir who is also a satyr) would that be possible? Can a mythological creature like that be made a scion without being the actual child of a god? I've seen that type of scion referred to a few times, but it seems to be unclear what might qualify someone to be made a scion if neither of their parents are gods.<br /> <br /> As an unrelated question, can you tell me anything about what the Tuatha will look like in 2E? I'm wondering if it will be possible to play a scion (maybe an incarnate) of CuChulainn.<br /> <br /> Thanks Neall!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12289-badgerconda","name":"Badgerconda","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12289_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T23:23:25-07:00","id":957430,"title":"","content":"Once they exist, will it be possible to play an Incarnate character at Hero lever?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T02:28:30-07:00","id":957483,"title":"","content":"You mentioned that Hephaestus has all of his Boons tied up in Forge, and all his Knacks in Creator. Does that mean that characters have a maximum limit on Knacks as well? I'm assuming that Hephaestus being associated with Fire indicates that he actually has a single Boon in Fire and uses marvels for most effects. What about Gods that are associated with many Purviews? Are even the greatest of Gods either jacks-of-all-trades or masters of one? How would such things affect character advancement?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T05:25:06-07:00","id":957539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=955893#post955893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, she did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome!<br /> <br /> Also, just want to thank you for all your recent responses. This thread has been getting very active which is making the wait for the kickstarter that much easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T06:57:50-07:00","id":957582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957483#post957483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mentioned that Hephaestus has all of his Boons tied up in Forge, and all his Knacks in Creator. Does that mean that characters have a maximum limit on Knacks as well? I'm assuming that Hephaestus being associated with Fire indicates that he actually has a single Boon in Fire and uses marvels for most effects. What about Gods that are associated with many Purviews? Are even the greatest of Gods either jacks-of-all-trades or masters of one? How would such things affect character advancement?</div> </div> </div> </div>Right now, Heroes have an upper limit on Boons and Knacks, but are able to slowly shift their Knack suites around after sessions end. So they're ever-changing and growing, but sometimes it's a lateral growth. If there's significant issues with the playtest, or if I figure out a better way to create a plateau in play (so you can keep being Heroes forever if you want), I'll incorporate it. The hybrid advancement rules are something new that I haven't seen done a lot before in RPGs, so we're doing a lot of fiddling to get them right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T07:03:54-07:00","id":957588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957539#post957539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread has been getting very active which is making the wait for the kickstarter that much easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell your friends, tell your family, tell the RPG groups on Facebook!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T07:04:36-07:00","id":957591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957430#post957430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once they exist, will it be possible to play an Incarnate character at Hero lever?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you will be able to do so. I just want to have Gods hammered out before we enable play for their splinters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T07:04:36-07:00","id":957592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are there other mythological creatures that are 'well supported' to be made scions as player characters, in the new edition? </div> </div> </div>Potentially! There's also the possibility of being a Scion and dipping into &quot;minor&quot; powers, like berserkers or valkyries.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And on the same subject, if one wanted to have a character that bridged between two cultures (like say, a Scion of the Aesir who is also a satyr) would that be possible? Can a mythological creature like that be made a scion without being the actual child of a god? I've seen that type of scion referred to a few times, but it seems to be unclear what might qualify someone to be made a scion if neither of their parents are gods. </div> </div> </div>Nothing in the rules or setting prevents you from doing so. If your character has the requisite supernatural sensitivity and mythological association (note: those are actually really high bars to entry), they can become a Scion. This more-or-less replaces the adoption from the last edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As an unrelated question, can you tell me anything about what the Tuatha will look like in 2E? I'm wondering if it will be possible to play a scion (maybe an incarnate) of CuChulainn. </div> </div> </div>Scion, no. Incarnation...probably!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 08-25-2016, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T08:24:09-07:00","id":957629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957582#post957582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right now, Heroes have an upper limit on Boons and Knacks, but are able to slowly shift their Knack suites around after sessions end. So they're ever-changing and growing, but sometimes it's a lateral growth. If there's significant issues with the playtest, or if I figure out a better way to create a plateau in play (so you can keep being Heroes forever if you want), I'll incorporate it. The hybrid advancement rules are something new that I haven't seen done a lot before in RPGs, so we're doing a lot of fiddling to get them right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keeping a close eye on this, as the ida of staying at Hero seems very cool.<br /> <br /> And thanks for being so involved with all of us here! Not many writers do that, and it means a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T09:25:01-07:00","id":957657,"title":"","content":"How hard it for a god to learn boons from a purview that was never associate with them? or Knancks from a Calling they don't have? Can hercules learn any Sage powers? or Hades learn War boons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T09:25:45-07:00","id":957658,"title":"","content":"So, late to reply, but hearing that the Orisha PSP is a motif of rootwork structured around possession I'm gonna be a bit sad(just really wanted to see Ashe finally done in a game), but I'm not mad. Cause if nothing else, this kind of cultural accuracy is really appreciated, and I&quot;m hype to see the rest of how the game works. Tho Neall, I have to ask, could you reveal what Purviews, Oya has(if you've included Oya)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2042-madxhatter0","name":"MadxHatter0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T09:43:28-07:00","id":957668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MadxHatter0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957658#post957658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, late to reply, but hearing that the Orisha PSP is a motif of rootwork structured around possession I'm gonna be a bit sad(just really wanted to see Ashe finally done in a game), but I'm not mad. Cause if nothing else, this kind of cultural accuracy is really appreciated, and I&quot;m hype to see the rest of how the game works. Tho Neall, I have to ask, could you reveal what Purviews, Oya has(if you've included Oya)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oya is, in fact, the parent of the Orisha sig, Omolara Muhammad.<br /> <br /> \u1eccya Iyansan's Callings are Guardian, Leader, Warrior; her Purviews are Epic Strength, Epic Dexterity, Artistry (Dance), Prosperity, Sky, Water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T09:53:53-07:00","id":957676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957588#post957588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tell your friends, tell your family, tell the RPG groups on Facebook!</div> </div> </div> </div>But not that one guy in accounting. He's a jerk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T09:57:10-07:00","id":957678,"title":"","content":"Neall, I'm happy again, this version of Oya sounds incredibly badass! Legit, as a black gamer I've never felt more loved than now. To see the Orisha done well(even if it's not to my dream list or whatever) is awesome. SO hype! Though I'm honestly caught between whether I should make an Orisha scion or a Netjeru scion first. Decisions!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2042-madxhatter0","name":"MadxHatter0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T10:22:29-07:00","id":957694,"title":"","content":"Would running a single-Pantheon campaign (chronicle?) run into any snarls on a mechanical diversity front, or is that easy enough within the rules?<br /> <br /> And is there any chance we could see the Callings for Sekhmet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 08-25-2016, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T10:48:58-07:00","id":957705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957694#post957694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would running a single-Pantheon campaign (chronicle?) run into any snarls on a mechanical diversity front, or is that easy enough within the rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's easy enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And is there any chance we could see the Callings for Sekhmet? </div> </div> </div>Okay, but this is the last one, folks!<br /> <br /> We made the somewhat controversial decision to merge Bast and Sekhmet, with Bastet being a later mantle/personality. The Egyptian pantheon, not unlike the Greco-Roman pantheon, presents difficulties where you can point to a god early in their religion's timeline and go &quot;these are clearly the same god&quot; but a couple of hundred new cities and a few years and they've <i>never </i>been the same god, how could you think that? Is Ptah actually Sokar or Tetenen, and is he married to Bast or Sehkmet or both?<br /> <br /> Thankfully, a lot of this is politics, and allows us to do interesting things like talk about how these singular beings change over time and use mantles to keep cognitive dissonance to a minimum.<br /> <br /> <b>Callings:</b> Hunter, Sage, Warrior; <b>Purviews:</b> Artistry (Brewing), Beasts (Cats), Epic Dexterity, Epic Strength, Fortune, Moon, Sun, War<br /> <br /> Scions of Sekhmet are also automatically eligible to buy Knacks from the Prophet Path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 08-25-2016, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T10:56:12-07:00","id":957710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957705#post957705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's easy enough.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, but this is the last one, folks!<br /> <br /> We made the somewhat controversial decision to merge Bast and Sekhmet, with Bastet being a later mantle/personality. The Egyptian pantheon, not unlike the Greco-Roman pantheon, presents difficulties where you can point to a god early in their religion's timeline and go &amp;quot;these are clearly the same god&amp;quot; but a couple of hundred new cities and a few years and they've <i>never </i>been the same god, how could you think that? Is Ptah actually Sokar or Tetenen, and is he married to Bast or Sehkmet or both?<br /> <br /> Thankfully, a lot of this is politics, and allows us to do interesting things like talk about how these singular beings change over time and use mantles to keep cognitive dissonance to a minimum.<br /> <br /> <b>Callings:</b> Hunter, Sage, Warrior; <b>Purviews:</b> Artistry (Brewing), Beasts (Cats), Epic Dexterity, Epic Strength, Fortune, Moon, Sun, War<br /> <br /> Scions of Sekhmet are also automatically eligible to buy Knacks from the Prophet Path.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. Some more orthodox folks might moan about that one, but it's easy enough to spin Sekhmet's myth of being soothed with alcohol as one of her domestication from lioness into the housecat Bast. I think it's a good move, and thank you for the spoiler!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T11:00:11-07:00","id":957712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957705#post957705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Purviews:</b> Artistry (Brewing)</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Huh, this booze is good but not quite what I expected.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, it's the good stuff. It just kinda sneaks up on you.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I CAN SEE THROUGH TIME!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T11:00:57-07:00","id":957713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MadxHatter0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957678#post957678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neall, I'm happy again, this version of Oya sounds incredibly badass! Legit, as a black gamer I've never felt more loved than now. To see the Orisha done well(even if it's not to my dream list or whatever) is awesome. SO hype! Though I'm honestly caught between whether I should make an Orisha scion or a Netjeru scion first. Decisions!</div> </div> </div> </div>Happy to do it! Diversity and representation in the art and gameline is a major focus and something we're really striving for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T11:02:39-07:00","id":957715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957710#post957710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh. Some more orthodox folks might moan about that one, but it's easy enough to spin Sekhmet's myth of being soothed with alcohol as one of her domestication from lioness into the housecat Bast. I think it's a good move, and thank you for the spoiler!</div> </div> </div> </div>If they don't like it, it's <i>super easy </i>to make their own version and say it's different. I say that up front: we need to make judgment calls on these sorts of things left and right, and if we spend all day worrying over one God we'll never get the damn book done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T11:11:55-07:00","id":957721,"title":"","content":"Are Purviews still tied to Callings, or did that change during playtesting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T11:16:03-07:00","id":957722,"title":"","content":"Any change we Will get enough material from scion origin, when the Kickstarter begins, so that we can begin playing with second edition characters ? Also how do the sorcerers work there magic ? And are they going to appear in origin ? Also thanks a lot Neall for replying and being so informative, it's hard to wait for the Kickstarter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8286-plotinus","name":"Plotinus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T11:18:26-07:00","id":957725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957721#post957721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Purviews still tied to Callings, or did that change during playtesting?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's changed. You now inherit just straight-up inherent one Purview from your divine parent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T11:19:27-07:00","id":957728,"title":"","content":"Also could you elaborate a litle on sorcery. Is it gonna be flexible like mage ? More spell list like as it was in 1. Edition ? What kind of power Can a sorcerer pool, Will a mixed group of sorcerers and scions be able to fit together on the powerscale, or will the sorcerers be left behind, when the scions reach hero or demigod level in legend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8286-plotinus","name":"Plotinus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T11:21:30-07:00","id":957731,"title":"","content":"Did you decide to have Sekhmet as Hathor as well, or is Hathor her own goddess?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T11:26:58-07:00","id":957733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957725#post957725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's changed. You now inherit just straight-up inherent one Purview from your divine parent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait,so I can't use the Leader calling to use sky Purviews without telics anymore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T11:28:26-07:00","id":957736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957731#post957731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you decide to have Sekhmet as Hathor as well, or is Hathor her own goddess?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hathor got merged with Isis. This whole discussion has caused a new sidebar to appear in the text:<br /> <br /> &quot;Divinity is not a static thing, even outside the world of <b>Scion</b>. Take the Goddess Sekhmet, for example: in the Upper Kingdom, she was the lioness goddess of war, yet there was a parallel deity with many (though not all) of the same attributes, called Bast, in the Lower Kingdom. Many parallel deities were much the same, and merged seamlessly when the Kingdoms unified, but Sekhmet stayed Sekhmet and Bast became Bastet, known more as a protector deity.<br /> <br /> Many gods across many pantheons change, alter, split apart from other gods and merge with others. Accuracy in myth is a shifting line over time, weaving through thousands of years of politics, art, and religion. <b>Scion</b>, however, must consider these beings to be largely singular who change over time. Judgment calls must be made: we posit that Sekhmet/Bastet began wild and untamed, but her love of beer has mellowed her into a fierce protector, a separate mantle known as Bast. If you or your group disagree, or want to use them as twin sister Scions of Ra who went two separate ways later in life, that\u2019s perfectly fine - just create new Callings and assign Purviews<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">.&quot;</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T11:32:31-07:00","id":957739,"title":"","content":"Get a Sky Relic? Tying Purviews to Callings piqued my interest, but saddling people with Purviews they don't want is a pretty obvious problem with it. <br /> <br /> On a side note, I'm liking these hard caps on Boons and Knacks. Most of the time, I like generalists or characters with lots of abilities that support a specific concept, so hard limits help me focus on what's most important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T11:36:50-07:00","id":957741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957736#post957736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hathor got merged with Isis. This whole discussion has caused a new sidebar to appear in the text:<br /> <br /> &quot;Divinity is not a static thing, even outside the world of <b>Scion</b>. Take the Goddess Sekhmet, for example: in the Upper Kingdom, she was the lioness goddess of war, yet there was a parallel deity with many (though not all) of the same attributes, called Bast, in the Lower Kingdom. Many parallel deities were much the same, and merged seamlessly when the Kingdoms unified, but Sekhmet stayed Sekhmet and Bast became Bastet, known more as a protector deity.<br /> <br /> Many gods across many pantheons change, alter, split apart from other gods and merge with others. Accuracy in myth is a shifting line over time, weaving through thousands of years of politics, art, and religion. <b>Scion</b>, however, must consider these beings to be largely singular who change over time. Judgment calls must be made: we posit that Sekhmet/Bastet began wild and untamed, but her love of beer has mellowed her into a fierce protector, a separate mantle known as Bast. If you or your group disagree, or want to use them as twin sister Scions of Ra who went two separate ways later in life, that\u2019s perfectly fine - just create new Callings and assign Purviews<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">.&quot;</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Was ra merged with anyone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T11:39:42-07:00","id":957743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957741#post957741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was ra merged with anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>Historically, damn near everyone. Though I don't think that's what you're looking for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 08-25-2016, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T11:41:40-07:00","id":957744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957743#post957743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Historical, damn near everyone. Though I don't think that's what you're looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Ra's kind of a prime example of this issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T11:48:34-07:00","id":957747,"title":"","content":"Neall, do you intend to write up how one would develop a PSP for the purpose of homebrewing within the books? I ask cause, a part of me wants to try my hand at homebrewing up Ashe for the Orisha, but then I also realized with how many pantheons we won't see for awhile potentially I imagine there are people who'd be interested in having guides on how to go about building one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2042-madxhatter0","name":"MadxHatter0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T11:57:35-07:00","id":957750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957744#post957744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, Ra's kind of a prime example of this issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that mean Sobek's made the cut?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T11:58:05-07:00","id":957751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957705#post957705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's easy enough.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, but this is the last one, folks!<br /> <br /> We made the somewhat controversial decision to merge Bast and Sekhmet, with Bastet being a later mantle/personality. The Egyptian pantheon, not unlike the Greco-Roman pantheon, presents difficulties where you can point to a god early in their religion's timeline and go &quot;these are clearly the same god&quot; but a couple of hundred new cities and a few years and they've <i>never </i>been the same god, how could you think that? Is Ptah actually Sokar or Tetenen, and is he married to Bast or Sehkmet or both?<br /> <br /> Thankfully, a lot of this is politics, and allows us to do interesting things like talk about how these singular beings change over time and use mantles to keep cognitive dissonance to a minimum.<br /> <br /> <b>Callings:</b> Hunter, Sage, Warrior; <b>Purviews:</b> Artistry (Brewing), Beasts (Cats), Epic Dexterity, Epic Strength, Fortune, Moon, Sun, War<br /> <br /> Scions of Sekhmet are also automatically eligible to buy Knacks from the Prophet Path.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm wondering there: Does that mean that all of these purviews are maxed out (like it had to be in 1st edition) or undecided currently? <br /> <br /> -------------------<br /> Another thing too. Some gods like Ares or Hades are often portrayed more on the darker side of things (almost evil). Will there be some sort of morality in the 2nd edition? (in 1st edition it was A BIT with virtues and some ppl houseruled that if you behaved too dark you get dark virtues,...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T11:59:17-07:00","id":957755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957743#post957743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Historically, damn near everyone. Though I don't think that's what you're looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted to know if he was or was not dethroned as Pharaoh of the Netjer","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T12:17:04-07:00","id":957767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MadxHatter0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957747#post957747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neall, do you intend to write up how one would develop a PSP for the purpose of homebrewing within the books? I ask cause, a part of me wants to try my hand at homebrewing up Ashe for the Orisha, but then I also realized with how many pantheons we won't see for awhile potentially I imagine there are people who'd be interested in having guides on how to go about building one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm probably going to rescue the Atlantean Pantheon from 1e as a blog post to show folks how you'd go about making your own pantheons and PSPs, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T12:18:41-07:00","id":957768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957750#post957750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does that mean Sobek's made the cut?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think I'd leave out the one god who loves kids out of Scion? No way. Sobek is the best parent in the pantheon, hands-down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T12:18:55-07:00","id":957769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957767#post957767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm probably going to rescue the Atlantean Pantheon from 1e as a blog post to show folks how you'd go about making your own pantheons and PSPs, yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>Titan: Black Manta","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T12:49:47-07:00","id":957783,"title":"","content":"What's the difference between Prosperity and Fortune?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T12:57:21-07:00","id":957786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957783#post957783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the difference between Prosperity and Fortune?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fertility, Fortune, and Prosperity have some conceptual overlap. Fortune is more about conceptual good luck on an individual level, while Prosperity is more about material and cultural wealth on a societal level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T12:59:29-07:00","id":957788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957751#post957751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering there: Does that mean that all of these purviews are maxed out (like it had to be in 1st edition) or undecided currently? <br /> <br /> -------------------<br /> Another thing too. Some gods like Ares or Hades are often portrayed more on the darker side of things (almost evil). Will there be some sort of morality in the 2nd edition? (in 1st edition it was A BIT with virtues and some ppl houseruled that if you behaved too dark you get dark virtues,...).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm hoping they took a less negative view of those two for second edition. Pop culture often seems to demonize them, and it is always irritating to me. I wonder, how would they feel about such things in Scion? I am also curious about the virtues of the Theoi, and how they might influence the characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T14:26:58-07:00","id":957844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957788#post957788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm hoping they took a less negative view of those two for second edition. Pop culture often seems to demonize them, and it is always irritating to me. I wonder, how would they feel about such things in Scion? I am also curious about the virtues of the Theoi, and how they might influence the characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Theoi Virtues revolve around strong emotions, and are Egotism and <i>Storge</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T14:36:40-07:00","id":957848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957844#post957844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Theoi Virtues revolve around strong emotions, and are Egotism and <i>Storge</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Storge as in familial love? It fits nicely,those theoi were always a tight-knit family,some of them had <i>really close </i>bondS with their sisters","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T14:54:01-07:00","id":957858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957844#post957844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Theoi Virtues revolve around strong emotions, and are Egotism and <i>Storge</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a newbie here; what are Virtues?<br /> <br /> More precisely, what are all the pieces of a Pantheon mechanically?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T15:06:21-07:00","id":957864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957858#post957858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For a newbie here; what are Virtues?<br /> <br /> More precisely, what are all the pieces of a Pantheon mechanically?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are a set of values that are important for each pantheon,acting according with one's virtues can grant you certain dice bonus on occasions. Especially to resist mind control","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T15:07:38-07:00","id":957865,"title":"","content":"Still wondering if sorcerers will be in scion origin, as mentioned way back on the threads ? And about magic. How flexible will it be compared to 1. Edition scion. More sphere/arcanum like or just spells or even more exiting, a complete third option? Can't find any place it has been mentioned before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8286-plotinus","name":"Plotinus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T15:08:40-07:00","id":957866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957858#post957858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a newbie here; what are Virtues?</div> </div> </div> </div>1e Virtues worked like they did in 2e Exalted - they were 4 arrangements (from a list of 16) objective values that a pantheon believed in. Courage, Piety, that sort of thing. The problem was that they failed to encompass a lot of what the pantheons actually valued and bringing them up in play was difficult.<br /> <br /> 2e Virtues effectively describe a warring (if false) dichotomy in the pantheon, what two issues repeatedly bring it into conflict. For the Norse, it's <i>Fatalism </i>(our lives are woven by the Norns, and we are fated to our end) and <i>Audacity </i>(Fate can go fuck itself! <i>Drengskapr</i> ahoy!). For the Devas, it's <i>Conscience</i> and <i>Duty</i>, or two warring interpretations on &quot;what is right&quot; of individual judgment and proper action. The Tuatha, <i>Honor </i>and <i>Prowess</i>; the Manitou, <i>Pride </i>and <i>Purpose</i>. <br /> <br /> You may notice that the Virtues don't always conflict in a lot of situations, and that's intentional. A tuning fork has two tines, but they're part of the same fork, and they point in the same direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T15:10:35-07:00","id":957868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957866#post957866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1e Virtues worked like they did in 2e Exalted - they were 4 arrangements (from a list of 16) objective values that a pantheon believed in. Courage, Piety, that sort of thing. The problem was that they failed to encompass a lot of what the pantheons actually valued and bringing them up in play was difficult.<br /> <br /> 2e Virtues effectively describe a warring (if false) dichotomy in the pantheon, what two issues repeatedly bring it into conflict. For the Norse, it's <i>Fatalism </i>(our lives are woven by the Norns, and we are fated to our end) and <i>Audacity </i>(Fate can go fuck itself! <i>Drengskapr</i> ahoy!). For the Devas, it's <i>Conscience</i> and <i>Duty</i>, or two warring interpretations on &quot;what is right&quot; of individual judgment and proper action. The Tuatha, <i>Honor </i>and <i>Prowess</i>; the Manitou, <i>Pride </i>and <i>Purpose</i>.<br /> <br /> You may notice that the Virtues don't always conflict in a lot of situations, and that's intentional. A tuning fork has two tines, but they're part of the same fork, and they point in the same direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does acting according to a virtue helps you gain positive Fatebindings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T15:11:11-07:00","id":957869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Plotinus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957865#post957865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still wondering if sorcerers will be in scion origin, as mentioned way back on the threads ? And about magic. How flexible will it be compared to 1. Edition scion. More sphere/arcanum like or just spells or even more exiting, a complete third option? Can't find any place it has been mentioned before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcerer Paths are mentioned, and will interact with full sorcery rules in a later book. For now, they pick a PSP motif and stick to it, depending on their culture. Sorcerers themselves must siphon Legend or some other source of power to fuel their deeds (and indeed, some Gods are patrons of sorcerers, like Hermes and Thoth).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T15:13:08-07:00","id":957870,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Hermes has any kind of sorcery group worshipping him,like a cabal,or a circle maybe even a <i>order</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T15:23:23-07:00","id":957879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957866#post957866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tuatha, <i>Honor </i>and <i>Prowess</i></div> </div> </div> </div>That is just so perfect. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T17:48:40-07:00","id":957954,"title":"","content":"I would argue that the core dichotomy of the Netjer would be Order/Chaos, except none of the deities have anything to do with Chaos other than Set/Sutek (and even he bows to Maat when push comes to shove) Apep, and various demons. Anyone else have any thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T18:15:21-07:00","id":957964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957954#post957954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue that the core dichotomy of the Netjer would be Order/Chaos, except none of the deities have anything to do with Chaos other than Set/Sutek (and even he bows to Maat when push comes to shove) Apep, and various demons. Anyone else have any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot Pantheons have an Order / Chaos breakdown like the Netjer. The Theoi have the Rule of Zeus v. the Rule of Cronus, along with their City v. Rurality split both centered on Order-Chaos themes respectively. The Shen are very concerned with the will of Tian and the results of periods of confusion. The Bogovi bound themselves with Law and Legality and then struggle to live up to their own ideals. The Teotl put every last drop of their power and energy into fueling the Fifth World and protecting it from the beings who wish to destroy it.<br /> <br /> However, it looks like from the examples Neall's given here, they're examining things in more detail. Additionally, in the five examples given here by Neall, the two Virtues are not a Good v. Bad thing (though, I know very little about the Algonquin, so I can't speak for the Manitou example given) but a complicated balance of two highly valued, but sometimes contradictory socital values. Since I know the Irish the best, I can give a breakdown.<br /> <br /> Honor is key, your honor, be you warrior, bard, man, woman, king, or pig farmer, <i>is</i> you, more than you are you. Your honor is what everyone will know, even if they don't know you. Misdeeds stain you, and great acts elevate you. Prowess ties deeply into this, everyone must be great. If you read Irish mythology, you will lose track of how many, &quot;Most skilled warriors,&quot; or &quot;most beautiful men or women of Ireland&quot; you read about. Being good isn't important, anyone can be good, you must be <i>the best</i>. This will tie in to your honor, these two things deeply entwined.<br /> <br /> But, they can at times clash, with dangerous results. The story of Bricriu's Feast is a great example of this. The Heroes of Ulster are all at a feast (along with the rest of Ulster) and the Hero's Portion is great indeed. Whomsoever gains this Hero's Portion will surely gain all others for it is the greatest (Prowess again, for the host, which converts to honor) ever to be seen. So, three of the Heroes of Ulster claim it. Crowd favorite, Cu Chulainn, along with Conall Cernach, and Loegaire Buadach. The portion ought to go to the greatest of them (Prowess) so whoever doesn't get it will be recognized as lesser than the winner (Honor) which results in the three Heroes falling to outright battle during the feast attempting to kill each other. During this same story, these three Hero's wives face a similar struggle, as whomsoever enters the feasting hall first will surely be the first to enter all others and lead the women of Ulster for it is the grandest hall to be seen. So, they turn upon each other.<br /> <br /> The conflict is only resolved (the Hero's conflict, Cu Chulain's wife Emer wins her contest pretty handily IIRC) after a long series of trials, running into Mabd, Anilil, The Dagda, with the heroes always arguing that the previous test proved nothing. Only when a stranger arrives daring the three to chop off his head and allow him to do the same the next day, Cu Chulain is shown to be the bravest <i>and</i> the strongest, being awarded the portion. (You will note that this is <i>very</i> Gawain and the Green Knight-y. This is probably a proto-version)<br /> <br /> So, I'd guess less Order and Chaos, and more... not sure, I don't know the Netjer well enough. But, I don't know if Chaos would be one of theirs. It doesn't seem to be a good v. bad, but a matter of internal cultural value conflict.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T18:22:59-07:00","id":957966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957954#post957954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue that the core dichotomy of the Netjer would be Order/Chaos, except none of the deities have anything to do with Chaos other than Set/Sutek (and even he bows to Maat when push comes to shove) Apep, and various demons. Anyone else have any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div> I go with Prosperity and Resignation. Prosperity because they all strive to live a good life in their own way,immortal or not. and Resignation because they understand than sooner or later we have to die and go to the underworld","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T18:31:36-07:00","id":957972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957966#post957966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I go with Prosperity and Resignation. Prosperity because they all strive to live a good life in their own way,immortal or not. and Resignation because they understand than sooner or later we have to die and go to the underworld</div> </div> </div> </div>Resignation isn't a huge thing to the Netjer like it would be to the Aesir; there's very little concept of being &quot;fated&quot; to do anything other than your purpose in life as defined by Maat. You could do something with that, focused on the importance of a given role contributing to the greater whole (of Egypt, of civilization, of the universe) versus individualism and freedom. There's a big emphasis on Duty in Egyptian myth as well, so maybe something with that?<br /> <br /> Also: does anyone know if the Kickstarter is supposed to have some or all of the rules up for preview, like other OPP Kickstarters have done?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T18:32:55-07:00","id":957973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957592#post957592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Potentially! There's also the possibility of being a Scion and dipping into &quot;minor&quot; powers, like berserkers or valkyries.<br /> <br /> Nothing in the rules or setting prevents you from doing so. If your character has the requisite supernatural sensitivity and mythological association (note: those are actually really high bars to entry), they can become a Scion. This more-or-less replaces the adoption from the last edition.<br /> <br /> Scion, no. Incarnation...probably!</div> </div> </div> </div>These are all incredibly exciting to me personally...! Can you tell us any more about the 'high bars to entry'? would it be enough to say, be Sidhe (full or part) for one of the Tuatha to make you their Scion? Or an Alfar for the Norse, etc?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12289-badgerconda","name":"Badgerconda","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12289_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T18:47:02-07:00","id":957980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957972#post957972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Resignation isn't a huge thing to the Netjer like it would be to the Aesir; there's very little concept of being &quot;fated&quot; to do anything other than your purpose in life as defined by Maat. You could do something with that, focused on the importance of a given role contributing to the greater whole (of Egypt, of civilization, of the universe) versus individualism and freedom. There's a big emphasis on Duty in Egyptian myth as well, so maybe something with that?<br /> <br /> Also: does anyone know if the Kickstarter is supposed to have some or all of the rules up for preview, like other OPP Kickstarters have done?</div> </div> </div> </div>The kickstarter its supposed to have part of the rules <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. and yes,Duty makes more sense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T20:37:40-07:00","id":958032,"title":"","content":"I'd agree on Duty being important. Also, yeah, chaos/order divide wouldn't work well. Since Ma'at isn't necessarily order so much as it's about the continuation of existence. It's everyone acting in a positive way towards their family, their community, their nation. It's very much the idea of, &quot;if you do your duty, you are upholding Ma'at&quot;. Which means in some ways you can still be a dick, you just have to be a dick who gets the job done(like Sutekh who may be a dick but every night he's fighting Ap*p on the solar barge). While Isfet, is kind of more about the dissolution of everything. It's not really chaos in the sense of change, upheaval, etc. Isfet is like out and out destruction, the dissolution of life, of the universe, of everything. A black hole is a good way of seeing Isfet, it just swallows and swallows consuming and destroying everything until there's nothing left.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2042-madxhatter0","name":"MadxHatter0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T20:38:47-07:00","id":958033,"title":"","content":"Though this leaves me with another thought. Neall, what kind of stuff should one expect if they say, go into space? Do we begin dealing with how different Pantheons perceive &quot;space&quot; and thus entering into similar but different realms? In regards to the answer of this, how would it effect things like the Space Race and stuff?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2042-madxhatter0","name":"MadxHatter0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T20:56:45-07:00","id":958038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MadxHatter0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=958033#post958033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though this leaves me with another thought. Neall, what kind of stuff should one expect if they say, go into space? Do we begin dealing with how different Pantheons perceive &amp;quot;space&amp;quot; and thus entering into similar but different realms? In regards to the answer of this, how would it effect things like the Space Race and stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think the United States named its program after Apollo? Why do you think Gagarin made a point of seeing no God(s) up there?<br /> <br /> I feel like I could to in a whole Unknown Armies rant about the Space Race as a proxy war between theism and atheism, and may in fact go do so elsewhere...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T02:42:02-07:00","id":958122,"title":"","content":"Lots of things have been said here and I'm sure we are all happy about all those great revelations (I am <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> Maybe we could transfer all information to the wiki page &quot;Scion 2E what we know&quot; what do you think? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T03:05:36-07:00","id":958129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=958122#post958122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lots of things have been said here and I'm sure we are all happy about all those great revelations (I am <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> Maybe we could transfer all information to the wiki page &amp;quot;Scion 2E what we know&amp;quot; what do you think? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>For reference: <a href=\"https://www.ttrarchive.com/store/index.php?title=Scion_2E:_What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.ttrarchive.com/store/ind...:_What_We_Know</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T03:40:39-07:00","id":958133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=958122#post958122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lots of things have been said here and I'm sure we are all happy about all those great revelations (I am <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> Maybe we could transfer all information to the wiki page &quot;Scion 2E what we know&quot; what do you think? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Everything to date from the thread should be up there; I try to stay as up-to-date as possible.<br /> <br /> If there's something I've missed, lemme know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T06:57:50-07:00","id":958203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957582#post957582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right now, Heroes have an upper limit on Boons and Knacks, but are able to slowly shift their Knack suites around after sessions end. So they're ever-changing and growing, but sometimes it's a lateral growth. If there's significant issues with the playtest, or if I figure out a better way to create a plateau in play (so you can keep being Heroes forever if you want), I'll incorporate it. The hybrid advancement rules are something new that I haven't seen done a lot before in RPGs, so we're doing a lot of fiddling to get them right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are the higher tiers limited in the same way? For example, would Zeus and Odin each only have 13 Boons spread throughout a handful of Purviews, or would such potent Gods have some other tricks that would make them a bit more daunting a target for a powerful player character at Legend 12 to challenge? I am definitely looking forward to seeing how the character advancement system works, but I'll admit that the hard limit on powers is something I am a bit concerned about. Is there some advantage to having many Boons in a few Purviews as opposed to a single Boon in several different ones? If a character shifts all of their Boons out of a given Purview, do they lose all access to it, even if it was the one that they'd originally favored at character creation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T08:21:41-07:00","id":958236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957964#post957964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, it looks like from the examples Neall's given here, they're examining things in more detail. Additionally, in the five examples given here by Neall, the two Virtues are not a Good v. Bad thing (though, I know very little about the Algonquin, so I can't speak for the Manitou example given) but a complicated balance of two highly valued, but sometimes contradictory socital values.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is precisely the thing we're going for.<br /> <br /> (The current Netjer Virtues are <i>Balance </i>and <i>Justice</i>. Sometimes pursuing Justice means upsetting a delicate balance, while sometimes Balance allows an injustice to occur.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 08-26-2016, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T08:22:19-07:00","id":958237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=958203#post958203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are the higher tiers limited in the same way?</div> </div> </div> </div>Undecided at the moment; we're still playtesting and designing systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T10:18:13-07:00","id":958276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=958237#post958237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Undecided at the moment; we're still playtesting and designing systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the note of this whole limit. I've got 2 questions there (hero tier)<br /> 1.) Are tehre still many ways to grow even supernaturally despite that limit?<br /> 2.) As you mentioned it was felt necessary after playtests, if I may inquire there: What was the cause for the limit? (I guess many first houserules will be to remove that limit and maybe some ppl decide better to leave it be if they know the bad side effects of removing the limit)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T10:23:47-07:00","id":958278,"title":"","content":"The Balance v Justice angle I can definitely see. Like, we see a bit of that play out in the myths and stuff, but on a cultural level not a lot was talked about it(since your average person wasn't full up on all the liturgy and stuff, and the temple priests were often cozy with the government). But like, in a contemporary view it'd be interesting to see that view of Balance v Justice come up as say like, a revolutionary Netjeru scion who asks themselves, &quot;Is an oppressive balance good because it's balance, or should I pursue Justice even if it means instability for an unknown amount of time,&quot; which is the kind of thoughts you want to have for a game. So with all the virtues being like this the story elements begin to write themselves!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2042-madxhatter0","name":"MadxHatter0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T10:26:10-07:00","id":958280,"title":"","content":"I don't remember if someonewhere in thread we got the Orisha virtues?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2042-madxhatter0","name":"MadxHatter0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T10:27:55-07:00","id":958281,"title":"","content":"When it comes to the names of the gods where do you find yourself on naming conventions? Do you try to get as close to the original name as possible, like in the netjeru's case going like, Aset, Heru, Wesir, etc. etc. or do you find you're leaning more towards the common names that people know for them like Isis, Horus, Osiris, etc. etc.?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2042-madxhatter0","name":"MadxHatter0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T10:53:41-07:00","id":958291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=958237#post958237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Undecided at the moment; we're still playtesting and designing systems.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Excellent! That means that there is still a chance for a wider diversity of abilities for more advanced characters. I also second Ryu's questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T10:54:43-07:00","id":958292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MadxHatter0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=958281#post958281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it comes to the names of the gods where do you find yourself on naming conventions? Do you try to get as close to the original name as possible, like in the netjeru's case going like, Aset, Heru, Wesir, etc. etc. or do you find you're leaning more towards the common names that people know for them like Isis, Horus, Osiris, etc. etc.?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe he said we're getting the proper Egyptian names.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T10:59:26-07:00","id":958296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MadxHatter0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=958280#post958280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't remember if someonewhere in thread we got the Orisha virtues?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tradition vs. Innovation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T11:37:22-07:00","id":958313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=958296#post958296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tradition vs. Innovation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now i'm picturing two Scions Orisha arguing. &quot;I don't know Joe,i feel like using a amaranth curse on the enemy side should do the trick.&quot; &quot;But Carl,throwing grenades in them it's just more fun!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T11:59:11-07:00","id":958324,"title":"","content":"I can totally see Tradition vs Innovation. Especially with how that might play out with the Loa later on, or if we ever got a write up on Umbanda. Just cause, those faiths are so much about innovation and change to survive. If nothing else, I'd be interested to see what Tradition necessarily looks like. Cause with a lot of West African religions there's this big focus on family, and tradtiion in that sense(familial roles, duties, etc.) but in this modern age of like so many queer black folks for example and others who are pushed out of their families that traditional mindset could be an interesting virtue to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2042-madxhatter0","name":"MadxHatter0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T12:03:46-07:00","id":958327,"title":"","content":"Hey Neall, question, when it comes to alternative forms of magic within a culture, how would you represent that? Like, using the Aesir for example, you have the use of Runes as their PSP, but what about Seidr? Would that be some sort of alternative PSP, a sorcerous path, like what would you do to represent that considering Odin was known for both Seidr, rune work, etc.?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2042-madxhatter0","name":"MadxHatter0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T12:20:53-07:00","id":958338,"title":"","content":"I think both runes and weaving are part of the Norse motif, actually. But the question stands for a culture with three or more famous motifs (though none come to mind).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T12:23:28-07:00","id":958340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MadxHatter0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=958327#post958327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Neall, question, when it comes to alternative forms of magic within a culture, how would you represent that? Like, using the Aesir for example, you have the use of Runes as their PSP, but what about Seidr? Would that be some sort of alternative PSP, a sorcerous path, like what would you do to represent that considering Odin was known for both Seidr, rune work, etc.?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seidr is part of the Wyrd Purview, in addition to runes and charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T12:30:35-07:00","id":958350,"title":"","content":"Can a Scion accidentally acquire an Omen they didn't want to? if they can,how does that happen,and can they Erase the Omen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T15:12:04-07:00","id":958444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=956286#post956286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <b>Netjer: Heku</b><br /> <i>Speaking the sacred ritual words releases sekhem, lending power to the soul.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Is this version of Sekhem/Heku going to be as powerful as it is for starting mummies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T17:11:39-07:00","id":958496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=958296#post958296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tradition vs. Innovation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like a whole campaign focused on the Scions of one pantheon could be done based entirely on the Virtue dichotomy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T17:29:20-07:00","id":958506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=958444#post958444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this version of Sekhem/Heku going to be as powerful as it is for starting mummies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming you're talking about Mummy: the Curse, I can't imagine so, at least not until you're out of Hero tier and well into Demigod or God.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T17:33:03-07:00","id":958510,"title":"","content":"Have we heard how many deities per Pantheon we can expect?<br /> <br /> And am I misremembering, or are the Theoi going to cover the Etruscans in addition to the Greeks and Romans?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T17:34:00-07:00","id":958514,"title":"","content":"Neall,i notice the teotl purview it's not Nahualism anymore,it's <b>Nextlahualli. </b>Can you show the <b>Nextlahualli </b>boons? i'm afraid i didn't get what this Purview do from the first description","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T21:57:29-07:00","id":958607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MadxHatter0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=958324#post958324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can totally see Tradition vs Innovation. Especially with how that might play out with the Loa later on, or if we ever got a write up on Umbanda. Just cause, those faiths are so much about innovation and change to survive. If nothing else, I'd be interested to see what Tradition necessarily looks like. Cause with a lot of West African religions there's this big focus on family, and tradtiion in that sense(familial roles, duties, etc.) but in this modern age of like so many queer black folks for example and others who are pushed out of their families that traditional mindset could be an interesting virtue to deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly what I'm going for. The combination of tension and continuity between, for example, Candombl\u00e9 and Umbanda is a Tradition vs. Innovation issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T06:44:18-07:00","id":958719,"title":"","content":"I know we are far from that point but is there any new system concerning experience points?<br /> I was wondering if it were possible to spend them while playing... one of my players has health boons but not Antidote (Health 3 from Company I think). Does it make sense if a system allows players to spend experience points into what they need in the heat of the action, in this case, to heal a NPC from a disease, like a sudden skill?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T09:58:01-07:00","id":958781,"title":"","content":"I'm sort of hoping for a real basic xp system. As much as I like beats i think I would enjoy just having a real simple give X amount of xp at the end of a session and for important moments in the story type of thing. Sort of basic but functional Onyx Path that allows u to focus more on all the other tiny details of the game system itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T16:18:47-07:00","id":958942,"title":"","content":"Here's a stupid question; what does PSP stand for? I get the impression that it's the style your magic/miracles need to be couched in, but I'm a little vague on what precisely the term <i>is.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T16:30:05-07:00","id":958946,"title":"","content":"Pantheon Specific Purview, the magics that are unique to the bloodlines of one particular pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11594-namillus","name":"Namillus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T16:31:40-07:00","id":958947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=958942#post958942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a stupid question; what does PSP stand for? I get the impression that it's the style your magic/miracles need to be couched in, but I'm a little vague on what precisely the term <i>is.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>PsP is a term from 1e, it just means Pantheon Specific Purview such as Arete for the Greeks, or Enech for the Irish. It's a power set only accessible to members of a specific Pantheon, compared to APPs which are All Purpose Purviews which anyone can access, such as Fire, War, Sky, ect. There are <i>also</i> the three 'Special' Purviews, Magic, Mystery, and Prophecy, but that's a weird sub-catagory that doesn't really get acknowledged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T16:42:47-07:00","id":958954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=958947#post958947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are <i>also</i> the three 'Special' Purviews, Magic, Mystery, and Prophecy, but that's a weird sub-catagory that doesn't really get acknowledged.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I never liked them, which is part of the reason they're gone in 2e. &quot;Cultural&quot; magic is folded into the PSPs, Mystery is folded into the Sage Knacks, and Prophecy gets split into two Knack trees that mortals can pick up and Gods can zap others with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T16:51:09-07:00","id":958958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=958947#post958947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> PsP is a term from 1e, it just means Pantheon Specific Purview such as Arete for the Greeks, or Enech for the Irish. It's a power set only accessible to members of a specific Pantheon, compared to APPs which are All Purpose Purviews which anyone can access, such as Fire, War, Sky, ect. There are <i>also</i> the three 'Special' Purviews, Magic, Mystery, and Prophecy, but that's a weird sub-catagory that doesn't really get acknowledged.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thank you. So you get one Purview from your Pantheon and the others from your Callings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T19:24:30-07:00","id":959027,"title":"","content":"I have a question.<br /> <br /> I know you choose one Purview from your parent to channel without the use of relics at character creation. How will you gain new Purviews to channel without the use of relics?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1494-deranged-goblin","name":"Deranged Goblin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T22:18:17-07:00","id":959097,"title":"","content":"To be more specific: in 1e each pantheon had its own purview representing something about that culture, with ~10 Boons (powers). The Norse had Jotunblut, which was all about being big and giantish, the Aztecs had Itztli which was all about blood sacrifice, etc. If I understand, they're the same shape and colour in 2e but have only a couple of specific powers and are more about contributing a motif to do magic by.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0