 so small that Thor would pull it seemingly out of nowhere. I imagine that's a very popular feature for relic weapons these days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T16:03:27-07:00","id":960727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=960703#post960703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there options for carrying Relics around and being subtle about it? You can hide a katana under a trenchcoat, but it's a lot harder with a spear, and airport security makes the whole thing much more complicated.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e, the Illusion purview had a Boon, Subtle Knife,\u200b that lets you hide an object on your person, making it either invisible, or simply unobtrusive. You can also give a Relic a one-dot unique power, that lets it transform into something more mundane; a spear become a pen, a piece of armor becomes a piece of jewelry, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T16:29:20-07:00","id":960735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=960726#post960726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Norse legends speak of Thor's hammer, Mjolnir, being able to shrink down so small that Thor would pull it seemingly out of nowhere. I imagine that's a very popular feature for relic weapons these days.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sun Wukong also liked to shrink his staff down so he could stash it away in his ear, from what recall. Long time since I read Journey to the West, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T19:05:38-07:00","id":960797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=960703#post960703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there options for carrying Relics around and being subtle about it? You can hide a katana under a trenchcoat, but it's a lot harder with a spear, and airport security makes the whole thing much more complicated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would hope there's something like how Changeling: the Lost has its relic-style goodies have a Mask of their own. Scion leans more towards pulp and action, so having the cops get called because you had your awesome items on you seems like a waste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T02:14:27-07:00","id":960951,"title":"","content":"Will time travel be possible in Scion 2E? As in, can Scions travel back in time to change the outcome of the Trojan War?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12342-dr-quantum","name":"Dr. Quantum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T00:08:45-07:00","id":961492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957768#post957768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you think I'd leave out the one god who loves kids out of Scion? No way. Sobek is the best parent in the pantheon, hands-down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sir! I do protest! Surely Bes must at least give Sobek a run for his coinage!<br /> <br /> Ahem.<br /> <br /> Questions, questions... Oh! Will there still be Virtue Extremities? I admit, while watching Suicide Squad, I found myself thinking one of the characters was practically perfect for a Scion, or at least a 1e Scion, with a certain event in his backstory providing an excellent example of a Virtue Extremity, along with other elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2286-indarkestknight","name":"indarkestknight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T00:27:56-07:00","id":961498,"title":"","content":"Do we know which Pantheons are planned for later books so we don't spend the entire Hero Kickstarter yelling about the Mesopotamian gods, for example?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T04:59:00-07:00","id":961575,"title":"","content":"Can someone lay out the differences between Purviews, Roles, Callings, Paths, and any other capitalized mechanics used in character creation that all vaguely seem to be the same initially?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T05:20:37-07:00","id":961589,"title":"","content":"Okay, I've got some time, I'll take a crack at it.<br /> <br /> Okay, starting with Paths - Paths are your character's backgrounds and concepts. As of Hero level, you get three -<br /> <br /> Your Origin - How you came to be. When referring to Scions, most likely who their parent is and how they were born. Like, say, Son of the Dagda for example.<br /> <br /> Your Role - How your character came by the skills and abilities they have at the start of the game. So our theoretical child of Dagda may have grown up the clever child of poor working class folk, but he made it in Hollywood through raw talent and some very careful planning. So his Role would be &quot;Cunning Actor.&quot;<br /> <br /> Your Pantheon - How you relate to your pantheon. Our boy - let's call him &quot;Connor McRae&quot; - received a visitation from his father, and now uses his connections and encyclopedic knowledge of popular media to hunt overly dramatic monsters in Los Angeles. Let's go with &quot;Sunset Huntsman.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, these three character backgrounds give us a fairly clear idea of who this guy is and how he operates.<br /> <br /> This entry has gone on long enough for the moment, so I'll post it and collect my thoughts for the next post explaining Callings and Purviews.<br /> <br /> Oh, and to give you an idea of how easy it is to come up with characters using this three background/concept idea? I literally just made this character up off the top of my head. And I am usually <i>terrible</i> with coming up with good character concepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 09-02-2016, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T06:01:31-07:00","id":961613,"title":"","content":"Alright, part 2.<br /> <br /> Paths affect some of the skills you start out with, without limiting what skills you can take in the future. From what I gather there are more benefits to this beyond getting an extra point in Occult or what have you, but Neall would be better at explaining the specifics than I.<br /> <br /> Callings! Callings are archetypes your character may have similarities to that resonate with ancient myth and legend. Things like being a <i>Warrior</i>, or a <i>Leader</i> or a <i>Creator</i>. Heroes, Demigods and Gods get three.<br /> <br /> Your Callings are chosen based on what would make sense for your Paths. Our &quot;Cunning Actor&quot; might be a <i>Trickster</i> or a <i>Lover</i>, but he's probably not a <i>Guardian</i> or a <i>Judge</i>. Important: At least one of your PC's Callings <i>must</i> be the same as one of his parent's Callings. PC's are not carbon copies of their parents, but they do inherit more than just their looks.<br /> <br /> Connor's Callings would be: <i>Sage</i>, because of his father, the &quot;Red Man of All Knowledge&quot; (really digging deep into pop culture can lead you to acquiring some strange knowledge.) This satisfies the &quot;one Calling the same&quot; requirement. Next, let's pick <i>Trickster</i> for his Cunning Actor Path - he's too clever for his own good, and being a top-notch actor means he can make the most ridiculous lies sound convincing. Finally, he naturally has the <i>Hunter</i> Calling from his &quot;Sunset Huntsman&quot; Path. Creatures of the night, you better stay out of L.A. and Hollywood - nobody messes with Connor's town.<br /> <br /> Callings aren't just labels, they give you access to Knacks - special tricks and qualities that don't fall neatly into out-and-out super powers, but are really useful to have. We don't know exactly what shape these will take in 2E yet, but an example might be Connor's <i>Trickster</i> Calling allowing him to buy something like &quot;Bavarian Fire Drill&quot; - Connor puffs himself up, puts on a lumenescent safety vest, grabs a clipboard and starts giving people orders, making them think he's a figure of authority. This offers a major boost to his attempts to deceive people into doing what he says when they normally wouldn't have any reason to.<br /> <br /> Finally, Purviews. Purviews are your awesome super powers - Superhuman strength, control over the weather, the ability to forge items of awesome mystical power. Buying a purview gives one general freeform application, like the Fire purview would make you immune to fire damage and allow you to put out small fires instantly. They also allow you to buy Boons - more specific and potent applications of a purview's ability. For instance, Connor picked up the Levin Fury boon for the Sky purview, and now he can hurl lightning bolts as attacks.<br /> <br /> You get access to one Purview for free from your parent's list. After that, you need Relics - magical items - to get access to more.<br /> <br /> ...And that's all I got. If I missed anything guys, please tell me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 09-02-2016, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T07:10:31-07:00","id":961641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=961613#post961613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, part 2.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ...And that's all I got. If I missed anything guys, please tell me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Similar to Knacks you have skill tricks, Mortal level Knacks essentially. Something like &quot;Parkor Master&quot; for an acrobatic character compared to a &quot;wall crawler&quot; knack for the truly gravity defying, as a random from thin air example. There are also Edges that are constant low end buffs.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T10:25:23-07:00","id":961761,"title":"","content":"Hmmm as they werent mentioned in a while any longer, I take it mantles come into play at later stages? (I guess god level?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"