t</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be very interested to hear about how the Cosmology is changing. Any changes to the way the Overworld and Underworld work?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We do know that Terra Incognita will be a bigger setting element this time, and I think a few things that were Overworld locals previously are going to be Terra Incognita this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T11:47:06-07:00","id":963310,"title":"","content":"I just thought of something important. <br /> <br /> Are there Relic powers that don't involve channeling Purviews? Like, if I just want a really sharp sword?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T12:38:08-07:00","id":963333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=963310#post963310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just thought of something important.<br /> <br /> Are there Relic powers that don't involve channeling Purviews? Like, if I just want a really sharp sword?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! at least according to the Storypath preview!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T12:45:31-07:00","id":963335,"title":"","content":"Really? I guess I'll have to reread it then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T21:26:44-07:00","id":963526,"title":"","content":"There's been mention of the Orishas as a coalition Pantheon. How broad is that coalition? Is it firmly rooted in the Yoruban deities, is it a not-Egyptian African-catchall (hope not), or something in between (such as a West African coalition, but not one that extends to the Bantu peoples or Khoisan of central and southern Africa)?<br /> <br /> For example would the Alusi of the Odinani religion of the Igbo people in Nigeria fall under the Orisha blanket, or be their own Pantheon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-05-2016, 12:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T10:17:24-07:00","id":963765,"title":"","content":"I think this is going a bit too far for what is, after all, a role-playing game intended for popular audiences, and not a text for students of world mythology. The intent is to give us a selection of complete, playable pantheons, rooted in reality, and accurately researched, that can be used as the basis for our own myths and tales. There is no way that it's realistic to expect every pantheon or God out there to get a spotlight. We're already getting more pantheons, and more accuracy, than in first edition, and I think there will be plenty of Gods to go around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T11:35:50-07:00","id":963810,"title":"","content":"Yep. I expect that in 2e, decisions from what a world mythology expert would expect will be deliberate design choices for the sake of keeping the game playable, not oversights due to insufficient research.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T11:42:14-07:00","id":963814,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying I want the game to cover everything - I would be (happily) shocked if the Alusi (the Igbo pantheon) got covered. I'm just wondering if its something left open, if the Orisha are intended to be a broader coalition catchall, because I'm hoping for <i><b>room for</b></i> diverse Pantheons in Africa as much as there are in Europe, Asia, etc.<br /> <br /> That said, It'd totally buy the Orisha coalition being broad enough to cover the Alusi as it specifically includes all the West African divinities touched by the Trans-Atlantic slave-trade. I'd still hope if that's the case there to be room for different central and southern African Bantu Pantheon(s), or Khoisan, or Mbuti, etc - because again, I think that provides a richer game environment if all of non-Egyptian Africa isn't covered by a single Pantheon","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T12:45:32-07:00","id":963850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=963526#post963526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's been mention of the Orishas as a coalition Pantheon. How broad is that coalition? Is it firmly rooted in the Yoruban deities, is it a not-Egyptian African-catchall (hope not), or something in between (such as a West African coalition, but not one that extends to the Bantu peoples or Khoisan of central and southern Africa)?<br /> <br /> For example would the Alusi of the Odinani religion of the Igbo people in Nigeria fall under the Orisha blanket, or be their own Pantheon?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't *think* the Orisha are a coalition at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T12:48:25-07:00","id":963853,"title":"","content":"Neall,is it true apotheosis takes more sacrifice this time? i mean,Hercules became immortal after burning on his own funeral pyre,Demophoon was also thrown by demeter in a fire to become a god . and divus julies got stabbed a ton. so,is apotheosis always like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T12:54:50-07:00","id":963858,"title":"","content":"I suspect that would depend on how likely it is that the customers who are buying the game are going to want/need those pantheons. The ten listed as first included are the best-known to Westerners (the biggest audience), with a few others (Incans, Atua, Inue) coming close behind. If they include &quot;how to make your own pantheon&quot; guidelines, then anything is possible if you want to do the work yourself. I'm just not sure that multiple African/Australian/South American pantheons would be a good return for Onyx Path in work vs. sales. Not because those cultures aren't interesting or important, but because they aren't well-known enough in the West to be included in most Chronicles. YMMV, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T13:09:23-07:00","id":963870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=963858#post963858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect that would depend on how likely it is that the customers who are buying the game are going to want/need those pantheons. The ten listed as first included are the best-known to Westerners (the biggest audience), with a few others (Incans, Atua, Inue) coming close behind. If they include &quot;how to make your own pantheon&quot; guidelines, then anything is possible if you want to do the work yourself. I'm just not sure that multiple African/Australian/South American pantheons would be a good return for Onyx Path in work vs. sales. Not because those cultures aren't interesting or important, but because they aren't well-known enough in the West to be included in most Chronicles. YMMV, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone would consider Algonquian or West African mythology as more known to Westerners than, say, the Mesopotamian gods. OPP has prided itself on diversity and representation so far, and I don't think less well known material hurts them any. The Chronicles of Darkness 2e corebooks have been very eclectic with their settings - Vampire tossed in Welsh and Chinese cities, Werewolf had an Iraqi one, Changeling is supposed to do Budapest and Cape Town - and that's been the subject of nothing of praise (save for some contention over the Tokyo material). Doing under-represented cultures and places is part of the Onyx Path brand by now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T13:14:34-07:00","id":963872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=963526#post963526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's been mention of the Orishas as a coalition Pantheon. How broad is that coalition? Is it firmly rooted in the Yoruban deities, is it a not-Egyptian African-catchall (hope not), or something in between (such as a West African coalition, but not one that extends to the Bantu peoples or Khoisan of central and southern Africa)?<br /> <br /> For example would the Alusi of the Odinani religion of the Igbo people in Nigeria fall under the Orisha blanket, or be their own Pantheon?</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, it's the <i>Loa</i> who are a coalition pantheon, not the Orisha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T13:37:42-07:00","id":963885,"title":"","content":"Ah, ok, cool. So lots of room for other African Pantheons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T13:40:34-07:00","id":963888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=963858#post963858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect that would depend on how likely it is that the customers who are buying the game are going to want/need those pantheons. The ten listed as first included are the best-known to Westerners (the biggest audience), with a few others (Incans, Atua, Inue) coming close behind. If they include &quot;how to make your own pantheon&quot; guidelines, then anything is possible if you want to do the work yourself. I'm just not sure that multiple African/Australian/South American pantheons would be a good return for Onyx Path in work vs. sales. Not because those cultures aren't interesting or important, but because they aren't well-known enough in the West to be included in most Chronicles. YMMV, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would assume most supplements with more Pantheons would go for a balance of well known Pantheons to attract purchasers, and less well known Pantheons to provide something they didn't expect but will want to play with after reading. Hence Demigod's likiness to cover the Mesopotamian gods (relatively well known, at least once you get in the roleplaying nerd subset of the population) and the Atua (not well known at all).<br /> <br /> The problem of &quot;well people are less interested in these specific lesser-known pantheons they haven't read yet&quot; is only a problem if we're talking about single pantheon pdfs, or doing a book like &quot;Pantheons of Africa&quot;. While I'd leap at buying that book, I'd be inclined to suspect it would indeed not be a comparatively strong seller. But mixing in... say... the Miungu as gods from Bantu pantheons, with the Elohim (Phoencian/Caananite), the Bogovi (Russian Slavic), and the Diyin Dine'e (Navajo/Apachean... which includes Coyote!), makes a lot of sense!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-05-2016, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T13:58:17-07:00","id":963897,"title":"","content":"Or using it to flesh out the Pesedjet and Irish while introducing a couple of new African ones\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-05-2016, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T15:14:30-07:00","id":963938,"title":"","content":"Forgive me if this sounds ignorant, but would a Pacific Northwestern Native pantheon (drawing on Haida, Tlingit, and the like) be a possibility? I'm afraid that a planned Inuit pantheon may scare something superficially similar away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T15:21:02-07:00","id":963941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=963938#post963938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive me if this sounds ignorant, but would a Pacific Northwestern Native pantheon (drawing on Haida, Tlingit, and the like) be a possibility? I'm afraid that a planned Inuit pantheon may scare something superficially similar away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting question! Who other than Raven would you hope to see in said Pantheons?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T21:10:40-07:00","id":964053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=963888#post963888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I would assume most supplements with more Pantheons would go for a balance of well known Pantheons to attract purchasers, and less well known Pantheons to provide something they didn't expect but will want to play with after reading. Hence Demigod's likiness to cover the Mesopotamian gods (relatively well known, at least once you get in the roleplaying nerd subset of the population) and the Atua (not well known at all).<br /> <br /> The problem of &quot;well people are less interested in these specific lesser-known pantheons they haven't read yet&quot; is only a problem if we're talking about single pantheon pdfs, or doing a book like &quot;Pantheons of Africa&quot;. While I'd leap at buying that book, I'd be inclined to suspect it would indeed not be a comparatively strong seller. But mixing in... say... the Miungu as gods from Bantu pantheons, with the Elohim (Phoencian/Caananite), the Bogovi (Russian Slavic), and the Diyin Dine'e (Navajo/Apachean... which includes Coyote!), makes a lot of sense!</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so much that people (i.e. gaming and mythology fans) aren't interested, so much as, is OPP going to spend the time researching and detailing multiple African/Australian/whatever pantheons for a relatively small niche of our relatively small niche, or are they going to work on powers, settings, optional rules, and other more frequently-used rules to flesh out the game line? Yes, they might drop in a few new ideas in the bigger context, but it's starting to sound too much like &quot;let's cover every world pantheon in detail&quot;, which isn't feasible where time, resources, or customer base are concerned. I love mythology as much as the next person, but do we need separate Greek/Roman/Etruscan supplements, or can we have details of one, and treatments/notes on the others? I want material to create and detail characters and my game world, sure, but there needs to be a practical limit - especially since we don't even have the basic books yet.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T21:12:13-07:00","id":964056,"title":"","content":"And yes, I do think Westerners are more likely to know Ishtar, Pazuzu, and Enki than Erinle, Ala, or Oya. It may not be a good thing, but it's true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T21:22:32-07:00","id":964062,"title":"","content":"I think there's a big difference between &quot; separate Greek, Roman, and Etruscan&quot; and &quot;the Yoruban Gods don't cover all of sub-Saharan Africa by themselves&quot;. One is unnecessary given the surviving myths - the other would be pretty ethnocentrist (not saying not doing other African Pantheons in the immediate future is ethnocentrist, just that trying to brush away cultural diversity by having the Orisha cover everything would run that risk, thankfully they aren't doing that!)<br /> <br /> I don't know what you mean by &quot;limits&quot;. I mean, there are limits and opportunity costs in what to give priority to, but as has been said before, Scion is not a limited-line. With unlimited future supplements in years to come there will be tons of other directions to go with the line. Not to mention fan-material for other pantheons too. As I said, a lot of these areas being open blanks to fill in is great, I just wanted to make sure it was a blank and not being treated as &quot;covered&quot;!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T21:29:03-07:00","id":964063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=964056#post964056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, I do think Westerners are more likely to know Ishtar, Pazuzu, and Enki than Erinle, Ala, or Oya. It may not be a good thing, but it's true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right... And yet the Orisha are in the core and the Anunnaki are not - so your premise that &quot;they put the ones that western audiences know the most about in the core&quot; is false, which i believe was the point atamajakki was making with that statement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-06-2016, 12:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T23:15:46-07:00","id":964097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=964063#post964063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right... And yet the Orisha are in the core and the Anunnaki are not - so your premise that &quot;they put the ones that western audiences know the most about in the core&quot; is false, which i believe was the point atamajakki was making with that statement.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Precisely. There are some juicy, familiar Pantheons in each book to hook passerby, and then more obscure Pantheons waiting once they get in past the cover. One of the reasons I'm so excited for this while line is as an excuse to delve into mythologies I would never touch on my own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T23:19:02-07:00","id":964099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=964062#post964062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's a big difference between &quot; separate Greek, Roman, and Etruscan&quot; and &quot;the Yoruban Gods don't cover all of sub-Saharan Africa by themselves&quot;. One is unnecessary given the surviving myths - the other would be pretty ethnocentrist (not saying not doing other African Pantheons in the immediate future is ethnocentrist, just that trying to brush away cultural diversity by having the Orisha cover everything would run that risk, thankfully they aren't doing that!)<br /> <br /> I don't know what you mean by &quot;limits&quot;. I mean, there are limits and opportunity costs in what to give priority to, but as has been said before, Scion is not a limited-line. With unlimited future supplements in years to come there will be tons of other directions to go with the line. Not to mention fan-material for other pantheons too. As I said, a lot of these areas being open blanks to fill in is great, I just wanted to make sure it was a blank and not being treated as &quot;covered&quot;!</div> </div> </div> </div>By limits, I mean that, as we don't even have the basic books in our hands, then the prevailing current conversations about including the multitudes of African, Australian, First Nations and other world pantheons seems premature, and overly specialized at this point. And I strongly suspect that the inclusion of the Yoruba in the basic ten is in response to all the criticism that they received for the &quot;voodoo pantheon&quot; in the first edition, and not a dismissal of the Anunnaki.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T23:24:19-07:00","id":964104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=964099#post964099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By limits, I mean that, as we don't even have the basic books in our hands, then the prevailing current conversations about including the multitudes of African, Australian, First Nations and other world pantheons seems premature, and overly specialized at this point. And I strongly suspect that the inclusion of the Yoruba in the basic ten is in response to all the criticism that they received for the &quot;voodoo pantheon&quot; in the first edition, and not a dismissal of the Anunnaki.</div> </div> </div> </div>...or they just wanted to include it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T00:06:53-07:00","id":964126,"title":"","content":"Well, obviously, or it wouldn't be there in the first place. My issue isn't &quot;Africa doesn't count&quot;. My issue is, let's get the basics down, then look at expanding the scope. I just don't think that it's ever going to be likely that Scion will cover five Australian or six African pantheons at any time in the forseeable future, because the likelihood of them getting much use in the average campaign is pretty small, given the primary audience for the game itself (i.e. Western gamers with a casual interest in the source material). It's far more likely that we'll get additional Greek or Egyptian deities beyond the &quot;core&quot; ones in supplements before anything esoteric. Unless, of course, there is a Kickstarter with that exact goal in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T00:43:01-07:00","id":964138,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's &quot;dismissal&quot; of the Anunnaki. We're getting the Anunnaki is a later book. My point was simply that global-balance is a factor in the pantheon selection, not just familiarity. If that wasn't the case, we wouldn't see the Manitou at all, given that it doesn't include pretty much the only Native North American divinity well known in pop-culture (Coyote).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-06-2016, 03:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T08:16:54-07:00","id":964303,"title":"","content":"And my point is simply that variety is great, but I doubt we'really getting multiple African/Australian pantheons any time soon, because there's only so much time, money, and space, and because of that they'll include things most likely to be used (i.e. Aztec, Mayan), and not the less-familiar (Tarascan, Olmec). One day, perhaps, but not soon enough to make it worth debating now.<br /> At any rate, it's good to see the new version, with (hopefully) more respect for the source material, and better rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T14:42:11-07:00","id":964541,"title":"","content":"I'm sure this was asked and answered but for the life of me I can't find it, will the game have enough of a preview that my players could create the characters they've had in mind since they heard about this a year ago when the kickstarter hits? I seem to remember that they said it was NOT ready for the whole &quot;99% - No Art&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T15:01:28-07:00","id":964550,"title":"","content":"I'm not 100% certain what a coalition pantheon is, but \u00e0w\u1ecdn \u00f2r\u00ec\u1e63\u00e0 are (assuming we hit the stretch goal) confederated with the loa because of the close and persistent relationship between those two pantheons especially in African-American religion. Bringing the Igbo gods into that confederation is an interesting idea, but I know less about them because their best sources are in Igbo and Spanish, which I don't speak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T15:05:07-07:00","id":964553,"title":"","content":"I think that reference to them being confederated with the Loa is what I must have previously misunderstood.<br /> <br /> So are gods like Papa Legba and Eshu Elegba the same guy, or different Mantles of the same guy, or straight up different gods of allied related Pantheons?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T15:41:55-07:00","id":964579,"title":"","content":"How would someone like Pandora be handled? She was given life/gifts by many of the gods. Does it work out that she is Hephaestus' child in the end with everyone sort of using their Boons on her?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T15:51:02-07:00","id":964586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=964541#post964541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure this was asked and answered but for the life of me I can't find it, will the game have enough of a preview that my players could create the characters they've had in mind since they heard about this a year ago when the kickstarter hits? I seem to remember that they said it was NOT ready for the whole &quot;99% - No Art&quot; thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can cobble something together with the Scion KS and the stuff we'll share. It won't be complete, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T15:53:58-07:00","id":964589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=964579#post964579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would someone like Pandora be handled? She was given life/gifts by many of the gods. Does it work out that she is Hephaestus' child in the end with everyone sort of using their Boons on her?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, she's a Created Scion of Haephestus.<br /> <br /> One of the playtesters today actually mentioned that it's easy to get a lot of Skills and Purviews through Birthrights if you stack them; I mentioned that they then have to guard all of those relics and keep those Guides happy, to the point that you'd be spending all your time in-character doing that and eventually something bad would happen when you fucked up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T16:06:14-07:00","id":964599,"title":"","content":"Any chance we Will see the kickstarter this week","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8286-plotinus","name":"Plotinus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T16:33:53-07:00","id":964617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=964589#post964589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, she's a Created Scion of Haephestus.<br /> <br /> One of the playtesters today actually mentioned that it's easy to get a lot of Skills and Purviews through Birthrights if you stack them; I mentioned that they then have to guard all of those relics and keep those Guides happy, to the point that you'd be spending all your time in-character doing that and eventually something bad would happen when you fucked up.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is impossible for Scion to learn to channel a purview through themselves?I Mean,beyond the one they inherited and their psp ? Are relics and guide Obligatory to have more thant two purviews?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T06:18:34-07:00","id":964920,"title":"","content":"Will it be possible to pick a Primordial or a Titan as the divine parent at character creation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12342-dr-quantum","name":"Dr. Quantum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T07:36:22-07:00","id":964950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dr. Quantum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=964920#post964920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will it be possible to pick a Primordial or a Titan as the divine parent at character creation?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> There <i>are </i>some deities who might otherwise be classed as Primordials (they represent massive concepts, have world-bodies, manifest only in the Overworld) who make Scions - the Goddess Danu, Kitchi-Manitou, among others. <br /> <br /> Titans do have children, but I really want to introduce separate Callings and Knacks that cause physical deformities for their Scions, and that just won't be in the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T08:34:52-07:00","id":964976,"title":"","content":"Would those deformities be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" 