65132#post965132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you know if you'll make material available to backers as it is completed? I should be able to stretch material from the Scion: Origin level for a good while, but I'll take anything that makes planning easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>As soon as it's completed, it's going into editing, then layout, and then it'll be out. We're full steam ahead. I do plan on spoiling big system chunks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T13:24:23-07:00","id":965226,"title":"","content":"Fucking A!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T13:41:40-07:00","id":965241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=965214#post965214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As soon as it's completed, it's going into editing, then layout, and then it'll be out. We're full steam ahead. I do plan on spoiling big system chunks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I can work with that. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T21:29:28-07:00","id":965479,"title":"","content":"I actually had a question regarding the initiative system in Scion 2E. So, if I'm reading this correctly, whoever is fastest in battle basically decides which &quot;side&quot; goes first, so to speak? Like if, say, Kane happens to roll a higher initiative than any of my PCs, it would go Kane -&gt; whoever I decided -&gt; whoever I decide -&gt; then PCs start their actions? Or am I misunderstanding?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6027-kobuddy","name":"Kobuddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6027_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T00:22:31-07:00","id":965536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kobuddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=965479#post965479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Or am I misunderstanding?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're misunderstanding... From my read it alternates between PCs and Director. So, if Kane had the highest Initiative, it'd go like this.<br /> <br /> Kane<br /> PC With Highest Initiative<br /> Enemy of your choice<br /> Another PC (Decided by previous PC)<br /> <br /> And so on until you're out of characters to act.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T13:04:19-07:00","id":965817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=965536#post965536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're misunderstanding... From my read it alternates between PCs and Director. So, if Kane had the highest Initiative, it'd go like this.<br /> <br /> Kane<br /> PC With Highest Initiative<br /> Enemy of your choice<br /> Another PC (Decided by previous PC)<br /> <br /> And so on until you're out of characters to act.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> okay, that would make a lot more sense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6027-kobuddy","name":"Kobuddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6027_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T13:19:10-07:00","id":965829,"title":"","content":"So, I just read something rather interesting, a review of a RPG game about wrestling:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.shutupandsitdown.com/rpg-review-the-world-wide-wrestling-rpg/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.shutupandsitdown.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/5gclYfg.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.shutupandsitdown.com/rpg-review-the-world-wide-wrestling-rpg/\" target=\"_blank\"> RPG Review: The World Wide Wrestling RPG - Shut Up &amp; Sit Down </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.shutupandsitdown.com/rpg-review-the-world-wide-wrestling-rpg/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.shutupandsitdown.com/rpg-review-the-world-wide-wrestling-rpg/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> [Everybody, please welcome back freelance writer Jon Bolding, who tackled the highly-recommended game of Orleans for us. This time, he's covering one of his favourite RPGs.] Review Soundtrack: Beat the Champ by The Mountain Goats Bolds:&nbsp;A siren call of my youth. The gravel-voiced radio or television announcer chanting &ldquo;Sunday!&rdquo; and&hellip; </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> There's an bit about 20 pages of the corebook being devoted to essays explaining what the appeal of the wrestling genre is, basically a tool for helping the players figure out how best to have fun with the game (as I understand it).<br /> <br /> The idea of such a thing is sort of wedged into a brain, and I'm struggling to form my thoughts into a coherent question.<br /> <br /> So, uh... anything like that in Scion 2e? Have you read World Wide Wrestling, and have you taken anything from it? (This review has intrigued me enough that I'm going to give it a read myself.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T14:17:55-07:00","id":965866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=965829#post965829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, uh... anything like that in Scion 2e? Have you read World Wide Wrestling, and have you taken anything from it? (This review has intrigued me enough that I'm going to give it a read myself.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I have not read the book.<br /> <br /> However, we take a lot of pains to drill down into <i>what a myth is</i> and <i>how different types of myth cycles work</i>, and how to make your games &quot;epic&quot; beyond throwing around lots of successes. Tales of success and tragedy follow patterns that can be manipulated, surprised, subverted or averted by the player characters. They offer wonderful toolboxes that the Storyguide can dig into to build patchwork plots and tropes into a coherent story. When your parent dies, are you in a theodicy story (that is a rumination on mortality), a journey to the underworld story (affecting a rescue of your progenitor through bargaining, representing ) or an extended family story (where you connect yourself to your larger family, thereby strengthening the community through ties of blood)?<br /> <br /> So yeah, we go into what mythologies tick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T14:22:06-07:00","id":965867,"title":"","content":"Mr. Price, I'm extremely pleased that the game will take the time to show it's players not only how to play the game, but what kind of game they're playing and how they can use it to tell great stories and have lots of fun.<br /> <br /> Please put up the Kickstarter so that I may give you my money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T14:55:53-07:00","id":965886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=965866#post965866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have not read the book.<br /> <br /> However, we take a lot of pains to drill down into <i>what a myth is</i> and <i>how different types of myth cycles work</i>, and how to make your games &quot;epic&quot; beyond throwing around lots of successes. Tales of success and tragedy follow patterns that can be manipulated, surprised, subverted or averted by the player characters. They offer wonderful toolboxes that the Storyguide can dig into to build patchwork plots and tropes into a coherent story. When your parent dies, are you in a theodicy story (that is a rumination on mortality), a journey to the underworld story (affecting a rescue of your progenitor through bargaining, representing ) or an extended family story (where you connect yourself to your larger family, thereby strengthening the community through ties of blood)?<br /> <br /> So yeah, we go into what mythologies tick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh,now 'im curious. would an incarnate of orpheus be a option? or maybe getting Orpheus himself as a guide?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T15:23:44-07:00","id":965898,"title":"","content":"So the Storypath Preview mentions the various modes of play (Action-Adventure, Procedural, Intrigue are the examples provided, though I'm not sure if others will exist down the line): does Scion incorporate these, or are they just an example of how modular Storypath is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T15:30:34-07:00","id":965902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=965898#post965898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Storypath Preview mentions the various modes of play (Action-Adventure, Procedural, Intrigue are the examples provided, though I'm not sure if others will exist down the line): does Scion incorporate these, or are they just an example of how modular Storypath is?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it works with those three. Judge Callings use a <i>lot </i>of Procedural and Intrigue action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T17:41:28-07:00","id":965947,"title":"","content":"... is there a Judge knack called Objection!? <br /> <br /> Or is that out since it's technically not a thing Judges do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T22:21:36-07:00","id":966059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=965947#post965947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... is there a Judge knack called Objection!? <br /> <br /> Or is that out since it's technically not a thing Judges do?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm wondering if judges can read minds,to find out the exact extent of an enemy crimes and to judge them properly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T00:34:02-07:00","id":966101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <s