to quote Prometheus in that. Seriously, everything from your work to giving us information as often as you could has been great. Thank you for taking Scion so close to the heart and committing so much to make a better game out of the one we already loved, despite its great problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T08:36:05-07:00","id":966246,"title":"","content":"@ Prometheus878 and Phersus: Here, Here! Ready to give my moral &amp; monetary support to Scion 2E <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T11:27:06-07:00","id":966344,"title":"","content":"Neall do other pantheons get suspicios of the Tuatha?Since so many of them slept with Titans and Titanspawn,even <i>during </i>the first war against them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 09-09-2016, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T12:12:43-07:00","id":966370,"title":"","content":"The Theoi sleep with the Titans, alot. Some examples include Amphitrite (daughter of Nerus/Doris) married to Poseidon, Metis and Zeus sort of begat Athena, Mnemosyne and Zeus begat the Muses, The sea nymphs of Artemis were all daughters of Okeanos/Tethys. Leto and Zeus begat Apollo and Artemis. I think it can't really be helped in most pantheons. <br /> <br /> Of course many of these children of titans may be considered gods/on the gods side now...like Amphitrite, Tyche and the sea nymphs of Artemis...but Mnemosyne is a Titan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T12:36:53-07:00","id":966384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=966344#post966344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neall do other pantheons get suspicios of the Tuatha?Since so many of them slept with Titans and Titanspawn,even <i>during </i>the first war against them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not especially, although they think the Irish are fucking crazy.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the Devas tend to call anyone they don't like an <i>asura</i> (their term for the Titans). And the Orishas don't even <i>believe</i> in Titans: they went through the Middle Passage, and they know the worst monsters in the World are only human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T12:46:52-07:00","id":966392,"title":"","content":"Thankx. and yeah the irish were never a very sane even at the best of times<br /> I'm getting the impression this time the Titans while still completely devoted to their Purviews are not always tied to a Greater Primordial being,and exist as individual entities. iis that it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T14:52:25-07:00","id":966448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=966392#post966392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thankx. and yeah the irish were never a very sane even at the best of times<br /> I'm getting the impression this time the Titans while still completely devoted to their Purviews are not always tied to a Greater Primordial being,and exist as individual entities. iis that it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, there are gods with much closer ties to Primordials than most titans have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T15:10:06-07:00","id":966456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=966448#post966448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, there are gods with much closer ties to Primordials than most titans have.</div> </div> </div> </div>How many primordial are mentioned in the Origins and Hero Books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T18:28:50-07:00","id":966512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=966370#post966370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Theoi sleep with the Titans, alot. Some examples include Amphitrite (daughter of Nerus/Doris) married to Poseidon, Metis and Zeus sort of begat Athena, Mnemosyne and Zeus begat the Muses, The sea nymphs of Artemis were all daughters of Okeanos/Tethys. Leto and Zeus begat Apollo and Artemis. I think it can't really be helped in most pantheons.<br /> <br /> Of course many of these children of titans may be considered gods/on the gods side now...like Amphitrite, Tyche and the sea nymphs of Artemis...but Mnemosyne is a Titan.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe Aesir are also famous for sleeping with Titanspawn. Two of the major Aesir are married to giantesses. Thor's twin sons, Magni and Modi, are the result of a union between him and a giantess. There are even giants who are simply allied with the Aesir.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, that makes me think of a question. Neall, have you guys decided which god to which Skadi is married? In some myths, she married Njord and stayed that way, but there are some myths that suggest she eventually divorced him and went on to marry Uller.<br /> <br /> Care to weigh in on this issue?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":679,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","user":"unnatural1","date":". 09-09-2016, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T19:18:17-07:00","id":966535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=966384#post966384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not especially, although they think the Irish are fucking crazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>As opposed to being crazy about fucking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T00:10:35-07:00","id":966659,"title":"","content":"Going to ask this again there (+1 additional question).<br /> 1.) It was mentioned that hero is limited to 5 boons max. Was it because with more they would get too powerful? Or that they jsut put too many xp into boons instead of other things?<br /> <br /> 2.) You have to choose the purview of your parent you want to use without a relic. The boons we know you CAN switch out, how does it stand with which purview you chose? (is that also changeable or is that fixated?)<br /> <br /> <br /> My reason for 1. is that I'm not sure about the reasoning and I'm pretty sure that players WILL ask there to houserule that that it is not limited (and then I would like to know beforehand already what the reason behind that one rule is before I fall into a pittrap).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T10:41:23-07:00","id":966824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=966659#post966659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going to ask this again there (+1 additional question).<br /> 1.) It was mentioned that hero is limited to 5 boons max. Was it because with more they would get too powerful? Or that they jsut put too many xp into boons instead of other things?<br /> <br /> 2.) You have to choose the purview of your parent you want to use without a relic. The boons we know you CAN switch out, how does it stand with which purview you chose? (is that also changeable or is that fixated?)<br /> <br /> <br /> My reason for 1. is that I'm not sure about the reasoning and I'm pretty sure that players WILL ask there to houserule that that it is not limited (and then I would like to know beforehand already what the reason behind that one rule is before I fall into a pittrap).</div> </div> </div> </div>Been curious about that too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 09-10-2016, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T13:57:37-07:00","id":966911,"title":"","content":"And another question, this one about Scions with kids...<br /> <br /> So, some friends of mine and I were talking Scion families, and one of the players wondered... &quot;My Scion character got married and had kids before his Visitation. Are his kids divine enough for a Visitation?&quot;<br /> <br /> How much divine blood does a Scion need for their God Relative to show up and go &quot;I'm awakening your Ichor&quot;? Could, say, Aphrodite appear before her granddaughter rather than her daughter because her daughter's married and settled down?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T00:28:39-07:00","id":967217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=966911#post966911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And another question, this one about Scions with kids...<br /> <br /> So, some friends of mine and I were talking Scion families, and one of the players wondered... &quot;My Scion character got married and had kids before his Visitation. Are his kids divine enough for a Visitation?&quot;<br /> <br /> How much divine blood does a Scion need for their God Relative to show up and go &quot;I'm awakening your Ichor&quot;? Could, say, Aphrodite appear before her granddaughter rather than her daughter because her daughter's married and settled down?</div> </div> </div> </div>At least in 1st edition: Yepp possible (as most scions never got a visit and still many bloodlines existed for centuries)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T15:05:46-07:00","id":968764,"title":"","content":"As a proud son of the auld sod, I can affirm that the Irish be crazy. Delightful crazy, but still. <br /> <br /> Definitely gonna be stalking this KS. I want my money in before the funding goal is met.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T04:56:31-07:00","id":969148,"title":"","content":"Arthurian Questions \ud83d\ude01<br /> 1) Arthur was an scion? If do,can he reincarnate in modern times?<br /> 2)Merlin,was he a humanidade sorcerer with no Divine blood whatsoever who manager to achieve a high level of Legend anyway? Or was he something weirdeir?<br /> 3)is Camelot still There somewhere in the Overworld?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T05:10:08-07:00","id":969150,"title":"","content":"While Neall was doing open dev, he said Arthur's sleeping in the terra incognita of Avalon, waiting until the hour of Britain's greatest need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T07:56:07-07:00","id":969231,"title":"","content":"How are Boons tiered? How much can Hero-level Boons ruin someone's day?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T09:13:54-07:00","id":969260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=969231#post969231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are Boons tiered?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hero, Demigod, God. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How much can Hero-level Boons ruin someone's day? </div> </div> </div>So, so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T10:53:44-07:00","id":969317,"title":"","content":"How much of the books are going to be available at the kickstarter? Will it be like Beast where you get the whole book minus art and formatting, or more like some of the other kickstarters where you don't get anything until the book is finished?<br /> <br /> Also, what's the status of the Iroquois pantheon in Scion, does anyone know? I'm part Mohawk, so this is of some personal interest to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T11:36:23-07:00","id":969338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notanautomaton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=969317#post969317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much of the books are going to be available at the kickstarter? Will it be like Beast where you get the whole book minus art and formatting, or more like some of the other kickstarters where you don't get anything until the book is finished?</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll be spoiling large snippets, but not the full text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, what's the status of the Iroquois pantheon in Scion, does anyone know? I'm part Mohawk, so this is of some personal interest to me. </div> </div> </div>The Manitou are &quot;of the Anishinaubaek&quot;, since those are the primary sources we're drawing from. However, after talking with a few Iroquois sources, we've decided that Winonah/Sky Woman's other children (Ioskeha/Sapling/Good Mind and Tawiscara/Flint/Bad Mind) are included, in a sort of angry cousin relationship to the rest of the pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T12:26:48-07:00","id":969377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=969338#post969338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We'll be spoiling large snippets, but not the full text.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't suppose the base systems will be fully spoiled at last? I want to get to work on seeing how the system plays and working on ports and stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T12:35:50-07:00","id":969385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notanautomaton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=969377#post969377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't suppose the base systems will be fully spoiled at last? I want to get to work on seeing how the system plays and working on ports and stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the base systems are available in basic form <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/187949/Storypath-System-Preview?sorttest=true\" target=\"_blank\">here at DriveThru</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T12:51:27-07:00","id":969399,"title":"","content":"Have you put any thought towards other Asian Pantheons beyond the Chinese, Japanese, and Indian? <br /> <br /> It might be fun to see an Ainu Pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T13:10:59-07:00","id":969410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=969385#post969385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, the base systems are available in basic form <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/187949/Storypath-System-Preview?sorttest=true\" target=\"_blank\">here at DriveThru</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, it has the base base system, like the dicerolling mechanic, but beyond that there are a bunch of things alluded to that aren't elaborated on. Like, it's implied that there's a relatively advanced social system, but it's not actually in the preview. (Unless I'm misremembering)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T09:15:46-07:00","id":969972,"title":"","content":"1. What's the Algonquin PSP like?<br /> <br /> On the same vein, when the Abrahamic Archangel Pantheon comes out in a later book, what's their PSP?<br /> <br /> 2. Hypothetically speaking, if there were to be a Lovecraft Pantheon would that be a copyright issue with that estate or not?<br /> <br /> 3. Do you have a favorite Pantheon?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":245,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","user":"Egg","date":". 09-15-2016, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T09:25:11-07:00","id":969980,"title":"","content":"Lovecraft is in the public domain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T09:29:03-07:00","id":969982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=969972#post969972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. What's the Algonquian PSP like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Having a conversation with the world, and the world listens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T09:47:58-07:00","id":969996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=969972#post969972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the same vein, when the Abrahamic Archangel Pantheon comes out in a later book, what's their PSP?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not going that route in the main game, it looks like. They're going with the Canaanite pantheon, origin of the Abrahamic faiths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T13:14:36-07:00","id":970149,"title":"","content":"So, this came up when chatting with a friend of mine about various Callings, and I wanted to check to see if I have the right basic idea.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunter</b> - The Hunter pursues their quarry, moving silent, unseen, finding clues and following leads before seizing it in a moment<br /> <br /> Mainly I was wondering if, via stretching it far enough, one could say someone who gets intel via computer hacking would fall under the Hunter Calling. Since, y'know, she IS hunting. She's just hunting for information rather than for deer or giant wolves.<br /> <br /> (The other Callings I had in mind for her were Sage and Trickster)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T13:31:30-07:00","id":970162,"title":"","content":"I Feel like there could be one more Calling. One for the gods who really are the god of many things,jacks of all trades with more associations than most gods who tend to specialize. Hermes, comes to mind,Lugh too obviously and Odin too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:23:15-07:00","id":970220,"title":"","content":"Okay, here we go: I am a fan of the Chronicles of Darkness setting, I love the Supernatural/ X-Files Urban Fantasy stuff, I am a fan of playing mortals rather than super heroes. Now here is my dilemma, what I read of the new Storypath System I like it way more than the &quot;old&quot; Storyteller System. But Scion seems to be about superpowered heroes on their way to godhood. Is Scion still interesting for me regarding my preferences I listed above or should I stick with the Chronicles of Darkness/Hunter: the Vigil nWoD 2e rules even though I like the Storypath ruleset way more?<br /> <br /> I am planning to start an Urban Fantasy campaign in the next months, any helpful answers are greatly appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:28:53-07:00","id":970229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belisarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=970220#post970220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, here we go: I am a fan of the Chronicles of Darkness setting, I love the Supernatural/ X-Files Urban Fantasy stuff, I am a fan of playing mortals rather than super heroes. Now here is my dilemma, what I read of the new Storypath System I like it way more than the &quot;old&quot; Storyteller System. But Scion seems to be about superpowered heroes on their way to godhood. Is Scion still interesting for me regarding my preferences I listed above or should I stick with the Chronicles of Darkness/Hunter: the Vigil nWoD 2e rules even though I like the Storypath ruleset way more?<br /> <br /> I am planning to start an Urban Fantasy campaign in the next months, any helpful answers are greatly appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said in your other thread, Origin is all about mortal urban fantasy, and Scions at the Hero level aren't really superheroic; they're more like the extraordinary people you see in a pulp than an actual super.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:46:28-07:00","id":970243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belisarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=970220#post970220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, here we go: I am a fan of the Chronicles of Darkness setting, I love the Supernatural/ X-Files Urban Fantasy stuff, I am a fan of playing mortals rather than super heroes. Now here is my dilemma, what I read of the new Storypath System I like it way more than the &quot;old&quot; Storyteller System. But Scion seems to be about superpowered heroes on their way to godhood. Is Scion still interesting for me regarding my preferences I listed above or should I stick with the Chronicles of Darkness/Hunter: the Vigil nWoD 2e rules even though I like the Storypath ruleset way more?<br /> <br /> I am planning to start an Urban Fantasy campaign in the next months, any helpful answers are greatly appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Origins will be <i>exactly </i>up your alley.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:48:49-07:00","id":970246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=970229#post970229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said in your other thread, Origin is all about mortal urban fantasy, and Scions at the Hero level aren't really superheroic; they're more like the extraordinary people you see in a pulp than an actual super.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds promising. Maybe there's one more question, is Scion sandbox enough to integrate a &quot;homebrew&quot; setting? I'd like to use &quot;The Secret World&quot; MMO setting with the Scion storypath ruleset, it's about urban fantasy, rivaling secret societies and lovecraftian antagonists/monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:55:48-07:00","id":970249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belisarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=970246#post970246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds promising. Maybe there's one more question, is Scion sandbox enough to integrate a &quot;homebrew&quot; setting? I'd like to use &quot;The Secret World&quot; MMO setting with the Scion storypath ruleset, it's about urban fantasy, rivaling secret societies and lovecraftian antagonists/monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scion is pretty heavily invested in its mythological framework. I'd hold off until we see some of the other Storypath games unless you want to basically build it from scratch.<br /> <br /> TSW is a lot closer to Hunter in tone than Scion, though. None of the Storypath games are built for horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:59:11-07:00","id":970250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=970243#post970243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, Origins will be <i>exactly </i>up your alley.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hoped you'd say this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Now it's waiting for the Kickstarter then. Is there any Quickstarter for the new Scion edition planned?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T15:06:48-07:00","id":970259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=970249#post970249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Scion is pretty heavily invested in its mythological framework. I'd hold off until we see some of the other Storypath games unless you want to basically build it from scratch.<br /> <br /> TSW is a lot closer to Hunter in tone than Scion, though. None of the Storypath games are built for horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely like the mythological framework, I wouldn't want to skip it entirely in favour for my TSWish approach. If there is enough tolerance in Scion for additional inventions I will be quite happy. If the influence of the pantheons can be toned down to the level of a &quot;secret war&quot; most humans aren't aware of, it would be quite perfect for my needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T15:41:51-07:00","id":970279,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you're good on all fronts, Belisarion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T16:56:39-07:00","id":970313,"title":"","content":"I'd guess Shadow in American Gods would be Origins level for most of the book, but maybe Hero when he came off the tree? Does that sound about right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T17:08:53-07:00","id":970317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=970313#post970313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd guess Shadow in American Gods would be Origins level for most of the book, but maybe Hero when he came off the tree? Does that sound about right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue he's up to Demigod by the end of the book and certainly by the later short stories where he's fighting full-on monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T19:05:58-07:00","id":970393,"title":"","content":"I don't know, you may be underestimating what Heroes are capable of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T19:32:11-07:00","id":970413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=970393#post970393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, you may be underestimating what Heroes are capable of.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't play 1e, but was told that Heroes are more extraordinary mortal than anything else. Am I wrong in that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T20:05:58-07:00","id":970436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=970413#post970413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't play 1e, but was told that Heroes are more extraordinary mortal than anything else. Am I wrong in that?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e, 3 dots in Epic Strength allows a character with a total Strength + Athletics score of 6 to break handcuffs, punch through brick walls, and lift an average sedan over their head.<br /> <br /> Starting hero builds achieve these scores <i>easily</i>.<br /> <br /> Heroes eat monsters for <i>breakfast</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T20:39:45-07:00","id":970451,"title":"","content":"When Heracles fought the Nemean Lion and the Hydra, etc he would have been at the Hero level. Around the time he's in Thrace and gets caught up in the Gigantomachy he enters Demigod domain, and he's at the top of that tiering when he holds up the sky and captures Cerberus. Achieving Godhood was likely theoretically open to him at that point, but he doesn't do so till he sheds his human life with his poisoning and burning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T20:42:21-07:00","id":970452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=970451#post970451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Heracles fought the Nemean Lion and the Hydra, etc he would have been at the Hero level. Around the time he's in Thrace and gets caught up in the Gigantomachy he enters Demigod domain, and he's at the top of that tiering when he holds up the sky and captures Cerberus. Achieving Godhood was likely theoretically open to him at that point, but he doesn't do so till he sheds his human life with his poisoning and burning.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then he jumps Mantles to the Romans!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T23:43:41-07:00","id":970533,"title":"","content":"One thing iv been interested in knowing. Will firearms ignore defense? This works great in CofD to bring a sense of realism with guns being deadly to most people but I find it doesnt scale well.<br /> <br /> In my perfect world guns would probably bypass normal defense for mortals but not for scions and some supernaturals.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 09-16-2016, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T03:34:37-07:00","id":970608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=970279#post970279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, you're good on all fronts, Belisarion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will there be some conversion guide for older storyteller horrors/monsters? I know, I become greedy now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T04:16:50-07:00","id":970616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belisarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=970608#post970608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will there be some conversion guide for older storyteller horrors/monsters? I know, I become greedy now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Mn. Onyx Path don't own the Storyteller or Storytelling games (the World of Darkness and the Chronicles of Darkness). They'd have to make arrangements with White Wolf for that. Then again, there are some CoD-<i>like</i> critters in Scion, such as vampires and shapeshifters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T06:24:32-07:00","id":970648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=970616#post970616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mn. Onyx Path don't own the Storyteller or Storytelling games (the World of Darkness and the Chronicles of Darkness). They'd have to make arrangements with White Wolf for that. Then again, there are some CoD-<i>like</i> critters in Scion, such as vampires and shapeshifters.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the standard stuff like undead, zombies, ghuls, ghosts and the like? If they can make a Scion: Origin's life miserable, like horrors in CoD, it's all I can ask. Or some neat rules to create such CoDish monsters myself. The PCs should feel quite squishy, at least early in their lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T09:07:45-07:00","id":970732,"title":"","content":"I'm always puzzled as to why people find a game that is, at it's core, all about playing the powerful divine offspring/champions of Gods and Goddesses, created and destined to do great deeds, to change the course of history, and to star in their own legends - and then ask if they can play ordinary mortals who are &quot;squishy&quot;. Aren't there dozens of other RPGs on the market that would enable that? Why play Scion if that's what you are looking for? If you want &quot;mortals vs. monsters&quot;, play CoD: Hunter, or GURPS Monster Hunters - you'll find plenty of squish factor there. The same if you want a gunslinger-style campaign - this really isn't the system for it. Scion is about larger-than-life characters performing larger-than-life deeds, and that's what is should focus on. There are lots of other games for the mortal stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T09:50:18-07:00","id":970753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=970732#post970732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm always puzzled as to why people find a game that is, at it's core, all about playing the powerful divine offspring/champions of Gods and Goddesses, created and destined to do great deeds, to change the course of history, and to star in their own legends - and then ask if they can play ordinary mortals who are &quot;squishy&quot;. Aren't there dozens of other RPGs on the market that would enable that? Why play Scion if that's what you are looking for? If you want &quot;mortals vs. monsters&quot;, play CoD: Hunter, or GURPS Monster Hunters - you'll find plenty of squish factor there. The same if you want a gunslinger-style campaign - this really isn't the system for it. Scion is about larger-than-life characters performing larger-than-life deeds, and that's what is should focus on. There are lots of other games for the mortal stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me personally, I want to be able to present a well balanced world. I don't like campaigns that just focus on the action and intrigue and just jump from scene to scene. I want to know the system can accurately portray the struggles of mortals in these worlds. Especially when a character may grow attached to a character and I want to accurately injure or challenge that mortal without just improvising and winging it. I mean sure, I could just say the mortal is barely alive but now crippled but the roll of the dice deciding that is much more satisfying to me to mix up planned events. Essentially you need rules to place them into the game and have them accurately interact with the system.<br /> <br /> On top of that, I just like the idea of a system being all inclusive in terms of what is in the world. Mortals exist, they should be properly usable/playable if u want to tell a story dealing with them. I could understand some rare creature not having a system to back it but mortals? When im building up my campaign to be a larger than life world and we finish the campaign, it would be nice to be able to then play a urban fantasy campaign that takes place in the aftermath of the previous player characters events without having to shift over to WoD and homebrew everything to hell.<br /> <br /> So long post slightly longer, it shows the devs care about world building and enforces that the setting can encompass stories told from many perspectives and many goals rather than only a narrow focus. 1st edition was guilty of that with how the book seemed to want every campaign to be a war vs the titans and due to the fact the narrative all pointed that way there was hardly any incentive to try and break that mold unless u were really ambitious.<br /> <br /> Hopefully my cluster of words cast some light on your question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 09-16-2016, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T09:51:41-07:00","id":970754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=970732#post970732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm always puzzled as to why people find a game that is, at it's core, all about playing the powerful divine offspring/champions of Gods and Goddesses, created and destined to do great deeds, to change the course of history, and to star in their own legends - and then ask if they can play ordinary mortals who are &quot;squishy&quot;. Aren't there dozens of other RPGs on the market that would enable that? Why play Scion if that's what you are looking for? If you want &quot;mortals vs. monsters&quot;, play CoD: Hunter, or GURPS Monster Hunters - you'll find plenty of squish factor there. The same if you want a gunslinger-style campaign - this really isn't the system for it. Scion is about larger-than-life characters performing larger-than-life deeds, and that's what is should focus on. There are lots of other games for the mortal stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand your confusion with my questions, so I will elaborate on my requests. In fact I do like CoD very much, I like urban fantasy and I like the idea behind The Secret World. And yes, I like the idea of PCs being (exceptional) normal humans who are still sweating when taking on &quot;lesser&quot; horrors. So as you empahasized, there are already settings like CoD which seem perfect for this. As of yet, in the past days I came to learn that Scion is about urban fantasy as well and it uses new enhanced mechanics based on storyteller but enriched by stunts and the like. And this new features caught my attention. I have in mind that my chars start as &quot;squishy&quot; ones with the potential to reach hero level competence after they endured enough hardship as normal mortals. For this reason I was going to check Scion out, which I didn't know before, if it could fit my needs. As an icing I really like the idea about historic pantheons meddling with the mortal world (although in my plans rather behind the scenes in a kind of secret war, not openly). So yeah, CoD and Scion are both about urban fantasy. The descision now hangs on which mechanics I like more and in this case Scion wins the day. And as I was reassured by Neall Scion: Origins is up my alley. But I am of course open to any suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T09:56:48-07:00","id":970757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=970753#post970753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me personally, I want to be able to present a well balanced world. I don't like campaigns that just focus on the action and intrigue and just jump from scene to scene. I want to know the system can accurately portray the struggles of mortals in these worlds. Especially when a character may grow attached to a character and I want to accurately injure or challenge that mortal without just improvising and winging it. I mean sure, I could just say the mortal is barely alive but now crippled but the roll of the dice deciding that is much more satisfying to me to mix up planned events. Essentially you need rules to place them into the game and have them accurately interact with the system.<br /> <br /> On top of that, I just like the idea of a system being all inclusive in terms of what is in the world. Mortals exist, they should be properly usable/playable if u want to tell a story dealing with them. I could understand some rare creature not having a system to back it but mortals? When im building up my campaign to be a larger than life world and we finish the campaign, it would be nice to be able to then play a urban fantasy campaign that takes place in the aftermath of the previous player characters events without having to shift over to WoD and homebrew everything to hell.<br /> <br /> So long post slightly longer, it shows the devs care about world building and enforces that the setting can encompass stories told from many perspectives and many goals rather than only a narrow focus. 1st edition was guilty of that with how the book seemed to want every campaign to be a war vs the titans and due to the fact the narrative all pointed that way there was hardly any incentive to try and break that mold unless u were really ambitious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly my thoughts! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T09:58:34-07:00","id":970758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belisarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=970648#post970648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the standard stuff like undead, zombies, ghuls, ghosts and the like? If they can make a Scion: Origin's life miserable, like horrors in CoD, it's all I can ask. Or some neat rules to create such CoDish monsters myself. The PCs should feel quite squishy, at least early in their lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghosts aren't a problem, as they're pretty much cross-pantheon.<br /> <br /> For the type of zombie you might be looking for, Scion 1e has hungry corpses (the standard flesh-eaters). Dunno if we'll see them in 2e, but they're pretty basic, and it should be easy to do up a 2e version.<br /> <br /> The Loa will probably have something with the original version of zombies, and the Arabian pantheon would get the original ghuls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T10:06:40-07:00","id":970761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=970758#post970758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ghosts aren't a problem, as they're pretty much cross-pantheon.<br /> <br /> For the type of zombie you might be looking for, Scion 1e has hungry corpses (the standard flesh-eaters). Dunno if we'll see them in 2e, but they're pretty basic, and it should be easy to do up a 2e version.<br /> <br /> The Loa will probably have something with the original version of zombies, and the Arabian pantheon would get the original ghuls.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there are monsters based on pantheons and historical myths all the better. I actually like the sound of &quot;hungry corpses&quot; better than zomies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T10:47:36-07:00","id":970776,"title":"","content":"re: Playing mortals<br /> <br /> I imagine that one can, I mean, that's what Origins is all about. The stuff before you add on &quot;So YOU are half-god&quot;. That said?<br /> <br /> I'm not adverse to playing a mortal in the Scion world. It's just that if I do play a mortal... I want to basically be like Karin Murphy from the Dresden Files. No magic, no supernatural umph, but still takes out an animated plant monster with a goddamn chainsaw. Yeah, there's very real threat, but if you pick your battles and play to your strengths <i>you can fight back</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T10:48:11-07:00","id":970779,"title":"","content":"Oh, one more question. Will there be a flexible magic system and supernatural merits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T11:02:34-07:00","id":970786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belisarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=970761#post970761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there are monsters based on pantheons and historical myths all the better. I actually like the sound of &quot;hungry corpses&quot; better than zomies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. Scion doesn't just have the gods and heroes of the pantheons, it also has their enemies and monsters. And on top of that, you can have both classic versions and modernised versions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T12:32:15-07:00","id":970834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belisarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=970220#post970220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scion seems to be about superpowered heroes on their way to godhood. Is Scion still interesting for me regarding my preferences I listed above or should I stick with the Chronicles of Darkness/Hunter: the Vigil nWoD 2e rules even though I like the Storypath ruleset way more?<br /> <br /> I am planning to start an Urban Fantasy campaign in the next months, any helpful answers are greatly appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a little late on this, but I wrote the urban fantasy part for Origins. I think it's the kind of thing you're looking for, and I've tried to make it something for people who don't want to escalate to the Hero/Demigod/God level to play. (Actually, I'd like to do this for every level. Sometimes it's fun just to be someone at Hero-level having adventures around the world without the whole &quot;and someday, you will be a Demigod&quot; thing.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T12:47:29-07:00","id":970844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geoffrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=970834#post970834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm a little late on this, but I wrote the urban fantasy part for Origins. I think it's the kind of thing you're looking for, and I've tried to make it something for people who don't want to escalate to the Hero/Demigod/God level to play. (Actually, I'd like to do this for every level. Sometimes it's fun just to be someone at Hero-level having adventures around the world without the whole &amp;quot;and someday, you will be a Demigod&amp;quot; thing.)</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone largely excited for lower-Tier play, this is great news.<br /> <br /> Pantheons introduced in books like Demigod and God will still scale down to Hero, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T12:55:56-07:00","id":970854,"title":"","content":"I'm concerned that too much emphasis on playing mortals might detract from the powers of the Gods. I don't want Scion to be an RPG about heroic mortals; I want it to be an RPG about divine beings and their Scions. If you want to play Karrin Murphy, there's a Dresden Files RPG out there. GURPS and Fate easily allow urban fantasy games. At it's core, CoD can be toned down from horror to UF. But there are few games that allow the dial to go to 11, and Scion should be one. Yes, mortals should be part of the background, as supporting characters, sidekicks, and the masses of the world, but just playing them, or writing extensive rules to cater to that level of play, seems to be outside of the spirit of the game in question. The Gods and Goddesses, and their chosen champions, should be the main focus of Scion 2nd edition, otherwise what's the point? I'm not looking for &quot;Cabbies and Chimeras, the RPG&quot;, at least not in this case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T13:07:35-07:00","id":970862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=970854#post970854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm concerned that too much emphasis on playing mortals might detract from the powers of the Gods. I don't want Scion to be an RPG about heroic mortals; I want it to be an RPG about divine beings and their Scions. If you want to play Karrin Murphy, there's a Dresden Files RPG out there. GURPS and Fate easily allow urban fantasy games. At it's core, CoD can be toned down from horror to UF. But there are few games that allow the dial to go to 11, and Scion should be one. Yes, mortals should be part of the background, as supporting characters, sidekicks, and the masses of the world, but just playing them, or writing extensive rules to cater to that level of play, seems to be outside of the spirit of the game in question. The Gods and Goddesses, and their chosen champions, should be the main focus of Scion 2nd edition, otherwise what's the point? I'm not looking for &quot;Cabbies and Chimeras, the RPG&quot;, at least not in this case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if I am not mistaken Hero, Demigods and Gods should satiate your hunger for godplay? Just Origins, which is the mechanical foundation, has an emphasis on mortals. So you should be good with 75% god power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T13:13:20-07:00","id":970867,"title":"","content":"oooh nice idea. A cabbie scion of hermes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T13:17:32-07:00","id":970870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=970854#post970854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm concerned that too much emphasis on playing mortals might detract from the powers of the Gods. I don't want Scion to be an RPG about heroic mortals; I want it to be an RPG about divine beings and their Scions. If you want to play Karrin Murphy, there's a Dresden Files RPG out there. GURPS and Fate easily allow urban fantasy games. At it's core, CoD can be toned down from horror to UF. But there are few games that allow the dial to go to 11, and Scion should be one. Yes, mortals should be part of the background, as supporting characters, sidekicks, and the masses of the world, but just playing them, or writing extensive rules to cater to that level of play, seems to be outside of the spirit of the game in question. The Gods and Goddesses, and their chosen champions, should be the main focus of Scion 2nd edition, otherwise what's the point? I'm not looking for &quot;Cabbies and Chimeras, the RPG&quot;, at least not in this case.</div> </div> </div> </div>No offense, but what you want in the game seems to go directly against what the devs want. They want a game that can be played endlessly at any of the four levels. They want to create a game that has strong world building capabilities. A game where u can play multiple campaigns from multiple angles and scopes within the same world. And quite honestly, they sold it as this from the start and now I'm sure a good amount of people were drawn to the game because of that focus.<br /> <br /> At this point you gotta have faith that the devs are going to make it a great game at every level. I mean, its not like they are going to suddenly change it all now when the redlines are already going and the hype has been built.<br /> <br /> I'm sure the above sounds way more negative than what I intended. I fully understand that you are making your posts because you want to see the game succeed. We all do. I just think you are cutting the devs a little short here. This is Onyx Path's baby. This is their first truly owned game line they are releaseing. With all the care they put into the 2nd editions of WoD I just know what to expect. And it's good.<br /> <br /> A Onyx Path line that doesn't allow low level play to make you feel weak and powerless? That wouldn't feel right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 09-16-2016, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T13:37:24-07:00","id":970881,"title":"","content":"Just to set expectations here, <i>Origins</i> is very much not CofD. We do have more than one chord in our songs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T13:37:46-07:00","id":970883,"title":"","content":"I have to say I agree with Purple Snit here. There are plenty of games even within the Storyteller system that give you gritty urban fantasy. All the NWoD books are designed that way and even have merits that allow you to be \u2018a little bit more\u2019 if you want to emulate your favorite TV show like Supernatural or Grimm or what have you. One of the earliest/loudest complaints about Scion 1<sup>st</sup> edition is that things worked really well in Hero (where you were basically at the power level being described) but fell apart after Legend 5.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m glad that Origins can easily handle this level of play but am much more interested that at Demigod and God there are plenty of things to do instead of just going with \u2018ok, this is mostly endgame/retiring your character time because ..well\u2026you\u2019re a god. Now what?\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T13:47:32-07:00","id":970893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=970883#post970883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m glad that Origins can easily handle this level of play but am much more interested that at Demigod and God there are plenty of things to do instead of just going with \u2018ok, this is mostly endgame/retiring your character time because ..well\u2026you\u2019re a god. Now what?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>But you are forgetting that the reason Demigod and God fell apart at those levels was because they had restrictions when making the system. 1st edition was created only slightly modding the normal storyteller system with very little thought into how things scaled. Storypath was designed from the ground up to scale properly at many different levels. I get that healthy skepticism is a good thing but you gotta admit the fact the system has been stated to be designed to fullfill the exact thing you want should be a good sign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 09-16-2016, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T14:05:12-07:00","id":970901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=970881#post970881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to set expectations here, <i>Origins</i> is very much not CofD. We do have more than one chord in our songs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>But it is still urban fantasy, right? I could shape it as gritty or lovecraftian as I like. The sky is the limit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T20:35:17-07:00","id":971115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=970883#post970883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say I agree with Purple Snit here. There are plenty of games even within the Storyteller system that give you gritty urban fantasy. All the NWoD books are designed that way and even have merits that allow you to be \u2018a little bit more\u2019 if you want to emulate your favorite TV show like Supernatural or Grimm or what have you. One of the earliest/loudest complaints about Scion 1<sup>st</sup> edition is that things worked really well in Hero (where you were basically at the power level being described) but fell apart after Legend 5.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m glad that Origins can easily handle this level of play but am much more interested that at Demigod and God there are plenty of things to do instead of just going with \u2018ok, this is mostly endgame/retiring your character time because ..well\u2026you\u2019re a god. Now what?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And I agree right back at you. \u263a<br /> <br /> Of course I have faith in the devs - I wouldn't be considering supporting the Kickstart if I didn't. I'm just concerned with the chorus of &quot;let's play mortals&quot; in a game about the Gods and their champions. As was pointed out, one big problem with 1st edition was that it fell apart at higher power levels. It needs to go UP in power, not down - that's the theme of the game. I'm not worried about the upper levels, I'm concerned that it might get too focused on mortals at the expense of immortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T22:31:47-07:00","id":971162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=971115#post971115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just concerned with the chorus of &quot;let's play mortals&quot; in a game about the Gods and their champions.</div> </div> </div> </div> In order to guard against misunderstandings, I just asked if playing mortals is just one option, not the sole purpose of Scion. I'm fully aware that Scion is primarily about playing &quot;larger than life&quot; heroes and godlike PCs. Still it's nice to see that the mechanics are designed with having every aspect of gaming in mind.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T22:43:19-07:00","id":971170,"title":"","content":"Totally, I get that. Mortals play a roll in myths all over the world. I just don't feel that it should be the <i>focus</i> of the game. The &quot;can we play mortals&quot; has come up before, and I'm just hoping it doesn't take away from the larger-than-life aspect or full-on God-level exploits of the game, and turn it into &quot;Urban Fantasy Godlings&quot;. There has been a fair bit of fiction like that, and it ruins the immersion and theme for me when I expect a story about Gods, and get mortal, low-powered detectives or reincarnated teenagers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5627,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","user":"Purple Snit","date":". 09-17-2016, 01:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T23:37:41-07:00","id":971183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=971170#post971170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Totally, I get that. Mortals play a roll in myths all over the world. I just don't feel that it should be the <i>focus</i> of the game. The &quot;can we play mortals&quot; has come up before, and I'm just hoping it doesn't take away from the larger-than-life aspect or full-on God-level exploits of the game, and turn it into &quot;Urban Fantasy Godlings&quot;. There has been a fair bit of fiction like that, and it ruins the immersion and theme for me when I expect a story about Gods, and get mortal, low-powered detectives or reincarnated teenagers.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I've seen so far, the idea is that you and your players can choose to pause development at a level you enjoy. You want to be pulp-style heroes? Sure. You want to be mythic heroes who aren't yet fully divine? Absolutely. You want to be demigods clawing their way to divinity against the machinations of Fate and the pantheons they think are outdated and cruel? Do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T06:20:52-07:00","id":971289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=971170#post971170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Totally, I get that. Mortals play a roll in myths all over the world. I just don't feel that it should be the <i>focus</i> of the game. The &quot;can we play mortals&quot; has come up before, and I'm just hoping it doesn't take away from the larger-than-life aspect or full-on God-level exploits of the game, and turn it into &quot;Urban Fantasy Godlings&quot;. There has been a fair bit of fiction like that, and it ruins the immersion and theme for me when I expect a story about Gods, and get mortal, low-powered detectives or reincarnated teenagers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get where you're coming from. It's just that, well, playing skilled mortals or near-mortals is <i>new</i>, and given how Fate is stated to be kinder and looser to mortals, the idea that the small are capable of doing what is physically impossible for the large...even if there wasn't a Humanity, Fuck Yeah! element to that (always popular among an audience of humans), it's an extremely intriguing idea that makes logical sense as to why gods don't just wave their Purviews at the problem and move on (it'd provoke Fate into screwing them over).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T09:46:41-07:00","id":971365,"title":"","content":"Hey there is a kickstarter thread on RPG net where neall is giving some spoilers. I dont know if the what we know wiki is public to edit so just a heads up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T10:10:09-07:00","id":971373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=971365#post971365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey there is a kickstarter thread on RPG net where neall is giving some spoilers. I dont know if the what we know wiki is public to edit so just a heads up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I'm on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T10:21:22-07:00","id":971381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=971170#post971170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Totally, I get that. Mortals play a roll in myths all over the world. I just don't feel that it should be the <i>focus</i> of the game. The &quot;can we play mortals&quot; has come up before, and I'm just hoping it doesn't take away from the larger-than-life aspect or full-on God-level exploits of the game, and turn it into &quot;Urban Fantasy Godlings&quot;. There has been a fair bit of fiction like that, and it ruins the immersion and theme for me when I expect a story about Gods, and get mortal, low-powered detectives or reincarnated teenagers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, I'm just going to be honest here. You are just overthinking the Hel out of this. At no point has any mortal play supporter or any of the devs ever said that they want to take away the scope of demigod and god games. The Demigod and God games are not even in development yet. This kickstarter is for Origins and Hero. Which means that half the hype/talk is going to be about basic mortals/supernaturals/and pre heroes and half the hype will be about pulp heros flying around like marvel. Initially there was very little information on Origins and most of the 120 pages of this topic are focused on the hero aspect of the game. Now they are being more free with mortal information so of course people are focusing on that at the moment.<br /> <br /> If Demigod and God turned out to be people walking down the streets like gods in human skin with very little impact (essentially Demon at that point) id be just as disappointed as you would be. However, nothing has pointed towards this occurring at all.<br /> <br /> Seems like you are trying to curb your hype by making up negatives to be honest. Instead, focus on the cool shit we got coming up next week. No disrespect. I'm just the kinda guy who likes to be direct with people. Think of it as tough love for fellow Scion fans. We both want the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 09-17-2016, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T10:59:50-07:00","id":971407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=970533#post970533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing iv been interested in knowing. Will firearms ignore defense? This works great in CofD to bring a sense of realism with guns being deadly to most people but I find it doesnt scale well.<br /> <br /> In my perfect world guns would probably bypass normal defense for mortals but not for scions and some supernaturals.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Another question besides this. How well does the book explain the particular myths behind all the Gods/Pantheons/Creatures in the book? Is it intended for someone who knows Mythology well enough or would it be possible for someone who knows very little outside of a few very specific myths to learn and run an accurate campaign about something they previously didn't know about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T13:37:28-07:00","id":971500,"title":"","content":"I am unsure if i am phrasing my question correctly so bear with me a bit.<br /> <br /> How do you envision playing a scion say from the algonquin pantheon who is not from that particular culture?? The same question could be said with a scion born in japan who is not from the kami pantheon. <br /> It is something i feel would be interesting to explore but i am unsure on how to do it well.<br /> Would that be something offensive in your opinion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T15:10:30-07:00","id":971531,"title":"","content":"How much mechanical effect do the various Geneses have? I'm curious if they're largely just flavor for your associated Path (it's hard to not call them Aspects, though I know they're different) or if a Chosen has significantly different rules from a Born.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T15:14:55-07:00","id":971534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=971500#post971500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am unsure if i am phrasing my question correctly so bear with me a bit.<br /> <br /> How do you envision playing a scion say from the algonquin pantheon who is not from that particular culture?? The same question could be said with a scion born in japan who is not from the kami pantheon.<br /> It is something i feel would be interesting to explore but i am unsure on how to do it well.<br /> Would that be something offensive in your opinion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously not on the Dev team, but this exact topic is actually a pretty common theme in Scion. Cultural differences are a huge note of a lot of Scion games, and cultural differences are incredibly significant even across time. A modern Algonquin Scion will not find themselves exactly at home immediately with the Algonquin Pantheon, there may even be significant points where they disagree. The same for someone born in Ireland with the Tuatha. Cultures shift over time to the extent that just being in the same region as your Pantheon doesn't mean you will feel familiar with that culture. As L.P. Hartley said, &quot;The past is a foreign country, they do things differently there.&quot; On top of this, most cultures of the Pantheons do not exist any more. The Theoi, Tuatha, Aesir, Teotl, and Netjer all lost their original cultures.<br /> <br /> A Japanese person who is not the Scion of one of the Kami would also be a reasonable point. The Gods do not (some exceptions, the Kami in general are probably unlikely to have Scions outside Japan) really care about borders. <i>Especially</i> the traveling Gods. Odin, Manannan, Hermes, Eshu, rambling along through the mortal world. More space for culture clashes, which is a amazing sub-theme of Scion.<br /> <br /> To do it well, just approach things with accuracy in mind. The easiest example that I can give is a Scion of the Teotl. Almost no modern person would be down with participating in the human sacrifices. However, have their Divine Parent explain that the blood is to ensure the Teotl can continue to protect and provide for humanity (Except for Tezcat who's a coin flip if he's helping or not) and that the sacrificed all get access to the nice afterlives unlike most other people. The Scion can chose to disagree, attempt to bridge a gap, or ect. Same for a Teotl Scion who is Homosexual, and finds themselves in the crosshairs of the Pantheon (or an Aesir Scion, or a Netjer Scion, ect) and have to deal with these issues of cultural clashing.<br /> <br /> Edit: Know what, I totally hadn't considered what Atamajakki said below me. I was just thinking about it from a &quot;would this make sense&quot; angle. If someone is being a racist idiot, playing offensive stereotypes, or essentially other branches of being a twat, I wouldn't even want them in my play group. I do think that it's totally reasonable to be a Scion of Odin who is Moroccan for example, a Irish son of Sun Wukong, or an Iraqui son of one of the Incan Gods, as long as you're not being a racist idiot about it. Pretty much, to do it best, don't do it badly, and don't be a racist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":".  Spelling, again. And adding Edit: comment. 09-17-2016, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T15:55:14-07:00","id":971553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=971500#post971500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am unsure if i am phrasing my question correctly so bear with me a bit.<br /> <br /> How do you envision playing a scion say from the algonquin pantheon who is not from that particular culture?? The same question could be said with a scion born in japan who is not from the kami pantheon.<br /> It is something i feel would be interesting to explore but i am unsure on how to do it well.<br /> Would that be something offensive in your opinion?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how comfortable I would be at someone at my table playing a character whose ethnic background doesn't match up with any Pantheon that still has existing modern worship; there are very few priests of Anpu to offend, but there are plenty of Hindus out there. That goes doubly so for closed cultures like the Native American Pantheons, as they're essentially a closed culture.<br /> <br /> Years of terrible, terrible run-ins with folks using clan Ravnos in <i>Vampire</i> as an excuse to be massively racist have made me cynical, and I figure a decent number of bad players just want an excuse to keep playing as white people, regardless of Pantheon they choose; just look back to the vitriol after <i>Mummy</i> said the player characters have to be North African in origin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T17:18:13-07:00","id":971593,"title":"","content":"All this talk of mortals makes me want to ask, are there any mortals who are just favored? Not being the scion of anyone but just looked fondly by a god but not a priest or anything? Like would Diomedes just be a kid Athena adopted secretly or was he a mortal man who once he could see Aphrodite, was able to hurt her?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T17:47:00-07:00","id":971605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=971593#post971593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All this talk of mortals makes me want to ask, are there any mortals who are just favored? Not being the scion of anyone but just looked fondly by a god but not a priest or anything? Like would Diomedes just be a kid Athena adopted secretly or was he a mortal man who once he could see Aphrodite, was able to hurt her?</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that there are Geneses beyond just being Born of the gods now; you can be a Scion without divine blood relation, either being Created by divine hands or Chosen by them. I'd argue that Diomedes is a pretty textbook Chosen Scion, as Athena is clearly rooting for him and offers him a lot of supernatural mojo to toss around.<br /> <br /> Honestly, Geneses are my favorite shift in 2e so far. My only complaint about them is Incarnates being pushed back, just because I love the idea so much!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T17:47:55-07:00","id":971606,"title":"","content":"My players have created a Wisconsin born scion of Shango based on Chris Pratt, A Japanese scion of Sun Wukong, A Baxoje scion of Kali. Love (and baser emotions) knows no boundaries and I'm not going to tell my player &quot;Sorry, your character's not black enough to be the son of Shango.&quot; <br /> <br /> The gods can pick and choose how they look and who they bang.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T17:52:41-07:00","id":971609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=971606#post971606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My players have created a Wisconsin born scion of Shango based on Chris Pratt, A Japanese scion of Sun Wukong, A Baxoje scion of Kali. Love (and baser emotions) knows no boundaries and I'm not going to tell my player &quot;Sorry, your character's not black enough to be the son of Shango.&quot;<br /> <br /> The gods can pick and choose how they look and who they bang.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would certainly raise an eyebrow at someone who wants to play a character of a Pantheon tied to a living African culture but didn't want to play a black character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T18:01:02-07:00","id":971617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=971381#post971381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ok, I'm just going to be honest here. You are just overthinking the Hel out of this. At no point has any mortal play supporter or any of the devs ever said that they want to take away the scope of demigod and god games. The Demigod and God games are not even in development yet. This kickstarter is for Origins and Hero. Which means that half the hype/talk is going to be about basic mortals/supernaturals/and pre heroes and half the hype will be about pulp heros flying around like marvel. Initially there was very little information on Origins and most of the 120 pages of this topic are focused on the hero aspect of the game. Now they are being more free with mortal information so of course people are focusing on that at the moment.<br /> <br /> If Demigod and God turned out to be people walking down the streets like gods in human skin with very little impact (essentially Demon at that point) id be just as disappointed as you would be. However, nothing has pointed towards this occurring at all.<br /> <br /> Seems like you are trying to curb your hype by making up negatives to be honest. Instead, focus on the cool shit we got coming up next week. No disrespect. I'm just the kinda guy who likes to be direct with people. Think of it as tough love for fellow Scion fans. We both want the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>No offense taken. I'd rather over-think the issue of &quot;Urban Fantasy Scion&quot; vs. &quot;God's and Monsters Scion&quot;, than say nothing and feel like I should have spoken up. And my enthusiasm isn't curbed by wanting the game to be bigger and better than 1st edition. I'm eagerly waiting for the Kickstart along with everyone else here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T18:01:40-07:00","id":971618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=971609#post971609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would certainly raise an eyebrow at someone who wants to play a character of a Pantheon tied to a living African culture but didn't want to play a black character.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ditto. That seems...unfortunate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T18:05:31-07:00","id":971621,"title":"","content":"Yeah... If I were worried about that I wouldn't allow them to be played at all. Her concept was cool, that's all that matters at my table. She made a character, went through the book and found a god that fit with her concept, Shango is a Warrior, Trickster and Leader (1st ed) so she chose him. Also which is worse telling someone their character isn't black enough or telling a black player they cant play a white character? I figure play what you want to play.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T18:14:11-07:00","id":971627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=971621#post971621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah... If I were worried about that I wouldn't allow them to be played at all. Her concept was cool, that's all that matters at my table. She made a character, went through the book and found a god that fit with her concept, Shango is a Warrior, Trickster and Leader (1st ed) so she chose him. Also which is worse telling someone their character isn't black enough or telling a black player they cant play a white character? I figure play what you want to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>White characters aren't underrepresented, while black characters almost certainly are, and accurate, respectful Yoruba characters doubly so. &quot;This bit of mythology seems cool but I want to tack it into a white character&quot; is the definition of cultural appropriation, and I have to wonder why they wouldn't play a black character in such a context, just the same as I'd be displeased with a white Manitou or Deva character. If the player approached me with an interesting concept and backstory respectful to the actual culture and mythology involved, I'd allow it, but &quot;I want to play someone the same race as me and picked this deity for their powers&quot; is definitely a troubling notion to me.<br /> <br /> And because the answer of &quot;you wouldn't do this for the Theoi!&quot; is incoming, I don't care to gatekeep dead (in our world, not Scion's) cultures nearly as hard as those that are still extant. If you're going to borrow from people that are still around, the least you can do is represent them. Especially in the case of the Orisha, you have a grouping of gods tied to the ethnic group among the most victimized by the African slave trade, and you're asking why taking their mythology and stapling it onto someone white might be unpleasant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 09-17-2016, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T18:33:24-07:00","id":971642,"title":"","content":"Is there any hope of us seeing historical settings as Stretch Goals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T18:38:01-07:00","id":971644,"title":"","content":"Apologies. I truly didnt mean it like that. I remembered a bit in scion 1e about bastet spent some time in japan and i liked the idea of a japanese scion of bastet. I just wondered how to expand on that idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T18:38:32-07:00","id":971646,"title":"","content":"I'm not going to tell anyone what to play at their table, but this topic is something we're addressing head-on in the book.<br /> <br /> I can say that the art, or at the very least my art notes, is definitely going to reflect a lot of diversity in the World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T18:57:44-07:00","id":971660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=971644#post971644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies. I truly didnt mean it like that. I remembered a bit in scion 1e about bastet spent some time in japan and i liked the idea of a japanese scion of bastet. I just wondered how to expand on that idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bastet's faith has been dead outside of a handful of neopagans for nearly two thousand years. It's a fair bit harder to consider that appropriation than material from something that's still around today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T18:59:05-07:00","id":971661,"title":"","content":"Actually the player's black. And again, if the Yoruban religion and the culture that it represents are so sacrosanct that one must do actual research to play them, maybe they should have been left out of the game. Its a game, not a Masters thesis.<br /> <br /> I have a bigger problem with telling a player, &quot;I'm sorry, but I set the game in 15th century france, so no you can't play a scion of Eshu the most prolific traveler in myth just didn't find any Europeans attractive enough to bed them.&quot; &quot;Your Chevalier scion of Hachiman is cool, but its just too goshed darned problematic, better go with Tyr or the Morrigan.&quot;<br /> <br /> You also completely cut off most American characters for not only the Yoruba but the Shen, Kami, Aesir and Deva. All of these religions hold some numbers in various parts of the world. I don't want all of my characters to be spotted by their ethnic heritage.<br /> <br /> BTW the scion of Shango would be completely oblivious to his heritage, just like most black American characters. Learning that his dad is not only a god, but an African God, would be quite a shock, and learning what that meant would lead to (what I think would be) some damned interesting story. By your logic, even most African American characters wouldn't be worthy of yoruban Scionhood because they're oblivious to their Yoruban heritage... if they have any... do we need to do character family trees? How African does a character have to be? How Chinese?<br /> <br /> Is a Korean character unworthy of the Shen or Kami because someone might infer that Hachiman didn't know the difference between the Korean and Japanese people?<br /> <br /> What if Heimdall became fond of a black English incarnation and kept it even in the godrealm?<br /> <br /> I honestly have a problem with the idea that only the greeks and Egyptian (and maybe the aesir) got around the world. What? Eshu was too afraid to cross the sea? Susanoo controls all the seas but never went ashore in cape hope or Cape cod? Who cares what's overrepresented at a given table? My games are set in Louisiana and white characters are actually a minority despite their only being one black player at my table (unless kids are playing... but that's not OP games)<br /> <br /> when gods go into the world they take whatever form will draw the least amount of attention. if its uncomfortable to you that Eshu (sorry, i'm a fan) took up a blond haired blue eyed incarnation to make a play for a particularly spry Nordic coffee waitress that says more about you than the character with the concept.<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: I worry that this post comes off as angry or aggressive, it wasn't meant to be.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":256,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","user":"Gnomish American","date":". 09-17-2016, 10:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T19:28:47-07:00","id":971672,"title":"","content":"How would the scion handle someone like Asteria. In order to get away from Zeus' lust she ran across the sky, transformed into a quail then jumped into the ocean and became the island of Delos where her sister took refuge and gave birth to the twins. I can easily work out flying and shape shifting or Animal boons. Turning into the island is where I become baffled. High level earth boon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T19:40:53-07:00","id":971681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=971672#post971672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would the scion handle someone like Asteria. In order to get away from Zeus' lust she ran across the sky, transformed into a quail then jumped into the ocean and became the island of Delos where her sister took refuge and gave birth to the twins. I can easily work out flying and shape shifting or Animal boons. Turning into the island is where I become baffled. High level earth boon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm,maybe when a god create Terra incognita he can choose the become it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T20:10:19-07:00","id":971698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=971617#post971617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No offense taken. I'd rather over-think the issue of &quot;Urban Fantasy Scion&quot; vs. &quot;God's and Monsters Scion&quot;, than say nothing and feel like I should have spoken up. And my enthusiasm isn't curbed by wanting the game to be bigger and better than 1st edition. I'm eagerly waiting for the Kickstart along with everyone else here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds good to me. Is it Tuesday/Thursday yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T20:12:23-07:00","id":971702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=971672#post971672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would the scion handle someone like Asteria. In order to get away from Zeus' lust she ran across the sky, transformed into a quail then jumped into the ocean and became the island of Delos where her sister took refuge and gave birth to the twins. I can easily work out flying and shape shifting or Animal boons. Turning into the island is where I become baffled. High level earth boon?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Theoi's Signature Purview is all but turning into weird things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T20:14:01-07:00","id":971705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=971672#post971672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would the scion handle someone like Asteria. In order to get away from Zeus' lust she ran across the sky, transformed into a quail then jumped into the ocean and became the island of Delos where her sister took refuge and gave birth to the twins. I can easily work out flying and shape shifting or Animal boons. Turning into the island is where I become baffled. High level earth boon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Scions of the Theoi are all about changing shape of both yourself and others. Changing into a bird is probably within Hero level of things, but turning into an island seems like some serious mojo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T20:14:01-07:00","id":971706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=971672#post971672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would the scion handle someone like Asteria. In order to get away from Zeus' lust she ran across the sky, transformed into a quail then jumped into the ocean and became the island of Delos where her sister took refuge and gave birth to the twins. I can easily work out flying and shape shifting or Animal boons. Turning into the island is where I become baffled. High level earth boon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Scions of the Theoi are all about changing shape of both yourself and others. Changing into a bird is probably within Hero level of things, but turning into an island seems like some serious mojo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T20:20:39-07:00","id":971713,"title":"","content":"Also, adding my two cents on the &quot;Playing a Scion of a different race than the traditional worshippers&quot;<br /> <br /> First of all, I wouldn't put restrictions down, but I <i>would</i> talk it out with people. I mean, I can understand people raising eyebrows if a character is descended from one of the Orisha but the character is white as the winter snow. If a player said to me &quot;Alright I'd like to play a character descended from the Orisha&quot; I'd probably try to gently say &quot;Well considering that the Orisha are from this area and might emulate people from this area when they manifest, maybe your character would look biracial?&quot;<br /> <br /> And also, if a hypothetical player used &quot;My character's mother is a Deva&quot; as an excuse to talk like Apu from The Simpsons or embrace any other number of stereotypes, I wouldn't call that a problem with the <i>system</i>.<br /> <br /> I admit I'm probably not going to know a lot about many of these pantheons beyond what's written in the book. But I figure that the least I can do is treat them with a decent amount of respect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T20:35:10-07:00","id":971722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=971713#post971713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, adding my two cents on the &quot;Playing a Scion of a different race than the traditional worshippers&quot;<br /> <br /> First of all, I wouldn't put restrictions down, but I <i>would</i> talk it out with people. I mean, I can understand people raising eyebrows if a character is descended from one of the Orisha but the character is white as the winter snow. If a player said to me &quot;Alright I'd like to play a character descended from the Orisha&quot; I'd probably try to gently say &quot;Well considering that the Orisha are from this area and might emulate people from this area when they manifest, maybe your character would look biracial?&quot;<br /> <br /> And also, if a hypothetical player used &quot;My character's mother is a Deva&quot; as an excuse to talk like Apu from The Simpsons or embrace any other number of stereotypes, I wouldn't call that a problem with the <i>system</i>.<br /> <br /> I admit I'm probably not going to know a lot about many of these pantheons beyond what's written in the book. But I figure that the least I can do is treat them with a decent amount of respect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of my upset upthread was that the character was chosen to be a Scion of one of the Orisha not because of an interest in their myth but because the rules matched up nicely. If someone made a white Scion of an African Pantheon but bothered to have a reason why that's the case, I'd be less defensive, but doing it the way that was described would be distasteful for <i>any </i>god, especially one with as much possible baggage as there possibly is regarding the Yoruba people's relationship to white people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T21:40:04-07:00","id":971755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=971722#post971722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Part of my upset upthread was that the character was chosen to be a Scion of one of the Orisha not because of an interest in their myth but because the rules matched up nicely. If someone made a white Scion of an African Pantheon but bothered to have a reason why that's the case, I'd be less defensive, but doing it the way that was described would be distasteful for <i>any </i>god, especially one with as much possible baggage as there possibly is regarding the Yoruba people's relationship to white people.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI dunno. As someone how is of Yoruba descent I'd be more offended by the player that creates a white Scion of Shango god that comes across as a Mighty Whitey, or worse a Wigger, than a player that's just a powergamer that mostly avoids touchy racial issues. But that's just me. Powergamers that ignore the fluff and just try to find the most combat effective build for their character can be just as annoying for some people at the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T02:46:49-07:00","id":971849,"title":"","content":"Mostly what I wanted to get across... Well, like Neall said, I wouldn't say no... But if there's not a sidebar dedicated to it in the book, I'd tell a player I'm unsure of &quot;Remember, people used to believe in this, quite intensely. Some of these pantheons STILL have active worshippers. Just... Don't be a jerk about it, alright?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T10:35:23-07:00","id":971999,"title":"","content":"Take the Trojan War for example. Trojans were technically no greek, nonetheless greek gods involved themselves on both sides in this mythical conflict. Most gods will have no problem with the ethnicity of their &quot;love interests&quot;, at least way less than humans have nowadays. Zeus used to tackle anything that pleased his eyes and he took plenty of forms to begat his ladies (bull, silver rain) and he didn't care if those women were barbarians (mind non-greek speaker for ancient greek) or native greek citystate ones.<br /> To speak for gods and their habits is quite &quot;cultural apropriation&quot; itself, just on a way higher level. So everybody should cool down a bit and focus on the joy parts of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T11:58:45-07:00","id":972051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belisarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=971999#post971999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take the Trojan War for example. Trojans were technically no greek, nonetheless greek gods involved themselves on both sides in this mythical conflict. Most gods will have no problem with the ethnicity of their &quot;love interests&quot;, at least way less than humans have nowadays. Zeus used to tackle anything that pleased his eyes and he took plenty of forms to begat his ladies (bull, silver rain) and he didn't care if those women were barbarians (mind non-greek speaker for ancient greek) or native greek citystate ones.<br /> To speak for gods and their habits is quite &quot;cultural apropriation&quot; itself, just on a way higher level. So everybody should cool down a bit and focus on the joy parts of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me add to your point,we all gotta keep in mindthat the Chosen genesis is there for a reason. Gods Chose mortals to become full fledged scion because they want to use you on their agenda. If Quetzcoatl thinks a swiss guys could be of use in screwing up Tezcatlipoca day he wont' care the swiss guy is not descedent from the Mexica Empire. Not all gods are stuck in the past","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T14:50:53-07:00","id":972138,"title":"","content":"Having followed this line for a few postings, I came to a realization: Wow - this really raises the bigger issues of including ANY pantheon that represents an existing culture, doesn't it? First Nations North America, Australian Aboriginal, Maori, Pacific Islander, Chinese, Japanese, Hindu/Sikh, Mayan, Muslim...essentially, what is being said here [&quot;be careful that you only play something that you can approach with sensitivity and knowledge, especially if you aren't of the appropriate racial/cultural background&quot;] would make it really tough for the game to include pretty much anything that is still worshiped in our real world. What does that leave us with? Only religions that are extinct, because you can't screw up playing a Scion of Osiris, Frigga, Taranis, or Anat, since no-one can say you're doing it wrong.<br /> I'm not sure if this is progressive cultural sensitivity, or taking a <i>game</i> and making it into something it isn't. No, don't play racial or cultural stereotypes that are offensive to the others in your group - but that's a general rule for all gaming, isn't it? Don't include rape, abuse, drug use, suicide, extreme violence, or anything that would upset the people you are gaming with. But I'd be leery of saying &quot;People really shouldn't play Orisha Scions, or Shen ones, or Inue ones, unless they belong to those groups, because that's inappropriate/offensive&quot;, because that might seriously limit any creativity or variety in the group and game. After all - is the GM going to ensure that they themselves are only playing NPCs of other faiths with the appropriate consideration? How far do we take this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5627,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","user":"Purple Snit","date":". 09-18-2016, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T15:03:45-07:00","id":972145,"title":"","content":"I am half germanic, half greek with a tad roman. So you could say I represent from Thor to Odin to Zeus to Jupiter quite some Pantheons. My children are half asian (because of their mother) so I could adopt the japanese pantheon in their name as well, Amaterasu be my guide. I invite every asian/african/native american player to culturaly appropriate Thor with non european chars as they see fit, a hurray to diversity I say.<br /> In one of my games we have an african player who enjoys playing a chalk white aquilonian and I say, yay, go for it. Why should he be limited to play chars from the dark kingdoms south of Stygia? RP is escapism, you slip into any possible shell you like, that is the beauty of roleplay. <br /> <br /> Just one final example to prove that limiting Scions of Gods to the ethnicity of their pantheons of origin, where ancient romans adopted gods from other people, even other continents.<br /> - Bubona: celticic<br /> - Endovelicus: iberian celtic<br /> - Isis: egyptian and thus african<br /> - Mithras: persian and thus asian<br /> - Serapis: egyptian and thus another african<br /> - Sol Invictus: syrian and thus another asian<br /> just to name a view. Then why shouldn't a north african not revere Mars for example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T15:06:41-07:00","id":972147,"title":"","content":"Nowhere in any of my posts did I say &quot;don't play a Scion of a culture you're not from yourself.&quot; I was simply just asking that people be respectful of still-living belief structures and highlighted why I'd personally be skeptical of a white Orisha Scion at my own table.<br /> <br /> And none of this is questions for Neal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T15:15:46-07:00","id":972151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=972147#post972147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nowhere in any of my posts did I say &quot;don't play a Scion of a culture you're not from yourself.&quot; I was simply just asking that people be respectful of still-living belief structures and highlighted why I'd personally be skeptical of a white Orisha Scion at my own table.<br /> <br /> And none of this is questions for Neal.</div> </div> </div> </div>By no means did I refer to your posts, it was a general statement. I do believe that everybody can make up their own minds and have their own decision in their sessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T16:23:45-07:00","id":972191,"title":"","content":"Question for Neal: when a Hero becomes a Demigod, what changes? Other than \u201cLegend increases\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T16:40:50-07:00","id":972200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=972191#post972191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question for Neal: when a Hero becomes a Demigod, what changes? Other than \u201cLegend increases\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanically, doesn't their target number lower?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T16:40:50-07:00","id":972201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=972191#post972191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question for Neal: when a Hero becomes a Demigod, what changes? Other than \u201cLegend increases\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanically, doesn't their target number lower?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T17:35:20-07:00","id":972229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=971553#post971553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm not sure how comfortable I would be at someone at my table playing a character whose ethnic background doesn't match up with any Pantheon that still has existing modern worship; there are very few priests of Anpu to offend, but there are plenty of Hindus out there. That goes doubly so for closed cultures like the Native American Pantheons, as they're essentially a closed culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>By no means am I saying your opinion is invalid, but I've played many games where people played priests, or christian angels, or other figures in Christianity, and I don't really see it as much different. Certainly could be done in a racist way, but may not be necessarily racist in and of itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12349-evilnerf","name":"evilnerf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12349_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T18:06:33-07:00","id":972247,"title":"","content":"Do scions get some kind of bonus when they act according to their Virtues? Since Theoi have Storge and Egotism,Do they have a Easier time using their powers to protect family members? Or to make themselves famous?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T08:55:59-07:00","id":972554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=971646#post971646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not going to tell anyone what to play at their table, but this topic is something we're addressing head-on in the book.<br /> <br /> I can say that the art, or at the very least my art notes, is definitely going to reflect a lot of diversity in the World.</div> </div> </div> </div>If exalted has show us anything, sometimes even specific art notes aren't enough to get artists to actually draw diverse characters lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:28:10-07:00","id":972718,"title":"","content":"I figure pantheons vary a great deal in their relationship to race.<br /> <br /> Some like the Aesir are barely aware of it as a concept (Vikings after all spread their seed and took wives and &quot;wives&quot; from all over the known world.... Also the Aesir having no relationship to whiteness and multi-racial Scions is a nice fuck-you to white-power Odinists).<br /> <br /> The Orisha an Loa on the other hand went through the Middle Passage and from that are inseparably linked to black experience, making it VERY rare to take lovers or pick Chosen from outside that experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-19-2016, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:35:27-07:00","id":972727,"title":"","content":"I want to thank everyone in this thread for having a surprisingly reasonable good-faith discussion of a really messy topic. I might make a separate thread to talk about this subject, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:52:53-07:00","id":972747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=972554#post972554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If exalted has show us anything, sometimes even specific art notes aren't enough to get artists to actually draw diverse characters lol</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just Exalted. I should see if I can dig up the horror stories of writers yelling at artists after &quot;racially diverse elves&quot; came back Caucasian, blue, and green.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T15:47:41-07:00","id":972787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=972718#post972718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figure pantheons vary a great deal in their relationship to race.<br /> <br /> Some like the Aesir are barely aware of it as a concept (Vikings after all spread their seed and took wives and &quot;wives&quot; from all over the known world.... Also the Aesir having no relationship to whiteness and multi-racial Scions is a nice fuck-you to white-power Odinists).<br /> <br /> The Orisha an Loa on the other hand went through the Middle Passage and from that are inseparably linked to black experience, making it VERY rare to take lovers or pick Chosen from outside that experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>But wouldn't it also be fair to say at least some of those gods might empathize with downtrodden groups that aren't descended from black slaves? Native Americans, Refugees, holocaust survivors, Irish during the 80s (Assuming the Tuatha didn\u2019t mind).<br /> <br /> More tied to an archetype than a specific race if that makes sense. Not saying if a group feels uncomfortable they should do that, but it does widen the possibilities without ignoring the important parts of a pantheons themes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","user":"vonpenguin","date":". 09-19-2016, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T17:10:38-07:00","id":972830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=972787#post972787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But wouldn't it also be fair to say at least some of those gods might empathize with downtrodden groups that aren't descended from black slaves? Native Americans, Refugees, holocaust survivors, Irish during the 80s (Assuming the Tuatha didn\u2019t mind).<br /> <br /> More tied to an archetype than a specific race if that makes sense. Not saying if a group feels uncomfortable they should do that, but it does widen the possibilities without ignoring the important parts of a pantheons themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they aren't the gods of the downtrodden, they're the gods of the Yoruba people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T17:41:26-07:00","id":972842,"title":"","content":"It was mentioned earlier the idea that Eshu-Elegba being the great traveller that he is, it should in theory fit his character to have kids all over the world with mothers of diverse races. That said, I think that was much more common before the middle passage than after, and I would certainly portray any children of his from non-black mothers as interracial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-20-2016, 01:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T19:45:02-07:00","id":972889,"title":"","content":"While a good discussion, I would still like to point out that nothing said here needs to dictate another person's game.<br /> <br /> If you see no issue with the Orisha choosing a Caucasian Scion, I wish you the best. If you are investing the time to make sure that the Scions match their Pantheon by whatever measure you choose, rock on.<br /> <br /> We play these games to tell stories and have fun. Let's not lose sight of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T00:45:22-07:00","id":972983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=972889#post972889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While a good discussion, I would still like to point out that nothing said here needs to dictate another person's game.<br /> <br /> If you see no issue with the Orisha choosing a Caucasian Scion, I wish you the best. If you are investing the time to make sure that the Scions match their Pantheon by whatever measure you choose, rock on.<br /> <br /> We play these games to tell stories and have fun. Let's not lose sight of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I second that *thumbs up*<br /> Egyptian gods had animal heads, would be funy to play a human Scion with a poodle head, though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T03:45:31-07:00","id":973023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=972842#post972842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was mentioned earlier the idea that Eshu-Elegba being the great traveller that he is, it should in theory fit his character to have kids all over the world with mothers of diverse races. That said, I think that was much more common before the middle passage than after, and I would certainly portray any children of his from non-black mothers as interracial.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that's fair there are plenty of biracial people that heavily take after one parent. I've even seen a picture around the net of two little girls who are twins and have the same hair, nose, eyes, et all except one is pale and blonde and the other has incredibly dark skin and hair.<br /> <br /> Which is just a long way of saying, play what you like, just make sure you have some kind of reasoning behind it that your group can swallow.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T05:38:28-07:00","id":973061,"title":"","content":"Just read some of the open development stuff, this really looks good Man! Neall you really put together some amazing stuff, I am officially excited for the kickstarter this week!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T07:13:39-07:00","id":973117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=957786#post957786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fertility, Fortune, and Prosperity have some conceptual overlap. Fortune is more about conceptual good luck on an individual level, while Prosperity is more about material and cultural wealth on a societal level.</div> </div> </div> </div>wait. does this mean I cold feasibly make Tyche/fortuna and nemesis? cause I would love to have them appear in games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","name":"Grimangel53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T12:23:39-07:00","id":973288,"title":"","content":"If they aren't already in the pantheon, evidently the number of Gods per Pantheon is quite higher this time around.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T13:11:32-07:00","id":973335,"title":"","content":"Also I'm as sure as I can be that the lists in the book won't be MEANT to be exhaustive. They're just the most well-known heavy hitters. A full list of every active deity of a given Pantheon would probably go on into the hundreds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T13:19:11-07:00","id":973343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=973335#post973335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I'm as sure as I can be that the lists in the book won't be MEANT to be exhaustive. They're just the most well-known heavy hitters. A full list of every active deity of a given Pantheon would probably go on into the hundreds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention,it'd be hard to assign Callings to a less well know god,without many tales to reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T13:19:11-07:00","id":973344,"title":"","content":"I'd give Fortuna Judge/Liminal/Guardian myself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T15:14:29-07:00","id":973423,"title":"","content":"Is it possible for a Scion to be unaware who their divine 'parent' actually is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T15:58:19-07:00","id":973457,"title":"","content":"Some people love statting up dozens and dozens of gods, though. One thing I'm really looking forward to, and excited about, is how this place is going to light up like a Christmas tree with post after post after the game comes out, as everyone excitedly posts their own takes on things, stats for things that didn't make the books, and thoughts on setting. It's one of the things that I truly do enjoy about this particular forum; the willingness for the fanbase to have those conversations. We've covered everything, in past times, ranging from the ethics of shapeshifting and and using one's Social epics in seduction to where does the Christian God fit in to things, to issues of race and culture, and while some of those conversations may have gotten a little passionate for the most part it has all been good, respectful, and useful dialogue.<br /> <br /> I honestly can't wait to see what everyone here makes of, and does with, this new edition <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T16:14:15-07:00","id":973467,"title":"","content":"My family tree looks like the registry at Ellis Island. As the only Multi-ethnic American in an otherwise white gaming group, I sometimes joke about having first dibs on playing Loa Scions in stories where everyone is from a different Pantheon. Likewise, one of the other players is a third generation Norwegian immigrant, and gets first dibs on Aesir. But really, it doesn't matter much; just don't be a vulgar stereotype of a culture you aren't part of and there shouldn't be a problem.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, while the Orishas may prefer to prioritize the decedents of their original worshipers, Loa worship is common in several areas of the Western Hemisphere, including New Orleans,(N'awlins, to the locals) Miami, Haiti, Cuba, and parts of Mexico. That includes white and Hispanic people. Chango/Shango is a big part of Santeria. To say that the Orishas would ignore so many people calling on their names...<br /> <br /> BTW, my Indian friends find my Apu impression hilarious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 09-21-2016, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T16:34:50-07:00","id":973481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=972718#post972718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figure pantheons vary a great deal in their relationship to race.<br /> <br /> Some like the Aesir are barely aware of it as a concept (Vikings after all spread their seed and took wives and &quot;wives&quot; from all over the known world.... Also the Aesir having no relationship to whiteness and multi-racial Scions is a nice fuck-you to white-power Odinists).<br /> <br /> The Orisha an Loa on the other hand went through the Middle Passage and from that are inseparably linked to black experience, making it VERY rare to take lovers or pick Chosen from outside that experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Re: \u00f2r\u00ecs\u0323\u00e0 and loa: You'd think so, wouldn't you? But they have their own internal complications related to ethnicity. First off, between 90% and 99% of their original kidnapped followers' New World descendants have at least a little non-African ancestry, for both good and really bad reasons. Second, some of the \u00f2r\u00ec\u1e63\u00e0 literally disguised themselves as other races in reaction to slavery's vicissitudes. They had many good reasons for doing so, most of them survival-related, but the results are still a little weird.<br /> <br /> First, let's Google Image Search Oshun (aka \u00d2\u0323\u1e63un). Did you notice how most of the pictures of her have long, straight hair? In fact, in one story (I think from Cuba), \u00d2\u0323\u1e63un, realizing what the Middle Passage is going to do to beauty standards, asks Yem\u1ecdja to give her pale skin and long blonde hair.<br /> <br /> Next, let's do the same for Oxossi (that's the Brazilian spelling for <span style=\"font-family:arial\">O\u1e63\u00f3ss\u00ed). You'll see a lot of bows and arrows, which have been an Oxossi signifier from the start. But \u2026 the jaguar skin and feather headdress? Why is he dressed like </span>Mot\u0113cuhz\u014dma?<br /> <br /> \u00d2\u0323\u1e63un is associated with beauty, and she sometimes appears in the Caribbean as a blonde white woman. O\u1e63\u00f3ss\u00ed is associated with bows, forests, and hunting, and he sometimes appears in Brazil as a Native American from Mexico. From a 2016 perspective, those changes are \u2026 confusing, to put it lightly. I'm still processing what they mean, and what they mean for Scion. Maybe I always will be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T16:59:11-07:00","id":973500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimangel53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=973117#post973117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> wait. does this mean I cold feasibly make Tyche/fortuna and nemesis? cause I would love to have them appear in games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adding new gods to existing pantheons is really really really easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T18:38:03-07:00","id":973560,"title":"","content":"Is Yem\u1ecdja the one known as Iemanj\u00e1 here in Brazil?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T18:45:57-07:00","id":973568,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T19:10:31-07:00","id":973583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=973560#post973560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Yem\u1ecdja the one known as Iemanj\u00e1 here in Brazil?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the one. There's a mosaic of her at my subway stop here in Harlem, New York, and another of \u1e62\u00e0ng\u00f3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T21:48:31-07:00","id":973650,"title":"","content":"First, I just want to thank you Neall for taking the time to answer all of these questions. So I apologize if this has been asked and answered already but was there any reason that made you choose to keep Aaron, Eric, and Annie X around in terms of pregen characters from the first edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/601-dioscuri","name":"Dioscuri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T00:01:13-07:00","id":973700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dioscuri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=973650#post973650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, I just want to thank you Neall for taking the time to answer all of these questions. So I apologize if this has been asked and answered already but was there any reason that made you choose to keep Aaron, Eric, and Annie X around in terms of pregen characters from the first edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>For Aaron and Eric, at least, it was because Neall thought they were the most interesting 1e pregens. (Brigitte too, but I imagine she'll show up if/when we hit the Loa stretch goal.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T00:12:21-07:00","id":973704,"title":"","content":"As someone who didn't play 1e I apologize if this question is dumb, but how does Scion handles ghosts, the underworld, and the afterlife? Is death still a mystery in The World or is there a place you can visit the dead - and is that one underworld with various areas divvied up by Pantheon, or are Mictlan and Duat and Hades all floating in the aether somewhere unrelated to each other?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T00:57:36-07:00","id":973711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=973704#post973704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who didn't play 1e I apologize if this question is dumb, but how does Scion handles ghosts, the underworld, and the afterlife? Is death still a mystery in The World or is there a place you can visit the dead - and is that one underworld with various areas divvied up by Pantheon, or are Mictlan and Duat and Hades all floating in the aether somewhere unrelated to each other?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e, it was somewhere between 'one underworld divvied up' and 'unrelated' - the pantheons' Underworlds existed on the same plane, metaphysically attached to the Titans' prison. When the Titans escaped, it sent the Underworlds into chaos.<br /> <br /> You could visit a pantheon's Underworld if you were a member of the pantheon, a child of a god with the Death Purview, had learned the Death Purview yourself, or a passenger with one of the others. Passages to an Underworld could include tombs &amp; funerary architecture, natural features, rituals and times associated with a culture's death practices.<br /> <br /> Not least because of the Shen and Devas, reincarnation is a thing in the World (this was pre-Incarnate Scions).<br /> <br /> I suspect the Underworld's going to see a few changes in 2e, thanks to the reimagining of the Titans if nothing else. Neall's mentioned an Underworld is effectively prime real estate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T01:05:21-07:00","id":973712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=973704#post973704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who didn't play 1e I apologize if this question is dumb, but how does Scion handles ghosts, the underworld, and the afterlife? Is death still a mystery in The World or is there a place you can visit the dead - and is that one underworld with various areas divvied up by Pantheon, or are Mictlan and Duat and Hades all floating in the aether somewhere unrelated to each other?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1E the Underworld has distinct domains ruled by different gods of the dead, but said afterlives are part of the same metaphysical plane. It is theoretically possible, but difficult, to move between them directly. Obviously the Death and Psychopomp purviews help.<br /> <br /> But yes, the underworld is definitely accessible and a central part of the setting. Too much mythology would have to be cut out for it not to be.<br /> <br /> Edit: to be more specific, in 1st edition, the Underword was introduced as a playable setting in the Demigod book, with rules for accessing it and the associated realms for each core Pantheon. Similarly, the Overworld, with the heavenly Godrealms of each core Pantheon, and the Titanrealms laying siege to them were introduced as playable settings in the God book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-21-2016, 04:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T11:56:24-07:00","id":973959,"title":"","content":"In 1e each pantheon had their own Underworld, though they were all sort of connected to each other and psychopomps or death gods could pretty much get into any Underworld, not just their own. I think some dead went to the realms of the gods that governed their afterlives, though -- I don't recall, but I think Tlaloc took the drowned to his own godrealm in the Overworld rather than somewhere in Mictlan.<br /> Also, Tartarus is a part in the deepest Underworld that the Titans got sent to, and when myth says a Titan was killed (with the exception of Ymir) it's just a poetic way of saying they were sent there. The actual death of Ymir turned the Ice Age into the Great Flood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T14:35:43-07:00","id":974034,"title":"","content":"Hmmm question about the KS itself: Any chance it will be up before 2pm new york time? (would be 8 pm my local time at that time)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"dat