d":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 09-22-2016, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T12:09:17-07:00","id":974579,"title":"","content":"Will there be rules for two gods getting together and having a kid? Like say Zeus and Hera or say Hercules and Freya?<br /> <br /> I've always wondered about the mechanics (not the politics...because I'm sure they would be there) between cross pantheon romances and their inevitable outcomes and say Zeus just said..&quot;I'm never giving the throne to Ares or Heph...need to start from scratch and he chooses Hera so there won't be years of her hunting down and attempting to kill the mother and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T13:12:06-07:00","id":974627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=974579#post974579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will there be rules for two gods getting together and having a kid? Like say Zeus and Hera or say Hercules and Freya?<br /> <br /> I've always wondered about the mechanics (not the politics...because I'm sure they would be there) between cross pantheon romances and their inevitable outcomes and say Zeus just said..&amp;quot;I'm never giving the throne to Ares or Heph...need to start from scratch and he chooses Hera so there won't be years of her hunting down and attempting to kill the mother and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the product of two gods would be a god so you may have to wait until the God book to get more information about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T15:49:56-07:00","id":974705,"title":"","content":"Will Hero/Origin have rules for playing Non-Humans, Like Dwarves, Nymphs, Spartoi .etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2448-dante","name":"Dante","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T15:51:46-07:00","id":974707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=974705#post974705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will Hero/Origin have rules for playing Non-Humans, Like Dwarves, Nymphs, Spartoi .etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Fauns, kitsune, and the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T17:15:25-07:00","id":974766,"title":"","content":"Are we going to get the rest of the base rules? The Social and Mental sets, or are we going to have to wait until May?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T06:20:23-07:00","id":975020,"title":"","content":"Okay, I'm thinking my ability to read is broken but what exactly is the Enhancement bonus for weapons? I'm assuming there is one otherwise... knuckledusters are a little redundant.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=974707#post974707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Fauns, kitsune, and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bWhat about one direction fans and pumpkin spice drinkers?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T06:42:34-07:00","id":975028,"title":"","content":"Knuckle dusters could very well just be something intended for origin level stuff. Maybe mortals or default things have negatives when fighting unarmed. If not, then claws are also super redundant with the lycanthropes as well. Although they would reasonably be lethal unarmed strikes instead of bashing.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Id probably give a person who fights unarmed the grapple tag as well. Easier to grab someone with open hands than while wearing knuckledusters or a similar equivalent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 09-23-2016, 09:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T10:05:28-07:00","id":975105,"title":"","content":"Are Callings locked to your divine parent or can you choose the one you want?<br /> <br /> Always found strange that a scion has to follow some footsteps of their father/mother. Even if gods of the same family clearly dont and they usually have different powers/domains.<br /> <br /> Ares being mostly a warrior and being son of Zeus and Hera (Both dont give the warrior calling) is a example of this.<br /> <br /> Of course &quot;He is a god&quot; would be a good answer, but it feels a bit cheap, considering that callings are supposed to be a big part of character creation.<br /> <br /> Anyway, not 100% sure with the system preview, but the rest of the fluff is great. keep the good work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12264-isengrim","name":"Isengrim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T10:20:50-07:00","id":975112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isengrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=975105#post975105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Callings locked to your divine parent or can you choose the one you want?<br /> <br /> Always found strange that a scion has to follow some footsteps of their father/mother. Even if gods of the same family clearly dont and they usually have different powers/domains.<br /> <br /> Ares being mostly a warrior and being son of Zeus and Hera (Both dont give the warrior calling) is a example of this.<br /> <br /> Of course &quot;He is a god&quot; would be a good answer, but it feels a bit cheap, considering that callings are supposed to be a big part of character creation.<br /> <br /> Anyway, not 100% sure with the system preview, but the rest of the fluff is great. keep the good work.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If I remember correctly, only one of your calings has to be shared with your parent. The other two can be whatever you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9296-zeldafan42","name":"Zeldafan42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9296_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T10:31:47-07:00","id":975113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeldafan42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=975112#post975112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I remember correctly, only one of your calings has to be shared with your parent. The other two can be whatever you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>So long as they match your Paths, anyway.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T11:18:42-07:00","id":975135,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Does the quickstart typically come out before the full book? If so, how long before?</div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T12:02:30-07:00","id":975152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notanautomaton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=975135#post975135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Does the quickstart typically come out before the full book? If so, how long before?</div></div> </div> </div> </div>I believe they usually come out after. It's basically an adventure module with some pre made characters, but because it is a stretch goal, it is not the focus of the project and therefore is not focused on until that is done. At least that's how it's happened with EX3, they may mix it up this time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T12:09:37-07:00","id":975156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notanautomaton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=975135#post975135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Does the quickstart typically come out before the full book? If so, how long before?</div></div> </div> </div> </div>For Demon: the Descent, I believe the Quickstart came out well before the main book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T12:25:25-07:00","id":975166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=975156#post975156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For Demon: the Descent, I believe the Quickstart came out well before the main book.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bThat's how I remember it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T12:52:50-07:00","id":975179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=975156#post975156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For Demon: the Descent, I believe the Quickstart came out well before the main book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm familiar with the Ex3 Deluxe kickstarter, where IIRC the Quickstart <i>still</i> isn't out.<br /> <br /> But, well, even fans of Ex3 will admit that mistakes were made with that Kickstarter.<br /> <br /> (I probably shouldn't keep going to Ex3's kickstarter as an example but I'm working off a sample size of one. For all I know the other Onyx Path kickstarters have gone much smoother)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T13:08:40-07:00","id":975188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=975156#post975156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For Demon: the Descent, I believe the Quickstart came out well before the main book.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, the Exalted Quickstart is still not out.<br /> <br /> Edit: but yes, the Ex3 kick starter is an outlier compared to most OP kickstarters. There have been normal delays here and there for others, but nothing comparable to Ex3, where they straight up did the kickstarter too early (and they learned from that mistake, the Deagon-Blooded kickstarter won't happen until the text is DONE, and they're sure they aren't throwing out their mechanical assumptions to start over from scratch 2 more times)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-23-2016, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T16:56:19-07:00","id":975280,"title":"","content":"(crossposting for this here and on rpg-net)<br /> <br /> I eagerly became a Scion-level backer, but I have a question that is rather essential to my enjoyment and interest in the game. As an ironclad rule of my playstyle across any RPG, I downright loathe my characters' 'magical' abilities and powers being dependent on any physical tools. I can only accept them as amplifiers for exceptional feats or enablers for specialized tricks, never as gates or prerequisites for 'ordinary' or 'common' abilities or powers. My default character absolutely need be able to use at least 80-90% of the 'magic' stuff on their sheet even if they are thrown naked into an empty cell. As a consequence, hyper-reliance on Relics to access Purviews was a most serious stumbling bloc to my enjoyment of Scion 1st ed. and one I was only able to bypass to my satisfaction by making all the Relics of my characters that were needed to tap the Purviews of the kind that could not really be stolen, destroyed, or lost short of mutilating the character: tattooes, magitech cybernetics, body enchantments, and the like (obviously I was a big fan of the Ragnarok rules for maimings acting as Relics). If a Relic is necessary to enhance the character's fighting prowess, their other skills, or provide some exceptional ability neither Knacks nor Boons can duplicate, it is all good they are shaped like objects that need be wielded or worn and can be stolen or lost; in such a case, it is proper they look and work like weapons or tools. But to access the character's Knacks, Boons, and Purviews, Relics need not be necessary at all, or at the very least of the kind the character cannot stolen or lost short of some serious surgery. This is a not-negotiable playstyle issue for me, no matter how the alternative may be (made to look) cool or in-theme. Can anyone tell if and how Scion 2 ed. is going to be any different in this regard ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 09-23-2016, 08:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T17:01:42-07:00","id":975284,"title":"","content":"Hey Neall, are Edges still a thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T17:07:42-07:00","id":975286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=975280#post975280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I eagerly became a Scion-level backer, but I have a question that is rather essential to my enjoyment and interest in the game. As an ironclad rule of my playstyle across any RPG, I downright loathe my characters' 'magical' abilities and powers being dependent on any physical tools. I can only accept them as amplifiers for exceptional feats or enablers for specialized tricks, never as gates or prerequisites for 'ordinary' or 'common' abilities or powers. My default character absolutely need be able to use at least 80-90% of the 'magic' stuff on their sheet even if they are thrown naked into an empty cell. As a consequence, hyper-reliance on Relics to access Purviews was a most serious stumbling bloc to my enjoyment of Scion 1st ed. and one I was only able to bypass to my satisfaction by making all the Relics of my characters that were needed to tap the Purviews of the kind that could not really be stolen, destroyed, or lost short of mutilating the character: tattooes, magitech cybernetics, body enchantments, and the like (obviously I was a big fan of the Ragnarok rules for maimings acting as Relics). If a Relic is necessary to enhance the character's fighting prowess, their other skills, or provide some exceptional ability neither Knacks nor Boons can duplicate, it is all good they are shaped like weapons or tools that need be wielded or worn and cannot be stolen or lost; in such a case, it is proper they look and work like weapons or tools. But to access the character's Knacks, Boons, and Purviews, relics need not be necessary at all, or at the very least of the kind the character cannot lose short of some serious surgery. This is a not-negotiable playstyle issue for me, no matter how the alternative may be (made to look) cool or in-theme. Can anyone tell if and how Scion 2 ed. is going to be any different in this regard ?</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I remember reading earlier in this thread, Relic reliance for boons is still a thing, except for I think your favored purview or the one you inherit from your parent. Something like that. But that may have changed or I remember it wrong. I don't remember if Miracles are going to be Relic dependent though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T17:10:31-07:00","id":975289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=975280#post975280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I eagerly became a Scion-level backer, but I have a question that is rather essential to my enjoyment and interest in the game. As an ironclad rule of my playstyle across any RPG, I downright loathe my characters' 'magical' abilities and powers being dependent on any physical tools. I can only accept them as amplifiers for exceptional feats or enablers for specialized tricks, never as gates or prerequisites for 'ordinary' or 'common' abilities or powers. My default character absolutely need be able to use at least 80-90% of the 'magic' stuff on their sheet even if they are thrown naked into an empty cell. As a consequence, hyper-reliance on Relics to access Purviews was a most serious stumbling bloc to my enjoyment of Scion 1st ed. and one I was only able to bypass to my satisfaction by making all the Relics of my characters that were needed to tap the Purviews of the kind that could not really be stolen, destroyed, or lost short of mutilating the character: tattooes, magitech cybernetics, body enchantments, and the like (obviously I was a big fan of the Ragnarok rules for maimings acting as Relics). If a Relic is necessary to enhance the character's fighting prowess, their other skills, or provide some exceptional ability neither Knacks nor Boons can duplicate, it is all good they are shaped like weapons or tools that need be wielded or worn and cannot be stolen or lost; in such a case, it is proper they look and work like weapons or tools. But to access the character's Knacks, Boons, and Purviews, relics need not be necessary at all, or at the very least of the kind the character cannot lose short of some serious surgery. This is a not-negotiable playstyle issue for me, no matter how the alternative may be (made to look) cool or in-theme. Can anyone tell if and how Scion 2 ed. is going to be any different in this regard ?</div> </div> </div> </div>You get one of your parent's Purviews innately, without needing to channel it through a Relic, out of character creation. The same goes for your Pantheon's Signature Virtue. <br /> <br /> Subtle, unobtrusive, hard-to-lose artifacts are pretty easy to design with the Relic system. Alternatively, you can gain access to Purviews through a divine Guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T17:21:07-07:00","id":975294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=975289#post975289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You get one of your parent's Purviews innately, without needing to channel it through a Relic, out of character creation. The same goes for your Pantheon's Signature Virtue.<br /> <br /> Subtle, unobtrusive, hard-to-lose artifacts are pretty easy to design with the Relic system. Alternatively, you can gain access to Purviews through a divine Guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, then I suppose it is going to be the usual way, and all PC of mine shall keep being huge fans of enchanted body art to access any Purview of theirs. If there are going to be official rules that make this easy and Guides provide an alternative for variety, it is good enough. I am puzzled, however, what Signature Virtue has to do with Purviews at all. Did you mean the Pantheon's signature Purview ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 09-23-2016, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-i