e":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T22:10:24-07:00","id":977599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=977593#post977593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Update: I'm still grouchy about the Hathor/Aset merger.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI have to agree.<br /> <br /> \u200bSekhmet/Bastet is at least somewhat understandable. But Hathor and Aset have no connection that I'm aware of. That one just makes no sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T23:22:40-07:00","id":977623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=977599#post977599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI have to agree.<br /> <br /> \u200bSekhmet/Bastet is at least somewhat understandable. But Hathor and Aset have no connection that I'm aware of. That one just makes no sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>The best I can imagine is that they're both technically mothers, but Hathor is really big on that role whereas Aset only really comes at that through being a wife; I've always seen her as more of a magic goddess.<br /> <br /> Which is why I wrote up Sekhmet, Hathor, and also Hecate <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/977621-a-handful-of-missing-goddesses-fan-made-2e\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T23:28:27-07:00","id":977627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=977599#post977599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bSekhmet/Bastet is at least somewhat understandable. But Hathor and Aset have no connection that I'm aware of. That one just makes no sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>It actually happened.<br /> <br /> At first Hathor-Sekhmet was an Ishtar figure, both sexy femininity and dangerous violence.<br /> Eventually as the years rolled on, Hathor got tamer and tamer until she was a wholesome mother figure.<br /> Then she started getting syncretized together with Aset as mother figures.<br /> <br /> But Aset is much more interesting by herself, and Hathor-Sekhmet is the one everyone is familiar with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","user":"Incendax","date":". 09-28-2016, 03:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T23:58:01-07:00","id":977639,"title":"","content":"How I'm inclined to divide things at my table...<br /> <br /> Aset as the queen, goddess of magic, goddess of family bonds (including dynastic authority), and uplifter of the downtrodden; she is daughter of Keb and Nut, wife of Azar, and mother of Heru.<br /> <br /> Hathor/Sekhmet as the fertility figure and war goddess of creation and destruction, not unlike Ishtar, but more divided in her duality, actually split between two mantles; daughter of Neith and Khnum (who is himself the Evening Mantle of Re, but like Khepri [dawn] separate enough to operate as his own god) wife of Heru, and mother of the four sons of Heru<br /> <br /> Bastet as the agent of Re in the darkness. While Sekhmet is his glorious warrior &quot;Eye&quot; in daylight, Bastet is the &quot;Eye&quot; that stalks the night and protects the will of Re where his light does not shine. She is more guardian and assassin than the direct warrior Sekhmet. Her exact origins are ambiguous, as some recall her as a mantle of Sekhmet, and being more lion than the cat she is now. Perhaps a Scion grew powerful enough to take one of their mother's names for themself?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T00:00:39-07:00","id":977640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=977639#post977639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How I'm inclined to divide things at my table...<br /> <br /> Aset as the queen, goddess of magic, goddess of family bonds (including dynastic authority), and uplifter of the downtrodden; she is daughter of Keb and Nut, wife of Azar, and mother of Heru.<br /> <br /> Hathor/Sekhmet as the fertility figure and war goddess of creation and destruction, not unlike Ishtar, but more divided in her duality, actually split between two mantles; daughter of Neith and Khnum (who is himself the Evening Mantle of Re, but like Khepri [dawn] separate enough to operate as his own god) wife of Heru, and mother of the four sons of Heru<br /> <br /> Bastet as the agent of Re in the darkness. While Sekhmet is his glorious warrior &amp;quot;Eye&amp;quot; in daylight, Bastet is the &amp;quot;Eye&amp;quot; that stalks the night and protects the will of Re where his light does not shine. She is more guardian and assassin than the direct warrior Sekhmet. Her exact origins are ambiguous, as some recall her as a mantle of Sekhmet, and being more lion than the cat she is now. Perhaps a Scion grew powerful enough to take one of their mother's names for themself?</div> </div> </div> </div>See, this merger I like quite a bit. I wonder if it's too late to have this approach in the book instead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T00:16:31-07:00","id":977646,"title":"","content":"Do we know if Nephthys is in? She is one of the nine gods of the Ennead of Heliopolis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T01:53:47-07:00","id":977664,"title":"","content":"While the Norse and the Greeks to a slightly lesser extent are there any pantheon who could be said to have made a deal with Fate that seems positive and puts them somewhat apart from the other pantheons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T03:53:20-07:00","id":977680,"title":"","content":"Can you reveal any secrets of the character progression system, other than the fact that it doesn't work like in Storyteller(ing)?<br /> <br /> Also: The fact that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/605-revlid\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar605_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"605\" data-vbnamecard=\"605\">Revlid</a> writes for Scion makes me feel warm and happy inside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T06:01:17-07:00","id":977715,"title":"","content":"Which mechanical benefits do Scions get for following their Virtues?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T06:21:19-07:00","id":977722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=977680#post977680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you reveal any secrets of the character progression system, other than the fact that it doesn't work like in Storyteller(ing)?<br /> <br /> Also: The fact that <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> writes for Scion makes me feel warm and happy inside.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great for Revlid. When was this announced?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T06:46:08-07:00","id":977732,"title":"","content":"Since Scions can get a supernatural being as their other parent (and their Origin Path), such beings are prime material for Guides, and in many Pantheons the demarcation between minor Gods and major supernatural beings is blurred, I'm thinking about various possible iterations of a classical changeling fantasy as the groundwork of a broad character concept. This Scion had a God(dess) as parent and a major supernatural being as the other parent and Guide. The character was given to adoption by mortal foster parents at birth for various possible reasons and is unaware of their own true nature and heritage till Visitation, although they sport a mystical birthmark (body art Relic). How much supernatural and how much mortal would such a character be before and after Visitation ? I assume the post-Visitation family dynamic between the Scion, God daddy, and Guide mommy (or vice versa) would be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T07:45:33-07:00","id":977759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=976203#post976203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Callings:<br /> Creator, Guardian, Healer, Hunter, Judge, Leader, Liminal, Lover, Sage, Trickster, Warrior<br /> <br /> Purviews:<br /> Artistry, Beasts, Chaos, Darkness, Death, Deception, Earth, Epic Dexterity, Epic Stamina, Epic Strength, Death, Fertility, Fire, Forge, Fortune, Healer, Journeys, Moon, Passion, Prosperity, Order, Sky, Sun, War, Water</div> </div> </div> </div>Has Frost been subsumed by Fire as an inverse-polarity variant ? Makes sense. Deception obviously includes Illusion. I'm curious about the interplay and overlapping between Chaos, Fortune, and Order. The previews suggest certain Purviews (Artistry, Beasts, probably Passion) may vary in scope from one specific field/type to all of them (it is fairly easy to think of a Scion or God that has interest in, and mastery of, multiple kinds of emotions).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 09-28-2016, 02:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T08:47:59-07:00","id":977787,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure order is covering the old justice boons... though I was hoping for a vengeance purview... also I missed stars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T08:54:43-07:00","id":977788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=977722#post977722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Great for Revlid. When was this announced?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It wasn't, but he posts on Sufficient Velocity. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/sardonyx-scion-and-trinity-continuum.19026/page-7\" target=\"_blank\">https://forums.sufficientvelocity.co...m.19026/page-7</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T08:58:36-07:00","id":977793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=977787#post977787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure order is covering the old justice boons... though I was hoping for a vengeance purview... also I missed stars.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right about Stars. I was under the impression from the spoilers compilation that the old Guardian and Justice Purviews were mostly going to go under the new namesake Callings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 09-28-2016, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T09:56:10-07:00","id":977817,"title":"","content":"Oh, I hadn't heard that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T10:10:48-07:00","id":977821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=977817#post977817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I hadn't heard that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I read the Callings are where all the old Mental/Social Epic Attributes and 'abstract' Purviews like Guardian and Justice are mostly going. Makes me wonder how they are going to settle the unbalance between the Callings (e.g. Guardian, Judge, Leader, Sage) that seem like they are going to have exclusive access on their fields, and the ones that obviously are going to share a major thematic overlapping with similar Purviews (e.g. Creator and Forge; Deception, Trickster, and Metamorphosis; Healer and Health; Liminal and Journeys; Lover and Passion; Warrior and War).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T10:42:35-07:00","id":977837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div c