7#post977837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Order Purview will cover vengeance carried out within the bounds of the law. The Passion Purview can govern the emotion of vengeance.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bThe word I'm looking for is &quot;Sploosh!&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T12:28:28-07:00","id":977893,"title":"","content":"Ok so Im currently obsessed with mystic alchemy and occultism. THe pursuit of divinity, perfection, and ultimate knowledge are all themes i love very much. Would my budding young alchemist with his eyes set on distilling the universal medicine be a viable character for scion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2107-wiwuno","name":"Wiwuno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T12:36:39-07:00","id":977901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wiwuno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=977893#post977893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok so Im currently obsessed with mystic alchemy and occultism. THe pursuit of divinity, perfection, and ultimate knowledge are all themes i love very much. Would my budding young alchemist with his eyes set on distilling the universal medicine be a viable character for scion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T12:48:59-07:00","id":977909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wiwuno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=977893#post977893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok so Im currently obsessed with mystic alchemy and occultism. THe pursuit of divinity, perfection, and ultimate knowledge are all themes i love very much. Would my budding young alchemist with his eyes set on distilling the universal medicine be a viable character for scion?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were running a game and you brought in that concept, I'd say &quot;Oh, we'll MAKE it work&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T13:06:02-07:00","id":977921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wiwuno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=977893#post977893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok so Im currently obsessed with mystic alchemy and occultism. THe pursuit of divinity, perfection, and ultimate knowledge are all themes i love very much. Would my budding young alchemist with his eyes set on distilling the universal medicine be a viable character for scion?</div> </div> </div> </div>ME AS GM: &quot;Interesting concept, let's take a look at the chapter on character creation and see how to make it work. We may need to change a little of the fluff, maybe whip up a houserule or two, but we'll make it work somehow. Perhaps your character will become a deity of alchemy or chemistry.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7395-meribson","name":"Meribson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7395_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T13:09:26-07:00","id":977925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wiwuno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=977893#post977893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok so Im currently obsessed with mystic alchemy and occultism. THe pursuit of divinity, perfection, and ultimate knowledge are all themes i love very much. Would my budding young alchemist with his eyes set on distilling the universal medicine be a viable character for scion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hello, Scion of Djehuti-as-Hermes Trismegustus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T14:20:36-07:00","id":977967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=977837#post977837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Order Purview will cover vengeance carried out within the bounds of the law. The Passion Purview can govern the emotion of vengeance.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the various kinds of combat-worthy Callings and Purviews cover direct application of vigilante justice. On a tangent, it questionable whether the vigilante label would properly apply to Scions, even less to Gods. If one assumes either Might is Right or Divine Law as legitimate, then these models empower them to deal rightful justice. Democracy does not, but then again the existence of a class of sapients that have exceedingly different levels of power, knowledge, and personal abilities from Muggles puts the premises of democracy into question, since Gods, Scions, supernatural beings, and mortals are most definitely not 'created equal'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T14:52:19-07:00","id":977978,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity, is Passion basically a purview for all kinds of emotion? Like if you wanted to have a deity of fear and nightmares, would they have Passion (fear)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7395-meribson","name":"Meribson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7395_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T14:54:41-07:00","id":977980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meribson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=977978#post977978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, is Passion basically a purview for all kinds of emotion? Like if you wanted to have a deity of fear and nightmares, would they have Passion (fear)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Passion encompasses all emotion. It's possible (and common in the corebook pantheons) to narrow it down to a subset, like Love or Fear or Anger, and there's a mechanical reward for taking that limitation.<br /> <br /> (this also applies with Beasts and Artistry)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T14:56:26-07:00","id":977981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=977967#post977967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the various kinds of combat-worthy Callings and Purviews cover direct application of vigilante justice. On a tangent, it questionable whether the vigilante label would properly apply to Scions, even less to Gods. If one assumes either Might is Right or Divine Law as legitimate, then these models empower them to deal rightful justice. Democracy does not, but then again the existence of a class of sapients that have exceedingly different levels of power, knowledge, and personal abilities from Muggles puts the premises of democracy into question, since Gods, Scions, supernatural beings, and mortals are most definitely not 'created equal'.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be technically illegal to go around doing vigilante justice, but the cops don't tend to mind when you punch out the frost giant in Time Square or haul in the weird snake cult guy with mind control eyes. As a whole, Scions don't have Batman or Spider-Man reputation problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T15:03:19-07:00","id":977988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=977980#post977980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Passion encompasses all emotion. It's possible (and common in the corebook pantheons) to narrow it down to a subset, like Love or Fear or Anger, and there's a mechanical reward for taking that limitation.<br /> <br /> (this also applies with Beasts and Artistry)</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to know. I'm just curious about the fine-tuning. Let's assume the character has a focus in a multiple, but finite subset, such as Love and Anger/Fear if it combines Lover and Hunter/Warrior aspects. Mechanically, would it belong in the former category or the latter, or be a third, halfway case all its own ? I can easily think of several character concepts built this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T15:13:11-07:00","id":977994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=977981#post977981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be technically illegal to go around doing vigilante justice, but the cops don't tend to mind when you punch out the frost giant in Time Square or haul in the weird snake cult guy with mind control eyes. As a whole, Scions don't have Batman or Spider-Man reputation problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find myself wondering if Fate has anything to do with this, or if it's just a setting choice you made?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T15:24:57-07:00","id":978002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horngeek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=977994#post977994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find myself wondering if Fate has anything to do with this, or if it's just a setting choice you made?</div> </div> </div> </div>If Fate truly has something to do with universal unconscious, we definitely know from a cursory review of the collected sum of fiction since the collective mind usually does not like boring stuff such as law concerns getting in the way of a good story. So I can totally see it being a Fate thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T15:45:58-07:00","id":978011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=978002#post978002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If Fate truly has something to do with universal unconscious, we definitely know from a cursory review of the collected sum of fiction since the collective mind usually does not like boring stuff such as law concerns getting in the way of a good story. So I can totally see it being a Fate thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>See also, why Scions never have to worry about weapons permits even in Japan. :P<br /> <br /> (Substitute another country with very, very strict gun laws as you choose)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T15:53:58-07:00","id":978014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horngeek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=977994#post977994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find myself wondering if Fate has anything to do with this, or if it's just a setting choice you made?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing to do with Fate\u2014Scions can get into trouble with the law just like anyone. On the other hand, a lot of things that Scions deal with are Big and Scary and completely beyond the scale of the law enforcement/government. It makes life a lot easier for law enforcement to just drop the charges and be thankful they're still alive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T16:08:14-07:00","id":978018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=978014#post978014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing to do with Fate\u2014Scions can get into trouble with the law just like anyone. On the other hand, a lot of things that Scions deal with are Big and Scary and completely beyond the scale of the law enforcement/government. It makes life a lot easier for law enforcement to just drop the charges and be thankful they're still alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Freeze! You're under arrest for destruction of public property!&quot;<br /> <br /> {*deadpan expression*}&quot;I just exploded and knocked out a snake so big that it makes Godzilla look like a mosquito.&quot; {*raise eyebrow*} &quot;How exactly do you plan to hold me until trial?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7395-meribson","name":"Meribson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7395_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T16:13:45-07:00","id":978020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=978014#post978014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing to do with Fate\u2014Scions can get into trouble with the law just like anyone. On the other hand, a lot of things that Scions deal with are Big and Scary and completely beyond the scale of the law enforcement/government. It makes life a lot easier for law enforcement to just drop the charges and be thankful they're still alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence my point why democracy and rule of *human* law tend to work poorly in settings with characters and beings that can beat armies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T17:01:04-07:00","id":978049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=978020#post978020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hence my point why democracy and rule of *human* law tend to work poorly in settings with characters and beings that can beat armies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Human Law isn't always human, especially when the Gods are real. Shamash, Jupiter, ect may all take their legal codes as being the originators of modern western legal systems, and will take offense at the violation of them. On top of that, a lot of basic modern legal principles have origins in the historical legal codes of these Pantheons.<br /> <br /> So, if you're a Scion of Zeus, and you ambush and murder someone, sure, you have the police coming for you. You <i>also</i> have your father turning his baleful gaze upon you. Nemesis, the Furies, ect.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T17:28:35-07:00","id":978059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=978049#post978049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Human Law isn't always human, especially when the Gods are real. Shamash, Jupiter, ect may all take their legal codes as being the originators of modern western legal systems, and will take offense at the violation of them. On top of that, a lot of basic modern legal principles have origins in the historical legal codes of these Pantheons.<br /> <br /> So, if you're a Scion of Zeus, and you ambush and murder someone, sure, you have the police coming for you. You <i>also</i> have your father turning his baleful gaze upon you. Nemesis, the Furies, ect.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but on the other hand I bet Zeus or Shamash don't give a damn about killings or property damage done as a result of an open combat or fighintg monsters (unless say you killed a blood-kin or sworn friend), or the very least would deem the issue entirely settled with some reparation. The Gods' notion of Justice is very much rooted in Heroic Age notions, and they don't care much about the changes human legislators churned out in the last 2500 years. As for ambush... trickery has its place in warfare, Hunters and Tricksters would approve even if Guardians and Warriors would frown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 09-28-2016, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T17:42:03-07:00","id":978072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=978014#post978014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing to do with Fate\u2014Scions can get into trouble with the law just like anyone. On the other hand, a lot of things that Scions deal with are Big and Scary and completely beyond the scale of the law enforcement/government. It makes life a lot easier for law enforcement to just drop the charges and be thankful they're still alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Um, Chief? Are we gonna bust that guy for destruction of public property and possession of a weapon?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Callahan, what did you just see?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Er, some guy with a sword run up some two-story giant and stab out its one eye, before the corpse dissolved into mist?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I didn't see a damn thing. MUST have been a gas explosion that took out that building.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;But, the giant-&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Gas explosion, Callahan.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T18:09:39-07:00","id":978090,"title":"","content":"With gods of law and order existing in the setting, it wouldn't surprise me if the police had divine sponsorship. So if they choose to arrest an errant Hero and said Hero doesn't submit to their authority, he's likely to face said divine sponsor's wrath. Now, Scion being the kind of setting that it is, I don't expect that this sort of thing will result in Heroes being arrested for the collateral damage that occurs while bringing down a monster. But I also don't think that a Hero who considers himself to be above the law will be able to maintain that attitude for long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T18:13:01-07:00","id":978095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=978090#post978090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With gods of law and order existing in the setting, it wouldn't surprise me if the police had divine sponsorship. So if they choose to arrest an errant Hero and said Hero doesn't submit to their authority, he's likely to face said divine sponsor's wrath. Now, Scion being the kind of setting that it is, I don't expect that this sort of thing will result in Heroes being arrested for the collateral damage that occurs while bringing down a monster. But I also don't think that a Hero who considers himself to be above the law will be able to maintain that attitude for long.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm dying to play a Scion of Sutek who breaks from the police department because he feels like their rigid adherence to order isn't real justice and becomes a hardboiled private eye. He still helps with important cases (as Sutek still guards the solar barge), but can't honestly wear a uniform anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T06:31:51-07:00","id":978345,"title":"","content":"Does Fate force gods to act according to their callings? I.E Ares is a Warrior,so he has no choice but try to fight all the time. Zeus is a Lover so he has to chase women? Just how much free will is denied to the gods?<br /> And if for some reason they want to try a new calling,but don't want to Re-Incarnate,can they Mantle an Incarnation with a different Calling than they have now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T08:52:02-07:00","id":978437,"title":"","content":"On Scion and law enforcement:<br /> <br /> I'm sure their are also Order powers that make anything you do LEGAL as a metaphysical truth (&quot;Obey the law? I AM THE LAW!&quot;)... Zeus probably has that one.<br /> <br /> And there are Chaos powers that make you unbindable by human institutions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T09:40:58-07:00","id":978449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=978345#post978345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Fate force gods to act according to their callings? I.E Ares is a Warrior,so he has no choice but try to fight all the time. Zeus is a Lover so he has to chase women? Just how much free will is denied to the gods?<br /> And if for some reason they want to try a new calling,but don't want to Re-Incarnate,can they Mantle an Incarnation with a different Calling than they have now?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How it worked in 1st edition was that Fate doesn't force anyone to do anything, it just sets up situations via conincidences and subtle influences. For example, Ares has a choice not to fight, but he's going to continue to find himself in situations that can only be solved by violence. Zeus won't be forced to seduce someone, but it just so happens all the women who cross his path are stunningly beautiful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12349-evilnerf","name":"evilnerf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12349_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T22:05:57-07:00","id":978853,"title":"","content":"There are gods who have special relationships with Fate right? Like the Moirae and the Norns? What is the main difference between them and the other gods, exactly? What about their Scions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12342,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12342-dr-quantum","user":"Dr. Quantum","date":". 09-30-2016, 01:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12342-dr-quantum","name":"Dr. Quantum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T22:17:30-07:00","id":978859,"title":"","content":"I have a developer/business type question.<br /> <br /> I am aware that Scion is a game that is fully owned by Onyxpath. I am an Exalted and Chronicles of darkness player so I know that licenced products require final approval from White Wolf in order to be released to backers or the public. I would also imagine that you have to submit material intermittenly so that any elements the licensor does not want are caught quickly and a situation in which you would have to remove large portions of material doesn't suddenly happen.<br /> <br /> So what is it like to not have to take those steps, to not have to submit material after every draft or every editing or layout pass. I'm not interested in how much time it saves (although I feel it probably should save some time) but how development feels in comparison to your other projects which are licensed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T07:00:24-07:00","id":978989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dr. Quantum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=978853#post978853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are gods who have special relationships with Fate right? Like the Moirae and the Norns? What is the main difference between them and the other gods, exactly? What about their Scions?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1st Edition, there were spells in the 'Magic' special purview that allowed one to see and manipulate Fate. So I'd say that the Moirae and Norns likely just have stronger spells that allow them to influence it. <br /> <br /> Of course, in 2nd Edition, they've removed the special purviews so I imagine it will work differently. Maybe Neall can answer that part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12349-evilnerf","name":"evilnerf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12349_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T12:52:38-07:00","id":979216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meribson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=978018#post978018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Freeze! You're under arrest for destruction of public property!&quot;<br /> <br /> {*deadpan expression*}&quot;I just exploded and knocked out a snake so big that it makes Godzilla look like a mosquito.&quot; {*raise eyebrow*} &quot;How exactly do you plan to hold me until trial?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I read the last bit in Nick Offerman's Voice. It was glorious, and now im thinking of making a version of Ron Swanson as a Scion/Demigod figure. Because Yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8023,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","user":"Grimangel53","date":". 09-30-2016, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","name":"Grimangel53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T13:03:12-07:00","id":979814,"title":"","content":"But don't forget property damage can be a problem if you are<br /> 1) You are Norse (They mess with their enemies stuff all the time, but when it comes to allies/hometurf there are fines to that stuff)<br /> 2) <b><i>Someone Important</i></b> might have property/loved one there which can cause trouble<br /> 3) Also nevermind that if it took place in an important area there might be a god who presides over it in general and puts you in the middle of Divine Politics. and...<br /> 4) As a complete lark... My dad had me watch Bridge over River Kwai way too much as a kid and I can't help but imagine a bunch of Scion/mythic empowered builders who seem to clean that stuff up in hours while whistling some sort of tune.<br /> <br /> On a different note, I'm a bit confused about the Chosen Genesis... I mean I thought it was people who fit a role. Pharaohs are always going to be scions, Caesar, Emperors, and others that filled similar roles. But now it sounds like it can be anybody the gods like? Not that I have an issue with that, but curious what the &quot;chosen&quot; genesis fully details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T08:28:13-07:00","id":980782,"title":"","content":"Wait, I noticed a few pages back in the listed purviews that Frost was missing. Is frost still a thing? Hopefully it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T10:59:58-07:00","id":980891,"title":"","content":"So I went through the wiki and various preview materials and im pretty sure this hasn't been asked yet.<br /> I have a question about feats of scale. From what I've read, one of the ways scion does scaling will be that beings of a higher tier get a bunch of extra success's to normal rolls. What i want to know is will these scale affects apply to all rolls or just some based on purviews and callings? It makes sense that ares or thor get a bunch of big bonus's when laying the smack down on someone, but i don't really see them being as good at poetry or something like that. So is there a mechanic for this? Like a boon in the passion or artistry purview that says 'you can now do feats of scale on poetry rolls' or other mechanics that control what rolls get scale bonus's and what dont?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","user":"Lionmanguy","date":". 10-03-2016, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T10:43:30-07:00","id":981519,"title":"","content":"Do Titans have callings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T10:02:20-07:00","id":982179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=974707#post974707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Fauns, kitsune, and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they have Mantles?If so,which are the mechanical effects of a legendary creature's mantle? or a scion's?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T10:06:36-07:00","id":982180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=982179#post982179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do they have Mantles?If so,which are the mechanical effects of a legendary creature's mantle? or a scion's?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, only(?) Gods have mantles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T10:26:44-07:00","id":982189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=982180#post982180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I know, only(?) Gods have mantles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know Heroes have,Neall mentioned it<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> Legend has certain themes according to the dot rating, which may be &quot;mantled&quot; by the god to produce certain divine attributes and power sets. These are acquired by a system of heroic deeds (both in actual play or in an outright character generation). If you're play a Scion, your first dot is always, &quot;Scion of X, God of Y,&quot; which allows you to adopt a lesser set of powers of your parent's most famous mantle. While parentage is clear and may even trace back generations through the Legend system, Scions needn't (and, in fact, it's hard for them) be clones of their parents. Certain relics may be Legend dots, meaning you can't mantle those powers without them.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>How much (if any) of the aove Info aplly to LegendaryCreatures?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T10:38:11-07:00","id":982196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=982189#post982189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much (if any) of the aove Info aplly to LegendaryCreatures?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a bit dated, and some of our thought on mantles has drifted from it. The &quot;adopting a lesser set of powers&quot; has become, I think, the innate access to one of your parent's Purviews and sharing a Calling with them, which non-Scions obviously would not do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T10:41:08-07:00","id":982199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=982196#post982196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's a bit dated, and some of our thought on mantles has drifted from it. The &quot;adopting a lesser set of powers&quot; has become, I think, the innate access to one of your parent's Purviews and sharing a Calling with them, which non-Scions obviously would not do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understood,just one more thing. How Purviews are Learned in game without picking a new relic or guide ? Do scions have to find teachers? Or raise their legend?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T11:04:51-07:00","id":982212,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Well, since the Kickstarter just hit the &quot;Including: The Yazata&quot; tier..