iner\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=987918#post987918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the use of Osiris might have been that this is a draft, and the guy writing that particular relic is more familiar with the Greek-based names, and during the editing it'll be changed to Azar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Neall said in the KS comments that they'll be changed once they're out of first drafts, thankfully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T18:02:04-07:00","id":988025,"title":"","content":"Question About Primordials :\u200b)<br /> <br /> <br /> 1)Are they active Like if their pantheon fights with another will they help?<br /> 2)Are they stronger than gods or titans?<br /> 3)Are they limited to one purview and one purview only like titans?<br /> 4)If he first gods and titans were born of Primordials can they give birth to brande new gods in this modern age?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T18:29:27-07:00","id":988039,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm... I bet Utgard-Loki is a Titan of Deception this time around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T20:50:00-07:00","id":988104,"title":"","content":"Any thoughts on how Ve and Vili (Lodurr and Hoenir?) will be handled in the Norse Pantheon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T07:52:57-07:00","id":988248,"title":"","content":"Since you're bringing The Keepers Of The World Back, I wanted to know. are they still planning to lock all of the other pantheons away so they're the only gods in the Word?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T16:00:20-07:00","id":988481,"title":"","content":"A question for Neall (or anyone else involved directly in the Kickstarter): Would it be possible to make the bestiary PDF purchasable as an extra, without having to jump up to hard copy? Or is it deliberately that way as an enticement?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T16:08:02-07:00","id":988488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=988481#post988481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question for Neall (or anyone else involved directly in the Kickstarter): Would it be possible to make the bestiary PDF purchasable as an extra, without having to jump up to hard copy? Or is it deliberately that way as an enticement?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would love to snag it as a PDF add-on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T01:11:10-07:00","id":988731,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar137_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"137\" data-vbnamecard=\"137\">Neall</a> Do you think we could get a description of Scale in practice to help us understand how it works?<br /> <br /> Like is Scale a statistic on a character sheet, or a descriptor for an action or ability?<br /> <br /> Like, am I a Scale 2 Jotun, or is it that Jotuns posses the Giant trait and are thus counted as Scale 2 with regards to Size? Can I have a gun that's Scale 2 (maybe its a laser cannon?) Or am I Scale 2, thus my pistol hits harder?<br /> <br /> Do abilities modify one's Scale for the purposes of an action ever?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T03:47:08-07:00","id":988771,"title":"","content":"If the inspiration for Scale is any indicator, it's a per-Attribute thing. Though traits like Size or Speed might also have it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T19:44:40-07:00","id":989159,"title":"","content":"One question that I had is,-- based on the stuff we've been told about Titans, I'm getting the impression that the Titan War is less of an overarching focus this time around. Leaving more room for more mythologically diverse stories rather than needing to deal with the whole &quot;the Titans have broken free!&quot; issue before you can do anything else. Which, I'm guessing, also suggests that Scions have probably gotten Visitations more regularly throughout history rather than that being something that happened because of the breakout...<br /> <br /> ...does that sound about right? I mean, does Scion have more room to tell a story just about the Theoi goofing around and getting up to their usual mischief, or some Pantheon versus Pantheon type stuff??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T19:57:08-07:00","id":989164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrownedSun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=989159#post989159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question that I had is,-- based on the stuff we've been told about Titans, I'm getting the impression that the Titan War is less of an overarching focus this time around. Leaving more room for more mythologically diverse stories rather than needing to deal with the whole &quot;the Titans have broken free!&quot; issue before you can do anything else. Which, I'm guessing, also suggests that Scions have probably gotten Visitations more regularly throughout history rather than that being something that happened because of the breakout...<br /> <br /> ...does that sound about right? I mean, does Scion have more room to tell a story just about the Theoi goofing around and getting up to their usual mischief, or some Pantheon versus Pantheon type stuff??</div> </div> </div> </div>The Titan War has been described as more of a cold war than an open conflict in 2e, and is apparently different enough that the 1e setting is an entirely different setting Shard to be described in the Translation Guide. That's before factoring in that some Pantheons get along pretty swimmingly with their Titans (the Netjer) or lack Titans entirely (the Orisha).<br /> <br /> It's much more about an open-ended urban fantasy with mythology theming this time around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T00:36:25-07:00","id":989244,"title":"","content":"Ya'know, I just thought of something. Because of the godly power of Incarnation, they can essentially be in multiple places at once. And the imbuing of incarnations seems to be indefinite - the gods keep it up as long as they want to.<br /> <br /> Which means that gods don't have to just sire a child and run - they can take responsibility and leave a mortal incarnation behind to raise their offspring.<br /> <br /> This also means that the gods that <i>don't</i> - well, they deliberately <i>choose</i> to distance themselves from their children.<br /> <br /> Hm. That factor doesn't really come up in the myths, so maybe there's something about Incarnation we just don't know yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T05:02:59-07:00","id":989295,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar527_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"527\" data-vbnamecard=\"527\">Robert Vance</a> . Since you've been answering purview questions. can you talk about what exactly does Passion do? because when i saw that Bres had Passion (Beauty) i got confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T09:34:01-07:00","id":989394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=989295#post989295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> . Since you've been answering purview questions. can you talk about what exactly does Passion do? because when i saw that Bres had Passion (Beauty) i got confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some Purviews can be further specified; we've seen it with both Beasts and Passion so far, where the God can drill down and focus on a specific animal or emotion instead of the broader whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T09:38:47-07:00","id":989398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=989394#post989394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some Purviews can be further specified; we've seen it with both Beasts and Passion so far, where the God can drill down and focus on a specific animal or emotion instead of the broader whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>what i stil don't get is what someone like Bres would do with Passion(beauty). I mean,beauty is a idea is something we experince with our senses isnteadof simply feeling it like we feel hate or happiness or sadness or excitement. what exactly is beauty as a Passion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-1