inclusion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T19:53:37-07:00","id":991230,"title":"","content":"They're from their stable of writers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T21:15:13-07:00","id":991259,"title":"","content":"So weird question. I'm making plans to reboot my first scion campaign with this new edition. One of my players and a long time friend has proposed an interesting idea that is a little difficult to work in 1E and I would like to know if it would work in 2E. The Daughter of Zeus She was a normal college sophomore when she got her visitation. went fairly normally except for one problem. Hera. She has promised not to damage any scions of her husband for the sake of them being needed but her nature wont let them go unpunished so she did the next best thing. She diverted the course of the girls power into her closest emotional attachment. A young man she had been friends with since childhood. This young man holds most of the characters power minus some of the more mental and social traits. The real stab in the gut (thats hilarious if you know the concept already) is that this young man has also been bonded to the character with a type of manic obsessive &quot;love&quot;. Think Yandere for you anime fans out there. Is there anyway to make this work in 2E? This player has been with me since my first game and i love out of the box character ideas so i want to be able to make this work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2107-wiwuno","name":"Wiwuno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T21:22:25-07:00","id":991268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wiwuno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=991259#post991259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So weird question. I'm making plans to reboot my first scion campaign with this new edition. One of my players and a long time friend has proposed an interesting idea that is a little difficult to work in 1E and I would like to know if it would work in 2E. The Daughter of Zeus She was a normal college sophomore when she got her visitation. went fairly normally except for one problem. Hera. She has promised not to damage any scions of her husband for the sake of them being needed but her nature wont let them go unpunished so she did the next best thing. She diverted the course of the girls power into her closest emotional attachment. A young man she had been friends with since childhood. This young man holds most of the characters power minus some of the more mental and social traits. The real stab in the gut (thats hilarious if you know the concept already) is that this young man has also been bonded to the character with a type of manic obsessive &quot;love&quot;. Think Yandere for you anime fans out there. Is there anyway to make this work in 2E? This player has been with me since my first game and i love out of the box character ideas so i want to be able to make this work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a pretty classic Fatebinding right there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T17:53:53-07:00","id":991629,"title":"","content":"Neall, is there any hope for the last Satyr stretch goal? I think we would all love to see it at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T06:20:09-07:00","id":991818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wiwuno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=991259#post991259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So weird question. I'm making plans to reboot my first scion campaign with this new edition. One of my players and a long time friend has proposed an interesting idea that is a little difficult to work in 1E and I would like to know if it would work in 2E. The Daughter of Zeus She was a normal college sophomore when she got her visitation. went fairly normally except for one problem. Hera. She has promised not to damage any scions of her husband for the sake of them being needed but her nature wont let them go unpunished so she did the next best thing. She diverted the course of the girls power into her closest emotional attachment. A young man she had been friends with since childhood. This young man holds most of the characters power minus some of the more mental and social traits. The real stab in the gut (thats hilarious if you know the concept already) is that this young man has also been bonded to the character with a type of manic obsessive &quot;love&quot;. Think Yandere for you anime fans out there. Is there anyway to make this work in 2E? This player has been with me since my first game and i love out of the box character ideas so i want to be able to make this work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it has been mentioned guides can be used to channel purviews. So you could probably work him as a fatebond &quot;guide&quot; or companion. At least on the mechanical end of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T07:47:40-07:00","id":991850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wiwuno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=991259#post991259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So weird question. I'm making plans to reboot my first scion campaign with this new edition. One of my players and a long time friend has proposed an interesting idea that is a little difficult to work in 1E and I would like to know if it would work in 2E. The Daughter of Zeus She was a normal college sophomore when she got her visitation. went fairly normally except for one problem. Hera. She has promised not to damage any scions of her husband for the sake of them being needed but her nature wont let them go unpunished so she did the next best thing. She diverted the course of the girls power into her closest emotional attachment. A young man she had been friends with since childhood. This young man holds most of the characters power minus some of the more mental and social traits. The real stab in the gut (thats hilarious if you know the concept already) is that this young man has also been bonded to the character with a type of manic obsessive &quot;love&quot;. Think Yandere for you anime fans out there. Is there anyway to make this work in 2E? This player has been with me since my first game and i love out of the box character ideas so i want to be able to make this work.</div> </div> </div> </div>agreed with the rest of them. Mechanically, i'd say its a fatebound companion, who, for whatever reason, is both the source of her power, and/or the person who has any relics or whatever that the scion needs. Like, the scion needs to get the relic from them, and return it to them, as part of the diverting of power. it sounds like a different and fun concept though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","name":"Grimangel53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T09:20:42-07:00","id":991869,"title":"","content":"Neall, can you tell us which gods can grant access to Fomorian knacks? You've mentioned Lugh, but I'm assuming Ogma can grant them as well?<br /> <br /> Actually, can you tell us what the Fomorian knacks can do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T06:23:56-07:00","id":992911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=991869#post991869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neall, can you tell us which gods can grant access to Fomorian knacks? You've mentioned Lugh, but I'm assuming Ogma can grant them as well?<br /> <br /> Actually, can you tell us what the Fomorian knacks can do?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was wondering if the opposite can happen. as in a fomorian with Geasa? I got HUGE love for the trope where characters of a evil race decides tp become good. Could one of the Tuatha turn a Fomor into a Chosen Scion granting him Geasa and one other purview along witht he fomorian abilities?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T22:27:12-07:00","id":993326,"title":"","content":"What is going to be in Origins, a couple things that I thought were going to be in it like Satyrs were listed as stretch goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm