how the fall out impacts mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T12:07:25-07:00","id":998360,"title":"","content":"For <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar137_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"137\" data-vbnamecard=\"137\">Neall</a> or <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar527_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"527\" data-vbnamecard=\"527\">Robert Vance</a>:<br /> <br /> I'm curious about the Kami (who haven't really been touched on, thus far). It's been mentioned that Inari will be joining the divine-patron lineup this go-round, and possibly Mikaboshi. Aside from that, though, how similar will the Kami lineup (at least in Hero) be to that of 1e's Amatsukami?<br /> <br /> I'm primarily interested in Tsuki-yomi (and recreating my long-running Scion of his by 2e rules), but also am interested in whether deities like Uzume and Takemikazuchi will be featured.<br /> <br /> (Feel free to say if this counts as a spoiler or something!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","user":"yukikaze","date":". 11-19-2016, 01:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T16:13:22-07:00","id":998490,"title":"","content":"Ah, okay. That explains a lot, actually. Thanks for answering, everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T14:20:42-08:00","id":999428,"title":"","content":"Hey, would powers like human clay be returning eventually? The power to create a new species was cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T23:24:08-08:00","id":999592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=998356#post998356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they are born with the magic or do they somehow steal it from the gods and scions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, saying they are &quot;classic antagonists&quot; is a bit much already - in general, witches are beyond good and evil; they are destructive, but assumed to be just, and are often revered, e.g. in the Gelede mask festival. The great, powerful witches the gods can get in trouble with (the <i>Iyami</i>, &quot;Our Mothers&quot;, often wrongly and offensively called <i>Aje</i>) are like a weird mixture between harpies and wise elders - they only punish the guilty, they even debate punishment in council before exacting it, but when they do, it is chaotic, destructive and extreme. As I said, there are myths about them confronting the gods, but those are by far not common enough to have the <i>Iyami</i> called &quot;classic antagonists&quot;, and usually, when gods and witches fight, the witches are in the right - the Orisha are anything but infallible. Obatala is attacked by witches for stealing water from their well, and Orunmila is cursed by them for threatening them with a sword while they were his pupils in divination.<br /> <br /> Goddesses like Onile/Nana Buruku, Oshun, and Oya can even be said to be members (or even leaders!) of the <i>Iyami</i> themselves. That's because <i>Eye</i>, the &quot;bird magic&quot; that gives the witches power, is inherent to every woman. Not every woman develops and uses that power, not every woman has it in her to become a true witch, but every woman <i>could </i>be a witch. And thus there are of course also lesser, more human witches than the grand &quot;Mothers&quot; or &quot;Elders of the Night&quot;, who are fully capable of acting injustly, even evilly. But these are not fit opponents for the gods, they trade in small curses and poisons, enacting revenges and jealousies, and can be punished for it by human courts (although calling upon the judicial might of Orisha Oko).<br /> <br /> So, to answer your question, the power of Yoruba witches is not stolen, but to say they're born with it is not quite enough either. Every woman has &quot;bird power&quot;, but only old age and proper cult practice will turn her into a proper witch. Then, however, her power is great: She can turn into a bird, can cause wounds without touching the victim, or make the words of even everyday smalltalk painful reality. The line between the oldest of human witches and the immortal, seemingly divine witches of myth and cult is smudged, and supposed to be so - all witches are like one, one community, one unity, all servants of the Earth. Some Gelede maskerades will, however, depict them with a leader, the &quot;Great Mother&quot;, a goddess-like hag, hunchbacked, bald, and bearded. Even this one, though, is revered and worshipped as much as she is feared.<br /> <br /> So yeah, cool in-game antagonists if your characters commit any crimes, sins or offenses against the<i> Iyami</i>, but they aren't really big-A-Antagonists like Titans who constantly and dangerously oppose the gods. The Orisha really lack in those - they have some elder figures, like Yemoja and Onile/Nana Buruku, but those are not consistently depicted as really being a former generation, and they really pale in comparison with Olodumare; they meanwhile also lack truly antagonistic figures, because even obvious assholes like Olokun and Shopona/Babalu Aiye have mixed morals and a lively cult base, not to mention that they lack the overwhelming power associated with Titans. Long story short, it's a quite accurate descision to depict the Orisha without Titans, and witches like the <i>Iyami</i> can't really fill that gap. Their biggest story catalyst, I'd say, is intra-pantheon strife - never forget those are the gods of many sepearate kingdoms compressed by some shared culture and the pressures of colonialism and slavery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T09:01:05-08:00","id":1002239,"title":"","content":"Is it too early to do another PSP preview? I'd kill to see what you guys did with Metamorphosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T05:09:08-08:00","id":1002837,"title":"","content":"Or a pantheon preview <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'd love to see some Aztec goodness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T06:52:59-08:00","id":1002868,"title":"","content":"Wolf as associated animal to some god? Please, I don't care about exact god or pantheon, just do it already!<br /> <img src=\"https://myfairdiary.files.wordpress.com/2012/12/begging.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T10:40:40-08:00","id":1002953,"title":"","content":"How do Omens work? What's their general deal? So far we don't have much more than 'animal heads???'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T10:48:45-08:00","id":1002960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taveena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1002953#post1002953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do Omens work? What's their general deal? So far we don't have much more than 'animal heads???'</div> </div> </div> </div>Q: Here's the question. I saw a Scion with four arms in most recent teaser. What kind of power is having four arms? Is it a knack or boon? Could a Scion have it as a specific power (sprout extra arms) or as part of a general shape-shifting power? (gyre)<br /> <br /> A: It's her Omen, a sometimes-supernatural effect associated with her growing Legend that allows you to identify her.<br /> <br /> It might also be part of the Deva PSP at this point, I can't recall, but you can write it up either way. (Neall)<br /> <br /> I think Annie X probably isn't getting it out of the Signature Purview, but another Dev\u00e1 Scion maybe could. (Robert Vance)<br /> <br /> Q: I have some many questions about [Omens].<br /> <br /> Do you need a certain level of Legend to get an Omen?<br /> Do Omens change with Legend?<br /> Can Scions forcibly activate their Omens to look divine and stuff?<br /> Do people of the Scion's religion automatically recognize Omens for what they are?<br /> Does activating an Omen have a cost?<br /> Do Omens trigger automatically when Scions spent a certain amount of Legend/activate certain Boons? (Tiresias)<br /> <br /> A: Yes, potentially, yes, yes, no, yes. (Neall)<br /> <br /> Q: LOL All these questions make me want to ask the Question are Omens just Animas? (SpruceStripedGoose)<br /> <br /> A: No, not really. Animas aren't &quot;always on&quot; while Omens always are. Omens are also non-optional added features to your Incarnations - you can leave off one, but powering up an Incarnation or creating one of sufficient power means you have to strap on Omens. That said, Odin's missing eye is a lot more socially acceptable than Ganesh's elephant head, so if you meet a older man with a missing eye and a bunch of ravens around him, give him hospitality. (Neall)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T11:39:25-08:00","id":1002985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1002837#post1002837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or a pantheon preview <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'd love to see some Aztec goodness.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar137_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"137\" data-vbnamecard=\"137\">Neall</a> could you do that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T04:22:45-08:00","id":1003313,"title":"","content":"So, hey... just a quick question; is being able to pick extra stuff [like extra copies books or the 1e PDFs] something that has already happened and I missed it, or is that still coming?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T04:37:31-08:00","id":1003316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1003313#post1003313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, hey... just a quick question; is being able to pick extra stuff [like extra copies books or the 1e PDFs] something that has already happened and I missed it, or is that still coming?</div> </div> </div> </div>It'll come when they open the Backerkit page up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T13:20:11-08:00","id":1003564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1003316#post1003316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It'll come when they open the Backerkit page up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T06:29:18-08:00","id":1004906,"title":"","content":"Question for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar137_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"137\" data-vbnamecard=\"137\">Neall</a> or <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar527_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"527\" data-vbnamecard=\"527\">Robert Vance</a>:<br /> <br /> One of you said awhile back that scions will be able to channel purviews through their guides as well as through relics. But I haven't seen anything that says guides grant a motif like relics do. So can a guide grant a motif or will the scion be required to channel that purview through a motif granted either by the PSP or a relic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T14:37:02-08:00","id":1005108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1002960#post1002960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, not really. Animas aren't &quot;always on&quot; while Omens always are. Omens are also non-optional added features to your Incarnations - you can leave off one, but powering up an Incarnation or creating one of sufficient power means you have to strap on Omens. That said, Odin's missing eye is a lot more socially acceptable than Ganesh's elephant head, so if you meet a older man with a missing eye and a bunch of ravens around him, give him hospitality. (Neall)</div> </div> </div> </div>So do we know anything about the mechanics, or how they're chosen/form? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T12:57:25-08:00","id":1005821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1004906#post1004906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar137_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"137\" data-vbnamecard=\"137\">Neall</a> or <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar527_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"527\" data-vbnamecard=\"527\">Robert Vance</a>:<br /> <br /> One of you said awhile back that scions will be able to channel purviews through their guides as well as through relics. But I haven't seen anything that says guides grant a motif like relics do. So can a guide grant a motif or will the scion be required to channel that purview through a motif granted either by the PSP or a relic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Guides don't grant motifs. <br /> <br /> Pantheon and Relic motifs are going to be most Scions' go-to, but there are some other ways to gain them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T13:11:50-08:00","id":1005828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1005821#post1005821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guides don't grant motifs.<br /> <br /> Pantheon and Relic motifs are going to be most Scions' go-to, but there are some other ways to gain them.</div> </div> </div> </div>i've noticed that there havent been much questions about Legend itself,so i got three <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200b1)How does a relic becomes part of a scion legend?<br /> \u200b2)How is Legend raised? both mechanically and inside the games World<br /> \u200b3)Is it true only zeus hades and poseidon have legend 12 in the Theoi?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T07:30:47-08:00","id":1006184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1005821#post1005821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guides don't grant motifs.<br /> <br /> Pantheon and Relic motifs are going to be most Scions' go-to, but there are some other ways to gain them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Thanks for the answer!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T10:03:22-08:00","id":1006251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=987070#post987070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would work. It would <i>still</i> be an oversimplification of matters; but the focus would be closer to the mark.<br /> <br /> Plus, the forge needs fire; so the \u201cstealing fire from the gods\u201d thing still makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the key here is not making Prometheus a titan. We could always make him a god who was called a titan who was allied politcally allied with the titans after his imprisionement. Neall di say god and titan can be more of a political difference than a metaphysical one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T19:31:57-08:00","id":1006968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1006251#post1006251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the key here is not making Prometheus a titan. We could always make him a god who was called a titan who was allied politcally allied with the titans after his imprisionement. Neall di say god and titan can be more of a political difference than a metaphysical one</div> </div> </div> </div>The Orisha don't even <i>believe </i>in Titans, they just think some gods are particularly jerky, and from a certain point of view they're absolutely right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T19:32:47-08:00","id":1006969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=999428#post999428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, would powers like human clay be returning eventually? The power to create a new species was cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. One of the Incarnations depends on being able to make humans, basically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T19:34:03-08:00","id":1006970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=997438#post997438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neall,I almost forgot. But what are you guys going tto to previiew another full pantheon before this month ends?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope! But I'm working on some Christmas presents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T19:46:06-08:00","id":1006980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1006970#post1006970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope! But I'm working on some Christmas presents.</div> </div> </div> </div>You tease! Can't wait to see it, whatever it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T09:11:35-08:00","id":1007281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1006251#post1006251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the key here is not making Prometheus a titan. We could always make him a god who was called a titan who was allied politcally allied with the titans after his imprisionement. Neall di say god and titan can be more of a political difference than a metaphysical one</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Always kinda felt that the line between God &amp; Titan, Immortal &amp; Titanspawn was kind of arbitrarily decided, especially when it came to lableing them with Virtues vs Dark Virtues. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Example: Aphrodite [this one I bring up because I notice that it IS being clarified in 2e] is technically a Titan by the way they seem to be treated in the books. She was born when Cronos lobbed off Uranus' dick, which fell to the ocean and bore Aphrodite into existence. Being the &quot;daughter&quot; of Uranus that actually makes Aphrodite the sister to Cronos and Aunt to Zeus, putting her firmly in the &quot;Titan&quot; camp. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But the book seems to equate Titan to Enemy of the Gods, which isn't fully correct as Promethus may have some serious beef with Zeus for his shit, he is no enemy of the gods. Hell he was one of the Titans that sided with the gods durring the Titanomancy. He was just punished because Zeus is a dick. </span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T09:18:28-08:00","id":1007284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1007281#post1007281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Always kinda felt that the line between God &amp; Titan, Immortal &amp; Titanspawn was kind of arbitrarily decided, especially when it came to lableing them with Virtues vs Dark Virtues. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Example: Aphrodite [this one I bring up because I notice that it IS being clarified in 2e] is technically a Titan by the way they seem to be treated in the books. She was born when Cronos lobbed off Uranus' dick, which fell to the ocean and bore Aphrodite into existence. Being the &quot;daughter&quot; of Uranus that actually makes Aphrodite the sister to Cronos and Aunt to Zeus, putting her firmly in the &quot;Titan&quot; camp. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But the book seems to equate Titan to Enemy of the Gods, which isn't fully correct as Promethus may have some serious beef with Zeus for his shit, he is no enemy of the gods. Hell he was one of the Titans that sided with the gods durring the Titanomancy. He was just punished because Zeus is a dick. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that in 1e a Titan wwas what came before the gods and what generally made the world or even part of the world. but in 2e any being powerful enough can be a Titan and they're also defined by their Titanic Virtues. Neall said scion is about the fact that who you are is defined by who you are to other people or that your relationships define you. i think anyone with no meaningful relationships to define them can be Titanic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T14:11:32-08:00","id":1007425,"title":"","content":"Conversely, 2e now has the Primordials, which are much like what 1e called Greater Titans (though presumably without the \u201cDark Virtues\u201d thing that rendered 1e's Titans as enemies of the Gods).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T21:31:07-08:00","id":1007553,"title":"","content":"For Neall: I'd like to hear about Firmaments (what can be said while avoiding spoilers/mechanical stuff, anyway)! Replies in this thread have suggested that the Overworld and Godrealms will work differently in 2e (and the fiction about Eileen Bran seems to indicate that Godrealm access isn't limited to deity-level beings), so I'm wondering how Firmaments fit into the picture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","user":"yukikaze","date":". 11-28-2016, 12:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T05:56:49-08:00","id":1008894,"title":"","content":"Neall. Are all Titans utterly devoted to one purview and one purview alone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T15:06:56-08:00","id":1009062,"title":"","content":"What benefits do you get from identifying so closely with a Purview that you become a Titan?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T21:37:34-08:00","id":1009169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1008894#post1008894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neall. Are all Titans utterly devoted to one purview and one purview alone?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like more info on this too - my impression is that every Titan is utterly consumed by/embodies one specific Purview, BUT can still have others in their arsenal reflecting a range of the concept of their primary Purview.<br /> <br /> Like the image I have of Kronus is that he'd be a scythe wielding Titan of Death, representing death as harvest &amp; natural selection. Besides his total reflection of the Death Purview, he also wields Stars (for the temporal aspect of aging and the certainty of the future), as well as Fertility and Health (to bring life to its fruition).<br /> <br /> Apep is utterly a Titan of Chaos, but he's probably got some Darkness (he is trying to devour the Sun every night after all), and of course Animal (Snakes).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 11-28-2016, 12:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T22:34:12-08:00","id":1009186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1009062#post1009062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What benefits do you get from identifying so closely with a Purview that you become a Titan?</div> </div> </div> </div>That might be looking at it the wrong way round - it may be they've never formed the connection to humanity the Gods have, for whatever reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T04:02:08-08:00","id":1009267,"title":"","content":"Like Prometheus. Oh, wait\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T04:31:45-08:00","id":1009278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1009267#post1009267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like Prometheus. Oh, wait\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm? Prometheus doesn't actually <i>care</i> about humans qua humans. <i>We</i> think he does, but that's not made him actually do so. It could be he's not actually made whatever changes are necessary to link himself to humanity like the Gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T12:29:24-08:00","id":1009430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1009267#post1009267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like Prometheus. Oh, wait\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think being capable of benevolence (or engaging in actions that happen to benefit humanity that humans interpret as benevolence) and having the more intimate Fate-based connection the Gods have is the same thing.<br /> <br /> It's also possible that in Scion's terminology, Prometheus was a Titan who made a transition to godhood. That transition isn't something that exists in Greek Myth, but it is something implied by Scion's usage of the terms.<br /> <br /> <br /> Based on the Titans in the Tuatha write-up, it seems that Titans who align with the gods take one Titan virtue and one Pantheon virtue, so were I writing up Prometheus as a Titan, he'd be dominated by the Forge Purview (so much so he wants it to spread to all beings regardless of the consequences), and his Virtues would be Fecundity (Titan Virtue, reflecting his drive to create) and Storge (Theoi Virtue, creating a familial bond to his creations)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T12:44:51-08:00","id":1009436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1009430#post1009430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think being capable of benevolence (or engaging in actions that happen to benefit humanity that humans interpret as benevolence) and having the more intimate Fate-based connection the Gods have is the same thing.<br /> <br /> It's also possible that in Scion's terminology, Prometheus was a Titan who made a transition to godhood. That transition isn't something that exists in Greek Myth, but it is something implied by Scion's usage of the terms.<br /> <br /> <br /> Based on the Titans in the Tuatha write-up, it seems that Titans who align with the gods take one Titan virtue and one Pantheon virtue, so were I writing up Prometheus as a Titan, he'd be dominated by the Forge Purview (so much so he wants it to spread to all beings regardless of the consequences), and his Virtues would be Fecundity (Titan Virtue, reflecting his drive to create) and Storge (Theoi Virtue, creating a familial bond to his creations)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHe also loved his brother didn't he?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T12:46:15-08:00","id":1009438,"title":"","content":"I'm really hoping that the final draft presents the Netjer as being allied to many Titans. Geb as the Titan of Earth, Nut as Titan of Sky, and Ma'at as Titan of Order are the obvious ones. The only Titan I see them feuding with is Apep, Titan of Chaos, as I'm really hoping 2e drops the dumb &quot;Aten is behind monotheism&quot; thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T13:06:21-08:00","id":1009446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1009438#post1009438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really hoping that the final draft presents the Netjer as being allied to many Titans. Geb as the Titan of Earth, Nut as Titan of Sky, and Ma'at as Titan of Order are the obvious ones. The only Titan I see them feuding with is Apep, Titan of Chaos, as I'm really hoping 2e drops the dumb &quot;Aten is behind monotheism&quot; thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not having them be Primordials?<br /> <br /> It's been mentioned that the basic concept for monotheism this time round is a culture-jamming technique the pantheons make use of. Aten's contribution to the mix was the creation of solipsistic monotheism, monotheism that denies the existence of other gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T13:32:36-08:00","id":1009461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1009446#post1009446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not having them be Primordials?<br /> <br /> It's been mentioned that the basic concept for monotheism this time round is a culture-jamming technique the pantheons make use of. Aten's contribution to the mix was the creation of solipsistic monotheism, monotheism that denies the existence of other gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truthfully, I'm still a little fuzzy on the Titan/Primordial divide.<br /> <br /> And while I like that take on monotheism, I dislike the idea that Aten is somehow related to the Abrahamic faiths' solipsistic monotheism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T13:37:12-08:00","id":1009462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1009446#post1009446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not having them be Primordials?<br /> <br /> It's been mentioned that the basic concept for monotheism this time round is a culture-jamming technique the pantheons make use of. Aten's contribution to the mix was the creation of solipsistic monotheism, monotheism that denies the existence of other gods.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm going to be honest, the treatment of monotheism is the thing I'm dreading most. I don't mind having baddies come from monotheism but I'm hoping monotheistic religions and myths get more respectful treatment than &quot;They're all a massive con that individual gods sometimes run.&quot; I mean I'm going to run a game that my players want to have run regardless but I'm going to be really disappointed if the cannon paints adherents of religions currently held by millions, if not billions, of people with a brush of &quot;They're all rubes.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T13:38:03-08:00","id":1009464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1009461#post1009461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Truthfully, I'm still a little fuzzy on the Titan/Primordial divide.<br /> <br /> And while I like that take on monotheism, I dislike the idea that Aten is somehow related to the Abrahamic faiths' solipsistic monotheism.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe way i understood Titans are either gods utterly obsessed with their purviews and no relations with humanity and usually are the first beings showing up in creation myths. Primordials literally are the things that make the universe,they are inseperable from their purview. Nut is one and the same with the heavens geb is one in the same with the Earth etc.... Primordials are also generally the beings who created the world in the first place and sometimes also <i>are </i>the world","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T13:39:30-08:00","id":1009465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1009462#post1009462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I'm going to be honest, the treatment of monotheism is the thing I'm dreading most. I don't mind having baddies come from monotheism but I'm hoping monotheistic religions and myths get more respectful treatment than &quot;They're all a massive con that individual gods sometimes run.&quot; I mean I'm going to run a game that my players want to have run regardless but I'm going to be really disappointed if the cannon paints adherents of religions currently held by millions, if not billions, of people with a brush of &quot;They're all rubes.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHoly mother of christ i agree with you 100%","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T13:55:49-08:00","id":1009470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1009462#post1009462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I'm going to be honest, the treatment of monotheism is the thing I'm dreading most. I don't mind having baddies come from monotheism but I'm hoping monotheistic religions and myths get more respectful treatment than &quot;They're all a massive con that individual gods sometimes run.&quot; I mean I'm going to run a game that my players want to have run regardless but I'm going to be really disappointed if the cannon paints adherents of religions currently held by millions, if not billions, of people with a brush of &quot;They're all rubes.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm right there with you, and while Neal has said we'll deal with the Abrahamic faiths in the Canaanite writeup I'm having a hard time imagining that as anything other than &quot;El has a Mantle named YHVH that some of his followers ran with and turned into a one god Pantheon.&quot; At least at my table, the Abrahamic faiths have as much magical mojo to throw around in The World as anyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T17:46:50-08:00","id":1009570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1009462#post1009462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I'm going to be honest, the treatment of monotheism is the thing I'm dreading most. I don't mind having baddies come from monotheism but I'm hoping monotheistic religions and myths get more respectful treatment than &quot;They're all a massive con that individual gods sometimes run.&quot; I mean I'm going to run a game that my players want to have run regardless but I'm going to be really disappointed if the cannon paints adherents of religions currently held by millions, if not billions, of people with a brush of &quot;They're all rubes.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well Monotheism (as opposed to Henotheism) is OBJECTIVELY FALSE in a setting that contains multiple gods. That's just unavoidable. To have &quot;Monotheism&quot; coexist as true along with Polytheism, you do have to adjust it to Henotheism.<br /> <br /> If In Nomine can do &quot;polytheistic deities are creatures of the Marches born from human dreams, as opposed to the Celestials who built the universe created by the One True God&quot;, and Demon: the Fallen can do &quot;polytheistic religions are inspired by Angels, particularly the Rebels, with cult idols often being Earthbound Demons&quot;, etc etc - I don't see what the problem with an explicitly polytheistic setting leaning into its specific truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T17:50:38-08:00","id":1009572,"title":"","content":"My working theory is that there are going to be several primordials that claim to be the One True God, and there will be hinted a possibility that they are all \u201cMantles\u201d of a single theoretical being similar to Fate, that nobody ever sees directly. These \u201cmonotheistic\u201d Primordials would belong to appropriate Pantheons, such as the Elohim, Orisha, Yazata, Devas, etc. \u2014 that is, any Pantheon whose mythology includes the concept of one greater god over all the rest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T00:13:18-08:00","id":1009661,"title":"","content":"*sigh*<br /> Guys.<br /> Can the game about pagan gods and their children stay polytheistic?<br /> please?<br /> pretty please?<br /> ... Well, I'll always have the first edition, I guess. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T03:20:08-08:00","id":1009704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanthias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1009661#post1009661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*sigh*<br /> ... Well, I'll always have the first edition, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having run some 1E games... Er, it'll probably be better for you to take 2E and if anything relating to Monotheistic religions comes just just gently scribble it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T04:25:31-08:00","id":1009719,"title":"","content":"Or don't worry about it; I don't foresee Scion becoming In Nominee any time soon. The issue isn't how to turn it into a game about monotheism, but rather how to address that elephant in the room that is the prominence of monotheistic faiths in the modern world, combined with the fact that the game is about myths coming alive in the modern world. <br /> <br /> And strict polytheism doesn't really work for many of the Pantheons that are already going to be included, several of which are borderline henotheistic; so if the game can handle Yoruba and a Caribbean mythology (the latter of which is a blend of native African and Christian beliefs), I don't what the big deal is about the third of fourth book in the series including an answer as to how Abrahamic faiths fit in, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T05:02:27-08:00","id":1009726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1009570#post1009570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well Monotheism (as opposed to Henotheism) is OBJECTIVELY FALSE in a setting that contains multiple gods. That's just unavoidable. To have &quot;Monotheism&quot; coexist as true along with Polytheism, you do have to adjust it to Henotheism.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's fair because the various monotheistic monotheistic religions and their myths could be given respectful treatment under that paradigm. All religions in this game have a level of fiction applied to them and if part of the fiction applied to monotheistic religions is that they are actually henotheistic, that's fine with me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1009570#post1009570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If In Nomine can do &quot;polytheistic deities are creatures of the Marches born from human dreams, as opposed to the Celestials who built the universe created by the One True God&quot;, and Demon: the Fallen can do &quot;polytheistic religions are inspired by Angels, particularly the Rebels, with cult idols often being Earthbound Demons&quot;, etc etc - I don't see what the problem with an explicitly polytheistic setting leaning into its specific truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well to be fair, Scion's specific truth is that ALL legends and myths are built on a grain of truth. That truth is put into question if the treatment some of those myths is boiled down to &quot;That god doesn't exist. It was a political play being run by X.&quot;<br /> <br /> And while don't know enough about Nomine to but your statement into context, I am at least vaguely aware of the Demon setting from having read things about the game. If what you said is true and the game specifically calls out all polytheistic religions as being created by fallen angels, I couldn't fault someone for either not playing the game or changing the default setting at their table because they were offended at the way their own religion was treated. It's one thing for a game to say &quot;Our game treats X as being true and all things not X are incorrect.&quot; But I don't really see it as necessary or adding anything to any setting to say &quot;Since our game says X is true, all things not X should be treated as a <b>purposeful </b>lie.&quot; <br /> <br /> <br /> I should also clarify that I haven't seen anything that lets me think Neall's not going to treat monotheistic religions with respect. 1e did a pretty bad job of handling those religions to the point that it would have done better to just stay silent about them. Neal's obviously got some plans for them since Knight Templars are going to be a thing. But since it's a topic that was handled poorly in the past edition, I have some trepidation about how it's going to be handled in the new one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T07:17:03-08:00","id":1009758,"title":"","content":"Truth be told all i need is a cobfirmation that ny god is just as real as the others and that he exists in his own right instead of being a ploy. I just need a &quot;yup Jesus is as real and as powerful as Hades&quot; thats isb enough","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T08:07:55-08:00","id":1009792,"title":"","content":"I've said this before, but it's a game about a fictional world where the polytheistic faiths of many cultures are all real and demonstrably involved in the lives of their faithful. It isn't a commentary on Christianity, Judaism, Islam, Jainism, Sikhism, or any of our real-world faiths (including those who still worship those same polytheistic Pantheons). If you want that, by all means do what works for you, but Scion isn't meant as a way to validate or detail the real faiths of the players - there are more than enough books and groups in the world who can and will do that. For all those here who are calling for more involvement and validation of the Abraham faiths, there are also those of us who hope that Scion focuses on what it's about at it's core; playing the Champions of the Great Deities of Old as they change their world, with information on those Pantheon and their Gods and Goddesses. If there <i>is </i>a focus on Abraham faiths, I would hope it comes as an optional supplement for those who want it, not as part of the core game rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5627,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","user":"Purple Snit","date":". 11-29-2016, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T09:49:43-08:00","id":1009837,"title":"","content":"Eh, okay so I wasn't intending to totally derail the thread. So in the interest of not getting the wrath of a mod called down on us, let me rephrase this as a question for Neall and anyone who wants to discuss the relative place of monotheism in the game can take it to another thread of some sort (not that I can boss people around, I'm just not going to participate in derailing this thread further).<br /> <br /> So Neall, are religions that are traditionally monotheistic going to be presented as being fundamentally different than a polytheistic ones? That is to say, will storytellers have to house rule significant elements of the game's setting in order to allow their players to make scions of a god from a traditionally monotheistic religion, or will there be sufficient play space left available in the writing to where a storyteller can simply use the &quot;create your own pantheon&quot; rules you're publishing in the companion to make the god and have the player go from there with little or no adjustment to the setting as a whole?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T10:57:27-08:00","id":1009864,"title":"","content":"The easiest solution to the monotheism issue is that a monotheistic tradition can simply claim there's a single overwhelming cosmic Godhead that is far above all the pantheons claiming to be gods. A particular god in a monotheistic tradition (e.g. El) can contend (s)he is the voice of the Godhead, or an incarnation of the Godhead, or something along those lines. That god becomes the (possibly unreliable) representative of the Godhead, and can be &quot;good&quot;, &quot;bad&quot; or whatever.<br /> <br /> After all, the gods of Scion really aren't in the same class as the truly transcendent gods of real-world monotheistic traditions. Scion's gods are powerful, but they aren't omniscient or omnipotent. So any player, or character, or NPC god can easily believe that there's something infinitely superior to the &quot;gods&quot; that appear in the game. You can then proceed to play the game on its own terms. ---Jim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4310-jagardner","name":"jagardner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T12:30:00-08:00","id":1009893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jagardner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1009864#post1009864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After all, the gods of Scion really aren't in the same class as the truly transcendent gods of real-world monotheistic traditions. Scion's gods are powerful, but they aren't omniscient or omnipotent.</div> </div> </div> </div> The gods aren't; but what about the Primordials?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T13:12:44-08:00","id":1009912,"title":"","content":"No, the easiest solution to the issue is to say that, in the presence of an active Netjer, Elohim, Anunnaki, Yazata, and Alihah, the worship of YHWH, Allah, and their ilk simply never got off the ground in the canon Scion world. [It isn't any different <i>for the purposes of this game</i>, to say that &quot;Capital G God isn't real, but Zeus is&quot; as opposed to &quot;Capital G God IS real, but Zeus isn't&quot;] And then to issue a separate supplement for those who wish to explore monotheism in their games. People don't try to shoehorn real-world faiths into their Pathfinder/D&amp;D campaigns - can we please not do so here? If the absence of a strong representation for the Abrahamic faiths is going to offend you, then maybe this isn't the right game for you.<br /> [To phrase this as something to the developer: Can we please keep the game on track to be what it has been - a game about Scions of the Gods of Myth - as opposed to trying to be inoffensive to and inclusive of faiths in the real world?]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T13:46:23-08:00","id":1009924,"title":"","content":"the Divine and the Wicked, a major inspiration for 2e, featured Lucifer as part of its roster. And you're setting up a false dichotomy in your final phrasing: you don't have to compromise the game's focus on mythology in the modern world in order to accommodate Abrahamic mythology \u2014 especially when some of the tools that allow for more accurate portrayals of some of the existing Pantheons can be easily repurposed to support the inclusion of Abraham's descendants (literal and spiritual). Given how easy and painless inclusion can be, why are you fighting for exclusion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T13:49:52-08:00","id":1009926,"title":"","content":"It may seem like the easiest, but the trouble is that removing the Abrahamic religions results in a history very different from the one we know.<br /> <br /> We're not getting that. We're getting a world where the Abrahamics do exist, if perhaps in modified form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T14:05:29-08:00","id":1009930,"title":"","content":"At some point, developers obviously have to say, &quot;Look, if the material seriously offends you, this isn't a game you should play.&quot; But I think it would be helpful to provide Storytellers with some guidance for talking with players who might be on the fence. Considering how sensitive the developers are trying to be toward people who believe in, say, Yoruban and Algonquin faiths, it doesn't seem out of line to be considerate toward believers in monotheistic faiths too. I'm really just suggesting a boxed sidebar saying, &quot;Here's are some approaches to consider if it becomes an issue.&quot; ---Jim<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4310-jagardner","name":"jagardner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T15:16:43-08:00","id":1009961,"title":"","content":"I'm not trying to derail this thread, so I'll keep my response as brief as possible. I'm not lobbying for exclusion - I'm lobbying against the people who seem to be trying to make Abrahamic faiths a major part of a game where the focus is supposed to be on <i>all the other faiths</i> instead. Put them in a sidebar, a separate supplement, no problem. But all the &quot;please include Jesus because I'll be upset if you don't&quot; or &quot;Include a godhead as a band-aid because the other Gods aren't omnipotent anyway&quot; or &quot;Give us a pantheon of angels and saints&quot; stuff is really not what Scion is supposed to be about, which is the Pantheons of Myth and their children. Abrahamic religion is all around us, and if someone wants to make their own game that way, go right ahead. But can we please keep the real-world monotheism on a back burner in a game about pantheism in it's full, fictional glory?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T15:29:23-08:00","id":1009967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1009912#post1009912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the easiest solution to the issue is to say that, in the presence of an active Netjer, Elohim, Anunnaki, Yazata, and Alihah, the worship of YHWH, Allah, and their ilk simply never got off the ground in the canon Scion world. [It isn't any different <i>for the purposes of this game</i>, to say that &quot;Capital G God isn't real, but Zeus is&quot; as opposed to &quot;Capital G God IS real, but Zeus isn't&quot;] And then to issue a separate supplement for those who wish to explore monotheism in their games. People don't try to shoehorn real-world faiths into their Pathfinder/D&amp;D campaigns - can we please not do so here? If the absence of a strong representation for the Abrahamic faiths is going to offend you, then maybe this isn't the right game for you.<br /> [To phrase this as something to the developer: Can we please keep the game on track to be what it has been - a game about Scions of the Gods of Myth - as opposed to trying to be inoffensive to and inclusive of faiths in the real world?]</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe only problem I see with saying &quot;Monotheism never really got off the ground in this world&quot; is the sheer, mindboggling amount of changes that would make for history. For better or worse, the rise of Christianity and, later, Islam had HUGE impact on the shaping of the world we know today. Take Christianity out of the picture? How much of history would be radically changed?<br /> <br /> \u200bA move like that would almost REQUIRE Neall and the team to sit down and spend a lot of time brainstorming on how radically different the Scion world must look like compared to ours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T15:49:26-08:00","id":1009976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1009961#post1009961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not trying to derail this thread, so I'll keep my response as brief as possible. I'm not lobbying for exclusion - I'm lobbying against the people who seem to be trying to make Abrahamic faiths a major part of a game where the focus is supposed to be on <i>all the other faiths</i> instead.</div> </div> </div> </div> Nobody's trying to make the Abrahamic faiths a major part of the game. What you're seeing is that the Abrahamic faiths are a puzzle right now; and since people are naturally drawn to a puzzle, it's getting an inordinate amount of attention. Once the matter is resolved, I'm pretty sure the hype will die down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1009961#post1009961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Put them in a sidebar, a separate supplement, no problem. But all the &quot;please include Jesus because I'll be upset if you don't&quot; or &quot;Include a godhead as a band-aid because the other Gods aren't omnipotent anyway&quot; or &quot;Give us a pantheon of angels and saints&quot; stuff is really not what Scion is supposed to be about, which is the Pantheons of Myth and their children. Abrahamic religion is all around us, and if someone wants to make their own game that way, go right ahead. But can we please keep the real-world monotheism on a back burner in a game about pantheism in it's full, fictional glory?</div> </div> </div> </div> There's a section in the \u201cwhat we know so far\u201d where one of the devs addresses the flame wars that we going on at the time concerning Atlantis and the National Pantheons:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">I<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> will say this - Scion has a focus, and that's my primary goal. But I'm sorry, I don't understand the gamer mentality that says a line ought never publish options that they themselves will never use. So no, I'm not making any promises not to revisit some of those concepts in the future. Grouse all you like about &quot;wasted word count&quot; or whatever you like, the fact is I intend to make of this system a broad, useful system for the telling of some great stories about heroes whose power derives from ancient legend, using that power to forge their own myths for the next age.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">I guarantee you that I'll put something in these books you hate. I guarantee that because we're going to put a LOT of stuff in them, over the lifespan of this line, because its potential is broad as well as deep. </span></span></div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">I'm pretty sure this applies equally well to the Abrahamic faiths.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T15:49:48-08:00","id":1009977,"title":"","content":"I hope they <i>have </i>sat down and brainstormed on exactly that. Isn't it going to require a whole lot of re-thinking to <i>include</i> all the powerful Pantheons that the game will center around? How different is a Middle East without Islam as almost the only surviving dominant faith? Do the Netjer fill that void? The Anunnaki? The Alihah? Or Western Europe or North America, where the Norse, Bogovi, Tuatha, Theoi, Finnish, Algonquian, Inue, Anasazi, Coast Salish, Tarascan, Olmec, Maya, Aztec, etc. Pantheons are still vibrant and alive, in place of the near-exclusivity of Christianity and Judaism? China and Japan? Aboriginal Australia? The Incans, Moche, Guarani, and their kin? Makemake on Easter Island? It requires a huge rethinking <i>anyway</i>, which is part of the fun - the whole &quot;what if&quot; world-building of it. And including the Abrahamic faiths, just as a way of minimizing having to make change in the world history, seems like a lazy way out that I don't think Neall and the others would take. The point is to write your own myths, in the spirit of the myths of our own ancient world, using the Pantheons of Old as your source, not to have &quot;the modern world as it is with a few odd cults of pagans worshiping nearly-dead myths.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T15:54:53-08:00","id":1009980,"title":"","content":"I hope whatever Neall and the writers come up with for Abrahamic faiths, that it is <i>not</i> any variation of &quot;There is a supreme godhead equivalent to fate.&quot; That edges way too far into &quot;one true religion&quot; territory and I don't really want to see that kind of endorsement in Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T16:15:38-08:00","id":1009988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1009977#post1009977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope they <i>have </i>sat down and brainstormed on exactly that. Isn't it going to require a whole lot of re-thinking to <i>include</i> all the powerful Pantheons that the game will center around? How different is a Middle East without Islam as almost the only surviving dominant faith? Do the Netjer fill that void? The Anunnaki? The Alihah? Or Western Europe or North America, where the Norse, Bogovi, Tuatha, Theoi, Finnish, Algonquian, Inue, Anasazi, Coast Salish, Tarascan, Olmec, Maya, Aztec, etc. Pantheons are still vibrant and alive, in place of the near-exclusivity of Christianity and Judaism? China and Japan? Aboriginal Australia? The Incans, Moche, Guarani, and their kin? Makemake on Easter Island? It requires a huge rethinking <i>anyway</i>, which is part of the fun - the whole &quot;what if&quot; world-building of it. And including the Abrahamic faiths, just as a way of minimizing having to make change in the world history, seems like a lazy way out that I don't think Neall and the others would take. The point is to write your own myths, in the spirit of the myths of our own ancient world, using the Pantheons of Old as your source, not to have &quot;the modern world as it is with a few odd cults of pagans worshiping nearly-dead myths.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> They may very well do that in a Shard. But in the main setting? I give you <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-world-scion-second-edition-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\">the World</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T16:18:18-08:00","id":1009990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1009980#post1009980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope whatever Neall and the writers come up with for Abrahamic faiths, that it is <i>not</i> any variation of &quot;There is a supreme godhead equivalent to fate.&quot; That edges way too far into &quot;one true religion&quot; territory and I don't really want to see that kind of endorsement in Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div> Even if it's perfectly fitting for, say, the Devas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T17:04:06-08:00","id":1010001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1009988#post1009988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They may very well do that in a Shard. But in the main setting? I give you <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-world-scion-second-edition-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\">the World</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I read that. I would hope that when fleshed out beyond a brief outline, that it will be more detailed than &quot;our world as it is, with a few small changes, some extra temples, and the odd new holy symbol&quot;, because that would oversimplify a world where there are multiple faiths, stronger cultures because of that, and a different base for everything from holidays to national boundaries. But they will do what they feel is best, I can change anything I don't like, and that's cool. No game survives contact with the players unchanged. I'm just arguing for more polytheism and less monotheism in the basic recipe. Hopefully, that's how it will work out in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T18:21:28-08:00","id":1010020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1009990#post1009990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Even if it's perfectly fitting for, say, the Devas?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just tired of people asking for a one true omniscient omnipotent god in this mythology game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T20:51:28-08:00","id":1010044,"title":"","content":"I'm kind of with Purple on this. The focus of the game should (and probably will) be on the polytheistic pantheons. I think it would be perfectly respectful to have a sidebar somewhere in the world section saying that there are those who believe in monotheism and a one true God theology but are not focused on in this book. There you go, monotheism validated and mentioned and left open for a future supplement or shard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T21:37:53-08:00","id":1010050,"title":"","content":"This has drifted way off-topic, so my final point on this:<br /> <br /> The devs have already revealed that the default setting is not going to exclude the Abrahamic faiths, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5627_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5627\" data-vbnamecard=\"5627\">Purple Snit</a> is requesting. They have also apparently revealed that the truth behind the Abrahamic faiths in the default setting will be addressed in the supplement that's going to be introducing the Canaanite Pantheon (Demigod, I think?); so we're not going to be getting a major focus on Abrahamic faiths before then, and probably not even then. I honestly don't expect to see the Abrahamic faiths getting any sort of special treatment<sup><span style=\"font-size:8px\">\u2605</span></sup>; but neither am I expecting them to be treated any more disrespectfully than any of the polytheistic mythologies that <i>will be</i> the focus of the game<sup><span style=\"font-size:8px\">\u2020</span></sup>. The only reason this is a big deal right now is that <i>we don't know how they're going to do that</i>. Like I said before, it's a puzzle; and puzzles attract attention.<br /> <hr /><span style=\"color:gray\">\u2605 That is, there won't be a single game mechanic or concept employed to depict the truth behind the Abrahamic faiths that doesn't apply equally well to already-confirmed polytheistic Pantheons.<br /> <br /> \u2020 as per the excerpt I provided from \u201cWhat we know\u201d, the devs are aiming for breadth as well as depth, and there <i>will</i> be things included in the game that will be hated by proponents of focusing exclusively on scions of polytheistic mythologies, because they lead to more options for the game.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-30-2016, 12:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T22:35:52-08:00","id":1010064,"title":"","content":"All I'll say is that it seems absurd to bar some of the biggest religions out there from the game about religions, and that I'll gladly play a game with angels over a game without.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T23:18:29-08:00","id":1010069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1010064#post1010064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I'll say is that it seems absurd to bar some of the biggest religions out there from the game about religions, and that I'll gladly play a game with angels over a game without.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of it is that there's a group of people for whom the thought of the Abrahamic Religion's influence in the game was literally something they didn't think about. They saw the prompt for Scion, and thought &quot;Oh sweet, I can be the kid of some of the classic gods? BADASS!&quot;<br /> <br /> And when someone asks about the Abrahamic Monotheistic faiths, it kind of crashes, since it might have been something they were content to just slot in &quot;Well it probably exists but at our table we're probably not going to bring it up&quot; because to them and their friends/future fellow players, <i>that wasn't something that would come up</i>. They may think it's an odd question to ask, like someone who's very into economics questioning how the economy of Dungeons and Dragons works when the PCs are flooding the markets with coins made of precious metals.<br /> <br /> Not that the economist is WRONG in noting that there's a lot to talk about with currency in older societies. Just... 99% of D&amp;D players don't think about the practicality and logistics and economic viability of D&amp;D because most of those players are playing to fight monsters and raid dungeons.<br /> <br /> (I admit I'm making a lot of assumptions here)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T07:20:20-08:00","id":1010193,"title":"","content":"Is it so hard to include them? No need for a full pantheon,just a sideline saying &quot;yes. the christian-judaic-islamic god is as real as the others&quot; Would that be stepping in someone toes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T07:47:20-08:00","id":1010199,"title":"","content":"They don't have to be excluded to make me happy. I just get frustrated when a cool game about playing the more-than-mortal children of the mythical deities is met with &quot;can I play a vanilla human?&quot; and &quot;can we please have more Christianity?&quot; I just want to speak up and let the devs know that I for one would like the focus to stay on the mythical Pantheons, and not get distracted by worrying about fitting the Abraham faiths in when they aren't necessary for the game world to function. Sidebar info, or, as I've said, a separate supplement, would work just fine to cover the matter, IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T08:01:42-08:00","id":1010206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1010199#post1010199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't have to be excluded to make me happy. I just get frustrated when a cool game about playing the more-than-mortal children of the mythical deities is met with &quot;can I play a vanilla human?&quot; and &quot;can we please have more Christianity?&quot; I just want to speak up and let the devs know that I for one would like the focus to stay on the mythical Pantheons, and not get distracted by worrying about fitting the Abraham faiths in when they aren't necessary for the game world to function. Sidebar info, or, as I've said, a separate supplement, would work just fine to cover the matter, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's a wide range of area between &quot;I hope monotheism isn't reduced to only being a political play by certain gods and people will be able to make an epic hero from that faith without changing the setting too much&quot; and &quot;I want the game line to stop focusing on other religions and only focus on this one.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T08:24:51-08:00","id":1010209,"title":"","content":"Yes, there is. But saying &quot;all the other Gods are just manifestations of human dreams&quot; [as in In Nomine] or something similar is disrespectful to the very source material that is the root of the game, not to mention all the people who believed/believe in those beings. I don't have an issue with monotheism being included - I just don't want it to be a major focus of the game. For me, this is about the Gods/Goddesses of world Pantheism and their champions, and I wanted to air my concerns that the &quot;don't forget the Abrahamic faiths&quot; voices weren't the only ones out here. And I think I've done that sufficiently on this particular thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T12:01:11-08:00","id":1010290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1010193#post1010193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it so hard to include them? No need for a full pantheon,just a sideline saying &quot;yes. the christian-judaic-islamic god is as real as the others&quot; Would that be stepping in someone toes?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be stepping on monotheism's toes, actually. Because then suddenly having other gods be real will become a problem.<br /> These things just don't mix.<br /> Even if one chooses to portray all legend as equally &quot;real/unreal&quot;, monotheistic legend that imagines a single true deity that encompasses everything will inevitably force the author to choose: either that deity is what it claims to be (and then polytheistic gods are either &quot;demons&quot; or some kind of &quot;underlings&quot; or &quot;emanations&quot;, both of which is wrong in a polytheistic setting even if it is the way some real-world faiths actually work.) or said deity is a faker at best (or first edition Aten).<br /> &quot;Including&quot; monotheism as something other than a faith a certain number of people adhere to into a polytheistic setting means excluding all other deities, because then they will have to be &quot;second-rate gods&quot;. And this is not fine. &quot;All views on religion are equal&quot; in the real world is the only acceptable approach precisely because there is no objective way to determine the truth. Here, we all are just seekers. But in Scion, your character can have Pele for his mother, and read something written by Djehuti himself, and if that is invalidated (which is looking very likely), then what is left of the game?<br /> Okay, yes, I should not be such a sore loser. Just had such high hopes for the game, and having a hard time letting go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5530,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","user":"Xanthias","date":". 11-30-2016, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T12:37:36-08:00","id":1010306,"title":"","content":"The other concern would be Monotheistic scions integrating into a group with other scions, not just from a story perspective but from a mechanical one as well. If we are respectfully following the lore and beliefs of the Abrahamic faiths, then there is only one god and no chance for apotheosis, so automatically we know that those scions can not reach god level. Depending on how powerful demigods are that may also be off limits if it tramples on the powers of Yahweh (his power created a series of miracles, not any power of those chosen by him, i.e. Moses didn't part the Red Sea, Yahweh did.) So there's a chance that these scions could only stay at Hero level. You could try to play an incarnate Scion, but that would basically be towing the line of sacrilege to even suggest that in the game. If we're talking about an &quot;Angelic&quot; pantheon, well that raises other questions. If there is an overarching God above them, what level are they at, Primordial? Something greater? Does that start to play into the &quot;only one true God/religion in a world of verified polytheistic beliefs? Can humans become angels in this pantheon as a form of apotheosis? And if so, where does the basis for that come from? Because I'm pretty sure that's not even something suggested in any of the Abrahamic faiths. I've seen the idea of Saints thrown around, but as far as I know, Saints are a primarily Catholic construct, so do Jewish and Protestant scions in this story not get to reach apotheosis because they have the wrong beliefs? (I'm purposefully not including Islam in my question because I don't know enough about their beliefs to comment. If someone here is Muslim maybe you can elaborate on how they would fit into this idea.) Not to mention the amount of syncretization and euhemerism that went on with various other gods and saints so are you saying that those gods are lesser again? That they were kind of taken into this pantheon by force? By choice? Are they mantles? I think if someone were to play in an Abrahamic faith pantheon it would have to be an ONLY Abrahamic faiths game because I'm not really seeing how the others can fit into a game with them. Which is fine, but in that case it should be it's own supplement or shard, not included in any corebook where it might cause confusion.<br /> <br /> Tldr: There's room for monotheism and the Abrahamic faiths in Scion, but as a standalone supplement with maybe some mechanical tweaks as opposed to included in any of the core books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T12:38:52-08:00","id":1010310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanthias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1010290#post1010290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be stepping on monotheism's toes, actually. Because then suddenly having other gods be real will become a problem.<br /> These things just don't mix.<br /> Even if one chooses to portray all legend as equally &quot;real/unreal&quot;, monotheistic legend that imagines a single true deity that encompasses everything will inevitably force the author to choose: either that deity is what it claims to be (and then polytheistic gods are either &quot;demons&quot; or some kind of &quot;underlings&quot; or &quot;emanations&quot;, both of which is wrong in a polytheistic setting even if it is the way some real-world faiths actually work.) or said deity is a faker at best (or first edition Aten).<br /> &quot;Including&quot; monotheism as something other than a faith a certain number of people adhere to into a polytheistic setting means excluding all other deities, because then they will have to be &quot;second-rate gods&quot;. And this is not fine. &quot;All views on religion are equal&quot; in the real world is the only acceptable approach precisely because there is no objective way to determine the truth. Here, we all are just seekers. But in Scion, your character can have Pele for his mother, and read something written by Djehuti himself, and if that is invalidated (which is looking very likely), then what is left of the game?<br /> Okay, yes, I should not be such a sore loser. Just had such high hopes for the game, and having a hard time letting go.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bBut all religions of scion have to make concessions. for instance the aztecs believed cipactli was the Earth and the greeks believed Gaea was the Earth. Thor is the only god of thunder if you ask a norseman and a ehyptian would say only nut controls thunder and etc.... there's Always concessions. the blog post about the world made a point of saying all myths are true. including the ones contradicting each other","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T14:30:52-08:00","id":1010340,"title":"","content":"Guys? There's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism\">a whole thread dedicated to this debate</a>. Could we maybe continue the argument there instead of further derailing the <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ask Neal</span></b> thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T14:35:10-08:00","id":1010345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1010340#post1010340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys? There's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/975846-monotheism\">a whole thread dedicated to this debate</a>. Could we maybe continue the argument there instead of further derailing the <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ask Neal</span></b> thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYer right. Anyways i do have 2 question.<br /> \u200bIs there any mechanics enabling &quot;lesser beings&quot; face the gods? Anway for an vampire to face am aesir and still have a chance to win?<br /> \u200bWhat makes someone legend go up one dot or down one dot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T14:35:49-08:00","id":1010346,"title":"","content":"Personally I think all it would take is putting a big in setting question mark over the whole thing. So, if you ask Mithra, Horus, or any other god that would have been active in the area about Moses, Jesus, and so on their honest answers could be, &quot;Well something was going on their, and it was divine, but no one ever met the god or gods responsible. Or at least no one owned up to it&quot; Now it's a mystery even to the gods, it might be a &quot;one true god&quot; even they can't comprehend, or it might have been Loki doing it for the lulz. But it isn't active now so it can be safely ignored as a maybe unless a group wants to explore it more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T15:03:22-08:00","id":1010355,"title":"","content":"So the atlazani preview seems to indicate that the new purview is going to be working off a universal sacrifice system. will the translation guide support the original psp for scions that want to use the legend boosting version, or is it getting completely reworked for 2.0?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T15:14:34-08:00","id":1010361,"title":"","content":"A teotl preview huh? well what i have to say is<br /> <span style=\"font-size:36px\">\u200bFUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUCK YEEEEEEEEEEES!</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T15:28:51-08:00","id":1010367,"title":"","content":"Now more seriously, I Have a deep love for this pantheon. they men something special to me. And i was hoping to see what the scion writers would do to them and i'm so happy about it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T18:17:30-08:00","id":1010438,"title":"","content":"I have noticed that we are again seeing a type of animal (or the more troubling &quot;all&quot;) associated with the Beasts purview.<br /> <br /> If this is how we still handle the Beasts (nee Animal) purview, can you please give a more direct answer within the text regarding whether a Scion must inherit their Parent's specific animal?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T19:53:13-08:00","id":1010465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1010438#post1010438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have noticed that we are again seeing a type of animal (or the more troubling &quot;all&quot;) associated with the Beasts purview.<br /> <br /> If this is how we still handle the Beasts (nee Animal) purview, can you please give a more direct answer within the text regarding whether a Scion must inherit their Parent's specific animal?</div> </div> </div> </div>We will, and the answer is &quot;nope.&quot; You can even pick the full Beasts Purview, without limits.<br /> <br /> Same for Passion and Artistry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T20:06:09-08:00","id":1010467,"title":"","content":"I noticed that the Teotl seem to have more references to their place/dealings within the modern World compared to the other pantheons we have seen. Is this just a difference in writers? or something that has been emphasized in later drafts since the earlier pantheons were released? or do some pantheons just have a significantly larger pressence in the World?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T20:06:36-08:00","id":1010915,"title":"","content":"I have to say I love the new write ups for the Teotl. As a pantheon I'm only passingly familiar with, 1e made all of them except Quetzalcoatl seem a stone's throw from bloodthirsty nutjob, this presentation offers a pantheon that you could actually see someone worshiping.<br /> <br /> The PSP mentioned being able to use a boon or marvel on someone that sacrifices within a certain distance of you, does that mean boons are going to have a good amount of long lasting, less impressive effects? Things along the lines of the old Blessing of health or confer protection boons for example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T09:53:26-08:00","id":1012048,"title":"","content":"Hey guys! I'm curious about what happens when a god is a member of two different pantheons. Does a Persian scion of Mithra have access to the same options as a Roman one? If I encounter Maman Brigitte in her mantle as Samedi's wife, could she still lay a geas on me? *Seinfeld Voice* And what's the deal with the Buddhist gods? Do they all just keep their native powers as written, even if one is Deva and the other is Shen, or do they put on slightly different mantles that change them somehow? And would that be similar to how a do-it-yourself multicultural pantheon would work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12598-karasu-sama","name":"Karasu-sama","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T12:17:13-08:00","id":1012097,"title":"","content":"Last we heard Mithra and Mithras we're going to be different gods, but it was still up in the air.<br /> <br /> Manman Brigitte is probably closer related to the Orisha wind goddess Oya. I imagine her political and personal relationship with the Irish goddess whose name she borrowed is complicated to say the least, but they're definitely different goddesses.<br /> <br /> There are gods who are part of multiple Pantheons though. Yama (Yan-luo, Emma-O) is perhaps the most proliferate example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T12:19:09-08:00","id":1012100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1012097#post1012097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last we heard Mithra and Mithras we're going to be different gods, but it was still up in the air.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where'd we hear that? Last I'd heard, Mithra and Mithra were the same god with different mantles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T20:56:38-08:00","id":1012965,"title":"","content":"Love! Love the Teotl preview!! So far,in my opinion, this is the best one! I can really see playing one their Scions. I would love to know wrote it. I saw the writers for the other pantheons but didn't see this author listed. Kudos to them! I can't wait to see more!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2386-katrina","name":"Katrina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T21:00:45-08:00","id":1012966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1012100#post1012100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where'd we hear that? Last I'd heard, Mithra and Mithra were the same god with different mantles.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought Neall had changed his mind from that position based on the evidence (and opinion of the majority of scholars on the subject) that there was no relationship at all besides Romans borrowing a name they'd heard. But maybe you are more up to date than me, I don't know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T22:37:24-08:00","id":1013014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1012966#post1012966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought Neall had changed his mind from that position based on the evidence (and opinion of the majority of scholars on the subject) that there was no relationship at all besides Romans borrowing a name they'd heard. But maybe you are more up to date than me, I don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just curious where he said he might be going with &quot;Mithra/Mithras aren't the same god&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T18:40:06-08:00","id":1014566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=530948#post530948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More than three powers per tier/also entirely different.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Knacks are a thing, but a little more concentrated. They're attached to something other than Attributes.<br /> <br /> Epics are gone in their original form. Sardonyx has an innate scaling mechanic right now (in the pre-playtesting phase of Scion); &quot;Epics&quot; are more permission to scale upwards, and there are Knacks that relate to Might. You can still shotput a Volkswagon.</div> </div> </div> </div>About Knacks. I was trying to figurate what Liminal Knacks do. Can you tell me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T19:19:00-08:00","id":1015095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1014566#post1014566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About Knacks. I was trying to figurate what Liminal Knacks do. Can you tell me?</div> </div> </div> </div>Liminal Knacks are about stealth, death, and thresholds. They do things like help you blend into cities and villages instantly, make strangers forget they saw you no matter how odd you appear, and bypass locks or use doorways with sympathetic teleportation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T04:30:25-08:00","id":1015209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1015095#post1015095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Liminal Knacks are about stealth, death, and thresholds. They do things like help you blend into cities and villages instantly, make strangers forget they saw you no matter how odd you appear, and bypass locks or use doorways with sympathetic teleportation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats liminawesome","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T10:49:42-08:00","id":1015301,"title":"","content":"Is a god's mantle by any chance, something with a phisyca manifestation? can it be touched or seen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T12:44:19-08:00","id":1015787,"title":"","content":"I remember somewhere I saw the suggestion that a scion might have innate access to one of their parent's purviews. Is that still a thing? If so, how early does that manifest? At the Visitation, or before that? I ask because the idea of a seven-year-old with the Sky purview causing a snow day to get out of school is as amusing as the idea of one accidentally electrocuting somebody is horrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T01:31:01-08:00","id":1016456,"title":"","content":"Previously, it was stated that &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">The Forge Purview is just as compatible with computer coding and super-science technology as it is with blacksmithing.&quot; <br /> <br /> Does that mean that you could play a constructed Scion that's purely software? A Divine AI?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12736-heliomance","name":"Heliomance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T02:04:46-08:00","id":1016460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heliomance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1016456#post1016456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Previously, it was stated that &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">The Forge Purview is just as compatible with computer coding and super-science technology as it is with blacksmithing.&quot;<br /> <br /> Does that mean that you could play a constructed Scion that's purely software? A Divine AI?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>As a gm I would allow that simply for the awesome factor, though I'd probably require you carry yourself around in a swarm of RC cars to justify having stats like Strength and such since those kind of have a default rating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T10:18:58-08:00","id":1016625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreepyShutIn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1015787#post1015787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember somewhere I saw the suggestion that a scion might have innate access to one of their parent's purviews. Is that still a thing? If so, how early does that manifest? At the Visitation, or before that? I ask because the idea of a seven-year-old with the Sky purview causing a snow day to get out of school is as amusing as the idea of one accidentally electrocuting somebody is horrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a vague recollection (so vague, in fact, that I might have made it up) that the preferred methodology for children with divine powers more had to do with Omens than actual access to purviews. Personally, I've always considered perviews something that can't really misfire the way that accidental magic can in Harry Potter for example. That said, it's your game. I'm sure you could make a seven-year-old with powers with a minimal amount of house ruling. If I'm even right about this whole thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12598-karasu-sama","name":"Karasu-sama","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T11:12:14-08:00","id":1016653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1012097#post1012097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last we heard Mithra and Mithras we're going to be different gods, but it was still up in the air.<br /> <br /> Manman Brigitte is probably closer related to the Orisha wind goddess Oya. I imagine her political and personal relationship with the Irish goddess whose name she borrowed is complicated to say the least, but they're definitely different goddesses.<br /> <br /> There are gods who are part of multiple Pantheons though. Yama (Yan-luo, Emma-O) is perhaps the most proliferate example.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Perhaps I should've used Yama as my example instead of Mithra.<br /> <br /> Still, even if you're right on both counts, it still raises some very interesting questions about how syncretism works in The World. I am no Vodouisant, nor a great (or even middling) scholar of Vodou, but I do have some small layman's knowledge. I know, for instance, that part of the transformation that turned the Orisha into their present Caribbean forms involved not only syncretism with Catholic saints, but also, to an admittedly FAR lesser extent, with the folk religion brought over by white Irish and Scottish indentured workers. After all, a not-insignificant number of depictions of Maman Brigitte show her as a white woman with red hair. <br /> <br /> And even if you've the right of it, and Maman Brigitte is Oya with nothing but a tangential relationship to Brigid of the Tuatha, that still leaves these two distinct goddesses syncretized with one Catholic saint, which still begs the question of how that relationship works. Is it like the Lugh/Lleu thing? I really want to know more about how such things work in game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12598-karasu-sama","name":"Karasu-sama","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T19:09:11-08:00","id":1016866,"title":"","content":"Regarding Callings<b>:</b> Will they have a transcendent form, akin to the avatar purviews or 1e's Ultimate Attributes?<br /> <br /> On another note: earlier, a purview for patron deities of cities was mentioned. Can you please tell us a little more about that, and how strongly said city would have to be tied to a pantheon's sphere of influence (i.e., could a Scion of Parvati who was born and raised in Pittsburgh aspire to become that city's divine patron)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","user":"yukikaze","date":". 12-18-2016, 03:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T15:07:23-08:00","id":1018930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=790453#post790453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can belong to multiple pantheons in the second edition.<br /> <br /> I <i>love </i>the Keepers of the World, and if anything they'll be a bigger part of 2e. There's even going to be a mechanic to sort of explain their big evil plan...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A lot of All-Mother or All-Father-class gods have the ability to invite someone into their pantheon, yeah. Since that's the level you're operating at, it's largely restricted to Legend 12.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mentioned before that sometimes Fate retroactively Changes history. Is it possible The Keepers Of the World could be trying to find a way to change history so all the other gods were locked Away since thousands of years ago, just like Zeus did with Kronos. And Tezcatlipoca did with the guy who was the Sun before him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T23:21:32-08:00","id":1022633,"title":"","content":"This isn't really a question for Neal so much as it is a general mythology question. I don't really know where else I would actually ask this question, since there isnn't any sort of thread for discussing mythology to my knowledge, so sorry.<br /> <br /> Anyway, can anybody actually tell me some myths about Ares/Mars? The only things I actually remember him doing are; getting his ass kicked by Diomedes, sleeping with Aphrodite then getting caught and publically humiliated along with said goddess by Hephaestus and being the father of Hippolyta and giving her the belt that Hercules had to steal from her. I think I also remember something about him avenging the rape of one of his daughters or something, I'm not too sure about that one though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T00:19:31-08:00","id":1022641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1022633#post1022633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't really a question for Neal so much as it is a general mythology question. I don't really know where else I would actually ask this question, since there isnn't any sort of thread for discussing mythology to my knowledge, so sorry.<br /> <br /> Anyway, can anybody actually tell me some myths about Ares/Mars? The only things I actually remember him doing are; getting his ass kicked by Diomedes, sleeping with Aphrodite then getting caught and publically humiliated along with said goddess by Hephaestus and being the father of Hippolyta and giving her the belt that Hercules had to steal from her. I think I also remember something about him avenging the rape of one of his daughters or something, I'm not too sure about that one though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will preface this by saying I'm cheating at this, Theoi.com is amazing for this sort of thing. I'm just explaining what they're talking about.<ul><li>Ares kills an unnamed Giant, one of Ekhidna's sons, who was powerful enough to challenge Zeus' during the Titan War. (This makes no sense chronologically, but, don't sweat it. The Titan War is filled with people who totally have not been born yet.)</li> <li>During the Gigantomachy he also fights Giants, but he can't kill them. There's a prophecy that results in Heracles being the only person who can kill them.</li> <li>He turns into a fish to run away from Typhon (again, ignore the chronology issue.) along with Apollo, and Hermes. (Athena stays behind with Zeus)</li> <li>He gets kidnapped by two giants and put in a bronze cauldron he could not escape from which almost broke him and has to get saved by Hermes.</li> <li>Ares rescued Thanatos from Sisyphus' imprisonment of the Death God.</li> <li>Fails to overcome Hephaestus by force of arms when he imprisoned Hera, driven back by the God slinging fire. (Phobos, Demios, and Kydoimos also failed at this task)</li> <li>Is beaten by Apollo at boxing during the first Olympic Games.</li> <li>Ares kept watch over Greece to make sure that nowhere allowed Leto to give birth to Apollo and Artemis. (He fails in this task, though at a quick glance through the passage, I'm not sure why. It's almost 3am here, not the best time for deep reading.)</li> <li>Gets wounded by Heracles during a war in Pylos.</li> <li>Helps the river God Akhelioios resist Heracles. (He fails at this, Heracles wins anyways)</li> <li>Breaks his word to side with the Greeks in the Trojan War (which he made to Athena and his mother Hera) when Aphrodite asked him to back the Trojans.</li> <li>Gets wounded by Diomodes guided by Athena given express permission to do this by Zeus since Ares was being a disruptive and going against the will of Zeus. Ares runs home to Zeus to whinge about getting hurt, to which Zeus responds, &quot;Do not sit beside me and whine, you double-faced liar. To me you are most hateful of all the gods who hold Olympus... but were you born of some other god and proved so ruinous long since you would have been dropped beneath the gods of the bright sky.&quot; [Note: again, 3am. But, Zeus <i>really</i> does not like Ares. If Ares was not Zeus' son, he would have thrown Ares... maybe into Tartarus, the poetic turns of phrase make it tricky. He would be kicked off Olympus at least.]</li> <li>Tries to return to the battle field of Troy when his son Askalaphos is killed, but gets restrained by Athena. In this passage he directly ignores the command of Zeus, and does not care about it.</li> <li>Gets Aeneas to repel an attack on Troy's gates.</li> <li>Battles with Athena during the fall of Troy, both quit it when Zeus rumbles at them.</li> <li>Gets caught in a magical unbreakable net by Hephaestus.</li> <li>Cheats on Aphrodite with Eos, which results in Eos being cursed with unending lust by Aphrodite in revenge.</li> <li>Maaaybe cheated on Aphrodite with Demeter and had a dragon, Kadmos, as a son from this.</li> <li>Was in love with Persephone. (Demeter refuses his, Hermes, and Apollo's advances)</li> <li>Has kids with Harmonia, who are the Amazons.</li> <li>Fathers Romulus and Remus with Rhea Silvia. (Technically this is Mars, divide as you wish)</li> <li>Murders Adonis in jealousy for Aphrodite's love for him. (A bit hypocritical there Ares, I didn't even list all the people he cheated on her with.)</li> <li>Kills Poseidon's son Halirrhothios for trying to rape Ares' daughter Alkippe. Ares is brought before a tribunal of the Gods and acquitted.</li> <li>Transforms his daughter Harmonia and her husband Cadmus into snakes since Cadmus killed his son Dracon (who might also be that other dragon I talked about previously)</li> <li>Gives King Aeetes the dragon that guarded the Golden Fleece (we all know how well this ends up)</li> <li>Protects his descendants Agrios and Oreios who were half-bear from the wrath of the Gods, transforming them into birds.</li> <li>Fought alongside his son Phlegyas who was conquering other mortals.</li> <li>Gives Diomedes (different one) his man-eating mares. (Which end up eating Diomedes)</li> <li>Favors Hippolyte and gives her his belt, Heracles kills her and takes it.</li> </ul>I cut some of the shorter, less interesting, or thematically repeditive ones. You can check them all out in detail right <a href=\"http://www.theoi.com/Olympios/Ares.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. Check the sidebar to the left for the detailed myths. (sections 4 - 6-ish)<br /> <br /> You know, I forgot just how bad a War God Ares actually is until I read through that again. He really is just not very good at it. Not great on actually beating people in fights either. He... really is getting that throne of the Dodekatheon on nepotism. He's... like, <i>problematically </i>weak compared to other Major Gods, even in areas he should be good at. He's physically weak, he keeps getting beaten in fights, fails far more often than he succeeds in general, would be thrown off Olympus if he wasn't Zeus' kid, gets trashed by a Demigod, etc. He <i>really</i> pushes getting that Legend 12 rating some nights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 12-27-2016, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T01:27:42-08:00","id":1022651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1022641#post1022641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I will preface this by saying I'm cheating at this, Theoi.com is amazing for this sort of thing. I'm just explaining what they're talking about.<ul><li>Ares kills an unnamed Giant, one of Ekhidna's sons, who was powerful enough to challenge Zeus' during the Titan War. (This makes no sense chronologically, but, don't sweat it. The Titan War is filled with people who totally have not been born yet.)</li> <li>He turns into a fish to run away from Typhon (again, ignore the chronology issue.) along with Apollo, and Hermes. (Athena stays behind with Zeus)</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Could be explained away via timeline fuckery from some of the Titans?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ul><li>During the Gigantomachy he also fights Giants, but he can't kill them. There's a prophecy that results in Heracles being the only person who can kill them.</li> <li>He gets kidnapped by two giants and put in a bronze cauldron he could not escape from which almost broke him and has to get saved by Hermes.</li> <li>Ares rescued Thanatos from Sisyphus' imprisonment of the Death God.</li> <li>Fails to overcome Hephaestus by force of arms when he imprisoned Hera, driven back by the God slinging fire. (Phobos, Demios, and Kydoimos also failed at this task)</li> <li>Is beaten by Apollo at boxing during the first Olympic Games.</li> <li>Gets wounded by Heracles during a war in Pylos.</li> <li>Gets wounded by Diomodes guided by Athena given express permission to do this by Zeus since Ares was being a disruptive and going against the will of Zeus. Ares runs home to Zeus to whinge about getting hurt, to which Zeus responds, &quot;Do not sit beside me and whine, you double-faced liar. To me you are most hateful of all the gods who hold Olympus... but were you born of some other god and proved so ruinous long since you would have been dropped beneath the gods of the bright sky.&quot; [Note: again, 3am. But, Zeus <i>really</i> does not like Ares. If Ares was not Zeus' son, he would have thrown Ares... maybe into Tartarus, the poetic turns of phrase make it tricky. He would be kicked off Olympus at least.]</li> <li>Tries to return to the battle field of Troy when his son Askalaphos is killed, but gets restrained by Athena. In this passage he directly ignores the command of Zeus, and does not care about it.</li> <li>Helps the river God Akhelioios resist Heracles. (He fails at this, Heracles wins anyways)</li> <li>Battles with Athena during the fall of Troy, both quit it when Zeus rumbles at them.</li> <li>Murders Adonis in jealousy for Aphrodite's love for him. (A bit hypocritical there Ares, I didn't even list all the people he cheated on her with.)</li> <li>Kills Poseidon's son Halirrhothios for trying to rape Ares' daughter Alkippe. Ares is brought before a tribunal of the Gods and acquitted.</li> <li>Fought alongside his son Phlegyas who was conquering other mortals.</li> </ul>You know, I forgot just how bad a War God Ares actually is until I read through that again. He really is just not very good at it. Not great on actually beating people in fights either. He... really is getting that throne of the Dodekatheon on nepotism. He's... like, <i>problematically </i>weak compared to other Major Gods, even in areas he should be good at. He's physically weak, he keeps getting beaten in fights, fails far more often than he succeeds in general, would be thrown off Olympus if he wasn't Zeus' kid, gets trashed by a Demigod, etc. He <i>really</i> pushes getting that Legend 12 rating some nights. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Ares' fighting ability seems to fluxuate a whole lot throughout Greek mythology. This is probablyy because a majority of our sources on it come from Athens, and the Athenians were not fans of Ares at all. I bet that if we had records of what the other city states thought of him we'd have an image of a much more competent war god. Oh well, the Roman's portrayal of him/Mars makes up for it, I suppose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ul><li>Has kids with Harmonia, who are the Amazons.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div><br /> Y'know, if the Theoi stopped inbreeding all the time they might be more well adjusted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ul><li>Ares kept watch over Greece to make sure that nowhere allowed Leto to give birth to Apollo and Artemis. (He fails in this task, though at a quick glance through the passage, I'm not sure why. It's almost 3am here, not the best time for deep reading.)</li> <li>Breaks his word to side with the Greeks in the Trojan War (which he made to Athena and his mother Hera) when Aphrodite asked him to back the Trojans.</li> <li>Tries to return to the battle field of Troy when his son Askalaphos is killed, but gets restrained by Athena. In this passage he directly ignores the command of Zeus, and does not care about it.</li> <li>Gets Aeneas to repel an attack on Troy's gates.</li> <li>Battles with Athena during the fall of Troy, both quit it when Zeus rumbles at them.</li> <li>Gets caught in a magical unbreakable net by Hephaestus.</li> <li>Cheats on Aphrodite with Eos, which results in Eos being cursed with unending lust by Aphrodite in revenge.</li> <li>Maaaybe cheated on Aphrodite with Demeter and had a dragon, Kadmos, as a son from this.</li> <li>Was in love with Persephone. (Demeter refuses his, Hermes, and Apollo's advances)</li> <li>Fathers Romulus and Remus with Rhea Silvia. (Technically this is Mars, divide as you wish)</li> <li>Transforms his daughter Harmonia and her husband Cadmus into snakes since Cadmus killed his son Dracon (who might also be that other dragon I talked about previously)</li> <li>Gives King Aeetes the dragon that guarded the Golden Fleece (we all know how well this ends up)</li> <li>Protects his descendants Agrios and Oreios who were half-bear from the wrath of the Gods, transforming them into birds.</li> <li>Fought alongside his son Phlegyas who was conquering other mortals.</li> <li>Gives Diomedes (different one) his man-eating mares. (Which end up eating Diomedes)</li> <li>Favors Hippolyte and gives her his belt, Heracles kills her and takes it.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div><br /> For the most part he seems fairly typical for the Theoi, maybe even a bit less of a dick than most of them. I assume that the Roman legends are basically the same, though they probably would have dumped some of his adultery myths since they weren't big fans of that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ul><li>I cut some of the shorter, less interesting, or thematically repeditive ones. You can check them all out in detail right <a href=\"http://www.theoi.com/Olympios/Ares.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. Check the sidebar to the left for the detailed myths. (sections 4 - 6-ish)</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div><br /> I already know about Theoi.com and was in fact reading it when you responded to this, but thanks anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12300,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","user":"Crying","date":". 12-27-2016, 04:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T08:51:18-08:00","id":1022780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1022641#post1022641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I forgot just how bad a War God Ares actually is until I read through that again. He really is just not very good at it. Not great on actually beating people in fights either. He... really is getting that throne of the Dodekatheon on nepotism. He's... like, <i>problematically </i>weak compared to other Major Gods, even in areas he should be good at. He's physically weak, he keeps getting beaten in fights, fails far more often than he succeeds in general, would be thrown off Olympus if he wasn't Zeus' kid, gets trashed by a Demigod, etc. He <i>really</i> pushes getting that Legend 12 rating some nights.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, he kind of does suck. You kind of have to stretch to make the glowing write up in the Theoi preview feel legitimate when you have his well documented list of failures like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T09:33:55-08:00","id":1022802,"title":"","content":"I do figure writer's bias is a part of that. Athens is the primary source of information we have on the Theoi, and as has been said, they were not fond of Ares. Hard to say how Ithaca or Thebes would've seen him. Safe to say the Spartans were much bigger fans. They just <i>weren't</i>\u200b big fans of writing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T10:52:06-08:00","id":1022836,"title":"","content":"Weirdest side effect of that is that since the Athenians weren't trying to link any royal bloodlines to Ares, Ares is basically the only male Olympian without rape myths. In fact he notably murders a rapist and is acquitted for it (though rather than this being because of women having inherent rights he was defending, we can assume it was because Alcippe was his daughter and thus the rape was a violation of his property... seriously, fuck the ancient Mediterranean...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T11:10:00-08:00","id":1022850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1022651#post1022651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could be explained away via timeline fuckery from some of the Titans?</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be! I tend to actually blame it on Fate if it's true in universe, or mortal worshipers wanting their personal favorites to be around for the big fight if it is not true in universe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1022651#post1022651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Ares' fighting ability seems to fluxuate a whole lot throughout Greek mythology. This is probablyy because a majority of our sources on it come from Athens, and the Athenians were not fans of Ares at all. I bet that if we had records of what the other city states thought of him we'd have an image of a much more competent war god. Oh well, the Roman's portrayal of him/Mars makes up for it, I suppose.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreepyShutIn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1022802#post1022802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do figure writer's bias is a part of that. Athens is the primary source of information we have on the Theoi, and as has been said, they were not fond of Ares. Hard to say how Ithaca or Thebes would've seen him. Safe to say the Spartans were much bigger fans. They just <i>weren't</i>\u200b big fans of writing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I have heard this before, and it totally is true for some parts of Ares myths. The Athenians commissioned what amounts to the 'cannonization' of the Homeric myths, so the Iliad and the Odyssey are both heavily pro-Athens. But, a lot of Ares martial failings come from non-Athenians, more than we get in the pro-Athenian works. Running away from Typhon is done by Antoninus Liberalis, a Roman (I don't know if he was a citizen or not, but he was in the Roman Empire). Failing to capture Hephaestus is from a Byzantine writer recording myths. Getting beaten by Apollo in boxing is recorded by Herodotus (non-Athenian [he passed through at one point IIRC, but wandered, and was non-native]) as was being brutally beaten down by Heracles. Not being able to support the River God so that he would be victorious over Heracles was recorded by a Lydian Greek. Getting trapped in a magical net is Ovid, a Roman.<br /> <br /> The big bits the Athenians contribute to Ares looking weak is the 'Jar incident' and getting slapped by Diomedies. But, outside of Athens' writing, he is beaten at boxing by Apollo, runs away from Typhon, and being beaten down by a Demigod are all non-Athenian works. He has suffered some character assassination, but even outside of Athenian influence, even centuries after Athens' influence was no more, and before Athens held colossal sway, Ares still is not coming out on top martially. It's really interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1022651#post1022651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I already know about Theoi.com and was in fact reading it when you responded to this, but thanks anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I'm glad! Theoi.com is just amazing, brilliantly done. You're totally welcome, I'm sorry I couldn't be of more help.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T11:20:15-08:00","id":1022855,"title":"","content":"TIL Area is Worf from TNG. Theoretically a great warrior but folds when the story needs it.<br /> <br /> Or if the authors don't like the guy, apparently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T11:31:25-08:00","id":1022861,"title":"","content":"Also bear in mind that Scion will be treating the Ares/Mars thing as \u201cAres was Mars when he was young and headstrong; Mars is Ares after he matured and learned discipline\u201d. Remember: the same way that the Greeks had few good things to say about Ares, the Romans had many good things to say about Mars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-27-2016, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T13:05:36-08:00","id":1022913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1022855#post1022855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TIL Area is Worf from TNG. Theoretically a great warrior but folds when the story needs it.<br /> <br /> Or if the authors don't like the guy, apparently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being Ares is suffering, except for the part where he's been screwing Aphrodite, goddess of carnal love and beauty, for millenia. I guess that's not bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T17:20:00-08:00","id":1023038,"title":"","content":"Was Mars ever tied by blood to Romulus and Remus, or was he just well-regarded by the Romans?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T17:33:21-08:00","id":1023042,"title":"","content":"Mars was the father of Romulus and Remus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T17:36:24-08:00","id":1023044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1023038#post1023038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was Mars ever tied by blood to Romulus and Remus, or was he just well-regarded by the Romans?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mars is their father. and they are also descendants of Venus through their ancestor Aeneas. Their mother, Rhea Silvia, was a Vestal Virgin, placed in that position by her uncle who had usurped her father's Kingship as to prevent her from having any children who would hold a legitimate claim to the crown against him. The twins go on to overthrow their great-uncle, restore their grandfather's crown, and go to found their own city which ends, well, you know. Not great for Remus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T19:29:02-08:00","id":1023070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1023038#post1023038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was Mars ever tied by blood to Romulus and Remus, or was he just well-regarded by the Romans?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As Dataweaver and Watcher said he was their father, and through them he was the god most regarded as patron of the city for most of its early history. The Julian Dynasty though was very invested in establishing their patron goddess Venus as the mother of the city, and that's a huge part of the role Virgil's Aeneid played - elevating the Aeneas myth over the Romulus &amp; Remus myth as the Roman founding identity myth, and thus elevating Venus.<br /> <br /> If you want to disregard the rl sequence of events and just look at the myths though, I like the idea that Rome was initially, for its handful of patron Olympians, a revenge plot by the pro-Trojan posse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 12-27-2016, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T09:25:56-08:00","id":1023312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1022913#post1022913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being Ares is suffering, except for the part where he's been screwing Aphrodite, goddess of carnal love and beauty, for millenia. I guess that's not bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ares: So I've got that going for me, which is nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T18:52:10-08:00","id":1023537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1022913#post1022913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being Ares is suffering, except for the part where he's been screwing Aphrodite, goddess of carnal love and beauty, for millenia. I guess that's not bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe if he spent more of his time training instead having sexy times he wouldn't be so sucky at his primary job.<br /> <br /> Hmm, maybe that's why Athena decided to be a virigin goddess. Far less distractions that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T21:06:32-08:00","id":1023573,"title":"","content":"I can think of logical reasons why he would lose at boxing to Apollo and fail to capture Hephaestus. Boxing is a sport simulating combat, not actual combat, Ares was having to hold back all the things he would normally do in an unarmed fight while apollo, who I believe had at least some association with sports and no heavy warrior aspects, would have far less of a semi-handicap. In the second case... &quot;I'm the god or WAR. What's my crippled, nerdy brother going to do? OH SWEET MERCIFUL DAD LAVA BALLS!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T08:20:47-08:00","id":1023770,"title":"","content":"Vonpenguin, you're my hero.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T14:29:39-08:00","id":1025167,"title":"","content":"So, I'm sure a few of these have been asked before, but I haven't been able to find them specifically or in some cases I was hoping for more clarification. Hope you don't mind kind of a barrage of questions, I've got a lot of them.<br /> <br /> The Aztec pantheon has been known to demand hearts ripped out of living humans to keep the sun moving through the sky. It's well established that this isn't the only thing they do by a long shot, and it's nice that the sacrifices get the best afterlife, but it is pretty distinctive. My question then is: What do Apollo, Ra, Amaterasu and other sun-related deities say to that? If there were no more such sacrifices, would the sun chariot stop? Would the goddess hide in a cave again? Would the barge be swallowed by Apophis?<br /> <br /> P.S. I don't mean to sound ungrateful for the answers we get, but I really hope this one isn't &quot;Nobody really wants to find out.&quot; I'm sure <i>something</i> of the sort has come up on some scale, to give us an idea.<br /> <br /> Just how well understood is the supernatural? We have a surprising amount of people studying myths of all kinds relating to people doing incredible things; that was practically the point of Mythbusters. Gotta figure mortals in the World are studying the tall tales and urban legends that pop up here and there, and probably televising it. Especially when everyone and their dog has a phone ready to record at a moment's notice. So how much do most mortals know, and how much do experts know?<br /> <br /> I have to admit I'm kind of upset about the Bastet/Sekhmet thing. I understand why it was done, I'm just wondering if there was an alternative. Maybe make them like some of those Irish deities, a triple goddess? Sekhmet, Hathor and Bastet, quite distinct from one another but also clearly linked.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the Irish pantheon, the preview noted that they had few primordials, but included &quot;Fintan, the Salmon of Wisdom&quot; among them, and that most of the others died in a flood. I'm not a scholar, so I'm probably missing something here, but I thought primordials were specifically incarnations of something deep and primal that were too big, metaphysically, to even fit in the world. How does that fit with a salmon? <i>Can</i>\u200b primordials even drown?<br /> <br /> Obviously many immortal or otherworldly beings don't really follow modern, human ethics, especially as they seem to change every century. That's part of the fun, after all, finding these strange and frankly dangerous beings in our familiar environments. But I wonder, is that a rule? Is the <i>aes sidhe</i>\u200b that moves to Dublin to pursue a career in fashion simply not able to grasp the human morals around him, or can he learn, adapt and integrate, even go native? Could a community even arise, of humans and fae in rural Ireland, or are they just too different on a basic level to really live in close proximity for very long?<br /> <br /> Is there an Aesir or possibly Vanir associated with ice and/or wolves? And if not, which of the Nordic gods do you think would be most likely to help out a lycanthrope praying to regain control of her life?<br /> <br /> The pantheon-specific motifs are fascinating and a cool insight into how Scions of these faiths might use their divine abilities, but some of them seem a bit odd for some uses. For example, one known boon is imbuing one legend to be able to make ranged attacks with fire for a scene: It seems a bit awkward to have to come up with new verses every time you throw one, or politely ask a Kami or Manitou for each new fireball. How would a Scion do that sort of thing?<br /> <br /> This one's a systems question, something I'm not sure I understood: Can one reassign all imbued legend between scenes? Like, if I have five legend points and five purviews, can I spread them evenly in one scene to get maximum social benefits, then come into the next scene with all the Fire and PSP boons?<br /> \u200b<br /> Wow, that turned out to be more than I thought... Hope it's not too much to deal with. Thanks for all the info so far, it's great getting this kind of direct access!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","user":"CreepyShutIn","date":". 01-01-2017, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T19:19:40-08:00","id":1025236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreepyShutIn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1025167#post1025167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm sure a few of these have been asked before, but I haven't been able to find them specifically or in some cases I was hoping for more clarification. Hope you don't mind kind of a barrage of questions, I've got a lot of them.<br /> <br /> The Aztec pantheon has been known to demand hearts ripped out of living humans to keep the sun moving through the sky. It's well established that this isn't the only thing they do by a long shot, and it's nice that the sacrifices get the best afterlife, but it is pretty distinctive. My question then is: What do Apollo, Ra, Amaterasu and other sun-related deities say to that? If there were no more such sacrifices, would the sun chariot stop? Would the goddess hide in a cave again? Would the barge be swallowed by Apophis?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot;The World has many histories. The World is a synthesis. The World is many creation myths and epics, collapsed and smoothed over by processes left for contemplation by the wisest Gods, or given to them by the Primordials. When scientists dig, they find flaked stone tools and pre-human hominid bones. When they study flesh and blood, they find mitochondria and DNA. The World\u2019s speed of light is a constant, and its physicists search for ways to unite General Relativity and Quantum Field Theory.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yet they know myths have standing. The fact that the World rests on the Great Turtle is literally true, but you can only perceive it from a certain point of view. From another such perspective, some humans are descended from bears. This is more than a state of mind. From this point of view, you can get a glimpse of the shell mighty enough to hold mountains, or see the fanged skulls of ancestors. History follows similar patterns. Archeologists find flint axes and copper helmets from the Achaean period of Greek history, but not the tripod prizes and other elements mentioned by Homer, unless they fit conventional history -- mostly.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> If the Titan Apophis slays Re and sunders his crown, fraying the mantle of Re/Sun Deity beyond recovery, the World will continue - but it will be colder, in ways both literal and not. Other pantheons will pick up the slack, but all the gods and Titans of the Sun will shudder in sympathy, and our own purely material globe will swell red in pain and convulse in great solar winds. Life will go on, and the Sun will rise, but it will not be the most pleasant. Should all the deities of the Sun perish, a mere ball of gas and light will illuminate the World, to steal Pratchett's words. A piece of creation will be forever gone, the poetry guttered out with the last God's life blood.<br /> <br /> Each pantheon reinforces the structure of the World, making it stranger - but also stronger.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just how well understood is the supernatural? We have a surprising amount of people studying myths of all kinds relating to people doing incredible things; that was practically the point of Mythbusters. Gotta figure mortals in the World are studying the tall tales and urban legends that pop up here and there, and probably televising it. Especially when everyone and their dog has a phone ready to record at a moment's notice. So how much do most mortals know, and how much do experts know? </div> </div> </div><i>\u201cOnce upon a time,\u201d says the storyteller. People in our world hear the phrase and know it means \u201ca long time ago,\u201d or \u201cbefore things were the way they are today,\u201d or \u201cin the beginning.\u201d<br /> In the World, \u201conce upon a time\u201d was last week, and everyone's still watching the story unfold on the evening news. In the World, legends weren't just made back in the day before video cameras and the internet. They're striding down the streets downtown right now, and #TeamTezcatlipoca is trending on Twitter. In the World, nobody disputes the wisdom of knocking on wood to ward off malignant spirits, because malignant spirits spew out of the Axis Mundi next door all the time. Inhabitants of the World wake up to just a little more wonder and a few more omens every morning.<br /> <br /> That's not to say the curtain between the mundane and the divine is shredded daily, or even often. Most people never see a God in the flesh. They work, party, study, travel, and make love without any overt interference from mystical forces nine times out of ten. But mystical forces live in their neighborhoods, and that tenth time could be the one to tangle a person's Fate up in something much bigger than herself.</i><br /> <br /> <i>The World has the oceans, continents and nations we know, but under the influence of meddling Gods, magic and obscure, supernaturally twisted history, some of the deep details might be a bit different from what you\u2019re familiar with. You may not know of certain sovereign states -- mere dots on a map -- that go unrecognized by the UN, but are well-known to many mystics and Scions. Some rivers take different courses, or sprout obscure tributaries. Any country might have big cities you\u2019ve never heard of, and that\u2019s before getting into Terra Incognita.<br /> <br /> Other sections of this book delve into the day to day realities of the World. Despite its superficial normalcy, and close resemblance to the world you and your fellow players live in, take the paragraph above as permission for the Director to make changes and create new places in the World without feeling that they might be \u201cdeviating from canon.\u201d Plus of course, you should be prepared for fictional parts of the world in <b>Scion</b>\u2019s books, where a good story might be found in a fictional neighbourhood that could belong to many cities, or a business that only exists thanks to divine interference.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have to admit I'm kind of upset about the Bastet/Sekhmet thing. I understand why it was done, I'm just wondering if there was an alternative. Maybe make them like some of those Irish deities, a triple goddess? Sekhmet, Hathor and Bastet, quite distinct from one another but also clearly linked. </div> </div> </div>Well, two things here.<br /> <br /> We're revising a lot of the way we look at the Egyptian deities, because the response was so temperamental, and I'm calling in a few more experts on other pantheons to look at them as well. Keep in mind that identities in Scion are mutable, and - to a degree - transferable. And lastly, if you don't like the canonical interpretation, we will have a paid community content structure. Make your own, polish it up and back it up with research, and you'll both enrich the game line and the community by making your own stuff and putting it out there. If you want to make a Scion Shard where the Gods imbue their signature Relics with their Mantles, such that mortals can wear said Mantles by wielding the relics, <i>by all means - </i>go for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Speaking of the Irish pantheon, the preview noted that they had few primordials, but included &quot;Fintan, the Salmon of Wisdom&quot; among them, and that most of the others died in a flood. I'm not a scholar, so I'm probably missing something here, but I thought primordials were specifically incarnations of something deep and primal that were too big, metaphysically, to even fit in the world. How does that fit with a salmon? <i>Can</i>\u200b primordials even drown? </div> </div> </div>Primordials can die and dissolve into the metaphor-laden chaos of the Overworld, although it's rather hard to tell if they're dead or not - they're not exactly chatty or approachable at the best of times. Not every mythology has the same kind of Primordials, either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Obviously many immortal or otherworldly beings don't really follow modern, human ethics, especially as they seem to change every century. That's part of the fun, after all, finding these strange and frankly dangerous beings in our familiar environments. But I wonder, is that a rule? Is the <i>aes sidhe</i>\u200b that moves to Dublin to pursue a career in fashion simply not able to grasp the human morals around him, or can he learn, adapt and integrate, even go native? Could a community even arise, of humans and fae in rural Ireland, or are they just too different on a basic level to really live in close proximity for very long? </div> </div> </div>Yes, they can integrate. The Jersey Devil might run a pawn shop over the river. If he does, he's probably an asshole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there an Aesir or possibly Vanir associated with ice and/or wolves? And if not, which of the Nordic gods do you think would be most likely to help out a lycanthrope praying to regain control of her life? </div> </div> </div>Not sure, but H\u00f6\u00f0r is associated with ice and darkness. He'd probably be willing to help, if you can get him to stop being so morose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The pantheon-specific motifs are fascinating and a cool insight into how Scions of these faiths might use their divine abilities, but some of them seem a bit odd for some uses. For example, one known boon is imbuing one legend to be able to make ranged attacks with fire for a scene: It seems a bit awkward to have to come up with new verses every time you throw one, or politely ask a Kami or Manitou for each new fireball. How would a Scion do that sort of thing? </div> </div> </div>Boons don't <i>have </i>to conform to motifs, though cosmetically they <i>very often </i>do, since that's the effective explanation for how their magic works - puffing out fireballs from your lit cigar, that sort of thing. Purviews represent your dominion over an elemental force of the World. If you say your Scion is muttering prayers to the Kami or Manitou, I wouldn't force the player to actually do so each time. Although for this example, you really only have to do it once in the scene, and the Kami will respond to your commands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This one's a systems question, something I'm not sure I understood: Can one reassign all imbued legend between scenes? Like, if I have five legend points and five purviews, can I spread them evenly in one scene to get maximum social benefits, then come into the next scene with all the Fire and PSP boons? </div> </div> </div>Legend is only imbued for as long as it's imbued, circular as that might be. Think of it this way: you have a certain amount of metaphysical juice in the tank from your divine narrative. You can pour this juice to fuel certain abilities, and then pour it back in your tank when you don't want to fuel them anymore. Some abilities are so potent they burn out your juice right off, though. So, yes, you can imbue some Boons or Marvels in one scene and then be back next scene. Be careful, though - regaining Legend is tough, and requires you to submit to the whims of Fate.<br /> <br /> Or it requires sacrifice. Whichever <i>you'd </i>prefer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T19:32:09-08:00","id":1025240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yukikaze</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1016866#post1016866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Callings<b>:</b> Will they have a transcendent form, akin to the avatar purviews or 1e's Ultimate Attributes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On another note: earlier, a purview for patron deities of cities was mentioned. Can you please tell us a little more about that, and how strongly said city would have to be tied to a pantheon's sphere of influence (i.e., could a Scion of Parvati who was born and raised in Pittsburgh aspire to become that city's divine patron)? </div> </div> </div>The Prosperity Purview is being reworked a little to provide more for city action and being, well, the heroes of neighborhoods, the demigods of boroughs, and the Gods of Cities and Peoples and Nations. The city's influence is a chicken-and-egg situation - expect a lot more Vedic temples to sprout up in Pittsburgh and a statue of Parvati (or the Scion) to pop up in front of the Cathedral of Learning.<br /> <br /> Purviews are dominions, but Gods <i>are </i>their Purviews in a very unique way. When you say Thor is slamming on his anvil in a thunderstorm, on some level both literal and metaphorical <i>that is happening</i>. When you say Parvati is love and devotion, on some level <i>she is</i>. When you say Ba'al Hammon is the God of Carthage and weather and vegetation and rulership, he is those things, including the city itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T20:14:04-08:00","id":1025254,"title":"","content":"Neall have I told you lately that I love you, man?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T20:55:13-08:00","id":1025275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1025254#post1025254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neall have I told you lately that I love you, man?</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://s2.quickmeme.com/img/74/7427a57511948c3d263db8a79fe8364b4c56f25e41127a35861fb086536ffee6.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T22:07:28-08:00","id":1025293,"title":"","content":"So when you mentioned the Sun gods/titans feeling it when a peer dies, how does this cast the 'Cold War' between the Gods and Titans? One of power usurpation rather than direct destruction? Would (should?) a God, with the knowledge of how much it lessons the world, ever really feel okay killing another one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T00:03:00-08:00","id":1025324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1025240#post1025240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Prosperity Purview is being reworked a little to provide more for city action and being, well, the heroes of neighborhoods, the demigods of boroughs, and the Gods of Cities and Peoples and Nations. The city's influence is a chicken-and-egg situation - expect a lot more Vedic temples to sprout up in Pittsburgh and a statue of Parvati (or the Scion) to pop up in front of the Cathedral of Learning.<br /> <br /> Purviews are dominions, but Gods <i>are </i>their Purviews in a very unique way. When you say Thor is slamming on his anvil in a thunderstorm, on some level both literal and metaphorical <i>that is happening</i>. When you say Parvati is love and devotion, on some level <i>she is</i>. When you say Ba'al Hammon is the God of Carthage and weather and vegetation and rulership, he is those things, including the city itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the detailed answer, and the perspective on its ramifications!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","user":"yukikaze","date":". 01-02-2017, 03:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T00:58:39-08:00","id":1025331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1025240#post1025240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Purviews are dominions, but Gods <i>are </i>their Purviews in a very unique way. When you say Thor is slamming on his anvil in a thunderstorm, on some level both literal and metaphorical <i>that is happening</i>. When you say Parvati is love and devotion, on some level <i>she is</i>. When you say Ba'al Hammon is the God of Carthage and weather and vegetation and rulership, he is those things, including the city itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;You're not dealing with a world of science, logic and orde, you're dealing with myths, fantasies and magic! The only thing sillier than expecting it to make sense is trying to make it make sense!&quot; - somebody, somewhere, sometime, probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T10:12:00-08:00","id":1025485,"title":"","content":"Since Fate can retroactively change history. Is there anyway a god can use that to his advantage, manipulating fate to change the past?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T11:31:34-08:00","id":1025504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1025485#post1025485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Fate can retroactively change history. Is there anyway a god can use that to his advantage, manipulating fate to change the past?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm. My sense of it is that essentially, another past is added to the ones already present, layers and layers of pasts coexisting in the World. All myths are true, including creation myths. So you add a new creation myth to the past, and... well, it gives you a <i>past</i>, but to what extent that past is an advantage is another matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T18:17:43-08:00","id":1026250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=807253#post807253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's actually a mechanic in the game, though after the last design discussion I think we're knocking it back to Director advice.<br /> <br /> The actual Creation Myth mechanics are something in <b>God</b>, for when you make a new pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you telll a little bit more about it? Maybe give an example!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T06:18:55-08:00","id":1026467,"title":"","content":"No answer to whether AI Scions are possible? Sadface.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12736-heliomance","name":"Heliomance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T10:31:05-08:00","id":1026597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heliomance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1026467#post1026467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No answer to whether AI Scions are possible? Sadface.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll just note that Created Genesis is possible. Sure, most Created are going to be &quot;Sekhmet found a Good Kitty and made him into a person&quot; or &quot;Loki carved someone out of wood&quot; or &quot;Shiva plucked a perfect lotus blossom out of a pond, and when it bloomed a woman came out&quot;... But I'm sure that a reasonable GM will be reasonable with &quot;And Haphaestus bust out his mad programmer skills and now I'm a hard light projection&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T14:58:44-08:00","id":1026708,"title":"","content":"&quot;And thus on the fifth coffee fueled night Ptah's code did gain sentience.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which would be a great use of the urban legend about the WoW programmer that finished code after such a night and had no idea how the code worked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T19:29:35-08:00","id":1026818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heliomance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1026467#post1026467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No answer to whether AI Scions are possible? Sadface.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, let me save you some time.<br /> <br /> My answer to something batshit like this is pretty much always gonna be &quot;yes&quot; or &quot;sure&quot;.<br /> <br /> There's some stuff I say no to, because it doesn't really happen in myths. &quot;Can I, as a demigod or God, be Iron Man or a Reed Richards&quot; is something I'll <i>mostly </i>say no to, if only because Iron Man Gods aren't actually too prevalent - most forge gods make shit <i>for other Gods </i>and outside of a few Sage Heroes redefining technology with a paradigm shift by inventing the wheel or the canoe or the whatever, you don't have 'em. <i>Tony Stark </i>the polymath inventor of a thousand myriad inventions for society and a few choice artifacts for himself and others is a Scion, and a good example of one. <i>Iron Man</i>, in the sense of refining his single greatest invention that's mostly for himself endlessly, is not. Doing something like inventing the Arc Reactor - clean energy on a citywide scale - is something a Hero would do, something that will transform society rapidly and have long aftereffects when they're gone. Because they do that paradigm shift and then they're off trying to find the Orichalcum Forge or whatever. In general, gods are more wise and clever than mortals, but they aren't smarter on the &quot;invent psychohistory on a lark&quot; level except in those rare heroes who get heroic off the paradigm shift. They're Zhuge Liang, not Iron Man.<br /> <br /> But that's a tangent. The answer to &quot;can a God breathe life into code&quot; is both &quot;it works for clay, so sure&quot; and, &quot;I, too, saw <i>Weird Science</i> as a young and hormonal teenager.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 01-04-2017, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T22:20:20-08:00","id":1026867,"title":"","content":"Besides, that sort of stuff strikes me as more of a \u201cScion/Trinity Crossover Chronicle\u201d sort of thing than something I'd expect either gameline to address on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T01:25:13-08:00","id":1026919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1026818#post1026818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, let me save you some time.<br /> <br /> My answer to something batshit like this is pretty much always gonna be &quot;yes&quot; or &quot;sure&quot;.<br /> <br /> There's some stuff I say no to, because it doesn't really happen in myths. &quot;Can I, as a demigod or God, be Iron Man or a Reed Richards&quot; is something I'll <i>mostly </i>say no to, if only because Iron Man Gods aren't actually too prevalent - most forge gods make shit <i>for other Gods </i>and outside of a few Sage Heroes redefining technology with a paradigm shift by inventing the wheel or the canoe or the whatever, you don't have 'em. <i>Tony Stark </i>the polymath inventor of a thousand myriad inventions for society and a few choice artifacts for himself and others is a Scion, and a good example of one. <i>Iron Man</i>, in the sense of refining his single greatest invention that's mostly for himself endlessly, is not. Doing something like inventing the Arc Reactor - clean energy on a citywide scale - is something a Hero would do, something that will transform society rapidly and have long aftereffects when they're gone. Because they do that paradigm shift and then they're off trying to find the Orichalcum Forge or whatever. In general, gods are more wise and clever than mortals, but they aren't smarter on the &quot;invent psychohistory on a lark&quot; level except in those rare heroes who get heroic off the paradigm shift. They're Zhuge Liang, not Iron Man.<br /> <br /> But that's a tangent. The answer to &quot;can a God breathe life into code&quot; is both &quot;it works for clay, so sure&quot; and, &quot;I, too, saw <i>Weird Science</i> as a young and hormonal teenager.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Welp, I know what my first character's going to be ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12736-heliomance","name":"Heliomance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T02:31:54-08:00","id":1026939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1026818#post1026818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that's a tangent. The answer to &quot;can a God breathe life into code&quot; is both &quot;it works for clay, so sure&quot; and, &quot;<b>I, too, saw <i>Weird Science</i> as a young and hormonal teenager</b>.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not gonna lie, but Lisa from Weird Science was an inspiration for a Scion I've been brainstorming. I was just to ashamed to ask about its feasibility in the setting.<br /> <br /> Thanks by the way Heliomance for indirectly answering a question for me.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T15:44:36-08:00","id":1029799,"title":"","content":"LMAO, and now I have to have an Incarnation of Aphrodite who started out as a Barbie doll... speaking of which, are all born scions sired by incarnations who, themselves, were born and grew up, or can a god just plop down, become flesh, get their freak on and move on?<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"