,"value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T18:32:36-08:00","id":1036969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shaddar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1036865#post1036865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahh, I was thinking on those as big monsters, not scions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hel, who is counted as a God, is a sibling to the giant wolf and snake by the very same mother. It's a good example of the political nature of the God/Titan divide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T20:12:29-08:00","id":1037024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1036969#post1036969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hel, who is counted as a God, is a sibling to the giant wolf and snake by the very same mother. It's a good example of the political nature of the God/Titan divide.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I always argued, even an elementary school student can put two and two together pointing out why Cronus is a Titan, and yet his son Zeus isn't because he is a God. Yet when some other titans have kids they may become Nymphs and what not. Out of game context Titans are just another tribe of God.<br /> <br /> <br /> Back in the day my setting had Sleipnir, Hugin, Munin, Freiki/Geiri, Garm and Cerberus as able to have human Scions. Similar to the 90s Thor run when Munin took the form of an unknown God and put merged Thor with the EMT Jake Olsen. God monsters are pretty good mining ground for Divine Patrons for the same reason they are often used as the names of Organizations, like Cerberus in Mass Effect. They are archetypical as the dickens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T19:56:00-08:00","id":1038213,"title":"","content":"Do we have something resembling a release date yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T12:32:30-08:00","id":1038521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1038213#post1038213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we have something resembling a release date yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Kickstarter says May for the PDF and October for the physicals. But given Onyx Path's history with KS delivery we'll have to see how close that is in actuality,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","user":"TheGraySoul","date":". 01-26-2017, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T14:21:09-08:00","id":1038573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheGraySoul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1038521#post1038521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Kickstarter says May for the PDF and October for the physicals. But given Onyx Path's history with guess KS delivery we'll have to see how close that is in actuality,</div> </div> </div> </div>If they DO happen to have the PDFs out this year I'll be both impressed and VERY happy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T14:43:57-08:00","id":1038589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1038573#post1038573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If they DO happen to have the PDFs out this year I'll be both impressed and VERY happy</div> </div> </div> </div>I think having the PDF's out this year is very doable given the amount of work that apparently had been put in already. I don't know if I should expect the physical or any of the stretch goal materials though.<br /> <br /> Edit: Although the fact that we're now a month behind on when the backers were supposed to receive their backerkit surveys with no word on what's up is a little concerning. But I imagine we'll hear about it in the monthly ks update which should be dropping any day now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","user":"TheGraySoul","date":". 01-26-2017, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T15:11:16-08:00","id":1038605,"title":"","content":"When it comes to KS stuff I think OPP badly overstretches itself and everything is slower as a result but I have hope this won't be a wait like some other game lines. It'll probably be later summer than intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T20:30:32-08:00","id":1038734,"title":"","content":"So, this bit from the Terra Incognita caught my eye:<br /> <br /> &quot;It is said the Primordials are the closest an unenlightened being can get to Platonic Forms or other primal principles. Beyond them lies <i><b>the Trimurti</b></i>, the Good the Absolute, the Mists of Creation, and so on. These can hardly be called places at all, and the Gods may know nothing more than what they might read in mortal wisdom literature.&quot;<br /> <br /> Does that mean the Trimurti of Brahma Vishnu Shiva are not playable patrons in 2e, but instead Primal Principles? That wouldn't necessarily be an incorrect way of going about it, but it definitely wasn't what I was expecting. And if they are, what about their wives? We know Kali is a playable patron since Annie X exists, which would make Shiva not being there kinda weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T10:52:21-08:00","id":1038979,"title":"","content":"It's stated that <i>most</i>\u200b Primordials never have Scions, but exceptions do exist - Danu is one example of an Irish Primordial who forms the occasional Scion. Could be that the Trimurti are the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T21:41:36-08:00","id":1041100,"title":"","content":"If you ever get around to it, how will the Philippines and their many, many pantheons be dealt with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T12:47:58-08:00","id":1041967,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about Hera being the goddess of marriage and then I wondered; how does she feel about polygamy? And that lead me to question playing a scion of Hera if she married the mortal? This could put the shoe on the other foot and have Zeus be the jealous one bringing ruin to the scion\u2019s life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3495-elroar","name":"Elroar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3495_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T11:05:30-08:00","id":1042520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1041100#post1041100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you ever get around to it, how will the Philippines and their many, many pantheons be dealt with?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about the many other pantheons but Neall said he was thinking of putting the Tagalog in God.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T17:01:55-08:00","id":1042683,"title":"","content":"Is it bad that I want the polynesian Pantheon now so i can make an incarnation of Maui based off the Maui from Moana? Like for real. I could easily see that character being at least hero level, if not demigod level, and having to utilize the hook as his way of accessing his purviews. I mean, he effectively states as such in the movie. <br /> <br /> not gonna lie, i do just want to make a bunch of pop culture people as Scions, mostly because I think it would be a good time trying to come up with the right balance of things to make the character viable. Like Ron Swanson as an American Scion of some kind.<br /> <br /> also hello everyone! I've been away for a time. it looks like neall decided to answer much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","name":"Grimangel53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T17:32:34-08:00","id":1042698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimangel53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1042683#post1042683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it bad that I want the polynesian Pantheon now so i can make an incarnation of Maui based off the Maui from Moana?</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently the Polynesian pantheon is slated to be in the Demigod book.<br /> <br /> And there's a thread dedicated to &quot;Moana - Totally Awesome!&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T23:23:17-08:00","id":1043396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elroar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1041967#post1041967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking about Hera being the goddess of marriage and then I wondered; how does she feel about polygamy? And that lead me to question playing a scion of Hera if she married the mortal? This could put the shoe on the other foot and have Zeus be the jealous one bringing ruin to the scion\u2019s life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to assume the canonical answer would be that she's too fate bound to the historic Greek model of marriage to embrace polygamy - but then again, at my own table she is a strong supporter of same-sex marriage as it expands her dominion, so obviously it's not something I think you're wrong to decide otherwise about at your own table!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edi