ontainer\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1097275#post1097275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think they'll have to exclud any gods from the original writeup to add the ones that were missing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt it; he said wordcount wasn't the issue there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T19:02:24-07:00","id":1097392,"title":"","content":"After reading about the edification of Confucius,Guanyin and Chiyou. I wanted to know,can a Shen scion deifi someone and turn into a spirit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T19:05:13-07:00","id":1097393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1097183#post1097183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Deception Purview began life as the Illusion Purview. I asked Neall if I could rename to something that sounded more mythic, and he approved!</div> </div> </div> </div>That is awesome. Thanks for the info. Nice to get some little behind the scenes facts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T21:16:10-07:00","id":1097412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1097327#post1097327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I doubt it; he said wordcount wasn't the issue there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wasn't the reason for the choices to conflate any of the gods (Sekhmet and Bast - who originated as the same goddess historically but grew apart over time; Hathor and Aset - who were not the same originally but grew conflated in later eras). It was the reason for things like &quot;not including Nephthys&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T05:12:50-07:00","id":1097492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1097412#post1097412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wasn't the reason for the choices to conflate any of the gods (Sekhmet and Bast - who originated as the same goddess historically but grew apart over time; Hathor and Aset - who were not the same originally but grew conflated in later eras). It was the reason for things like &quot;not including Nephthys&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't that get a little messy though? I'm no expert but wasn't Sobek folded into Horus at one point? And I'm pretty sure they're both in.<br /> <br /> I guess we'll see once the pdf hits.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T08:16:48-07:00","id":1097525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1097492#post1097492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't that get a little messy though? I'm no expert but wasn't Sobek folded into Horus at one point? And I'm pretty sure they're both in.<br /> <br /> I guess we'll see once the pdf hits.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It is messy and completely unavoidable with the Egyptian gods. Whichever ones you are thinking of as the core group, someone else is going to see you as conflating gods they see as distinct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T23:31:37-07:00","id":1097698,"title":"","content":"I'd rather that specific Gods and Goddesses were left out of the initial game to be included later, rather than conflate them into fewer deities, whether that's historically accurate or not. Just my feelings on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T04:23:44-07:00","id":1097743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1097698#post1097698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd rather that specific Gods and Goddesses were left out of the initial game to be included later, rather than conflate them into fewer deities, whether that's historically accurate or not. Just my feelings on the matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds difficult considering the concept of the RPG....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T07:41:45-07:00","id":1097771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1097698#post1097698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd rather that specific Gods and Goddesses were left out of the initial game to be included later, rather than conflate them into fewer deities, whether that's historically accurate or not. Just my feelings on the matter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Concessions have to be made for playability and making a consistent world. Do you really expect non-hindu players to shift through the several thousand Deva to find the right one for example? It\u2019s not like homebrewing it would be at all difficult if you know enough about the pantheon in question to care. Just split the callings and purviews up, add in ones that you feel got dropped and boom, done.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T08:57:17-07:00","id":1097790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1097771#post1097771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Concessions have to be made for playability and making a consistent world. Do you really expect non-hindu players to shift through the several thousand Deva to find the right one for example? It\u2019s not like homebrewing it would be at all difficult if you know enough about the pantheon in question to care. Just split the callings and purviews up, add in ones that you feel got dropped and boom, done.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a difference between choosing not to include Periyatchi the midwife Goddess aspect of Parvati and deciding that Parvati and Lakshmi are the same person, even though both those decisions have religious justification.<br /> <br /> Horus and Ra were also conflated, as were Ra and Khnum... all of these Gods are separate in the Netjer write-up, and there's really no reason Hathor and Sekhmet shouldn't be given the same treatment. No one is asking for a write-up of Sopdet here (not that that wouldn't be cool), but a little more consistency is exactly what we're asking for, where Horus and Khnum apparently deserve to be their own things but Hathor and Sekhmet don't.<br /> <br /> Neall has said before that Scion is first a game about the Gods of mythology, not necessarily the Gods of the religions of the people. If they decide to conflate Parvati and Kali into one Goddess, I would be fine with that, since those two have popular myths where they turn into each other. I would be pretty pissed if they decided Sarasvati Lakshmi and Parvati are all mantles of one person, even though as a Shakta Hindu myself that is something I believe in in real life. Similarly, if they'd decided to make Hathor and Sekhmet two mantles of the same Goddess, I'd have been mostly ok with that, but as it stands, they have about as much reason to be the same person as the dudes mentioned above.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I do also agree with Purple Snit... especially since adding new Gods to the Companion was a Stretch Goal that was achieved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 05-28-2017, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T09:21:05-07:00","id":1097799,"title":"","content":"When it comes to the better-known deities (Sekhmet, Hathor, Lakshmi, Kali, and so on), if there isn't room, time, or money to put them in the basic books, then I just think it would be better if such beings were left out of the rules for now, rather than being officially conflated with other deities*. No-one wants or expects a listing of every God and Goddess - but there is more potential for adventure, politics, and Scions if there are more potential parents and rivals, not fewer.<br /> <br /> *And there are many who will read that (for example) Kali and Parvati are one, and insist it be played that way &quot;because it's in the rules&quot;, and not allow a different perspective from a player or ST. We've all had that kind of player. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T15:04:55-07:00","id":1097880,"title":"","content":"I thought it was Bast and Sekhmet they conflated in the preview, not Sekhmet and Hathor? I feel like the latter would have less room for complaint than there was, considering the myth where Sekhmet literally gets drunk and turns into Hathor. Or was it all three?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm mostly willing to trust the team will do a good job, given their quick response to and willingness to hear feedback on the initial preview.<br /> <br /> As to players (including st's) insisting only the single interpretation in the book be allowed, I feel like that's best solved by explicitly mentioning there are other interpretations that could and would work just as well, rather than limiting the writers to only the interpretations that would be hardest to claim. Probably a good sidebar (and from what we've seen so far, one I'd be surprised if isn't already planned.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13075-malicwanderer","name":"MalicWanderer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T15:36:42-07:00","id":1097889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MalicWanderer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1097880#post1097880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought it was Bast and Sekhmet they conflated in the preview, not Sekhmet and Hathor? I feel like the latter would have less room for complaint than there was, considering the myth where Sekhmet literally gets drunk and turns into Hathor. Or was it all three?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm mostly willing to trust the team will do a good job, given their quick response to and willingness to hear feedback on the initial preview.<br /> <br /> As to players (including st's) insisting only the single interpretation in the book be allowed, I feel like that's best solved by explicitly mentioning there are other interpretations that could and would work just as well, rather than limiting the writers to only the interpretations that would be hardest to claim. Probably a good sidebar (and from what we've seen so far, one I'd be surprised if isn't already planned.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Het-Heru was rolled into Aset for some bizarre reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T16:05:38-07:00","id":1097895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1097889#post1097889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Het-Heru was rolled into Aset for some bizarre reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were conflated at times in Egyptian history. It's not my preferred combo either, but there is literally no lineup of Egyptian gods that do not conflate gods who are separate entities at other times in Egyptian history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T20:43:16-07:00","id":1097960,"title":"","content":"Before the Egyptian pantheon discussion re-ignites into full traction, could it be taken to another thread and leave this one for asking Neall questions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T04:39:52-07:00","id":1098728,"title":"","content":"Neall,in Scion verse how many hero level creatures can scale up to demigod level? Can satyrs or hulders do it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T04:47:26-07:00","id":1098729,"title":"","content":"How many purviews overlap? So far we have seen fire boons that effect the targets creative passion, which would be covered by artistry and passion as well, and fertility has both an innate power that heals, the ability to ensure healthy children, and can give you cancer. All which would also be appropriate for health. While I love this fact since it means you don't have to get an entirly new purview for something you want as a side thing I am curious on just how widespread it is. Do Chaos and Moon both have insanity inducing powers? Can Earth and Forge both shape raw ore to differing degrees?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T16:08:52-07:00","id":1099317,"title":"","content":"After reading the Shen Preview again, I'm curious about how you guys are handling shapeshifting as a divine power.<br /> <br /> We already know that the Theoi are getting a PSP that's all about changing form, so all of their many transformations are covered under that, one assumes.<br /> <br /> What about other Pantheons that don't get access to that PSP? As I read the Shen Preview, I saw the parts talking about Erlang and Sun Wukong's transformation duel. Now Sun Wukon, of course, has the Trickster Calling, and it would make sense for at least some of his transformations to be something from there. But Erlang? I don't see anything in his list of Callings or Purviews that seem to explain his ability to shapeshift. <br /> <br /> How does he do it? Does the Shen PSP also cover shapeshifting? Do some gods just have unique powers that don't necessarily have to apply to their list of powers? Does the Purview system retain 1E's rule of being able to purchase Boons out of order, so he just has a few Boons from other Purviews, without having those Purviews at Associated levels?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T16:16:14-07:00","id":1099319,"title":"","content":"I'd love to hear what supernatural Paths we can expect in the first two books here, especially because I plan to use Origin as my new default urban fantasy system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T16:47:48-07:00","id":1099331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1099317#post1099317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see anything in his list of Callings or Purviews that seem to explain his ability to shapeshift.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never noticed that and now feel like an idiot. I guess maybe it could be hand waved with a relic or something","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12596,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","user":"Alpharius","date":". 06-01-2017, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T18:05:18-07:00","id":1099342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1099331#post1099331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never noticed that and now feel like an idiot. I guess maybe it could be hand waved with a relic or something</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Marvels. We still don't know for sure what the limits on those are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T11:19:16-07:00","id":1099590,"title":"","content":"I forgot if this was already answered, but since the Gaulish pantheon is in the companion does that mean that the incarnate origin is going to be in the hero Corebook or the Scion companion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T13:14:06-07:00","id":1099623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1099590#post1099590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forgot if this was already answered, but since the Gaulish pantheon is in the companion does that mean that the incarnate origin is going to be in the hero Corebook or the Scion companion?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Per Neall, he wants \u200bto be sure he knows how Incarnations work before he includes them as playable option. So that's waiting until God, unless something changed while I wasn't looking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T13:27:34-07:00","id":1099631,"title":"","content":"I believe he said since then the Gaulish Pantheon did raise the possibility that Incarnate characters will be addressed in the Companion (or at least a patch for them that will get fleshed out later), but he wasn't sure yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T21:41:05-07:00","id":1099751,"title":"","content":"Edit: Ninja'd by Glamourweaver","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T23:49:42-07:00","id":1099765,"title":"","content":"Aaaand there's the &quot;changed while I wasn't looking.&quot; Thanks for the update. ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T10:05:05-07:00","id":1099850,"title":"","content":"Any chance the June preview will have anything on the Manitu or character creation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T12:01:43-07:00","id":1099876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1099850#post1099850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any chance the June preview will have anything on the Manitu or character creation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. I'll also do my best to get the Egyptians to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 06-03-2017, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T14:43:14-07:00","id":1099920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1099876#post1099876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure. I'll also do my best to get the Egyptians to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are a benevolent overlord and let it never be said otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T20:03:27-07:00","id":1099993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1099920#post1099920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are a benevolent overlord and let it never be said otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>A possible Manitou/Netjer double feature? You got that right!<br /> <br /> \u200bAll hail Overlord Neall! Long may he reign!<br /> <br /> \u200bWell, at least until the next time his own Overlords fire him, anyway! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T15:55:23-07:00","id":1100235,"title":"","content":"Just how well do the pantheons get along? Excepting the scion bands that seem to frequently involve inter-pantheon cooperation, how united are the gods themselves in this cold war/war against terror thing against the Titans? <br /> <br /> \u200bCorollary to the above, have there been wars between pantheons before? Is that something that happens often, and is it likely to happen again? Or has the Overworld, like the World, come to a place where large-scale conflict looks less desirable than it used to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T19:30:49-07:00","id":1100299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreepyShutIn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1100235#post1100235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bCorollary to the above, have there been wars between pantheons before? Is that something that happens often, and is it likely to happen again? Or has the Overworld, like the World, come to a place where large-scale conflict looks less desirable than it used to?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well remember... While Rome crushed the Gauls, the Theoi waged war on their gods. So-","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T19:35:44-07:00","id":1100301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreepyShutIn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1100235#post1100235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just how well do the pantheons get along? Excepting the scion bands that seem to frequently involve inter-pantheon cooperation, how united are the gods themselves in this cold war/war against terror thing against the Titans?<br /> <br /> \u200bCorollary to the above, have there been wars between pantheons before? Is that something that happens often, and is it likely to happen again? Or has the Overworld, like the World, come to a place where large-scale conflict looks less desirable than it used to?</div> </div> </div> </div>Total war between Pantheons, the kind of war where everyone in both Pantheons gets involved, is rare amongst surviving Pantheons. More common are instances of a handful of Scions from one pantheon griefing another Pantheon and then hightailing it before things got really serious; for example, the Pandava heroes of the Mahabharata once conquered Greece and Rome because they had nothing better to do, but left without actually leaving any kind of governance in place because they didn\u2019t feel like administering an empire (and because they didn\u2019t feel like fighting an inevitably successful Theoi rebellion on its home turf). That said, many of the modern Pantheons have almost certainly wiped out at least one long-forgotten Pantheon sometime in the past; but hey, they were probably Titans anyway, right? The Devas and Yazatas remember a time when they were actively at each other\u2019s throats, but they\u2019ve developed some chill since then.<br /> <br /> Here\u2019s my understanding of most of the Pantheons\u2019 attitudes towards Titanomachy, much of which is based on old drafts so take this all with a grain of salt:<br /> <br /> The Devas, Theoi, and Teotl aggressively promote and prosecute the Titanomachy. The Devas have decided, as usual without caring to ask anyone else, that they are in charge of this alliance, treating the Teotl with honorable respect and the Theoi with patronizing condescension (which might have to do with the stronger Titan blood amongst the Theoi). Among the Devas, Durga, Indra, and Karttikeya are the most hawkish, whereas Ganesha may have single-handedly (okay, four-hands-and-a-trunkedly) averted more international incidents than any other deity by beating those three to conflict zones and telling people to smile and nod at Indra until he goes away instead of rising to his bait.<br /> <br /> The \u00c6sir, Netjer, Shen, Yazatas, and Tuatha have mixed approaches. The \u00c6sir love a good fight but the Devas\u2019 obnoxious suspicion of them (not to mention the J\u00f6tnar among their own ranks) prevents them from participating as uncomplicatedly as the Theoi and the Teotl. The Netjer hate certain Titans, but they also have a lot of Titan friends of whom they\u2019re quite protective. The Shen are on board as far as fighting Titans goes, but they keep hiring defeated Titans instead of imprisoning or killing them, which weirds their Deva friends out. The Yazatas like the concept of Titanomachy, but they were pretty sure the most dangerous Titans were the D(a)evas, and now they\u2019re not really sure what to do. The Tuatha say they\u2019re down with Titanomachy, but the cross-pollination between them and their Titans might be more confusing than any other Pantheon\u2019s, so no one from outside is entirely sure what to do to help them.<br /> <br /> The Manitou, \u00d2r\u00ecsh\u00e0, and Loa are on the dove-ish side. The Manitou view violence against Titans as a last resort; they play defense against their own Titans and will only help with anyone else\u2019s in extreme cases. With the exception of King Od\u00f9duw\u00e0, who throws around the word \u201cTitan\u201d the way you and I might use the word \u201cjerk,\u201d the \u00d2r\u00ecsh\u00e0 and Loa reject the designation \u201cTitan\u201d and the concept of Titanomachy as racist warmongering bullshit.<br /> <br /> The Palas [REDACTED].","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T19:47:57-07:00","id":1100304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1100301#post1100301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the \u00d2r\u00ecsh\u00e0 and Loa reject the designation \u201cTitan\u201d and the concept of Titanomachy as racist warmongering bullshit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like there's more than a little truth to this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T20:55:08-07:00","id":1100324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1100304#post1100304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds like there's more than a little truth to this.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Given the relatively small (By modern standards) population of gods/titans/primordials I don't think you can really say there are enough of them to constitute &quot;races&quot;. Families, clubs, political parties sure, but it all smacks of Hatfield and McCoy smalltown rivalry stuff. At least until you start counting lesser immortals and titanspawn.<br /> <br /> Except everyone involved can level at least a small country if they felt like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T21:48:43-07:00","id":1100337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1100301#post1100301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Devas, Theoi, and Teotl aggressively promote and prosecute the Titanomachy. The Devas have decided, as usual without caring to ask anyone else, that they are in charge of this alliance, treating the Teotl with honorable respect and the Theoi with patronizing condescension (which might have to do with the stronger Titan blood amongst the Theoi). Among the Devas, Durga, Indra, and Karttikeya are the most hawkish, whereas Ganesha may have single-handedly (okay, four-hands-and-a-trunkedly) averted more international incidents than any other deity by beating those three to conflict zones and telling people to smile and nod at Indra until he goes away instead of rising to his bait.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really love this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Not least because the Theoi and Teotl are amongst my favourite non-Deva Pantheons and having them in a kind of pseudo alliance is amazing. The Deva deciding that they are, of course, the leaders in this endeavor is also completely something they would do <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But I love the implication that Durga and Kartikkeya are finally playable patrons for once! Also Ganesh is amazing, but that was never in any doubt. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I have to ask though... where are the Kami in all this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T07:43:45-07:00","id":1100447,"title":"","content":"Here's a weird question that consumed far too much time at our last gaming-night: How will firearm ammunition be dealt with in Scion? Bean-counting each bullet, something more stylistic (like Hurt Locker), or full-on cinematic (you have enough until you botch a roll, or maybe spray-and-pray)? Just curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/820-gyre","name":"gyre","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T17:32:11-07:00","id":1100654,"title":"","content":"2 questions related to origins: how hard will it homebrew new supernatural character paths for a versatile urban fantasy game? like making new knacks and the like?<br /> and how hard but it be to play a witch in the classic sense? Cauldrons, crystal balls, curses that sort of thing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T20:07:11-07:00","id":1100683,"title":"","content":"One thing I really liked about 1e were the paired landscape portraits of the pantheons, with one showing the pantheon with an ancient appearance and the other a modern one. Will this be making a return in 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12989-center-of-all","name":"Center-of-All","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T22:17:17-07:00","id":1100714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1100301#post1100301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Palas [REDACTED].</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay so for someone who didn't get any results from a 10-second Google search (aside from Pallas, apparently a Greek Titan), am I just thick for not knowing who the Palas are?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T23:49:15-07:00","id":1100728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1100714#post1100714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay so for someone who didn't get any results from a 10-second Google search (aside from Pallas, apparently a Greek Titan), am I just thick for not knowing who the Palas are?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, not really. It's one people have been trying to figure out since Lula started mentioning them.<br /> <br /> They're name-dropped in the Shen preview as sharing an Underworld with the Shen, Kami, and Devas, and their name in that context suggests they're from the Indian subcontinent. Which gods they <i>are</i>, though...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T00:25:32-07:00","id":1100738,"title":"","content":"So I found this, and I think this may be the Palas?<br /> <br /> &quot;The Ashtadikpalas are eight in number. As their collective name suggests, they rule the eight quarters or the eight directions of the universe. Ashta means eight, dik means quarters or directions and palas means rulers. According to Hinduism each quarter is assigned to a particular divinity, who presides over it and acts as its chief guardian spirit ensuring the orderliness (rta) of the universe and the protection of its occupants. (It is interesting to note that there are no goddesses in this list, just as there are none in the list of navagrahas also). Symbolically the eight rules of directions are represented as eight elephants standing in eight directions.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The concept of Ashtadikpalas was a post vedic development. In the Vedic period it was the Adityas who ruled the skies and kept a watch over the world from one end to another. The Adityas knew all the deeds, because they had eyes and spies everywhere. The Adityas were born out of Aditi, the mother of all Gods. While the Adityas rule the skies, on earth it is Pusan, the handsome god with a shaft who knew the directions and who shows the paths that lead to green pastures and safe places. In the Rigvedic hymns we do not find any reference to the dikpalas. But as individual gods each of them enjoyed a supreme status and commanded his own following and veneration.&quot;<br /> <br /> Full name is Ashtadikpalas, they seem to be a branch of Hindu thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","user":"TheGraySoul","date":". 06-06-2017, 03:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T00:53:51-07:00","id":1100746,"title":"","content":"I did think of the Dikpala too when I heard the name, but the Dikpalas are pretty much a set of Hindu Gods, Indra to the East, Agni to the South-East, Yama to the South, Nirrti to the South-West (who technically is a Goddess at least most of the time), Varuna to the West, Vayu to the North-West, Kubera to the North and Ishaan (a form of Shiva) to the North-East. Some latter groupings add Brahma Above and Vishnu Below to include all ten directions in Hindu thought. While a lot of them do have a presence in other cultures (like Indra and Brahma in certain branches of Buddhism, or Varuna and Vayu amongst the Yazata), I'm not sure they really function as a Pantheon on their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 06-06-2017, 04:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T08:49:04-07:00","id":1100859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1100301#post1100301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Total war between Pantheons, the kind of war where everyone in both Pantheons gets involved, is rare amongst surviving Pantheons. More common are instances of a handful of Scions from one pantheon griefing another Pantheon and then hightailing it before things got really serious; for example, the Pandava heroes of the Mahabharata once conquered Greece and Rome because they had nothing better to do, but left without actually leaving any kind of governance in place because they didn\u2019t feel like administering an empire (and because they didn\u2019t feel like fighting an inevitably successful Theoi rebellion on its home turf). That said, many of the modern Pantheons have almost certainly wiped out at least one long-forgotten Pantheon sometime in the past; but hey, they were probably Titans anyway, right? The Devas and Yazatas remember a time when they were actively at each other\u2019s throats, but they\u2019ve developed some chill since then.<br /> <br /> Here\u2019s my understanding of most of the Pantheons\u2019 attitudes towards Titanomachy, much of which is based on old drafts so take this all with a grain of salt:<br /> <br /> The Devas, Theoi, and Teotl aggressively promote and prosecute the Titanomachy. The Devas have decided, as usual without caring to ask anyone else, that they are in charge of this alliance, treating the Teotl with honorable respect and the Theoi with patronizing condescension (which might have to do with the stronger Titan blood amongst the Theoi). Among the Devas, Durga, Indra, and Karttikeya are the most hawkish, whereas Ganesha may have single-handedly (okay, four-hands-and-a-trunkedly) averted more international incidents than any other deity by beating those three to conflict zones and telling people to smile and nod at Indra until he goes away instead of rising to his bait.<br /> <br /> The \u00c6sir, Netjer, Shen, Yazatas, and Tuatha have mixed approaches. The \u00c6sir love a good fight but the Devas\u2019 obnoxious suspicion of them (not to mention the J\u00f6tnar among their own ranks) prevents them from participating as uncomplicatedly as the Theoi and the Teotl. The Netjer hate certain Titans, but they also have a lot of Titan friends of whom they\u2019re quite protective. The Shen are on board as far as fighting Titans goes, but they keep hiring defeated Titans instead of imprisoning or killing them, which weirds their Deva friends out. The Yazatas like the concept of Titanomachy, but they were pretty sure the most dangerous Titans were the D(a)evas, and now they\u2019re not really sure what to do. The Tuatha say they\u2019re down with Titanomachy, but the cross-pollination between them and their Titans might be more confusing than any other Pantheon\u2019s, so no one from outside is entirely sure what to do to help them.<br /> <br /> The Manitou, \u00d2r\u00ecsh\u00e0, and Loa are on the dove-ish side. The Manitou view violence against Titans as a last resort; they play defense against their own Titans and will only help with anyone else\u2019s in extreme cases. With the exception of King Od\u00f9duw\u00e0, who throws around the word \u201cTitan\u201d the way you and I might use the word \u201cjerk,\u201d the \u00d2r\u00ecsh\u00e0 and Loa reject the designation \u201cTitan\u201d and the concept of Titanomachy as racist warmongering bullshit.<br /> <br /> The Palas [REDACTED].</div> </div> </div> </div>I love everything in this! THIS is the kind of world-depth that I found sorely lacking in 1E. Now, I know that 1E was approached from a completely different perspective than 2E is, so that's not a knock on the people who made 1E. But this is just so much more compelling and interesting and I'm glad to see it. <br /> <br /> That thing about the Pandava heroes conquering Greece and Rome? Is that an actual mythological event? Or did you guys just make that up to make the history of the Scion World more interesting? I know there's a myth about Dionysus invading India and eventually being repulsed. We know Alexander the Great invaded India and was defeated there as well. But I don't think I've ever seen or heard of a myth involving India invading Greece and Italy. <br /> <br /> Either way, it sounds kickass!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T13:19:19-07:00","id":1100935,"title":"","content":"I imagine the Annuna would be in on the hardliners alliance? What with the leadership of Marduk and threat of a return of Tiamat?<br /> <br /> And the Kami are probably with the &quot;least concerned with Titanomachy&quot; group?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 06-06-2017, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T16:30:15-07:00","id":1101012,"title":"","content":"So Neall, what's the latest on Paths and Callings? If I'm correct, they've undergone some revisions lately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T16:33:35-07:00","id":1101018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-ne