{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T06:47:59-07:00","id":1101202,"title":"","content":"So what's his all consuming purview? I don't know much about these myths but a quick wikipedia skim makes him seem like a many headed man of equally many arts and abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T07:29:54-07:00","id":1101213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1101202#post1101202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what's his all consuming purview? I don't know much about these myths but a quick wikipedia skim makes him seem like a many headed man of equally many arts and abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd take a guess at any one of War, Deception, Passion, or Prosperity. War is a good choice for any Asura especially one that kicked Indra out of Svarga, but then that happens once a week, so it's not the most original or best choice. Deception, since, as a Rakshasha, Ravana is skilled at illusion, but there are better people for that, including his uncle Maricha, father in law Mayadanava or even his son Indrajit. He also never really shows the kind of dedication to illusions that a Titan might be expected to show... it's more a way for him to get other stuff that what he's all about. Passion makes sense if you consider his noted virility, his extensive harem, and his major myth cycle basically being about his extreme acts of Devotion to Shiva (though that just may be the Yoga PSP) and his lust for Sita, which ultimately causes his downfall. But as much as Ravana has and symbolizes passions run rampant, he's not particularly associated with spreading them. But my favourite choice for him, honestly, is Prosperity. Ravana is lord of the domain of Lanka, called Swarna Lanka, literally Golden Lanka, the mightiest and most prosperous of rulers; and Prosperity can also cover his Passion type associations... his virility and harem as an outgrowth of his mighty rulership and realm. Even the kidnapping of Sita makes sense from a Prosperity lens... his kingdom has all the jewels in Heaven and Earth... only the most beautiful woman on Earth is not in his domain, so he seeks to make her part of it.<br /> <br /> You could also make an argument for Epic Strength or Stamina, and he definitely has powers from all these Purviews, but Prosperity has my vote. I wonder if, the way Gods have 3 callings, Titans can have more than one Purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 06-07-2017, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T07:37:52-07:00","id":1101218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1101213#post1101213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could also make an argument for Epic Strength or Stamina, and he definitely has powers from all these Purviews, but Prosperity has my vote. I wonder if, the way Gods have 3 callings, Titans can have more than one Purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neall's said most Titans have between 1-3 Purviews.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T17:08:37-07:00","id":1101796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=519776#post519776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Descent from Legendary creatures is something I <i>really</i> want to have in there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that in the main book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T19:17:02-07:00","id":1102410,"title":"","content":"So if gods are shaped to match the beliefs of humanity, does this apply to platonic ideals as well? Is there one perfect dog out there which matches exactly what everyone imagines when they hear the word &quot;dog&quot;? Not just a good boy, but the best?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13499,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13499-not-quite-yoda","user":"Not Quite Yoda","date":". 06-10-2017, 10:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13499-not-quite-yoda","name":"Not Quite Yoda","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T06:45:05-07:00","id":1102492,"title":"","content":"Some time since I last went by for some insights. Last I checked backerkit, a pledge level can still be upped and I consider it in earnest. First I'd like to have more insight into the mechanics of Scion 2nd Ed:<br /> <br /> - Are the mechanics depicted in Scion Origins generic enough to be implemented for home brew settings (fantasy, scifi, ...) like for example Cortex plus? I'm still searching a kind of a flexible system.<br /> Another example, Numenera, I like the setting but not so the mechanics. Could I use storypath for it?<br /> <br /> - Will the Scion Jumpstart be published in near future?<br /> <br /> - Are there other documents giving more insight into the storypath system apart from the 12 page document on drivethrurpg?<br /> <br /> Maybe some additional questions like will there be rules for mass combat? Rules for traps and exploration like in dungeon delving style adventures?<br /> <br /> Any answer would help me making my mind about upping my pledge. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 06-11-2017, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T09:12:37-07:00","id":1102527,"title":"","content":"Storypath is being used to power a sci-fi game as well, so you might want to wait for Trinity to come out and use it since they'll have done all the necessary work to gussy it up as needed for the space-future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T09:36:07-07:00","id":1102538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1102527#post1102527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Storypath is being used to power a sci-fi game as well, so you might want to wait for Trinity to come out and use it since they'll have done all the necessary work to gussy it up as needed for the space-future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also supers (Aberrant) and pulp (Adventure!). So... much like its Storyteller ancestor, Storypath's being used to power multiple genres, but it's been designed with an eye to handling scaling, an area where Storyteller has great trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T09:53:52-07:00","id":1102542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1102527#post1102527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Storypath is being used to power a sci-fi game as well, so you might want to wait for Trinity to come out and use it since they'll have done all the necessary work to gussy it up as needed for the space-future.</div> </div> </div> </div>And for classical fantasy settings including magic? Would Scion Origins be the real deal or would it be better to wait for Trinity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T06:01:58-07:00","id":1102783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belisarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1102542#post1102542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And for classical fantasy settings including magic? Would Scion Origins be the real deal or would it be better to wait for Trinity?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Storypath can handle those, although I don't know the specifics - whether Scion or Trinity's version would be better, or whether they'd be about the same, for example.<br /> <br /> Pugmire runs on a tweaked D&amp;D 5e engine, including its magic system. A potential stretch goal, which it didn't reach, was for a Storypath conversion. If Storypath can be modified to handle a D&amp;D-esque setting, it'd probably be able to handle what you're looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T12:45:05-07:00","id":1102893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belisarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1102542#post1102542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And for classical fantasy settings including magic? Would Scion Origins be the real deal or would it be better to wait for Trinity?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been mentioned Trinity will be a bit more mechanically gritty/simulationist than Scion n, while Scion will be a bit more narrative. Neither are super gritty or narrative system wise, just in comparison to each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T13:58:22-07:00","id":1102907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1102893#post1102893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's been mentioned Trinity will be a bit more mechanically gritty/simulationist than Scion n, while Scion will be a bit more narrative. Neither are super gritty or narrative system wise, just in comparison to each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>And from that we could take a stab in the dark and say Scion for high Fantasy and Trinity for Low?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T16:57:23-07:00","id":1102949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1102907#post1102907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And from that we could take a stab in the dark and say Scion for high Fantasy and Trinity for Low?</div> </div> </div> </div>Those genres don't correspond to more or less narrative roleplaying systems. Trinity is going to support superheroes (Aberrant) and Scion is going to support lower magic urban fantasy (Origins).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","