4,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belisarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1103230#post1103230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar137_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"137\" data-vbnamecard=\"137\">Neall</a>, is the Jumpstart Adventure anywhere in sight?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll start work on it after the cores are in editing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T17:50:20-07:00","id":1107454,"title":"","content":"I've managed to get my group interested in Scion, but with American Gods having just finished up I'm worried about keeping their enthusiasm levels up. Is there any chance the Bestiary or Companion will start getting released between now and the core books' release, to help tide them over?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13499-not-quite-yoda","name":"Not Quite Yoda","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T20:18:42-07:00","id":1107500,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Whoops, nevermind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 06-25-2017, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T10:52:41-07:00","id":1107682,"title":"","content":"Are follows useful now? And is there a birthright for a close companion or just a fatebound role? In first ed RAW you sort of had to have a guide that was, well a lousy source of information if you wanted them to be available for most of your adventures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T13:23:27-07:00","id":1107736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1107682#post1107682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are follows useful now? And is there a birthright for a close companion or just a fatebound role? In first ed RAW you sort of had to have a guide that was, well a lousy source of information if you wanted them to be available for most of your adventures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most followers actually contribute directly to your own statistics, allowing you to use particular Stunts. Guides are the same, but perhaps a little more versatile; they can be used to pull Stunts and esoteric supernatural powers, as well as Purview access, in exchange for favors. It's a mentorship role, but you definitely have to get coffee for them once in a while, for a value of &quot;coffee&quot; that means &quot;kill this giant lion&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T13:52:25-07:00","id":1107749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=601757#post601757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Baba Yaga isn't a goddess in <b>Scion 2e</b>. Her riders, though, can go toe-to-toe with demigods.<br /> <br /> Atticus is a viable character concept, although he's probably going to be a bit lower-powered than the books portray; the name of the game is <b>Scion</b>, not <b>Iron Druid</b>. Still, I adored the Iron Druid books, so take that for what you will.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Teotl are actually the Aztec pantheon this edition; the Inca and Mayan pantheons are slated for inclusion in later books, though they'll be mentioned (and the Aztecs and Maya share Quetzacoatl/Kukulkan). There are confederate pantheons in the game, but those aren't them.</div> </div> </div> </div>What creatures from the bestiary can go toe toe to demigods?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T16:42:32-07:00","id":1107801,"title":"","content":"man... following that quote back, I almost responded to another post and reawaken a debate from well over a hundred pages ago!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"M