1110253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1110170#post1110170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm crunching on finishing Origins, and that's the priority. The update will come after that, so expect it Sunday or Monday, or maybe over the holiday.</div> </div> </div> </div>Crunch! Crunch like the wind!<br /> <br /> But seriously, don't burn out. As anxious as we all are it won't spell death and doom to wait an extra few days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T10:49:56-07:00","id":1110257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1110238#post1110238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Print it out, toss it on a bun, and add condiments as desired. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd eat it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thanks for the update, Neall. I'm fairly certain I speak for everybody when I say finishing Origins is more important than an update.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T07:05:20-07:00","id":1110830,"title":"","content":"awesome. I'm gonna be waiting eagerly. and hopefully, we get things soon. but as long as origins and hero get done, im good.<br /> <br /> as of now, all the other books im anticipating from onyx path are in dev. so thats good (from Origins/Hero to Changeling 2e and Geist 2e (which im super fraking excited about))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","name":"Grimangel53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T13:41:50-07:00","id":1110987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1110194#post1110194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd not object to a joyous American explosion meat day coincidence with the update. Now if only there were some way to put it on a bun and eat it</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm doing chili and sausages that day, so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T16:38:08-07:00","id":1111062,"title":"","content":"Put the meat on the meat on the bread and then inside of the human meat. Meatception","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T11:33:20-07:00","id":1111742,"title":"","content":"So in the World, was historic Christianity less militantly hostile toward polytheists in Europe and the Americas, and Islam less so in the Middle East and Central and Southern Asia? I get the premise that the various dead/reconstructed traditions have continuously survived as minority faiths in the World, I'm just wondering how that looked historically.<br /> <br /> Like are British Catholics historically more tolerant and integrationist toward Celtic paganism, while British Protestants have a better relationship with Germanic paganism?<br /> <br /> Did the obliteration of the Nemetondevos later make France a bastion of hardline absolute Christianity without indigenous paganism, or did Theoi worship stick around from the Roman Empire?<br /> <br /> Did the precedent of European Christianity tolerating pagans in their midst affect the treatment of Jews in the World, or the relationship between Catholicism and Protestantism in the Early Modern period?<br /> <br /> As the people who actually killed Jesus were Theoi worshippers, do Jews still get scapegoated when Theoi worshippers are right there? Or maybe that just makes it more important to scapegoat Jews since the Eleucinan Mysteries included powerful medieval nobles...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-05-2017, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T15:09:48-07:00","id":1111828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1111742#post1111742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the people who actually killed Jesus were Theoi worshippers, do Jews still get scapegoated when Theoi worshippers are right there? Or maybe that just makes it more important to scapegoat Jews since the Eleucinan Mysteries included powerful medieval nobles...</div> </div> </div> </div>This thought never actually occurred to me before but that's a great point. I am also 100% going to find some way to slip it into my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T19:20:37-07:00","id":1111939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1111742#post1111742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the people who actually killed Jesus were Theoi worshippers, do Jews still get scapegoated when Theoi worshippers are right there? Or maybe that just makes it more important to scapegoat Jews since the Eleucinan Mysteries included powerful medieval nobles...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, assuming that the Bible in Scion is exactly like the Bible we know, then the Jews may still get the blame for the death of Jesus. An important fact that often gets overlooked is that the Theoi worshippers who actually nailed Jesus to the cross did so essentially at the bidding of the Jewish religious leadership. Pontius Pilate interrogated Jesus and found no real fault with him. He was never formally charged with any crime under Roman law.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs was customary back then, Pilate gave the Jewish people an annual choice of convicted criminal to be released. He offered them the choice of Jesus: a man with whom he personally found no fault, and Barabas: a convicted murderer and rebel. The people chose Barabas and demanded that Jesus be executed. They didn't have the legal authority to condemn him to death themselves, so Pilate had the choice of carry out the execution himself, or face a full-scale riot from his subjects. Such riots broke out fairly frequently in Judea, and Pilate was under orders to keep things quiet. Hence? The decision to execute Jesus. Pilate, of course, washed his hands of the whole matter and refused to accept any responsibility for Jesus' death.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Theoi worshippers were merely the &quot;tools&quot; who carried out the will of the Jewish people, so I'm guessing the Jews would still get at least the majority of the blame. You could even argue that Jesus' declaration &quot;Father, forgive them. They know not what they do.&quot; could've been Jesus personally absolving the men who killed him. Heck, technically, a Theoi worshipper (Pilate) was the first person to ever proclaim Jesus &quot;The King of the Jews.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T19:24:47-07:00","id":1111943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1111939#post1111939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAs was customary back then, Pilate gave the Jewish people an annual choice of convicted criminal to be released.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware that's what the Biblical narrative says, particularly the Gospel of Matthew, but I need to point out there isn't a shred of contemporary evidence of this being customary back then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T19:33:52-07:00","id":1111948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1111943#post1111943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm aware that's what the Biblical narrative says, particularly the Gospel of Matthew, but I need to point out there isn't a shred of contemporary evidence of this being customary back then.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIs that so? Didn't know. I just know the stories.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd considering that Scion's default assumption is that &quot;All myths are true?&quot; If all we have are myths, then one assumes the myths are what we go with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T19:51:43-07:00","id":1111951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1111948#post1111948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bIs that so? Didn't know. I just know the stories.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd considering that Scion's default assumption is that &quot;All myths are true?&quot; If all we have are myths, then one assumes the myths are what we go with.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True, but in some cases, when the symbolic is more important than the literal, it might be more meaningful if it isn't reduced to a literal event. If we understand the crowd and the whole &quot;blood on the hands of our descendants&quot; element to be about HUMANITY, rather than the specific gathered Jews; and Barabbas representative of a sinner saved by Christ's sacrifice (the name Barabbas literally just means &quot;Son of Father&quot;), the theological relevance of the telling starts to become much clearer than it is with a crowd of Jews wanting a murderer freed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-05-2017, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T20:11:59-07:00","id":1111960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1111951#post1111951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> True, but in some cases, when the symbolic is more important than the literal, it might be more meaningful if it isn't reduced to a literal event. If we understand the crowd and the whole &quot;blood on the hands of our descendants&quot; element to be about HUMANITY, rather than the specific gathered Jews; and Barabbas representative of a sinner saved by Christ's sacrifice (the name Barabbas literally just means &quot;Son of Father&quot;), the theological relevance of the telling starts to become much clearer than it is with a crowd of Jews wanting a murderer freed.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHm. Interesting. Never looked at it that way before.<br /> <br /> \u200bOf course, even if that particular part of the story is wrong, it doesn't really change much. Unless we choose to throw out the entire story, then the story remains that it was the Jews who gave the order for Jesus' execution. It's easy enough to see how Christian could still be made to view the Jews as the responsible party. Sure, maybe in a world in which both Jews AND Theoi worshippers are still around, Christians may come to blame both groups. Since both Jews and Theoi worshippers are likely to be a minority in any predominantly Christian areas, both groups would be relatively easy prey most of the time. When people blame a group for some perceived wrong, they always tend to be bolder about persecuting that group if they know they outnumber them by a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T21:34:13-07:00","id":1111973,"title":"","content":"As I understand it, the key points in Christian development were:<br /> <br /> \u00b7 Jesus' ministry, a three-year period where he went around performing miracles and teaching his disciples, preparing them for what would come next<br /> \u00b7 the birth of the Church, which started with the events of Easter (from Palm Sunday through his crucifixion, Resurrection, and Ascension), and culminating in the day of Pentecost, when the Holy Spirit entered his followers, empowering them to perform the sorts of miracles that Jesus had been known for. This was followed by a period of persecution when the Jewish leadership attempted top stamp out what they considered a new heresy.<br /> \u00b7 The destruction of the Jewish Temple 40 years later. This was when the persecution of the Church shifted from being Jewish to being Roman. It's also when the divide between Judaism and Christianity really kicked in: before this event, Christianity was considered to be a branch of Judaism, and after this event, Christianity was seen more and more as its own thing.<br /> \u00b7 Constantine's conversion to Christianity, which ended the Roman persecution of the Church. Note that when Constantine legitimized Christianity, that didn't start the persecution <i>by</i> Christianity of other faiths; for a while there, Christianity coexisted more or less peacefully with other religions.<br /> \u00b7 If I recall correctly, the Council of Nicea was the point when Christianity started to develop an intolerance for other religions. It was intended to establish what the Christian orthodoxy was, so that it wouldn't become watered down and meaningless; but it had the side effect of not just purging heresies from the Church, but also viewing other religions as false and harmful and thus to be opposed (whereas previously, the other religions were merely viewed as wrong, and the extent of \u201chostility\u201d from Christianity came from efforts to recruit non-Christians). <br /> <br /> There's more, but I think the above covers the major points where other religions are concerned. For Scion, If be inclined to alter aspects of how the Council of Nicea played out. Meanwhile, in keeping with the \u201cAll Myths are True\u201d aspect of Scion, I'd keep as much as possible as literal as possible, and say that the Biblical account is accurate as far as Judaism and Christianity go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T21:50:25-07:00","id":1111978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1111973#post1111973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> say that the Biblical account is accurate as far as Judaism and Christianity go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem is this statement is mutually exclusive with itself, at least from the Jewish perspective it is. Unless they have separate Pantheons/cosmologies, if the Christian Biblical narrative is true-in-setting with regard to an Abrahamic Pantheon, than Judaism is invalidated as a belief system for turning away from the true messiah that was promised.<br /> <br /> I think both being wrong, and just going with the Caananite/Phoenician Pantheon as the source of YHWH is probably the most neutral solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-06-2017, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T22:45:14-07:00","id":1111985,"title":"","content":"I'm talking about the events on the ground, not the metaphysics or cosmology behind them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T19:20:14-07:00","id":1112455,"title":"","content":"Hey i'm curious: if each of these books (origins, hero, ect.) is meant to have a different playstyle and approach then what is demigod's: origins is very dresden files, hero is more your superhero-y child of the gods handling mythical problems and and god is self explanatory in how it differs, but in what way is demigod different from hero in terms of concept and playstyle. I mean you're still half mortal children handling mythic problems so beyond powerups what has changed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T19:44:20-07:00","id":1112462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1112455#post1112455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey i'm curious: if each of these books (origins, hero, ect.) is meant to have a different playstyle and approach then what is demigod's: origins is very dresden files, hero is more your superhero-y child of the gods handling mythical problems and and god is self explanatory in how it differs, but in what way is demigod different from hero in terms of concept and playstyle. I mean you're still half mortal children handling mythic problems so beyond powerups what has changed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Culture heroism and the end of the hero's journey in a few ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T21:07:08-07:00","id":1112487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1112462#post1112462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Culture heroism and the end of the hero's journey in a few ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having just read Campbell and Vogler's books on the journey, I'm pleased that it's getting open consideration in this most fitting of lines.<br /> <br /> I also appreciate how much effort you're spending trying to get the corebooks out. We'd all love some new information, but we will love having the actual books in our hands much more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T18:30:06-07:00","id":1114348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1111960#post1111960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bHm. Interesting. Never looked at it that way before.<br /> <br /> \u200bOf course, even if that particular part of the story is wrong, it doesn't really change much. Unless we choose to throw out the entire story, then the story remains that it was the Jews who gave the order for Jesus' execution. It's easy enough to see how Christian could still be made to view the Jews as the responsible party. Sure, maybe in a world in which both Jews AND Theoi worshippers are still around, Christians may come to blame both groups. Since both Jews and Theoi worshippers are likely to be a minority in any predominantly Christian areas, both groups would be relatively easy prey most of the time. When people blame a group for some perceived wrong, they always tend to be bolder about persecuting that group if they know they outnumber them by a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> why is blood libel apologism being spoken so casually on here? even going by the traditional christian accounting of events the pharisees were a group of religious leaders who had no power to carry out any kind of violent acts on their own, and even if that were not the case their actions are not representative of the entire jewish people of that time and certainly not of this time. The romans were the ones who held all their power in their conquered territories, assuming jesus lived, the romans tortures, crucified, and ultimately killed him.<br /> If it is easy to see why christians would still be made to view jewish people as the responsible party for the actions of a long dead empire it is because there has been thousands of years of antisemitic propagandizing to scape goat jewish people, cementing in the minds of western christians and western people in general that jewish people are inherently evil and untrustworthy as they have supposedly done the unthinkable by killing jesus.<br /> <br /> the question that glamourweaver posed was to ask what would happen in a setting where the people actually responsible for killing jesus were still around preventing the church from as easily propagandizing jewish people. <br /> <br /> that being said given the fact that similar scapegoating has been experienced by the rroma people for as long as they have been in europe, it is easy to see that european people have had a long courtship with hating marginalized and stateless peoples, had christianity not been used by the later roman empire as a means and justification of conquest as it was by later colonial powers then it's possible that the existence of many such groups who did not fall into a single group might have lessened this persecution of other groups that were so obviously othered as well, however the most likely occurrence is that anyone who was not a white christian in europe would have faced heavy persecution in the region just as other people who were not white christians faced heavy persecution in our own world. Its important to remember that for much of its history white christianity was anathema to all groups not similar to itself, including non-white christians, so unless the setting in the game is extremely different then i don't see much of that changing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T19:27:53-07:00","id":1114364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>norraba</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1114348#post1114348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> why is blood libel apologism being spoken so casually on here? even going by the traditional christian accounting of events the pharisees were a group of religious leaders who had no power to carry out any kind of violent acts on their own, and even if that were not the case their actions are not representative of the entire jewish people of that time and certainly not of this time. The romans were the ones who held all their power in their conquered territories, assuming jesus lived, the romans tortures, crucified, and ultimately killed him.<br /> If it is easy to see why christians would still be made to view jewish people as the responsible party for the actions of a long dead empire it is because there has been thousands of years of antisemitic propagandizing to scape goat jewish people, cementing in the minds of western christians and western people in general that jewish people are inherently evil and untrustworthy as they have supposedly done the unthinkable by killing jesus.<br /> <br /> the question that glamourweaver posed was to ask what would happen in a setting where the people actually responsible for killing jesus were still around preventing the church from as easily propagandizing jewish people.<br /> <br /> that being said given the fact that similar scapegoating has been experienced by the rroma people for as long as they have been in europe, it is easy to see that european people have had a long courtship with hating marginalized and stateless peoples, had christianity not been used by the later roman empire as a means and justification of conquest as it was by later colonial powers then it's possible that the existence of many such groups who did not fall into a single group might have lessened this persecution of other groups that were so obviously othered as well, however the most likely occurrence is that anyone who was not a white christian in europe would have faced heavy persecution in the region just as other people who were not white christians faced heavy persecution in our own world. Its important to remember that for much of its history white christianity was anathema to all groups not similar to itself, including non-white christians, so unless the setting in the game is extremely different then i don't see much of that changing.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why we cannot have nice things.<br /> This is also why we cannot have discussions about a PRETEND history of a world that contains PRETEND versions of Abrahamic faiths.<br /> <br /> I'm out until the books appear at my door.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T20:05:16-07:00","id":1114375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>norraba</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1114348#post1114348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">why is blood libel apologism being spoken so casually on here?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't aware that it was? I thought we were talking hypothetically about the fictional history of these faiths in a fictional world in which we have to reconcile their histories in a world in which all their myths happened? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> even going by the traditional christian accounting of events the pharisees were a group of religious leaders who had no power to carry out any kind of violent acts on their own, and even if that were not the case their actions are not representative of the entire jewish people of that time and certainly not of this time. The romans were the ones who held all their power in their conquered territories, assuming jesus lived, the romans tortures, crucified, and ultimately killed him. </div> </div> </div>\u200bOnce again? If the traditional accounting of events is correct, then in this particular case, the Pharisees DID in fact have the power to carry out violent acts. Pilate GAVE them the choice to spare or kill Jesus after personally declaring that he didn't find him guilty of any wrongdoing that merited execution. If the Pharisees chose to spare Jesus, then he would've walked away from the whole incident none the worse for wear. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it is easy to see why christians would still be made to view jewish people as the responsible party for the actions of a long dead empire it is because there has been thousands of years of antisemitic propagandizing to scape goat jewish people, cementing in the minds of western christians and western people in general that jewish people are inherently evil and untrustworthy as they have supposedly done the unthinkable by killing jesus. </div> </div> </div>\u200bIf the Christian story is correct and the Jews did, in fact, order Jesus' execution, then yes, it IS easy to see how their historical blood feud with Judaism was able to perpetuate. If they sincerely (and correctly) believe that they ordered the death of their Messiah, then that is exactly the kind of situation in which long-standing blood feuds tend to appear. <br /> <br /> \u200bNow is this a RIGHT attitude for them to take? Of course not! According to Christian beliefs, Jesus HAD to die in order to fulfill the prophecy and redeem all of mankind. It shouldn't MATTER who actually did the deed. According to Christian beliefs, that deed needed to be done. Also? Jesus' declaration of forgiveness for his killers should make it pretty clear that Jesus himself would not approve of any long-term vendettas against a group of people whom he forgave. To say nothing of the fact that his entire message was all about forgiving and showing mercy to those who wrong you. <br /> <br /> \u200bRegardless of whether or not the Christian story is accurate, Christians should not hold any animosity in their hearts toward anyone regarding Jesus' death. What some of them have done over the course of millennia is still wrong whether their story is right or not. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the question that glamourweaver posed was to ask what would happen in a setting where the people actually responsible for killing jesus were still around preventing the church from as easily propagandizing jewish people. </div> </div> </div>\u200bAnd my answer was to present at least one scenario in which the Christians could still come to view the Jews as being the ones responsible for Jesus' death. These are NOT my beliefs. I was presenting a possible scenario. Not quoting one of the Laws of Physics.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T20:15:46-07:00","id":1114378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1114364#post1114364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why we cannot have nice things.<br /> This is also why we cannot have discussions about a PRETEND history of a world that contains PRETEND versions of Abrahamic faiths.<br /> <br /> I'm out until the books appear at my door.</div> </div> </div> </div> This. My apologies for contributing to this tangent; but bear in mind that this is \u201cAsk Neall\u201d.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T21:34:02-07:00","id":1114416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1114364#post1114364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why we cannot have nice things.<br /> This is also why we cannot have discussions about a PRETEND history of a world that contains PRETEND versions of Abrahamic faiths.<br /> <br /> I'm out until the books appear at my door.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assigning guilt for Christ's death is responsible for countless deaths through history, so people take it seriously. &quot;Jews killed Christ&quot; was the cornerstone claim of Jewish persecution and slaughter in Europe until the 20th century when eugenics and Marxist-conspiracy claims superseded it for the Nazis, though they were building on centuries of antisemitism that that had been central to the foundation of.<br /> <br /> It's a serious subject matter and people are going to respond to it accordingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-11-2017, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T23:02:37-07:00","id":1114452,"title":"","content":"I have a question Neall do you have any idea when we will get something from the Kickstarter many of us backed? There hasn't even been a real update in 3 months. I've been watching the news letter for the last 4 months the books have been in development which sounds like the whole system has been scrapped and is being rewritten from scratch. Is this the case if so let your investors know what's going on. If not maybe you can give us a clearer picture of what stage we are in and what being done.<br /> <br /> I don't mean to attack you or anything but 3 months with anyword is not right","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6379-tytalan","name":"tytalan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T23:37:29-07:00","id":1114457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tytalan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1114452#post1114452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question Neall do you have any idea when we will get something from the Kickstarter many of us backed? There hasn't even been a real update in 3 months. I've been watching the news letter for the last 4 months the books have been in development which sounds like the whole system has been scrapped and is being rewritten from scratch. Is this the case if so let your investors know what's going on. If not maybe you can give us a clearer picture of what stage we are in and what being done.<br /> <br /> I don't mean to attack you or anything but 3 months with anyword is not right</div> </div> </div> </div>*cough* Shen preview in May's update, a month and a half ago.<br /> <br /> Looking at Development, a couple of things were/have been in development for ages, but likely no-one would claim this was because the system was scrapped (Apocalypse's Changing Ways (almost two years), Awakening's Signs of Sorcery (over a year and counting)). Others, meanwhile, zip through comparatively quickly. It's a variable thing.<br /> <br /> And the books have only been in development for a month (June 19th Monday Meeting, where they moved from Second Draft into Development).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":".  Added thing on length of development. 07-11-2017, 02:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T23:57:57-07:00","id":1114463,"title":"","content":"Been waitin on that Netjer revision for about eight months now...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T00:36:37-07:00","id":1114468,"title":"","content":"I can tell you guys from Neall's comments on Facebook, that it sounds like Danielle Lauzon's breakthroughs with Storypath for Trinity impacted Scion development (for the better), so it is all continuously moving forward, but with playtest feedback and stuff there's also changes being incorporated that slow things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-11-2017, 03:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T05:03:57-07:00","id":1114531,"title":"","content":"Rich mentions a backer update should be out this week in <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/always-darkest-before-the-era-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\">the Monday Meeting comments</a>, so we'll see how that goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T15:36:21-07:00","id":1114784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tytalan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1114452#post1114452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question Neall do you have any idea when we will get something from the Kickstarter many of us backed?<br /> <br /> I don't mean to attack you or anything but 3 months with anyword is not right</div> </div> </div> </div>We've been doing monthly updates, but there should be another pantheon going live within the next day or so. I just turned in the manuscript for Origins, and Hero will be going in soon. I'll talk to Rich about putting out more substantial chunks of things, but we're moving along.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T15:37:24-07:00","id":1114786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1114463#post1114463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Been waitin on that Netjer revision for about eight months now...</div> </div> </div> </div>That'll be July-August.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T17:02:01-07:00","id":1114812,"title":"","content":"I was wondering which creatures from the bestiary can scale up to demigod level","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T10:58:16-07:00","id":1115140,"title":"","content":"May I ask why Geasa is being used as the Pantheon Specific Purview of the Tuatha de Danann? I have been doing academic research on the subject and Geasa seems to be a introduction of the Christian monks who transcribed the mythology. I can prove through comparative theology and literary studies that concept is derived from the Arthurian romantic sagas simply to provide a tragic element to the Story of Cu Chulainn. It was a story element which was favored at the time. In addition if you read all of Irish mythology nowhere else is the subject of geasa broached. I personally feel that an artistry type purview (representing the unique poetic sorcery of the Tuatha) would be a better approach. Do you have any comments to offer on such a suggestion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T12:23:58-07:00","id":1115185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manannansun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1115140#post1115140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">May I ask why Geasa is being used as the Pantheon Specific Purview of the Tuatha de Danann? I have been doing academic research on the subject and Geasa seems to be a introduction of the Christian monks who transcribed the mythology. I can prove through comparative theology and literary studies that concept is derived from the Arthurian romantic sagas simply to provide a tragic element to the Story of Cu Chulainn. It was a story element which was favored at the time. In addition if you read all of Irish mythology nowhere else is the subject of geasa broached. I personally feel that an artistry type purview (representing the unique poetic sorcery of the Tuatha) would be a better approach. Do you have any comments to offer on such a suggestion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Geasa are not only limited to the story of C\u00fa Chulainn, they appear as a narrative device in several pieces of early Irish literature. Potentially the best example of Geasa come from <i>The Destruction of D\u00e1 Derga's Hostel</i>, with the Geasa placed on King Conaire. Just off the top of my head, they are also present in the story of <i>The Sons of Tuireann</i>. The presence of Geasa-esque concepts in early Welsh, and thus Arthurian texts, has normally been suggested to be the result of an older shared cultural concept due between the Welsh and Irish rather than it being a direct influence by the early monastic scholars.<br /> <br /> What have you been reading that suggests the Geasa are an imported concept by the monks who wrote the texts down? The manuscripts we have of the <i>Tain</i> are from between the 11th through 12th centuries, with the first mentions of Arthur coming solidly in the 12th. (The Destruction is first in the 12th century) I would be very interested to see the proof for such as I work on the topic of the Christian influence, or occasional interesting lack there of, on Early Irish Sagas.<br /> <br /> For the idea of lyrical, rhyming magic, that is actually already incorporated into the Pantheon from what Neall has said here in the thread. Their Pantheon Motif is verse and satire according to Neall's post <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1050830#post1050830\">here</a>. I think that this is the only way to properly represent the variance you see in the Sagas in how the rhyming magic works. Rhyming magic is used to influence healing, with Miach's restoring of Nuada's hand for instance. It is also used to curse, influence battles, and various other magics (though sadly the more overt uses of magic, such as bringing the trees, and rocks of Ireland to battle as soldiers are not explicitly stated to be rhyming spells) which would cause a lot of tricky issues. If these magics were all simply functions of the PsP rather than Health, War, Fortune, etc, then the Tuatha would have rather short Power lists. When the concept is used as a Motif, however, all Purviews can be included in rhyming magic. From Miach's healing (Health), to Goibniu's creation of the boil/burning stick (Forge?) these things can all be represented by the use of the rhyming magic concept as a Motif.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":"07-12-2017, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T12:51:58-07:00","id":1115204,"title":"","content":"Thank-you Watcher. I don't know what I was thinking when I wrote that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T12:58:10-07:00","id":1115207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Origina