'm pretty sure I remember this from before... but like I said, I can't find the post, and we have had the least amount of info on the Kami out of all the Pantheons, so I could totally be misremembering something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T10:16:42-07:00","id":1128501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1128477#post1128477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Semi-Related - Can you officially say if the Incarnation genesis will be in Hero? I remember you were considering since the Gaul pantheon milestone was reached, but I don't recall if you officially said it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The last I remember was that Incarnates might be in the Companion with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T10:46:45-07:00","id":1128510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1128485#post1128485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does get mentioned there, yes, but the actual Netjer Virtues are Balance and Justice... also I'm pretty sure I remember this from before... but like I said, I can't find the post, and we have had the least amount of info on the Kami out of all the Pantheons, so I could totally be misremembering something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just did a little searching with google and I think you're right about the Kami's Virtues. Sincerity (<i>makoto</i>) and Right Action (<i>rei</i>) are listed as part of the Seven Principles of Bushido (Right Action here meaning respect/courtesy). Thanks for the help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12342-dr-quantum","name":"Dr. Quantum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T01:58:00-07:00","id":1128734,"title":"","content":"Am I right that the Teotl are the only corebook pantheon whose Virtues we don't know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T03:29:47-07:00","id":1128743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1128734#post1128734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I right that the Teotl are the only corebook pantheon whose Virtues we don't know?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Teotl Virtues are Hunger and Sacrifice, if I remember correctly, which means we know all ten sets of Virtues:<br /> <br /> Aesir : Audacity vs. Fatalism<br /> Deva : Conscience vs. Duty<br /> Kami : Right Action vs. Sincerity<br /> Manitou : Pride vs. Purpose<br /> Netjer : Balance vs. Justice<br /> Orisha : Tradition vs. Innovation<br /> Shen : Yang vs. Yin<br /> Teotl : Hunger vs. Sacrifice<br /> Theoi : Egotism vs. Kinship<br /> Tuatha : Honor vs. Prowess<br /> <br /> Unless something changed/I'm remembering something wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 08-14-2017, 06:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T17:54:28-07:00","id":1129050,"title":"","content":"If a changeling child were left in place of a human who qualified for scionhood through one of the origins, does that mean that they could potentially become a divinity eventually?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T17:52:21-07:00","id":1129508,"title":"","content":"Is Cybele/Magna Mater anywhere in the line, possibly as a relative newcomer to the Theoi?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T18:06:21-07:00","id":1129521,"title":"","content":"(taking Cybele commentary to other thread)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-15-2017, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T21:00:35-07:00","id":1129638,"title":"","content":"How much leeway would a Scion of the Tuatha have when it comes to thinking up or employing geas, either on themselves or on others? If that's even still how it works?<br /> <br /> For example, could a Scion deliberately get geas placed on himself or place one on himself with loopholes or caveeats in it, both to protect himself from a more severe one and to prevent him from being trapped in the situation that led to Cu Chulainn's downfall?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T02:59:33-07:00","id":1129723,"title":"","content":"Given that the idea of a geas seems to be to make someone's life more challenging, to show that the geased individual can overcome even with these extra burdens placed on them, I'd imagine that loopholes where you can slip or shirk the geas/geasa on themselves would be counter to the point of it all. Unfortunately sometimes you end up being trapped, when you have too many of them on you. Especially when they contradict. That's part of the challenge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T11:47:02-07:00","id":1131810,"title":"","content":"Are we going to see a preview including knacks from all Callings? In addition how many levels does a Calling tree have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T13:09:31-07:00","id":1131854,"title":"","content":"Are the deified Roman Emperors distinct deities, or is it a Mantle (perhaps originating with Divis Julius, Scion of Venus, or perhaps going all the way back to Romulus/Quirinus, Scion of Mars) that they inherited?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T18:34:59-07:00","id":1131982,"title":"","content":"Re sails on his barque through the sky during the day and through the Duat every night, but at every point in time half of the World is at night and the other half is at daytime. How do you determine whether it is currently day or night in the Duat? Does it follow Egypt's time zone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12342-dr-quantum","name":"Dr. Quantum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T20:58:23-07:00","id":1132043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dr. Quantum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1131982#post1131982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re sails on his barque through the sky during the day and through the Duat every night, but at every point in time half of the World is at night and the other half is at daytime. How do you determine whether it is currently day or night in the Duat? Does it follow Egypt's time zone?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine it is more complicated than that, at least one Otherworld is involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T09:05:55-07:00","id":1132646,"title":"","content":"How are you handling the concept of the Wild Hunt Neal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T14:41:09-07:00","id":1132809,"title":"","content":"I have an Exalted Character Creation tool that I made that works out of google sheets. I would like to modify it for Scion, but of course, I can't start to do that until the rules for character creation and a proper attribute and ability spread drop. I know we got a little bit of a preview as to character creation earlier, but will be get a preview of the ability/attribute spread being used in the game and more complete character generation rules before the books are published?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T08:12:00-07:00","id":1133378,"title":"","content":"When it comes to monsters, are only the ones associated with high myth confirmed to exist in-universe, or is it same to assume that all mythological and folkloric creatures exist, down to and including things like the Mothman and Jersey Devil which have no real connection to any religion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T09:29:05-07:00","id":1133418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1133378#post1133378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it comes to monsters, are only the ones associated with high myth confirmed to exist in-universe, or is it same to assume that all mythological and folkloric creatures exist, down to and including things like the Mothman and Jersey Devil which have no real connection to any religion?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'm pretty sure we have at least some folkloric stuff. When I asked about mythological beings integrating with modern society, Neall mentioned that the Jersey Devil could be running a pawn shop south of the river. If so, he said, he's probably an asshole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T13:09:46-07:00","id":1133520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreepyShutIn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1133418#post1133418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI'm pretty sure we have at least some folkloric stuff. When I asked about mythological beings integrating with modern society, Neall mentioned that the Jersey Devil could be running a pawn shop south of the river. If so, he said, he's probably an asshole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of the stuff about Lore in the World mentions sewer alligators and the man with a hook for a hand don't they?<br /> <br /> <br /> Jersey Devil Fun fact, one of my ancestors was supposedly the brother of the &quot;Mrs. Leeds&quot; that birthed the Jersey Devil.<br /> <br /> I have a long and &quot;proud&quot; family history <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T17:12:45-07:00","id":1133593,"title":"","content":"When the Maya pantheon comes around (it's planned for Demigod, right, along with Slavic, Mesopotamian, Polynesian, Navajo, and probably Canaanite?) would Camazotz be one of the gods selected as a potential divine parent, or would he be a Titan? He's one of my favorite mythical figures, and I'm rather curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T19:57:15-07:00","id":1134027,"title":"","content":"In an earlier answer, you hinted that existing Birthrights could be upgraded. Is this something that can be accomplished through story events/with XP, or will Demigod and God have upgrade templates similar to the ones in 1e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T20:29:34-07:00","id":1134342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1133593#post1133593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the Maya pantheon comes around (it's planned for Demigod, right, along with Slavic, Mesopotamian, Polynesian, Navajo, and probably Canaanite?) would Camazotz be one of the gods selected as a potential divine parent, or would he be a Titan? He's one of my favorite mythical figures, and I'm rather curious.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Aren't Camazotz a type of being? Hunahpu and Xbalanque encounter multiple in the underworld, don't they?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T23:46:54-07:00","id":1134371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1134342#post1134342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Aren't Camazotz a type of being? Hunahpu and Xbalanque encounter multiple in the underworld, don't they?</div> </div> </div> </div>Camazotz is the ruler of a race of bat-like creatures. As I understand it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T16:34:53-07:00","id":1135292,"title":"","content":"I just thought of something. Pre-Visitation Scions get one Calling, right? Does that mean Callings and Knacks are in Scion: Origin, not Scion: Hero?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T10:55:18-07:00","id":1135839,"title":"","content":"Okay, a simpler silly question.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar137_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"137\" data-vbnamecard=\"137\">Neall</a> in your opinion... <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H5ZNOUIhGPA\" target=\"_blank\">Would this video</a> be Hero-tier Epic Strength, Demigod-tier, or God-tier?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T18:32:00-07:00","id":1137541,"title":"","content":"So something occurred to me in the shower today.<br /> <br /> \u200bI can understand why gods might want to rein it in when dealing with mortal society and try not to dole out too many commandments, but I have to wonder what they do about less social and more physical phenomena. As one example: Global warming. Yes, mortals are causing it, but a gaping hole in the ozone layer isn't itself a social matter. At some point you'd think Zeus would look at it and say &quot;Hey, my sky is falling apart! Dammit, now I have to patch that up. Wife! Bring me my ozone repair kit!&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bTo which Hera would of course respond &quot;You don't have one. There is no such thing as an ozone repair kit.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd then the Lord of the Heavens would of course take the sensible measure by yelling &quot;HEPHAESTUS!&quot; <br /> <br /> \u200bWho would hear it all the way from his volcano because the thunderbolt guy is not quiet and grumble to himself about lazy celestial jerks. <br /> <br /> \u200bYes, all of that, in exactly those words. So is that something that happens, or is there some reason it wouldn't?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T19:17:51-07:00","id":1137548,"title":"","content":"WHY DO YOU THINK I DIDN'T WANT HUMANS TO HAVE FIRE?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T20:56:37-07:00","id":1137580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreepyShutIn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1137541#post1137541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So something occurred to me in the shower today.<br /> <br /> \u200bI can understand why gods might want to rein it in when dealing with mortal society and try not to dole out too many commandments, but I have to wonder what they do about less social and more physical phenomena. As one example: Global warming. Yes, mortals are causing it, but a gaping hole in the ozone layer isn't itself a social matter. At some point you'd think Zeus would look at it and say &quot;Hey, my sky is falling apart! Dammit, now I have to patch that up. Wife! Bring me my ozone repair kit!&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bTo which Hera would of course respond &quot;You don't have one. There is no such thing as an ozone repair kit.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd then the Lord of the Heavens would of course take the sensible measure by yelling &quot;HEPHAESTUS!&quot; <br /> <br /> \u200bWho would hear it all the way from his volcano because the thunderbolt guy is not quiet and grumble to himself about lazy celestial jerks. <br /> <br /> \u200bYes, all of that, in exactly those words. So is that something that happens, or is there some reason it wouldn't?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it would set a bad precedent? Like humans can just mess up the world however they want, as long as it inconveniences a god they will fix it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T21:06:01-07:00","id":1137587,"title":"","content":"also isnt the sky ouranos's job???","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T23:19:19-07:00","id":1137614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1137587#post1137587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">also isnt the sky ouranos's job???</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ouranos doesn't have a job. He was literally the heavens. He has no agency after his castration by Kronus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T03:34:42-07:00","id":1137635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreepyShutIn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1137541#post1137541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So something occurred to me in the shower today.<br /> <br /> \u200bI can understand why gods might want to rein it in when dealing with mortal society and try not to dole out too many commandments, but I have to wonder what they do about less social and more physical phenomena. As one example: Global warming. Yes, mortals are causing it, but a gaping hole in the ozone layer isn't itself a social matter. At some point you'd think Zeus would look at it and say &quot;Hey, my sky is falling apart! Dammit, now I have to patch that up. Wife! Bring me my ozone repair kit!&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bTo which Hera would of course respond &quot;You don't have one. There is no such thing as an ozone repair kit.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd then the Lord of the Heavens would of course take the sensible measure by yelling &quot;HEPHAESTUS!&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bWho would hear it all the way from his volcano because the thunderbolt guy is not quiet and grumble to himself about lazy celestial jerks.<br /> <br /> \u200bYes, all of that, in exactly those words. So is that something that happens, or is there some reason it wouldn't?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can think of three potential reasons. The first is that since the gods mirror themselves off of humans, one or more of the sky gods created an overworld equivalent of the hole in the ozone by mistake, and they have to deal with that before they can deal with the mortal one. Another possibility is that, as I recall, the most damage to the Ozone is over Australia, perhaps the Australian Aborigines deities are dead or otherwise inactive, but the part of the world the once had sway in is still hostile to other pantheons. The third would be one of the less pleasant Titans likes it that way and they can\u2019t fix it without provoking war, and since it\u2019s not a direct threat to existence yet the gods are in \u201cwait and see\u201d mode.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T23:33:53-07:00","id":1137931,"title":"","content":"Based on the previews, it seems the &quot;elemental&quot; Purviews will also govern metaphorical expressions, with Fire = Inspiration and Water = Despair (I'm guessing, since there's a Boon called Sink Hopes). What are the metaphorical expressions of Earth and Sky, then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12342-dr-quantum","name":"Dr. Quantum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T00:53:17-07:00","id":1137940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dr. Quantum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1137931#post1137931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on the previews, it seems the &amp;quot;elemental&amp;quot; Purviews will also govern metaphorical expressions, with Fire = Inspiration and Water = Despair (I'm guessing, since there's a Boon called Sink Hopes). What are the metaphorical expressions of Earth and Sky, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt it's that one dimensional... Various elements have diverse metaphorical associations across the world... Sure, inspiration is most strongly associated with fire nowadays, but in Hinduism inspiration is also strongly associated with Water, since the Divine Muse Sarasvati is also a river goddess. Also, these aren't the only possible Boons in existence, just the ones that I assume the developers felt would most widely cover their bases, given they can't possibly write up every possible one... I'm assuming that with Marvels you could make any number of metaphorical associations work with any number of elements provided you can convince your ST. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T12:46:25-07:00","id":1138966,"title":"","content":"So any hints at what we can expect from the September preview?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T23:57:53-07:00","id":1140104,"title":"","content":"In the first century ce, did the sailor Thamus actually hear &quot;Tammuz Panmegus Tethneke&quot; (All-Great Tammuz is Dead) [an expected religious statement given that Tammuz is a dying/resurrecting god] OR was he correct and he heard &quot;Thamous, Pan ho megas tethneke&quot; (Thamus, Great Pan is Dead!) [a tragic word shifting event that he was being personally informed of]?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/