":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T10:13:30-07:00","id":1142580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1142510#post1142510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The most all appropriate seems to just be Beasts (Snake)... I can see the argument that at the very least marvels for that Purview should be able to influence Toxicity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming it has a power similar to 1e's animal aspect I can't imagine why animal could involve toxicity. He might also have some small influence with water and Earth, being the world serpent and all. I know he doesn't do much with it in myth other than get caught by thor on a fishing trip though so I don't know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T10:26:56-07:00","id":1142585,"title":"","content":"Health would seem to be the relevant Purview here, covering both healing and sickness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T11:16:51-07:00","id":1142609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1142580#post1142580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Assuming it has a power similar to 1e's animal aspect I can't imagine why animal could involve toxicity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Animal might not, but Beasts (Snake), at least through Marvels should be able to at the very least let him breathe out poison like he does in the Thor myths, since Snakes are inextricably tied to Poison and Venom across many cultures... also, you know, he IS a giant Snake so that Purview seems fitting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T11:21:07-07:00","id":1142613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1142585#post1142585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Health would seem to be the relevant Purview here, covering both healing and sickness.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question is, does Sickness = Poison? Then again even Fertility has a boon called Mother of Pestilence which lets you both sense poison (including Cobra venom) and also poison people, so poison options abound <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Both Health and Fertility seem just a little bit on the stretching it side for the World Serpent though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T11:26:29-07:00","id":1142618,"title":"","content":"I mean the Health/Snake-Venom correlation exists to a significant degree in some mythologies (Asclepius anyone?), especially when you throw in skin-shedding as rejuvination. But I'm not aware of those elements in Norse culture specifically.<br /> <br /> Ugh... I don't think his primary Purview should be Epic Strength... though he is strong enough to be a match eventually pulling away from Thor.... there are Titans where that fits to a cool degree (Atlas for example), but it seems disappointing for Jormugandr.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T12:29:43-07:00","id":1142651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1142618#post1142618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean the Health/Snake-Venom correlation exists to a significant degree in some mythologies (Asclepius anyone?), especially when you throw in skin-shedding as rejuvination. But I'm not aware of those elements in Norse culture specifically.<br /> <br /> Ugh... I don't think his primary Purview should be Epic Strength... though he is strong enough to be a match eventually pulling away from Thor.... there are Titans where that fits to a cool degree (Atlas for example), but it seems disappointing for Jormugandr.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think the new Wild Purview might be relevant? It's supposed to be like Fertility but governing non-domesticated plant and animal life. If Fertility can cover poison so should Wild and maybe make it a little more lethal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T14:48:06-07:00","id":1142704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1142329#post1142329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Ao Guang and Ryujin the same guy?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have conflated them in the past in other media. I'm cool with that interpretation. He has more chill in Japanese myth, probably because Prince N\u00e9zh\u0101 and the Monkey King aren't always around to piss him off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T14:52:43-07:00","id":1142706,"title":"","content":"Is art the big hold up at the moment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T08:45:53-07:00","id":1142922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1025236#post1025236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Legend is only imbued for as long as it's imbued, circular as that might be. Think of it this way: you have a certain amount of metaphysical juice in the tank from your divine narrative. You can pour this juice to fuel certain abilities, and then pour it back in your tank when you don't want to fuel them anymore. Some abilities are so potent they burn out your juice right off, though. So, yes, you can imbue some Boons or Marvels in one scene and then be back next scene. Be careful, though - regaining Legend is tough, and requires you to submit to the whims of Fate.<br /> <br /> Or it requires sacrifice. Whichever <i>you'd </i>prefer.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does Fate do with Scions when they regain Legend?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T17:40:26-07:00","id":1143096,"title":"","content":"Can you have an Incarnate Scion of a God who hasn't died? I'm just wondering how Deva avatars work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T18:32:24-07:00","id":1143103,"title":"","content":"Has anything been said about the Amatsukami? I was watching a tv show called Noragami and it got me thinking about them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T19:47:37-07:00","id":1143121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1143103#post1143103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anything been said about the Amatsukami? I was watching a tv show called Noragami and it got me thinking about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's the entire &quot;Kami&quot; as the Pantheon this time (including both Amatsukami and Kunitsukami)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T16:26:34-07:00","id":1143351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=646563#post646563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gods still go along a Legend 8-12 scale, but not every Scion's parent is a 12. There's a way for gods to act with a degree of omnipotence they don't usually possess, hearkening back to a Mythic Era. .</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you tell me more about that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T22:44:35-07:00","id":1143408,"title":"","content":"Will the upcoming Kickstarters for Demigod and God be separate ones, or combined?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T00:26:27-07:00","id":1143417,"title":"","content":"I've been recently doing some reading about the Indo-Greeks and how Herakles became the basis for Vajrapani/Shukongoshin through a tale of him facing off against the Buddha and coming a Buddhist. There's also Mithra being the basis for the Maitreya.<br /> <br /> On that note, can gods adopt religions/philosophies associated with the mortal realm and not necessarily their own &quot;home&quot; pantheons? Some Chinese/Hindu/Japanese deities/beings are a variety of religions, after all. Is this a thing in the Scion world? The conversion of gods?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Religions Academic. Zoroastrian Convert.</i><br /> <b>Official Work:</b> Scion: Companion, Scion: Demigod.<br /> <b>Nexus Work:</b> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/293097/The-Cortes-Divinas-of-Maria-Lionza?cPath=8329_32938\" target=\"_blank\">Cortes Divinas of Maria Lionza</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17311-xhepablo","name":"xhepablo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17311_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T19:50:26-07:00","id":1143644,"title":"","content":"Also, who's working on Yazata? As a Zoroastrian and someone doing my grad work in it, I'm super curious whether they'll go the Zurvanite route with Zurvan as a titan (which is outdated, no one believes that anymore) or more something like Ahura Mazda as a primordial, Angra Mainyu as a titan and his legion of Daeva as the spawn? Also willing to advise on anything if you need anyone for that section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Religions Academic. Zoroastrian Convert.</i><br /> <b>Official Work:</b> Scion: Companion, Scion: Demigod.<br /> <b>Nexus Work:</b> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/293097/The-Cortes-Divinas-of-Maria-Lionza?cPath=8329_32938\" target=\"_blank\">Cortes Divinas of Maria Lionza</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17311-xhepablo","name":"xhepablo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17311_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T20:22:17-07:00","id":1143650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xhepablo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1143644#post1143644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm super curious whether they'll go the Zurvanite route with Zurvan as a titan (which is outdated, no one believes that anymore)</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;No one believes that anymore&quot; as in no one holds those religious beliefs, or &quot;no one believes that anymore&quot; as in academics don't think it was ever a thing in the first place (like Slavic dualism)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T20:32:42-07:00","id":1143653,"title":"","content":"Both, really, in a way.<br /> <br /> Zurvanism was a Mazdayasnian heresy that enjoyed some prominence during the Sassanid Empire, but otherwise disappeared after the 10th century. Zoroastrian Mazdayasna was always the dominant strain and remains as such today. It's like representing Pelagianism as the dominant strain of Christian theology despite it definitely not being the case ever. Zurvan is always represented as subordinate to Ahura Mazda, not as the primordial force, in the Avesta. Basically, whomever wrote the previous Yazata book seemed to not have knowledge of Zoroastrianism except through those Greek sources that thought that they were all Zurvanites back then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Religions Academic. Zoroastrian Convert.</i><br /> <b>Official Work:</b> Scion: Companion, Scion: Demigod.<br /> <b>Nexus Work:</b> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/293097/The-Cortes-Divinas-of-Maria-Lionza?cPath=8329_32938\" target=\"_blank\">Cortes Divinas of Maria Lionza</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17311-xhepablo","name":"xhepablo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17311_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T21:06:29-07:00","id":1143658,"title":"","content":"Iirc, the author of the Yazata in the previous edition was of Persian/Iranian background, but may have chosen that particular heresy to work off of because it worked best with 1E's broader metaphysics (which lacked the Primordial vs Titan distinction which allows more flexibility now).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T21:20:51-07:00","id":1143662,"title":"","content":"I keep hearing rumors that the Scion 2nd Edition will be finished and released in October [no specific day given]. As I have not actually gotten anything like this confirmed to be fact in my Kickstarter Update I was wondering if this is just a rumor or is it true. Also if this is true as most of the people I'm hearing it from are backers as well that leads to my question of, is this the backer release date or the public release date?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T21:25:52-07:00","id":1143664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1143658#post1143658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iirc, the author of the Yazata in the previous edition was of Persian/Iranian background, but may have chosen that particular heresy to work off of because it worked best with 1E's broader metaphysics (which lacked the Primordial vs Titan distinction which allows more flexibility now).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm really liking the reworking of the metaphysics, considering that the best way to describe Zoroastrianism is that it is cosmologically monist/monotheistic, metaphysically polytheistic, and ethically dualistic. The primordial element helps with this complexity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Religions Academic. Zoroastrian Convert.</i><br /> <b>Official Work:</b> Scion: Companion, Scion: Demigod.<br /> <b>Nexus Work:</b> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/293097/The-Cortes-Divinas-of-Maria-Lionza?cPath=8329_32938\" target=\"_blank\">Cortes Divinas of Maria Lionza</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17311-xhepablo","name":"xhepablo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17311_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T22:27:53-07:00","id":1143676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1142704#post1142704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have conflated them in the past in other media. I'm cool with that interpretation. He has more chill in Japanese myth, probably because Prince N\u00e9zh\u0101 and the Monkey King aren't always around to piss him off.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well his daughter is a goddess in the titan's court, and is bound by marriage and blood to the kami and the imperial family of Japan!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T23:45:12-07:00","id":1143689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1143662#post1143662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep hearing rumors that the Scion 2nd Edition will be finished and released in October [no specific day given]. As I have not actually gotten anything like this confirmed to be fact in my Kickstarter Update I was wondering if this is just a rumor or is it true. Also if this is true as most of the people I'm hearing it from are backers as well that leads to my question of, is this the backer release date or the public release date?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems unlikely, as the books aren't in editing or layout yet.<br /> <br /> When they do come out, it'll be backers first, then public release some time later.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T23:54:25-07:00","id":1143691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xhepablo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1143417#post1143417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been recently doing some reading about the Indo-Greeks and how Herakles became the basis for Vajrapani/Shukongoshin through a tale of him facing off against the Buddha and coming a Buddhist. There's also Mithra being the basis for the Maitreya.<br /> <br /> On that note, can gods adopt religions/philosophies associated with the mortal realm and not necessarily their own &quot;home&quot; pantheons? Some Chinese/Hindu/Japanese deities/beings are a variety of religions, after all. Is this a thing in the Scion world? The conversion of gods?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well Buddhism specifically works as a philosophy to appeal to gods as much as mortals, and (at least on its side) doesn't forbid any form of cultural theistic tradition. We have thanks to Journey West the explicit story of Sun Wukong adopting Buddhism. I don't see any reason Heracles couldn't have become a Buddhist during the Greco-Bactrian era, or at least he maintains a Mantle that did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T03:47:27-07:00","id":1143721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1143662#post1143662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep hearing rumors that the Scion 2nd Edition will be finished and released in October [no specific day given]. As I have not actually gotten anything like this confirmed to be fact in my Kickstarter Update I was wondering if this is just a rumor or is it true. Also if this is true as most of the people I'm hearing it from are backers as well that leads to my question of, is this the backer release date or the public release date?</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't heard anything like this but Neal did tease the possibility of useing the base system as a preview, which would be something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T12:58:08-07:00","id":1144176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=930352#post930352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The exact number has been in flux. At the moment we have 23 (a good Erisian number), not counting the pantheon purviews.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forgive me if it's a silly question. But can you tell me the differences between the kami and manitou previews? They both seen to be about taking to spirits","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T22:49:40-07:00","id":1144642,"title":"","content":"Is the conflict between the Devas and the Yazata stated in the Devas preview only between the Vedic Devas and Yazata? I mean, there are instances of Parsis in India worshiping Ganesh as a Yazata, and here's one recent example that is heavily attended and organized by Parsi Zoroastrians: <a href=\"https://www.indiablooms.com/ibns_new/video-details/N/109172/mumbai-parsi-family-visits-gujarat-to-revere-lord-ganesha.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.indiablooms.com/ibns_new...d-ganesha.html</a><br /> <br /> The critique is mostly of the Vedic devas and how they used to be violent, sacrificing, caste-imposing deities, not really many of the modern Hindu ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Religions Academic. Zoroastrian Convert.</i><br /> <b>Official Work:</b> Scion: Companion, Scion: Demigod.<br /> <b>Nexus Work:</b> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/293097/The-Cortes-Divinas-of-Maria-Lionza?cPath=8329_32938\" target=\"_blank\">Cortes Divinas of Maria Lionza</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17311-xhepablo","name":"xhepablo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17311_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T23:18:00-07:00","id":1144651,"title":"","content":"I doubt it breaks completely perfectly along lines between the Rigvedic and the later Trimurti-era deities, but I do expect Ganesha to be a peacemaker who eagerly reaches out to and does good work with non-hostile Yazata. We've already had the example of Ganesha working against Indra's hardline &quot;destroy all Titans&quot; policy; and the Titanomachy is directly intertwined with the emnity between the Yazata (who conflate Deva and Daeva) and the Deva (who conflate Ahura and Asura).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T13:47:52-07:00","id":1144923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xhepablo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1144642#post1144642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the conflict between the Devas and the Yazata stated in the Devas preview only between the Vedic Devas and Yazata? I mean, there are instances of Parsis in India worshiping Ganesh as a Yazata, and here's one recent example that is heavily attended and organized by Parsi Zoroastrians: <a href=\"https://www.indiablooms.com/ibns_new/video-details/N/109172/mumbai-parsi-family-visits-gujarat-to-revere-lord-ganesha.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.indiablooms.com/ibns_new...d-ganesha.html</a><br /> <br /> The critique is mostly of the Vedic devas and how they used to be violent, sacrificing, caste-imposing deities, not really many of the modern Hindu ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ganesha has already been stated in the Preview as being very open to working with people his Pantheon might in general be wary of... in addition, the largest communities of Parsis in India live in Mumbai, which is Ganesha's city... they likely have his explicit protection, and I do not doubt that the community's interactions with him, both IRL and in the World, were significant factors in his viewpoints towards working with Asura. The Preview also mentions that no matter what the Deva think of the Yazata, they strongly disapprove of taking any of that out on the Parsi community.<br /> <br /> All that being said, the modern day Deva are just as involved, by and large, with fighting Asura as the Vedic era Gods, and the conflation of Asura and Ahura (and the same for Deva and Daeva on the other side) ensures that even the modern day Deva are likely to be wary of an entire Pantheon self-identifying as Titans (and vice versa).<br /> <br /> Of the Deva, Indra is definitely the most likely to blow up against the Yazata and take action against them... he's entire fame as a Vedic deity is in his exploits against various Asura like Vritra and the Panis...and even his more modern myths have him constantly coming into conflict with them (sometimes even completely innocent ones whom he works against for no other reason than that they are Asura).<br /> <br /> Durga is an interesting case due to her function... as THE Guardian Goddess, Durga's myths only ever feature evil Asura because her myths need to feature her saving the World, unlike Indra's myths which focus primarily on his glory in combat (Vedic era) or his insecurities about his throne (Puranic era)... therefore, while Durga acts against Asura all the time, she never acts against innocent Asura like Indra does... and it is noteworthy that her myths always mention her starting the battle with a warning to leave and let these people be, and she will let the Asura go unharmed... they always reply with 'Hey, pretty lady, have sex with me!'... only following which does she ever enter battle. So basically, Durga is unlikely to ever start trouble... she's just very, very likely to finish it.<br /> <br /> Among the other Gods, Brahma doesn't care much, and has blessed countless Asura in myth before... Shiva is also known to be fairly impartial, and Vishnu has explicitly had notable Asura devotees like Prahlad and Bali whom he has blessed. Lakshmi and Parvati don't interact with Asura much outside of a few obscure myths a piece where some Asura or the other tries to kidnap/seduce them, and likely don't have strong opinions on the matter, while Sarasvati on the other hand, is a Vedic era Goddess who is described in the Veda as riding into battle against Asura... so she may have more negative reactions.. on the other hand I can't imagine her not getting along with Anahita.<br /> <br /> Agni is pretty much a Vedic era Ganesha in his job as bridge between worlds, and likely would be open to Yazata relations... Surya probably toes the party line in a general 'why not' way without being too invested personally, and Varuna is probably still pissed that his boyfriend Mitra left him for the Yazata (I'm not getting into the whole 'is Varuna Ahura Mazda' can of worms). Yama is too busy for this shit... also he MAY be Yima over in that Pantheon.<br /> <br /> Kali will probably just do whatever the fuck she wants to, unless the Yazata attack one of her sister selves.<br /> <br /> (Btw, I know I'm using Asura and Yazata interchangeably in that piece... I am fully aware that they are not actually the same groups in the modern day, whatever they might have been in the depths of time... but the Deva still see them that way, much as the Yazata see the Deva as the same as the Daeva, so I was writing it from their perspective).<br /> <br /> Out of curiosity, we see a fair few stories of Asura who are good and often devoted to the Deva in myth... are there any similar stories of Daeva in Persian myth who are good and/or convert to the worship of Ahura Mazda and the Yazata?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T16:50:02-07:00","id":1145011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1144176#post1144176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Forgive me if it's a silly question. But can you tell me the differences between the kami and manitou previews? They both seen to be about taking to spirits</div> </div> </div> </div>Gonna quote myself here,cause i really wanna know","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T18:33:23-07:00","id":1145044,"title":"","content":"I just want to say Samudra that as a historian (well almost historian) its been a real pleasure reading your posts here and those in the reaction to the devas preview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T19:32:08-07:00","id":1145062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1145044#post1145044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want to say Samudra that as a historian (well almost historian) its been a real pleasure reading your posts here and those in the reaction to the devas preview.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Samudra, that was an excellent response that adds the nuance and development I was looking for. Seems we both know our stuff for our respective groups fairly well!<br /> <br /> Yeah, Indra's the big one. The Pahlavi texts (and I believe the Vendidad) lists him as one of the chief Daevas (along with Rudra and Nasatya), so he's bound to be pissed still. Good point on Durga too and reflects the love that her and Kali get like Ganesh from the Parsi community, who sometimes tend to view them as destroyers of evil and as such on their side since Ahura Mazda is all-good. On Sarasvati, a goddess of wisdom and art is bound to fit in well with a pantheon that worships wisdom made manifest. so perhaps Ganesh introduced her and Anahita at a party?<br /> <br /> On the Daeva doing good, one of the theological strains has the belief that their choice to follow Angra Mainyu/Ahriman was exactly that: A Choice. Being that the religion is built on the belief of personal responsibility and freedom of choice, even for the gods, there is the hope that the Daevas will basically quit their nonsense and come home and do good again. Only Ahriman is viewed as irredeemable, but there are folks who pray for even his redemption. He didn't create the Daevas or give birth to them, however, so it's viewed that they can hopefully make the right choice and join the Yazata.Astiwihad, for example, is Death, but is viewed as being so destructive that he's even a danger for the Daevas and sometimes even thanked and respected for bring death even to the Daeva, who are not viewed as truly immortal like the Yazata or even humans (which are a lesser divinity in the order of things). People can also be Daevas/ally with them and we know how unpredictable people can be too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Religions Academic. Zoroastrian Convert.</i><br /> <b>Official Work:</b> Scion: Companion, Scion: Demigod.<br /> <b>Nexus Work:</b> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/293097/The-Cortes-Divinas-of-Maria-Lionza?cPath=8329_32938\" target=\"_blank\">Cortes Divinas of Maria Lionza</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17311-xhepablo","name":"xhepablo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17311_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T05:06:25-07:00","id":1145171,"title":"","content":"The best thing about Samudra is everything about Samudra","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T10:27:10-07:00","id":1145287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1145044#post1145044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want to say Samudra that as a historian (well almost historian) its been a real pleasure reading your posts here and those in the reaction to the devas preview.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I do my best... I hope your path to full historianship (historianhood?) goes smoothly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xhepablo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1145062#post1145062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This. Samudra, that was an excellent response that adds the nuance and development I was looking for. Seems we both know our stuff for our respective groups fairly well!<br /> <br /> Yeah, Indra's the big one. The Pahlavi texts (and I believe the Vendidad) lists him as one of the chief Daevas (along with Rudra and Nasatya), so he's bound to be pissed still. Good point on Durga too and reflects the love that her and Kali get like Ganesh from the Parsi community, who sometimes tend to view them as destroyers of evil and as such on their side since Ahura Mazda is all-good. On Sarasvati, a goddess of wisdom and art is bound to fit in well with a pantheon that worships wisdom made manifest. so perhaps Ganesh introduced her and Anahita at a party?<br /> <br /> On the Daeva doing good, one of the theological strains has the belief that their choice to follow Angra Mainyu/Ahriman was exactly that: A Choice. Being that the religion is built on the belief of personal responsibility and freedom of choice, even for the gods, there is the hope that the Daevas will basically quit their nonsense and come home and do good again. Only Ahriman is viewed as irredeemable, but there are folks who pray for even his redemption. He didn't create the Daevas or give birth to them, however, so it's viewed that they can hopefully make the right choice and join the Yazata.Astiwihad, for example, is Death, but is viewed as being so destructive that he's even a danger for the Daevas and sometimes even thanked and respected for bring death even to the Daeva, who are not viewed as truly immortal like the Yazata or even humans (which are a lesser divinity in the order of things). People can also be Daevas/ally with them and we know how unpredictable people can be too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figure that if nothing else Sarasvati can get behind Freddie Mercury <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's also interesting to know the Parsi communities views on Durga and Kali.<br /> <br /> And thank you... it's great to have a Yazata expert on the forums as well... I'm really looking forward to seeing what 2e does with them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1145171#post1145171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best thing about Samudra is everything about Samudra</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you so much <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's actually Durga Puja here in Kolkata right now... that big festival in Durga's honour that is spoken of in both the Durga and Kartikkeya write-ups, and the biggest event in town... the Deva Preview actually went up almost exactly the day before the festival began, and it was kind of amazing for me to see how much interest there is in the Deva, and how many people were disappointed at the lack of Kali, as well of course the bang up job Mendez did on the write-up to begin with.. it's all been kind of an unexpected (but no less graciously received) Durga Puja gift for me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So once again, thank you, and happy Durga Puja everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T23:26:06-07:00","id":1145722,"title":"","content":"What place is there for the gods of all of these new religious movements in the world, like the UFO cults, Ascended Master teachings, cyber-deities (XaTuring, anyone?), Maria Lionza type regional deities, and more?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Religions Academic. Zoroastrian Convert.</i><br /> <b>Official Work:</b> Scion: Companion, Scion: Demigod.<br /> <b>Nexus Work:</b> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/293097/The-Cortes-Divinas-of-Maria-Lionza?cPath=8329_32938\" target=\"_blank\">Cortes Divinas of Maria Lionza</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17311-xhepablo","name":"xhepablo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17311_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T23:35:25-07:00","id":1145723,"title":"","content":"I would hope the same place as the Atlantean Gods - filed under &quot;how to make your own pantheon.&quot; There are enough legitimate historical pantheons to cover without including modern new age fringe groups. If you want them in your game, go for it, and there's room for pretty much anything under open license. But I don't think too many would want the central rules to spend time on the kinds of groups you mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T23:53:28-07:00","id":1145725,"title":"","content":"I mean, what makes one historical? Maria Lionza and her pantheon have been around since the colonization of the Americas about. People have been communing and worshiping ascended masters for centuries now. Hell, all of these are actually real too compared to the Atlantean pantheon. I mean, there's no need to make a whole set of rules for them, but I just wonder how some of them operate in the scheme of things, y'know? Fluff setting text is always welcome for these sorts of things.<br /> <br /> Oh, and for those curious about the Maria Lionza religion: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mar%C3%ADa_Lionza\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mar%C3%ADa_Lionza</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Religions Academic. Zoroastrian Convert.</i><br /> <b>Official Work:</b> Scion: Companion, Scion: Demigod.<br /> <b>Nexus Work:</b> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/293097/The-Cortes-Divinas-of-Maria-Lionza?cPath=8329_32938\" target=\"_blank\">Cortes Divinas of Maria Lionza</a>","edited":{"userid":17311,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17311-xhepablo","user":"xhepablo","date":". 10-01-2017, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17311-xhepablo","name":"xhepablo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17311_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T00:22:28-07:00","id":1145727,"title":"","content":"I''ve seriously considered using Xenu as a Scion antagonist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T03:52:07-07:00","id":1145749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1145727#post1145727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I''ve seriously considered using Xenu as a Scion antagonist.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Hubbard, your massive scam has doomed us all!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T10:13:03-07:00","id":1145833,"title":"","content":"A trio of people who could have been Scions, or who might just have been ordinary folks who were martyred and defied by their followers. Either way, the rules would cover what is needed for mechanics of making your own faith and pantheon, from what we've been told. There are many small regional faiths in the world (plus many more in history), too many to cover in the basic rulebook in detail. But that's what the fan-generated supplements will be used for, I'm sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T10:50:12-07:00","id":1145838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xhepablo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1145722#post1145722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What place is there for the gods of all of these new religious movements in the world, like the UFO cults, Ascended Master teachings, cyber-deities (XaTuring, anyone?), Maria Lionza type regional deities, and more?</div> </div> </div> </div>From what we've seen of the way Scion's Gods operate, there really doesn't seem to be any reason to find a 'special' place for them... they have the exact same place as all Gods... if the ST wants them to exist, they exist, if not they don't. The system by which Gods are represented seems more than adequate to model them, and any special quirks or deviations can be modeled into PSP powers.<br /> <br /> It seems like a potential place for a future supplement, if the line authors ever want to tackle it, though admittedly not one I'd be personally very interested in. As for how they relate to other Pantheons... well that's another area best handled in the supplement where they come out... after all, the Deva Preview didn't include their thoughts on the Mayan or Slavic or Korean Pantheons, since those haven't been written up yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T11:18:44-07:00","id":1145850,"title":"","content":"I'm still not clear on what the &quot;Liminal&quot; Calling refers to. There are a lot of liminal figures who don't have it. Is it exclusively for psychopomps and underworld gods? So Janus, for example, despite being literally the god of the threshold, wouldn't have it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T11:43:15-07:00","id":1145855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1145850#post1145850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still not clear on what the &quot;Liminal&quot; Calling refers to. There are a lot of liminal figures who don't have it. Is it exclusively for psychopomps and underworld gods? So Janus, for example, despite being literally the god of the threshold, wouldn't have it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks a bit more complicated than that, on a quick search through the previews - it's certainly not limited to psychopomps and underworld gods, and not all underworld gods have it. Here's the list:<br /> <br /> Quetzalcoatl, Chantico<br /> Agni, Ganesha, Yamaraja<br /> Anpu, Ptah, Thoth<br /> Eshu, Oshossi, Oya, Sonponna<br /> Sun Wukong<br /> Hades, Hermes, Persephone<br /> Donn, Manannan mac Lir, the Morrigan","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T11:45:13-07:00","id":1145856,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but under what definition of liminal is Dionysus, god of that which is foreign and other, transgresses gender and the self, NOT liminal; but both Quetzacoatl and Yamaraja are?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-01-2017, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T11:47:41-07:00","id":1145857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1145850#post1145850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still not clear on what the &quot;Liminal&quot; Calling refers to. There are a lot of liminal figures who don't have it. Is it exclusively for psychopomps and underworld gods? So Janus, for example, despite being literally the god of the threshold, wouldn't have it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that might be a side effect of the Three Calling Limit... Liminal deities by definition do a bunch of other stuff, since they are 'in-between' Gods, meaning they have a bunch of potential Callings... Shiva, for example, is very definitely a Liminal God, but I'm stumped as to which of his current set to dump to make way for it since those all make sense for him. I think this leads to the situation where Psychopomps and Underworld Gods (who are 'double-dipping' in Liminal, so to speak) are the ones who very clearly have it and a whole bunch of other Gods have picked up Knacks from it.<br /> <br /> Out of curiosity, which other figures revealed so far do you think should have it but don't, and which of their current Callings would you replace?<br /> <br /> Also, as question for the devs... how complicated is the process of picking up Knacks from Callings outside your main three?<br /> <br /> EDIT : Wait, Dionysus <i>doesn't</i> have it?...(Runs off to check Theoi Preview)... well, I'll be damned, I think I must have subconsciously just given him Liminal and not even noticed that he had Leader.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 10-01-2017, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T12:17:02-07:00","id":1145865,"title":"","content":"Also, looking through that list, I have an opposite question... why does Chantico, whose write-up spends half of itself describing her connections to banks and protections, not have Guardian, but does have Liminal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T23:54:59-07:00","id":1145989,"title":"","content":"I can't remember - is the Companion supposed to cover Tutelary deities, and thus presumably having a specific &quot;location&quot; as a purview (i.e. as god of this neighborhood, I'm very powerful over it, but that power doesn't extend over anywhere else)?<br /> <br /> (alternatively it occurs to me that possessing a location as its divine spirit might work nicely as the PSP of the &quot;Numina&quot;, the indigenous gods of Italy not subsumed by the more powerful narratives of the Theoi... the greatest remaining number of whom is obviously Janus)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T01:00:30-07:00","id":1145997,"title":"","content":"I was just thinking on how the Yazata and Orisha would get along on the point of mutual suspicion: malicious sorcerers. Theological texts and the myths declare the main servants of the Daevas to be the Yatus (wizards) and Pairikas (witches), who conduct themselves in sorcery instead of ritual and theurgy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Religions Academic. Zoroastrian Convert.</i><br /> <b>Official Work:</b> Scion: Companion, Scion: Demigod.<br /> <b>Nexus Work:</b> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/293097/The-Cortes-Divinas-of-Maria-Lionza?cPath=8329_32938\" target=\"_blank\">Cortes Divinas of Maria Lionza</a>","edited":{"userid":17311,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17311-xhepablo","user":"xhepablo","date":". 10-02-2017, 06:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17311-xhepablo","name":"xhepablo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17311_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T03:41:50-07:00","id":1146018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1145989#post1145989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't remember - is the Companion supposed to cover Tutelary deities, and thus presumably having a specific &quot;location&quot; as a purview (i.e. as god of this neighborhood, I'm very powerful over it, but that power doesn't extend over anywhere else)?<br /> <br /> (alternatively it occurs to me that possessing a location as its divine spirit might work nicely as the PSP of the &quot;Numina&quot;, the indigenous gods of Italy not subsumed by the more powerful narratives of the Theoi... the greatest remaining number of whom is obviously Janus)</div> </div> </div> </div>It does cover tutelary deities, from what Neall's said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T14:04:31-07:00","id":1146156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xhepablo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1145997#post1145997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was just thinking on how the Yazata and Orisha would get along on the point of mutual suspicion: malicious sorcerers. Theological texts and the myths declare the main servants of the Daevas to be the Karapans (wizards) and Partigans (witches), who conduct themselves in sorcery instead of ritual and theurgy.</div> </div> </div> </div> I can't seem to find anything on the Partigans, is there another transliteration I can Google?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T14:09:58-07:00","id":1146157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1146018#post1146018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does cover tutelary deities, from what Neall's said.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if that means we\u2019ll see location as purview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T15:40:24-07:00","id":1146175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1146156#post1146156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't seem to find anything on the Partigans, is there another transliteration I can Google?</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad! It was late at night and autocorrect was likely kicking in! The terms you're looking for are Yatu and Pairika. I've edited the original post to fix that mistake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Religions Academic. Zoroastrian Convert.</i><br /> <b>Official Work:</b> Scion: Companion, Scion: Demigod.<br /> <b>Nexus Work:</b> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/293097/The-Cortes-Divinas-of-Maria-Lionza?cPath=8329_32938\" target=\"_blank\">Cortes Divinas of Maria Lionza</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17311-xhepablo","name":"xhepablo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17311_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T16:31:58-07:00","id":1146186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1146157#post1146157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder if that means we\u2019ll see location as purview.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Awhile back, didn't Neall mention that the relevant purview for a would-be tutelary deity was Prosperity (to bring prosperity and security to the people you're acting as patron to)? (That said, it's entirely possible that the focus has changed since he said that...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","user":"yukikaze","date":". 10-03-2017, 12:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T18:24:11-07:00","id":1146209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yukikaze</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1146186#post1146186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Awhile back, didn't Neall mention that the relevant purview for a would-be tutelary deity was Prosperity (to bring prosperity and security to the people you're acting patron to)? (That said, it's entirely possible that the focus has changed since he said that...)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok cool - that still leaves me wondering if &quot;Possessing a place&quot; is a viable PSP concept then, or if that'll be covered elsewhere. As I said, my first thought on where to apply it would be the PSP of the indigenous gods of Italy - hence Romans not having a strong sense of an Overworld their gods dwell in (rather associating them directly with their temples or the forests/fields/springs they represented) outside of when Olympus comes up in stories they directly crib from the Greeks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-02-2017, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T21:10:51-07:00","id":1146237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1146209#post1146209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ok cool - that still leaves me wondering if &quot;Possessing a place&quot; is a viable PSP concept then, or if that'll be covered elsewhere. As I said, my first thought on where to apply it would be the PSP of the indigenous gods of Italy - hence Romans not having a strong sense of an Overworld their gods dwell in (rather associating them directly with their temples or the forests/fields/springs they represented) outside of when Olympus comes up in stories they directly crib from the Greeks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It'd be interesting if that kind of thing was explored, either as a purview or as some other kind of mechanic.<br /> <br /> If they were going to start introducing additional purviews, the Companion is as likely a place as any to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T00:55:51-07:00","id":1146929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1146209#post1146209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ok cool - that still leaves me wondering if &amp;quot;Possessing a place&amp;quot; is a viable PSP concept then, or if that'll be covered elsewhere. As I said, my first thought on where to apply it would be the PSP of the indigenous gods of Italy - hence Romans not having a strong sense of an Overworld their gods dwell in (rather associating them directly with their temples or the forests/fields/springs they represented) outside of when Olympus comes up in stories they directly crib from the Greeks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn\u2019t \u201cbeing a god of a place\u201d a stretch goal that funded?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T05:20:31-07:00","id":1146977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1146929#post1146929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn\u2019t \u201cbeing a god of a place\u201d a stretch goal that funded?</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought so, but I wasn\u2019t sure","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T05:23:25-07:00","id":1146980,"title":"","content":"To Neall/writers,<br /> <br /> Is the impression that Titans don\u2019t have Callings correct?<br /> <br /> Does the setting have room for anti-Titans... embodiments ruled by a given CALLING, forsaking Purviews?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T14:29:14-07:00","id":1147203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1146980#post1146980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To Neall/writers,<br /> <br /> Is the impression that Titans don\u2019t have Callings correct?<br /> <br /> Does the setting have room for anti-Titans... embodiments ruled by a given CALLING, forsaking Purviews?</div> </div> </div> </div>Titans have different Callings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T14:37:02-07:00","id":1147205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1147203#post1147203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Titans have different Callings.</div> </div> </div> </div> Can you Tell me what the Judge calling knacks do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T16:17:00-07:00","id":1147232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1147203#post1147203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Titans have different Callings.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's veeeeeery interesting, until now I was working with the idea they only had Purviews and titanic Virtues. Is there anything you can tell us right now about those?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 10-06-2017, 07:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T00:29:27-07:00","id":1147699,"title":"","content":"What Purview is best associated with memory at the past? Like, what purview would Mnemosyne embody as a Titan?<br /> <br /> - Stars (for gazing into the past and temporal shenanigans)?<br /> - Death (the ghost association is pretty self explanatory)?<br /> - Would Passion (Memory) be viable as a purview, despite memory not being an emotion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T01:00:04-07:00","id":1147702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1147699#post1147699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Purview is best associated with memory at the past? Like, what purview would Mnemosyne embody as a Titan?<br /> <br /> - Stars (for gazing into the past and temporal shenanigans)?<br /> - Death (the ghost association is pretty self explanatory)?<br /> - Would Passion (Memory) be viable as a purview, despite memory not being an emotion?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're willing to extend that to storyteling and history, I wonder if Artistry could also work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T12:10:31-07:00","id":1147844,"title":"","content":"I've got a complicated question: Do the gods see the entire World as their territory? I ask that because, the ancient vikings didn't think just their lands were made by Odin when he killed Yair they thought all lands were ymir's body,same thing for the Greeks they thought everywhere, even not greek lands,was Gaea. So,do the gods see the entire world as their dominion?Or just the places where their worshippers came from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T12:33:26-07:00","id":1147852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1147702#post1147702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you're willing to extend that to storyteling and history, I wonder if Artistry could also work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, i\u2019m tinkering with writeups for the Muses, and they\u2019re coming out 2 Purviews each (mostly an Artistry and a Passion, but there are exceptions like Terpsichore has Artistry [Dance] and Epic Dex, and Urania has Stars and Passion [Curiosity]). So Clio definitely has Artistry (Histories/Nonfiction)! But Her other purview is a bit hard to pick, and I figure it would be whatever purview her mother embodies as Titaness of Memory. I\u2019m leaning mostly toward Death for dealing with people and events dead and buried - but if Passion can be used to deal directly with Memory that would work too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T12:55:12-07:00","id":1147855,"title":"","content":"This might be a thing that goes differently depending on Pantheon... how do the Greeks look at Memory? For the Deva, at least in some Traditions, Memory is a byproduct of Attachment, and Attachment is a byproduct of the Material World, all three of which are covered by Deception to some degree... hence why Durga, who is Parama Prakriti (The Supreme Embodiment of Material Nature) is also MahaMaya (The Grand Illusion of Attachment) and MahaSmriti (The Great Embodiment of Memory)... all of which, for her, are technically channeled through Deception because that's how her Legend is built (same as how Kali channels Beauty through Death, and Sun Wukong through Beasts). For a topic as obscure as Memory, you might be best served by seeing what Memory is to the culture in question and giving it to the closest Purview.<br /> <br /> That being said, I am curious to know if Memory is a valid target for Passion... and if it isn't, could Passion (Nostalgia) exist and cover much the same base?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T11:08:07-07:00","id":1149736,"title":"","content":"How much more complicated do Canaanite Polytheists make the Israel/Palestinian conflict?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-14-2017, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T11:27:41-07:00","id":1149746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1149736#post1149736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much more complicated to Canaanite Polytheists make the Israel/Palestinian conflict?</div> </div> </div> </div>And putting THAT in my big folder of &quot;Well that shit's not coming up at my table-&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T11:38:25-07:00","id":1149749,"title":"","content":"So I recall it being asked earlier why someone would want something like Beasts(birds) instead of Beasts all with the answer being something about being able to do more advanced marvels with the narrower focus, Does this continue on to say, the Morrigan's Beast(crows)? How many levels of specificity do these sorts of purview go?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T16:24:54-07:00","id":1149785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1147844#post1147844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got a complicated question: Do the gods see the entire World as their territory? I ask that because, the ancient vikings didn't think just their lands were made by Odin when he killed Yair they thought all lands were ymir's body,same thing for the Greeks they thought everywhere, even not greek lands,was Gaea. So,do the gods see the entire world as their dominion?Or just the places where their worshippers came from?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since nothing was discovered further than their own lands, it is difficult to say. As the way they used to think when they created deities, I would say yeah, all over the world but think, since they share the Overworld, they DO share the mortal World too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T16:33:51-07:00","id":1149788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1149785#post1149785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since nothing was discovered further than their own lands, it is difficult to say. As the way they used to think when they created deities, I would say yeah, all over the world but think, since they share the Overworld, they DO share the mortal World too.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T11:45:47-07:00","id":1149967,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it isn't like you can't find worshipers of faiths half the world away from the point of origin of their religion in large numbers. I mean, maybe in the World there's some regional favoritism or something because home is where the heart is, but I can't see any reason you can't have incarnations of Zeus walking the streets of Berlin or the Monkey King deciding to tear it up in New Orleans, or any reason the myriad cults and faiths out there couldn't be just as spread out. Which probably leads to some really weird interpersonal issues if like, multiple storm gods try to do something in New York.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T22:50:08-07:00","id":1150900,"title":"","content":"With the Anunna and the Elohim both potentially existing as covered Pantheons in future books, is it likely that Inanna/Ishtar will just also be a member of the Elohim as &quot;Astarte&quot;, the same way Yamaraja is also a member of the Shen as Yanlou, and the Kami as Emma-O? Or is it more likely Astarte will be a separate deity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T12:41:45-07:00","id":1151089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1150900#post1150900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the Anunna and the Elohim both potentially existing as covered Pantheons in future books, is it likely that Inanna/Ishtar will just also be a member of the Elohim as &quot;Astarte&quot;, the same way Yamaraja is also a member of the Shen as Yanlou, and the Kami as Emma-O? Or is it more likely Astarte will be a separate deity?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rather she be listed as a separate deity as Asherah (the actual Semitic goddess you may be thinking of) as opposed to Astarte (a Hellenized Ishtar).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Religions Academic. Zoroastrian Convert.</i><br /> <b>Official Work:</b> Scion: Companion, Scion: Demigod.<br /> <b>Nexus Work:</b> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/293097/The-Cortes-Divinas-of-Maria-Lionza?cPath=8329_32938\" target=\"_blank\">Cortes Divinas of Maria Lionza</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17311-xhepablo","name":"xhepablo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17311_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T16:38:41-07:00","id":1151150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xhepablo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1151089#post1151089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd rather she be listed as a separate deity as Asherah (the actual Semitic goddess you may be thinking of) as opposed to Astarte (a Hellenized Ishtar).</div> </div> </div> </div>Asherah is a separate figure. I was referring (using to the more well known name) to Athtart, who is the west Semitic counterpart to Inanna/Ishtar who features in myths with Anat and Ba\u2019al.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T20:51:06-07:00","id":1151550,"title":"","content":"It was mentioned that some Tutelary gods are planned, specifically for Companion if I remember correctly. Any hints as to which ones will be included?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T08:08:35-07:00","id":1151642,"title":"","content":"Has it been discussed yet whether the new edition Nemetondevos are going to follow the French version and give them a PSP based around being \u201cpost-Fate\u201d because they already died and their legends are gone?<br /> <br /> It was a clever way to handle how little we know about Gaulish myth - making that the premise around which the Pantheon was built.<br /> <br /> My guess for their predestruction existence is that Geas (possibly under different related names) was a Pan-Celtic PSP, the way the Orisha and the Loa share the same PSP under different names. I suppose, if the Nemetondevos have a PSP that doesn\u2019t fit what it would have been in the ancient world, we\u2019ll see if the Plant Don get Geas (seems plausible) - that would be a strong point in the Pan-Celtic theory\u2019s favor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T08:40:29-07:00","id":1151650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1151642#post1151642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has it been discussed yet whether the new edition Nemetondevos are going to follow the French version and give them a PSP based around being \u201cpost-Fate\u201d because they already died and their legends are gone?<br /> <br /> It was a clever way to handle how little we know about Gaulish myth - making that the premise around which the Pantheon was built.<br /> <br /> My guess for their predestruction existence is that Geas (possibly under different related names) was a Pan-Celtic PSP, the way the Orisha and the Loa share the same PSP under different names. I suppose, if the Nemetondevos have a PSP that doesn\u2019t fit what it would have been in the ancient world, we\u2019ll see if the Plant Don get Geas (seems plausible) - that would be a strong point in the Pan-Celtic theory\u2019s favor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last Neall said, a chunk of the Nemetondevos are in the cycle of reincarnation (ie, Incarnate candidates), while the others are sitting in their Underworld, really upset.<br /> <br /> The last he said on reincarnation, meanwhile, it involves partially rebuilding your Mantle from the ground up - I <i>think</i> the idea is there's a good part of your Mantle still there, something that embodies the archetypes and power of your previous incarnation, but you have a certain degree of leeway in remaking it.<br /> <br /> So... not all the Nemetondevos are dead, and even the ones who <i>are</i> still have a fair part of themselves in Fate. My hunch is that, essentially, this time round how little we know of the Nemetondevos will be the basis for their Incarnates' play experience - the players get to (re)define what the gods of Gaul are now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T09:02:11-07:00","id":1151652,"title":"","content":"That does leave me wondering what their PSP could be - if it\u2019s not \u201cFate has no hold on us because we finished our Fates already\u201d ala 1E, and it can\u2019t be anything from Gaulish myth because we don\u2019t have any Gaulish myths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T09:54:40-07:00","id":1151664,"title":"","content":"Hm. Neall's said the Nemetondevos are the game's primary example of a dead pantheon - ie, it's not just that a number of the gods are dead, but that the pantheon is essentially dead too, with the shrines abandoned or destroyed, the worshippers killed or enslaved, and the gods dead or in the Underworld, with virtually all knowledge of them wiped out...<br /> <br /> It could be that basically, with the pantheon gone, there's no PSP any more... and making one would be a goal as their Incarnates ascend to godhood again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T11:09:30-07:00","id":1151685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1151664#post1151664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. Neall's said the Nemetondevos are the game's primary example of a dead pantheon - ie, it's not just that a number of the gods are dead, but that the pantheon is essentially dead too, with the shrines abandoned or destroyed, the worshippers killed or enslaved, and the gods dead or in the Underworld, with virtually all knowledge of them wiped out...<br /> <br /> It could be that basically, with the pantheon gone, there's no PSP any more... and making one would be a goal as their Incarnates ascend to godhood again.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Same question as who comes first between egg and hen but do u think it's because the pantheon dies because of, let's say, Titans that worshippers are fewer or vanished or the other way around: because worshippers are not fed of legends from their pantheons so they are weaker enough to be attacked by Titans and because of the attack, it DOES completely vanish?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T11:20:51-07:00","id":1151689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1151685#post1151685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same question as who comes first between egg and hen but do u think it's because the pantheon dies because of, let's say, Titans that worshippers are fewer or vanished or the other way around: because worshippers are not fed of legends from their pantheons so they are weaker enough to be attacked by Titans and because of the attack, it DOES completely vanish?</div> </div> </div> </div>With the Nemetondevos, Neall's said it was the obliteration of their people in the Gallic Wars that destroyed the pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T11:46:32-07:00","id":1151700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1151689#post1151689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With the Nemetondevos, Neall's said it was the obliteration of their people in the Gallic Wars that destroyed the pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Divus Julius, Scion of Venus literally killed them. Loss of worship was a consequence of their death, not the cause.<br /> <br /> My headcanon is that Romulus, Scion of Mars, did the same thing with the preexisting Sabine gods (except Janus who betrayed his colleagues with that volcanic geyser), and took the Mantle of Quirinus from their slain war god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-21-2017, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T20:19:36-07:00","id":1151835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1151652#post1151652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That does leave me wondering what their PSP could be - if it\u2019s not \u201cFate has no hold on us because we finished our Fates already\u201d ala 1E, and it can\u2019t be anything from Gaulish myth because we don\u2019t have any Gaulish myths.</div> </div> </div> </div>... Okay, I SWEAR this happened...<br /> <br /> I remember there was a live IRC Q&amp;A session back during the Kickstarter. I remember being there.<br /> <br /> I vaguely recall that there was a collection of the questions and answers that was posted <i>on this forum</i> but I can't seem to find it.<br /> <br /> But I <i>swear to all the Gods</i> that when there, I asked a question about the Nemetondevos PSP.<br /> <br /> \u200bUgh... <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar137_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"137\" data-vbnamecard=\"137\">Neall</a> - Do you remember this? Do you feel like answering what the Nemetondevos PSP is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T20:22:57-07:00","id":1151836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1151700#post1151700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, Divus Julius, Scion of Venus literally killed them. Loss of worship was a consequence of their death, not the cause.<br /> <br /> My headcanon is that Romulus, Scion of Mars, did the same thing with the preexisting Sabine gods (except Janus who betrayed his colleagues with that volcanic geyser), and took the Mantle of Quirinus from their slain war god.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you elaborate on the volcanic geyser thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T20:54:14-07:00","id":1151846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1151836#post1151836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you elaborate on the volcanic geyser thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>During the kidnapping of the Sabine women by Romulus\u2019 forces, Janus is attributed with the eruption of a boiling geyser that buried the pursuing forces of King Tatius.<br /> <br /> If we assume that in the World, the Latins were a distinctly Theoi worshipping people having brought their religion with them from the fall of Troy led by Aeneas (not true in reality, but that\u2019s what their own myths say was the case), making Janus different from the other major Roman gods because he was an indigenous Sabine god rather than a Mantle of one of the Theoi, or a Roman-born Scion of the Theoi, then as a Sabine god he betrayed his people to the victorious Romans securing his place in the new order.<br /> <br /> He\u2019s nothing if not two-faced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material