nimate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we please see a preview of the Geneses soon? Also, did you settle on whether the Incarnate Genesis will be in the Companion or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it will be in there. After a lot of consideration it won't take much more to do than the SG plotting out some advancement story arcs ahead of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T13:24:24-07:00","id":1153572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1153458#post1153458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, it will be in there. After a lot of consideration it won't take much more to do than the SG plotting out some advancement story arcs ahead of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, happy day!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T18:20:36-07:00","id":1153847,"title":"","content":"Do we know if the Loa have the same Virtues as the Orisha in addition to sharing the same PSP?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T12:33:30-07:00","id":1153957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1153847#post1153847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we know if the Loa have the same Virtues as the Orisha in addition to sharing the same PSP?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T13:10:56-07:00","id":1153963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1153957#post1153957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, thanks! I imagine there\u2019s a tendency toward Rada favoring Tradition and Petwo favoring Innovation?<br /> <br /> Is it likely the Plant Don will similarly share PSP (with a different name) and Virtues with the Tuatha de Danann?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T13:28:22-07:00","id":1153968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noneofyourbusiness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a Q&amp;A (<a href=\"https://gmshoe.wordpress.com/2016/10/11/qa-neall-raemonn-price-scion-2e/\" target=\"_blank\">https://gmshoe.wordpress.com/2016/10...rice-scion-2e/</a>) I just read from last year, there was a question &quot;&lt;+[FallenEco]&gt; What is the relationship between the Titans and Primordials like? Obviously it varies on individuals but in general\u2026&quot;<br /> <br /> which you answered with &quot;Cold War&quot; as though they had been asking about Titans and Gods. Could you say more about the relationship between Titans and Primordials in general? Especially given that in the same Q&amp;A you said that how a Titan relates to the Primordials influences that Titan's Virtues?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, sorry.<br /> <br /> Some Titans aren't truly independent deities, but are <i>emanations </i>of a larger Primordial - a manifest element of their power. Gods try not to think too hard about the relationship between Incarnates, Gods, Emanations, and Primordials. <br /> <br /> Some Primordials take a fairly direct hand in their pantheons, manifesting within the Overworld and warring against Titans. In general, the Primordials create vast lands, and sometimes they birth Titans or <i>are</i> them. They typically have the same relations as other gods, but more distant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T13:56:06-07:00","id":1153977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1153968#post1153968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, sorry.<br /> <br /> Some Titans aren't truly independent deities, but are <i>emanations </i>of a larger Primordial - a manifest element of their power. Gods try not to think too hard about the relationship between Incarnates, Gods, Emanations, and Primordials.<br /> <br /> Some Primordials take a fairly direct hand in their pantheons, manifesting within the Overworld and warring against Titans. In general, the Primordials create vast lands, and sometimes they birth Titans or <i>are</i> them. They typically have the same relations as other gods, but more distant.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting! That's much closer to 1E's Titan Avatars than I previously had gotten the impression was the case. I had thought Titans this time around were individual divinities like Gods who were dominated by a specific Purview in a way Gods are not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T15:06:49-07:00","id":1153998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1153963#post1153963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awesome, thanks! I imagine there\u2019s a tendency toward Rada favoring Tradition and Petwo favoring Innovation?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't necessarily make that association this late in history, but that was probably true at some point. If anything I'd associate Tradition with the smaller nasyons like Ibo who have more to lose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T15:53:17-07:00","id":1154008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1153998#post1153998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't necessarily make that association this late in history, but that was probably true at some point. If anything I'd associate Tradition with the smaller nasyons like Ibo who have more to lose.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair enough.<br /> <br /> Out of curiosity, can you let us in on the degree of interrelation between the Orisha and their direct Loa equivalents?<br /> <br /> Like...<br /> <br /> 1) Papa Legba and Kalfu are both Mantles of Eshu Elegba<br /> <br /> 2) Papa Legba is a Mantle of Eshu Elegba, but Kalfu is distinctly an independent Loa<br /> <br /> 3) Papa Legba and Kalfu are both independent younger divinities distinct from Eshu Elegba<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Obviously that question applies as easily with Oshun, Erzulie Freda and Erzulie Dantor, among others.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T13:14:37-07:00","id":1154818,"title":"","content":"Hi Neall,<br /> <br /> Like many others i'm really hyped on this project (that i backed on KS) and i can't wait to receive the pdf and physical books but i know that a quality project takes time.<br /> <br /> My game master and our group are already talking about preparation for a Scion campaign and we would like to know if you already have some idea about how and when Demigod and God will be made.<br /> <br /> I imagine that the production of these two books will be shorter than Origin and Hero, since the basic system will already be published but our gamemaster as a hard time writing his campaign without knowing how much time he'll have to wait to transition us from Hero to Demigod and so forth.<br /> <br /> Thanks for all the great works on your game lines !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20788-burbankfr","name":"Burbankfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T07:34:22-07:00","id":1155051,"title":"","content":"Can a character from a supernatural race be a Scion for a different mythology\u2019s pantheon?<br /> <br /> Loki beds a kitsune, gives birth to a kitsune Scion daughter?<br /> <br /> A satyr who struggles to control his passions through Buddhism (linked to the Greco-Bactrian tradition) becomes Chosen of one of the Palas?<br /> <br /> Immigration creates a Kemetic synchronist offshoot of Naga (with Netjer and Deva Scions) in Africa and the West?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T19:15:50-07:00","id":1155252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1155051#post1155051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a character from a supernatural race be a Scion for a different mythology\u2019s pantheon?<br /> <br /> Loki beds a kitsune, gives birth to a kitsune Scion daughter?<br /> <br /> A satyr who struggles to control his passions through Buddhism (linked to the Greco-Bactrian tradition) becomes Chosen of one of the Palas?<br /> <br /> Immigration creates a Kemetic synchronist offshoot of Naga (with Netjer and Deva Scions) in Africa and the West?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In the preview a short while back on Character Creation, there is a line that says:<br /> <br /> &quot;...the World is a surprisingly cosmopolitan place, and if you have an idea for a Kitsune associated with the Manitou or something equally unexpected, that\u2019s perfectly fine.&quot;<br /> <br /> I imagine that if you can come up with a concept (and have it approved by your Story Teller!) then you can go with it. 2E appears to be MUCH more fluid in regards to characters than 1E could ever hope to be!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13182-eltheriond","name":"Eltheriond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T20:43:52-07:00","id":1155273,"title":"","content":"Awesome! Missed that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T12:59:34-08:00","id":1156139,"title":"","content":"Tiamat: Water or Chaos?<br /> <br /> Obviously the other is her strongest Purview that she is dominated by, but which one dominates her?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T04:58:38-08:00","id":1156285,"title":"","content":"I was reading through the World preview again and started wondering - if one were to go beyond the borders of an Overworld, would one fall directly into a Primordial's maw? Or are there more-or-less survivable spaces beyond Godsrealms, possibly malleable by someone sufficiently forceful of will? And am I right in assuming the answer would be the same for Underworlds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13499-not-quite-yoda","name":"Not Quite Yoda","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T09:21:09-08:00","id":1156373,"title":"","content":"What are some of your favorite cross pantheon friendships and rivalries that you guys put into the books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T06:24:33-08:00","id":1156981,"title":""