n Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T05:25:10-08:00","id":1165554,"title":"","content":"Deleted double post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":22488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22488-ventruestereotype","user":"VentrueStereotype","date":". 12-06-2017, 08:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22488-ventruestereotype","name":"VentrueStereotype","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T05:26:42-08:00","id":1165555,"title":"","content":"Deleted double post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22488-ventruestereotype","name":"VentrueStereotype","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T06:04:08-08:00","id":1166071,"title":"","content":"Can we expect a big table cross-listing gods and purviews, plus another with gods and callings? I\u2019m sure that some fan will make such a thing as soon as the game is released, but it would be nice to have such tables directly in the books.<br /> <br /> \u2014Jim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4310-jagardner","name":"jagardner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T16:21:48-08:00","id":1166561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=790453#post790453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I <i>love </i>the Keepers of the World, and if anything they'll be a bigger part of 2e. There's even going to be a mechanic to sort of explain their big evil plan...<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Is it really possible for the keepers to banish all other gods from the world according to the their plan? How does that work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 12-10-2017, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T19:45:51-08:00","id":1167204,"title":"","content":"I knew way before the kickstarter ended that we wouldn't get the books in October like they told us. I'm just wondering if we will get them this year.<br /> I have cancer and I will die of it for sure. All I wanted was to build a setting for my pool of players to enjoy in the new edition for we had much fun in the first (with alot of house ruling per se) before I'm gone, as a reminder of our friendship.<br /> <br /> Is it that hard to tell us at the very least the month It'll be released?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4754-ironskin","name":"Ironskin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T06:49:39-08:00","id":1167285,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, it probably IS &quot;that hard&quot; to tell us when it's coming out. They didn't know that a major system change would occur part way through development, which is how the current delay happened. And they can't predict illness, weather, war with Korea, or anything else that could possibly delay things - they gave a date way off in the future for the Cavaliers of Mars KS, for exactly that reason. Sorry to hear about your health; if you really want to design a campaign, you could still construct a setting, even without the rules, by setting up the campaign premise, outlining the major NPCs, and writing out a basic metaplot, and leave that as a legacy to a future ST, just without the actual character generation. And if things do turn around for you all that work is still done for you to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T08:13:25-08:00","id":1167307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1167285#post1167285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, it probably IS &quot;that hard&quot; to tell us when it's coming out. They didn't know that a major system change would occur part way through development, which is how the current delay happened. And they can't predict illness, weather, war with Korea, or anything else that could possibly delay things - they gave a date way off in the future for the Cavaliers of Mars KS, for exactly that reason. Sorry to hear about your health; if you really want to design a campaign, you could still construct a setting, even without the rules, by setting up the campaign premise, outlining the major NPCs, and writing out a basic metaplot, and leave that as a legacy to a future ST, just without the actual character generation. And if things do turn around for you all that work is still done for you to use.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> totally agree with you. Ironskin if you're really in this situation try to use this time to create a legacy, an heir for em","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T09:44:30-08:00","id":1167338,"title":"","content":"Everything is ready to go ''setting wise'', all we need now are actual rules and content for 2nd edition. <br /> <br /> My situation was stable up until like 2 weeks ago when they found out cancer started to spread again (brain). I know my players won't reprise this setting, I just want to build great content they will remember. As I imagine all of you, our journey with Scion can be counted in years and the news of a new (and fingers crossed, more polished) edition had us thrilled. Sorry if my previous post sounded rude or something, let's just say I'm on a deadline. Literally lol.<br /> <br /> Also I know this ain't the topic but what will be your first setting guys? Modern stuff, futuristic, medieval, etc...? (reply in PM if this is inapropriate here)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4754-ironskin","name":"Ironskin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T09:54:19-08:00","id":1167341,"title":"","content":"Open a new thread about you asking for suggests, so we can talk there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T15:14:52-08:00","id":1167427,"title":"","content":"I was reading through the previous articles and the article about satyrs caught my attention. It says that they can gain legend, and that their max legend rating is 3. So I got to thinking about the other non Scion supernatural beings, what is the most powerful non Scion option and what is their max legend rating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T06:18:04-08:00","id":1168173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rickayelm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1167427#post1167427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was reading through the previous articles and the article about satyrs caught my attention. It says that they can gain legend, and that their max legend rating is 3. So I got to thinking about the other non Scion supernatural beings, what is the most powerful non Scion option and what is their max legend rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kitsune max out around Legend 7 or so. That's all I know off the top of my head!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T06:26:27-08:00","id":1168175,"title":"","content":"Could a supernatural being also be a Scion an thus transcend their normal Legend limit? I'm just thinking if &quot;Great Pan is dead&quot; and a Satyr PC is an Incarnate, or if Loki beds a Kitsune, etc...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T06:50:57-08:00","id":1168177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1168175#post1168175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a supernatural being also be a Scion an thus transcend their normal Legend limit? I'm just thinking if &amp;quot;Great Pan is dead&amp;quot; and a Satyr PC is an Incarnate, or if Loki beds a Kitsune, etc...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. A Supernatural Path replaces one of your Callings. You're (maybe) a bit more powerful but you're definitely less versatile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T06:52:14-08:00","id":1168178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ironskin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1167204#post1167204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it that hard to tell us at the very least the month It'll be released?</div> </div> </div> </div>Check your Inbox messages!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T07:28:27-08:00","id":1168188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1168178#post1168178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Check your Inbox messages!</div> </div> </div> </div>Neall,could you \u00e2nswer my question about the keepers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T08:42:39-08:00","id":1168196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1168178#post1168178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Check your Inbox messages!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh that's just cruel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T09:55:57-08:00","id":1168208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1166561#post1166561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it really possible for the keepers to banish all other gods from the world according to the their plan? How does that work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gods of different pantheons can rewrite their own history into a coherent, singular timeline that has &quot;always&quot; been true, in a theomantic working called a Creation Myth. Such a Myth reinforces the structure of the World and reinforces reality itself (and the prisons of the Titans), at a cost of potentially introducing new Titans from the Primordial forces invoked. Imhotep believes he's found a way to <i>seal </i>the World rather than reinforce it, cutting it off permanently from the Overworld and Underworld and leaving humanity free to chart their own destiny free of the capricious influence of the Gods and the threat of the Titans.<br /> <br /> The Keepers are working to forge their own pantheon that is not just in defiance of, or in opposition to, other pantheons - but one that is in fact anathema to them, a sweeping change that renders the World safer, if a bit lesser.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T10:32:07-08:00","id":1168220,"title":"","content":"Given his feelings about being a God and the Celestial Bureauceacy, is Master Kung in with the Keepers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T10:50:19-08:00","id":1168224,"title":"","content":"Secretely Imhotep wants to seal the world because he's pissed at the new Mummy movie","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T10:52:22-08:00","id":1168225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1168208#post1168208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gods of different pantheons can rewrite their own history into a coherent, singular timeline that has &quot;always&quot; been true, in a theomantic working called a Creation Myth. Such a Myth reinforces the structure of the World and reinforces reality itself (and the prisons of the Titans), at a cost of potentially introducing new Titans from the Primordial forces invoked. Imhotep believes he's found a way to <i>seal </i>the World rather than reinforce it, cutting it off permanently from the Overworld and Underworld and leaving humanity free to chart their own destiny free of the capricious influence of the Gods and the threat of the Titans.<br /> <br /> The Keepers are working to forge their own pantheon that is not just in defiance of, or in opposition to, other pantheons - but one that is in fact anathema to them, a sweeping change that renders the World safer, if a bit lesser.</div> </div> </div> </div>fascinating. thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T17:48:03-08:00","id":1168279,"title":"","content":"In the Shen preview, it is said that Erlang can discharge thunderbolts from his third eye, but he doesn\u2019t have the Sky Purview. Which Purview does he use to shoot thunderbolts then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12342-dr-quantum","name":"Dr. Quantum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T19:59:16-08:00","id":1168294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dr. Quantum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1168279#post1168279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Shen preview, it is said that Erlang can discharge thunderbolts from his third eye, but he doesn\u2019t have the Sky Purview. Which Purview does he use to shoot thunderbolts then?</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be that he has the sky boon required but doesn't meet the requirements for it to be a true Associated Purview. whatever those are in 2E.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T07:37:41-08:00","id":1168368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dr. Quantum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1168279#post1168279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Shen preview, it is said that Erlang can discharge thunderbolts from his third eye, but he doesn\u2019t have the Sky Purview. Which Purview does he use to shoot thunderbolts then?</div> </div> </div> </div>He likely does so either as a result of his third eye (which may be a relic) or through an esoteric application of the War Purview (replicating the Sky Boon, but only against foes, for example).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T07:56:06-08:00","id":1168372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1168368#post1168368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He likely does so either as a result of his third eye (which may be a relic) or through an esoteric application of the War Purview (replicating the Sky Boon, but only against foes, for example).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the awesome answer! By the way, this makes me curious, does the War Purview cover all sorts of combat? Back in 1E it seemed that War only covers battles that are ideologically inspired. Is it the same in 2E?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12342-dr-quantum","name":"Dr. Quantum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T09:11:13-08:00","id":1168384,"title":"","content":"One question that occurred to me. It seems many of the pantheon previews we\u2019ve seen, in discussing commonalities among the scions of certain gods, list careers and professions they often go into. If the supernatural is a known factor in the setting, and as one preview mentions, mortals expect Scions to be liaisons to the gods and a buffer against supernatural things, how can they have normal careers like businessmen, law enforcement or farmers? Politics would seem right out once mortals caught on to the existence of social knacks, I can only imagine the brutality claims against Scion cops and mistrials declared because of a Scion lawyer or Judge. Clearly not every Scion is born to actively adventure like a player character but wouldn\u2019t Social pressure, and especially fate, force them out of such \u201cmundane\u201d jobs? Or do most simply find ways to deal with supernatural equivalents of those jobs? Scion farmers ensuring that nothing curses someone\u2019s fields rather than being an actual \u201cfarmer\u201d.<br /> <br /> Or does this simply mean what they might have done pre-visitation?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T16:59:59-08:00","id":1168443,"title":"","content":"While I'm on board with the notion of multiple contradicting truths coexisting, I do have to ask about the practical results of that. For example, Plato described three parts to a soul, while the Kemetic notion holds there are five. If we assume both of these are correct, what happens when an Egyptian sorcerer steals a Greek warrior's shadow? What would a Greek mystic see if they tried to divine that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T17:25:49-08:00","id":1168445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1168384#post1168384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question that occurred to me. It seems many of the pantheon previews we\u2019ve seen, in discussing commonalities among the scions of certain gods, list careers and professions they often go into. If the supernatural is a known factor in the setting, and as one preview mentions, mortals expect Scions to be liaisons to the gods and a buffer against supernatural things, how can they have normal careers like businessmen, law enforcement or farmers? Politics would seem right out once mortals caught on to the existence of social knacks, I can only imagine the brutality claims against Scion cops and mistrials declared because of a Scion lawyer or Judge. Clearly not every Scion is born to actively adventure like a player character but wouldn\u2019t Social pressure, and especially fate, force them out of such \u201cmundane\u201d jobs? Or do most simply find ways to deal with supernatural equivalents of those jobs? Scion farmers ensuring that nothing curses someone\u2019s fields rather than being an actual \u201cfarmer\u201d.<br /> <br /> Or does this simply mean what they might have done pre-visitation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both pre-Visitation and post, if the Scion decides to keep their nature a secret. And some might not either believe the Scion or care, though if they're open about their nature trouble will come to them sooner rather than later. Boons are expensive to maintain and can cause Fatebindings, so you don't pull them out for every Doubting Thomas. Some Scions might appear mostly like lucky and exceptional mortals most of the time. <br /> <br /> Even acknowledged, Scions are shunted off to certain roles - a lawyer might be expected to handle negotiations with the Fair Folk over zoning laws (don't laugh - it really happens in Iceland), while law enforcement might be relegated to the &quot;Special Operations Unit&quot; and given the &quot;really fuckin' weird&quot; assignments with a wide degree of latitude. I don't expect a lot of Scion farmers to be PCs, but they probably end off fighting Ratatoskr's giant squirrel spawn. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreepyShutin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I'm on board with the notion of multiple contradicting truths coexisting, I do have to ask about the practical results of that. For example, Plato described three parts to a soul, while the Kemetic notion holds there are five. If we assume both of these are correct, what happens when an Egyptian sorcerer steals a Greek warrior's shadow? What would a Greek mystic see if they tried to divine that?</div> </div> </div> </div>In general, the active or offensive theology predominates, so the Greek mystic would see the warrior as &quot;wrong&quot; or somehow spiritually complete yet incomplete at the same time. If the reverse occurred, for example, the Egyptian sorcerer would see large chunks of the soul missing, encompassing ba and ka or other elements.<br /> <br /> I'm loathe to give hard-and-fast answers because those should be determined at the table. With so many mythologies and theologies intermixing, hard-and-fast rules are impossible to determine. I realize it's a bit of a judgment call on the part of the Storyguide, but that's the only way this will work. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T17:41:59-08:00","id":1168447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dr. Quantum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1168372#post1168372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the awesome answer! By the way, this makes me curious, does the War Purview cover all sorts of combat? Back in 1E it seemed that War only covers battles that are ideologically inspired. Is it the same in 2E?</div> </div> </div> </div> The War Purview governs strife on a conceptual level as well as armed conflict. It may shape the tide of battles, uplift the destinies of soldiers and generals, or shatter fragile edifices of peace. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T17:51:22-08:00","id":1168448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1168445#post1168445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both pre-Visitation and post, if the Scion decides to keep their nature a secret. And some might not either believe the Scion or care, though if they're open about their nature trouble will come to them sooner rather than later. Boons are expensive to maintain and can cause Fatebindings, so you don't pull them out for every Doubting Thomas. Some Scions might appear mostly like lucky and exceptional mortals most of the time.<br /> <br /> Even acknowledged, Scions are shunted off to certain roles - a lawyer might be expected to handle negotiations with the Fair Folk over zoning laws (don't laugh - it really happens in Iceland), while law enforcement might be relegated to the &quot;Special Operations Unit&quot; and given the &quot;really fuckin' weird&quot; assignments with a wide degree of latitude. I don't expect a lot of Scion farmers to be PCs, but they probably end off fighting Ratatoskr's giant squirrel spawn.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Speaking as an Icelander, that does happen from time to time. I imagine carefully relocating suspected dwellings is a lot worse when they're confirmed and the owner can curse you if they don't like the new view. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1168445#post1168445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, the active or offensive theology predominates, so the Greek mystic would see the warrior as &quot;wrong&quot; or somehow spiritually complete yet incomplete at the same time. If the reverse occurred, for example, the Egyptian sorcerer would see large chunks of the soul missing, encompassing ba and ka or other elements.<br /> <br /> I'm loathe to give hard-and-fast answers because those should be determined at the table. With so many mythologies and theologies intermixing, hard-and-fast rules are impossible to determine. I realize it's a bit of a judgment call on the part of the Storyguide, but that's the only way this will work.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI see! Thanks for the info. I get that it's never easy trying to hold together a lot of conflicting belief systems, so making it a matter of judgment calls is probably the right decision. Still, it's always interesting to get some insight into how the World hangs together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T19:40:17-08:00","id":1169259,"title":"","content":"This has probably been asked, but I haven't seen it, is there a 2e equivalent to the Order of the Divine Glory written in to the vanilla setting? Also, Buhdism has been mentioned earlier, with some gods converting, how does that interact with fatebinding?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5727-racain23","name":"racain23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T07:00:18-08:00","id":1169910,"title":"","content":"where is the greek preview? i can't find it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T08:41:02-08:00","id":1169933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1169910#post1169910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">where is the greek preview? i can't find it</div> </div> </div> </div>It's on the Kickstarter main page.<br /> <br /> Here. <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B01LwCGSbE8kZmtQNHJjd3cyRkE/view\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B01...Jjd3cyRkE/view</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T22:34:35-08:00","id":1170867,"title":"","content":"So I've been thinking about how many people would claim to be scions in the World, when they just happened to have a little supernatural blood/study some magic/be utterly crazy. Are there any easy ways for one scion to recognise another, or for miracles to be distinguished from magic/illusions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13499-not-quite-yoda","name":"Not Quite Yoda","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T21:43:47-08:00","id":1171450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Not Quite Yoda</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1170867#post1170867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've been thinking about how many people would claim to be scions in the World, when they just happened to have a little supernatural blood/study some magic/be utterly crazy. Are there any easy ways for one scion to recognise another, or for miracles to be distinguished from magic/illusions?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWhile a proper mystic might well know the difference, I'd be a lot more worried about the god you're claiming to be descended from. That's a genuine divine name you're pinning to yourself. Do they wanna be associated with some faker? I mean, maybe Loki, if he thinks it's funny, but if you tell people you're the daughter of Indra the Storm King and Indra hears about it, the best you can hope for is a century or so of hard labor. More likely you'll be declared an Asura on the spot and take an astra to the face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T02:58:39-08:00","id":1171497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>racain23</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1169259#post1169259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has probably been asked, but I haven't seen it, is there a 2e equivalent to the Order of the Divine Glory written in to the vanilla setting? Also, Buhdism has been mentioned earlier, with some gods converting, how does that interact with fatebinding?</div> </div> </div> </div>There isn't as of yet, but I may decide to add something into Demigod. Given that monotheism isn't monolithic, and I'd rather not say the Abrahamic religions are all collaborating perfectly, it's likely there will be different elements spread throughout the setting. The Templars are a historical example of this.<br /> <br /> Buddhist Gods are just Gods, though it does affect their Fatebinding weirdly. Gods can join multiple pantheons without significant difficulty beyond inserting themselves into the Legend of the other pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T20:23:36-08:00","id":1171702,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if this has been asked, but I need something clarified. It was mentioned somewhere that the affects of Fate are worse for say a demigod then a god, so I have to ask, do the affects of Fate scale off of legend or just tier? Like does a legend 4 hero have it worse then a legend 1 hero?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T15:47:21-08:00","id":1171907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lionmanguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1171702#post1171702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if this has been asked, but I need something clarified. It was mentioned somewhere that the affects of Fate are worse for say a demigod then a god, so I have to ask, do the affects of Fate scale off of legend or just tier? Like does a legend 4 hero have it worse then a legend 1 hero?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tier is probably what you're really asking about, although Fatebinding does itself has some small effects that key off rating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T16:09:33-08:00","id":1171910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1171907#post1171907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tier is probably what you're really asking about, although Fatebinding does itself has some small effects that key off rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>could you give an example of how a god's fatebindings differ from a hero's?<br /> Oh,and after seeing your Mikola preview,i wanted to know does that mean that saint nicholas belongs to both an native russian pantheon and a abrahamic pantheon?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T19:41:31-08:00","id":1171941,"title":"","content":"One thing I am curious about is if Scion will have mortal sorcerers. Your heretics, minor psychics, ect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T19:49:54-08:00","id":1171942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1171941#post1171941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I am curious about is if Scion will have mortal sorcerers. Your heretics, minor psychics, ect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcerers are mentioned mora than once in this thread,they will be present in origins","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T19:51:48-08:00","id":1171943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1171941#post1171941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I am curious about is if Scion will have mortal sorcerers. Your heretics, minor psychics, ect.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bDefinitely. They revealed that very early on. Sorcerers somehow steal power from the Gods. <br /> <br /> \u200bThere will also be Prophets, Holy Men/Women, and Saints! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T11:36:16-08:00","id":1172033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1171497#post1171497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There isn't as of yet, but I may decide to add something into Demigod. Given that monotheism isn't monolithic, and I'd rather not say the Abrahamic religions are all collaborating perfectly, it's likely there will be different elements spread throughout the setting. The Templars are a historical example of this.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the subject of monotheism, can I just make one request? Whatever you do, <b>please</b> don't go with the &quot;Allah = Hubal&quot; theory. Not only is it historically dubious, it's become strongly associated with various Islamophobic groups. (I realize you probably know all this and are too smart to make that mistake, but I just felt compelled to ask.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/40-dspaul","name":"DSPaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T13:19:35-08:00","id":1172057,"title":"","content":"Reza Aslan\u2019s book \u201cNo God, But God\u201d presents a much stronger historic narrative in which the pre-Islamic understanding of Allah was that of a distant creator (essentially a Primordial in Scion 2E terms) who was seen as non-intercessionary. Hubal was the main actively worshipped deity, seen as the central most false idol by the Prophet Muhammed and the original Umma that needed to be cast out of the Kaaba in favor of the sole worship of Allah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 12-31-2017, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T20:24:35-08:00","id":1172148,"title":"","content":"The big question for me is the status of Manat, Allat, and Uzza in the World. I figure the dominant strains of Islam are strict absolute monotheists as in reality, but \u201cAllah\u2019s daughters\u201d are still honored by minority sects violently repressed by Wahabists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T06:47:05-08:00","id":1172244,"title":"","content":"So, it was mentioned earlier that the reason to take purviews like Beasts or Artistry for a specific animal or craft rather than a general one was that it effected what you can do with marvels. How much granularity is there in that? Say four scions each had artistry, one has Artistry all, on has artistry music, on have artistry woodwinds, and one has artistry clarinet. Is there a difference? How much is too much or too little? Or is it purely GM discretion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T10:02:44-08:00","id":1172292,"title":"","content":"So not sure if this is the right place to ask this or not probably not but anyway. I had an unexpected move after filling out the backer kit. Is there anyway to change my mailing address so that my parents dont receive two big books in their mail when this gets finished and ships?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2107-wiwuno","name":"Wiwuno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T10:33:31-08:00","id":1172302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wiwuno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1172292#post1172292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So not sure if this is the right place to ask this or not probably not but anyway. I had an unexpected move after filling out the backer kit. Is there anyway to change my mailing address so that my parents dont receive two big books in their mail when this gets finished and ships?</div> </div> </div> </div>You should be able to change your address in your backerkit account.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T10:43:23-08:00","id":1172306,"title":"","content":"What about changing one's email address on Backerkit? I also moved recently and I had no problem changing my home address, but I can't figure out how to change the email address for the life of me. I also had to establish a new email account. but Backerkit is still showing my old one.<br /> <br /> \u200bSounds like they'll be sending out links soon, and I need to make sure they'll be going to the right place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T11:00:03-08:00","id":1172310,"title":"","content":"Neall, I was perusing the White Wolf wiki today and I came across something which peaked my interest on the Tuatha page. In the table at the top it states the pantheon purview is Glamour. There also seem to have been intent to create a page for this purview according to the connected disambiguation page. Do you know anything about this? Was this purview ever actually outlined or drawn up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T11:11:08-08:00","id":1172320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1172306#post1172306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about changing one's email address on Backerkit? I also moved recently and I had no problem changing my home address, but I can't figure out how to change the email address for the life of me. I also had to establish a new email account. but Backerkit is still showing my old one.<br /> <br /> \u200bSounds like they'll be sending out links soon, and I need to make sure they'll be going to the right place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Contact Rich through Kickstarter, and he should be able to sort it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T12:16:23-08:00","id":1172343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1172320#post1172320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Contact Rich through Kickstarter, and he should be able to sort it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThanks for the advice! Message sent!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T13:57:50-08:00","id":1172376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manannansun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1172310#post1172310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neall, I was perusing the White Wolf wiki today and I came across something which peaked my interest on the Tuatha page. In the table at the top it states the pantheon purview is Glamour. There also seem to have been intent to create a page for this purview according to the connected disambiguation page. Do you know anything about this? Was this purview ever actually outlined or drawn up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that Scion 2E isn\u2019t even a White Wolf game (Onyx Path owns it outright, they aren\u2019t licensing it like World of Darkness, Chronicles of Darkness, or Exalted) I doubt that wiki has any remotely up to date info. It\u2019s probably referring to some 1st Edition fan Work preceding the official 1E Tuatha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T16:11:00-08:00","id":1172413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manannansun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1172310#post1172310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neall, I was perusing the White Wolf wiki today and I came across something which peaked my interest on the Tuatha page. In the table at the top it states the pantheon purview is Glamour. There also seem to have been intent to create a page for this purview according to the connected disambiguation page. Do you know anything about this? Was this purview ever actually outlined or drawn up?</div> </div> </div> </div>That was designed for 1e by a fan, not as official content, and it was pretty much just the Illusion Purview. I don't think it was ever completed, I think it went up to late Demigod.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T03:22:03-08:00","id":1172587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manannansun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1172310#post1172310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neall, I was perusing the White Wolf wiki today and I came across something which peaked my interest on the Tuatha page. In the table at the top it states the pantheon purview is Glamour. There also seem to have been intent to create a page for this purview according to the connected disambiguation page. Do you know anything about this? Was this purview ever actually outlined or drawn up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Watcher and Glamourweaver already answered for me. The 1e PSP was Enech; the 2e PSP is Geasa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T17:53:00-08:00","id":1172809,"title":"","content":"Now the system is complete, do you think people will typically be able to begin campaigns as soon as the text file gets sent out and still receive Demigod before it's game-relevant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13499-not-quite-yoda","name":"Not Quite Yoda","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T03:55:56-08:00","id":1172962,"title":"","content":"Is the character sheet ready? There is some heavy change between the 1d and 2d (related to the sheet)? Are the 30 abilities the same? The epics are no more squares on the sheet, now are like boons, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T15:32:06-08:00","id":1173347,"title":"","content":"Neall what can you tell me about skin walkers and other shape changers in scion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T15:50:49-08:00","id":1173352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1173347#post1173347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neall what can you tell me about skin walkers and other shape changers in scion?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're there, and they're Paths you can take. Some are pure Antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T16:02:59-08:00","id":1173355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1173352#post1173352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're there, and they're Paths you can take. Some are pure Antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you remember if they can go powerful enough to be Legend 7 like kitsunes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T00:08:24-08:00","id":1173426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1173352#post1173352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're there, and they're Paths you can take. Some are pure Antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry to be the eternal nag to point that out, but isn't it absolutely and expressly forbidden to talk about skinwalkers in the cultures their stories originate from (Din\u00e9/Navajo and related cultures)? I think J. K. Rowling herself recently caught a lot of flack from Native Americans over including them in her American wizardry concepts. I know Scion 2e put a lot of effort into getting the Manitou respectful and right, so I'm a bit surprised about that. Or is there a specific strategy for dealing with that prohibition? Or were you just referring to shapechangers in general in that question, and not to skinwalkers specifically?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T08:55:58-08:00","id":1173499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1173426#post1173426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry to be the eternal nag to point that out, but isn't it absolutely and expressly forbidden to talk about skinwalkers in the cultures their stories originate from (Din\u00e9/Navajo and related cultures)? I think J. K. Rowling herself recently caught a lot of flack from Native Americans over including them in her American wizardry concepts. I know Scion 2e put a lot of effort into getting the Manitou respectful and right, so I'm a bit surprised about that. Or is there a specific strategy for dealing with that prohibition? Or were you just referring to shapechangers in general in that question, and not to skinwalkers specifically?</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't there have to be some loophole there for the stories to exist at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T09:00:47-08:00","id":1173500,"title":"","content":"Couple miscellaneous questions.<br /> If an incarnation has a child is that child a scion as well, and if so are they considered scions of the main god?<br /> Is Izanami considered a god or titan in 2nd. Just wondering cause she's kind of been a little controversial among the scion base and I might have considered being a scion of hers.<br /> You have to share one calling with your divine patron, but at origins you only get one calling. Does that one calling have to match one of your divine patrons or can that come at hero level?<br /> Are Created scions available at origins tier, or does the act of being created by a god automatically put you into hero tier?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23666-turtle314","name":"Turtle314","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T02:00:15-08:00","id":1173717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1173499#post1173499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't there have to be some loophole there for the stories to exist at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>The loophole is mostly white people snooping in stuff they're not supposed to snoop in, once again. I expect there are experts among the Navajo, healers and such, who have to deal with knowledge about these horrible creatures because of their occupations, but that is secret knowledge that doesn't concern outsiders, <i>especially </i>non-Navajo outsiders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T07:49:49-08:00","id":1173752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1173426#post1173426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry to be the eternal nag to point that out, but isn't it absolutely and expressly forbidden to talk about skinwalkers in the cultures their stories originate from (Din\u00e9/Navajo and related cultures)? I think J. K. Rowling herself recently caught a lot of flack from Native Americans over including them in her American wizardry concepts. I know Scion 2e put a lot of effort into getting the Manitou respectful and right, so I'm a bit surprised about that. Or is there a specific strategy for dealing with that prohibition? Or were you just referring to shapechangers in general in that question, and not to skinwalkers specifically?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referring to shapechangers in general and not to skinwalkers specifically. I plan on addressing the Navajo later on, but this - like many other marginalized religions - relies on my finding someone willing to talk about it and share things for the purposes of a game. Scion is an odd sort of cultural primer, but in the sense that it is, I want the culture being transmitted to be a true expression. If the Din\u00e9 don't want to talk about skinwalkers, I'm not going to put something in there that's an express secret of a living religion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T07:59:26-08:00","id":1173755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Turtle314</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1173500#post1173500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couple miscellaneous questions.<br /> If an incarnation has a child is that child a scion as well, and if so are they considered scions of the main god?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes - in fact, most Scions are the children of Incarnations. In the intro story to Hero, Eric Donner meets another Scion of Thor, the son of a different Incarnation of his father. 0<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is Izanami considered a god or titan in 2nd. Just wondering cause she's kind of been a little controversial among the scion base and I might have considered being a scion of hers. </div> </div> </div>She's considered a Primordial deity. You can still be a Scion of hers, you'll just have a very different relationship.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You have to share one calling with your divine patron, but at origins you only get one calling. Does that one calling have to match one of your divine patrons or can that come at hero level? </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are Created scions available at origins tier, or does the act of being created by a god automatically put you into hero tier? </div> </div> </div>They're not available at Hero tier normally, but there's language in <b>Hero </b>that gives your express permission to just wake up on the beach naked if that's the kind of character you really want to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T08:00:26-08:00","id":1173756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1173355#post1173355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you remember if they can go powerful enough to be Legend 7 like kitsunes?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only ones we have in there are therianthropes, various were-creatures. My general feeling is that most of them cap out at the Hero level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T08:03:50-08:00","id":1173757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Not Quite Yoda</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1172809#post1172809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now the system is complete, do you think people will typically be able to begin campaigns as soon as the text file gets sent out and still receive Demigod before it's game-relevant?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm looking to do a lot of open development on Demigod, so <i>hopefully</i>. There's a built-in plateau in <b>Hero</b>, though, so you can keep games going at that level for a while.<br /> <br /> That said, things change at Demigod - in some ways, it's a different game. The difference between Hero and God is actually kind of stark at this point in the design phase. It still uses Momentum and Storypath and the like, but you're going from street-level divine heroes to conceptual incarnations of reality. Maybe a bit bigger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T08:20:53-08:00","id":1173764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1173756#post1173756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only ones we have in there are therianthropes, various were-creatures. My general feeling is that most of them cap out at the Hero level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice,thank you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T09:27:44-08:00","id":1173776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1172962#post1172962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the character sheet ready? There is some heavy change between the 1d and 2d (related to the sheet)? Are the 30 abilities the same? The epics are no more squares on the sheet, now are like boons, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, there's some heavy changes. Epics are indeed Boons (you'll see the three physicals and Epic Appearance as Beauty). There's a new and highly condensed Skill list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T09:40:26-08:00","id":1173779,"title":"","content":"What are the consequences of gods visiting the world without Incarnating,just going here with all their power? what happens?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T13:58:36-08:00","id":1173833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1173779#post1173779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the consequences of gods visiting the world without Incarnating,just going here with all their power? what happens?</div> </div> </div> </div>They tend to invoke Fatebinding far more strongly, and occasionally blow up nearby mortals who are doing nothing but looking at them without protection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T14:09:20-08:00","id":1173837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1173833#post1173833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They tend to invoke Fatebinding far more strongly, and occasionally blow up nearby mortals who are doing nothing but looking at them without protection.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's Suitably Epic. I like it.<br /> Althought of couse,it's real sad for gods who loves their faithful and want to be close to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T14:10:25-08:00","id":1173838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1173757#post1173757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm looking to do a lot of open development on Demigod, so <i>hopefully</i>. There's a built-in plateau in <b>Hero</b>, though, so you can keep games going at that level for a while.<br /> <br /> That said, things change at Demigod - in some ways, it's a different game. The difference between Hero and God is actually kind of stark at this point in the design phase. It still uses Momentum and Storypath and the like, but you're going from street-level divine heroes to conceptual incarnations of reality. Maybe a bit bigger.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's how you'd describe heroes and gods, how would you describe demi-god gameplay?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T14:14:39-08:00","id":1173840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1173838#post1173838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that's how you'd describe heroes and gods, how would you describe demi-god gameplay?</div> </div> </div> </div> Neall said it's about : <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">&quot;Culture heroism and the end of the hero's journey in a few ways.&quot; <b>(Neall)</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1112462#post1112462\">[512]</a></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:",