</div>you're welcome","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T15:17:04-08:00","id":1181507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1181492#post1181492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we sure Prophets, Cassandras, and Oracles are all different things?<br /> <br /> I would have assumed Oracle and Prophet were one in the same, and Cassandra was the same thing with a specific drawback added in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cassandras have the ability to see the absolute truth of things, but with the drawback that noone believes them unless they have divine blood. So they can see through all lies and deceptions, but pretty much only pople like Scions can get past her curse.<br /> <br /> Prophets IIRC have the ability to predict the future by seeing how fate ties things togheter. They can pretty much actually see Fatebindings","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23677-the-eternal-keeper","name":"The Eternal Keeper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T16:44:18-08:00","id":1181516,"title":"","content":"Also @Neall<br /> Does it not make more sense to have Soft and Hard Armor switch effects? With Soft Armor dampening blows, thus making you more resistant to blows, and Hard Armor stopping attacks outright, much like how it's pretty much impossible to penetrate plate armor for a human","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23677-the-eternal-keeper","name":"The Eternal Keeper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T16:58:43-08:00","id":1181521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Eternal Keeper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1181516#post1181516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also @Neall<br /> Does it not make more sense to have Soft and Hard Armor switch effects? With Soft Armor dampening blows, thus making you more resistant to blows, and Hard Armor stopping attacks outright, much like how it's pretty much impossible to penetrate plate armor for a human</div> </div> </div> </div>That kind of is how it works, You are more resistant, thus higher defense since it's not a telling blow. Heavy armor stops it outright by taking wounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T18:49:19-08:00","id":1181547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1181521#post1181521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That kind of is how it works, You are more resistant, thus higher defense since it's not a telling blow. Heavy armor stops it outright by taking wounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm thinking more with that at least how I see it the additional wounds reflect that you soften it so you feel it, but it deals less damage. With Hard Armor it stops it completely and it doesn't hurt you at all, unless it penetrates or you bypass it, and then either way it's going to hurt a looot. <br /> <br /> A clarification on if Lethal can cause Bruised injury conditions would also be really nice","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23677-the-eternal-keeper","name":"The Eternal Keeper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T22:02:44-08:00","id":1181908,"title":"","content":"Some companies add the money from backerit to Kickstarter for the purpose of stretch goals. Are you doing this? I would love to see the chapter on satyrs, but it didn't quite make it into funding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T04:37:32-08:00","id":1181969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1181521#post1181521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That kind of is how it works, You are more resistant, thus higher defense since it's not a telling blow. Heavy armor stops it outright by taking wounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. Hard armor is essentially wearable cover. <br /> <br /> But which kind of Armor is the Well Tempered knack? I\u2019m thinking it is Soft, and it makes the Inflict Injury stunt cost 2s instead of 1. Do I have that right?<br /> <br /> Also, the Combat Medic knack says you heal -1 levels automatically when treating an ally during combat. But First Aid takes a scene. How does treating wounds during combat work?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m thinking here that it would be mental+medicine, like First Aid, but instead of downgrading the Injury Condition it turns the difficulty into a Complication. If you can\u2019t pay off the complication with successes, you take a bashing health level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23791-ashnak","name":"Ashnak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T18:12:48-08:00","id":1182138,"title":"","content":"Sorry if this has been asked before, but why does the Morrigan not have the Warrior calling associated with her?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11958-zerobadguy","name":"ZeroBadguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T19:25:38-08:00","id":1182151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZeroBadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1182138#post1182138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if this has been asked before, but why does the Morrigan not have the Warrior calling associated with her?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, not Neall, but <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"394\" data-vbnamecard=\"394\">Watcher</a> did an <b>amazing</b> look at the Morrigan's stats <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180156#post1180156\">here</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T22:26:03-08:00","id":1182181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1182151#post1182151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, not Neall, but <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"394\" data-vbnamecard=\"394\">Watcher</a> did an <b>amazing</b> look at the Morrigan's stats <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1179705-origins-on-backerkit?p=1180156#post1180156\">here</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the compliment Kyman! <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T05:16:54-08:00","id":1182234,"title":"","content":"A quick mechanics question on the preview, regarding Defence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Defending<br /> Defending creates the basic difficulty an attack must beat in order to successfully hit its target, requiring the defending character to roll the highest of her Resistance attributes. Apply the successes on this roll to generate Defensive Stunts. Defensive Stunts persist until the end of the round.<br /> <br /> Defensive Stunts<br /> Dodge: Unlike most Stunts, Dodge generates successes, which an opponent must overcome in order to inflict an Injury. If this roll generates no successes, the base Difficulty to hit a character is 1. </div> </div> </div>It looks like what should happen is the following. Someone declares an attack, and I roll Defence. If I roll 0 Successes, my Defence is 1 (I.e. this roll generates no successes, so base Difficulty is 1). If I roll 1 Success, my Defence is <i>still</i> one (Dodge generates 1 success which the opponent must overcome). If I roll 2 successes, my Defence becomes 2, etc.<br /> <br /> This means that, generally, most characters will sit at one Defence, because that's the average for a 3 dice pool. <br /> <br /> My instincts (And the Trinity Core previews) make me think that Dodge should be <i>additional</i> Defence, rather than substituting for a base Defence, but that doesn't seem to be what's actually written here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T11:23:48-08:00","id":1182330,"title":"","content":"How does Visitation work for a Created Scion? I mean for example you have the Loki-Carved and Loki-Denying person they were discussing before, isn't she fully aware of her origin and parentage? Wouldn't that mean she's just Hero level immediately, or am I missing some important element of the Visitation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T14:47:57-08:00","id":1182393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1182234#post1182234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A quick mechanics question on the preview, regarding Defence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It looks like what should happen is the following. Someone declares an attack, and I roll Defence. If I roll 0 Successes, my Defence is 1 (I.e. this roll generates no successes, so base Difficulty is 1). If I roll 1 Success, my Defence is <i>still</i> one (Dodge generates 1 success which the opponent must overcome). If I roll 2 successes, my Defence becomes 2, etc.<br /> <br /> This means that, generally, most characters will sit at one Defence, because that's the average for a 3 dice pool.<br /> <br /> My instincts (And the Trinity Core previews) make me think that Dodge should be <i>additional</i> Defence, rather than substituting for a base Defence, but that doesn't seem to be what's actually written here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> but what's the Dodge roll? same as the standard defense one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T07:24:38-08:00","id":1182589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1182393#post1182393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> but what's the Dodge roll? same as the standard defense one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dodge is a Defensive Stunt, so you roll Defence and can then spend successes on dodging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T10:01:08-08:00","id":1182638,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar137_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"137\" data-vbnamecard=\"137\">Neall</a><br /> <br /> While looking at the supernatural paths for playing as mythological creatures and such (saytrs, amazons, kitsune) I noticed something very interesting that has some pretty heavy implications. A person who wants to play as a Satyr would start at legend 0 the same as anyone else. It says that when you reach legend 1 you gain hooves which now makes it clearly appear that you are not human. Other races have similar things saying that at legend 1 they get a defining aspect of the race they are. This creates a really interesting implication.<br /> <br /> Are all legend 0 mythological creatures essentially indistinguishable from mortals? As such, would a person choosing to play as an Ogre or a Troll simply be some big looking dude until they reach Legend 1 and then gain tusks or more pronounced features? Me and my buddy kinda love this concept but we are not sure how far we can really take it with assuming.<br /> <br /> For instance, what about Dragons and Centaurs? Are they human looking and gain scales (like D&amp;D dragon disciples) or become a quadruped? (although I guess hooves at legend 1 and the quadruped aspect coming at legend 2)<br /> <br /> The Kitsune section seems to imply that their base form is that of a fox entirely and they can become human with a knack. Without the knack they are confined to the fox form. This leads me to believe that even a legend 0 centaur would have the general form of a centaur. (but that clashes with Saytrs not even having hooves until legend 1)<br /> <br /> So basically I'm just wondering if this is the intent or not. I figured with this perspective any npc creatures u find in mythological locations already likely have the legend level associated with having their full and true form. In the case of a dragon this would be a much higher legend then say a Satyr. Which means if all the above is correct that means eventually the dragon player should have a base form that is entirely that of a dragon when they reach the appropriate legend.<br /> <br /> This reminds me of the surgeon guy from 1st edition. His early appearance was very human but when he reached god he looked very very different. (Even though he really wasn't a particular special race)<br /> <br /> I appreciate any insight that anyone else can give as well. I have not had a chance to read through all the lore in the book so this may have been explained and I missed it. If so, sorry! lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 02-05-2018, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T10:24:47-08:00","id":1182643,"title":"","content":"A skill based question. What skill would a performer (actor, Dancer, Singer) be most likely to have? Would it be Culture or something like Empathy or Persuasion. Or Athletics in the case of a dancer? While I like the broad skills it does leave some weird little grey areas like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T11:02:13-08:00","id":1182655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1182643#post1182643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A skill based question. What skill would a performer (actor, Dancer, Singer) be most likely to have? Would it be Culture or something like Empathy or Persuasion. Or Athletics in the case of a dancer? While I like the broad skills it does leave some weird little grey areas like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think any would be possible, based on the character build.<br /> <br /> With purely Athletics, observers would be conscious of the skill that the dancer showed.<br /> Culture would represent understanding the background of the dance.<br /> Empathy would represent a dancer who communicated feeling through dance (&quot;Her Odette (from <i>Swan Lake</i>) was so beautiful, and so sad!&quot;)<br /> Persuasion would represent a dancer who compelled people to act through dance (I'm picturing interpretive dance here).<br /> <br /> You could also flip the narrative in multiple ways, depending on Specialties.<br /> <br /> Athletics (Dance) could allow a Physical + Empathy roll in the Intrigue system, either alone, or to add Enhancements to someone with a high Presence score.<br /> Empathy (Dance) could allow a Social + Athletics roll for a Dive for Cover action (Usually Physical + Athletics), where the dive was so graceful it distracted the attacker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23791-ashnak","name":"Ashnak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T11:09:55-08:00","id":1182658,"title":"","content":"Is the Origin Core Rules download mentioned in the latest update the storypath core download from update #55? Or is there a download I missed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5727-racain23","name":"racain23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T11:33:18-08:00","id":1182666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>racain23</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1182658#post1182658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the Origin Core Rules download mentioned in the latest update the storypath core download from update #55? Or is there a download I missed?</div> </div> </div> </div>You missed it. Go to the Scion Backerkit page, then click on View Confirmation, then on Digital Downloads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T12:17:08-08:00","id":1182677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1182589#post1182589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dodge is a Defensive Stunt, so you roll Defence and can then spend successes on dodging.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seems tricky... say I get 4s. I can spend them all on the Dodge sunt and the oppenent only has to get 5 successes to beat my Dodge as I could have gone Full Defense stunt to maybe get more than 4s since I get two rolls... when do you decide to Dodge then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T12:34:11-08:00","id":1182680,"title":"","content":"Also, what skills (if any) do you use for crafting by the way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23677-the-eternal-keeper","name":"The Eternal Keeper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T13:02:31-08:00","id":1182685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Eternal Keeper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1182680#post1182680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, what skills (if any) do you use for crafting by the way?</div> </div> </div> </div>From what it looks like... It depends.<br /> <br /> Crafting isn't Exalted's system of &quot;Okay roll and get an improbable number of successes&quot;, it's more &quot;Get the stuff you need to MAKE it&quot;.<br /> <br /> Using my read of the system, it may be that there's like, an Athletics check to represent a day spent in your forge, perhaps you can use Culture or Persuasion to speak to a smith in order to get a design, perhaps you spend a scene getting the right ingredients (and may require Subterfuge to spot whether the guy is trying to sell crap steel to you).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T13:05:43-08:00","id":1182687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1182677#post1182677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Seems tricky... say I get 4s. I can spend them all on the Dodge sunt and the oppenent only has to get 5 successes to beat my Dodge as I could have gone Full Defense stunt to maybe get more than 4s since I get two rolls... when do you decide to Dodge then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Full defense costs your standard action for the round. So you can't use it if you already attacked, or can't attack if you use it and haven't gone yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T13:56:13-08:00","id":1182695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1182687#post1182687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Full defense costs your standard action for the round. So you can't use it if you already attacked, or can't attack if you use it and haven't gone yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>So why would you go Full Defense? If I get to roll my Defense every turn where I am attacked, wouldn't Full Defense be less useful?<br /> <br /> 4 person combat, I'm third, and I have Defense 4:<br /> <br /> Turn 1: [1 3 8 10] [9] = 3s<br /> Turn 2: [3 3 3 9] = 1s<br /> Turn 3 (Me): [2 2 3 7 7 8 9 9] = 3s<br /> Turn 4: I spend 3s<br /> <br /> I got just as much benefit to my defense on Turn 1 as I did from Turn 4. After that turn, I'm back to rolling Defense again.<br /> <br /> If FULL Defense gave me a static value until my next action, that would be helpful.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23791-ashnak","name":"Ashnak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T14:57:53-08:00","id":1182714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1182685#post1182685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what it looks like... It depends.<br /> <br /> Crafting isn't Exalted's system of &amp;quot;Okay roll and get an improbable number of successes&amp;quot;, it's more &amp;quot;Get the stuff you need to MAKE it&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Using my read of the system, it may be that there's like, an Athletics check to represent a day spent in your forge, perhaps you can use Culture or Persuasion to speak to a smith in order to get a design, perhaps you spend a scene getting the right ingredients (and may require Subterfuge to spot whether the guy is trying to sell crap steel to you).</div> </div> </div> </div>I expect we haven\u2019t seen full details on crafting yet since generally (especially at Origins level in a modern setting) mundane crafting isn\u2019t going to create much nuance in products\u2019 capabilities. The main distinction will just be artistry, but with modern tools, your mundane ability to craft a sword or build a gun isn\u2019t going to make a huge game relevant distinction in final product once you bring modern technology in production to bare.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER, once the Forge purview comes into play and we\u2019re talking about the power of magical products of crafting... that will be a whole other story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T16:26:57-08:00","id":1182743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashnak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1182695#post1182695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So why would you go Full Defense? If I get to roll my Defense every turn where I am attacked, wouldn't Full Defense be less useful?<br /> <br /> 4 person combat, I'm third, and I have Defense 4:<br /> <br /> Turn 1: [1 3 8 10] [9] = 3s<br /> Turn 2: [3 3 3 9] = 1s<br /> Turn 3 (Me): [2 2 3 7 7 8 9 9] = 3s<br /> Turn 4: I spend 3s<br /> <br /> I got just as much benefit to my defense on Turn 1 as I did from Turn 4. After that turn, I'm back to rolling Defense again.<br /> <br /> If FULL Defense gave me a static value until my next action, that would be helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>It says you only roll the first time you are attacked in a round. I would assume that means you set the value with that very first roll,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T23:50:11-08:00","id":1182827,"title":"","content":"Has it been said whether Demigod and God will have character creation rules for games starting at that level (either because the PCs, being born solely from divine parentage, start at a higher tier as brand new characters, or because you're playing with more developed characters with established backgrounds)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T01:32:41-08:00","id":1182831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1182666#post1182666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You missed it. Go to the Scion Backerkit page, then click on View Confirmation, then on Digital Downloads.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for that, got it now \ud83d\ude01","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5727-racain23","name":"racain23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T01:38:47-08:00","id":1182832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashnak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1182695#post1182695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If FULL Defense gave me a static value until my next action, that would be helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Full Defense says &quot;In place of Dodge, roll your Defense pool twice. Each success increases the Difficulty required to inflict Injury, or may be split among other Defensive Stunts (including any Defensive Stunts granted by Knacks or Boons). This is a simple action, and may not be part of a Mixed action.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> I think I understood the Stunt better by reading again. I think Full Defense will be the perfect Defense, hard to break through but while you Dodge, you can have a Mixed Action instead of Full Defense. So while Dodging, you may attack. I think this is interesting part. <br /> <br /> Did you read correctly?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T03:49:07-08:00","id":1182858,"title":"","content":"As much as I enjoyed reading the preview and am excited for the Hero text to drop, I can't help but think that a sample combat in the book that includes some of the atypical elements unique to Storypath (defending with different Attributes, how exactly damage works, difference between Dodge and Full Defense, etc...), would probably be a good idea to help clear up some of the confusion.<br /> <br /> Just my 2 cents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T04:01:34-08:00","id":1182862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1182827#post1182827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has it been said whether Demigod and God will have character creation rules for games starting at that level (either because the PCs, being born solely from divine parentage, start at a higher tier as brand new characters, or because you're playing with more developed characters with established backgrounds)?</div> </div> </div> </div>It has been said that being born from Divine parentage doesn't start you off at a higher tier: all Scions begin life as mortals, even the likes of Hermes and Thor; heck, even Athena. Then they become Heroes, Demigods, and finally Gods.<br /> <br /> I can't speak to starting out a game as a Demigod or God; but Onyx Path <i>does</i> have a history of assigning a pool of Experience for characters who don't start out at the beginning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T06:32:01-08:00","id":1182890,"title":"","content":"Will rules for larger scale combat be added in Hero where it's more appropriate? I think large scale combat rules will be crucial for portraying many mythological scenarios.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T07:27:50-08:00","id":1182911,"title":"","content":"EDIT: sorry everybody, I found the answer in another thread.<br /> <br /> Hi Neall, hi everybody,<br /> I have a quick question. I didn't find any answer to it in the pages of the thread.<br /> <br /> How are stealth actions handled? I failed to find a &quot;stealth skill&quot; or something similar.<br /> The closest element are ambushes, in which the entity ambushing rolls Athletics (the text says Agility, which somehow resounds with Athletics) + Dexterity, whereas the defender rolls Integrity + Cunning.<br /> By looking at this it seems that:<br /> 1. there should be no &quot;stealth&quot; (or similar) skill, and we should use athletics for these actions<br /> (2. there should be an &quot;integrity&quot; skill, which I also failed to find in the text)<br /> <br /> Am I correct? Am I missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7302,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7302-darknailo","user":"darknailo","date":".  found answer in another thread 02-06-2018, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7302-darknailo","name":"darknailo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T08:53:07-08:00","id":1182946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>darknailo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1182911#post1182911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: sorry everybody, I found the answer in another thread.<br /> <br /> Hi Neall, hi everybody,<br /> I have a quick question. I didn't find any answer to it in the pages of the thread.<br /> <br /> How are stealth actions handled? I failed to find a &quot;stealth skill&quot; or something similar.<br /> The closest element are ambushes, in which the entity ambushing rolls Athletics (the text says Agility, which somehow resounds with Athletics) + Dexterity, whereas the defender rolls Integrity + Cunning.<br /> By looking at this it seems that:<br /> 1. there should be no &quot;stealth&quot; (or similar) skill, and we should use athletics for these actions<br /> (2. there should be an &quot;integrity&quot; skill, which I also failed to find in the text)<br /> <br /> Am I correct? Am I missing something?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For Stealth, my go to would be using subterfuge, but in the physical arena instead of social.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T09:38:12-08:00","id":1182955,"title":"","content":"And as mentioned in other threads, a larger list of example weapons, and weapon tags would be great, for example a tag that increases the amount of damage dealt by the inflict damage stunt would be great, to make larger weapons like greatswords actually useful","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23677-the-eternal-keeper","name":"The Eternal Keeper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T10:00:42-08:00","id":1182967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1182832#post1182832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Full Defense says &quot;In place of Dodge, roll your Defense pool twice. Each success increases the Difficulty required to inflict Injury, or may be split among other Defensive Stunts (including any Defensive Stunts granted by Knacks or Boons). This is a simple action, and may not be part of a Mixed action.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> I think I understood the Stunt better by reading again. I think Full Defense will be the perfect Defense, hard to break through but while you Dodge, you can have a Mixed Action instead of Full Defense. So while Dodging, you may attack. I think this is interesting part.<br /> <br /> Did you read correctly?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think regular dodge is reflexive. But basically yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T13:57:21-08:00","id":1183035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1182743#post1182743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It says you only roll the first time you are attacked in a round. I would assume that means you set the value with that very first roll,</div> </div> </div> </div>In my copy of the PDF it says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scion:Origin Full Text Preview p. 132</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The target(s) declare the Defense action they wish to take, and roll for a Defensive action if it\u2019s their first time in the turn being attacked.</div> </div> </div> </div>First time in a <b>round</b> makes more sense. Did you see this elsewhere in the text?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23791-ashnak","name":"Ashnak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T14:07:16-08:00","id":1183038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashnak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1183035#post1183035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my copy of the PDF it says:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> First time in a <b>round</b> makes more sense. Did you see this elsewhere in the text?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they ever specify the turn vs round distinction so it's probably another case of a word slipping by unnoticed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T15:25:30-08:00","id":1183060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1182946#post1182946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> For Stealth, my go to would be using subterfuge, but in the physical arena instead of social.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Subterfuge is pretty explicitly the Stealth skill, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T17:31:18-08:00","id":1183104,"title":"","content":"Question: for supernatural paths that scale to higher legend tiers, does this just mean that they have higher tier knacks available to them? Like the Kitsune is supposed to scale up to Demigod level, does this mean there will simply be more choices for them at the higher tier or will there be unique mechanics we would need. I ask as I imagine that once the community content vault is out I could see a number of people building off these paths for various reasons and I wanted to know how difficult it would be (Some people in my group have expressed interest in a mythic fantasy setting so race design is a must)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T17:47:22-08:00","id":1183107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Eternal Keeper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1182955#post1182955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as mentioned in other threads, a larger list of example weapons, and weapon tags would be great, for example a tag that increases the amount of damage dealt by the inflict damage stunt would be great, to make larger weapons like greatswords actually useful</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems like it would be a slippery slope without some sort of mitigating factor, especially since I imagine Relics would allow for that via Enhancement, which could be spent on the Inflict Damage and Critical Hit stunts.<br /> <br /> But a mundane Greatsword (other than the one in the book) seems to me like it would be Lethal, Melee, Two-Handed, Unconcealable (like the book), but also would have Piercing, Arcing, and maybe even Reach, giving it a total of 1 or 2, instead of -2. And now you have a giant sword that cleaves through cover, rips through armor, and can hit people that are farther away. Seems like a happy middle ground","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T06:26:09-08:00","id":1183237,"title":"","content":"Assuming a ST allows all their players to sort of build their own weapons at creation with a point total rather than using the examples in the book then as long as the damage increasing tags are appropriately balanced in cost then there wouldn't be any slippery slope to comment on. Each person would have equal values in tags.<br /> <br /> As much as I have pointed out errors and made my opinions known on the Scion text the biggest thing I just think this book needs is more examples. More examples of weapons (like unarmed), armor, tags, combat, and everything really. Examples clarify things and help people understand how to build their own custom content. I guess ultimately the companion book is going to help coming up with more content but I still feel a couple more examples could be helpful. They also need to look over the current examples they give such as the example characters and make sure they are correct. The current example characters have varying point totals and whatnot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T13:11:24-08:00","id":1184854,"title":"","content":"I'm a little confused about supernatural paths, are they also a calling as well? <br /> <br /> I was under the impression that origins would be the stand-alone game, but there are a lot of references to &quot;see Hero.&quot; Will that stay the same in the final copy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5727-racain23","name":"racain23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T13:17:10-08:00","id":1184859,"title":"","content":"Given that these are the base rules for the whole engine those may just be there to not forcibly repeat whole passages in the companion book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T15:10:35-08:00","id":1184907,"title":"","content":"How would you make a feint?? how should work??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T01:57:00-08:00","id":1185521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1184907#post1184907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you make a feint?? how should work??</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bMy guess would be as a standard Close Combat check, using Cunning or Manipulation in place of a physical stat. If you get a success over their defense and use it to inflict injury, that means the feint worked and you tricked them into opening their guard so you could strike. If you get more successes and impose a Complication (or was it Difficulty? I'm not clear on the difference) then the feint left them off-balance for a future attack by you or an ally. <br /> <br /> \u200bDoes that sound right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T21:53:31-08:00","id":1186175,"title":"","content":"Is Scion Hero being fast-tracked the way Scion Origin was? That is, can we expect to see the text of Hero as soon as it's in halfway decent shape, or do we wait until layout, graphics, etc. are done and the book is ready for the regular troubleshooting release?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T23:15:53-08:00","id":1186190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1186175#post1186175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Scion Hero being fast-tracked the way Scion Origin was? That is, can we expect to see the text of Hero as soon as it's in halfway decent shape, or do we wait until layout, graphics, etc. are done and the book is ready for the regular troubleshooting release?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Neall said that he'll get the Pre-Layout Raws to the backers/pre-order folks, like with Origin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T23:37:59-08:00","id":1186196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1186175#post1186175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Scion Hero being fast-tracked the way Scion Origin was? That is, can we expect to see the text of Hero as soon as it's in halfway decent shape, or do we wait until layout, graphics, etc. are done and the book is ready for the regular troubleshooting release?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's being fast-tracked; as per the last KS update, Neall wanted it out to backers before end of this month.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T15:59:09-08:00","id":1186454,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing Neall is taking longer in his dev pass for hero then he did with origins because he wants to avoid the sorts of mistakes and flaws that people pointed out when that manuscript came out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T16:25:44-08:00","id":1186467,"title":"","content":"Yep. I hope to have it out by the end of the month.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T16:50:57-08:00","id":1186477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1177881#post1177881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not <i>hard </i>for a Creator or Forge/Wild/Health deity to create life, depending on what that life is. Yes, there are different ways, but they generally have to conform to the PSP motif.<br /> <br /> You'll note that a great many mythologies have the Gods creating humanity. This is neither an irreproducible nor particularly impossible act. The Created Scion is proof of that. One of our 2e signature characters was carved from a living ash tree by Loki themself, which conforms to Ask and Embla's creation by the Norse.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> One of our demigod antagonists, Ixion, created the centaurs - and continues to do so, except with motorcycles instead of horses. There's a lot of little details that go into it, but creation of life is definitely possible, and you're sort of responsible for the behavior of that life by popular acclaim.</div> </div> </div> </div>What exacty does a god need to do to Create A Scion? What does it take to make your creation have the potential to become a god too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T13:14:31-08:00","id":1187628,"title":"","content":"Neal I've got a question about loki: I read he has epic STRENGTH? Is that correct or a typo? (can't phathom loki having strength over mental epics)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T13:25:38-08:00","id":1187629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1187628#post1187628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neal I've got a question about loki: I read he has epic STRENGTH? Is that correct or a typo? (can't phathom loki having strength over mental epics)</div> </div> </div> </div>Loki is a full blooded giant and wrestles Heimdall to a standstill during the Last Battle. The idea that Loki is slim and effete is not really in line with mythology (though I <i>am</i> a big fan of Tom Hiddleston) where he quite literally a giant who is entirely capable of matching, if not overcoming people with physical might.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T13:50:36-08:00","id":1187635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1187628#post1187628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neal I've got a question about loki: I read he has epic STRENGTH? Is that correct or a typo? (can't phathom loki having strength over mental epics)</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, non-physical epics are no longer a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T14:04:24-08:00","id":1187640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ffanxii4ever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1187635#post1187635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, non-physical epics are no longer a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I imagine they're being folded into other Purviews and Callings. Like a lot of the tricks of Epic Manipulation will probably be in the Trickster Knacks and the Deception Purview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar"