"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T23:19:54-08:00","id":1187760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1187629#post1187629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Loki is a full blooded giant and wrestles Heimdall to a standstill during the Last Battle. The idea that Loki is slim and effete is not really in line with mythology (though I <i>am</i> a big fan of Tom Hiddleston) where he quite literally a giant who is entirely capable of matching, if not overcoming people with physical might.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know they kill each other but where is it said they wrestle to a standstill? And Loki might be a giant but Norse myth seem to have giants that range from maybe a few inches taller than most Aesir all the way up to the ground shakes when it walks and it's glove can be mistaken for a building. Loki seems to be on the smaller end of the scale. I doubt he's a noodle armed wimp but epic strength might be going too far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T07:37:35-08:00","id":1187833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div cla