submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T11:37:41-08:00","id":1187920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1187898#post1187898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To nitpick: Epic Appearance kinda-sorta lives on as the Beauty Purview.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Should we assume that Aphrodite has said purview, despite not having it listed in the Origins preview?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T12:35:56-08:00","id":1187939,"title":"","content":"I hope they go over all the gods/goddesses again before release and make sure everything is right in terms of callings and purviews. Seems things changed a little here and there with them and it would really suck to have omissions or old data that makes it look confusing or unfitting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T14:33:22-08:00","id":1187977,"title":"","content":"Copying my question from the other thread : So, in light of the Crafting Rules, does the Celestial Artifice Boon in the earlier previewed Forge Purview make it possible for Heroes to create Tier 3 Items (by bringing the project down to Tier 2) or does it just mean that Heroes can build Tier 2 Items with the ease of Tier 1, and you still can't create Items that would be naturally out of your reach?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T16:14:13-08:00","id":1188009,"title":"","content":"One more question, sorry. Reading the Eddas and there's this line at one point &quot;The prophetess Sybil; that we know as Sif&quot; And that Thor took her for a wife, so definitely the deity. Shouldn't she have the fortune purview? It seems they reference her prophecy quite a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T16:43:52-08:00","id":1188018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1188009#post1188009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One more question, sorry. Reading the Eddas and there's this line at one point &quot;The prophetess Sybil; that we know as Sif&quot; And that Thor took her for a wife, so definitely the deity. Shouldn't she have the fortune purview? It seems they reference her prophecy quite a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wouldn't use what foreign mythic figures they're casually conflated with as a guide to any deity's purviews. That road leads to madness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T17:07:12-08:00","id":1188024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1188018#post1188018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I wouldn't use what foreign mythic figures they're casually conflated with as a guide to any deity's purviews. That road leads to madness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, but since the name does come up often in the explanation from high, higher, and most high I figured it was an actual part of the religion. It seemed like it wasn\u2019t a foreign figure the way it was worded. And hell, it is at least as good explanation as historians going \u201cWell gold hair must mean grain!\u201d giving her fertility.<br /> <br /> Lucky Theoi having most of their documents preserved. My favorite three of the officaial ones are teotl, Aesir, and Tuatha and they were all either oral tradition or mostly wiped out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T18:20:26-08:00","id":1188044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1187898#post1187898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To nitpick: Epic Appearance kinda-sorta lives on as the Beauty Purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T17:58:00-08:00","id":1188357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1188024#post1188024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair enough, but since the name does come up often in the explanation from high, higher, and most high I figured it was an actual part of the religion. It seemed like it wasn\u2019t a foreign figure the way it was worded. And hell, it is at least as good explanation as historians going \u201cWell gold hair must mean grain!\u201d giving her fertility.<br /> <br /> Lucky Theoi having most of their documents preserved. My favorite three of the officaial ones are teotl, Aesir, and Tuatha and they were all either oral tradition or mostly wiped out.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not that having all the documents help if the culture kept changing things. The egyptian pantheon looks like a comic book continuity","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T19:14:50-08:00","id":1188371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1187977#post1187977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Copying my question from the other thread : So, in light of the Crafting Rules, does the Celestial Artifice Boon in the earlier previewed Forge Purview make it possible for Heroes to create Tier 3 Items (by bringing the project down to Tier 2) or does it just mean that Heroes can build Tier 2 Items with the ease of Tier 1, and you still can't create Items that would be naturally out of your reach?</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter. But good clarification!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T19:15:22-08:00","id":1188372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1187939#post1187939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope they go over all the gods/goddesses again before release and make sure everything is right in terms of callings and purviews. Seems things changed a little here and there with them and it would really suck to have omissions or old data that makes it look confusing or unfitting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, we are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T21:27:20-08:00","id":1188404,"title":"","content":"How long are Knacks supposed to last if they don\u2019t list a duration (Like Cloak of Dread from the Leader Calling)? A scene?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T21:56:11-08:00","id":1188405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1188372#post1188372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, we are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, thats good to hear. Looking forward to seeing all the clarifications in the next draft. <br /> <br /> Also, someone noticed in another thread that there isn't a section in the book detailing a description of each attribute and what 1, 3, and 5 dots mean. (Similar to skills) Will a section like that be added?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 02-22-2018, 12:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T04:37:04-08:00","id":1188462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1188405#post1188405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Awesome, thats good to hear. Looking forward to seeing all the clarifications in the next draft. <br /> <br /> Also, someone noticed in another thread that there isn't a section in the book detailing a description of each attribute and what 1, 3, and 5 dots mean. (Similar to skills) Will a section like that be added?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. That was deliberate. <br /> <br /> When designing the the system I explicitly wanted to get away from Attributes as representing definitive performance benchmarks in a person. Unlike Skills, they don\u2019t have other mechanics keyed to their ratings. <br /> <br /> Storypath isn\u2019t Storyteller or Storytelling, but I\u2019m surprising none if I say many of our design principles were the same. One of the more eye-rolling things I\u2019d see is an insistence that Dexterity 3 meant far less than Dexterity 5, despite it ultimately meaning the loss of two dice - yet one\u2019s supposed to be \u201cI do yoga\u201d versus \u201cI\u2019m an Olympic gymnast\u201d. Storypath does away with that and leaves finer points for your Paths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 02-22-2018, 07:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T05:31:02-08:00","id":1188468,"title":"","content":"Why not a paragraph of clarifying description on what the attributes represent then without the benchmark comparisons? I still feel like those would be decent for new GMs. I recall my first time running games, sometimes you need all the hand holding and explicit text helping you out that you can get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T06:30:06-08:00","id":1188482,"title":"","content":"Yea, a small section just detailing their descriptions would be great to make scion feels like it stands on it's own and doesn't need knowledge of previous systems.<br /> <br /> Haven't played a storyteller system for a couple months and while making my buddie's origin level character he asked me what presence was used for. Basing it off what I saw in the Scion Origins book specifically I answered &quot;Its your Social Power&quot;. Although looking back I guess the better answer is that its how you approach a social situation in a powerful and direct manner. Technically Manipulation is just as much Social Power as Presence and it all comes down to the players approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T06:54:25-08:00","id":1188494,"title":"","content":"Saying \u201cSocial Power\u201d is legit, but I take your point. I\u2019ll see what I can do!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T07:07:55-08:00","id":1188498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1188494#post1188494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying \u201cSocial Power\u201d is legit, but I take your point. I\u2019ll see what I can do!</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome. Great to have you answering questions more frequently at the moment.<br /> <br /> Utilizing this opportunity... defense is at base 1 and any successes add to that, correct? Rolling 1 Success would then end up as 2 defense instead of 1, right? The details in dodge makes it seems like the base defense is only ever 1 if they roll zero successes which would mean a single success doesn't yield any additional benefit. Trying hard not to be the guy that always compares things to Trinity... but it specifies that base defense is 1 and successes used for the dodge stunt increase your defense by 1 per success. Just wondering if this is a intentional design decision to generally make defense 1 lower in Scion or if its just a product of the rough draft side of things. Adding successes to a base 1 just feels better. Makes it to where a single success doesn't feel somewhat pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T13:47:32-08:00","id":1188646,"title":"","content":"So, I saw a bit further back that most Scions are the kids of Incarnations of the god in question, since obviously most deities don't want to risk going all Ark of the Covenant on people just to have a roll in the hay with a mortal.<br /> <br /> So is there a limitation to the number of Incarnations or risk from having too many for a given god? Most of the example Scions present a pretty formula result of the kids not being aware they're the result of divine parentage until their Visitation. They might have hints here and there that they're a little above the average guy, but it seems like most of the gods stay out of their lives until That Moment.<br /> <br /> This makes more sense if each god was some kind of monolithic progenitor for any Scions trailing back to him, like the 1E bloodline concept. But is there anything that prevents a god from, say, spinning off an Incarnation to look after their lover and kid rather than just remaining aloof and far off until Fate conspires to bring it out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","name":"OpMegs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1817_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T15:07:22-08:00","id":1188675,"title":"","content":"And another consideration - do Gods have more Scions than Goddesses, simply because it is technically easier for males to have more offspring in the same amount of time? Or is there the assumption that divine beings are pregnant for as much or as little time as they want?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T11:52:41-08:00","id":1188952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1188372#post1188372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, we are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Referencing back to the whole looking over the purviews and callings of each Diety. Just noticed that Freyr, God of Fertility and Prosperity, is oddly missing the Prosperity purview. Just thought that was a little funny and figured I should point that out.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually it seems that several have fairly small purview lists comparatively to other deities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 02-23-2018, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T13:35:03-08:00","id":1188978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1188952#post1188952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Referencing back to the whole looking over the purviews and callings of each Diety. Just noticed that Freyr, God of Fertility and Prosperity, is oddly missing the Prosperity purview. Just thought that was a little funny and figured I should point that out.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually it seems that several have fairly small purview lists comparatively to other deities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope the second pass also gives Freyja the Beauty purview. Because IIRC, Freyja was literally the prettiest goddess of the Aesir and pretty much everybody wanted her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T13:36:59-08:00","id":1188980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1188952#post1188952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Referencing back to the whole looking over the purviews and callings of each Diety. Just noticed that Freyr, God of Fertility and Prosperity, is oddly missing the Prosperity purview. Just thought that was a little funny and figured I should point that out.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually it seems that several have fairly small purview lists comparatively to other deities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blame the Eddas, not me. That said there are mechanical benefits to only having a few Purviews. Note that Titans only have one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T13:47:24-08:00","id":1188986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1188980#post1188980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blame the Eddas, not me. That said there are mechanical benefits to only having a few Purviews. Note that Titans only have one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jack of All Trades versus Hyperspecialization?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T13:59:41-08:00","id":1188998,"title":"","content":"Well, I found the answer to my previous question in the Trinity backer previews (don't worry, I'm a backer). Turns out, shields are modeled in this system by giving a weapon the &quot;Shield&quot; tag. So, you can totally do the Captain America thing of having a shield that is also a weapon.<br /> <br /> This does make me wonder how many mechanical difference there are between Scion and Trinity, though...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T16:12:22-08:00","id":1189035,"title":"","content":"Sooo...<br /> <br /> Say as a deity, it was a long-term project of mine to give humans access to psychic powers. How would I go about that, what Purviews would I need, and can Purviews be re-skinned to act like psychic abilities? To clarify, I might drift my first scion game into a fantasy setting. But I could see giving everyone psychic abilities (and all the accompanying headaches) as a suitable legendary quest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T17:31:07-08:00","id":1189051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1188980#post1188980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blame the Eddas, not me. That said there are mechanical benefits to only having a few Purviews. Note that Titans only have one.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Looks up Eddas* Still confused. Not sure if I'm missing a reference/nickname here or if it's my mythology noobness showing.<br /> <br /> Honestly, there is no reason for blame provided a pass over these dieties happens and things get properly represented by release. It makes sense though that it needs a final overpass based purely by the fact they were in development at the same exact time the actual purviews/systems were under development.<br /> <br /> But yea, looking forward to seeing how this all comes together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T18:12:43-08:00","id":1189066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1187760#post1187760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know they kill each other but where is it said they wrestle to a standstill? And Loki might be a giant but Norse myth seem to have giants that range from maybe a few inches taller than most Aesir all the way up to the ground shakes when it walks and it's glove can be mistaken for a building. Loki seems to be on the smaller end of the scale. I doubt he's a noodle armed wimp but epic strength might be going too far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for taking so long to respond to this, it's been a really busy weak. By &quot;Wrestle to a Standstill,&quot; I meant that they were a match for each other, and neither could overcome the other. However! Upon going and double checking the Prose Edda (Gylfanginning) I'm totally wrong about it having been a wrestling match. I have no idea where I got the wrestling scene in my head, I don't think any other saga gives the scene in more detail either. I think it might be something that Gotham By Night mentioned way back, but I honestly have no idea. You're totally right Vonpenguin!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1189051#post1189051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Looks up Eddas* Still confused. Not sure if I'm missing a reference/nickname here or if it's my mythology noobness showing.<br /> <br /> Honestly, there is no reason for blame provided a pass over these dieties happens and things get properly represented by release. It makes sense though that it needs a final overpass based purely by the fact they were in development at the same exact time the actual purviews/systems were under development.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Eddas are not my thing as just evidenced here, but do you know where Freyr's prosperity function is actually stated? Neall might mean that the prosperity function of Freyr isn't attested strongly enough in the Eddas to give it to him. <br /> <br /> For example, if someone asked me why Lug doesn't have Sun (I promise I'm actually better at the Irish Sagas than the Norse Eddas), I could say &quot;Blame the Sagas,&quot; since the Sun thing isn't actually attested there. It's just something that people sort of decided in the 19th-20th century and got stuck in pop culture for a bit and doesn't have a basis in the actual mythology.<br /> <br /> And also, it's impossible for the Pantheons to fit everyone's idea of what the Deities are. It's impossible for these to be perfect, because there is no perfect here. I would draw different conclusions for the Tuatha D\u00e9 Danann than other people would, a lot of these things are still really up in the air in the actual study of these things. Like, two years ago someone got around to doing a study of Mars in the Imperial Period and noted that he loses like all of his Agricultural and Guardian functions around the first century BCE for example. And then there's &quot;The Bar,&quot; for what counts as an association. Where I might not think Zeus deserves Beast (Wolf) because of his Lyceus Epithet and Cult, but someone else might think that's totally enough reason to give him sed Purview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T18:24:32-08:00","id":1189073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1189066#post1189066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry for taking so long to respond to this, it's been a really busy weak. By &quot;Wrestle to a Standstill,&quot; I meant that they were a match for each other, and neither could overcome the other. However! Upon going and double checking the Prose Edda (Gylfanginning) I'm totally wrong about it having been a wrestling match. I have no idea where I got the wrestling scene in my head, I don't think any other saga gives the scene in more detail either. I think it might be something that Gotham By Night mentioned way back, but I honestly have no idea. You're totally right Vonpenguin!<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair there is one other time they fight after shapeshifting into seals. I can't recall the reason or outcome but they are definitely a martial match for each other. And you can't even assume that Loki tricks Heimdall at Ragnorok because i imagine that a trickster god and a god who's biggest thing is being the closest Aesir to omniscient without a magic chair involved naturaly cancel each other out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T18:35:22-08:00","id":1189074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1189073#post1189073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair there is one other time they fight after shapeshifting into seals. I can't recall the reason or outcome but they are definitely a martial match for each other. And you can't even assume that Loki tricks Heimdall at Ragnorok because i imagine that a trickster god and a god who's biggest thing is being the closest Aesir to omniscient without a magic chair involved naturaly cancel each other out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it is there, this is going to be one of those things that will annoy me until I go find it, or find out why I got that stuck in my head for some reason. I think you're totally right that it isn't a clash of trickery though, the pair of them effectively cancel each other out. It would just become a slow grind.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T18:54:54-08:00","id":1189079,"title":"","content":"I haven't had much time to read the whole preview through, only bits and pieces. From what I can see though, mook antagonists are designed to only be fought in small groups, like a group of five. Does Origins assume characters at this level won't be going against companies of fifty or a hundred mooks at once?<br /> <br /> I can see the logic of it, what with PCs at this level being Action Heroes, but still Mortal. Saving the army breaking for Hero or Demigod?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T19:02:03-08:00","id":1189083,"title":"","content":"I think that's where Scale comes in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T19:41:39-08:00","id":1189087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1189083#post1189083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's where Scale comes in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possible, but what I mean is what if you have ten mooks who are identical? Are they tracked separately or as one group? Do their stats change if they're in a group? Do they roll initiative separately, and take separate attacks? Do they &quot;count as&quot; one mook antagonist, but go up in scale to represent greater numbers?<br /> <br /> Edit: Examining the Antagonists chapter reveals an antagonist ability allowing an opponent to summon a number of mooks equal to the number of PCs present. So Origins seems to assume the players will be fighting no more than say, ten enemies at most in one engagement; not too many for a Storyguide to track individually. I will hold off future questions until I've actually read the whole manuscript through.<br /> <br /> Edit 2: By the way, this game is firin' up my imagination, Neall. Great work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 02-23-2018, 11:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T02:25:56-08:00","id":1189161,"title":"","content":"I was purely going off the fact that the book literally refers to him as &quot;Freyr, God of Fertility and Prosperity&quot; and prosperity isn't a thing in the list. Wasn't coming from any mythological stance.<br /> <br /> Also, just wanted to requote my previous message because it seems like a odd difference to have between the two games.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1188498#post1188498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Awesome. Great to have you answering questions more frequently at the moment.<br /> <br /> Utilizing this opportunity... defense is at base 1 and any successes add to that, correct? Rolling 1 Success would then end up as 2 defense instead of 1, right? The details in dodge makes it seems like the base defense is only ever 1 if they roll zero successes which would mean a single success doesn't yield any additional benefit. Trying hard not to be the guy that always compares things to Trinity... but it specifies that base defense is 1 and successes used for the dodge stunt increase your defense by 1 per success. Just wondering if this is a intentional design decision to generally make defense 1 lower in Scion or if its just a product of the rough draft side of things. Adding successes to a base 1 just feels better. Makes it to where a single success doesn't feel somewhat pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, I do really want to know if mass combat is coming in hero as well. Large scale combat resolution is important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 02-24-2018, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T10:35:18-08:00","id":1189624,"title":"","content":"For an Alchemist type character, one that creates potions and tinctures and the like, would their craft be benefited by Forge or Artistry?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T12:40:21-08:00","id":1189662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1189624#post1189624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For an Alchemist type character, one that creates potions and tinctures and the like, would their craft be benefited by Forge or Artistry?</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds more like you'd want a Motif for that, to be able to do marvels in many purviews with it or just apply a mechanical justification onto fluff you do when activating your boons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T10:11:26-08:00","id":1189915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1189662#post1189662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds more like you'd want a Motif for that, to be able to do marvels in many purviews with it or just apply a mechanical justification onto fluff you do when activating your boons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point, I hadn't thought of Motifs, though I was thinking more along the lines of, instead of building a sword that cleaves through spirits (the sample suggested Tier 2 Project) my character might develop an oil coating that can be applied to any sword to let it do the same. I think I'll reserve judgement on exact;y what kind of route he takes until after I've seen all the potential Powers in Hero once that is previewed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T15:01:51-08:00","id":1190017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1189915#post1189915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Point, I hadn't thought of Motifs, though I was thinking more along the lines of, instead of building a sword that cleaves through spirits (the sample suggested Tier 2 Project) my character might develop an oil coating that can be applied to any sword to let it do the same. I think I'll reserve judgement on exact;y what kind of route he takes until after I've seen all the potential Powers in Hero once that is previewed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would assume forge under the general concept of Forge=functional Artistry=pleasing/emotional/expressive. Now if you wanted a potion to also be delicious you might want to mix some artistry in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T05:21:43-08:00","id":1190210,"title":"","content":"So Neall is the end of the month goal for Hero still on the books?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T14:05:23-08:00","id":1190781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1190210#post1190210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Neall is the end of the month goal for Hero still on the books?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is something I am wondering about too. <br /> <br /> Also Yig is got me thinking about mass combat rules too.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T20:48:05-08:00","id":1190899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1190210#post1190210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Neall is the end of the month goal for Hero still on the books?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bLooks like it didn't happen. I'm not upset about that, personally. I'm excited for it, but he's said they're going through it more carefully this time so there aren't a bunch of odd, mismatched segments like with Origins. That's good. I certainly want the PDF, but I also want it to be done right, and that can take a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T05:28:01-08:00","id":1190950,"title":"","content":"The only thing that even hints at mass combat in the book is scale. It mentions apply scale if fighting a room of nameless mooks but the issue with this is it doesn't really tell us how. I assume you give scale advantage to the player when they are attacking and maybe scale advantage to the group when attacking if you want to avoid having to roll 5-6 attacks. I mean, even if mass combat isn't included, using scale in this way seems like it will help. If the group of enemies are not weaklings then only they would get scale on their attacks while you would still need to damage them normally. You could also apply the mook rule to the group even if they are not mooks. (ie, if you kill or cause damage to one of them then you can just turn the rest of your dice pool into 1 damage per success and drain their group health. Which would be their health multiplied by the number of enemies in the group) Honestly though, the mook rule kinda feels awkward when they are not actually 1hp mooks because the key benefit of it is that you dont need to beat the defense of the targets after the first. Technically due to mixed actions every character can declare attacking multiple targets and then spread their successes out to let their damage spread over to their next target but the key thing is you need to buy off each enemy's defense separately. With mooks, and I'd assume groups of identical enemies you probably shouldn't have to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 03-02-2018, 09:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T06:30:04-08:00","id":1190960,"title":"","content":"If the army is big enough you can probably justify applying Scale to the army","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T03:28:57-07:00","id":1194783,"title":"","content":"Any news on the Hero text?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T04:14:24-07:00","id":1194789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_duck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1194783#post1194783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any news on the Hero text?</div> </div> </div> </div>It should pop out on Backerkit soonish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T04:24:07-07:00","id":1194791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1194789#post1194789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should pop out on Backerkit soonish.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Great news, thanks for the timely response!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T10:58:00-07:00","id":1194894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1194789#post1194789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should pop out on Backerkit soonish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Soonish = right now, BTW. I've downloaded it and will begin reading shortly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T11:21:49-07:00","id":1194906,"title":"","content":"neall pls no<br /> <br /> i have so much work to do<br /> <br /> and im already procrastinating three different ways<br /> <br /> i cant handle four different ways of procrastinating at the same time","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T12:23:13-07:00","id":1194926,"title":"","content":"Will Prophets, Oracles, and Cassandras be in the Companion? Are there any immortal saint knacks?<br /> Edit:<br /> \u200bThere also doesn't appear to be any rules for how the virtue track works, though I'm assuming you can just use the Origin stuff for saint more or less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2472,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2472-trebius","user":"trebius","date":". 03-14-2018, 12:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2472-trebius","name":"trebius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T12:25:51-07:00","id":1194928,"title":"","content":"I was just going to ask the same thing. The previews mention them but no entries seem to exist in either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T02:18:30-07:00","id":1195189,"title":"","content":"Anyone know where exactly the feat of scale rules are?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T05:09:13-07:00","id":1195229,"title":"","content":"There seems to be some kind of confusion as to how many dots of callings (and thus knacks) you start with, as well as boons.<br /> <br /> The actual character creation rules suggest 4 dots of callings, 2/1/1, while everywhere else suggests 5, (2/2/1, or maybe even 3/1/1)<br /> <br /> Boons, similarly,--<br /> --I think it's likely to be &quot;two boons&quot;.<br /> <br /> That said, the legend rules suggest that you have 1-boon per dot of legend.<br /> <br /> Period.<br /> <br /> There isn't even a way to get extra boons with XP, as far as I can tell from a quick readthrough, so... yeah.<br /> <br /> &lt;.&lt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T08:21:25-07:00","id":1195301,"title":"","content":"Im fairly confused on path/asset skills and what their purpose is. In a old preview or statement (can't remember where I read this) you were forced to pick one of your Pantheon's Asset Skills as part of your Society Path but otherwise they seemed to do nothing. This seems to have changed, which is fine, but now things seem confusing.<br /> <br /> In the origins preview on page 204 it refers to path skills and says the below examples give 2 out of the 3 skills associated with that pantheon. Going over to the Hero book we now see that only a single Pantheon has 3 asset skills and the rest only have two. Norse don't even have theirs listed.<br /> <br /> At no point is there even a single section that directly states what Asset Skills actually do. The guide section of Hero implies they normally grant +1 to a scion but instead asset skills for a guide simply determine what rolls you can use their unique stunt with. On page 236 of the Hero guide it begins the explination of asset skills by saying &quot;As path asset skills&quot; which implies that perhaps Asset Skills are identical to Path skills in that the +1 granted that they are referring to is literally just the general bonus of +1 to +3 you get when you rank your paths primary secondary and tertiary. This would mean that asset skills are practically just suggestions (except in the case of guides) of which skills you may want to include in your paths that are fitting to that pantheon or supernatural path and otherwise don't have any mechanical benefit.<br /> <br /> So at the end of the day we seem to have 3 different ways asset skills can be interpreted.<br /> <br /> 1. They are skills you have to take within your paths<br /> 2. They grant you a bonus +1 enhancement for free simply for being associated with that pantheon or being a particular supernatural entity.<br /> 3. They are merely suggestions to help you make your character more thematically connected to their pantheon or supernatural path.<br /> <br /> Neither of the 3 above answer the confusing issue with page 204 in origins though in clearing up if a Pantheon/Supernatural path should have 2 or 3 asset skills.<br /> <br /> Whichever way they work is obviously fine, I was just wondering if you could give some insight into how they are supposed to work as this does impact situations with our testing at the moment. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T09:55:55-07:00","id":1195343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trebius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1194926#post1194926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will Prophets, Oracles, and Cassandras be in the Companion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Neall answered this on another thread and provided the Prophets and Cassandras writeup (I don't think Oracles are a separate thing).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero?p=1195198#post1195198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is my fault for not double-checking the file I was using. The Prophet Paths will go into the final book.<br /> <br /> New Paths<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/#_msocom_1\" target=\"_blank\">[NP1]</a><br /> Mortals cannot help but be puppets of Fate, but a rare few are able to see the strings. Lacking the full power of Scions or other creatures of Myth, they are nonetheless a cut above ordinary, ignorant mortals\u2014at least insofar as their ability to get themselves into trouble is concerned. They are <b>Prophets</b> when their abilities manifest as a gift, or <b>Cassandras </b>when it appears as a curse. Though seldom the heroes of their own sagas, they often appear as Guides or Companions to Scions, operating on the principle that, if one can see the horrible monsters that lurk in the shadows of the World, one should make friends with someone capable of fighting them at one\u2019s earliest opportunity.<br /> <br /> <b>Prophet</b><br /> Whether \u201cblessed\u201d by a God or born under a Fateful signifier (being born with a caul or with one or more teeth are common marks of a Prophet), the Prophet sees the skein of Fate laid out before him and reads it like a book. It\u2019s not the ability to see the future, precisely; rather, it\u2019s the ability to understand the weird narrative logic that Fate operates under, to recognize symbolically-relevant details, and thereby get a sense of where events are heading. Just like a student of cinematography can tell which elements in a shot are important by the composition and lighting or a student of theater can predict the course of events in a play thanks to her understanding of dramaturgical archetypes, a Prophet can glimpse, however briefly or incompletely, the courses Fate sets in motion.<br /> <b>Path Effect</b><br /> Prophets can automatically recognize creatures of Myth and those touched by Fate, including but not limited to Scions, manifest Gods, Titanspawn, and Fatebound mortals. They can likewise recognize portals to Terra Incognita, Underworlds and Overworlds. This Effect requires no roll (and indeed, Prophets are incapable of turning it off), but it is defeated by Knacks or similar powers that conceal the subject\u2019s mystical nature.<br /> <br /> <b>Knacks</b><br /> \u2022 <b>Glimpses Forward:</b> A Prophet can learn to read the symbolism Fate spins into the world, assembling cues and signifiers to glean an understanding of the future Fate holds. Once per session, the Prophet may ask one of the following questions about a particular topic (an individual, group, or course of action, for example):<br /> \u2022 <i>What is the greatest peril the subject faces?</i><br /> <i>\u2022 What must be done to ensure the subject does not come to disaster?</i><br /> <i>\u2022 What must never come to pass, if the subject is to prosper?</i><br /> <i>\u2022 How will the subject change the World, in ways great or small?</i><br /> \u2022 <b>Obnoxiously Prepared:</b> Once per session, the Prophet can remove all complications from a single action by retroactively having the foresight to prepare just the right tool, circumstances, etc.<br /> \u2022 <b>As the Prophecy Foretold: </b>Once per session, the Prophet can declare that events happening in-game match a previously-made prediction and completely refill the Momentum pool.<br /> \u2022 <b>Inauspicious Signs:</b> Once per session, the Prophet may remove up to 5 dice from the red Momentum pool, and half that amount (rounded up) from the black pool.<br /> <br /> <b>Cassandra</b><br /> Named for the figure in Greek mythology (though gods of nearly every Pantheon have created them), Cassandras are a special kind of Prophet cursed by the gods to speak absolute truth, but to never be believed by those who hear their prophecies. Where Prophets understand the structures of Fate and thus glimpse what <i>must</i> happen next, Cassandras see how the World flows within those structures, understanding what <i>is happening</i>. Theirs is a more immediate gift of prophecy, but no less useful\u2014the problem is getting other people to act on it.<br /> Cassandras often find themselves pulled into the orbit of Scions for the simple fact that those of divine blood are immune to the curse. They make excellent Guides, and are often fiercely loyal to those rare few people who believe them.<br /> <b>Path Effect</b><br /> Once per session, the Storyguide tells the Cassandra the absolute truth of a situation. This includes, but isn\u2019t limited to, the agendas of those present, anything concealed or hidden nearby, and the immediate outcome of whatever is happening around her. This gift doesn\u2019t extend to anything outside the Cassandra\u2019s immediate vicinity.<br /> <br /> <i>Example: The original Cassandra, for whom this Path is named, saw the Greek army bring the Trojan Horse to the gates of Troy as a \u201cpeace offering.\u201d This triggered her Path effect, making her immediately aware that the Greeks were not seeking peace and that many soldiers were hiding within the Horse. As the Trojans brought the Horse into the city, she was also aware that the immediate outcome would be ambush and slaughter. She was not able to perceive the rest of the Greek fleet waiting just beyond the horizon, nor was she able to predict that the long-term consequences would include Aeneas fleeing the city\u2019s destruction and ultimately founding Rome.</i><br /> <br /> No matter the information a Cassandra gleans from this effect, no one she tells will believe her until it\u2019s too late to change the outcome of events. No amount of persuasion or social skill short of God-level Knacks can make someone believe a Cassandra\u2019s prophecies, but it is possible to force people to act in accordance with the Cassandra\u2019s warnings. It\u2019s only the prophecies gleaned from the Cassandra Path effect that evoke this effect; general statements and inferences aren\u2019t automatically disbelieved.<br /> <br /> Continuing the example of the Trojan Horse, the Trojan soldiers didn\u2019t continue disbelieving Cassandra\u2019s warnings when the Greeks sprung their trap, but by then it was far too late to do anything about it. If Cassandra remarked that the Trojan Horse was certainly large enough to hold a phalanx of angry Greeks, the Trojans would likely agree, but would immediately discount the possibility that it actually was. If Cassandra had managed to get some leverage (say, a knife at King Priam\u2019s throat), she might have been able to force the Trojans into destroying the Horse anyways, but they\u2019d still steadfastly refuse to believe there was any point to it.<br /> <br /> This curse doesn't affect with divine blood. Post-Visitation Scions, Gods, and anyone related to them are free to believe or disbelieve a Cassandra\u2019s warnings as they see fit.<br /> <br /> <b>Birthrights</b><br /> \u2022 <b>Creature or Guide \u2022:</b> Cassandras may be accompanied by snakes, who whisper wisdom and sage counsel into their ears. Some merely have tattoos of snakes, hearing the sibilant whispers in their minds.<br /> <br /> <b>Knacks<br /> The</b> <b>Ties That Bind:</b> Once per scene, a Cassandra reads someone's Fate at a glance and discern their strongest Fatebound relationship (if any). If the subject has more than one Fatebond at the same strength, this Knack reveals the oldest one first. Subsequent uses of this Knack on the same subject reveal sequentially younger and weaker Fatebonds. Each time the Cassandra uses this Knack, they suffer a Path Condition on an unrelated Path, related to their reputation as a liar who can't be believed.<br /> <b>Truth, Lies, and Alibis:</b> Sometimes there are advantages to nobody believing you. Once per session, a Cassandra automatically succeeds on a simple Manipulation by telling the simple, unvarnished truth. This is a conscious manipulation of the effects of the Cassandra curse, making whatever the Cassandra says seem utterly ridiculous and inconsequential in the moment (and the Cassandra herself, therefore, not worth bothering with). Once the Cassandra leaves the scene, this Knack\u2019s effects end. For example, a Cassandra caught by a police officer while en route to the Pine Barrens to dispose of a body might use this Knack in response to the cop\u2019s questioning her presence and answer \u201cI\u2019m here to bury Sal Gemino\u2019s body.\u201d The Knack\u2019s effect will make the cop dismiss the story and the Cassandra herself as inconsequential, but later, when Mrs. Gemino files a missing persons report for her husband, he\u2019ll remember the story. (\u201cAt the time I thought she was joking, but now\u2026\u201d)<br /> This Knack doesn\u2019t affect anyone with divine blood.<br /> <b>Self-Consistency Principle:</b> If you can\u2019t warn people about the future, you can at least take perverse joy in guaranteeing your predictions will come to pass. Once per session, after using her Path effect, the Cassandra adds a Complication equal to her Cunning to <i>all</i> actions that would prevent her prophecy from coming true. Maybe those Trojans would have checked inside the Horse, just to be 100% sure, but once Cassandra starts raving about hidden Greeks, it seems like a terrible idea.<br /> Self-Consistency Principle <i>does</i> affect those with divine blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T10:10:47-07:00","id":1195353,"title":"","content":"Are Signature Purviews mandatory? I was thinking of doing a write-up of Princess Diana of Thymescria as a Hero; but then I realized that as a Scion of the Theoi, she would have to have a minimal facility with shapeshifting. Which <i>really</i> doesn't suit her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T10:22:38-07:00","id":1195356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1195353#post1195353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Signature Purviews mandatory? I was thinking of doing a write-up of Princess Diana of Thymescria as a Hero; but then I realized that as a Scion of the Theoi, she would have to have a minimal facility with shapeshifting. Which <i>really</i> doesn't suit her.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wouldn't that just be a matter of not taking Metamorphosis Boons?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T10:30:51-07:00","id":1195360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1195356#post1195356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wouldn't that just be a matter of not taking Metamorphosis Boons?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what it seems like. They would automatically get the innate bonus of Metamorphosis but that ultimately just lets them use disguises to extreme effectiveness. A little easier to fit into a concept or simply not use if they are not the sort to be interested in that sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T10:35:34-07:00","id":1195364,"title":"","content":"True enough. And some versions of the character <i>do</i> have the \u201csecret identity without a mask\u201d thing going on.<br /> <br /> That said, I do miss Arete, at least conceptually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-14-2018, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T10:50:01-07:00","id":1195373,"title":"","content":"Yea, the concept of Arete was good, but fairly plain compared to other PSPs. Ultimately though you could likely show those aspects of it by simply hyper focusing on a particular thing you want your character to be good in by picking the proper purviews and boons that compliment that image. It means someone else could do the same from a different pantheon but the concept of being an exemplary example of a particular aspect is still doable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 03-14-2018, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T11:15:26-07:00","id":1195384,"title":"","content":"Just getting into Scion (only played a game or two in 1ed) after backing this one (heard only good things).<br /> <br /> I am uncertain as to how dots work as relates to Paths and how many a Scion begins with.<br /> <br /> Would you be able to clarify how many dots in Callings we are supposed to begin with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T11:26:49-07:00","id":1195389,"title":"","content":"You should start with 1 dot in callings as an origin (previsitation scion) character. 4 dots as a hero. As a origin (previsitation) character this is a single dot in a single calling, as a hero it is 2 dots in one calling and 1 dot in two other callings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T11:31:17-07:00","id":1195393,"title":"","content":"Is it intentional that Aphrodite doesn't have Beauty? That seems... bizarre to say the least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T11:33:53-07:00","id":1195395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1195389#post1195389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You should start with 1 dot in callings as an origin (previsitation scion) character. 4 dots as a hero. As a origin (previsitation) character this is a single dot in a single calling, as a hero it is 2 dots in one calling and 1 dot in two other callings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just confused because it mentions five dots in Callings in the other sections of the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T11:44:01-07:00","id":1195399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1195395#post1195395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was just confused because it mentions five dots in Callings in the other sections of the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is stated and backed up twice in the character creation section. Personally im going to go with that for now.<br /> <br /> And yea, Aphrodite without Beauty is odd... I noticed they added a couple more purviews to a few gods but it seems that even another pass is going to be required before its officially done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T11:46:40-07:00","id":1195400,"title":"","content":"Anyone else find it weird that Zeus, keeper of Oaths and Hospitality and what not, has neither Judge nor Order? Especially when he did have Order in the preview draft oh so long ago?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T11:48:23-07:00","id":1195401,"title":"","content":"Admittedly, I am a little torn on weather you should start with 1 or 2 boons. I'll likely make it 1 just cus its cleaner to think 1 boon per legend.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Atleast until we get official word.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T11:50:06-07:00","id":1195402,"title":"","content":"What are these Virtues in the Theoi\u2019s Titan list... Patience, Endurance, Foresight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T11:51:11-07:00","id":1195403,"title":"","content":"Edit: Nvm, saw it has already been discussed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 03-14-2018, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T12:16:22-07:00","id":1195414,"title":"","content":"Just a comment on something I saw in a recent movie..Annihilation...damn me if that wasn't a titan...(Chaos and maybe Life purviews...but couldn't create life but definitely mutate it)<br /> <br /> scary to think about. And some titans are just that. Scary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T12:30:44-07:00","id":1195421,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar137_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"137\" data-vbnamecard=\"137\">Neall</a> <br /> <br /> The character creation chapter says to take 4 dots for Callings, and 2 Boons. The Traits chapter says 5 dots in Callings at Legend 1, and 1 Boon per Legend. Which is intended to be correct?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T12:42:30-07:00","id":1195427,"title":"","content":"I desperately need 2 things.:<br /> 1) A &quot;quick&quot; tutorial to make a character<br /> 2) the sheet...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T12:57:17-07:00","id":1195433,"title":"","content":"Also on the Theoi and their Purviews - Artemis could probably stand to pick up Wild...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T12:57:58-07:00","id":1195434,"title":"","content":"Quick question on Followers.<br /> <br /> It says that Followers come with what fits their descriptions but then we get the Tags and Arena. <br /> <br /> So if we get a Kitsune for example, would we have to buy the three Knacks tied to them or are those implied before we start getting the tags?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T13:03:36-07:00","id":1195437,"title":"","content":"More complicated followers that you want to be able to use knacks and several arenas of expertise would require them to be higher dot birthrights. So yes, Kitsune followers that fully mechanically function as Kitsune would be more expensive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T14:30:28-07:00","id":1195468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1195399#post1195399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is stated and backed up twice in the character creation section. Personally im going to go with that for now.<br /> <br /> And yea, Aphrodite without Beauty is odd... I noticed they added a couple more purviews to a few gods but it seems that even another pass is going to be required before its officially done.</div> </div> </div> </div>I literally have no idea, honestly, I feel like it's mentioned to be 5 dots of callings at Legacy 1 in more places. It also makes sense that a legend 4 scion would have 7 dots of callings, instead of only 6, since that'd potentially let you have 5, 1, 1, and thus max out one calling if you wanted to do so.<br /> <br /> Though the difference between that and 4, 1, 1 isn't THAT different.<br /> <br /> &lt;.&lt;<br /> <br /> The number of boons, though, is what I'm most curious about.<br /> <br /> At the moment, I'm going with 5-dots of callings and two boons, one from Legend and one just for being a Scion. &lt;.&lt;<br /> <br /> So a maxxed out Hero has 7 dots of callings and 5 boons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T14:34:14-07:00","id":1195471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrownedSun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1195468#post1195468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I literally have no idea, honestly, I feel like it's mentioned to be 5 dots of callings at Legacy 1 in more places. It also makes sense that a legend 4 scion would have 7 dots of callings, instead of only 6, since that'd potentially let you have 5, 1, 1, and thus max out one calling if you wanted to do so.<br /> <br /> Though the difference between that and 4, 1, 1 isn't THAT different.<br /> <br /> &lt;.&lt;<br /> <br /> The number of boons, though, is what I'm most curious about.<br /> <br /> At the moment, I'm going with 5-dots of callings and two boons, one from Legend and one just for being a Scion. &lt;.&lt;<br /> <br /> So a maxxed out Hero has 7 dots of callings and 5 boons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like your idea, and I'm going with it for my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T14:56:11-07:00","id":1195481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1195400#post1195400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone else find it weird that Zeus, keeper of Oaths and Hospitality and what not, has neither Judge nor Order? Especially when he did have Order in the preview draft oh so long ago?</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of me likes the idea of Zeus ruling through highest Legend, direct Leadership, and raw power, while he's actually dependent on Hera (who has both Judge and Order) for the more legalistic administrative aspects of governance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T15:04:25-07:00","id":1195488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1195481#post1195481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of me likes the idea of Zeus ruling through highest Legend, direct Leadership, and raw power, while he's actually dependent on Hera (who has both Judge and Order) for the more legalistic administrative aspects of governance.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be more or less my take on this too, yeah, honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T15:07:07-07:00","id":1195490,"title":"","content":"I'm still wondering when Aphrodite is going to get Beauty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T15:10:45-07:00","id":1195491,"title":"","content":"I was also wondering something: Have it changed so that in Scion Origins your character can start with any calling, and the calling related to your divine parent only need to be taken Post-Visitation? Thinking for a potential Warrior Scion of Amaterasu, or similiar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23677-the-eternal-keeper","name":"The Eternal Keeper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T15:15:38-07:00","id":1195493,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Kami entry, there doesn't seem to be any section about their views on titanomachy, but considering the write up in the preview about their nature and order, that Kami are like the Shen in that respect. Or perhaps the all-inclusive nature of Kami (an aspect I really like about the write up) makes them dovish (to use the word the preview has)<br /> <br /> Or perhaps they are meant to stand outside of this system of titans and gods, but I think more clarification is needed in this area, unless it important for it to be nebulous.<br /> <br /> On a side note, I do have some mixed feelings about some of the titles and purviews that these gods have (and yes I know how hard it is to apply purview type categories to Kami, but I was hoping to be pleasantly surprised)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T15:42:26-07:00","id":1195508,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry but, neall once said that every calling was connected to a specific boon ( trickster with deception, leader with sky ) and that if you match calling boon with gods favourite boon you can us it without a relic<br /> <br /> but i can't see this in the manual... is this thing changed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T15:57:21-07:00","id":1195516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1195508#post1195508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry but, neall once said that every calling was connected to a specific boon ( trickster with deception, leader with sky ) and that if you match calling boon with gods favourite boon you can us it without a relic<br /> <br /> but i can't see this in the manual... is this thing changed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. You only get 1 Innate Purview chosen from your Divine Parents list, all other Purviews must come from your Birthrights. Boons are limited by your Legend, the exact # at legend 1 is either 1 or 2, depending on which part of the book you are currently looking at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T16:19:31-07:00","id":1195522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1195508#post1195508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry but, neall once said that every calling was connected to a specific boon ( trickster with deception, leader with sky ) and that if you match calling boon with gods favourite boon you can us it without a relic<br /> <br /> but i can't see this in the manual... is this thing changed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know what you're talking about. At one point, Neall said that a Calling would be associated with a Purview, like Leaders getting Sky.<br /> <br /> This has been tossed out and I believe it was tossed out some time ago","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T17:13:27-07:00","id":1195534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1195490#post1195490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still wondering when Aphrodite is going to get Beauty.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Oc0-8BBkkq4\" target=\"_blank\">I have a suspicion a different company may have answered this for us, obliquely.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T17:16:45-07:00","id":1195535,"title":"","content":"I've looked around both books preview, but I can't find any reference to what a Feat of Scale is. I have found a place mentioning (see Origin, p. XX) but except for scale (which doesn't seem to give any information on Feats of Scale) I haven't found anything that looks related. So what is a Feat of Scale?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14855-mystril","name":"Mystril","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T17:38:41-07:00","id":1195544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mystril</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1195535#post1195535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've looked around both books preview, but I can't find any reference to what a Feat of Scale is. I have found a place mentioning (see Origin, p. XX) but except for scale (which doesn't seem to give any information on Feats of Scale) I haven't found anything that looks related. So what is a Feat of Scale?</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember seeing it somewhere. Basically, if you attempt something that falls under your Title, you can spend a point of Legend and gain half your Legend rating in Scale to the action.<br /> <br /> I can only assume you round up, otherwise FoS would be useless at Legend 1<br /> <br /> Also, Neall got asked a couple things on the Discord. So yeah, rest assured that Aphrodite will have Beauty in the final draft","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 03-14-2018, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T18:08:25-07:00","id":1195557,"title":"","content":"Has anyone heard anything about virtue track rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2472-trebius","name":"trebius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T18:15:14-07:00","id":1195559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trebius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1195557#post1195557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone heard anything about virtue track rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine they're identical to the ones in Origin","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T21:09:02-07:00","id":1195607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1195544#post1195544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember seeing it somewhere. Basically, if you attempt something that falls under your Title, you can spend a point of Legend and gain half your Legend rating in Scale to the action.<br /> <br /> I can only assume you round up, otherwise FoS would be useless at Legend 1<br /> <br /> Also, Neall got asked a couple things on the Discord. So yeah, rest assured that Aphrodite will have Beauty in the final draft</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait what Discord?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T21:30:24-07:00","id":1195614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1195607#post1195607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait what Discord?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://discord.gg/Er29BWz\" target=\"_blank\">This one</a>. Someone asked about it last month.<br /> <br /> (Post made for people who were unaware of the Discord)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T01:49:32-07:00","id":1195658,"title":"","content":"Are characters made as heroes meant to lack the couple extra attribute and skill points origin characters get at the end or was that an oversight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T03:57:40-07:00","id":1195680,"title":"","content":"Rules-based question: I want my Scion to have a creature-birthright that grants them access to the Journeys Purview - however only Guides and Relics seem to be able to grant relics - is there is method to allow this? On a similar note: I would want this creature-birthright to remain relevant as the Scion increases their Legend - would this be as simple as investing experience to increase the dice pool available to the creature, or would there need to be a method to apply the Scion's Scale to their creature-birthright?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13182-eltheriond","name":"Eltheriond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T04:47:26-07:00","id":1195683,"title":"","content":"A Guide can provide access to a Calling that you do not normally have, but how many Knacks from that Calling can be active? Likewise, if you drop a Calling and Adopt a new one, do you still have the old Knacks (even though you should only have 0 active, in accordance with your rank in the dropped Calling)?<br /> What about other Birthright Knacks, such as unique ones from Relics?<br /> <br /> Also, what happened to Inari scions having access to Kitsune Knacks, or Apollo's Scions having Oracle ones? Does that now mean you have to take the 'Creature' Calling if you want to pull that off?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T04:54:51-07:00","id":1195685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eltheriond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1195680#post1195680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rules-based question: I want my Scion to have a creature-birthright that grants them access to the Journeys Purview - however only Guides and Relics seem to be able to grant relics - is there is method to allow this? On a similar note: I would want this creature-birthright to remain relevant as the Scion increases their Legend - would this be as simple as investing experience to increase the dice pool available to the creature, or would there need to be a method to apply the Scion's Scale to their creature-birthright?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe let the Creature double as a Guide? If it s a 3 dot Creature, treat it as if it had two dots and acted as a Guide for the purposes of Purview access. Do Not forget about the Paying Tribute condition; I'd rule that asking the Creature to make a roll or take an Injury counts as 'invoking the path' for this purpose.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T07:00:05-07:00","id":1195714,"title":"","content":"Can we get some clarification the contradictory ways that Path Contact stuff is supposed to work? I really want to run a game but if I do I feel like I just have to disallow Path Contact stuff entirely because I have no idea how it works, or where the example Path Conditions are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T07:28:45-07:00","id":1195719,"title":"","content":"To be honest, Ive always felt that trying to add mechanics to things such as contacts always seemed really forced. I fully intend to ignore every contact rule within the game and treat it purely as a story thing or a product of invoking paths in various situations. A martial artist needing help could invoke a path based on that in order to contact his Sensei for advice/help with a situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 03-15-2018, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T11:07:32-07:00","id":1195792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1195658#post1195658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are characters made as heroes meant to lack the couple extra attribute and skill points origin characters get at the end or was that an oversight?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say no at my table because that's Unfun. Probably just an oversight; I think Neall mentioned that there were moments in Chargen that were artifacts of assuming you're porting an Origin character rather than making a Hero wholesale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T13:56:05-07:00","id":1195836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1195792#post1195792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say no at my table because that's Unfun. Probably just an oversight; I think Neall mentioned that there were moments in Chargen that were artifacts of assuming you're porting an Origin character rather than making a Hero wholesale.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my thoughts as well but I wanted to be sure. I guess I can see that even though they have separate rules for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T18:39:35-07:00","id":1195921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1195658#post1195658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are characters made as heroes meant to lack the couple extra attribute and skill points origin characters get at the end or was that an oversight?</div> </div> </div> </div>Stupid oversight! I used the wrong file. They get the extras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T06:24:15-07:00","id":1196028,"title":"","content":"I may have missed this being answered elsewhere: How many dots of Callings should Heroes have at Legend 1? You have 3 Chosen Callings and either 4 or 5 dots split between them. Character creation says 4 (One at 2, two at 1). The Calling section of the book says 5 (2, 2 &amp; 1).<br /> <br /> EDIT: Scratch that. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1194995-my-thoughts-on-hero/page4\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-on-hero/page4</a><br /> <br /> Should be 5. Good to know.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Right, reading through Hero. Is it intended that experience feels relatively... I don't want to say useless, but unimportant?<br /> <br /> Legend covers Boons and Callings, and Legend develops through Deeds.<br /> <br /> Experience gives you attributes and skills, but they're relatively cheap for their effect and you already start out pretty good at the things you want to be good at, and shoring up your few weaknesses won't take that long. Unless you're looking for 5s across the board, you'll be done with that relatively soon.<br /> <br /> After that, the only things you can purchase are Specialties, &quot;extra&quot; Knacks and Birthrights. Since you can't actually purchase the ability to <i>use</i> the extra Knacks, you're not actually getting more powerful, just getting the option to swap your Knacks around. Which is fine, but if you're happy with the Knacks you chose at the beginning, you'd probably end up not doing it too much.<br /> <br /> Basically, the only real power advancement from experience comes from your Birthrights. And, actually, the more I think about it, the more okay I am with that. Because your individual Follower can become the leader of a Group, or Mob of Followers as the story progresses. Your Creature can develop weird powers or just become bigger and more powerful as it grows alongside you. As the legend of your Relic grows, it fits you better, or it's Flaws stop being quite so disadvantageous.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, I've got no idea how a Guide should progress. I suppose it's something that's worth thinking about when planning your Guide.<br /> <br /> EDIT again: One last thing, honest. Origins tier characters get Birthrights as an option. Relics seem vaguely awkward for this, while also being an obvious choice.<br /> <br /> Pre-Visitation, do they just not get associated with any Deeds?<br /> Purviews and Motifs are obviously not useful, due to the abject lack of Legend. Seems like adding Purviews and Motifs is a good explanation of &quot;upgrading&quot; a Relic post-Visitation.<br /> <br /> But Enhancements/Knacks seem like a solid bonus for Origins characters, along with some of the Flaws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2649,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","user":"Tarion","date":". 03-16-2018, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T08:58:17-07:00","id":1196083,"title":"","content":"What about the final touches of origin? it says that we can choose beetwen 2 knack or 4 point of relic<br /> <br /> in hero there is no such things, i have to count it??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T09:48:42-07:00","id":1196099,"title":"","content":"&quot;A Relic can\u2019t grant more than three Purviews. If the Relic grants at least one Purview, it also gains a motif.&quot;<br /> <br /> doest this mean that if i give a relic a purview i gain a free motif or i have to buy the motif too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T12:15:10-07:00","id":1196155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1196083#post1196083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the final touches of origin? it says that we can choose beetwen 2 knack or 4 point of relic<br /> <br /> in hero there is no such things, i have to count it??</div> </div> </div> </div>You get those points. Some of the writeup was made assuming you're converting an Origin character, who would have those bonuses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> doest this mean that if i give a relic a purview i gain a free motif or i have to buy the motif too? </div> </div> </div>You get the Motif for free, best I can tell. If you had to buy the Motif it probably would have said &quot;It <i>requires</i> a Motif&quot; rather than &quot;Gains a Motif&quot;. Quick English lesson: 'Gains' implies that it gets it out of nowhere.<br /> <br /> Also, you can use 'Edit' to put another question into your post, rather than double-posting. Looks neater.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, for those who aren't on the Discord, I've been trying to collect Neall's answers to questions on the Discord in a Google Doc.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1etYiuHfHR-nTI5obsKhL44stbRmLkuvw2Z6qae_lbWM\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> it is, it will be updated as I get more answers and as more questions are asked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T12:15:19-07:00","id":1196156,"title":"","content":"In Hero, what are the rules for a Crisis in a Calling? All the Fate conditions refer to this, but I can\u2019t find what it means or what the effects are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4310-jagardner","name":"jagardner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T12:23:43-07:00","id":1196161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1196155#post1196155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Also, for those who aren't on the Discord, I've been trying to collect Neall's answers to questions on the Discord in a Google Doc.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1etYiuHfHR-nTI5obsKhL44stbRmLkuvw2Z6qae_lbWM\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> it is, it will be updated as I get more answers and as more questions are asked.</div> </div> </div> </div>What Discord? There's a Discord?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T12:47:21-07:00","id":1196179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorsRattus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1196161#post1196161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Discord? There's a Discord?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://discord.gg/bXwENH\" target=\"_blank\">Yo</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jagardner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1196156#post1196156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Hero, what are the rules for a Crisis in a Calling? All the Fate conditions refer to this, but I can\u2019t find what it means or what the effects are.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I had to guess (Disclaimer: Not Neall) I'd say that a Crisis is another name for the Failure Deeds mentioned under the Calling section (page 215 of the pre-layout manuscript) saying how you can shed one of your Callings. At this point, you can do an Adoption Deed to pick up another one... Or, were I GM, perform an Adoption Deed of the same Calling to reaffirm it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 03-16-2018, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T12:51:08-07:00","id":1196182,"title":"","content":"Edit: Double-post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T15:29:34-07:00","id":1196243,"title":"","content":"On the topic of Specialities, Relics that grant Purviews, and getting Purviews from Relic that you then specialize...<br /> <br /> ...if someone, say, takes a relic that gives them Passion (Joy)--<br /> --by my understanding they get 1 motiff from being granted a purview by a relic, which is tied to the Relic itself.<br /> --they ALSO get a motiff from specializing in that purview, rather than taking the general form...<br /> <br /> ...is that &quot;speciality motiff&quot; also tied to the relic?<br /> <br /> I.e., can you use it without access to the relic? If the relic has a flaw, can you use the motiff without fulfilling whatever the requirements are from the flaw??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T15:44:18-07:00","id":1196252,"title":"","content":"So, if I wanted to make a Scion of, say, Bres the Beautiful, it seems like I probably could. I'd have to get my ST to figure out what Callings are appropriate for the guy, but he's got a Purview here and Virtues. Which leads me to ask: If I am a Scion of Bres, do I have Honor/Prowess, or do I have Dominance/Prowess?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T15:46:46-07:00","id":1196255,"title":"","content":"Grammar question on Starry Path:<br /> <br /> &quot;Other Scions and mortals Fatebound to you don\u2019t count towards this limit.&quot;<br /> <br /> Is that [other Scions] and [mortals Fatebound to you], or is it that anyone Fatebound to you, Scion or Mortal?<br /> <br /> Or, to put it another way, is it intended to be able to teleport your entire Band? Because being able to only transport other characters equal to your Legend and being able to transport your Band + other characters equal to your Legend is a big difference. Particularly early on, when Legend 1 or 2 means that you can't actually use it as effective transport (Although it will still be a very useful utility power)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T16:06:25-07:00","id":1196264,"title":"","content":"Will innate purviews increase as you proceed to demigod and god? Just asking because I remeber that being brought up in 1E companion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5727-racain23","name":"racain23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T19:11:45-07:00","id":1196315,"title":"","content":"Denizens can use Marvels once they aquire access to Purviews via Birthrights; in the case of Sorcerers, do they inherently gain access to a motif outsider of any provided by Relics?<br /> I feel like they should, but it never says...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T19:45:25-07:00","id":1196327,"title":"","content":"What\u2019s the poinr of \u201cSurgeon with the Hands of God\u201d? There are no rules for surgery in either Origin or Hero, and no rules about how long surgery might take. In fact, the onliy means of healing that I can see are First Aid (which a character can only do for one wound per session, immediately after a battle) and the Healer Knacks \u201cCombat Medic\u201d, \u201cDamage Conversion\u201d, and \u201cDoctor\u2019s Kit\u201d (which all only seem to be relevant during combat). Apart from that, I see no rules for healing wounds except by waiting for them to heal naturally (2 days for Bruising, 2 weeks for everything else).<br /> <br /> So the idea of doing surgery just seems to be narrative color, with no tangible consequences for any characters. Halving the time has no meaningful benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4310-jagardner","name":"jagardner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T00:08:27-07:00","id":1196395,"title":"","content":"It's a bit of a longer question, so <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar137_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"137\" data-vbnamecard=\"137\">Neall</a> could we pretty please see a definitive list of which Skills are associated with which Pantheon Paths? The Origin and Core have some pretty distinctive contradictions, such as the Hero Teotl having three skills, the Hero Aesir having NONE, and Origin says the Manitou skills are Athletics and Persuasion while Hero says it's Medicine and Occult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T07:33:26-07:00","id":1196473,"title":"","content":"According to Momentum<br /> <br /> &quot;When a Scion, God, or other being with the track takes an action in line with one of their<br /> Virtues, they slide on the track closer to that trait, and any Momentum spent out<br /> of the Black Pool to add dice to that roll results in bonus dice added&quot;<br /> <br /> Is this for ANY action taken towards a virtue? Or is it as the Saint's Virtuous says and only when at the far end?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12919-mystrich","name":"Mystrich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T08:49:15-07:00","id":1196500,"title":"","content":"On Legendary titles: The example characters seem to just have scion of X or incarnation of X as their legend one titles, but the title section seems to imply it should be something related to a keyword. What should it be? And how do you decide on a more specific one for a character that probably hasn't done anything too spectacular yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T09:54:50-07:00","id":1196516,"title":"","content":"I'm a little lost on how Fatebinding strength is supposed to work. I'm guessing new Fatebindings start at strength 1, but then, how do you get them to strength 2, since you need 2 Milestones (to exceed strength 1) but can only Invoke once a session, with it fading at the end of the current one? Is it supposed to be milestones equal to current strength or am I missing something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13075-malicwanderer","name":"MalicWanderer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T10:07:23-07:00","id":1196520,"title":"","content":"Do you gain experience for your Band-Term Deed? I'm assuming so (And that it's just not here because copy and paste and it's not a thing in Trinity) but I could also see an argument that it's covered by Story Milestone/Group Story and doesn't generate experience separately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T10:34:04-07:00","id":1196530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1196520#post1196520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you gain experience for your Band-Term Deed? I'm assuming so (And that it's just not here because copy and paste and it's not a thing in Trinity) but I could also see an argument that it's covered by Story Milestone/Group Story and doesn't generate experience separately.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a group story and a group deed are the same thing, just a word misuse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MalicWander</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little lost on how Fatebinding strength is supposed to work. I'm guessing new Fatebindings start at strength 1, but then, how do you get them to strength 2, since you need 2 Milestones (to exceed strength 1) but can only Invoke once a session, with it fading at the end of the current one? Is it supposed to be milestones equal to current strength or am I missing something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>With a Strength one binding on a legend one character you'd basically have to roll two dice and have both come up as a success. That would be two milestones I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","user":"vonpenguin","date":". 03-17-2018, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T10:39:11-07:00","id":1196531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1196530#post1196530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think a group story and a group deed are the same thing, just a word misuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would make sense. Feel a bit stupid for not realising","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T10:56:07-07:00","id":1196534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1196530#post1196530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With a Strength one binding on a legend one character you'd basically have to roll two dice and have both come up as a success. That would be two milestones I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my original assumption, but on actually checking the Complex Action rules in Origins it looks like it's one Milestone per successful action, not per success rolled. (Which is probably a thing worth making a note of and pointing out to any who, like me, are more used to CofD and start off assuming Complex Action = Extended Action.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13075-malicwanderer","name":"MalicWanderer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T11:49:57-07:00","id":1196551,"title":"","content":"Off hand, the Tempered Knack (and a few other places, like in Armor under biker jacket) mention the Armored Tag, but... I don't know where the tag is. What is it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T12:25:15-07:00","id":1196559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1196551#post1196551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Off hand, the Tempered Knack (and a few other places, like in Armor under biker jacket) mention the Armored Tag, but... I don't know where the tag is. What is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>From context, it looks like it's meant to be soft armour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T16:38:36-07:00","id":1196637,"title":"","content":"So asked Neall about how Drawbacks work on players if playing a Creature (ie. A werewolf Scion receives Vulnerability: Silver)<br /> Answer: When you're affected by that, it functions as a Persistent condition, therefore grants you Momentum.<br /> <br /> However, Creature knacks also might end up changing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12919-mystrich","name":"Mystrich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T17:19:52-07:00","id":1196648,"title":"","content":"&quot;the higher of the Follower\u2019s rating or your Leadership.&quot;<br /> <br /> what does this mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T17:35:43-07:00","id":1196655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1196648#post1196648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;the higher of the Follower\u2019s rating or your Leadership.&quot;<br /> <br /> what does this mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your Follower's Birthright rating or your Leadership Skill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T17:37:04-07:00","id":1196656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1196500#post1196500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On Legendary titles: The example characters seem to just have scion of X or incarnation of X as their legend one titles, but the title section seems to imply it should be something related to a keyword. What should it be? And how do you decide on a more specific one for a character that probably hasn't done anything too spectacular yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>You record the Keywords and it should probably have a Keyword in it, but the Legendary Title is recorded like any other Path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T18:47:39-07:00","id":1196678,"title":"","content":"Alright, about Legend and Knacks and Boons.<br /> <br /> One point of Legend per Legend rating? One extra Knack or Boon? Doesn't that seem kinda low-powered? How does that work? I'm kinda confused on the limited amount of stuff that Heroes are getting. Does it increase at Demigod or God? Between Callings and Purviews, it seems like characters don't really have a lot of tricks up their sleeves in the event of a Big Bad coming to town.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T03:46:54-07:00","id":1196760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1196678#post1196678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, about Legend and Knacks and Boons.<br /> <br /> One point of Legend per Legend rating? One extra Knack or Boon? Doesn't that seem kinda low-powered? How does that work? I'm kinda confused on the limited amount of stuff that Heroes are getting. Does it increase at Demigod or God? Between Callings and Purviews, it seems like characters don't really have a lot of tricks up their sleeves in the event of a Big Bad coming to town.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> i was asking the same thing<br /> <br /> I mean, i know you can imbue legend to do some stuff but... one legend X legend is pretty... low.<br /> <br /> <br /> you can regain legend with fatebound and sacrifice, ok, but there is some other way?? a quickest way?? in a fight of tier 4, the first that ends his legend have... &quot;lost&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T04:14:51-07:00","id":1196762,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, you spend Legend for big, flashy, one-time effects, or to stretch yourself beyond your core competencies. You Imbue Legend to be incredibly competent over a long time period. I suspect that most combat focused characters will be all about Imbuing Legend. <br /> <br /> A Warrior Calling Scion with Earth and Epic Stamina can sit at a Soft Armour of 5 and Resistant to a single source of damage (So if anyone's got any Piercing weapons, you can counter them), with 2 Legend Imbued. That's tough enough that Critical Hits become the easier way of hurting them (... which is a really weird interaction, but okay). That's just two Boons and a Knack. With more Knacks invested (I've got no clue whether Perfect Defense is amazing or useless here - I'm not sure when it triggers. If it lets you no-sell <i>after</i> they've rolled, it's awesome, when you know that they need to beat your Defence by <i>four</i> to even hurt you) and the potential for more Boons you could be an absolute combat monster without ever having to actually spend Legend. <br /> <br /> And if I'm reading it right, you can pull your Legend out of those Boons at any time, ending them prematurely. So if you need to re-focus (Or someone pulls a Piercing weapon that you're not currently Resistant to), it just takes an action<br /> <br /> &quot;Legend imbued in a Boon or marvel is committed to that effect for the specified duration, and you cannot use it for other purposes during that time. However, when you reclaim imbued Legend from a Boon or other effect, it is immediately added back to your pool of Legend points. <b>Reclaiming Legend is instantaneous and can be done at any time.</b>&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T07:06:00-07:00","id":1196783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1196762#post1196762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally speaking, you spend Legend for big, flashy, one-time effects, or to stretch yourself beyond your core competencies. You Imbue Legend to be incredibly competent over a long time period. I suspect that most combat focused characters will be all about Imbuing Legend.<br /> <br /> A Warrior Calling Scion with Earth and Epic Stamina can sit at a Soft Armour of 5 and Resistant to a single source of damage (So if anyone's got any Piercing weapons, you can counter them), with 2 Legend Imbued. That's tough enough that Critical Hits become the easier way of hurting them (... which is a really weird interaction, but okay). That's just two Boons and a Knack. With more Knacks invested (I've got no clue whether Perfect Defense is amazing or useless here - I'm not sure when it triggers. If it lets you no-sell <i>after</i> they've rolled, it's awesome, when you know that they need to beat your Defence by <i>four</i> to even hurt you) and the potential for more Boons you could be an absolute combat monster without ever having to actually spend Legend.<br /> <br /> And if I'm reading it right, you can pull your Legend out of those Boons at any time, ending them prematurely. So if you need to re-focus (Or someone pulls a Piercing weapon that you're not currently Resistant to), it just takes an action<br /> <br /> &quot;Legend imbued in a Boon or marvel is committed to that effect for the specified duration, and you cannot use it for other purposes during that time. However, when you reclaim imbued Legend from a Boon or other effect, it is immediately added back to your pool of Legend points. <b>Reclaiming Legend is instantaneous and can be done at any time.</b>&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And that's before we take into account that knacks just require momentum, which flows at a much higher rate. It only seems small compared to first ed, which gave much higher numbers but also cost more per boon/knack. Once you get to demi-god and the trivial target rules start to come into play some of those boons are free a good portion of the time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T07:12:11-07:00","id":1196785,"title":"","content":"I'm not entirely sure I get how Army of One works, but because I don't know what sorts of penalties and Complications you'll face from more enemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T08:15:56-07:00","id":1196796,"title":"","content":"So, as i said before i'm dumb.<br /> <br /> <br /> Can someone give me some example of narrative and drama scale??<br /> <br /> What i've understood till now is:<br /> <br /> <br /> Simple man vs simple man there is no scale.<br /> <br /> <br /> Simple man vs bruce lee, there is the scale and in this scale Bruce lee gain a x2 success on narrative scale OR a +2 enhancements on a drammatic scale while the simple man gains nothing.<br /> <br /> <br /> BUT what happen' when bruce lee Vs NEGA bruce lee?? there is no scale because they are of the same scale? <br /> <br /> what is the difference beetwen drama and narrative?? i feel pretty confused<br /> <br /> Heroes in what scale fits?? are they elite or supernatural?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T08:19:06-07:00","id":1196799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1196785#post1196785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not entirely sure I get how Army of One works, but because I don't know what sorts of penalties and Complications you'll face from more enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mass opponents are rendered as a Scale against you, so you get bonuses when you fight against that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T09:13:13-07:00","id":1196822,"title":"","content":"Thanks so much for being so quick to answer these Neall. One last one from me for now. It was mentioned in one of your earlier answers that knacks granted by guides use their dots to &quot;equip&quot;, if a PC and their guide shared a calling, would those dots stack? For example a four dot guide with Warrior allowing a scion with warrior 2 to have 6 points of warrior knacks active?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T09:25:00-07:00","id":1196827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1196796#post1196796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, as i said before i'm dumb.<br /> <br /> <br /> Can someone give me some example of narrative and drama scale??<br /> <br /> What i've understood till now is:<br /> <br /> <br /> Simple man vs simple man there is no scale.<br /> <br /> <br /> Simple man vs bruce lee, there is the scale and in this scale Bruce lee gain a x2 success on narrative scale OR a +2 enhancements on a drammatic scale while the simple man gains nothing.<br /> <br /> <br /> BUT what happen' when bruce lee Vs NEGA bruce lee?? there is no scale because they are of the same scale? <br /> <br /> what is the difference beetwen drama and narrative?? i feel pretty confused<br /> <br /> Heroes in what scale fits?? are they elite or supernatural?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most Scale comes from size or divine might. In your case, Bruce Lee wouldn't get Scale because as good as he is, he's still human-sized and human-tier.<br /> <br /> Now, if it were Bruce Lee versus a literal giant, the giant may have less training and may even be scrawny for a giant, but it's still a giant with a reach greater than Bruce Lee's height. Let's give this Giant Scale 2.<br /> <br /> If this Giant tried to smash Bruce Lee, it would enjoy +4 successes against him. And if Lee tried to retaliate, the Giant's defense would be 2 higher due to again being big and tough.<br /> <br /> Now if that giant wrestled against something with Scale 1, the Giant wouldn't get the full bonuses of its Scale. But since its Scale is one higher than the opponent, it still enjoys the benefits of Scale 1. That is, +2 successes against its foe.<br /> <br /> In some cases the Scale is big enough to handwave. That Scale 2 Giant against some background mook wouldn't even be rolled. Joe Salaryman is pulped without any dice being thrown.<br /> <br /> As for the question of your Hero PCs... Normally they are Scale 0. Human-sized, human speed.<br /> <br /> But the ichor in their veins let them push past those limits. For example, Epic Strength has the innate power of &quot;+1 Scale when lifting and breaking things&quot;. So if Brick Hardmeat has Epic Stength, he can try to lift a dumpster and will enjoy +2 successes to do so, without any Imbued Legend.<br /> <br /> All Scion's also have the ability to perform Fears of Scale, which can add Scale equal to half their Legend. They most often do this by invoking their Legendary Title.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T10:25:08-07:00","id":1196846,"title":"","content":"If you have a Knack that lets you imbue a Legend for a particular Feat of Scale, but you don't have a Title, just a keyword that fits the cost is 1 imbued Legend and 2 Momentum, yes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T16:00:30-07:00","id":1196939,"title":"","content":"Pantheon Specific Purviews outside of your own are not possible to use via Relic correct?<br /> <br /> Will Relics still be limited in terms of how many enhancements, purviews, elements etc. someone can put in a singular relic?<br /> <br /> Edit: Never mind, others have answered this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4983,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4983-graywalker","user":"GrayWalker","date":". 03-21-2018, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4983-graywalker","name":"GrayWalker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T16:41:19-07:00","id":1196950,"title":"","content":"Could we get any clarification on how Apprentice's Invoke is supposed to work? I think it's referencing the rules from the old Storypath preview where when you failed the storyguide would offer either a consolation or a complication, but that seems to have been removed from the current iteration?<br /> <br /> Edit: I just thought of an idea I think I'll go with until further clarification, sharing in case others find it useful. Take the difference in the failed roll's difficulty and what they would've been able to succeed at (with the successes they rolled) and act as if the roll had had the lower difficulty and a complication of that rating. Not entirely sure how it should interact with threshold successes on stunts or other, existing complications. Other than definitely no buying off the complication that got added by the Invoke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13075,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13075-malicwanderer","user":"MalicWanderer","date":". 03-18-2018, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13075-malicwanderer","name":"MalicWanderer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T17:00:40-07:00","id":1196955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GrayWalker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1196939#post1196939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will Relics still be limited in terms of how many... <i>purviews</i>... someone can put in a singular relic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hero Text Only Preview, pg.245 &quot;A Relic can\u2019t grant more than three Purviews.&quot; Besides no one getting more then their own PSP, that's the restrictions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T06:26:43-07:00","id":1197161,"title":"","content":"Yeah I know this is a load of questions but I'm unsure whether I should make individual posts asking each or just have a compendium post like this.<br /> <br /> Is the Kami of a relic of significance to a non Japanese Pantheon (eg Kami of the Golden Fleece) considered part of the Japanese Pantheon or the Pantheon that the relic is significant to?<br /> Are Dodaem Spirits and Kami the same spirit, separate spirits or two different incarnations of the same spirit?<br /> <br /> If one has a sentient item can one use Metamorphosis' Transfigure ability on it? Also when one uses Change Shape what happens to their clothes and any items on their person?<br /> <br /> Do tattoos or modifications to one's body count as valid relics? I think imitating Siegfried by bathing in dragon's blood to gain Epic Stamina or at least extra tough skin should be a valid option.<br /> <br /> Are Crises and Transfiguration synonyms to Failure Deed and Adoption Deed? In the description of Trickster in the Traits chapter it has the crises in place of where failure deed is and transfigurations in place of Adoption deed.<br /> <br /> Can effects that target one character as their subject be redirected at just oneself? For example can my character use the Muse of Fire boon on themselves for self inspiration?<br /> <br /> Similarly can effects that target multiple characters be targeted at one individual or oneself? For example can my character use the Cooler Heads boon to calm one person in front of them or just calm themselves down?<br /> <br /> Do Peaches of Immortality grant permanent immortality?<br /> <br /> Do the Theoi require Ambrosia and Nectar to retain their immortality? Are any gods/pantheons inherently immortal/ageless as it seems the Aesir, the Tuatha and possibly the Deva require periodic rituals or consumption of some divine food to maintain their eternal youth?<br /> <br /> Are callings for deities listed in order of importance to their character?<br /> <br /> Do you have any plans on having Boons increase their ability as characters ascend in Legend or character Tier? For example the flight boon lasts one scene but as one ascends in Legend could it be possible for the duration to be extended?<br /> <br /> Can Gods adopt titanspawn as scions?<br /> <br /> Can one use marvels to emulate pantheon specific purviews? For example is it possible to using Beast(Dove) to emulate the change shape Boon from Metamorphosis to transform into a dove, or using Forge to communicate with the Kami or Dodaem of an item you have personally created?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4983,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4983-graywalker","user":"GrayWalker","date":". 03-26-2018, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4983-graywalker","name":"GrayWalker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T10:15:26-07:00","id":1197249,"title":"","content":"Hey guys !<br /> <br /> I got a question about followers rules, lets imagine i got 5 dots of birthright and outro it on followers i can get 5 tags to then, if i get group/mob/knack/tough/defensive, i would get a mob of 50 followers i na can use a mixed action to comand then to attack twice as mixed action and myself can still give a blow, so it is effectivelly a 3 hits per turn ? Or i got that wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T02:16:22-07:00","id":1197521,"title":"","content":"Is there a mechanical way to use Close Combat with Dexterity to represent a more agile melee combatant like a duelist, knife fighter, some types of martial artists, etc? Not just a question for Neall, by the way - if there's some knack or whatever that opens up close combat to dexterity that I've missed please let me know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T02:29:45-07:00","id":1197526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197521#post1197521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a mechanical way to use Close Combat with Dexterity to represent a more agile melee combatant like a duelist, knife fighter, some types of martial artists, etc? Not just a question for Neall, by the way - if there's some knack or whatever that opens up close combat to dexterity that I've missed please let me know.</div> </div> </div> </div>No Knacks or Birthrights needed.<br /> <br /> Scion: Origin (Text Only) pg.65 &quot;Every dramatic challenge in the game exists in one of three different Arenas, reflecting the abilities it requires and obstacles it involves. <b>On every role, the Storyguide determines the Arena of a challenge.</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> Scion: Origin (Text Only) pg.66 &quot;A character\u2019s Approach defines the way they tackle challenges. Whenever a character faces a challenge requiring a roll, <b>their player should describe their Approach after the Storyguide decides the Arena.</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> Scion: Origin (Text Only) pg.66 &quot;<b>In a Physical underground boxing match</b>, a fighter could dive in and hammer away with Might (Force), <b>weave around for a perfect shot with Dexterity (Finesse)</b>, or drain his opponent with a Stamina (Resilience) rope-a-dope.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T02:31:04-07:00","id":1197527,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, asking this here as well- Heroes only get to apply Feats of Scale to singular action for the most part, with a few Boons and Knacks letting you Imbue instead of Spending Legend. Would I be correct in assuming that Demigods and Gods get more ways to perform Feats of Scale on a scene-long or even permanent basis s, or is it just a matter of a God having more Legend to burn than a Hero?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T02:35:38-07:00","id":1197531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197526#post1197526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No Knacks or Birthrights needed.<br /> <br /> Scion: Origin (Text Only) pg.65 &quot;Every dramatic challenge in the game exists in one of three different Arenas, reflecting the abilities it requires and obstacles it involves. <b>On every role, the Storyguide determines the Arena of a challenge.</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> Scion: Origin (Text Only) pg.66 &quot;A character\u2019s Approach defines the way they tackle challenges. Whenever a character faces a challenge requiring a roll, <b>their player should describe their Approach after the Storyguide decides the Arena.</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> Scion: Origin (Text Only) pg.66 &quot;<b>In a Physical underground boxing match</b>, a fighter could dive in and hammer away with Might (Force), <b>weave around for a perfect shot with Dexterity (Finesse)</b>, or drain his opponent with a Stamina (Resilience) rope-a-dope.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That directly contradicts the very specific rules listed in the combat section, which very clearly indicate that close combat is always Might based. Unless there's some other rule in play that I'm missing, I would assume that specific rules for specific situations trump general rules. The alternative is that you can just use whatever attributes wanted on any roll (including Knacks, Boons, Social situations, Combat, whatever), as long as you can have a long extended conversation with the ST first. The boxing example seems to be one where the issue is being settled by a couple of dice rolls instead of actually going into the combat system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","user":"HighPriest","date":". 03-20-2018, 05:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T02:47:30-07:00","id":1197532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197531#post1197531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That directly contradicts the very specific rules listed in the combat section, which very clearly indicate that close combat is always Might based. Unless there's some other rule in play that I'm missing, specific rules for specific situations trump general rules. The alternative is that you can just use whatever attributes wanted on any roll (including Knacks, Boons, Social situations, Combat, whatever), as long as you can have a long extended conversation with the ST first. The boxing example seems to be one where the issue is being settled by a couple of dice rolls instead of actually going into the combat system.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not the Core rules fault that who ever wrote the combat chapter didn't know what they were doing.<br /> <br /> Scion: Origin (Text Only) pg.59 &quot;<b>The player decides which Skill from their character sheet best matches the challenge he\u2019s facing, and then decides which Attribute best matches his approach to using that Skill.</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> Scion: Origin (Text Only) pg.60 &quot;<b>Any Skill can pair with any Attribute.</b> An Attribute can reflect a character\u2019s Physical, Mental, or Social strengths, and displays their Force, Control, or Resilience in that area, but a <b>physical Attribute does not have to pair with a physical Skill</b>. <b>Brawling may be a test of physical force (i.e., Close Combat + Might), but it may also be a test of mental control (i.e., Close Combat + Cunning)</b> as a character focuses on finding weaknesses to exploit. The Skills section on p. XX lists some <b>common pairings</b>, but those are <b>only suggestions.</b>&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T02:52:49-07:00","id":1197534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197532#post1197532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not the Core rules fault that who ever wrote the combat chapter didn't know what they were doing.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's disappointing to hear that the game is still in a totally unplayable state, then. There are also a lot of bad mistakes in Hero that indicate which dice pools you should be using in the purviews section. Oh well. Guess I'll wait to check again in 8 months or so when PDFs get sent out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","user":"HighPriest","date":". 03-20-2018, 05:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T03:06:28-07:00","id":1197537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197534#post1197534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's disappointing to hear that the game is still in a totally unplayable state, then. Oh well. Guess I'll wait to check again in 8 months or so when the PDFs get sent out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me get this straight...<br /> <br /> 1) You ask if there is something you can take that allows you to use Dex with Close Combat...<br /> 2) You are told you don't need to get anything, and are given specific examples that sight boxing as examples that the core rules already allow this...<br /> 3) You then try and argue that it isn't the case by arguing specific beats general, and making a baseless claim that my examples aren't &quot;combat&quot; even though in Boxing one trades blows in an attempt to damage the opponent... just like combat... so like combat in fact, that it is combat...<br /> 4) When even more evidence is presented, and you are again proven wrong, you resort to claiming that the game is therefore unplayable...<br /> 5) All of this is because you are already able to do what it is that you wanted to do in the first place. Without having to buy something that allows an exception...<br /> <br /> Okay...<br /> <br /> You keep being you...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T03:59:44-07:00","id":1197546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197537#post1197537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me get this straight...<br /> <br /> 1) You ask if there is something you can take that allows you to use Dex with Close Combat...<br /> 2) You are told you don't need to get anything, and are given specific examples that sight boxing as examples that the core rules already allow this...<br /> 3) You then try and argue that it isn't the case by arguing specific beats general, and making a baseless claim that my examples aren't &quot;combat&quot; even though in Boxing one trades blows in an attempt to damage the opponent... just like combat... so like combat in fact, that it is combat...<br /> 4) When even more evidence is presented, and you are again proven wrong, you resort to claiming that the game is therefore unplayable...<br /> 5) All of this is because you are already able to do what it is that you wanted to do in the first place. Without having to buy something that allows an exception...<br /> <br /> Okay...<br /> <br /> You keep being you...</div> </div> </div> </div>There's two entirely separate sets of rules, and pointing to one bit doesn't make the other bits go away. <br /> <br /> &quot;Use whatever attribute makes sense&quot; is fine for the general rules, but it just doesn't fit with the combat section specifically listing attributes. &quot;The dice pool for melee attacks is Close Combat + Might&quot;. There's no room for flexibility there. It's also entirely consistent through the range chapter - there's an explicit list of Attributes that ties directly to range - The Combat Attribute at Close range is Might, even with a ranged weapon. There's no flexibility there. <br /> <br /> The <i>very best</i> you can say is that there are contradictory rules. Jumping down a guys throat because he disagrees with you as to which rules are correct is... well, it's not particularly nice, and it's certainly not fair. Especially given that this is a document that is acknowledged to have significant flaws from being built on the bones of the Trinity Core manuscript, and that generally speaking HighPriest is right - If a specific rule later in the book overrules the general rule, you're usually right to follow the specific rule. <br /> <br /> Now, it's not 100%, but Trinity Continuum adds in a sidebar to the combat section specifically stating that &quot;all dice pools listed in this chapter are merely guidelines or suggestions for the most common, or basic dice pool.&quot; It looks like it's certainly intended to just pick an Attribute that makes sense. But I don't think its unreasonable to read the bits saying &quot;The dice pool for melee attacks is Close Combat + Might&quot; and think that this means that the dice pool for melee attacks is Close Combat and Might.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T04:47:58-07:00","id":1197556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197546#post1197546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's two entirely separate sets of rules, and pointing to one bit doesn't make the other bits go away.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, the Combat chapters lack of awareness of the general rules of the game does not make them go away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197546#post1197546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Use whatever attribute makes sense&quot; is fine for the general rules, but it just doesn't fit with the combat section specifically listing attributes. &quot;The dice pool for melee attacks is Close Combat + Might&quot;. There's no room for flexibility there. It's also entirely consistent through the range chapter - there's an explicit list of Attributes that ties directly to range - The Combat Attribute at Close range is Might, even with a ranged weapon. There's no flexibility there.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's why it's wrong. There are 5 examples given earlier in the book that all reference the Close Combat Skill. Only 2 of them use Might, 1 uses Dex, another 1 uses Stamina, and yet another 1 uses Cunning. All specific examples, that the person writing the Combat chapter was unaware of, and in a fit of D&amp;D'ism, gave us the Close Combat is always + Might BS that we have now. That is far from that chapters only flaw (Grappling being &quot;Skill: Agility (Might)&quot;, in the section right after Close Combat... Brilliant...) but it is more then enough to let me know that the pairings are simply common ones, and can be ignored in specifics, just like the rules, and examples thru out the rest of the book, clearly show again, and again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197546#post1197546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <i>very best</i> you can say is that there are contradictory rules. Jumping down a guys throat because he disagrees with you as to which rules are correct is... well, it's not particularly nice, and it's certainly not fair. Especially given that this is a document that is acknowledged to have significant flaws from being built on the bones of the Trinity Core manuscript, and that generally speaking HighPriest is right - If a specific rule later in the book overrules the general rule, you're usually right to follow the specific rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not jumping down his throat because he disagreed with me, I'm mocking him because he threw a fit when it was shown that he got what he wanted, the ability to use Close Combat with Dex, and then went on to complain that because he got what he wanted, the game was therefore &quot;unplayable&quot;. There are 5 specific examples of the Scion: Origin book telling you to use what ever approach, with Close Combat being the specific example, that fits your description best, even if it's not the standard one, and yet you... stubborn individuals... keep wanting the book to be more restrictive then it is, then wanting exceptions to your own perceived restrictions, and after it's pointed out to you that the game is designed to be far more flexible then you are giving it credit for, you get mad at the messenger. I just don't get it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197546#post1197546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, it's not 100%, but Trinity Continuum adds in a sidebar to the combat section specifically stating that &quot;all dice pools listed in this chapter are merely guidelines or suggestions for the most common, or basic dice pool.&quot; It looks like it's certainly intended to just pick an Attribute that makes sense. But I don't think its unreasonable to read the bits saying &quot;The dice pool for melee attacks is Close Combat + Might&quot; and think that this means that the dice pool for melee attacks is Close Combat and Might.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me repost this: &quot;The Skills section on p. XX lists some <b>common pairings</b>, but those are <b>only suggestions.</b>&quot; also &quot;<b>Fights</b> and chases are the most common challenges in the <b>Physical Arena</b>&quot;. This proves that Combat is nothing special in regards to being exempt from the usual rules regarding Arena, and Approach.<br /> <br /> The Knack rules state: &quot;Many Knacks reference Knack Skill rolls. The Storyguide and player choose the most appropriate Skill for each Knack. <b>As usual, the Storyguide chooses the Arena for any Knack Skill roll, and the player chooses an Approach.</b>&quot;.<br /> <br /> Most Boons don't have rolls, but in the Miracle Section under Attacks &quot;Melee attacks are rolled with Close Combat + Might, while ranged attacks are rolled with Occult + Cunning. <b>The Storyguide may let you roll an alternative pool if it fits your marvel.</b>&quot; and then goes on to having the few boons that do have attack rolls roll anything but the aforementioned dice pools.<br /> <br /> Name one place besides the deeply flawed combat chapter that has &quot;Must Roll (X) with (Y)&quot;. The whole system is based on Arena's and Approaches, Combat is simply one more type of roll. Even under the Attack example for Miracles is has a fire attack dice pool that doesn't match the fire attack boon dice pool.<br /> <br /> Everything in this system is designed to be flexible and adapted to the needs of the group and the moment, but the person who wrote the Combat chapter either forgot to put in the side bar about &quot;Common Dice Pools&quot; or never got the memo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","user":"TheSarcasticSage","date":". 03-20-2018, 08:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T05:05:19-07:00","id":1197560,"title":"","content":"Just asked Neall in the Discord, the Attributes given in the combat chapter are strong suggestion# but suggestions nonetheless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T05:05:36-07:00","id":1197561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> yet you... stubborn individuals... keep wanting the book to be more restrictive then it is, and then wanting exceptions to your own perceived restrictions. I just don't get it. </div> </div> </div>You're reading a lot more into what I wrote than I actually put there. <br /> <br /> I agree with you that you pick the most appropriate Attribute. I just think that, given how poorly the Combat section is worded, it's not surprising that people are getting it wrong. <br /> <br /> The general rule is that specific overrules general - I can't point to the bit saying that you only get Enhancement if you get at least one success to disallow the specific Knacks that provide Enhancements before rolling. The specific rule in the Knack section overrules that. <br /> <br /> But the current Combat section is such a poor fit for the actual rules of the game that if you played it Rules As Written, with no sense of judgement, the &quot;correct&quot; reading is the clearly wrong one. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T05:16:14-07:00","id":1197563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197561#post1197561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're reading a lot more into what I wrote than I actually put there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't referencing you specifically. This isn't the first time I've had to point out the flaws of the Combat chapter, and it probably wont be my last, and every time, it's the same series of events.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197561#post1197561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with you that you pick the most appropriate Attribute. I just think that, given how poorly the Combat section is worded, it's not surprising that people are getting it wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not surprised either, it's why I have all my refutations and references bookmarked on my copy of the PDF. What I dislike is peoples stubborn insistence that the rule they don't like, and are trying to find an exception to, must be right, and I, who am trying to help show them that they can in fact do that thing that they want, am wrong. That's what I don't get.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197561#post1197561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The general rule is that specific overrules general - I can't point to the bit saying that you only get Enhancement if you get at least one success to disallow the specific Knacks that provide Enhancements before rolling. The specific rule in the Knack section overrules that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire rule section is written with the premise that the &quot;Specifics&quot; of your own group, and the needs of the moment, will over rule the &quot;general&quot; rules presented in the book. That is the entire basis that the Storypath System is build upon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197561#post1197561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the current Combat section is such a poor fit for the actual rules of the game that if you played it Rules As Written, with no sense of judgement, the &quot;correct&quot; reading is the clearly wrong one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that, which is why I try and point out it's many flaws, and that the actual rules, that allow that &quot;cool thing&quot; that the player/SG wants to do, are already there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T07:08:15-07:00","id":1197587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197563#post1197563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that, which is why I try and point out it's many flaws, and that the actual rules, that allow that &quot;cool thing&quot; that the player/SG wants to do, are already there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, even knowing how it works, I'm still not sure that it actually does what HighPriest is wanting to do. Because according to the Discord, 95% of the time, you should be rolling the dice pools in the combat section. You can't do that <i>and</i> consistently use Dex to attack with Close Combat, as HighPriest wants to do. <br /> <br /> I don't see a situation in which &quot;Use any Attribute you can justify&quot; and &quot;But 95% of the time, it's Might&quot; are going to fit. Because with my players at least, it's going to end up being highest Physical Attribute almost all of the time (The exceptions being the occasional &quot;I attack with Intellect&quot;-type unusual moves). And why wouldn't it be? If you're a dexterous guy, why would you engage in brute force? You're going to use speed and accuracy (And probably light, agile weapons) in order to play to your strengths. If you're seriously into your conditioning, you'll wear them down and attack with Stamina. That's both the sensible, in-universe approach, and the out-of-character optimal approach. <br /> <br /> Also, I'm not sure whether the Purviews/Boons that call for specific dice pools are meant to be optional, or whether that's a part of the power (And if you want a different dice pool you should create a slightly different Boon that comes off a different pool).<br /> <br /> One of the advantages of Epic Strength is literally to change what dice pool you can use for certain actions: <br /> &quot;You can use Strength in place of Presence for intimidation, seduction, or building Bonds of camaraderie&quot; - According to the rules, I can already do that anyway, so why is it there? Moon calls for a Cunning+Legend with its Innate - Once you're pulling in Legend, that's different to the normal Attribute+Skill dice pools - Does it still follow the general &quot;Pick whatever feels right&quot;?<br /> <br /> The attack Boons are fairly specific too - There's no equivocation, it's just a straight &quot;You can attack with [Specific Dice pool]&quot; (Usually Dex&amp;Athletics or [Highest Power Attribute]&amp;Occult) <br /> <br /> And while Knacks use Knack skills for Clashes, Boons seem to have predefined ones. Is that intended to be something the player alters? My understanding is yes (Although, again, the fact that it's Legend rather than Skill+Attribute complicates it), but if that's the case, why are so many words being spent on defining them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T08:11:29-07:00","id":1197608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197587#post1197587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, even knowing how it works, I'm still not sure that it actually does what HighPriest is wanting to do. Because according to the Discord, 95% of the time, you should be rolling the dice pools in the combat section. You can't do that <i>and</i> consistently use Dex to attack with Close Combat, as HighPriest wants to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is Neall HighPriest's SG? I know he's not mine, and I'm pretty sure he's not most peoples SG either. So in a year or so, when the book has come out, and the side bar that is currently missing is there, and all it says is &quot;the skill pairing are suggestions&quot;. How many people are going to care that Neall, in his own house games, has a certain % that he thinks that they should be followed? I won't, and I'm betting that most others wont either. All that matters to me is the opinion of my group, and I bet most everyone else feels the same way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197587#post1197587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see a situation in which &quot;Use any Attribute you can justify&quot; and &quot;But 95% of the time, it's Might&quot; are going to fit. Because with my players at least, it's going to end up being highest Physical Attribute almost all of the time (The exceptions being the occasional &quot;I attack with Intellect&quot;-type unusual moves). And why wouldn't it be? If you're a dexterous guy, why would you engage in brute force? You're going to use speed and accuracy (And probably light, agile weapons) in order to play to your strengths. If you're seriously into your conditioning, you'll wear them down and attack with Stamina. That's both the sensible, in-universe approach, and the out-of-character optimal approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>You right, they don't, because one was a developer ruling (only suggestions), and the other was his personal opinion (he would expect them to be followed ~95%). The two don't mix because the second is irrelevant to the first. It's up to each individual group and SG to determine their own way, as it should be. The rules are mere guidelines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197587#post1197587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I'm not sure whether the Purviews/Boons that call for specific dice pools are meant to be optional, or whether that's a part of the power (And if you want a different dice pool you should create a slightly different Boon that comes off a different pool).<br /> <br /> One of the advantages of Epic Strength is literally to change what dice pool you can use for certain actions:<br /> &quot;You can use Strength in place of Presence for intimidation, seduction, or building Bonds of camaraderie&quot; - According to the rules, I can already do that anyway, so why is it there? Moon calls for a Cunning+Legend with its Innate - Once you're pulling in Legend, that's different to the normal Attribute+Skill dice pools - Does it still follow the general &quot;Pick whatever feels right&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Everything follows this basic general format.<br /> Step 1) You describe your Intent - &quot;I seduce him.&quot;<br /> Step 2) You and the SG determine the appropriate Skill together - &quot;That will be a Persuasion roll&quot; &quot;Right&quot;<br /> Step 3) The SG determines the Arena - &quot;Seducing him will be a social roll&quot;<br /> Step 4) You determine your Approach - &quot;I'm going to be charming and make him want me more then that hussy on his arm. I'm using Presence.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Steps continue, but we've covered the important part that Epic Strength changes. With Epic Strength you can do the Following:<br /> Step 1) You describe your Intent - &quot;I seduce him.&quot;<br /> Step 2) You and the SG determine the appropriate Skill together - &quot;That will be a Persuasion roll&quot; &quot;Right&quot;<br /> Step 3) The SG determines the Arena - &quot;Seducing him will be a social roll&quot;<br /> Step 4) You are allowed to change it from a Social Arena to a Physical Arena if you use Might as your Approach - &quot;But I just finished working out, so I've got my swole on! I'm using Might.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197587#post1197587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The attack Boons are fairly specific too - There's no equivocation, it's just a straight &quot;You can attack with [Specific Dice pool]&quot; (Usually Dex&amp;Athletics or [Highest Power Attribute]&amp;Occult)<br /> <br /> And while Knacks use Knack skills for Clashes, Boons seem to have predefined ones. Is that intended to be something the player alters? My understanding is yes (Although, again, the fact that it's Legend rather than Skill+Attribute complicates it), but if that's the case, why are so many words being spent on defining them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like everything else, it comes down to the Social Contract at the table. The more trust there is, on both sides, the easier the game will run, and the less these discrepancies matter. If I have a Scion of Thor, and I want a Lightning Aura Boon, then the SG and I will have to work together to determine the Effects, Costs, and what the appropriate dice pool would be. This process is no different when there is a player wanting to change the dice pool or Effects of an existing Boon. Discussion and trust are vital in any game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T08:44:21-07:00","id":1197620,"title":"","content":"Guys... Horngeek already posted that he asked Neall about this. The argument has been resolved. &quot;Strong suggestions, but suggestions nonetheless.&quot; There's really no need to keep doing this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T23:51:10-07:00","id":1197897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197556#post1197556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not jumping down his throat because he disagreed with me, I'm mocking him because...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">You can stop right there. That's a rule 1 and 2 violation and unless you feel like having your posting privileges suspended I recommend not doing so again in the future, in any thread on any subject.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T02:57:23-07:00","id":1197918,"title":"","content":"Okay, I\u2019m not answering any rules questions in Discord anymore. They need to be posted here. Thanks all!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T03:14:49-07:00","id":1197921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197918#post1197918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I\u2019m not answering any rules questions in Discord anymore. They need to be posted here. Thanks all!</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. There is a question as to how many Flaws a Relic may have, my reading suggests 1, but it's not explicit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T03:15:54-07:00","id":1197922,"title":"","content":"How would shields generally be represented?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T05:54:24-07:00","id":1197949,"title":"","content":"Another dumb question<br /> <br /> <br /> I noticed that the weapon doesn't have any damage number... or it's just me unable to find it??<br /> <br /> in case there is no damage to the weapon how it works?<br /> <br /> <br /> once i reached with successes the defense of my enemy i deal 1 damage, if i do more successes i can do the stunt damage and deal one more damage<br /> <br /> that's how it work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T06:32:00-07:00","id":1197958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197949#post1197949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another dumb question<br /> <br /> <br /> I noticed that the weapon doesn't have any damage number... or it's just me unable to find it??<br /> <br /> in case there is no damage to the weapon how it works?<br /> <br /> <br /> once i reached with successes the defense of my enemy i deal 1 damage, if i do more successes i can do the stunt damage and deal one more damage<br /> <br /> that's how it work?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Somewhat. Unless I am sorely mistaken, you need to meet the Defense of your target to first hit. At that point, you use any remaining successes to buy stunts, one of which is the &quot;Inflict Damage&quot; stunt, typically costing 1 success (and there is a Critical Hit stunt to do an additional point of damage). It is entirely, 100% possible to hit your target, but have no remaining successes, so you do no damage.<br /> <br /> The way that a weapon can cause more damage is by having an Enhancement, which will typically be a Relic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T07:16:38-07:00","id":1197962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197918#post1197918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I\u2019m not answering any rules questions in Discord anymore. They need to be posted here. Thanks all!</div> </div> </div> </div>One question that comes to mind given the recent revelation that the attributes in the combat section are suggestions, what good is the Epic dex boon that let's you use Dex for any range band in that case?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T07:48:17-07:00","id":1197969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197962#post1197962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One question that comes to mind given the recent revelation that the attributes in the combat section are suggestions, what good is the Epic dex boon that let's you use Dex for any range band in that case?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this one is the fact that Long and Extreme range require Mental attributes (Long = Cunning, Extreme = Intellect). Unerring Flight means that even if you're firing a sniper rifle from a different Field, or if you're firing an ICBM over the horizon, you can still use your Dexterity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23791-ashnak","name":"Ashnak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T12:51:39-07:00","id":1198077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1196520#post1196520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you gain experience for your Band-Term Deed? I'm assuming so (And that it's just not here because copy and paste and it's not a thing in Trinity) but I could also see an argument that it's covered by Story Milestone/Group Story and doesn't generate experience separately.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it doesn't generate experience separately, but it does allow you to increase in Legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T13:01:03-07:00","id":1198081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horngeek</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, asking this here as well- Heroes only get to apply Feats of Scale to singular action for the most part, with a few Boons and Knacks letting you Imbue instead of Spending Legend. Would I be correct in assuming that Demigods and Gods get more ways to perform Feats of Scale on a scene-long or even permanent basis s, or is it just a matter of a God having more Legend to burn than a Hero?</div> </div> </div> </div>You would be correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T13:22:52-07:00","id":1198088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashnak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197969#post1197969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this one is the fact that Long and Extreme range require Mental attributes (Long = Cunning, Extreme = Intellect). Unerring Flight means that even if you're firing a sniper rifle from a different Field, or if you're firing an ICBM over the horizon, you can still use your Dexterity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely this, yes. If you're divine, Epic Dex is a god-stat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T13:24:58-07:00","id":1198089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horngeek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197922#post1197922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would shields generally be represented?</div> </div> </div> </div>Through a tag that adds an Enhancement to the Defense roll. The tricky thing is that if you narrate that you\u2019re using shield or no shield during your Defense roll, you\u2019re stuck with that when your turn comes up, or vice versa. You\u2019re either using your shield to block and bash someone with (and your options for injury are limited) or you\u2019re using your primary weapon, so you can't also be using your shield.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T13:30:31-07:00","id":1198094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashnak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197969#post1197969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this one is the fact that Long and Extreme range require Mental attributes (Long = Cunning, Extreme = Intellect). Unerring Flight means that even if you're firing a sniper rifle from a different Field, or if you're firing an ICBM over the horizon, you can still use your Dexterity.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I originally assumed, but since those apparently aren't a strict requirement it would only come into play if the gm declared dex off limits for certain rolls. I still think it's useful since as a gm I would restrict things like that based on circumstance, but I know people that might argue the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T14:28:56-07:00","id":1198118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1198094#post1198094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's what I originally assumed, but since those apparently aren't a strict requirement it would only come into play if the gm declared dex off limits for certain rolls. I still think it's useful since as a gm I would restrict things like that based on circumstance, but I know people that might argue the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>The GM generally sets the arena (Mental, Social, Physical) and the Player argues the Approach (Force, Finesse, Resistancd).<br /> <br /> If long-range sniping is by and large ruled a MENTAL roll, having high dex is less likely to be justified. Unless you have a Boon that says you can make a ranged attack from any range using Dex, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T14:36:22-07:00","id":1198125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197962#post1197962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question that comes to mind given the recent revelation that the attributes in the combat section are suggestions, what good is the Epic dex boon that let's you use Dex for any range band in that case?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're <i>strong </i>suggestions. You <i>can </i>use any combination of Skills and Attributes - the key factors here are <i>what </i>you're doing (Skill) and <i>how </i>you're doing it (Attribute). You can use your Might to appear lift a refridgerator and prove your virility and seduce someone, for instance - but in a bar, you'd be restricted to flexing your muscles or something. It might not make a ton of sense. Similarly, Might's most often used in Close Combat, but yes, you can use other Attributes if you justify them - the difficulty lies in justifying them, and the Storyguide is the final arbiter there. If you're trying to fight a water horse, Physical Finesse and Resistance aren't going to be as useful as just bashing the thing. <br /> <br /> For the Epic Dex or Epic Strength Boons/innates? You don't need to justify it, it's magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 03-21-2018, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T14:50:49-07:00","id":1198131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197921#post1197921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. There is a question as to how many Flaws a Relic may have, my reading suggests 1, but it's not explicit.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can have a total of five points, especially for character-made ones, but most don't have more than 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T15:01:32-07:00","id":1198139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1198131#post1198131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can have a total of five points, especially for character-made ones, but most don't have more than 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for clarifying that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T15:12:57-07:00","id":1198143,"title":"","content":"Neall,about the Fair Folk,what are your plans for fleshing out in the Bestiary. Specifically,what kind of powers do you think the should have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T16:24:24-07:00","id":1198160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1198131#post1198131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can have a total of five points, especially for character-made ones, but most don't have more than 1.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> wait, sorry<br /> <br /> so you can have just 1 flaw for relic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T16:30:17-07:00","id":1198161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1198160#post1198160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wait, sorry<br /> <br /> so you can have just 1 flaw for relic?</div> </div> </div> </div>All Relics can have a maximum of 5 total points worth of Flaws. Most Relics will only have 1 Flaw (If any at all) of what ever value that Flaw happens to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T20:22:41-07:00","id":1198225,"title":"","content":"A couple questions:<br /> <br /> First --<br /> A relic that provides access to a purview grants a motif that serves as a guide for the marvels that can be performed with that purview.<br /> A purview which allows you to pick a narrowed focus provides a motif which allows the character to work marvels based on it with any purview.<br /> <br /> How is this supposed to work when combined? For example, a scion has a relic that grants access to the Beasts (Jaguar) purview. Do they get one motif that is used in both ways or two motifs, one for each function, or only one of motif options?<br /> <br /> I have not been able to find anything that states how this works one way or the other. The example character Emmanuel Montero has a relic with the Beasts (Jaguar) motif which lists only a single motif, which would imply a certain approach, but doesn't provide a clear answer, especially since I don't know how 'finished' the sample characters are in the preview are considered to be.<br /> <br /> Second --<br /> A weapon can have up to 3 pts in tags; When building a relic based on a weapon which normally uses 2pts of tags and I want to add an additional 2pt tag, does that (a) cost 2 relic dots (for the added 2pt tag) or (b) cost 1 relic dot (for a total of 4 tag pts - 3 'freebie' tag pts)? RAW appears to indicate that (a) is the correct answer, but I thought I would double-check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1039-brennanhawkwood","name":"Brennanhawkwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T22:30:27-07:00","id":1198248,"title":"","content":"There's no mention of a prohibition against Born scions of chaste gods (eg. Artemis). Is this just because it's considered obvious, or to allow for more mythic means of conception?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5727-racain23","name":"racain23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T23:49:32-07:00","id":1198266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>racain23</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1198248#post1198248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no mention of a prohibition against Born scions of chaste gods (eg. Artemis). Is this just because it's considered obvious, or to allow for more mythic means of conception?</div> </div> </div> </div>There <i>is</i> a mention in the Origins Appendix that Artemis and Athena only take Chosen Scions. Maybe it'll be added in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T01:52:24-07:00","id":1198271,"title":"","content":"Neall, question regarding changing your callings by Failure Deed and then Adoption Deed- can you change your Callings until you have none of your Divine Parents' callings this way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T02:04:42-07:00","id":1198273,"title":"","content":"Quick Question,-- if you have Beasts (Owl), does the specialization affect the Innate Power as well?<br /> <br /> i.e., is it &quot;non-legendary animals will not attack you unless compelled by magic,&quot; OR, &quot;non-legendary OWLS will not attack you unless compelled by magic.&quot;<br /> <br /> ...one of these seems WAAAY more limited than the other..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T02:25:40-07:00","id":1198276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1198266#post1198266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There <i>is</i> a mention in the Origins Appendix that Artemis and Athena only take Chosen Scions. Maybe it'll be added in?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I've been a bit lazy about reading origins, I'm finding it a little difficult without all the usual layout/formatting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5727-racain23","name":"racain23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T03:03:34-07:00","id":1198281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1198125#post1198125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're <i>strong </i>suggestions. You <i>can </i>use any combination of Skills and Attributes - the key factors here are <i>what </i>you're doing (Skill) and <i>how </i>you're doing it (Attribute). You can use your Might to appear lift a refridgerator and prove your virility and seduce someone, for instance - but in a bar, you'd be restricted to flexing your muscles or something. It might not make a ton of sense. Similarly, Might's most often used in Close Combat, but yes, you can use other Attributes if you justify them - the difficulty lies in justifying them, and the Storyguide is the final arbiter there. If you're trying to fight a water horse, Physical Finesse and Resistance aren't going to be as useful as just bashing the thing.<br /> <br /> For the Epic Dex or Epic Strength Boons/innates? You don't need to justify it, it's magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, that makes more sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T05:09:11-07:00","id":1198298,"title":"","content":"So... there is no mechanical difference between what kind of scion a player can chooses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T05:41:38-07:00","id":1198302,"title":"","content":"Im upping it again since it didnt get answered.<br /> <br /> I got a question about followers rules, lets imagine i got 5 dots of birthright and outro it on followers i can get 5 tags to then, if i get group/mob/knack/tough/defensive, i would get a mob of 50 followers i na can use a mixed action to comand then to attack twice as mixed action and myself can still give a blow, so it is effectivelly a 3 hits per turn ? Or i got that wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T05:52:26-07:00","id":1198303,"title":"","content":"Not sure if you can share this yet, Neall, but there is one thing I'm kinda curious about. Hero's get one innate Purview. I'm assuming all of the Purviews of a God are innate, and Demigods will have some way of gaining more innate Purviews beyond the one they gain at Hero level. Would that assumption be correct, or am I off base?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1494-deranged-goblin","name":"Deranged Goblin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T08:13:31-07:00","id":1198325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1198298#post1198298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... there is no mechanical difference between what kind of scion a player can chooses?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is not, beyond, y'know, how you describe your Paths. So, there is equal mechanical difference between types of Scion and, say, what your character's job is as compared to another's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T04:13:55-07:00","id":1198606,"title":"","content":"about specialities<br /> <br /> -1 point enhancement to other<br /> <br /> what does it mean??<br /> <br /> if i use a shotgun and i'm specialized with it, the person i'm shooting have a -1 enhancement against me??<br /> <br /> if so, maybe is a little... not so good? I mean, if i have a specialties in art, how am i supposed to use it ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T06:41:52-07:00","id":1198627,"title":"","content":"When do Knacks cost Momentum? I got the impression from the text that Knacks always cost Momentum, but others seem to think that they cost Momentum only if they specifically require it in their text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24028-mike-mccall","name":"Mike McCall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T06:55:27-07:00","id":1198630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1198606#post1198606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">about specialities<br /> <br /> -1 point enhancement to other<br /> <br /> what does it mean??<br /> <br /> if i use a shotgun and i'm specialized with it, the person i'm shooting have a -1 enhancement against me??<br /> <br /> if so, maybe is a little... not so good? I mean, if i have a specialties in art, how am i supposed to use it ?</div> </div> </div> </div>1 Enhancement to other does not mean other characters get any kind of enhancement... instead, if you have a specialty in a skill, it gives an enhancement to your other skills if applicable... if you have a Close Combat specialty of Swords, you have a +1 Enhancement to recognizing a rare sword with Culture. If you have a Medicine specialty in Anatomy, you have a + 1 Enhancement to hitting vital spots on a target with Firearms or Athletics etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T06:56:27-07:00","id":1198631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mike McCall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1198627#post1198627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When do Knacks cost Momentum? I got the impression from the text that Knacks always cost Momentum, but others seem to think that they cost Momentum only if they specifically require it in their text.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't find the exact quote where Neall clarified this, but Knacks only cost Momentum if they specify they do so in the description.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T11:32:15-07:00","id":1198776,"title":"","content":"Early on, it was said that Scions with the Sage Calling could also take Prophet Knacks. Will this still apply?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T09:05:59-07:00","id":1199078,"title":"","content":"Any plans in the near future for a book on those titans that didn't make the Gods' hate list? Those that could have a scion or three floating around?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T09:48:50-07:00","id":1199094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thiagocord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1198302#post1198302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im upping it again since it didnt get answered.<br /> <br /> I got a question about followers rules, lets imagine i got 5 dots of birthright and outro it on followers i can get 5 tags to then, if i get group/mob/knack/tough/defensive, i would get a mob of 50 followers i na can use a mixed action to comand then to attack twice as mixed action and myself can still give a blow, so it is effectivelly a 3 hits per turn ? Or i got that wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It looks that way, but it would all be one Mixed Action, which means you'd be rolling the smallest die pool out of your Attribute+Leadership/Follower rating (so probably 5) and whatever your attack's die pool is. And then you would need to spend the successes across the three sets of Difficulty &amp; Complication. So can you? Sure, but you might run out of successes to spend, not to mention the narrative logistics of having 50 followers, plus yourself, being in a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T11:48:49-07:00","id":1199133,"title":"","content":"Can a relic grant a motif on its own as well as the motif you get if it grants one of the more limited Beast or Artistry focuses, or does that count as its motif? Like Artistry (Fashion) with the motif 'Dressed to Kill' and it comes from a necklace or something which might in turn have its own related motif?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T12:19:09-07:00","id":1199144,"title":"","content":"I know that you start with 2 boons, and gain a new one per legend point/level gained...but do you have access to all the innate powers that your parental lineage allows? Or only the purviews that you have purchased boons in?<br /> <br /> Take Indra-The Storm King. You start with two boons chosen from among Epic Strength, Epic Dexterity, Beasts(Cattle), Fertility, Order, Wild, Sky, and War...that's a lot of boons to choose from...but would you have the innate powers from all those as well, or just say Epic Strength and Sky if that's where you went with your boon choice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T12:25:13-07:00","id":1199147,"title":"","content":"You have to select the ONE purview you inherit innately, and any others you get are from relics. Any purview you have grants the innate power and becomes one you can buy boons from as your legend goes up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T12:41:55-07:00","id":1199153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManBearPig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1199144#post1199144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that you start with 2 boons, and gain a new one per legend point/level gained...but do you have access to all the innate powers that your parental lineage allows? Or only the purviews that you have purchased boons in?<br /> <br /> Take Indra-The Storm King. You start with two boons chosen from among Epic Strength, Epic Dexterity, Beasts(Cattle), Fertility, Order, Wild, Sky, and War...that's a lot of boons to choose from...but would you have the innate powers from all those as well, or just say Epic Strength and Sky if that's where you went with your boon choice?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. You only have innate powers from Purviews you have access to. One of those is from your parent; the other are from Guides or Relics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T12:53:30-07:00","id":1199158,"title":"","content":"Ok, so for example, in my previously stated list: At character creation i pick Strength. That's the innate i have access to. Then my 2nd boon taken is from sky. I then have access to its innate. I buy relic dots that has Order and War...I have access to their innates as long as I have my relic on me?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T13:01:07-07:00","id":1199159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManBearPig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1199158#post1199158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so for example, in my previously stated list: At character creation i pick Strength. That's the innate i have access to. Then my 2nd boon taken is from sky. I then have access to its innate. I buy relic dots that has Order and War...I have access to their innates as long as I have my relic on me?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't buy the Sky Boon since you don't have anything that gives you access to Sky. The rest of it is accurate. You can choose your two Boons from any of Epic Strength, Order or War, as those are the Purviews you can access based on your innate (Strength) and granted by Relics (Order, War).<br /> <br /> In addition, your starting Boons can be from any Purviews you have access to, not just your parent's. If you had a Relic or Guide that gave you access to Darkness, you could buy Darkness Boons at character creation (and would also automatically have access to the Darkness innate power).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 03-24-2018, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T13:57:31-07:00","id":1199172,"title":"","content":"Ok, so You start with 1 innate purview boon, and you get 1 more, but it has to be from either what your relic or guide gives access to. Got it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T14:01:16-07:00","id":1199174,"title":"","content":"I need a good example to understand the difference between Narrative and Drama scale please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T14:03:03-07:00","id":1199175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManBearPig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1199172#post1199172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so You start with 1 innate purview boon, and you get 1 more, but it has to be from either what your relic or guide gives access to. Got it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You start with one innate Purview from your Parent's list. You get the Innate Power for this Purview automatically... but you're not required to buy Boons from it. So both your starting Boons can be from other Purviews. Also note that your Pantheon Specific Purview is always automatically innate and you always have access to it's innate power.<br /> <br /> Edit : Ok, I think I was unclear in my earlier post by completely forgetting to mention innate powers and just talking about Boons... you get the innate power of any Purview you have access to, even if you don't know any Boons from them... including all Purviews you get from Relics and Guides. In your example above you would have the Innate Powers from Strength, War and Order, all three, as well as Yoga, which is always innate for Deva Scions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 03-24-2018, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T14:16:55-07:00","id":1199181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManBearPig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1199172#post1199172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so You start with 1 innate purview boon, and you get 1 more, but it has to be from either what your relic or guide gives access to. Got it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I see part of the problem. You can have access to a Purview without any Boons. If you have a Relic that gives you access to Sky, you don't need to buy Boons to get the Sky Innate power.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, as noted, you have access to the Purviews like so:<br /> <br /> One from your parent (innate)<br /> The Pantheon Signature (innate)<br /> Any Purviews granted to you from Relics or Guides. Please note that these do not have to be from your Divine Parent's list of Purviews.<br /> <br /> Then at Chargen, you pick two Boons. They can be from any of the Purviews you have access to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T14:18:04-07:00","id":1199182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ffanxii4ever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1199094#post1199094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It looks that way, but it would all be one Mixed Action, which means you'd be rolling the smallest die pool out of your Attribute+Leadership/Follower rating (so probably 5) and whatever your attack's die pool is. And then you would need to spend the successes across the three sets of Difficulty &amp; Complication. So can you? Sure, but you might run out of successes to spend, not to mention the narrative logistics of having 50 followers, plus yourself, being in a fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey thanks!<br /> <br /> The logistic problem was solved, that caracter hardly use 50 followers at same time, he is based on azir of league of legends, a scion of ra, he is followers is Sand soldiers who servers him in times of need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T14:38:46-07:00","id":1199199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1199174#post1199174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need a good example to understand the difference between Narrative and Drama scale please.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the difference between someone punching you and you flying back and hitting a car, and someone punching you and putting their fist through you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T14:39:42-07:00","id":1199200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yukikaze</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1198776#post1198776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Early on, it was said that Scions with the Sage Calling could also take Prophet Knacks. Will this still apply?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, prophets are something special, and it needs to be taken with permission.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T14:46:02-07:00","id":1199203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1199200#post1199200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, prophets are something special, and it needs to be taken with permission.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neall,speaking of special things. What are your plans for the Bestiary,especially for the fair folk?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T15:34:02-07:00","id":1199222,"title":"","content":"Are questions in this thread answered in a linear fashion or as they come up?<br /> Since my questions from an earlier post weren't answered I figure I'd add any new questions I had to that post<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GrayWalker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1197161#post1197161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I know this is a load of questions but I'm unsure whether I should make individual posts asking each or just have a compendium post like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the aformentioned post.<br /> <br /> Anyways I have some questions about the five dot Relic flaw that requires a Scion to imbue a dot of Legend into it.<br /> If I have a relic with that flaw at Legend one, that means I can still spend a point of Legends or Imbue it into things that aren't the Relic correct? I just need the relic on my person to be able to use any Legend at all.<br /> <br /> If one loses a Relic with that flaw (let's say it gets destroyed or stolen or something) does one lose Knacks or Boons that weren't tied to said item?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4983-graywalker","name":"GrayWalker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T15:37:29-07:00","id":1199225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1199199#post1199199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's the difference between someone punching you and you flying back and hitting a car, and someone punching you and putting their fist through you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> this is the greatest example ever.<br /> <br /> Thank you.<br /> <br /> Another question related:<br /> <br /> <br /> when a knack, legendary titles or a boon says that you can upgrade by one your scale, wich scale is it talking about? narrative or drama?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12508,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","user":"ElanConnor","date":". 03-24-2018, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T15:50:08-07:00","id":1199229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1199225#post1199225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> this is the greatest example ever.<br /> <br /> Thank you.<br /> <br /> Another question related:<br /> <br /> <br /> when a knack or a boon says that you can upgrade by one your scale, wich scale is it talking about? narrative or drama?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Both, but not quite at the same time. <br /> <br /> See, narrative scale applies to those without Legend, those who are not divine. Mere mortals, in other words. In Neall's example, if you have Epic Strength and you hit some palooka/mook/nobody, you'll put your fist right through them. If you hit someone with Legend, like another PC or an NPC Scion, you only get a bonus Enhancement. You won't have as big an effect because you're innately on an even playing field. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T15:59:45-07:00","id":1199235,"title":"","content":"Actually, it's not \u201cwith or without Legend\u201d; it's \u201cimportant or expendable\u201d in terms of the game. A Legend 1 satyr who's just there for color will suffer the Narrative Scale; a girl without Legend but whose death will impact the game will only suffer the Dramatic Scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T16:14:04-07:00","id":1199243,"title":"","content":"let's findt out if i got it:<br /> <br /> <br /> - The narrative scale is used for the common/normal stuff like: a running person have 0 scale Vs a Ferrari with a x10 scale<br /> <br /> But when divine and magic things appear, there is drama. like: the running scion have half of his legend (if he uses the legendary titles) against the ferrari<br /> <br /> another example: Bruce lee, son of sonwukong, faces a poor drunk racist guy. Usually there is no scale because is human vs human, but as storyteller i decide that bruce lee gain a drama +2 enhance to hit the assholes.<br /> <br /> But the poor guy have A LOT of friends and 20 mobs showes up <br /> <br /> Now is bruce lee vs 21 racists drunks guys. <br /> <br /> as the storyteller, i would not give the scale to bruce lee (except if he uses the legendary titles) but i would give it to the 20 mobs with a X2 successess on the narrative scale (but not the +2 on the drama because they are just trivial characters)<br /> <br /> am i barely right?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T18:16:28-07:00","id":1199271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thiagocord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1199182#post1199182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey thanks!<br /> <br /> The logistic problem was solved, that caracter hardly use 50 followers at same time, he is based on azir of league of legends, a scion of ra, he is followers is Sand soldiers who servers him in times of need.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there is a limit of one attack per round isn't there? So you could have your follows attack, and construct a barricade while you hack a computer, but not shoot twice while you swing a sword at someone's head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T13:11:39-07:00","id":1199458,"title":"","content":"Neall, if you have the time could you answer a question for me, please? Where are Eileen Bran's character stats? I thought she was a cover character for Origins or Hero, so shouldn't they be there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T14:01:33-07:00","id":1199470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1199271#post1199271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there is a limit of one attack per round isn't there? So you could have your follows attack, and construct a barricade while you hack a computer, but not shoot twice while you swing a sword at someone's head.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a limit? I didnt find anything, i think there is a example of \u201cflurry of atacks\u201d on book, i think it should balance it,with that hack my scion can solo even powerfull monsters antagonist level without break sweat, i also give the followers the \u201ceye for eye\u201d knack making it really broken.<br /> <br /> So Neall there is a limit to one attack turn or something like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T15:39:50-07:00","id":1199509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thiagocord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1199470#post1199470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a limit? I didnt find anything, i think there is a example of \u201cflurry of atacks\u201d on book, i think it should balance it,with that hack my scion can solo even powerfull monsters antagonist level without break sweat, i also give the followers the \u201ceye for eye\u201d knack making it really broken.<br /> <br /> So Neall there is a limit to one attack turn or something like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>From Page 131 of the origins preview: &quot;Once initiative is rolled, the round begins. When it is a character\u2019s turn to act, they can take either one simple or one mixed action, though they may only attack once per turn. Reflexive actions can be taken at any time, even if it\u2019s not your character\u2019s turn.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T21:18:06-07:00","id":1199578,"title":"","content":"\u200bWhen you use Beauty's Innate Power to perform a Feat of Scale, do you still spend a point of Legend?<br /> <br /> When you use Earth's Skin of Stone Boon, if you are wearing armor that has the Hard Armor tag but not the Soft Armor, do you get 1 or 3 points of Soft Armor?<br /> <br /> Three-Faced Moon has a cost listed of Free or Imbue 1 Legend, but no details in the text which should apply. I'm guessing it's Imbue if you use it on yourself, since that's the only time it gives an immediate mechanical benefit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T21:52:03-07:00","id":1199582,"title":"","content":"I'm curious if Neall or any of the writers can comment...<br /> <br /> - Is there a plan for how Pantheons and Purviews presented in the Companion will get their Demigod and God level updates?<br /> <br /> - IIRC, Frost was originally going to be in the Companion to be used as an example for building your own Purview. Since it's in the Hero book, will some other new Purview be used to demonstrate that process? (&quot;Toil&quot; and &quot;Aridity&quot; jump to mind as potentially useful examples)<br /> <br /> - Another subject to be addressed in the Companion was how to make a sub-Purview for more &quot;specific&quot; deities. Is that pretty much going to be &quot;Do what Passion, Artistry, and Beast already do with other Purviews. Your-would be Autumnal God can take Fertility but limit it only to reaping fruition and decay, and in exchange you get an appropriate Motif?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T07:24:59-07:00","id":1199710,"title":"","content":"Up my last question/example and add a new question:<br /> <br /> let's findt out if i got it:<br /> <br /> <br /> - The narrative scale is used for the common/normal stuff like: a running person have 0 scale Vs a Ferrari with a x10 scale<br /> <br /> But when divine and magic things appear, there is drama. like: the running scion have half of his legend (if he uses the legendary titles) against the ferrari<br /> <br /> another example: Bruce lee, son of sonwukong, faces a poor drunk racist guy. Usually there is no scale because is human vs human, but as storyteller i decide that bruce lee gain a drama +2 enhance to hit the assholes.<br /> <br /> But the poor guy have A LOT of friends and 20 mobs showes up <br /> <br /> Now is bruce lee vs 21 racists drunks guys. <br /> <br /> as the storyteller, i would not give the scale to bruce lee (except if he uses the legendary titles) but i would give it to the 20 mobs with a X2 successess on the narrative scale (but not the +2 on the drama because they are just trivial characters)<br /> <br /> am i barely right?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Question 2:<br /> <br /> <br /> If a character have the pierce tag and attack a defense 2 character, the pierce attack works even if the defender has no soft/hard armour?? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T07:27:34-07:00","id":1199712,"title":"","content":"Am I missing some critical property of Tianming that makes it more than a restricted subset of Order? The Boons are different of course, but given that a bureaucracy is just humans following a set of authorities and rules I can't think of a marvel Tianming could do that Order couldn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T08:08:09-07:00","id":1199716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1199582#post1199582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- IIRC, Frost was originally going to be in the Companion to be used as an example for building your own Purview. Since it's in the Hero book, will some other new Purview be used to demonstrate that process? (&quot;Toil&quot; and &quot;Aridity&quot; jump to mind as potentially useful examples)</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably! I think it'd be pretty boring to just revisit Frost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Another subject to be addressed in the Companion was how to make a sub-Purview for more &quot;specific&quot; deities. Is that pretty much going to be &quot;Do what Passion, Artistry, and Beast already do with other Purviews. Your-would be Autumnal God can take Fertility but limit it only to reaping fruition and decay, and in exchange you get an appropriate Motif?&quot; </div> </div> </div>I've got some ideas that are a bit more distinctive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T10:06:05-07:00","id":1199748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1199712#post1199712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I missing some critical property of Tianming that makes it more than a restricted subset of Order? The Boons are different of course, but given that a bureaucracy is just humans following a set of authorities and rules I can't think of a marvel Tianming could do that Order couldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are pretty similar, but I would say the big difference would be that Tianming could do more supernatural Marvels, whereas Order has to deal with more human conceptions of authority and laws.<br /> <br /> So while an Order Marvel could potentially fabricate a law, or some sort of response to authority, I would say that Tianming could alter a natural law. For example, an Order Marvel might make all law enforcement personnel hunt somebody down (a divine APB, essentially), a Tianming Marvel could declare that the only divinely-legal dumping ground for bird excrement in the city is the car, house, and head of the person who cut you off in traffic. Sucks to be them.<br /> <br /> Overall, I think it's more that there might not be anything that Order can do, that Tianming can't. At least that's the distinction that I would make at my table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T14:42:30-07:00","id":1199841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1199710#post1199710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Up my last question/example and add a new question:<br /> <br /> let's findt out if i got it:<br /> <br /> <br /> - The narrative scale is used for the common/normal stuff like: a running person have 0 scale Vs a Ferrari with a x10 scale<br /> <br /> But when divine and magic things appear, there is drama. like: the running scion have half of his legend (if he uses the legendary titles) against the ferrari<br /> <br /> another example: Bruce lee, son of sonwukong, faces a poor drunk racist guy. Usually there is no scale because is human vs human, but as storyteller i decide that bruce lee gain a drama +2 enhance to hit the assholes.<br /> <br /> But the poor guy have A LOT of friends and 20 mobs showes up<br /> <br /> Now is bruce lee vs 21 racists drunks guys.<br /> <br /> as the storyteller, i would not give the scale to bruce lee (except if he uses the legendary titles) but i would give it to the 20 mobs with a X2 successess on the narrative scale (but not the +2 on the drama because they are just trivial characters)<br /> <br /> am i barely right?</div> </div> </div> </div>My impression is that it goes like this:<br /> A character/item has Scale (perhaps temporarily) mostly independent of other characters/items/context. A bus is always Size 1, a scion uses her Title to increase Leadership Scale to 2<br /> Dramatic Scale affects anything that would normally involve a roll (a Size 0 scion tries to dodge a Size 1 bus), providing Enhancement to the higher scale<br /> Narrative Scale affects things that normally wouldn't need a roll (that Leadership 2 scion orders civilians to run away). If the specifics are important (how many people run?), you multiply successes.<br /> In general, Scale has Dramatic effects when Scales are within 1 of each other, or when a PC has lower Scale.<br /> Likewise, Scale generally has Narrative effects when Scales differ by 2+, but not when a PC is the lower Scale<br /> <br /> So, to look at your examples:<br /> A running person has Speed 0. A Ferrari has Speed 3. A legend 4 scion of Hermes using their title has Speed 2.<br /> A Ferrari is going to beat the running person, so it's Narrative; if the specifics matter, we give it 10x successes. Likewise, the scion is going to win; if specifics matter, the scion gets 5x successes<br /> When the Ferrari and scion race, we aren't sure who will win and it is important, so it's Dramatic. The Ferarri gets Enhancement 2<br /> <br /> Bruce Lee has Scale 0 unless he's using an ability. Drunk Racist Guy also has Scale 0. A Mob has Scale 1.<br /> When the Mob attacks Guy, Mob wins (Narrative - only 1 difference, but outcome isn't important or in doubt). If the hits/turn matters, Mob gets x2.<br /> When Bruce Lee attacks Guy, he rolls with no Enhancement (no Scale effect). (or, you judge that he wins, and base successes on his Attack Pool / 3)<br /> When Mob attacks Bruce Lee, outcome matters (Dramatic). Mob gets Enhancement 2<br /> If Bruce Lee uses his Title to boost his Scale to 2, he gets Enhancement 2 vs Mob (or you judge that he wins, and give 2 x Attack Pool / 3 successes)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1199710#post1199710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a character have the pierce tag and attack a defense 2 character, the pierce attack works even if the defender has no soft/hard armour??</div> </div> </div> </div>Piercing (2): This weapon is meant to punch through the protective layers of armor. Reduce a target\u2019s armor-granted Defense value by 1 when dealing damage with a weapon with this quality.<br /> <br /> I believe that &quot;armor-granted Defense&quot; = Soft Armor. Or, in the case of antagonists who only have Defense, it's a judgement call as to whether some of it is from armor","signature":"","edited":{"userid":18839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18839-zilaenor","user":"zilaenor","date":". 03-26-2018, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18839-zilaenor","name":"zilaenor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T01:22:41-07:00","id":1200369,"title":"","content":"So, with reference to Supernatural Origin Paths... the Origins book says they establish <i>permissions</i> to take associated Knacks. Does this mean that if my character has the Origin Path &quot;Oracle of Dodona reborn&quot; I now have permission to take Prophet Knacks and slot them into my standard three Calling slots... or do I specifically have to replace a Calling with the Prophet Path? In addition, for God's where it's appropriate, like Inari with Kitsune, could the Origin Path As Calling fulfill the requirement of having to share a Calling with the Divine Parent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T08:42:03-07:00","id":1200444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1200369#post1200369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, with reference to Supernatural Origin Paths... the Origins book says they establish <i>permissions</i> to take associated Knacks. Does this mean that if my character has the Origin Path &quot;Oracle of Dodona reborn&quot; I now have permission to take Prophet Knacks and slot them into my standard three Calling slots... or do I specifically have to replace a Calling with the Prophet Path? In addition, for God's where it's appropriate, like Inari with Kitsune, could the Origin Path As Calling fulfill the requirement of having to share a Calling with the Divine Parent?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I was asking about this... if i make a created character born by the last spark of the great fire that burned the ancient forest of wakanda (i'm sorry, i pushed too far with this example) can i give to him a knack like &quot; born from the fire&quot; that allows him to have the passive of fire?? or making his body her own relic allowing her the purview fire??<br /> <br /> <br /> Another question:<br /> <br /> <br /> How would you create a cape of invisibility as a relic???","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12508,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","user":"ElanConnor","date":". 03-28-2018, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T10:44:32-07:00","id":1200480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1200444#post1200444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you create a cape of invisibility as a relic???</div> </div> </div> </div>There are numerous relics from myth that achieved this effect to take inspiration from if that is of concern.<br /> Hades' Helm of Darkness and Sigurd's magical cloak Tarnkappe granted their wearer's invisibility.<br /> <br /> If your asking from a mechanical perspective look at the description for The Obsidian Butterfly guide in Hero who grants a stunt that allows you to become invisible.<br /> You can probably homebrew it into a knack from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4983-graywalker","name":"GrayWalker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T11:02:54-07:00","id":1200488,"title":"","content":"the obsidian butterfly just gave me a good help, thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T12:11:17-07:00","id":1200513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ffanxii4ever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1199748#post1199748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are pretty similar, but I would say the big difference would be that Tianming could do more supernatural Marvels, whereas Order has to deal with more human conceptions of authority and laws.<br /> <br /> So while an Order Marvel could potentially fabricate a law, or some sort of response to authority, I would say that Tianming could alter a natural law. For example, an Order Marvel might make all law enforcement personnel hunt somebody down (a divine APB, essentially), a Tianming Marvel could declare that the only divinely-legal dumping ground for bird excrement in the city is the car, house, and head of the person who cut you off in traffic. Sucks to be them.<br /> <br /> Overall, I think it's more that there might not be anything that Order can do, that Tianming can't. At least that's the distinction that I would make at my table.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat's disgusting and I can't wait to make it happen in my game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T13:55:47-07:00","id":1200561,"title":"","content":"So... i was asking... how would you do a perception check?? what att+skill? cunning + subterfuge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T15:38:03-07:00","id":1200613,"title":"","content":"Oh great and mighty Neall, I leave this offering of coffee, tea and a cheeseburger in hopes of your answering, for mine is a large list.<br /> <br /> 1. What is the armored tag exactly? Most people I see are guessing it's just Soft Armor, but I haven't been able to find any official answer on this.<br /> <br /> 2. Perhaps I'm just reading it wrong but it feels like Scions are just kind of worse off when it comes to defense. The text makes it seem that Scions roll their defense(Which is based off of their highest resistance attribute) with only a few powers adding to this value. So a scion with some really good stats would roll 5 dice for their defense. With how the rules work, it is very very rare that this will do anything, since you need 2 successes to see any increase in your defense and 5 dice is not a whole lot when you need an 8 or higher. Meanwhile NPCs have static values for defense, making even a defense of 2 much better than what even a really skilled scion can get. Am I just reading things wrong here?<br /> <br /> 3. The versatile tag gives +1 successes towards stunts. Does this include the inflict damage stunt? Or am I misinterpreting this rule?<br /> <br /> 4. The book says when you do a feat of scale that it increases your scale by 1, but I've heard some other people say it increases your scale by half your legend(rounding up I assume). What is correct?<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> 5. Why is the Greatsword an objectively bad weapon? It has lethal, melee, two-handed and unconcealable. That's a total tag cost of -2. Literally any other sharp melee weapon is a better choice. A knife will do just as much damage from what I understand of how damage works, but it can be concealed easily, can be thrown and can be wielded in one hand. It's just so odd to see something be...objectively worse than a knife. <br /> <br /> I hope to hear back from you. :3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24038,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24038-hemata","user":"Hemata","date":". 03-29-2018, 01:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24038-hemata","name":"Hemata","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T15:59:49-07:00","id":1200619,"title":"","content":"I'll second the Armored Tag, and how does the Resistant tag work with say... Adamant Skin? Because we're having a lot of disagreements over what it means on the Discord, and some versions are plain BAD, others SUPER GOOD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T06:03:46-07:00","id":1200774,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this is the right spot to ask, but is there still a way to get the preview documents? Like by pre-ordering the books? I'd really like to start a game with the new system in the near future and I still get flashbacks from the time Exalted spent in layout.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24080-cybertier","name":"cybertier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T07:39:16-07:00","id":1200799,"title":"","content":"i think that takin something in the bakerkit will allow you to have the preview","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T07:55:26-07:00","id":1200804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybertier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1200774#post1200774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if this is the right spot to ask, but is there still a way to get the preview documents? Like by pre-ordering the books? I'd really like to start a game with the new system in the near future and I still get flashbacks from the time Exalted spent in layout.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you go to Backerkit you should be able to pre-order the books, and then get links to the manuscripts","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T08:59:53-07:00","id":1200829,"title":"","content":"Thanks, BackerKit worked <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Is it correct that those documents are already a year old?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24080-cybertier","name":"cybertier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T09:38:08-07:00","id":1200840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1200561#post1200561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... i was asking... how would you do a perception check?? what att+skill? cunning + subterfuge?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> \u200bIt depends. Are you looking for someone sneaking up on you? Yes. Are you looking for a concealed weapon? Firearms or Close Combat + Cunning, are you looking for a tell? Manipulation (I think) + Empathy. A lie? Subterfuge + Composure. A forgery? Academics + Cunning.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm pretty sure Manipulation is social perception/intelligence. Cunning is obviously your perceptibility and mental awareness. Composure is your ability to notice bullshit.<br /> <br /> \u200bAt least that's how I interpreted it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T11:49:17-07:00","id":1200906,"title":"","content":"Is Huehuecoyotl not supposed to have the Beasts (Coyote) Purview? Because he doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T10:48:33-07:00","id":1201322,"title":"","content":"How exactly is grappling supposed to work? The description of the &quot;Grappled&quot; condition doesn't seem to have much in common with the rules presented under the Grapple action. Which also don't seem to refer to the &quot;establish grapple&quot; stunt, since they talk about &quot;success equal to the number of successes your opponent spent establishing the grapple&quot;, but the establish stunt only requires the one success.<br /> <br /> Also this may just be me, but it seems weird that you can't Disarm or Seize someone your grappling, because wrestling someone for a weapon or artifact seems quintessentially Heroic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T14:52:23-07:00","id":1201423,"title":"","content":"i was wondering:<br /> <br /> if you want to use the marvels for a generic purview you have to take it with the relic and the motiff<br /> <br /> if you want to use the marvels of your pantheon specific purview, you can use the motiff of your pantheon<br /> <br /> but... what about the marvels of the Innate purview you choose in the creation phase?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12508,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","user":"ElanConnor","date":". 03-30-2018, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T15:19:01-07:00","id":1201433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1201423#post1201423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i was wondering:<br /> <br /> if you want to use the marvels for a generic purview you have to take it with the relic and the motiff<br /> <br /> if you want to use the marvels of your pantheon specific purview, you can use the motiff of your pantheon<br /> <br /> but... what about the marvels of the Innate purview you choose in the creation phase?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Pantheon Motif can be used to create Marvels for any Purview... including Purviews you get from Relics/Guides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T18:03:30-07:00","id":1201491,"title":"","content":"Are guides restricted to granting access to only one purview?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4983-graywalker","name":"GrayWalker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T23:29:00-07:00","id":1201547,"title":"","content":"Was looking at the Devas and I was wondering (Apologies if there has been an answer to this already) Origin Appendix states that the asset skills are Firearms, Survival yet in Hero it states that under the Pantheon Path of the Dev\u00e1s that their Asset Skills are Athletics, Survival.... So <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar137_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"137\" data-vbnamecard=\"137\">Neall</a> I'm curious as to which one? With all the discussion about their ability to unleash hell I would assume Firearms was correct as it comes in the form of an arrow mostly.... but Athletics? What would be the reasoning there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/488-blackwood","name":"Blackwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar488_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T00:45:57-07:00","id":1201557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1201547#post1201547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was looking at the Devas and I was wondering (Apologies if there has been an answer to this already) Origin Appendix states that the asset skills are Firearms, Survival yet in Hero it states that under the Pantheon Path of the Dev\u00e1s that their Asset Skills are Athletics, Survival.... So <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> I'm curious as to which one? With all the discussion about their ability to unleash hell I would assume Firearms was correct as it comes in the form of an arrow mostly.... but Athletics? What would be the reasoning there?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are aware of the skill inconsistencies, so those'll be resolved in the next draft (whether that's another text-only or the backer pdf I don't know). I'm pretty sure Athletics covers all pre-gunpowder ranged weapons, so that'd explain the choice","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18839-zilaenor","name":"zilaenor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T01:30:59-07:00","id":1201565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1201433#post1201433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Pantheon Motif can be used to create Marvels for any Purview... including Purviews you get from Relics/Guides.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, really? Doesn't it completely negate the point of Relics having Motifs at all if you can circumvent them by saying a prayer or doing a quick tai chi exercise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T03:16:32-07:00","id":1201570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1201565#post1201565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, really? Doesn't it completely negate the point of Relics having Motifs at all if you can circumvent them by saying a prayer or doing a quick tai chi exercise?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> i think that is a matter of specific case scenario<br /> <br /> i mean: with the azlanti motif you can get bonusses performing rituals. but with the same motiff you can't, for example, cast a fireball.<br /> <br /> To cast the fireball you need the right motiff on your relics","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T03:39:41-07:00","id":1201572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1201570#post1201570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> i think that is a matter of specific case scenario<br /> <br /> i mean: with the azlanti motif you can get bonusses performing rituals. but with the same motiff you can't, for example, cast a fireball.<br /> <br /> To cast the fireball you need the right motiff on your relics</div> </div> </div> </div>The examples make it pretty clear to me that you perform a ritual to cast the fireball. For example:<br /> <br /> &quot;Nikasios, Scion of Athena, offers up a prayer to Uncle Ares asking to borrow some firepower as an Order marvel, and receives a police-issue riot taser.&quot;<br /> <br /> A taser isn't thematically linked to prayer. Prayer is just the means by which a Theoi Scion invokes arbitrary Marvels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T04:02:16-07:00","id":1201579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1201565#post1201565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, really? Doesn't it completely negate the point of Relics having Motifs at all if you can circumvent them by saying a prayer or doing a quick tai chi exercise?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I could tell, Purviews from Relics use their own motifs, all other purviews use your pantheon's motif or motifs you make from things like Art and Beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T04:49:05-07:00","id":1201585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1201579#post1201579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I could tell, Purviews from Relics use their own motifs, all other purviews use your pantheon's motif or motifs you make from things like Art and Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my initial reading, too, but going back through the text I can't find anywhere where it actually says that. There's this passage tho:<br /> <br /> &quot;Most of the time, you\u2019ll use the Motif associated with the pantheon you belong to. Relics also have their own motifs, which you can call upon when you perform marvels of the Purviews associated with that Relic. Finally, it\u2019s also possible to gain motifs from miscellaneous sources, such as a sacred animal chosen through the Beasts Purview (p. XX).&quot;<br /> <br /> Which still isn't explicit, but sounds more consistent with Samudra's interpretation. There's also this sentence:<br /> <br /> &quot;He may only channel a Purview the Relic provides and his Pantheon Signature Purview through its motif for marvels.&quot;<br /> <br /> But it's not clear to me if that means &quot;he has to channel the granted Purview through the Relics motif&quot; or &quot;the motif can only be used with the granted Purview&quot;<br /> <br /> e: also Motifs from Beasts etc. explicitly say they work with &quot;all&quot; of your Purviews, so I presume they work with Relic Purviews as well. They'd be pretty useless otherwise, and btw are equally useless if you can just naturally use your pantheon motif for Relics","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","user":"Terrorforge","date":". 03-31-2018, 07:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T05:57:40-07:00","id":1201590,"title":"","content":"It's pretty clear here that relics are limited to their motifs:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Relic Section</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Motif: A short phrase that determines the scope of the marvels that a Scion can \u2014 and<br /> thus, can\u2019t \u2014 perform through the Relic. For instance, Eric Donner\u2019s Giantsbane has a motif of<br /> \u201cthe flash and fury of the thunderstorm.\u201d It can perform Sky marvels that are forceful and flashy,<br /> but couldn\u2019t call up a gentle breeze or cause the sun to shine.</div> </div> </div> </div>as for &quot;&quot;He may only channel a Purview the Relic provides and his Pantheon Signature Purview through its motif for marvels.&quot;<br /> That means that you can use Giantsbane with Sky and whatever your pantheon signature preview is through it's (the relics) motif.<br /> <br /> There isn't any text suggesting you can use your pantheon's motif to use a purview gained from a relic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 03-31-2018, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T08:44:51-07:00","id":1201632,"title":"","content":"This relic motif line of questioning seems like a good time to ask something I did before but didn't see answered: How does the use of one of the limiting motifs from Beasts or Artistry apply if you get it through a relic? Like say you have a sweet necklace with a jaguar's fang on it that gives you Beasts (Jaguars) and the motif 'King of the Night' through hitting on the themes they're the largest predatory cat in the Americas and night time stalking themes.<br /> <br /> Can you then use King of the Night as a motif with the Darkness purview you know innately? Or your PSP?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T09:35:05-07:00","id":1201649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1201572#post1201572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The examples make it pretty clear to me that you perform a ritual to cast the fireball. For example:<br /> <br /> &quot;Nikasios, Scion of Athena, offers up a prayer to Uncle Ares asking to borrow some firepower as an Order marvel, and receives a police-issue riot taser.&quot;<br /> <br /> A taser isn't thematically linked to prayer. Prayer is just the means by which a Theoi Scion invokes arbitrary Marvels.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but a taser is linked to order. Which is granted by praying. This seems to be a case of the scion using the marvel to gain equipment, through the motif of praying, and receiving said taser. If you perform a ritual to throw a fireball the ritual would have to be done prior to the fight to grant you the attack form of the marvel, then you can throw around fireballs for the fight.<br /> <br /> So by gagging a Theo scion, you deny him his marvels. A teotl would need a few moments and a way to sacrifice some of their blood or something to use a marvel as another example.<br /> <br /> It seems pantheon motifs are intended to be things you do out of combat mostly. Rituals, prayers, and sacrifices all take time. So Giantsbane would be useful to use if you needed to rapidly summon a wind to blow a flying truck out of your way by pointing it and pulling the trigger, but you can still sit and scribble some runic symbols when it isn't urgent. Otherwise Relic motifs would be a burden, wouldn't they?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T11:41:34-07:00","id":1201675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1201649#post1201649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, but a taser is linked to order. Which is granted by praying. This seems to be a case of the scion using the marvel to gain equipment, through the motif of praying, and receiving said taser. If you perform a ritual to throw a fireball the ritual would have to be done prior to the fight to grant you the attack form of the marvel, then you can throw around fireballs for the fight.<br /> <br /> So by gagging a Theo scion, you deny him his marvels. A teotl would need a few moments and a way to sacrifice some of their blood or something to use a marvel as another example.<br /> <br /> It seems pantheon motifs are intended to be things you do out of combat mostly. Rituals, prayers, and sacrifices all take time. So Giantsbane would be useful to use if you needed to rapidly summon a wind to blow a flying truck out of your way by pointing it and pulling the trigger, but you can still sit and scribble some runic symbols when it isn't urgent. Otherwise Relic motifs would be a burden, wouldn't they?</div> </div> </div> </div>The trouble is that there's absolutely nothing in the rules or examples that suggests they're time consuming. The rules say invoking a marvel is a simple action, and all the examples are of things that could easily be simple actions like drinking a potion or crushing a handful of rose petals.<br /> <br /> And yes, my argument is that Relic motifs are supposed to be burdens. They're supposed to limit the ways in which the relics Purview can be used. If you can use your pantheon motif with them, that burden disappears, which is why even if it's meant to work that way, it shouldn't.<br /> <br /> Or it should be clarified that it takes time as you suggest or rejigger the pantheon motifs do they have actual restrictions, whichever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T13:07:30-07:00","id":1201684,"title":"","content":"Who is Mammon in Scion? He's definitely not one of the old Canaanite deities, so do references to him imply the existence of a Devil pantheon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T14:07:14-07:00","id":1201695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1201675#post1201675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The trouble is that there's absolutely nothing in the rules or examples that suggests they're time consuming. The rules say invoking a marvel is a simple action, and all the examples are of things that could easily be simple actions like drinking a potion or crushing a handful of rose petals.<br /> <br /> And yes, my argument is that Relic motifs are supposed to be burdens. They're supposed to limit the ways in which the relics Purview can be used. If you can use your pantheon motif with them, that burden disappears, which is why even if it's meant to work that way, it shouldn't.<br /> <br /> Or it should be clarified that it takes time as you suggest or rejigger the pantheon motifs do they have actual restrictions, whichever.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> but pantheon motiffs do put limits on marvels<br /> <br /> I mean: for the teotl you have to perform a sacrifice.<br /> <br /> As a gamemaster i would not let you throw a fireball sacrificing a rabbit in the middle of a fight. That's because teolt performs miracles with sacrifices, that's their limit. So the manitou and maybe Devas.<br /> <br /> But with a shen with alchemy motiff and elemental shit? Fuck yeah. Cast a rune of fire with Aesir? Great. Drink peppermind and chilli dragon pees with loa stuff? Incredible.<br /> <br /> <br /> You have to put limits, just how it says on the manual &quot; if your motif is &quot; with the fury of the storm&quot; you can't use a light breeze as a marvel&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T14:38:16-07:00","id":1201709,"title":"","content":"If my divine parent has a specific version of a purview, eg. Beasts (Monkey), can I take the more general version of the purview as my innate purview? Or can I take this purview with a different specification even, eg. Beasts (Bear)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5727-racain23","name":"racain23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T14:43:25-07:00","id":1201710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1201684#post1201684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who is Mammon in Scion? He's definitely not one of the old Canaanite deities, so do references to him imply the existence of a Devil pantheon?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I dont think its clarified. But my own take is that Mammon is a scion from an unknown parentage (probably on purpose) that took/found the name Mammon and made it his own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T14:50:08-07:00","id":1201711,"title":"","content":"technically speaking i would put mammon into the Eloim antagonists since he's one of the lucifer commander","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T15:49:50-07:00","id":1201726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1201711#post1201711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">technically speaking i would put mammon into the Eloim antagonists since he's one of the lucifer commander</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Elohim are a Canaanite/Phoenician Pantheon (including such figures as the brothers Ba'al Hadad, Yam, and Mot; and the virgin goddess Anat), they're unlikely to incorporate Medieval Christian lore.<br /> <br /> That said figures like Mammon could be descended from them but broke away in the Middle Ages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-31-2018, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T00:50:23-07:00","id":1201871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1201695#post1201695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> but pantheon motiffs do put limits on marvels<br /> <br /> I mean: for the teotl you have to perform a sacrifice.<br /> <br /> As a gamemaster i would not let you throw a fireball sacrificing a rabbit in the middle of a fight. That's because teolt performs miracles with sacrifices, that's their limit. So the manitou and maybe Devas.<br /> <br /> But with a shen with alchemy motiff and elemental shit? Fuck yeah. Cast a rune of fire with Aesir? Great. Drink peppermind and chilli dragon pees with loa stuff? Incredible.<br /> <br /> <br /> You have to put limits, just how it says on the manual &amp;quot; if your motif is &amp;quot; with the fury of the storm&amp;quot; you can't use a light breeze as a marvel&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;sacrifice&quot; mentioned in the examples is crushing a handful of rose petals. It's pretty minor, and demanding big concessions like that from e.g. Teotl players instead of taking a spell component pouch attitude and assuming they usually have what they need would be a pretty shitty move when their Theoi friends can just say &quot;yeah I pray to Hera&quot; in any situation.<br /> <br /> You see the thing is that Relic motifs determine what you can do, but the pantheon motif determines HOW you do it. They don't seem to have any restrictions whatsoever, apart from the really extreme cases where for example a Deva can't recite spells if you cut their tongue out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T00:51:59-07:00","id":1201872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>racain23</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1201709#post1201709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If my divine parent has a specific version of a purview, eg. Beasts (Monkey), can I take the more general version of the purview as my innate purview? Or can I take this purview with a different specification even, eg. Beasts (Bear)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes to both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T01:19:45-07:00","id":1201876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1201872#post1201872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes to both.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5727-racain23","name":"racain23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T09:35:37-07:00","id":1201942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1201871#post1201871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The &quot;sacrifice&quot; mentioned in the examples is crushing a handful of rose petals. It's pretty minor, and demanding big concessions like that from e.g. Teotl players instead of taking a spell component pouch attitude and assuming they usually have what they need would be a pretty shitty move when their Theoi friends can just say &quot;yeah I pray to Hera&quot; in any situation.<br /> <br /> You see the thing is that Relic motifs determine what you can do, but the pantheon motif determines HOW you do it. They don't seem to have any restrictions whatsoever, apart from the really extreme cases where for example a Deva can't recite spells if you cut their tongue out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say it's big concessions. Sure it's logical to assume a Teotl Hero would carry around something most of the time, but if they get jumped getting out of the pool they probably don't have the pouch of quicky sacrifices in hand and might have to make a mad scramble to get them. Or if someone is captured and has their potions taken away, or are bound up and gagged and can't dance or pray.<br /> <br /> The Theoi have the issue of their divine family are a bunch of petty jerks and might not like being invoked too often, especially if a scion of Hephestus keeps bugging his Uncle Ares for example. Don't think of them as penalties, think of them as chances to make life interesting.<br /> <br /> Or look awesome by having your scion of Zeus annoy Hera on purpose by asking for help against &quot;This chick that kind looks like Leda&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T09:45:28-07:00","id":1201945,"title":"","content":"Can we please get some clarification on how the Virtue Track is intended to work? The Virtuous condition seems clear enough, but under the Momentum entry it states that the any action taken to advance one of the virtues also grants extra dice when Momentum is spent on the roll that shifts virtue. Is the Virtuous condition only for Saints then? What are the requirements for a roll to be virtuous enough to cause a shift?, and how often can it happen? I assume there's some restrictions, otherwise a Tuatha D\u00e9 Danann Scion could peg that Prowess virtue in the course of a single battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/972-fairlyhyperman","name":"Fairlyhyperman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T12:52:42-07:00","id":1201993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1201942#post1201942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't say it's big concessions. Sure it's logical to assume a Teotl Hero would carry around something most of the time, but if they get jumped getting out of the pool they probably don't have the pouch of quicky sacrifices in hand and might have to make a mad scramble to get them. Or if someone is captured and has their potions taken away, or are bound up and gagged and can't dance or pray.<br /> <br /> The Theoi have the issue of their divine family are a bunch of petty jerks and might not like being invoked too often, especially if a scion of Hephestus keeps bugging his Uncle Ares for example. Don't think of them as penalties, think of them as chances to make life interesting.<br /> <br /> Or look awesome by having your scion of Zeus annoy Hera on purpose by asking for help against &amp;quot;This chick that kind looks like Leda&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>And all that is great, but it's pretty narrow narrative stuff. It's pretty much never going to happen unless the SG (and/or antagonist) goes out of their way to make it so, and Relic motifs only coming into play when you've gotten a facefull of kryptonite seems like a waste of a really cool mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T13:58:32-07:00","id":1202012,"title":"","content":"I am confused entirely by the &quot;virtue track&quot;. Is there a section in either book i must have skimmed past?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T16:17:08-07:00","id":1202046,"title":"","content":"Does a Hero with Somebody's Watching Me still just get Mooks or a Professional, or do they upgrade to Foes or a Rival once they stop being Origin-tier?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T16:28:36-07:00","id":1202048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1201993#post1201993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And all that is great, but it's pretty narrow narrative stuff. It's pretty much never going to happen unless the SG (and/or antagonist) goes out of their way to make it so, and Relic motifs only coming into play when you've gotten a facefull of kryptonite seems like a waste of a really cool mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I suppose that way does make a bit more sense since you are channeling through the relic. I imagine it's at least partially GM fiat until we get clarification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T11:29:53-07:00","id":1202270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManBearPig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1202012#post1202012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am confused entirely by the &quot;virtue track&quot;. Is there a section in either book i must have skimmed past?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in Origins, page 192, under Saints. I think Neall said he'll see about putting the Virtue Explanation in the Hero book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T12:11:03-07:00","id":1202278,"title":"","content":"So, I'm a little confused about Creature Birthrights.<br /> <br /> Hero has the following text in that section:<br /> Examples have been provided in Chapter 6: Storyguiding (p. XX),<br /> listed by how many dots in the Creature Birthright would be required to obtain that creature as a<br /> companion.<br /> <br /> However, I can't find those examples.<br /> <br /> Trying to extrapolate from the guidance given would suggest looking at Flairs + Primary Pool. Would Qualities also be included? Or do Creatures just get all of their qualities? Consider the Nemean Lion: Is it Creature 3 (9 Pool + 0 Flairs) or Creature 5 (9 Pool + 0 Flairs + 3 Qualities)?<br /> <br /> Further confusing things is that the Building the Creature section of Hero suggests Miasmic Presence as an example of a Flair/Knack, listed as a Sandbag in Origin, and a Quality in the Antagonist examples.<br /> <br /> Disclaimer: This is a x-post from another thread but didn't get any traction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18560-saedar","name":"saedar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T15:33:58-07:00","id":1202761,"title":"","content":"Is soothing presence only meant to reduce negative attitude? Or is the calming effect meant to move them towards the middle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T06:19:45-07:00","id":1202963,"title":"","content":"The Paramour references that at Fatebinding Strength 1-3, invoking it lets you get a single use of a Soul or Heroic Lover Knack.<br /> <br /> What's a Soul Knack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T13:50:51-07:00","id":1203123,"title":"","content":"Cross posting from Discord:<br /> <br /> Origins question: If I take a Birthright (such as a Relic) that provides access to a Purview, do I still get access to the Innate Power, even if I don't have any Legend and thus have no access to Marvels or Boons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T09:48:54-07:00","id":1203436,"title":"","content":"A Judge Knack references dealing Stress or a -1 Injury.<br /> <br /> What's Stress, in this context?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T10:41:47-07:00","id":1203451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorsRattus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1203436#post1203436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Judge Knack references dealing Stress or a -1 Injury.<br /> <br /> What's Stress, in this context?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's some kind of health equivalent? There are references to a stress track like the injury track and two of the example antagonists (SWAT and Men in Black) seem to have Stress instead of Health. Unfortunately the significance of stress vs injury doesn't seem to be explained anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T11:25:04-07:00","id":1203466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1203451#post1203451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's some kind of health equivalent? There are references to a stress track like the injury track and two of the example antagonists (SWAT and Men in Black) seem to have Stress instead of Health. Unfortunately the significance of stress vs injury doesn't seem to be explained anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Health boxes in Fate are called Stress. Maybe it was a working title that missed being changed in places?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T12:40:39-07:00","id":1203485,"title":"","content":"Do marvels that end up being costless due to no real mechanical or major narrative effect count against your 1/scene limit on marvels?<br /> <br /> Why do marvels have a 1/scene limit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T22:29:07-07:00","id":1203719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saedar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1202278#post1202278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm a little confused about Creature Birthrights.<br /> <br /> Hero has the following text in that section:<br /> Examples have been provided in Chapter 6: Storyguiding (p. XX),<br /> listed by how many dots in the Creature Birthright would be required to obtain that creature as a<br /> companion.<br /> <br /> However, I can't find those examples.<br /> <br /> Trying to extrapolate from the guidance given would suggest looking at Flairs + Primary Pool. Would Qualities also be included? Or do Creatures just get all of their qualities? Consider the Nemean Lion: Is it Creature 3 (9 Pool + 0 Flairs) or Creature 5 (9 Pool + 0 Flairs + 3 Qualities)?<br /> <br /> Further confusing things is that the Building the Creature section of Hero suggests Miasmic Presence as an example of a Flair/Knack, listed as a Sandbag in Origin, and a Quality in the Antagonist examples.<br /> <br /> Disclaimer: This is a x-post from another thread but didn't get any traction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am also really confused by the Creature Birthright. For something so integrel to your character's story there needs to be a clearer way of making a creature instead of refer to antagonist knacks for your flairs at the cost of 2 dice out of your pool. It doesn't really state where your flairs should be spent but looking over them I could quite easily make a godlike beast that could take out anything with some of those antag knacks stacked. So could it be a bit clearer what we are supposed to do please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/488-blackwood","name":"Blackwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar488_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T05:51:34-07:00","id":1203798,"title":"","content":"Does the innate power of the Beauty Purview still cost 1 Legend when you want your action to be a Feat of Scale, but allow you to do so without relying on a Keyword or Title, or does it just make <i>all</i> relevant actions Feats of Scale automatically?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T10:13:56-07:00","id":1205645,"title":"","content":"So kinda tricky question. The Hero text says that spent Legend can be regained through Fatebinding and Sacrifice. Sacrifice is broken down into major and minor, with characters only able to benefit from minor once per arc but major is unlimited but hard to get. Here is a quote:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Major sacrifices tend to involve multiple scenes (sometimes entire sessions) of effort to acquire, and/or have potential consequences severe enough that even a Scion would not undertake them lightly.<br /> <br /> Human sacrifice is major, but so is burning a masterfully crafted handmade effigy or offering the last cigar from a box that formerly belonged to an Incarnation of Eshu. Scarification, bloodletting, and other ritual self-mutilation are minor sacrifices, which result in accepting an Injury Condition. </div> </div> </div>The first part seems to define a major sacrifice by the degree of effort required to acquire it. The second part makes it really easy (with downsides) if you are evil enough because humans are super plentiful. The part I really want to ask about is the middle ground &quot;Masterfully crafted handmade effigy.&quot;<br /> <br /> I have real life experience helping someone make by hand a large ornamental cross to donate to a church, putting in an hour or two a day for two weeks to make it. That would be a Major Sacrifice.<br /> <br /> However in the game, if a character goes deep into the Creator Knacks (with Afternoon of Fortnights and Flawlessly Platonic Ideal) and the Forge Domain (Innate power, Celestial Artifice, and possibly While the Iron is Hot) they could knock out that same project, and do it better, in a single scene with time to spare.<br /> <br /> On one hand, this wasn't &quot;hard&quot; for the player to do so it shouldn't count as a Major Sacrifice. On the other hand, the absolute value of the sacrifice is really high and it is the result of a <i>great</i> deal of work on the character's part to get that good, and from the player perspective it was a very large investment of character resources that could have been used to make them more combat or socially optimized. And it is definitely more significant than a Minor Sacrifice of a garland of flowers or some cigarettes/alcohol. So how do you rule it?<br /> <br /> Ok, big question out of the way. Now for a quick follow-up on further crafting shenanigans<br /> <br /> Crafting your own relics requires being Demigod tier. If a Hero also has Guide then they can do this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Scion may also call upon his guide for a deus ex machina once per arc. Only one deus ex machina may be in effect at a time. Whether by literal divine intervention, occult ritual, the fulfillment of a dire prophecy, or some other method within the guide\u2019s power, the Scion gains the following for the rest of the scene: <b>He acts in all ways as though he were one Tier higher than he is,</b> and may use one boon he doesn\u2019t know in a Purview to which he has access. In exchange, at the end of the scene, he gains the Tempted Fate Condition. </div> </div> </div>If they gather the materials as unrolled milestones then trigger Deus Ex Machina right before they hammer it all together and perform a ritual in one scene, does it work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4862,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4862-sequal","user":"Sequal","date":". 04-11-2018, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4862-sequal","name":"Sequal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4862_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T08:04:54-07:00","id":1206026,"title":"","content":"another question here:<br /> <br /> <br /> So, the books says &quot; if you already have a legend and perform a minor or a major sacrifice you will get an extra legend to imbue or spend&quot;<br /> <br /> This is pretty clear but... Can a character &quot;keep&quot; the extra legend point for some amount of time?? if so, how much time will keep it before lose it?<br /> <br /> Me and my players decided that a character can keep the extra legend point for &quot;24HoursXLegend&quot;, seem fair, no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T09:46:45-07:00","id":1206049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1206026#post1206026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">another question here:<br /> <br /> <br /> So, the books says &quot; if you already have a legend and perform a minor or a major sacrifice you will get an extra legend to imbue or spend&quot;<br /> <br /> This is pretty clear but... Can a character &quot;keep&quot; the extra legend point for some amount of time?? if so, how much time will keep it before lose it?<br /> <br /> Me and my players decided that a character can keep the extra legend point for &quot;24HoursXLegend&quot;, seem fair, no?</div> </div> </div> </div>By my reading (Golden Rule, etc.), you can only have one point of Legend available at any time, but as a 1-Legend character and that point in your pool, you can certainly:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">1) Drive your armored car off a cliff, dedicating the sacrifice to your father Ioskeha, gaining a point of Legend, and immediately Imbue it into your Bear-Warrior's Bludgeon to activate the Dizzying Blow Stunt for the scene;<br /> 2) Offer a burnt offering to Geezhigo-Quae to gain a point of Legend, and immediately invoke your Legendary Title &quot;The Dark Knight, defender of the City&quot; to defend Gotham City all night using Eternal Guardian,<br /> 3) Accept a Fatebinding to gain an Apprentice (The SG decides a local circus performer becomes impressed by your aerial acrobatics during your nightly patrol) and immediately Imbue that point of Legend to Bless yourself with a +2e Marvel from the Darkness purview to help you avoid detection.</div> <br /> The end result of this is 1 Legend available, 3 Legend Imbued. At any time, you can release that Imbue to have another point available, but you can only have one free at a time. You could:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">1) Spend 1 Legend on a Darkness Marvel, to create Arcing, Piercing, Bashing missiles out of freezing Darkness itself<br /> 2) Release the Darkness blessing to recover a point of Legend<br /> 3) Spend 1 Legend on Unerring Flight to knock a Mook's gun out of his hand with your new Darkness missiles (definitely not boomerangs, no sir),<br /> 4) Release the Dizzying Blow activation,<br /> 5) Spend 1 Legend on Unbreakable to completely ignore the shotgun blast fired by your Nemesis, the purple-suited son of Nana'b'oozoo<br /> 6) Compel that young Apprentice to jump between you and the acid stream from the Laughing Clown, which forces you to split your next action (Why is he dressed in red and yellow? Does he want to be a target?), but gives you one point of Legend,<br /> 7) Spend your last point of Legend to summon a night-black motorbike to you, as a Darkness Equipment Marvel.<br /> 8) Release your Eternal Guardian to recover a point of Legend.</div> <br /> That's at Legend 1. and you still end with 1 Legend in your pool at the end. At the end of the Scene, you lose all of your Imbued powers, but you still have 1 Legend available for the next scene.<br /> <br /> Just for bookkeeping, and to keep me honest, I used one Knack (Immortal Guardian: Eternal Guardian), and two Boons across three Purviews (Darkness: three Marvels; Epic Dexterity: Unerring Flight; Epic Stamina: Unbreakable). This is a valid level 1 character, with a Birthright armor that gives him access to Epic Dexterity and Epic Stamina. He has Dodaem and Darkness as innate purviews.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23791-ashnak","name":"Ashnak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T12:53:42-07:00","id":1206135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashnak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1206049#post1206049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By my reading (Golden Rule, etc.), you can only have one point of Legend available at any time, but as a 1-Legend character and that point in your pool, you can certainly:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">1) Drive your armored car off a cliff, dedicating the sacrifice to your father Ioskeha, gaining a point of Legend, and immediately Imbue it into your Bear-Warrior's Bludgeon to activate the Dizzying Blow Stunt for the scene;<br /> 2) Offer a burnt offering to Geezhigo-Quae to gain a point of Legend, and immediately invoke your Legendary Title &quot;The Dark Knight, defender of the City&quot; to defend Gotham City all night using Eternal Guardian,<br /> 3) Accept a Fatebinding to gain an Apprentice (The SG decides a local circus performer becomes impressed by your aerial acrobatics during your nightly patrol) and immediately Imbue that point of Legend to Bless yourself with a +2e Marvel from the Darkness purview to help you avoid detection.</div><br /> The end result of this is 1 Legend available, 3 Legend Imbued. At any time, you can release that Imbue to have another point available, but you can only have one free at a time. You could:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">1) Spend 1 Legend on a Darkness Marvel, to create Arcing, Piercing, Bashing missiles out of freezing Darkness itself<br /> 2) Release the Darkness blessing to recover a point of Legend<br /> 3) Spend 1 Legend on Unerring Flight to knock a Mook's gun out of his hand with your new Darkness missiles (definitely not boomerangs, no sir),<br /> 4) Release the Dizzying Blow activation,<br /> 5) Spend 1 Legend on Unbreakable to completely ignore the shotgun blast fired by your Nemesis, the purple-suited son of Nana'b'oozoo<br /> 6) Compel that young Apprentice to jump between you and the acid stream from the Laughing Clown, which forces you to split your next action (Why is he dressed in red and yellow? Does he want to be a target?), but gives you one point of Legend,<br /> 7) Spend your last point of Legend to summon a night-black motorbike to you, as a Darkness Equipment Marvel.<br /> 8) Release your Eternal Guardian to recover a point of Legend.</div><br /> That's at Legend 1. and you still end with 1 Legend in your pool at the end. At the end of the Scene, you lose all of your Imbued powers, but you still have 1 Legend available for the next scene.<br /> <br /> Just for bookkeeping, and to keep me honest, I used one Knack (Immortal Guardian: Eternal Guardian), and two Boons across three Purviews (Darkness: three Marvels; Epic Dexterity: Unerring Flight; Epic Stamina: Unbreakable). This is a valid level 1 character, with a Birthright armor that gives him access to Epic Dexterity and Epic Stamina. He has Dodaem and Darkness as innate purviews.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> understand your point but there is some problem with the time intended to do the sacrifice<br /> <br /> <br /> if i'm running away from policeman i can't make a sacrifice to get a legend because i need an entire scene to do the ritual<br /> <br /> or am i just misunderstood in how much time a character can make a minor ritual?<br /> <br /> <br /> the teotl pantheon motiff says that you can take a single action to make a sacrifice, for the minor sacrifice you need a scene, am i right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T14:16:51-07:00","id":1206160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1206135#post1206135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> understand your point but there is some problem with the time intended to do the sacrifice<br /> <br /> <br /> if i'm running away from policeman i can't make a sacrifice to get a legend because i need an entire scene to do the ritual<br /> <br /> or am i just misunderstood in how much time a character can make a minor ritual?<br /> <br /> <br /> the teotl pantheon motiff says that you can take a single action to make a sacrifice, for the minor sacrifice you need a scene, am i right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of this is Narrative vs. Dramatic timing. In my first two gain-and-imbue examples, the actual creation/acquisition of the Sacrifices (e.g. building the not-the-Batmobile) takes time, but I would allow the sacrific<i>ing</i> to happen quickly.<br /> <br /> However, sometimes it makes sense for a sacrifice to take a while - if stopping it would create good narrative tension, or if you're trying to stop an opponent's Sacrifice. In that case, I would require it to take time.<br /> <br /> Of course, it's all subjective.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23791-ashnak","name":"Ashnak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T15:41:02-07:00","id":1206180,"title":"","content":"Am I alone in feeling that, a) this all seems really ungainly in an action-oriented game, and b) it doesn't seem terribly true to the myths? Where are the stories of god-blooded heroes stopping to make an offering before every great feat or deed? Do you have to make a sacrifice/offering in order to use the very powers that define Scions? Honestly, it just seems like a clunky &quot;game balance&quot; rule to me, akin to the blood pool or paradox for vampires or mages - something designed solely to limit power use in-game. Maybe I'm missing something, but I'm not thrilled with the mechanics of this at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T20:56:58-07:00","id":1206261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1206180#post1206180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I alone in feeling that, a) this all seems really ungainly in an action-oriented game, and b) it doesn't seem terribly true to the myths? Where are the stories of god-blooded heroes stopping to make an offering before every great feat or deed? Do you have to make a sacrifice/offering in order to use the very powers that define Scions? Honestly, it just seems like a clunky &quot;game balance&quot; rule to me, akin to the blood pool or paradox for vampires or mages - something designed solely to limit power use in-game. Maybe I'm missing something, but I'm not thrilled with the mechanics of this at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Unless, I'm misinterpreting the rules, you're usually only going to get 1 or possibly 2 Legend in most sessions. Even that will usually come from Fatebinding, which seems more reliable than sacrifice, though it comes with its own issues - I'm concerned that it will prove far more work for the ST, possibly too much to keep up with for 4-5 characters each working on multiple Fatebindings by the higher ends of Hero. Which is a shame, because I like the concept of some of the stuff you can do with Legend, but I don't see less mechanically optimal options like invoking your Title happening at the current cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T00:06:48-07:00","id":1206805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1206180#post1206180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I alone in feeling that, a) this all seems really ungainly in an action-oriented game, and b) it doesn't seem terribly true to the myths? Where are the stories of god-blooded heroes stopping to make an offering before every great feat or deed? Do you have to make a sacrifice/offering in order to use the very powers that define Scions? Honestly, it just seems like a clunky &amp;quot;game balance&amp;quot; rule to me, akin to the blood pool or paradox for vampires or mages - something designed solely to limit power use in-game. Maybe I'm missing something, but I'm not thrilled with the mechanics of this at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stories of heroes do in fact frequently feature sacrifice. I'm sure it varies from pantheon to pantheon, but it's a frequent motif in Norse mythology at least. Plenty of both offhand mentions and stories that specifically revolve around sacrifices made, failed, promised etc.<br /> <br /> Now the Legend system IS obviously an RPG balancing mechanic. It's not like the heroes of the sagas performed sacrifice to recharge some innate divine power they had, but the notion that a juicy sacrifice to the gods could replenish your vigor and bend fate (even to an overtly supernatural degree) in your favor wasn't plucked out of thin air.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T02:43:23-07:00","id":1206835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1206180#post1206180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I alone in feeling that, a) this all seems really ungainly in an action-oriented game, and b) it doesn't seem terribly true to the myths? Where are the stories of god-blooded heroes stopping to make an offering before every great feat or deed? Do you have to make a sacrifice/offering in order to use the very powers that define Scions? Honestly, it just seems like a clunky &quot;game balance&quot; rule to me, akin to the blood pool or paradox for vampires or mages - something designed solely to limit power use in-game. Maybe I'm missing something, but I'm not thrilled with the mechanics of this at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's supposed to be ungainly... Gods don't tend to listen to prayers without a little flair. Heroes in the Illiad pray to the Gods all the time... most of the time the Gods don't actually reply. Ravana makes hundreds of sacrifices to Shiva... it's not until he starts cutting his own heads off that Shiva so much as glances his way. Heroes stop to make offerings before every great deed because that is just the done thing when dealing with Gods... Actually catching their attention requires something big, and this is totally in line with myth.<br /> <br /> Hero Characters have access to powerful Knacks, mystical Relics, terrifying creatures, devoted followers and wise Guides... they have an entire suite of mythic abilities that does not depend on Legend at all, and many of these, like Immortal Knacks and Relic Powers, are explicitly there to make Legend costs cheaper.<br /> <br /> You say you might be missing something Purple... maybe it's all that? The fact that Purviews are neither the only powers Scions have, nor the 'definitive' ones. Heroes of myth are much more strongly tied to, and likely to use, their archetypal prowess, their mentors and weapons, their magic items and familiars, than they are to call down lightning-strikes willy-nilly. And as the game is designed right now, with the help of Fatebindings you can <i>already</i> do that twice a session... And that is only against actual challenges, that are meant to be, you know, challenging, and achieved at a cost... against trivial opponents you actually <i>can</i> throw lightning bolts all day because, as is pointed out in the book, affecting trivial targets is free. How much more of a power boost do you think Heroes need?<br /> <br /> I'm actually seriously asking that question, because between Relics, Knacks and Innate Purview Powers Heroes already seem pretty powerful to me, and that's ignoring the Boons and Marvels that only Imbue Legend. They need somewhere to grow to at Demigod and God.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 04-14-2018, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T06:52:21-07:00","id":1206867,"title":"","content":"Nitpick: IIRC, one of the things about Marvels is that they <i>never</i> Imbue Legend: by definition, if you're attempting the Marvel equivalent of a Boon that would Imbue Legend, you must expend Legend instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T06:54:35-07:00","id":1206868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1206867#post1206867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nitpick: IIRC, one of the things about Marvels is that they <i>never</i> Imbue Legend: by definition, if you're attempting the Marvel equivalent of a Boon that would Imbue Legend, you must expend Legend instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bActually you <i>do</i> imbue Legend in Marvels, just not ones that emulate Boons. For example, the Marvel that lets you summon equipment. You imbue Legend in that, get the equipment and use it until you reclaim that Legend, at which point it either vanishes or just isn't being used and fades between scenes, whichever seems more appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T07:09:29-07:00","id":1206872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1206867#post1206867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nitpick: IIRC, one of the things about Marvels is that they <i>never</i> Imbue Legend: by definition, if you're attempting the Marvel equivalent of a Boon that would Imbue Legend, you must expend Legend instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did actually mean what CreepyShutIn has already pointed out... Marvels that copy Boons <i>do</i> cost Spent Legend, but there are a lot of Marvel types that don't. Also, the thing with trivial targets still applies... so if you were to copy Bolt From The Blue as a Marvel against a bunch of trivial targets, it would still be free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T10:11:32-07:00","id":1206933,"title":"","content":"On reflection, I think perhaps that it's not so much that I missed something, as that I'm perhaps not gung-ho about trying to run/play something where the PCs <i>need </i>relics, guides, companions, and creatures to be all that they can be. I'm not arguing mythical accuracy on that point, I'm just not sure how tough that would be to keep track of, let alone hide from the mortals to avoid the fatebinding mechanic. It's just my personal tastes, I guess. I've been running a very Scion-like game for many years now, and in my experience, players don't like obvious game-system baggage and limitations on their power. And, frankly, I don't either. But that's just me, and I'm kind of picky about stuff anyway. I still hate &quot;come up with an appropriate sacrifice to use your Purview&quot; as a mechanic, but I could just house-rule it away if I wanted to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T10:38:09-07:00","id":1206946,"title":"","content":"why avoid fatebinding?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T10:55:51-07:00","id":1206950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1206933#post1206933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On reflection, I think perhaps that it's not so much that I missed something, as that I'm perhaps not gung-ho about trying to run/play something where the PCs <i>need </i>relics, guides, companions, and creatures to be all that they can be. I'm not arguing mythical accuracy on that point, I'm just not sure how tough that would be to keep track of, let alone hide from the mortals to avoid the fatebinding mechanic. It's just my personal tastes, I guess. I've been running a very Scion-like game for many years now, and in my experience, players don't like obvious game-system baggage and limitations on their power. And, frankly, I don't either. But that's just me, and I'm kind of picky about stuff anyway. I still hate &quot;come up with an appropriate sacrifice to use your Purview&quot; as a mechanic, but I could just house-rule it away if I wanted to.</div> </div> </div> </div>This just seems like a fundamental disconnect between the game you were hoping to play and the one the developers made at this point. Birthrights are important to myth, they appear in stories across the world for all Pantheons, and this is ultimately a game about myths. I will just note though, that there is no Masquerade, so why you would need to hide from mortals is lost on me, and Fatebindings are accepted and even partially designed by the Player, so you don't really have to explicitly <i>do</i> anything to avoid them. Fate is a carrot, not a stick, and the carrot is the regained Legend point. Also, Purviews do not require you to perform sacrifices... most Boons Imbue Legend instead of spending it, so you'll get it back, Fatebindings can help you get back at least your permanent Legend worth of Legend points back every session, so you can spend Legend and still have a way to readily get them back, and using Purviews on trivial targets remains free, so you can happily set entire restaurants full of random people on fire if you so wish.<br /> <br /> But honestly, all those options have been pointed out to you already, and I feel like we're going in circles at this point, so I hope you can homebrew the game to something of your liking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T13:57:03-07:00","id":1207006,"title":"","content":"I didn't find anything conclusive to answer my question so here it goes:<br /> <br /> The scale table describes the first 3 ranks as: Standard, Elite and Supernatural.<br /> This implies that once someone breaks a certain profiency treshhold they count as a scale higher, but it's never really specified in the rules.<br /> For example:<br /> Does the Strongest Mortal Alive (Might 5, Athletics 5) count as &quot;Standard&quot; scale for Feats of strength?<br /> Does he count as Elite?<br /> Does he count only as Elite if he is an NPC?<br /> Does he count as Elite when he gets a Visitation by his daddy Susano-O?<br /> Or only after getting Epic Strength and thus (through the inate boon) putting him at +1 Scale for Feats of Strength?<br /> <br /> The last seems to be what the rules imply, but wouldn't really fit into the scale table, since narratively that puts him clearly on the Supernatural spot on the Table, but rules-wise only at Elite.<br /> In the last case removing the Elite step from the table would simplify things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24080-cybertier","name":"cybertier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T18:06:44-07:00","id":1207091,"title":"","content":"For me, I found Fatebinding in 1st edition [and, to a lesser extent, in 2nd edition] to be too much of a ball-and-chain on the characters. If you use your full powers in godly fashion [which is why you are playing a game about gods in the first place, yes?], you run the risk of being Fatebound to not only mortals, but even entire cultures [as stated in the Hero rules preview], with your view of the world being affected by these bonds - &quot;[Fatebinds] act to define a God and how the God\u2019s relationships will play out in the future, which is another reason many Gods are careful to stay in the Overworld&quot;. So the system is designed to encourage development from mortal to God, then to tie you down with a mechanic that limits how much you can openly do unless you want a culture's expectations changing your very perception of your &quot;self&quot;. Too much &quot;stick&quot;, not enough &quot;carrot&quot; for my tastes. Yes, the sacrifice rule is optional - don't do a sacrifice if you don't want the Legend point - but what's the purpose of playing a divine character who can't use their full divine power without making time-consuming sacrifices and risking stalkers? It balances out power use vs. consequences, true, and maybe it fits with legends in some cultures, but it just seems that the whole concept of the game is supposed to be about <i>gaining</i> power, not limiting it. [Obviously, people disagree with my perceptions, and that's fine; different strokes, and all]<br /> Yes, I am aware of the role companions [and relics/creatures/followers] play in mythology; I'm no expert, but I have read a fair bit of folklore and mythology in my time, partly out of interest, partly for gathering info for my own campaign. Giving <i>options</i> for including such things is great - it just feels to me that there are too many aspects of playing [particularly] the Demigod/God level characters that are limited by game mechanics that take away too much player/GM freedom.<br /> I wonder; how many people are buying this game to play a faithful recreation of real mythology and religion [which it certainly seems to be trying hard to be], and how many are buying it because they think playing Gods [read; divine superheroes like Marvel's Thor] will be a blast?<br /> Perhaps this isn't the game system for me - that's fine, I'll add it to my collection and pillage the excellent mythology stuff for inspiration. It wouldn't be the first game that had bits I liked and bits I didn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T19:04:11-07:00","id":1207114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1207091#post1207091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, I found Fatebinding in 1st edition [and, to a lesser extent, in 2nd edition] to be too much of a ball-and-chain on the characters. If you use your full powers in godly fashion [which is why you are playing a game about gods in the first place, yes?], you run the risk of being Fatebound to not only mortals, but even entire cultures [as stated in the Hero rules preview], with your view of the world being affected by these bonds - &quot;[Fatebinds] act to define a God and how the God\u2019s relationships will play out in the future, which is another reason many Gods are careful to stay in the Overworld&quot;. So the system is designed to encourage development from mortal to God, then to tie you down with a mechanic that limits how much you can openly do unless you want a culture's expectations changing your very perception of your &quot;self&quot;. Too much &quot;stick&quot;, not enough &quot;carrot&quot; for my tastes. Yes, the sacrifice rule is optional - don't do a sacrifice if you don't want the Legend point - but what's the purpose of playing a divine character who can't use their full divine power without making time-consuming sacrifices and risking stalkers? It balances out power use vs. consequences, true, and maybe it fits with legends in some cultures, but it just seems that the whole concept of the game is supposed to be about <i>gaining</i> power, not limiting it. [Obviously, people disagree with my perceptions, and that's fine; different strokes, and all]<br /> Yes, I am aware of the role companions [and relics/creatures/followers] play in mythology; I'm no expert, but I have read a fair bit of folklore and mythology in my time, partly out of interest, partly for gathering info for my own campaign. Giving <i>options</i> for including such things is great - it just feels to me that there are too many aspects of playing [particularly] the Demigod/God level characters that are limited by game mechanics that take away too much player/GM freedom.<br /> I wonder; how many people are buying this game to play a faithful recreation of real mythology and religion [which it certainly seems to be trying hard to be], and how many are buying it because they think playing Gods [read; divine superheroes like Marvel's Thor] will be a blast?<br /> Perhaps this isn't the game system for me - that's fine, I'll add it to my collection and pillage the excellent mythology stuff for inspiration. It wouldn't be the first game that had bits I liked and bits I didn't.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Uh i think i'm getting an inkling to what a lot of people are complaining about.<br /> I notice that you keep mentionning demigods/gods. Like how they are affected by fatebinding and its the reason they stick to the overworld. Or that people would want to play a god like thor.<br /> Except the books we are getting are Origin and Hero, not Demigod and God (well not yet). <br /> So far we cant play the likes of Thor (marvel or mytho) they are firmly in the scales of Demigods at least. First we'll be playing the likes of Jason of the argonauts, Beowulf (pre-grendel) and Hercules (pre 12 labors). We start with those that havent had they deeds sung by anyone. You need somewhere to start before you fling lightnings willy-nilly.<br /> <br /> As for fatebinding, i think the problem is a mix between in 1st ed fatebinding being harsh (like you said) and the scion team warning about fatebinding a bit too well for 2nd ed. I mean, at hero lvl fatebinding would barely count as an annoyance. <br /> <br /> So i dont think your wrong in your concerns so much as mixing the books and what they offer. <br /> <br /> Also i want to say that i really relate to your last sentence. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1207091#post1207091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wouldn't be the first game that had bits I liked and bits I didn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T21:20:57-07:00","id":1207149,"title":"","content":"How much does an Immortal Knack cost in terms of XP?<br /> <br /> The general consensus at the moment seems to be that &quot;a knack is a knack is a knack,&quot; and <i>all</i> knacks cost 10xp each. Heroic or Immortal. You still have to have two dots of calling to slot an Immortal Knack and make it &quot;active&quot; though.<br /> <br /> ...if this is the case..<br /> <br /> Do you start with &quot;five dots worth of knacks&quot; at character creation, or &quot;five knacks&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you elect to get two bonus knacks, instead of +4 birthright dots, can you purchase two immortal knacks? Or does a single one use both 'free knacks' that you get?<br /> <br /> Or, are Immortal Knacks supposed to cost 20xp, which eliminates all of the above problems, even if it makes them.. very expensive...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T21:44:33-07:00","id":1207157,"title":"","content":"I'm a little bit confused on the Manitou' s Dream virtue. What behavior is it exactly trying to encourage? What type of conflict it brings? What's it's relationship with Pride? I feel like I don't have a clear grasp on that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T11:04:54-07:00","id":1207335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1207091#post1207091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, I found Fatebinding in 1st edition [and, to a lesser extent, in 2nd edition] to be too much of a ball-and-chain on the characters. If you use your full powers in godly fashion [which is why you are playing a game about gods in the first place, yes?], you run the risk of being Fatebound to not only mortals, but even entire cultures [as stated in the Hero rules preview], with your view of the world being affected by these bonds - &quot;[Fatebinds] act to define a God and how the God\u2019s relationships will play out in the future, which is another reason many Gods are careful to stay in the Overworld&quot;. So the system is designed to encourage development from mortal to God, then to tie you down with a mechanic that limits how much you can openly do unless you want a culture's expectations changing your very perception of your &quot;self&quot;. Too much &quot;stick&quot;, not enough &quot;carrot&quot; for my tastes. Yes, the sacrifice rule is optional - don't do a sacrifice if you don't want the Legend point - but what's the purpose of playing a divine character who can't use their full divine power without making time-consuming sacrifices and risking stalkers? It balances out power use vs. consequences, true, and maybe it fits with legends in some cultures, but it just seems that the whole concept of the game is supposed to be about <i>gaining</i> power, not limiting it. [Obviously, people disagree with my perceptions, and that's fine; different strokes, and all]<br /> Yes, I am aware of the role companions [and relics/creatures/followers] play in mythology; I'm no expert, but I have read a fair bit of folklore and mythology in my time, partly out of interest, partly for gathering info for my own campaign. Giving <i>options</i> for including such things is great - it just feels to me that there are too many aspects of playing [particularly] the Demigod/God level characters that are limited by game mechanics that take away too much player/GM freedom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Different strokes and all aside, you have some very negative opinions on Fatebinding based largely on how they are going to play out in Demigod &amp; God, books which aren't written yet. We have a general sense of how these things affect Scions from what is more or less fluff text in the Hero book, but to me it doesn't make sense to make assumptions about how limiting those things are going to be in the future.<br /> <br /> I realize that you don't like the effects of Fatebinding even at a Hero level, and that's your business. But don't try to justify your opinions with non-existent data.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24028-mike-mccall","name":"Mike McCall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T20:09:42-07:00","id":1207504,"title":"","content":"I'm not. The passage on fatebinding that I quoted, was from the Scion Hero 2nd edition text that backers received not too long ago. Hardly &quot;non-existent data&quot;. And yes, I am concerned with how rules will affect the Demigod and God books, even though they aren't out yet, because Origins, Hero, Demigod and God aren't four separate games - they are one progressing game that takes your character from mortal Scion to God of whatever. So I don't think it's unreasonable to reflect on how game systems impact the development of those same characters.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm off-topic for this thread, and will now end my comments on this particular matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5627,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","user":"Purple Snit","date":". 04-16-2018, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T06:47:13-07:00","id":1207635,"title":"","content":"I still think you're extrapolating to an unreasonable degree, but since I'm also not on board with your perspective at all, there's no real reason to debate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24028-mike-mccall","name":"Mike McCall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T23:56:00-07:00","id":1207904,"title":"","content":"So invoking a Path allows you to &quot;add two dice to any roll that plausibly applies to your Path&quot;<br /> This is a very rare example of adding dice rather than an Enhancement (the only other that comes to mind is Momentum) so I just wanted to know: is this an intentional departure from standard procedure or is it a mistake and it should give some amount of Enhancement instead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T02:54:05-07:00","id":1208378,"title":"","content":"So about the Beauty Purview innate power:<br /> <br /> It says that you may attempt a Feat of Scale when you roll to influence a character using<br /> your beauty, appearance, and body language.<br /> <br /> Is this like invoking your Legendary title, where you need to spend a point of Legend? There's a boon in Epic Strength that explicitly says the you can make a Feat of Scale without spending a point of Legend, and it limits it to once a scene.<br /> <br /> If you don't have to spend a point of Legend, it seems overly powerful, as it doesn't limit the effect to once per scene.<br /> If you do have to spend a point of Legend, then the innate power seems very weak, as it is the only innate power that requires spending Legend to get any use out of it. Sun and Moon both have the option to spend Legend, but there's also a free base effect to use.<br /> <br /> If Legendary Titles are a special type of path, that means that they can each be invoked once per session, and a use of that invocation is to make a Feat of Scale. Is the intent that Beauty provides a way to make Feats of Scale in terms of attraction as often as you have Legend to spend on it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/458-indivisible","name":"Indivisible","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T14:50:16-07:00","id":1209411,"title":"","content":"Maybe jumping the gun, but I have some questions about future books:<br /> <br /> 1) Considering that Origins and Hero will likely be out this year, will we be seeing a Kickstarter for Demigod and God this year too?<br /> <br /> 2) Can you elaborate on how Relics are supposed to &quot;grow&quot; with characters as they advanced (as stated in Hero's section on Birthrights)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T04:02:43-07:00","id":1210358,"title":"","content":"So, I noticed that on page 140 of origins, in the text-description of what stats to use at what range-bands, it says &quot;Might OR Dexterity&quot; for Short and &quot;Dexterity OR Cunning&quot; for Medium, but in the table later, it jut has &quot;Dexterity&quot; listed for Short, and just has &quot;Cunning&quot; listed for Medium. Which is it? I can see the argument for both ways, both from a rules-lawyerey perspective and from a game design perspective. On the one hand, player choice/agency seems to be a general thing that's promoted, as well as PC exceptionalism, which meshes with the material, so... point for the &quot;either/or&quot; reading. On the other hand, this makes dexterity an obvious &quot;dump-stat&quot; for combat-focussed scions worried about using different stats at different range-bands, reducing the number of stats they have to care about to Might and Cunning, which could cause a decrease in build-variation. I was just wondering which was intended.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1206950#post1206950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will just note though, that there is no Masquerade, so why you would need to hide from mortals is lost on me</div> </div> </div> </div>Many people have been running Scion a certain way for years already, and aren't going to change to a completely new genre just because we got a better set of rules. From the gyst of it (though I must admit I'm not about to pour through backlogs of forum) Purple seems to have an existing Scion group that's interested in testing out the new rules with their existing game. I myself am in the same boat with my group, and ideally, the new rules SHOULD be able to easily run games with or without &quot;the masquerade&quot; regardless of what the new default setting is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1576-mjorkk","user":"mjorkk","date":". 04-23-2018, 07:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1576-mjorkk","name":"mjorkk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T09:17:55-07:00","id":1210446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mjorkk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1210358#post1210358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I noticed that on page 140 of origins, in the text-description of what stats to use at what range-bands, it says &quot;Might OR Dexterity&quot; for Short and &quot;Dexterity OR Cunning&quot; for Medium, but in the table later, it jut has &quot;Dexterity&quot; listed for Short, and just has &quot;Cunning&quot; listed for Medium. Which is it? I can see the argument for both ways, both from a rules-lawyerey perspective and from a game design perspective. On the one hand, player choice/agency seems to be a general thing that's promoted, as well as PC exceptionalism, which meshes with the material, so... point for the &quot;either/or&quot; reading. On the other hand, this makes dexterity an obvious &quot;dump-stat&quot; for combat-focussed scions worried about using different stats at different range-bands, reducing the number of stats they have to care about to Might and Cunning, which could cause a decrease in build-variation. I was just wondering which was intended.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Neil has stated that the Attributes listed are just strong suggestions, but if the gm accepts the reasoning any can be used (I think as long as it's the same physical for physical, social for social and mental for mental. Not sure if the boon rolls and defense rolls are the same though).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T12:52:49-07:00","id":1210552,"title":"","content":"Thank you. I don't have discord, so often miss the comments made there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1576-mjorkk","name":"mjorkk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T16:18:01-07:00","id":1210668,"title":"","content":"Would Hecate have godly or titan virtues? I suppose one could argue both depending on mantle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T11:16:23-07:00","id":1211065,"title":"","content":"I have a second question about how enhancement interacts with opposed rolls. Is it the pre-enhancement or the post-enhancement rolls that determine which side won, since in this case number of successes matters.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: after multiple re-reads, I THIIINK I've got it<br /> <br /> If there is a clear attacker and defender in the opposed action THEN the defender rolls first, thus their enhancement does in-fact contribute to setting the difficulty, then the attacker rolls against the now-set dificulty. This does make enhancement more valuable on the defensive side of an opposed roll, but this seems to gel with the direction of the general game: favoring defenders.<br /> <br /> If there is NOT a clear defender, then FIRST both roll WITHOUT enhancement, thus determining the attacker and defender, then both parties roll enhancement, though only the newly defined &quot;attacker&quot; can really do anything with the resulting successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1576-mjorkk","user":"mjorkk","date":". 04-24-2018, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1576-mjorkk","name":"mjorkk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T17:29:04-07:00","id":1211235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1207904#post1207904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So invoking a Path allows you to &quot;add two dice to any roll that plausibly applies to your Path&quot;<br /> This is a very rare example of adding dice rather than an Enhancement (the only other that comes to mind is Momentum) so I just wanted to know: is this an intentional departure from standard procedure or is it a mistake and it should give some amount of Enhancement instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, that's totally legit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T06:16:32-07:00","id":1211385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mjorkk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1211065#post1211065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a second question about how enhancement interacts with opposed rolls. Is it the pre-enhancement or the post-enhancement rolls that determine which side won, since in this case number of successes matters.<br /> <br /> Edit: after multiple re-reads, I THIIINK I've got it<br /> <br /> If there is a clear attacker and defender in the opposed action THEN the defender rolls first, thus their enhancement does in-fact contribute to setting the difficulty, then the attacker rolls against the now-set dificulty. This does make enhancement more valuable on the defensive side of an opposed roll, but this seems to gel with the direction of the general game: favoring defenders.<br /> <br /> If there is NOT a clear defender, then FIRST both roll WITHOUT enhancement, thus determining the attacker and defender, then both parties roll enhancement, though only the newly defined &quot;attacker&quot; can really do anything with the resulting successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless I am sorely mistaken, Enhancement applies to every (applicable) roll that you achieve at least one success on, regardless if it is an opposed roll or a fixed difficulty. So if an attacker with a pool of 6 dice and +3e and a defender with a pool of 8 dice and +2e are going head-to-head and both roll 1 success on their pools, the attacker will win. So only post-enhancement rolls matter (in a sense). Also, you don't roll enhancement, it is (essentially) bonus successes, not dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T16:20:53-07:00","id":1211603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ffanxii4ever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1211385#post1211385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless I am sorely mistaken, Enhancement applies to every (applicable) roll that you achieve at least one success on, regardless if it is an opposed roll or a fixed difficulty. So if an attacker with a pool of 6 dice and +3e and a defender with a pool of 8 dice and +2e are going head-to-head and both roll 1 success on their pools, the attacker will win. So only post-enhancement rolls matter (in a sense). Also, you don't roll enhancement, it is (essentially) bonus successes, not dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm....not sure why, but until now I've been under the impression that enhancement was bonus dice that you only got to roll after succeeding to spend on stunts. It made sense in my mind that outside of avoiding dififculty/complication from inappropriate scale, legend wouldn't make you succeed when you would otherwise fail, but it would make your successes more EPIC. Hmm, this changes a lot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1576-mjorkk","name":"mjorkk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T04:14:39-07:00","id":1211732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mjorkk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1211603#post1211603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm....not sure why, but until now I've been under the impression that enhancement was bonus dice that you only got to roll after succeeding to spend on stunts. It made sense in my mind that outside of avoiding dififculty/complication from inappropriate scale, legend wouldn't make you succeed when you would otherwise fail, but it would make your successes more EPIC. Hmm, this changes a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>You still have to roll at least one success. So you don't auto succeed a diff 2 roll because you have 3e, because you still need the the one from the roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T17:16:43-07:00","id":1212071,"title":"","content":"Hello folks in the Ask Neall thread! I know, I know, I've been absent for a while. But this weekend I'm going through the last few pages and I'll answer everything, I swear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T19:44:48-07:00","id":1212113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1212071#post1212071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello folks in the Ask Neall thread! I know, I know, I've been absent for a while. But this weekend I'm going through the last few pages and I'll answer everything, I swear.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's ok Neall, we still love you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T07:29:59-07:00","id":1212266,"title":"","content":"quick question!<br /> <br /> do i have to roll the defense of mooks and professionals/ nemesis etcetc??<br /> <br /> <br /> I mean: police guards with defense 1, i have to roll the single dice of defense?<br /> <br /> For enemies with many dices in defense like an hydra or an evil boss with 5,6 dices seems okay to roll, but what about mooks and professionals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T10:43:07-07:00","id":1212356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1212266#post1212266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">quick question!<br /> <br /> do i have to roll the defense of mooks and professionals/ nemesis etcetc??<br /> <br /> <br /> I mean: police guards with defense 1, i have to roll the single dice of defense?<br /> <br /> For enemies with many dices in defense like an hydra or an evil boss with 5,6 dices seems okay to roll, but what about mooks and professionals?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, at least according Origins, under the &quot;Variable Stunts&quot; under Attacking in Chapter Four, Defense for Antagonists is static.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T06:12:32-07:00","id":1212621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1212266#post1212266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">quick question!<br /> <br /> do i have to roll the defense of mooks and professionals/ nemesis etcetc??</div> </div> </div> </div>You never roll the Defense of any Antagonist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T09:51:37-07:00","id":1212702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1206180#post1206180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I alone in feeling that, a) this all seems really ungainly in an action-oriented game, and b) it doesn't seem terribly true to the myths? Where are the stories of god-blooded heroes stopping to make an offering before every great feat or deed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Achilles makes a prayer to Zeus and sacrifices wine, asking the God to protect Patroclus. The Pandavas build a temple to Lord Shiva to pray for the God's forgiveness. Beowulf invokes, sacrifices to and asks the blessing of what may be the Christian God before he slays Grendel.<br /> <br /> That's just off the top of my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T03:15:24-07:00","id":1213718,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I understand one thing about the Denizen paths. I think one of those replaces one Calling, since they have the Knacks, but some of those Knacks are drawbacks. I'm all for taking a drawback that makes sense for the character, like a Werewolf who can't control herself when she transforms unless she wears her relic white wolf pelt, but should it take up a Knack slot? Those are in high demand.<br /> <br /> Tangentially related: Does a Denizen Scion also need to take one Calling from her divine patron/parent? And what Calling would that be in the case of a Titan? Asking for a possible Jiaoren daughter of Ao Guang.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T03:53:57-07:00","id":1213726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreepyShutIn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1213718#post1213718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I understand one thing about the Denizen paths. I think one of those replaces one Calling, since they have the Knacks, but some of those Knacks are drawbacks. I'm all for taking a drawback that makes sense for the character, like a Werewolf who can't control herself when she transforms unless she wears her relic white wolf pelt, but should it take up a Knack slot? Those are in high demand.<br /> <br /> Tangentially related: Does a Denizen Scion also need to take one Calling from her divine patron/parent? And what Calling would that be in the case of a Titan? Asking for a possible Jiaoren daughter of Ao Guang.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Paths are getting a slight rework to make it more clear. Denizens can take their species path as a Calling, complete with knacks, but each Path will also have a negative persistent Condition that generates Momentum when it inconveniences you, such as the Kitsune Tail. That won't take a Knack Slot, I'll just be something you have for being a Kitsune.<br /> <br /> And if someone made a Kitsune scion of Inari, I'd allow them to say that the Kitsune calling is the one they inherited from Inari.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T07:20:56-07:00","id":1213783,"title":"","content":"When making a relic it says that a 2 dot relic can have a purview, is that a requirement that you have to spend 2 dots of effect in order to get the purview, or does a relic that has 2 or more dots just have the potential to grant a purview for free?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T12:10:19-07:00","id":1213854,"title":"","content":"I noticed that it states that Yamaraja is described as ALSO being a Shen and a Kami AND knowing the Tianming and Yaoyorozu-noKamaigami, AND includes the names of what were formerly Chinese and Japanese Buddhist-Death-gods in the previous edition, AND the Shen and Kami don't seem to have a PROPER death/underworld god.... was it the intent to imply that Yama can sire Kami, Shen, and/or Pala scions depending on which aspect he used during the siring and/or visitation? Naturally, it's not implying his scions get all three signature purviews, as that would be rediculous, but being variable, with different aspects being genuinely mechanically parents of different pantheons, while not explicitly stated, seems the intent... am I right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1576-mjorkk","name":"mjorkk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T13:17:26-07:00","id":1213872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mjorkk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1213854#post1213854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I noticed that it states that Yamaraja is described as ALSO being a Shen and a Kami AND knowing the Tianming and Yaoyorozu-noKamaigami, AND includes the names of what were formerly Chinese and Japanese Buddhist-Death-gods in the previous edition, AND the Shen and Kami don't seem to have a PROPER death/underworld god.... was it the intent to imply that Yama can sire Kami, Shen, and/or Pala scions depending on which aspect he used during the siring and/or visitation? Naturally, it's not implying his scions get all three signature purviews, as that would be rediculous, but being variable, with different aspects being genuinely mechanically parents of different pantheons, while not explicitly stated, seems the intent... am I right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't find the exact post where it was clarified right now, but yes, the intent is that Yama's Scions inherit different PSPs depending on which part of him they take after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T13:35:35-07:00","id":1213876,"title":"","content":"There's language to the effect of &quot;if the Scion's parent belongs to multiple pantheons, just pick one of the available purviews/motifs.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T11:45:19-07:00","id":1214240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1213783#post1213783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When making a relic it says that a 2 dot relic can have a purview, is that a requirement that you have to spend 2 dots of effect in order to get the purview, or does a relic that has 2 or more dots just have the potential to grant a purview for free?</div> </div> </div> </div>From the other Relics in the book, I'd say it's the former. We have like 2-dot Relics that have Purviews but no other Enhancements or Knacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T14:26:54-07:00","id":1214318,"title":"","content":"If a hero takes [Purview A] as his/her non-PSP innate purview, takes [Relic Z] that has the power that allows him/her to learn [Boon Q] as a [Purview A] boon, does the hero have access to [Boon Q] when he/she is missing [Relic Z]?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1576-mjorkk","name":"mjorkk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T15:01:56-07:00","id":1214331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mjorkk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1214318#post1214318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a hero takes [Purview A] as his/her non-PSP innate purview, takes [Relic Z] that has the power that allows him/her to learn [Boon Q] as a [Purview A] boon, does the hero have access to [Boon Q] when he/she is missing [Relic Z]?</div> </div> </div> </div>(sorry, no page numbers; I'm reading the pdf on my Kindle right now)<br /> <br /> Related to powers, Relics can do two things:<br /> a) Give you access to a Purview (through the Relic's Motif)<br /> b) Give you access to a custom Knack that emulates a Boon<br /> <br /> If a Relic grants access to a Purview which the character already has as Innate, using the Relic reduces relevant Complications by 1 per dot of the Relic's rating.<br /> <br /> So if a Scion of Eshu has the Twofold Guise (grants Deception), Assess Attitude rolls from other characters are always at +3 Complication when he is wearing it.<br /> He can learn and use False History, convincing someone that their memory is false, if they look at it from another perspective. This roll is a Clash, Manipulation+Legend vs. his target's Resolve+Legend.<br /> <br /> Until a scion of Anansi comes along and steals his hat. He immediately loses access to the Purview, but he still knows the Boon. If he manages to steal the Scion of Anansi's spider pendant later (a great short term goal), he gets access to the Boon again, but he has to spend Momentum equal to the pendant's rating when he uses it (until it becomes Fatebound to him).<br /> <br /> A different Scion of Eshu could have a different item (let's say it's a pocketwatch) that gives no Purview access, but it lets him hypnotize a target and rewrite memories (basically, False History as a custom Relic Knack). The roll would be different - instead of using the character's stats, I would rule that the roll would be a value related to the power of the relic, to represent the power imbued in the Relic during its creation. When this gets stolen, he loses the power completely. If it were to get destroyed, he would have to quest for another relic with the same properties. This is a great long term goal.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23791-ashnak","name":"Ashnak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T15:19:50-07:00","id":1214336,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the prompt reply, but that still doesn't answer my question. Sorry for not explaining it well. I will try to do better this time.<br /> <br /> I wasn't talking about relics that emulate the effects of boons, as that's a more clear cut ruling that's directly deducible from the text as is... and it seems we agree on that ruling. Cool <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I am talking about the multiple times the text uses the exact words &quot;can learn ______ as a _____ boon&quot; which isn't as cut and dry from the text itself (though there was probably a clear intent, which is why I'm in this thread in particular. The instances I can find are<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeroP254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1214331#post1214331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Knack: </b>The mirror\u2019s wielder can learn Blurt It Out (p. XX) as a Fortune boon, but rather than speaking aloud, the subject is reflected in the mirror and their thoughts are clear to anyone who can see them in the glass.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeroP255</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1214331#post1214331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\">Knack: </span><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">The constellation\u2019s ruler can learn Muse\u2019s Kiss (p. XX) for any kind of art as a Stars </span><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">Boon. </span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeroP259</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1214331#post1214331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\">Knack: </span><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">Xiuhcoatl\u2019s wielder can learn Blinding Glory (p. XX) as a Fire boon.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>The repeated use of these exact words seems to imply that it's intended to be one of the more common &quot;unique&quot; things a relic can do with a custom knack... and as far as I can reverse engineer (though each relic involved has multiple variable elements, so it's not certain) it appears to be a 3-dot unique knack each time. This is what my question was about.<br /> <br /> Again, thanks though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In your example, if the Anansi Scion's spider pendant has &quot;<b>Knack: </b>The pendant's wielder can learn Overwhelming Chaos(p. XX) as a Deception boon, as he confuses the target with an unending stream of confusing untruths and doubts about reality,&quot; and Deception is his Innate purview (the only one outside of his PSP that he has access to without a relic) AND he's already spent XP to buy Overwhelming Chaos as a Deception boon.... can he still use the Deception version of Overwhelming Chaos after the scion of Eshu has stolen both the spider pendant and the two-colored hat back?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1576-mjorkk","user":"mjorkk","date":". 05-02-2018, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1576-mjorkk","name":"mjorkk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T00:12:46-07:00","id":1214452,"title":"","content":"There's two ways to get a Boon from another Purview under a different Purview. Birthrights or your own Legend or your parent's. I think it makes sense that you lose access to the Boon if you lose access to the Birthright... Since while you still have access to the Purview, it is not a Boon from that Purview anymore. If you got it from your legend though, as mentioned in the sidebar next to the Beauty Purview. Then you always have access to it,.<br /> <br /> Also, slight pedantic point... But you can't buy Boons with XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 05-03-2018, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T06:46:43-07:00","id":1214579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mjorkk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1214336#post1214336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for the prompt reply, but that still doesn't answer my question. Sorry for not explaining it well. I will try to do better this time.<br /> <br /> I wasn't talking about relics that emulate the effects of boons, as that's a more clear cut ruling that's directly deducible from the text as is... and it seems we agree on that ruling. Cool <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I am talking about the multiple times the text uses the exact words &quot;can learn ______ as a _____ boon&quot; which isn't as cut and dry from the text itself (though there was probably a clear intent, which is why I'm in this thread in particular. The instances I can find are<br /> <br /> (Great examples)<br /> <br /> The repeated use of these exact words seems to imply that it's intended to be one of the more common &quot;unique&quot; things a relic can do with a custom knack... and as far as I can reverse engineer (though each relic involved has multiple variable elements, so it's not certain) it appears to be a 3-dot unique knack each time. This is what my question was about.<br /> <br /> Again, thanks though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In your example, if the Anansi Scion's spider pendant has &quot;<b>Knack: </b>The pendant's wielder can learn Overwhelming Chaos(p. XX) as a Deception boon, as he confuses the target with an unending stream of confusing untruths and doubts about reality,&quot; and Deception is his Innate purview (the only one outside of his PSP that he has access to without a relic) AND he's already spent XP to buy Overwhelming Chaos as a Deception boon.... can he still use the Deception version of Overwhelming Chaos after the scion of Eshu has stolen both the spider pendant and the two-colored hat back?</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, I hadn't caught that in the text. I would say that losing the item would <i>not</i> cause you to lose the Boon, because the Relic allows you to <i>learn</i> the Boon. Once it's learned, it's learned.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23791-ashnak","name":"Ashnak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T12:38:34-07:00","id":1214734,"title":"","content":"I feel like it really depends on how much the &quot;learn X boon Y purview instead&quot; knack costs compared to access to a purview, unfortunately, all three of the relics with the knack have multiple variable features, making deducing the exact cost difficult. If the learned boon is lost without the relic, than it should cost LESS than raw access to a purview, because ultimately you are gaining access to a single boon, rather than an entire purview's worth of boons... and a whole new type of marvel... and a motif. Alternatively, IF you DO NOT lose the boon when losing the relic, then it should cost MORE, because while it is still fewer total boons... you are getting to pick and choose, and getting the potential for inherent access to a boon, which is scarce at Hero tier.<br /> <br /> Like I said... it's unfortunate that this particular unique knack is not super easy to deduce directly, because of the multiple variables... however a RANGE of potential values can be determined<br /> <br /> Tezcatlipoca only has two variables that don't have clearly defined point values: Blurt it Out as a Fortune Boon and Remote Viewing<br /> <br /> For Tezcatlipoca's Mirror, the MAXIMUM cost is<br /> 2(Fortune Purview)+X(Blurt it Out as Fortune)+1(Remote Viewing Knack)-3(Tension Pool On Each Use)=3(Listed Price)<br /> <br /> X=3<br /> <br /> While for the same relic the MINIMUM cost is<br /> 2(Fortune Purview)+Y(Blurt it Out as Fortune)+3(Remote Viewing Knack)-3(Tension Pool On Each Use)=3(Listed Price)<br /> Y=1<br /> <br /> HOWEVER, this one's description for the USE of the boon implies that it requires the relic to work, because the information is displayed on the mirror itself. So, either they ALL require the relic to work, or this relic uses the cheaper version that DOES require the relic to work. Either way, we can deduce that the version that DOES require the relic to work, which MAY be the ONLY version, costs somewhere between 1 and 3 dots.... the thing is... it really should cost Equal-to-or-less-than just plain access to a new purview, and straight up remote viewing is MUCH more valuable than 1-dot, so that pretty much narrows it down to 2 or 1<br /> <br /> Designated Constellation is a bit more complicated, because it has THREE undefined variables: Muse's Kiss as a Stars Boon, The ability to send a message through the constellation, AND the flaw that you can only use the relic when it is in the sky visibly.<br /> <br /> For Designated Constellation, the MAXIMUM cost is<br /> 4(Fortune and Stars Purview)+X(Muse's Kiss as Stars)+1(Send Message)-5(Only Usable When Visible)=4(Listed Price)<br /> X=4<br /> <br /> Now, I'm working under the assumption that sending a message can't possibly be more expensive than acess to a whole purview, and losing access to the relic for at-least all daylight must be worth at-least 3<br /> Under those those assumptions, for Designated Constellation, the MINIMUM cost is<br /> 4(Fortune and Stars Purview)+y(Muse's Kiss as Stars)+2(Send Message)-3(Only Usable When Visible)=4(Listed Price)<br /> y=1<br /> <br /> So, whichever version of the knack that Designated constellation uses must be valued between 1 and 4<br /> <br /> Now, The Flaming Serpent has a whopping 4 not clearly costed variables: Blinding Glory as a Fire Boon, Shooting Aggrivated fire bolts that can get ENHANCEMENT rather than bonus-dice from momentum, the ability to add the Shockwave tag to Heaven's fire, and the flaw of not being able to back down from a fight once using the boon. Honestly, I'm not even going to wager a guess at the value within that relic.<br /> <br /> <br /> My best tummy-feels estimation based on what information I DO have tells me that<br /> A: the version with which you DO lose the boon without the relic should probably cost 1<br /> B: the version with which you do NOT lose the boon should probably cost 3 or 4... if it even exists at all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1576-mjorkk","name":"mjorkk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T17:29:44-07:00","id":1214846,"title":"","content":"Gonna repeat a question I had before. What powers do you plan to give the fair folk in the Bestiary?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T00:54:06-07:00","id":1215395,"title":"","content":"Hey Neall, was wondering if there could be suggestions on how to play gods Visiting their Scions? Or simplier: how did you all plan to make them come to the World? Avatars again? <br /> Cause when I was not aware of the avatar form, it was just hard to explain how a God could be so powerful once on Earth and could vanish, let's say with the 7th dot Psychopomp Boon as he did everything to hide his Legend and became Legend 3 to Visit. Am I making any sense?<br /> <br /> Just don't wanna guess how Gods come to the World this time, that's it ^^' <br /> (A full page may be enough without spoiling the God book?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T12:59:25-07:00","id":1215578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1215395#post1215395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Neall, was wondering if there could be suggestions on how to play gods Visiting their Scions? Or simplier: how did you all plan to make them come to the World? Avatars again? <br /> Cause when I was not aware of the avatar form, it was just hard to explain how a God could be so powerful once on Earth and could vanish, let's say with the 7th dot Psychopomp Boon as he did everything to hide his Legend and became Legend 3 to Visit. Am I making any sense?<br /> <br /> Just don't wanna guess how Gods come to the World this time, that's it ^^' <br /> (A full page may be enough without spoiling the God book?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well first of all, Boons in 2e aren't ranked anymore. Most Gods spin off Incarnations to live as mortals.<br /> <br /> I believe there's a sidebar in Origin suggesting to keep it subtle for your players when they meet a God's Incarnation. Like, have the players be told they're dealing with a guy with red hair and the clouds have been rumbling ominously all day, and only after will the players think &quot;Wait a minute was that Thor?&quot;<br /> <br /> The individual God writeups have sections about how the Gods act, which will help playing them in your games","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T14:11:25-07:00","id":1215589,"title":"","content":"Reading over the Text, there's some weirdness going on with certain weapon and armor tags; as asked by others, the Armored Tag isn't listed, but additionally, Piercings effect doesn't actually work by RAW. The Piercing Tag references &quot;reducing Defense granted by Armor by 1&quot;, but the text for Armor doesn't actually list it as giving any defense bonuses; Armor just has the tags that grant soft armor, hard armor, etc. I was wondering if this is a similar problem to how the Weapons section in Close Combat doesn't talk about how weapons give Enhancement Bonuses, while the example table of enhancements in the Storyteller Section does. If you didn't give a Weapon Enhancement, you run into situations where things like Knuckledusters have 0 mechanical value vs fighting unarmed.<br /> <br /> To gather them up a bit more neatly;<br /> <br /> -Piercing references reducing Armor-Given Defense. Unfortunately, Armor doesn't actually give Defense<br /> -The Weapons section doesn't mention that Weapons give Enhancement Bonuses to attack, making some weapons mechanically worthless compared to fighting unarmed.<br /> -The Armored Tag is referenced often throughout both books, but is not described in the Armor section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur","name":"Grindavikur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T01:47:35-07:00","id":1215711,"title":"","content":"My read on Piercing was that the intent was that it counters Soft armour. Rather than Defense, it's reducing the increased difficulty of the Inflict Damage stunt. Functionally the same if you're injuring someone, but doesn't make it easier to do non-damaging stunts.<br /> <br /> With regards to Weapon Enhancement, I took that mostly as working as intended and more of a problem with knuckledusters than anything else. I'd probably also give weapon tags to martial arts though, so it's possible that my read of it is off.<br /> <br /> And yeah, Armored needs fixing. I've been assuming it's meant to be Soft Armor, and it's from an earlier draft with only one type of armour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T15:16:02-07:00","id":1215910,"title":"","content":"On the subject of the Yazatas, is Ahura Mazda going to be a Primordial?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T02:15:55-07:00","id":1216545,"title":"","content":"Hi guys, I'm going through the whole system again and I got something unclear about Condition and Momentum. Let me quote:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some Conditions are so tied up with a character that removing them would be a dramatic change, like permanent blindness or paraplegia. These are <b>Persistent Conditions</b>, and can usually only be resolved with Boons or other divine attention. Instead, they provide the band with a good source of Momentum. </div> </div> </div>Is it determined of how many Momentums we get from Persistent Conditions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T09:33:32-07:00","id":1216704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1216545#post1216545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it determined of how many Momentums we get from Persistent Conditions?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a rule, one point whenever the Condition significantly impedes your character. Being blind is generally annoying, but being blind when you fail to notice an assassin in your hotel room is worth a point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T17:15:46-07:00","id":1216861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1216545#post1216545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi guys, I'm going through the whole system again and I got something unclear about Condition and Momentum. Let me quote:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Is it determined of how many Momentums we get from Persistent Conditions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, always one. It just doesn't ever fall off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T07:07:01-07:00","id":1216984,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Conditions: Are there going to be sample conditions in the book? Because there are a few unexplained conditions in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T16:45:29-07:00","id":1217187,"title":"","content":"Fate often seems to behave as if it was a sapient force - intelligent and capable of making decisions. Is that known to be the case? Or are these the questions that keep Odin awake at night?<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso: The Mythic Underground seems really cool. Will we see that expanded upon in later books? I always like to see the magical and cultural crossroads, even if it's one where angry Orisha Scions buy plants from the Greek Underworld to see if they can't brew up a really evil curse. <br /> <br /> Finally, the Teotl entry says they now hold to a golden rule that all human sacrifice be willing, but in the same paragraph says that they take &quot;prisoners&quot; who are never seen again when warring with rival gangs or cartels or whatnot. Hard to imagine those sacrifices are willing. Are the &quot;Flower wars&quot; only between followers of the Teotl? Or is there some other explanation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T17:13:55-07:00","id":1217196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreepyShutIn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1217187#post1217187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, the Teotl entry says they now hold to a golden rule that all human sacrifice be willing, but in the same paragraph says that they take &quot;prisoners&quot; who are never seen again when warring with rival gangs or cartels or whatnot. Hard to imagine those sacrifices are willing. Are the &quot;Flower wars&quot; only between followers of the Teotl? Or is there some other explanation?</div> </div> </div> </div>I say this can be handwaved in a couple of ways. First, that warriors today who swear to the Teotl know what they're getting into and know that losing means going under the obsidian knife.<br /> <br /> Secondly, that the Gods say &quot;Okay we're more civilized now, willing sacrifices only&quot; but their followers go &quot;Sorry couldn't hear that, too busy cutting the heart out of a prisoner&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 05-09-2018, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T18:13:28-07:00","id":1217215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1217196#post1217196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I say this can be handwaved in a couple of ways. First, that warriors today who swear to the Teotl know what they're getting into and know that losing means going under the obsidian knife.<br /> <br /> Secondly, that the Gods say &quot;Okay we're more civilized now, willing sacrifices only&quot; but their followers go &quot;Sorry couldn't hear that, too busy cutting the heart out of a prisoner&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also nothing that says the Teotl won't accept a &quot;willing sacrifice&quot; that said yes because they were being waterboarded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T16:47:49-07:00","id":1217526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreepyShutIn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1217187#post1217187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fate often seems to behave as if it was a sapient force - intelligent and capable of making decisions. Is that known to be the case? Or are these the questions that keep Odin awake at night?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fate is sentient, but not sapient per se. Attempts to perceive Fate's weave bind you to it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bAlso: The Mythic Underground seems really cool. Will we see that expanded upon in later books? I always like to see the magical and cultural crossroads, even if it's one where angry Orisha Scions buy plants from the Greek Underworld to see if they can't brew up a really evil curse. </div> </div> </div>I want to do a big book of factions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally, the Teotl entry says they now hold to a golden rule that all human sacrifice be willing, but in the same paragraph says that they take &quot;prisoners&quot; who are never seen again when warring with rival gangs or cartels or whatnot. Hard to imagine those sacrifices are willing. Are the &quot;Flower wars&quot; only between followers of the Teotl? Or is there some other explanation? </div> </div> </div>Torture works. It's deeply unpleasant, and the Gods do gently discourage it, but it works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T16:50:05-07:00","id":1217527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1207904#post1207904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So invoking a Path allows you to &quot;add two dice to any roll that plausibly applies to your Path&quot;<br /> This is a very rare example of adding dice rather than an Enhancement (the only other that comes to mind is Momentum) so I just wanted to know: is this an intentional departure from standard procedure or is it a mistake and it should give some amount of Enhancement instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally intentional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T16:50:05-07:00","id":1217528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1207904#post1207904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So invoking a Path allows you to &quot;add two dice to any roll that plausibly applies to your Path&quot;<br /> This is a very rare example of adding dice rather than an Enhancement (the only other that comes to mind is Momentum) so I just wanted to know: is this an intentional departure from standard procedure or is it a mistake and it should give some amount of Enhancement instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally intentional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T16:51:35-07:00","id":1217529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1215910#post1215910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of the Yazatas, is Ahura Mazda going to be a Primordial?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, he's the Yazata Primordial. Angra Mainyu is the Yazata Titan of Chaos; he may be an Emanation of Ahura Mazda, nobody's really sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T16:54:20-07:00","id":1217530,"title":"","content":"I know it is slightly aside from the standard narrative of Scion but a concept that i rather like is the self made hero.<br /> Is it possible to have mortals, untouched in any way by the divine that nonetheless succeed to imbue themselves with Legend and become Heroes (with the possibility to go to demigod status and even god eventually)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T17:57:26-07:00","id":1217544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1217215#post1217215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's also nothing that says the Teotl won't accept a &quot;willing sacrifice&quot; that said yes because they were being waterboarded.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI suppose it should also be mentioned that the Teotl very likely ALWAYS insisted on willing sacrifices. I don't remember where, but I swear I read somewhere that the Aztecs would actually just kill you if you struggled, tried to escape, or generally acted like a coward on your way to being sacrificed. Even if you didn't offer yourself up for sacrifice, they expected you to accept your fate with at least a modicum of dignity. If you acted &quot;cowardly&quot; by their standards, they may very well decide &quot;Okay! Screw it! You aren't a worthy sacrifice anyway!&quot; and just kill you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T20:38:21-07:00","id":1217571,"title":"","content":"Two question about feats of scale.<br /> <br /> 1: How long does the legend stay imbued when you perform a feat of scale with one of the knacks that lets you imbue instead of spending?<br /> <br /> 2: If you perform a feat of scale to lift/procure/break-off/etc... an improvised weapon, does that in turn mean the weapon has a scale equivalent to the feat required to wield it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1576-mjorkk","name":"mjorkk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T06:54:00-07:00","id":1217648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1217530#post1217530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know it is slightly aside from the standard narrative of Scion but a concept that i rather like is the self made hero.<br /> Is it possible to have mortals, untouched in any way by the divine that nonetheless succeed to imbue themselves with Legend and become Heroes (with the possibility to go to demigod status and even god eventually)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I <b><i>think</i></b> that is the MO of in-setting Sorcerers: Mortal who thirsted for divine power, took it, and imbued themselves with strength.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18560-saedar","name":"saedar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T07:04:17-07:00","id":1217650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1217530#post1217530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know it is slightly aside from the standard narrative of Scion but a concept that i rather like is the self made hero.<br /> Is it possible to have mortals, untouched in any way by the divine that nonetheless succeed to imbue themselves with Legend and become Heroes (with the possibility to go to demigod status and even god eventually)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know how you define &quot;untouched in any way by the divine&quot;, but Wolf-Warriors are listed as being able to gain Legend, and they're fundamentally human. Saints are also human, and I don't see why they couldn't gain Legend (even if they don't have any Immortal Knacks).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24028-mike-mccall","name":"Mike McCall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T07:32:57-07:00","id":1217661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saedar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1217648#post1217648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <b><i>think</i></b> that is the MO of in-setting Sorcerers: Mortal who thirsted for divine power, took it, and imbued themselves with strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be interesting. But it is still a bit too involved with the gods for what i'm thinking.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mike McCall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1217650#post1217650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know how you define &quot;untouched in any way by the divine&quot;, but Wolf-Warriors are listed as being able to gain Legend, and they're fundamentally human. Saints are also human, and I don't see why they couldn't gain Legend (even if they don't have any Immortal Knacks).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, i was so focused on a complicated solution that i overlooked the Wolf-Warriors. That could work quite well. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T12:25:57-07:00","id":1217739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1216861#post1216861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yup, always one. It just doesn't ever fall off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, a good source of Momentum, I thought it meant 2 or 3...<br /> <br /> So this Momentum is in the black pool until the persistent condition is resolved. All right. Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T15:57:34-07:00","id":1217807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1217530#post1217530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know it is slightly aside from the standard narrative of Scion but a concept that i rather like is the self made hero.<br /> Is it possible to have mortals, untouched in any way by the divine that nonetheless succeed to imbue themselves with Legend and become Heroes (with the possibility to go to demigod status and even god eventually)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Others mentioned wolf-warriors, who really gain Legend by being blessed by a God. They can't go to true Hero or Demigod status, however. <br /> <br /> They can be reincarnated as Heroes, however, again from a chosen deity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T16:06:21-07:00","id":1217809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1217807#post1217807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Others mentioned wolf-warriors, who really gain Legend by being blessed by a God. They can't go to true Hero or Demigod status, however.<br /> <br /> They can be reincarnated as Heroes, however, again from a chosen deity.</div> </div> </div> </div>They seem like ideal candidates for being chosen though, correct?<br /> <br /> One question related to them, with the varients like Amozan, Dahoty, and Shieldmadein for Wolfwarrior, are they restricted to the knacks list or do they have access to any of the knacks of the &quot;core&quot; version? Because otherwise some of them seem to have fairly sparse selections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T05:46:57-07:00","id":1217936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1217809#post1217809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They seem like ideal candidates for being chosen though, correct?<br /> <br /> One question related to them, with the varients like Amozan, Dahoty, and Shieldmadein for Wolfwarrior, are they restricted to the knacks list or do they have access to any of the knacks of the &quot;core&quot; version? Because otherwise some of them seem to have fairly sparse selections.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are Knacks in addition to the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T06:32:13-07:00","id":1217953,"title":"","content":"The 'Emulate Boons' Marvel notes that Boons emulated through Marvels cost extra... the 'Terrible to Behold' Sidebar in Beauty notes that 'Its cost isn\u2019t increased when you emulate it with a marvel of the chosen Purview' which sort of implies that Marvels to emulate Boons of the same Purview don't increase in cost... are Marvels only supposed to be costlier when emulating Boons if they're not naturally from the Purview being used or am I reading the sidebar incorrectly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T08:07:42-07:00","id":1217964,"title":"","content":"One thing has been bugging me the more I read it. I feel like I'm definitely not understanding something, but I'm not sure how. The issue is the Tuatha motif: &quot;Magic flows from verse and satire.&quot; I figured at first that this meant you make up a rhyme and magic happens, but every example I see seems to be more about mocking someone to make them do something. And that seems kind of limited. It obviously works great when you need a War marvel to make the enemy lose heart or a Fire marvel to inspire people, but what do you do when you want to open a stone door with Earth? Insult the door? How do you make yourself fly, or hurl bolts of lightning for a scene? If you're limited to what you can accomplish by taunting someone in rhyme, then it seems... well, really weak.<br /> <br /> \u200bI do like the Tuatha, I should add. My main idea for a character is a son of Mannanan who struggles to uphold the virtues of Enech and meet the expectations of his family and the faith while being, at heart, a humble person who just wants to explore. But I am concerned now that the motif he'd be stuck with is a lot more limited than the others. So I guess the question is: What am I not seeing? Am I just getting it wrong in general, and the examples given don't show the full breadth of it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T08:35:39-07:00","id":1217971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreepyShutIn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1217964#post1217964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing has been bugging me the more I read it. I feel like I'm definitely not understanding something, but I'm not sure how. The issue is the Tuatha motif: &amp;quot;Magic flows from verse and satire.&amp;quot; I figured at first that this meant you make up a rhyme and magic happens, but every example I see seems to be more about mocking someone to make them do something. And that seems kind of limited. It obviously works great when you need a War marvel to make the enemy lose heart or a Fire marvel to inspire people, but what do you do when you want to open a stone door with Earth? Insult the door? How do you make yourself fly, or hurl bolts of lightning for a scene? If you're limited to what you can accomplish by taunting someone in rhyme, then it seems... well, really weak.<br /> <br /> \u200bI do like the Tuatha, I should add. My main idea for a character is a son of Mannanan who struggles to uphold the virtues of Enech and meet the expectations of his family and the faith while being, at heart, a humble person who just wants to explore. But I am concerned now that the motif he'd be stuck with is a lot more limited than the others. So I guess the question is: What am I not seeing? Am I just getting it wrong in general, and the examples given don't show the full breadth of it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given what I know of the 2e design philosophy, a good rule of thumb is this: If you have two potential reads of something, and one sounds more restrictive and less fun, go with the other reading.<br /> <br /> Remember that the motif does mention satire, but it also mentions verse. Don't assume that they'd mention that unless it counted. Yeah, a lot of power done a from sick burns, but I'd totally allow a Tuatha Scion to use, say, Epic Dex to emulate the Flight boon by making a little rhyme about how they're so light in their feet they can run through the sky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T09:26:22-07:00","id":1217988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreepyShutIn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1217964#post1217964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing has been bugging me the more I read it. I feel like I'm definitely not understanding something, but I'm not sure how. The issue is the Tuatha motif: &quot;Magic flows from verse and satire.&quot; I figured at first that this meant you make up a rhyme and magic happens, but every example I see seems to be more about mocking someone to make them do something. And that seems kind of limited. It obviously works great when you need a War marvel to make the enemy lose heart or a Fire marvel to inspire people, but what do you do when you want to open a stone door with Earth? Insult the door? How do you make yourself fly, or hurl bolts of lightning for a scene? If you're limited to what you can accomplish by taunting someone in rhyme, then it seems... well, really weak.<br /> <br /> \u200bI do like the Tuatha, I should add. My main idea for a character is a son of Mannanan who struggles to uphold the virtues of Enech and meet the expectations of his family and the faith while being, at heart, a humble person who just wants to explore. But I am concerned now that the motif he'd be stuck with is a lot more limited than the others. So I guess the question is: What am I not seeing? Am I just getting it wrong in general, and the examples given don't show the full breadth of it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Motif isn't just for insults, though I can totally see how the sentence can be read like that. From what I understand, it is intended to be either making a statement in a poem that causes the magic to take hold, or insulting someone through satire (which would <i>also</i> be in rhyme traditionally) rather than always having to be a satirical mocking. For instance, this is one of the examples of this Motif in use in a Myth called <i>Cath Maige Tuired</i> where Miach, son of Dian C\u00e9cht healed the arm/hand of Nuada. (It rhymes in Old Irish)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He went to the hand and said \u2018joint to joint of it, and sinew to sinew\u2019; and he healed it in nine days and nights. The first three days he carried it against his side, and it became covered with skin. The second three days he carried it against his chest. The third three days he would cast white wisps of black bulrushes after they had been blackened in a fire. </div> </div> </div>So, if you wanted to open a stone door, you could recite a quick poem about your skill as a mason, and going through some motions as you have this door open up before you. If you wanted to fly, you could, depending on how you are fluffing your use of Sky, you could give a poem about your father who is an Otherworldly Bird, or if you wanted to hurl lightning, you could give a poem about the quickness of your movement as a warrior and physically grab bolts of lightning as they fall from the sky and hurl them at people.<br /> <br /> Essentially, all you need to do is make a poem. What I have done for Scion 2e is I find a Poem for each of my Purviews to grab selections from when I need to make a Marvel when I first make the character, and then every few weeks maybe go back and pick up a new poem to use to keep things fresh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T11:44:33-07:00","id":1218027,"title":"","content":"Also free verse is an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T11:50:07-07:00","id":1218031,"title":"","content":"Question: what does Pele want? I know the Atua are still a bit off, but what might interest her to make this stop?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-12-2018, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T21:41:42-07:00","id":1218147,"title":"","content":"Question: Been playing around with the Creature Birthright rules, and how do qualities interact with the dice pools? Also, how should one go about calculating the secondary, desperation, health, defense, and initiative pools? Assigning Scale to the players critters?<br /> <br /> I ask because the sample antagonist creatures are all over the map for qualities and flairs, and the dice pools don't sync to to the creature guidelines in Birthrights chapter, and the mentioned examples in the Birthrights section (supposedly in chapter 6) are not there. Further, of the four dot example creatures, none are given stats.<br /> <br /> Basically, I'm confused as to what is meant to be appropriate for each dot level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/963-kylar","name":"Kylar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar963_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T01:28:58-07:00","id":1218158,"title":"","content":"Can you spoil what the Pantheon Motif for the Yazatas will likely be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1494-deranged-goblin","name":"Deranged Goblin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T14:30:21-07:00","id":1218324,"title":"","content":"Hi Neall,<br /> <br /> I really appreciated some of the clarifications and things said in the Storypath chapter of Heroes. There was one bit I was curious about, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While certain religions and cultures don\u2019t, properly speaking, exist anymore (the Kemetic Egyptians), some are heavily reconstructed (Greco-Roman polytheism) and one religion was made up whole-cloth for this work (the Laukr Norse faith, which differs in tone and style from reconstructed Germanic Heathenism) </div> </div> </div>I was particularly interested because you brought up Greco-Roman Polytheism, and that Laukr was described as 'different in tone' than Asatru/Heathen reconstruction. As it happens, there is actually a branch of faith known as Northern Tradition Paganism, which is itself a polytheistic (as opposed to pantheistic) faith that focuses on the Norse pantheons. The focus they place on something called 'UPG' (Unverified Personal Gnosis), struck me as very similar to the watery tone ascribed to Laukr.<br /> <br /> There's also the fact that Northern Tradition types insist that Loki is free to go about, and not bound up in a cave, or preferring to refer to them with they/then pronouns.<br /> <br /> To get to my actual question, I guess I was curious if that faith had any influence on Laukr, and whether or not it would be a good resource for fleshing out that hand-crafted Norse faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":". 05-13-2018, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T08:15:08-07:00","id":1218550,"title":"","content":"Can i use marvels to heal? or the marvel can heal only magical wounds and curses? <br /> <br /> <br /> i mean: if i get burned and fill an injured box can i use a marvel of frost to heal the burn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T08:41:04-07:00","id":1218559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kylar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1218147#post1218147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: Been playing around with the Creature Birthright rules, and how do qualities interact with the dice pools? Also, how should one go about calculating the secondary, desperation, health, defense, and initiative pools? Assigning Scale to the players critters?<br /> <br /> I ask because the sample antagonist creatures are all over the map for qualities and flairs, and the dice pools don't sync to to the creature guidelines in Birthrights chapter, and the mentioned examples in the Birthrights section (supposedly in chapter 6) are not there. Further, of the four dot example creatures, none are given stats.<br /> <br /> Basically, I'm confused as to what is meant to be appropriate for each dot level.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've asked this in a couple of threads now but haven't received feedback. I assume it is something that they needed to do significant revision on and we will see the fruits when the books are ready.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18560-saedar","name":"saedar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T08:53:48-07:00","id":1218569,"title":"","content":"For effects such as &quot;a sentinel&quot; that add +1 defense is that plus one die to the roll or a flat +1 to the result of the roll when applied to the PC?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T17:00:59-07:00","id":1219110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1218569#post1218569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For effects such as &quot;a sentinel&quot; that add +1 defense is that plus one die to the roll or a flat +1 to the result of the roll when applied to the PC?</div> </div> </div> </div>Always +1 Enhancement. Never change the dice pool unless the book explicitly tells you to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T17:03:54-07:00","id":1219112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1218324#post1218324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was particularly interested because you brought up Greco-Roman Polytheism, and that Laukr was described as 'different in tone' than Asatru/Heathen reconstruction. As it happens, there is actually a branch of faith known as Northern Tradition Paganism, which is itself a polytheistic (as opposed to pantheistic) faith that focuses on the Norse pantheons. The focus they place on something called 'UPG' (Unverified Personal Gnosis), struck me as very similar to the watery tone ascribed to Laukr.<br /> <br /> There's also the fact that Northern Tradition types insist that Loki is free to go about, and not bound up in a cave, or preferring to refer to them with they/then pronouns.<br /> <br /> To get to my actual question, I guess I was curious if that faith had any influence on Laukr, and whether or not it would be a good resource for fleshing out that hand-crafted Norse faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting! It sounds almost like a mix of Greek-Norse polytheism.<br /> <br /> Laukr was a creation of the author, who may have done her own research on this and just didn't tell me, and my adding in some supplemental elements of Heathen reconstruction and cosmetic details from dramatic depictions. I'll be sure to ask her, but we did source it in actual recreations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T17:04:34-07:00","id":1219114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deranged Goblin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1218158#post1218158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you spoil what the Pantheon Motif for the Yazatas will likely be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not written yet, but it'll likely have to do with the righteousness of Ahura Mazda.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T17:06:28-07:00","id":1219115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kylar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1218147#post1218147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, I'm confused as to what is meant to be appropriate for each dot level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Go by the Creature Birthright rather than the Antagonists, but I'll see what I can do to add language to clear things up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T17:34:32-07:00","id":1219122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1219115#post1219115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Go by the Creature Birthright rather than the Antagonists, but I'll see what I can do to add language to clear things up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh,speaking of Creatures. what kind of powers will the Bestiary give to Fair Folk?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T19:47:01-07:00","id":1219519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1219112#post1219112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting! It sounds almost like a mix of Greek-Norse polytheism.<br /> <br /> Laukr was a creation of the author, who may have done her own research on this and just didn't tell me, and my adding in some supplemental elements of Heathen reconstruction and cosmetic details from dramatic depictions. I'll be sure to ask her, but we did source it in actual recreations.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a lot of interaction between the two, including a surprising amount of influence from various communities that worship the loa/iwa, believe it or not. It's all very interesting, and I'd personally love to see more of the process she went through with some of the Norse brainstorming, maybe even through a note in a Kickstarter update or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T11:04:24-07:00","id":1220024,"title":"","content":"From all different types of Scion, I don't really understand what are the incarnates for? <br /> Youre still in a mortal form and you would relive your divine life or at least encounter what you already did... so what? You just happen to have 12 labors if you are an Incarnate of Heracles? Or chasing a beautiful Muse if you are an Incarnate of Apollo? <br /> <br /> I don't see how would these situations be entertaining. Players would be expecting them, wouldn't they?<br /> <br /> Or am I misunderstanding something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T11:33:10-07:00","id":1220032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1220024#post1220024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From all different types of Scion, I don't really understand what are the incarnates for?<br /> Youre still in a mortal form and you would relive your divine life or at least encounter what you already did... so what? You just happen to have 12 labors if you are an Incarnate of Heracles? Or chasing a beautiful Muse if you are an Incarnate of Apollo?<br /> <br /> I don't see how would these situations be entertaining. Players would be expecting them, wouldn't they?<br /> <br /> Or am I misunderstanding something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Those things don't necessarily happen to Incarnates any more than they do to any other Scion, and they don't play out exactly as they did in myth anyway. As always with stories about fate (or Fate in this case) they may <i>think</i> they know what's going to happen, but they'll still be surprised. I'm reminded of the story of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%96rvar-Oddr\" target=\"_blank\">\u00d6rvar-Oddr</a>, who was told it was his fate to be killed by his horse Faxi. He summarily killed the horse, lived another three hundred years, and then one day he stumbled on the old horse skull and was killed by the serpent that now lived in it.<br /> <br /> Also, do not underestimate how much even the slightest degree of obfuscation can throw your players off. 9/10 times you can introduce Mr. Zeut of the Olympus Corporation to recruit the band for Project Lightning Bolt and it'll still take six sessions and some judicious elbow-jabbing before they realize he may have some relation to the Theoi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T11:51:51-07:00","id":1220039,"title":"","content":"One possible take on Incarnates is that they're a chance for a do-over. If a god believes (s)he's too tightly hemmed in by Fate, going through a completely new rebirth may open up new possibilities and directions. One certainly expects that the Incarnate stands a risk of going down the same path as the original -- Fate will be nudging the Incarnate in that direction. But because the Incarnate's Legend is much lower that the original god, Fate's influence is much weaker and different reactions might happen.<br /> <br /> This is exactly what Young Loki tried to do in Kieron Gillen's run on &quot;Journey Into Mystery&quot;. Young Loki wanted to change from a God of Evil into a God of Mischief, and to change his ultimate destiny. He sort-of-kind-of succeeded...but not the way he intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4310-jagardner","name":"jagardner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T12:24:10-07:00","id":1220056,"title":"","content":"Also, consider gods where we have virtually no mythology for them, like the Gaulish gods. In those cases, the player and Director are basically creating the legend as they go along, which can be presented as a straight take or subversion of what originally happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T15:56:37-07:00","id":1220123,"title":"","content":"Also, it's a way of playing your favorite god or goddess as a Hero or Demigod instead of jumping into God-tier action. For instance, I have a fondness for Iris, Theoi Goddess of the rainbow and messenger of the Gods; but I'd much rather play her at the demigod level of power than as a goddess. Playing an Incarnate of Iris allows for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T19:27:45-07:00","id":1220156,"title":"","content":"To add to the list of suggestions, it's also a way for Scions to play currently dead deities and weaving them into the story by continuing the narratives of their reincarnations. Nuada, Dian C\u00e9cht, Goibniu, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T23:24:14-07:00","id":1220188,"title":"","content":"Thanks guys. It will help when a player will ask about it, and they will... hehe<br /> <br /> Oh, wanted to know if you guys or Neall did think about what would happen if a god and a goddess would try to have children. I have players from Scion 1E who are gods and I just don't want to say it does not work on I dont know because the game does not mention anything about this and I really dont have a clue. I mean it will give birth to a god-level creature most of the time, or at least demigod level, even in myths, it's not quite simple... or maybe invoke Fate? :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T23:40:51-07:00","id":1220190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1220188#post1220188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks guys. It will help when a player will ask about it, and they will... hehe<br /> <br /> Oh, wanted to know if you guys or Neall did think about what would happen if a god and a goddess would try to have children. I have players from Scion 1E who are gods and I just don't want to say it does not work on I dont know because the game does not mention anything about this and I really dont have a clue. I mean it will give birth to a god-level creature most of the time, or at least demigod level, even in myths, it's not quite simple... or maybe invoke Fate? :/</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the result is still a Legend 1 Scion. They just start Visited instead of having to go through Origins Tier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T23:51:23-07:00","id":1220192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1220190#post1220190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe the result is still a Legend 1 Scion. They just start Visited instead of having to go through Origins Tier.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would you explain that as in myths, gods have god level children?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T01:09:08-07:00","id":1220198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1220192#post1220192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How would you explain that as in myths, gods have god level children?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, it's not that big of a stretch... Baby Hermes' trick with the cattle is something any Trickster could do at Hero. Ganesh battling Shiva's followers to a standstill is easily a case of Army of One, probably backed up by an Astra given by Parvati. Huitzilopochtli does take on the Southern Stars right at birth, but a. Again, Army of One and b. He's the child of a Primordial, so I can see that rule not strictly applying there. The children of gods do a lot of crazy stuff but that's by and large covered by Heroes already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T11:45:43-07:00","id":1220293,"title":"","content":"Is there going to be an official expansion to the Orenda in the foreseeable future? The reason I ask this is that I'm actually interested in possibly writing up entries for the remainder of the pantheon myself if there isn't going to be one. I've never homebrewed before, but it's something I'd always wanted to learn, and I felt that it would easiest to expand on them before tackling an entirely new pantheon by myself. However, if there is going to be an official expansion, I don't want to provide a free alternative to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T17:36:01-07:00","id":1220369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1220198#post1220198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, it's not that big of a stretch... Baby Hermes' trick with the cattle is something any Trickster could do at Hero. Ganesh battling Shiva's followers to a standstill is easily a case of Army of One, probably backed up by an Astra given by Parvati. Huitzilopochtli does take on the Southern Stars right at birth, but a. Again, Army of One and b. He's the child of a Primordial, so I can see that rule not strictly applying there. The children of gods do a lot of crazy stuff but that's by and large covered by Heroes already.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, what troubles me is the mechanism, the system that existed for Gods. I mean, there are rules to create Scion Lvl 1 with all the associated powers. How, let's say, Horus, Athena or even Fenris are born independantly from their parents where we need to create Scions that follow partly our divine parents' paths. Clearly, Loki doesn't look like a wolf. How a God would give birth to genuine Creatures/ beings that is not even the sum or the average of both parents? <br /> <br /> Hephaestus is the God of forge at birth and directly God. Does this system work at all with Scion game or we should not try to understand how it works?<br /> <br /> Also, Scions do evolve. Why do Gods are frozen with their powers. Why Wukong wouldn't keep on trying to be more than the Monkey king? I mean, wouldn't they receive experience points too? If Scion players reach their levels and keep going up, they would be stronger than Gods and it will be disturbing.<br /> <br /> The roleplay part is okay I think. I just wanted to know if it were put into a system, how would this work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T19:29:47-07:00","id":1220399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1220369#post1220369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do Gods are frozen with their powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't, not always. Loki's write-up mentions that his Monster Maker days were represented by possessing the Creator Calling. However, around the time he consumed Logi's mantle and took Logi's wife (which is also where he gained the Fire purview) Loki have up the Creator Calling and gained the Lover Calling.<br /> <br /> Consider the writeups to be snapshots of where the Gods are as we know them. They may change in time, with worship, but Change may not come easily to Gods. Plus, gaining new Boons doesn't come with experience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I just wanted to know if it were put into a system, how would this work? </div> </div> </div>I think the best answer to this is &quot;The God book is years away, chillax&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: Though if I had to guess now... We know that a group of Gods who form their own Pantheon can retroactively write a Genesis Myth into history. Who's to say that a God, upon ascending to full Legend 9 Godhood, can't say &quot;I am and always was the Forge God&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 05-19-2018, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T21:49:03-07:00","id":1220436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1220369#post1220369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, what troubles me is the mechanism, the system that existed for Gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>The system that existed for Gods is not necessarily the system that exists for Gods.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1220369#post1220369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, there are rules to create Scion Lvl 1 with all the associated powers. How, let's say, Horus, Athena or even Fenris are born independantly from their parents where we need to create Scions that follow partly our divine parents' paths. Clearly, Loki doesn't look like a wolf. How a God would give birth to genuine Creatures/ beings that is not even the sum or the average of both parents?</div> </div> </div> </div>Horus is a Scion of Aset, Athena is a Scion of Metis... both of those parents were totally there and neither was born independently of them, so I'm not sure what the issue is here. Fenris is more difficult, I'll give you that, but we know that Scions of Inari can be Kitsune and Scions of Apollo can be Prophets... and we also know that Loki has some sort of Mother of Monsters Title... Fenris is <i>also</i> child of Angrbroda, Giantess of the Iron Wood, and if he takes after her more than his father then he can totally have more Wild charecteristics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1220369#post1220369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hephaestus is the God of forge at birth and directly God. Does this system work at all with Scion game or we should not try to understand how it works?</div> </div> </div> </div>Heph is born of Zeus and Hera, survives getting kicked off of Olympus and then builds things... that's nothing Epic Stamina and the Creator Calling wouldn't let him do at Hero.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1220369#post1220369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Scions do evolve. Why do Gods are frozen with their powers. Why Wukong wouldn't keep on trying to be more than the Monkey king?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not, necessarily. Gods evolve and gain new Mantles all the time. Heracles even converted to Buddhism once. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1220369#post1220369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, wouldn't they receive experience points too? If Scion players reach their levels and keep going up, they would be stronger than Gods and it will be disturbing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't buy Boons and Callings with XP so that this is a moot point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1220369#post1220369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The roleplay part is okay I think. I just wanted to know if it were put into a system, how would this work?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is, frankly, no system in existence that can accurately model all of mythology... it's way too crazy a thing for that to actually be possible... but Scion comes pretty darn close.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T03:03:26-07:00","id":1220482,"title":"","content":"So, in the writeups about soft armor in Origin, and in the Skin Like Stone boon in Hero, it is strongly implied that one can have multiple stacks/levels of soft-armor... however, outside of reverse engineering the fact that Skin Like Stone gives multiple levels of soft armor, therefore multiple levels of soft armor must be possible, it is never explicitly stated that it can come in increasing levels.<br /> <br /> Also... if it have multiple &quot;stacks&quot; or levels... is there some sort of maximum, because there most certainly SHOULD be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1576-mjorkk","name":"mjorkk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T13:32:13-07:00","id":1220613,"title":"","content":"Wait, did I miss something saying that the children of God on God action produces Scions? I thought Scions were mortal children.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T14:15:26-07:00","id":1220623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1220613#post1220613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, did I miss something saying that the children of God on God action produces Scions? I thought Scions were mortal children.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's been lines here and there. Basically any Godchild, even one born of two Gods, would be a Legend 1 Hero at the start and grow into a stronger being.<br /> <br /> If two Gods have a kid, the general consensus seems to be that the kid will take after one parent for the sake of Innate Purview and Calling. Nothing stops the other parent from being a Guide or giving the Scion some other Birthrights","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T15:59:12-07:00","id":1220643,"title":"","content":"In the first version of scion, two full powered gods produced a scion at the lowest possible legend for God. Two gods where one or more was in an avatar . (read incarnation) form during conception, produced a scion at the lowest legend for the lowest tier that any of the involved parents at the time of conception (A two gods, one of them in a demigod-tier avatar form would produce a starting demigod, and two gods who both took a heroic-tier avatar form to live out a romantic-comedy version of their lives would produce a starting hero.)<br /> <br /> In this version... nothing has been definitively said one way or the other, but someone here said they should be L1 Heroes regardless of the tier of the parents given incarnation/avatar, and a lot of the more active members have liked it, and the books are still being written, so there's a decent chance that that's what going to be &quot;standard&quot; when the book finally comes out.<br /> <br /> Every game I've ever run or played in where it became an issue, rather than using any set of procedural rules, it followed the system of &quot;whatever is most dramatically appropriate, because Fate is a tangible, semi-sapient, and narratively-charged force in the legendary universe.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ..... should we have two of these threads, one for fluff, and one for crunch? I'm having to wade through a lot of fluff questions that I know my table is going to rewrite anyway to find the answers mechanical questions that inevitably come from a first draft (like that &quot;can soft armor have multiple levels&quot; question, or &quot;what the hell is the 'armored tag.'&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1576-mjorkk","name":"mjorkk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T17:12:01-07:00","id":1220663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mjorkk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1220643#post1220643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;what the hell is the 'armored tag.'&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't Neall answer that one? I'm pretty sure the Armored tag is an artifact and should be 'Soft Armor'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T19:52:11-07:00","id":1220691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1220663#post1220663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Didn't Neall answer that one? I'm pretty sure the Armored tag is an artifact and should be 'Soft Armor'</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct.... which further complicates the issue of how/when one gains &quot;levels&quot; of soft armor, if one even can, as it's not explicitly stated yet... which was the main locus of my question. Thanks though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1576-mjorkk","user":"mjorkk","date":". 05-21-2018, 12:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1576-mjorkk","name":"mjorkk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T12:31:17-07:00","id":1220906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1218550#post1218550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can i use marvels to heal? or the marvel can heal only magical wounds and curses?<br /> <br /> <br /> i mean: if i get burned and fill an injured box can i use a marvel of frost to heal the burn?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> up! sorry, i really need this answer <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T14:30:39-07:00","id":1220944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1220906#post1220906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> up! sorry, i really need this answer <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>My non-Dev answer would be &quot;Why not?&quot;<br /> <br /> More seriously, I believe one of the explicit things mentioned as a Marvel type is &quot;Remove Condition&quot;, and injuries are conditions, so-","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T08:15:27-07:00","id":1221476,"title":"","content":"how to balance a fight??<br /> <br /> how many mob/rival/nemesis will you put against a group of 3 scions (legend 1)?? and how would you scale in case of legend 2 characters??<br /> a monster how many dice should throw with his pool? how much life, how much defense with a group of 3 scions?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T16:14:35-07:00","id":1221569,"title":"","content":"Use the antagonists in the back. Ballpark, lowballing it. If your players breeze through, use Tension to empower one of the enemies.<br /> <br /> Your question, however, has many variables. What kind of Scions? Are they combat focused? How many have the Warrior Calling? Do any of them have Creatures or Followers to do the fighting for them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T05:28:01-07:00","id":1221663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1220623#post1220623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If two Gods have a kid, the general consensus seems to be that the kid will take after one parent for the sake of Innate Purview and Calling.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true only for future gods. As I mentioned earlier, not every god born from two gods is partly his parent. Athena is not linked to Zeus in anyway. Hephaestus is a blacksmith... Zeus nor Hera are. Thor, the god of thunder is born from the All father whose powers are mostly linked to prophecies and Jord who is mother earth.<br /> <br /> Horus, god of Sun, nothing like Osiris or Isis. <br /> <br /> So why new gods are linked, somehow, to their parents?<br /> <br /> My partner and I came up with a simple idea that is kind of linked to what you said is that even old Gods are born heroes but no myth talks about them like heroes but only their god's prowesses.<br /> <br /> One of the things that could explain that is when Athena was challenged by Arachne... well, Athena challenged her actually, she failed to prove she was better than a mere mortal, probably because her crafts were not what they &quot;are&quot; right now and she needed those power to grow as her status of god.<br /> <br /> I mean, I am not talking about gods like Sun Wukong who clearly climbed every ladder to reach godhood. But if this is the case, what differs scions from two gods and scions half god half mortal? The access to the Overworld?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T07:07:32-07:00","id":1221692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1221663#post1221663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is true only for future gods. As I mentioned earlier, not every god born from two gods is partly his parent. Athena is not linked to Zeus in anyway. Hephaestus is a blacksmith... Zeus nor Hera are. Thor, the god of thunder is born from the All father whose powers are mostly linked to prophecies and Jord who is mother earth.<br /> <br /> Horus, god of Sun, nothing like Osiris or Isis.<br /> <br /> So why new gods are linked, somehow, to their parents?</div> </div> </div> </div>Athena takes after her mother, Metis, Goddess of Cunning. Hephaestus has Trickster as a Calling, in reference to the times he's trapped Hera and Aphrodite in hidden constructed traps... guess who <i>else</i> has Trickster... his father, Zeus. Thor is also a God of Fertility, and his mother is an Earth Deity. Horus is the easiest... he has Leader like his Father and Guardian like his Mother, and he has Purviews in common with both.<br /> <br /> Also, you inherit some things from your parent, but <i>none</i> of that defines you... you have to start out sharing a Calling, but there are rules for shedding and adopting new Callings, and the only other benefit is that you get to channel a single one of their Purviews for free... which you can choose to completely ignore for anything beyond it's Innate Power while you build up your Legend with other Purviews, so even new Gods barely need to be connected to their parents now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T09:36:34-07:00","id":1221733,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I don't buy the Callings you mentioned. I mean clearly you are trying to dig them out which I understand because you need it to make sens but Athena is the goddess of wisdom and strategy above all. Cunning is that what you really remember of her?<br /> <br /> Thor is fertility? Well, okay he can call rain to fall... but again, how many times he is represented or worshipped as the god of fertility?<br /> <br /> So if I follow your reasoning. I could be... Wukong's son and be the God of water and oh, I'll add Prophecy, Prosperity and Beauty but since I need to be related somehow to my father, i will choose Trickster. <br /> <br /> If I want other Purviews than Wukong's, won't I just go for N\u00fcwa or someone else? <br /> <br /> If I want to play the sexiest Scion to be a future god of lust and beauty, shouldn't I go for Aphrodite, Apollo, Bast, Isis, Freyja instead of Thor, Tezcatlipoca or Hachiman?<br /> <br /> What's the point in choosing Nezha if you want to play a merciful Scion. God, Guanyin is just on the previous page, man!<br /> <br /> My first point was there are better parents to come from when you become a blacksmith than Zeus and Hera. <br /> <br /> It might not be explanable, I just wanted to point that out. Or maybe an official answer would help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T10:02:56-07:00","id":1221744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1221733#post1221733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I don't buy the Callings you mentioned. I mean clearly you are trying to dig them out which I understand because you need it to make sens but Athena is the goddess of wisdom and strategy above all. Cunning is that what you really remember of her?</div> </div> </div> </div>To quote Theoi.com<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theoi.com</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">METIS was one of the elder Okeanides and the Titan-goddess of good counsel, planning, cunning and wisdom</div> </div> </div> </div>So yes, Athena does take after her Mother.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1221733#post1221733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thor is fertility? Well, okay he can call rain to fall... but again, how many times he is represented or worshipped as the god of fertility?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, Thor literally <i>has</i> Fertility in the book... his Title is God of Thunder, Rain and <b>Crops</b>. I don't know what else you need.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1221733#post1221733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if I follow your reasoning. I could be... Wukong's son and be the God of water and oh, I'll add Prophecy, Prosperity and Beauty but since I need to be related somehow to my father, i will choose Trickster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absoluely! Glad we're on the same page here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Though Prophecy isn't a Purview anymore, so you'll need to take the Prophet Path or the Fortune Purview.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1221733#post1221733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I want to play the sexiest Scion to be a future god of lust and beauty, shouldn't I go for Aphrodite, Apollo, Bast, Isis, Freyja instead of Thor, Tezcatlipoca or Hachiman?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? All you need to do is pick up the Beauty Purview... there's <i>literally <b>no</b> penalty</i> to using and having a Purview not associated with your Parent anymore, so why <i>woudln't</i> you be a sexy child of Osanyin or whatever?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1221733#post1221733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the point in choosing Nezha if you want to play a merciful Scion. God, Guanyin is just on the previous page, man!</div> </div> </div> </div>Erm, maybe you <i>like</i> Nehza as a character and want to be his Scion, and not be punished for not making a carbon copy of him? It's not my job to fill in your character's backstory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1221733#post1221733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first point was there are better parents to come from when you become a blacksmith than Zeus and Hera.</div> </div> </div> </div>And my point is there's literally no reason a child of Zeus and Hera can't be as great or even better Smith than a child of Ptah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T10:25:57-07:00","id":1221751,"title":"","content":"Cunning and wisdom aren't exclusive. Also taking some aspects doesn't mean it would be the same. Scion's take only pieces of their parent and build them to fit them to there liking.<br /> <br /> Also Thor being represented with Fertility no.but he was probably worshiped as such yeah. What we conceptualize from media doesn't necessarily correlate to how it really was in history.<br /> <br /> Edit. Ah sniped","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T11:19:20-07:00","id":1221771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1221733#post1221733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first point was there are better parents to come from when you become a blacksmith than Zeus and Hera.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, Neall's mentioned you can add new Innate Purviews to your powerset when you become a God. So Haphaestus <i>grew</i> into his power, mechanically. Again, there's not going to be a complete 1:1 mapping to perfectly capture all myth, like Samudra said, but this Edition comes close.<br /> <br /> Scions are going to inherit things from their parents. That's just how it goes. And as Samudra said, there's no XP tax for investing in Purviews that neither of your parents have, if you want to be a rebellious pissant. You want to be a Scion of Hades with the Beauty Purview? Relic Makeup, boom. Pick those Boons instead of say, Darkness or Prosperity or whatever you inherited from Hades. Paint on that smokey eyeshadow and make the living and the dead swoon with your awe-inspiring good looks.<br /> <br /> Honestly, 2e, for all concerns to the contrary, is actually far more merciful to Scions being different from their divine patron than 1e. There's no tax for getting skills your parents don't have, there's no tax for getting Purviews your parent doesn't have, you don't buy Boons with XP anymore so there's no tax for buying Boons that aren't associated with your patron.<br /> <br /> I could <i>quite easily</i> make three mechanically and personally distinct and viable Scions of Loki. I might, actually, to prove a point. (Not in this thread though)<br /> <br /> Eh, short version.<ul><li>The Thief - In the vein of Leverage. Uses the Trickster Calling and the Deception Purview to target white-collar jackasses who abuse the 99%</li> <li>The Activist - A social butterfly and ambitious lass. Uses the inspiring Fire Boon in combination with Liminal Knacks to put on multi-person art shows.</li> <li>The Warrior - Wrestler by day, monster hunter by night. Gets good use out of the Epic Strength he inherited from Loki (it's been stated as canon and not changing <b>SEVERAL</b> times now so nyeh) and uses the Lover Calling to motivate his fans and make allies.</li> </ul>Boom. Three Scion concepts, all legally viable, all taking <i>something</i> from Loki, all <i>different</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 05-24-2018, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T11:58:29-07:00","id":1221785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1221751#post1221751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cunning and wisdom aren't exclusive. Also taking some aspects doesn't mean it would be the same. Scion's take only pieces of their parent and build them to fit them to there liking.<br /> <br /> Also Thor being represented with Fertility no.but he was probably worshiped as such yeah. What we conceptualize from media doesn't necessarily correlate to how it really was in history.<br /> <br /> Edit. Ah sniped</div> </div> </div> </div>Thor wasn't explicitly related to fertility if I recall correctly, but there was a tradition of planting small hammer charms when they planted the seasons crops, and he was the god that blessed weddings. So the connection in Scion terms is understandable, it's probably just his weakest associated.<br /> <br /> Edit, as for playing characters that only have one calling and one purview in common and are otherwise entirely different; Drama. When Maudjee-Kawiss snubs you because you use leader and epic dexterity to coordinate and perform complicated surgery's, or when Heimdall doesn't like the way you use his Hunter and Epic Stamina tricks to perform Loki style burglaries it open's up dramatic scenes, and ways to craft great deeds and legends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","user":"vonpenguin","date":". 05-24-2018, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T13:27:51-07:00","id":1221824,"title":"","content":"I guess when you wanna be right so badly, there's nothing much to say ^^<br /> <br /> if you find joy in changing all the concepts because you just like Nezha but nothing linked to his story or his attributes... then find. Suit yourselves <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T13:53:24-07:00","id":1221829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1221824#post1221824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess when you wanna be right so badly, there's nothing much to say ^^<br /> <br /> if you find joy in changing all the concepts because you just like Nezha but nothing linked to his story or his attributes... then find. Suit yourselves <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Why on earth would you change Nehza's concepts if you like him? Presumably you like him as character <i>because</i> of those concepts.<br /> <br /> Nobody has suggested that at all... we've simply been pointing out what should be self-evident : That Nehza's Scions are <i><b>not</b></i> Nehza and should not be punished for not being carbon copies of Nehza... which, thankfully in this edition, they are not.<br /> <br /> So, again thankfully, I don't have to change anything to suit my preferences. You, on the other hand, are going to need to change a hell of a lot to get this system to conform to your expectations. Which, if you wish to do so... Suit yourself <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T15:09:28-07:00","id":1221853,"title":"","content":"You just contradict yourself man but it's fine if you all understand yourselves. I'll wait for the God book to have the final answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T17:02:36-07:00","id":1221883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1221733#post1221733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I don't buy the Callings you mentioned. I mean clearly you are trying to dig them out which I understand because you need it to make sens but Athena is the goddess of wisdom and strategy above all. Cunning is that what you really remember of her?<br /> <br /> Thor is fertility? Well, okay he can call rain to fall... but again, how many times he is represented or worshipped as the god of fertility?</div> </div> </div> </div>Frequently. Mjolnir is a phallus symbol used at weddings and farming for that reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T23:40:29-07:00","id":1221955,"title":"","content":"So I'm playing a daughter of two incarnates. Sif and Thor as youtubing backpackers. Still in origin but my plan for her is:<br /> <br /> Liminal - neither in Sif nor Thor because of how much traveling she's done. <br /> Lover - from Sif and leveraged as love for the fans and love for her peers as her concept is a daredevil media darling who's known for pulling of great stunts. <br /> Warrior - definitely a bit from Thor but she's prone to making more emphasis on putting on a show than on efficiently defeating her enemies. <br /> <br /> Fertility because it's the only thing on Sif that was vaguely connected and I'm probably only likely to ever use the innate power. <br /> <br /> Sun and Prosperity through a &quot;relic&quot; that is her having been born with golden hair like her mother. <br /> <br /> Neither Thor nor Sif have either Prosperity or Sun as purviews. And these are going to be her primary purviews. <br /> <br /> I am considering Epic Dex or Epic Sta because of the stunt aspect of her personality. But it would be largely extra. <br /> <br /> She is a little bit her of her parents but it has been noted that she's far more Vanir than Aesir in some of her habits of presentation enjoying more flash and spectacle than most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T23:41:44-07:00","id":1221956,"title":"","content":"I'm also surprised that anybody would find it odd for cunning to be Attributed to Athena. She is the one that taught Odysseus all his tricks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T04:31:36-07:00","id":1221986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1221824#post1221824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess when you wanna be right so badly, there's nothing much to say ^^<br /> <br /> if you find joy in changing all the concepts because you just like Nezha but nothing linked to his story or his attributes... then find. Suit yourselves <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oi, don't go putting words in someone else's mouth. Least of all someone who's been nothing but patient with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T05:29:32-07:00","id":1221992,"title":"","content":"I have seen nothing contradictory in any of their arguments.<br /> <br /> Original position: Scion 2e forces you to play carbon copies of your parents which doesn't work when you look at myth.<br /> <br /> Argument: Samudra, Kyman, and others presented several example characters that show that this is demonstrably not a problem with 2nd edition Scion.<br /> <br /> Counter Argument: Examples from myth to that seemingly could not be done with the rules as they exist. Athena was one specific and that &quot;there are better parents to come from when you become a blacksmith than Zeus and Hera.&quot; Thor being primarily worshipped in a fertility role was scoffed at. You also accused people of changing the stats and stories of Nezha.<br /> <br /> Argument 2: Several presented you with evidence to show that Athena was a scion of her mother and that Hephaestus could have grown into his power at God because you can apparently pick an additional innate purview at that point.<br /> <br /> Counter 2: Declaration that God will have the final answer.<br /> <br /> <br /> The problem here is that the argument shifts around.<br /> <br /> When evidence is shown that a scion can go completely left field of their parents evidence is presented out of myth of things that don't appear to fit the rules.<br /> <br /> On the face of it this is a good tactic, but on the other hand, they showed that a perceived problem wasn't actually a problem, so it seems odd to continue the argument.<br /> <br /> However, the argument did continue.<br /> <br /> The Athena example was countered by pointing out that Athena was primarily the child of Metis. After all it was the prophecy that Metis's child would be greater than her parents which prompted Zeus to swallow her in the first place, so clearly Fate (or the ancient Greeks) attached more impetus to the maternal bloodline than the paternal.<br /> <br /> The Hephaestus example was countered by noting that Hephaestus could have gained the Forge purview as innate at the God stage.<br /> <br /> The accusation of them changing Nezha's story and nature is completely bizarre because all the discussion has been about scions deviating from their parents and I didn't see anybody even touch the idea of altering the parents stats in a homebrew or such.<br /> <br /> The Thor protest is also odd because Thor was massively popular among farmers, indeed he was primarily the god of manual labor in general and especially farming. There are a lot of his stories that start with him farming or building something and getting interrupted for some cause. The bit about thunder bolts and his hammer is just what got latched onto when adventure stories were read or superhero comics were written. And also, in earlier days, because of the juxtaposition with Zeus/Jupiter which had also been syncretized with the Christian concept of the Abrahamic god causing that entity to shift from a nebulous inhuman concept to the anthropomorphized bearded guy in the sky.<br /> <br /> I assume the &quot;wait until God book&quot; thing is based on the comment that, by word of Neall, at least one extra innate purview is to be had at God rank. This does present a neat little delay and escape for the argument but it still doesn't help the original argument.<br /> <br /> In order to prove that it is hard to not play a carbon copy of your parent, a person would have to show difficulty in finding even one example character that isn't a carbon copy. My example Sif-child isn't the best one because while she differs on several key themes on story arc and personality from both Thor and Sif, she is very much deliberately modeled to be similar on a cosmetic level to her mother. However, Kyman provided three very good examples of Loki children who are quite different from each other or Loki.<br /> <br /> Contrary to finding difficulty in finding an example that wasn't a carbon copy, it has proven a struggle to find even one example from myth where parents and child were very different and could not have been done by the rules. Even if, by some small chance, it should prove that new innates are not gained at God tier and thus that Hephaestus by myth is impossible by rules it still fails to prove the initial argument that the game is forcing one to play a mini-me of the parent. Because there are already numerous examples to show that plenty of scions go off at tangential directions to their parents.<br /> <br /> As an aside, the original argument is something I disliked heavily about 1st edition Scion, but it is not really present in 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> The inherited purviews and epics in 1st edition were never really the problem, especially since the only purview you really inherited was the Pantheon one and every other purview came through relics. The inherited experience point discounts were the problem.<br /> <br /> In 1st edition, a character that went off at right angles to their parent would advance much slower than a character who followed in step with their parent's abilities. As such, the carbon copy issue was very much a problem. You could shift it about here and there like change the way you approach fire or sky with some custom boons, but you'd still be sort of Zeus 2.0 in many ways. And their iconic characters reflected that to a degree. Some were very different in personality to their parents, but most of them were also very alike in powers.<br /> <br /> In 2nd edition experience point costs are flat. There's no discount or bonus. So a character that goes a different path than their parent is going to advance at roughly the same speed as a character who follows their parents' skills to the tee.<br /> <br /> You're never really going to get a good match up of rules to story. Just like you're never going to get a good match up of story to reality.<br /> <br /> Reality is very nebulous, chaotic. Most events have no real purpose and are really just quite random.<br /> <br /> Stories are more structured but still very fluid and very flexible. While they might have a vaguely predictable overall shape and present a perceivable purpose, the details are still very shifty.<br /> <br /> Game rules are far more defined even a role-playing game is going to have a lot of things that are more precise and limited than a story. RPGs always fail to get precise perfect replications of fiction because at most they can present a snap-shot of the fictional character as they existed for a brief moment in time before something about the story was adapted or reinterpreted.<br /> <br /> I suppose this won't matter overall, but still thought I should say it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","user":"Thrythlind","date":". 05-25-2018, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T07:56:05-07:00","id":1222034,"title":"","content":"In addition to all the points made by people above, I'd just like to add that, other than the fact that it doesn't need to be channeled via Birthrights, Innate Purviews have <i>no</i> power benefit over Channeled ones. They are <i>not</i> somehow <i>better</i> than Channeled ones. So, even if Hephaestus never ever makes Forge Innate, he will <i>still</i> be just as good at Forging things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T09:41:39-07:00","id":1222066,"title":"","content":"And this is a bit delayed, but the argument of &quot;Athena is Wisdom and Strategy, not cunning&quot;<br /> <br /> ... Cunning is like THE adjective most applied to strategies.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ah, a cunning strategy&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T10:37:15-07:00","id":1222077,"title":"","content":"And how many variations of the statement &quot;all martial arts is deception&quot; or &quot;all war is deception&quot; are there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T00:15:17-07:00","id":1222840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Indivisible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1208378#post1208378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So about the Beauty Purview innate power:<br /> <br /> It says that you may attempt a Feat of Scale when you roll to influence a character using<br /> your beauty, appearance, and body language.<br /> <br /> Is this like invoking your Legendary title, where you need to spend a point of Legend? There's a boon in Epic Strength that explicitly says the you can make a Feat of Scale without spending a point of Legend, and it limits it to once a scene.<br /> <br /> If you don't have to spend a point of Legend, it seems overly powerful, as it doesn't limit the effect to once per scene.<br /> If you do have to spend a point of Legend, then the innate power seems very weak, as it is the only innate power that requires spending Legend to get any use out of it. Sun and Moon both have the option to spend Legend, but there's also a free base effect to use.<br /> <br /> If Legendary Titles are a special type of path, that means that they can each be invoked once per session, and a use of that invocation is to make a Feat of Scale. Is the intent that Beauty provides a way to make Feats of Scale in terms of attraction as often as you have Legend to spend on it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry to quote myself, but it has been a month and reading through the thread again other people had the same question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/458-indivisible","name":"Indivisible","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T09:57:35-07:00","id":1222931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Indivisible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1222840#post1222840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry to quote myself, but it has been a month and reading through the thread again other people had the same question.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have to spend a point of Legend. The bonus of the Beauty Innate Power is that you can use a Feat of Scale for <i>any</i> action that falls under your appearance and body language, regardless of whether it falls under your Title or Keywords or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T13:09:38-07:00","id":1223367,"title":"","content":"in which pantheon would you put Anansi? what powers should he have?<br /> <br /> pantheon purview? cheval?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T13:21:10-07:00","id":1223373,"title":"","content":"Anansi originates with the Akan people of Ghana/Ashanteland and is of an entirely different pantheon than either the Loa or the Orisha - the Anak are from an entirely different part of Africa. The stories and myths did spread to the West Indies and general Caribbean area along with the Americas via slavery, of course. He'd be part of a theoretical Akan-derived pantheon. The religion is <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akan_religion\" target=\"_blank\">Akom</a>, much as the Orisha have Vodun in Yorubaland. The pantheon would likely be the Abosom, which refers to the lesser spirits and deities that serve under the creator god, who has many names but we'll call Nyame for ease right this second.<br /> <br /> E: All that said, you <i>might</i> be able to get away with Gun/Cheval, because of a Surinamese syncretization of the Orisha and the Abosom, called <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winti\" target=\"_blank\">Winti</a>. However, I'd probably go with a Purview closer to the Manitou one, given how Akom worship works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1778,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","user":"MorsRattus","date":". 05-30-2018, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T13:26:42-07:00","id":1223377,"title":"","content":"Watcher and Sacerdos are writing that pantheon up, and by the looks of it, it's going to be awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T16:43:31-07:00","id":1223429,"title":"","content":"A friend of mine works at a gaming store and he wanted to know what company you were going to use for distribution, and when it would be ready for pre-order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T06:54:12-07:00","id":1223611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rickayelm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1223429#post1223429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A friend of mine works at a gaming store and he wanted to know what company you were going to use for distribution, and when it would be ready for pre-order.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Probably better for your friend to reach out to Rich through his Onyx Path contact info (<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/about/contact/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/about/contact/</a>), rather than here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18560-saedar","name":"saedar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T02:53:32-07:00","id":1223864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1222931#post1222931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have to spend a point of Legend. The bonus of the Beauty Innate Power is that you can use a Feat of Scale for <i>any</i> action that falls under your appearance and body language, regardless of whether it falls under your Title or Keywords or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. I thought it was something like that, though I'm still not sure if it suffers from the same limitations on frequency of use that titles do.<br /> <br /> That makes it the only innate power that has no effect unless you're spending Legend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/458-indivisible","name":"Indivisible","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T19:53:52-07:00","id":1224266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Indivisible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1223864#post1223864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you. I thought it was something like that, though I'm still not sure if it suffers from the same limitations on frequency of use that titles do.<br /> <br /> That makes it the only innate power that has no effect unless you're spending Legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>It expands the range of what you can declare a Feat of Scale. If your Title has nothing to do with the action you're doing, but you have Beauty, and you're doing something that would benefit from your appearance or body language, the Beauty Purview can let you make it a Feat of Scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T00:20:45-07:00","id":1224292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Indivisible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1223864#post1223864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you. I thought it was something like that, though I'm still not sure if it suffers from the same limitations on frequency of use that titles do.<br /> <br /> That makes it the only innate power that has no effect unless you're spending Legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically speaking, the Beauty Innate doesn't require you to spend Legend at all... It expands the category of actions that you can turn into a Feat of Scale, which is an entirely passive effect. Invoking the Feat of Scale is what is costing the Legend. And while this might seem a little less than the Epic Strength Innate, that one isn't as universally applicable... It won't help you with a ballet recital, for instance... By contrast, the Beauty Innate can turn any action where looks and body language can have an effect into a Feat of Scale... Which is, frankly, every single social action ever. The ability to turn almost any Social Action into a Feat is very strong, and needs the Legend cost to balance it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T19:00:33-07:00","id":1224870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1221771#post1221771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Neall's mentioned you can add new Innate Purviews to your powerset when you become a God. So Haphaestus <i>grew</i> into his power, mechanically. Again, there's not going to be a complete 1:1 mapping to perfectly capture all myth, like Samudra said, but this Edition comes close.<br /> <br /> Scions are going to inherit things from their parents. That's just how it goes. And as Samudra said, there's no XP tax for investing in Purviews that neither of your parents have, if you want to be a rebellious pissant. You want to be a Scion of Hades with the Beauty Purview? Relic Makeup, boom. Pick those Boons instead of say, Darkness or Prosperity or whatever you inherited from Hades. Paint on that smokey eyeshadow and make the living and the dead swoon with your awe-inspiring good looks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. I can just imagine taking your favorite &quot;sitcom centered on family that struggles with everyone being so different&quot; and converting it to Scion. Actually, I s'pose that's Dragonball. I have a related question, possibly answered but I haven't been following the development. I'm curious if you can extend that back a generation to 2E equivalent to Titans, say Chronos/Rhea and their children? Seems like Hestia is the odd one out as not being cunning/backstabbing/cray cray like her sibs - maybe she takes more after Rhea? I'd be stumped if I had to explain the Norse cow ancestor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T05:11:01-07:00","id":1224929,"title":"","content":"I understand that being able to turn many actions into a Feat of Scale is powerful, and if it can apply to any social action rather than just ones playing on the character's appearance, then it is probably strong enough to stand on its own. I was always pretty sure that it required a point of Legend, but I wanted to note that I found the wording ambiguous in a thread that I know a developer reads, especially as there were similar questions earlier in the thread.<br /> <br /> However, there is a genuine question about how often you can attempt a Feat of Scale with the Beauty innate power. Invoking a title for a Feat of Scale is limited in the same way as invoking a path, and Boons that allow you to make a Feat of Scale include how often they can be used in their description. The Beauty innate power does not have any limitations on frequency of use listed and does not have the invocation limitations of a path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/458-indivisible","name":"Indivisible","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T12:19:42-07:00","id":1227491,"title":"","content":"What's the maximum cap on the tension pool?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13508-necrobotany","name":"necrobotany","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T13:52:15-07:00","id":1227514,"title":"","content":"Hi Neall<br /> <br /> Is Sc\u00e1thach the Shadow going to be in any of the books ( as a Scion, Mentor, or even a God?) <br /> <br /> and if so what pantheon is she going to be connected too, The Irish pantheon or the Scottish/ Welsh pantheon.<br /> <br /> Its just that as a legendary Scottish warrior queen/goddess and martial arts teacher who is only really remembered in Irish myth she is in a weird place when it comes to where she should go. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24326-jester","name":"Jester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T14:04:44-07:00","id":1227515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jester</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1227514#post1227514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi Neall<br /> <br /> Is Sc\u00e1thach the Shadow going to be in any of the books ( as a Scion, Mentor, or even a God?)<br /> <br /> and if so what pantheon is she going to be connected too, The Irish pantheon or the Scottish/ Welsh pantheon.<br /> <br /> Its just that as a legendary Scottish warrior queen/goddess and martial arts teacher who is only really remembered in Irish myth she is in a weird place when it comes to where she should go.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not Neall of course, but Sc\u00e1thach is a great Guide for any Scion of the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 Danann. There is no scholarly evidence that suggests a role of a deity for her, though a half-argument could be made that she might be one of the S\u00edd due to the nature of her realm having several markers of being an Otherworld. Though, normally the manuscripts make the identity of S\u00edd plainly known through outright statement or descriptions of clothing and hair.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, there is no Scottish Pantheon she could fit into due to the assimilation of the various Pictish kingdoms into D\u00e1l Riata, and the lack of any details towards their native pre-Scotti invasion (and conversion to Christianity by the various early Ionan missionaries) religious beliefs asides from some absolutely beautiful stones. The Plant Don do not have any record of her from what I have read. She is a unique to early Irish saga literature.<br /> <br /> She is a brilliant Guide for a Scion of the Irish Pantheon (or any other, to be fair) who wishes to be trained in the profession of Hero from the Irish context. Weapon Feats, and the like. A great oppertunity for cross-Pantheon interactions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 06-14-2018, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T14:15:49-07:00","id":1227520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1227515#post1227515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not Neall of course, but Sc\u00e1thach is a great Guide for any Scion of the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 Danann. There is no scholarly evidence that suggests a role of a deity for her, though a half-argument could be made that she might be one of the S\u00edd due to the nature of her realm having several markers of being an Otherworld. Though, normally the manuscripts make the identity of S\u00edd plainly known through outright statement or descriptions of clothing and hair.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, there is no Scottish Pantheon she could fit into due to the assimilation of the various Pictish kingdoms into D\u00e1l Riata, and the lack of any details towards their native pre-Scotti invasion (and conversion to Christianity by the various early Ionan missionaries) religious beliefs asides from some absolutely beautiful stones. The Plant Don do not have any record of her from what I have read. She is a unique to early Irish saga literature.<br /> <br /> She is a brilliant Guide for a Scion of the Irish Pantheon (or any other, to be fair) who wishes to be trained in the profession of Hero from the Irish context. Weapon Feats, and the like. A great oppertunity for cross-Pantheon interactions.</div> </div> </div> </div>thank you for the quick reply!<br /> <br /> so does that mean we will be seeing her in the examples for mentors or will i need to stat her myself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24326-jester","name":"Jester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T14:27:06-07:00","id":1227525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jester</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1227520#post1227520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">thank you for the quick reply!<br /> <br /> so does that mean we will be seeing her in the examples for mentors or will i need to stat her myself?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, happy to help. She is not presented in the pre-written Guides from what has been released to the Backers, though changes may be put in before things go to print as always. You could easily take some of the already existing Guides mechanical skeletons and rewrite them into Sc\u00e1thach, or you could write her from scratch. She has a lot of potential uses as a Guide, tons of different Unique Knacks, and Guide Stunts based on the various Weapon Feats C\u00faChulainn knows is a great place to start, as well as potentially being the source of other Birthrights herself.<br /> <br /> If there's anything I can do to help you writing her up, just toss me a PM. I am a wealth of otherwise hyper-niche information regarding the Irish saga texts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T15:20:39-07:00","id":1227540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>necrobotany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1227491#post1227491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the maximum cap on the tension pool?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is none. Spend it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T18:00:45-07:00","id":1235760,"title":"","content":"Hi Neall, with regards to Supernatural Paths in Scion:Origin, is there anything stopping a PC from being a Saint and a pre-visitation Scion?<br /> <br /> And do they retain their Saint knacks after their visitation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T16:28:46-07:00","id":1236198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1235760#post1235760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi Neall, with regards to Supernatural Paths in Scion:Origin, is there anything stopping a PC from being a Saint and a pre-visitation Scion?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And do they retain their Saint knacks after their visitation? </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to say no. Scions tend to be a little more visceral, and it's best to keep the themes separate. That said, you could probably be okay with it on the Hero level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T16:47:55-07:00","id":1236205,"title":"","content":"Neall! Question about the Bestiary. What powers do you plan to give the Fair Folk?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T17:06:17-07:00","id":1236208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1236198#post1236198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, but...<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm inclined to say no. Scions tend to be a little more visceral, and it's best to keep the themes separate. That said, you could probably be okay with it on the Hero level.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a bit confused by what you mean Visceral...?<br /> <br /> If it is that you believe that the Saint is a milkwater path, then I beg to differ. For one scene, you can punch out things way above your tier (I gave the example of a human clocking Yamata no Orochi), if that isn't visceral, then I truly am confused.<br /> <br /> I would envision it possibly as a Path for a Scion who is appointed by fate to render judgement onto a Pantheon who hasn't lived up to their own standards:<br /> <br /> Case in point: Kratos from the god of war series. Even as a pre-visitation human, he was capable of taking on Scylla, after the revelation of what he was, he is able to punch way-way above his weight class (eventually taking on Zeus).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T17:19:02-07:00","id":1236214,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't think that saints would be...well, &quot;in yo face&quot; much at first.<br /> I would however think that they'd progress into something similar to a paladin fighter of a sort. Maybe something along the lines of a &quot;Knight of a Cross&quot; that Jim Butcher's &quot;Dresden Files&quot; has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T18:17:19-07:00","id":1236231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1236208#post1236208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm a bit confused by what you mean Visceral...?<br /> <br /> If it is that you believe that the Saint is a milkwater path, then I beg to differ. For one scene, you can punch out things way above your tier (I gave the example of a human clocking Yamata no Orochi), if that isn't visceral, then I truly am confused.<br /> <br /> I would envision it possibly as a Path for a Scion who is appointed by fate to render judgement onto a Pantheon who hasn't lived up to their own standards:<br /> <br /> Case in point: Kratos from the god of war series. Even as a pre-visitation human, he was capable of taking on Scylla, after the revelation of what he was, he is able to punch way-way above his weight class (eventually taking on Zeus).</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I believe visceral in this case refers to (active) Scions having their own inherent power to create miracles, and not relying on the more abstract relationship between fate and the virtues the way saints do. <br /> <br /> It may not be broken to stack the two (at least at Hero, it sounds like it would be at Demigod) but it would be too redundant for a lot of people\u2019s tastes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T18:20:42-07:00","id":1236236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1236214#post1236214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't think that saints would be...well, &quot;in yo face&quot; much at first.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would depend entirely on which Virtue they were exemplifying. If it\u2019s Egotism, Audacity, Prowess, etc.... I think you start to see why you shouldn\u2019t necessarily associate \u201cSaint\u201d with the kind of compassionate meekness or passivity honored by other cultures\u2019 concepts of religious virtue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T03:02:10-07:00","id":1236706,"title":"","content":"So now that the worst of this rush is over, when are you folks thinking about getting underway with Demigod? And which new pantheons can we look forwards to seeing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13499-not-quite-yoda","name":"Not Quite Yoda","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T08:26:00-07:00","id":1236781,"title":"","content":"Quick question. Since Creator and Hunter mention applying to less literal applications does that extend to other callings as well? For example, Healer mentions &quot;putting things right&quot; and &quot;purification&quot; in the fluff but with the exception of reconstructions all the knacks only deal with literal, physical, injuries. Could surgeon with the Hands of God halve the time to purify a sacred groove? Or could immunization booster help protect a &quot;patient&quot; from the &quot;disease&quot; of being lured into a titanic cult? Could Guardian Knacks help a defense lawyer in court?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T12:46:58-07:00","id":1236868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1236781#post1236781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question. Since Creator and Hunter mention applying to less literal applications does that extend to other callings as well? For example, Healer mentions &amp;quot;putting things right&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;purification&amp;quot; in the fluff but with the exception of reconstructions all the knacks only deal with literal, physical, injuries. Could surgeon with the Hands of God halve the time to purify a sacred groove? Or could immunization booster help protect a &amp;quot;patient&amp;quot; from the &amp;quot;disease&amp;quot; of being lured into a titanic cult? Could Guardian Knacks help a defense lawyer in court?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not Neall, but if a player approached me with some Knacks that fit those themes I'd look then over for balance but I'd allow them thematically","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T15:29:21-07:00","id":1237308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1236868#post1236868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not Neall, but if a player approached me with some Knacks that fit those themes I'd look then over for balance but I'd allow them thematically</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean you'd consider them entirely separate knacks from the original ones in the book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T10:04:53-07:00","id":1237527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1237308#post1237308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you mean you'd consider them entirely separate knacks from the original ones in the book?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure the Knack list isn't meant to be comprehensive, so if someone wanted to make their own Knack and could explain how this one fit under another Calling to my satisfaction I'd probably allow it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T14:48:00-07:00","id":1237813,"title":"","content":"Are there any plans on how to make Anansi a viable divine parent since an npc in Origins is one of his Scions? Is an Ashanti Pantheon write-up likely? If not, how should we handle things like Virtues, PSP, Asset Skills, Motifs, etc for the Scions of popular gods like Anansi without detailed Pantheons?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T22:59:01-07:00","id":1237896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1237813#post1237813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any plans on how to make Anansi a viable divine parent since an npc in Origins is one of his Scions? Is an Ashanti Pantheon write-up likely? If not, how should we handle things like Virtues, PSP, Asset Skills, Motifs, etc for the Scions of popular gods like Anansi without detailed Pantheons?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Companion book is gonna have a Build Your Own Pantheon section. I'd be shocked if there weren't steps for Virtues, PSPs, and Motifs","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T10:17:39-07:00","id":1238001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1237896#post1237896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Companion book is gonna have a Build Your Own Pantheon section. I'd be shocked if there weren't steps for Virtues, PSPs, and Motifs</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine so, but I was more asking if there were plans to deal specifically with individually popular gods like Anansi (who they\u2019ve already included a Scion of in Origins) in a more supported way than every table hacking together their own idea of what Ashanti Virtues, PSP, etc, should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-23-2018, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T11:43:32-07:00","id":1238023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1238001#post1238001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagine so, but I was more asking if there were plans to deal specifically with individually popular gods like Anansi (who they\u2019ve already included a Scion of in Origins) in a more supported way than every table doing their own idea of what\u2019s Ashanti Virtues should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per Neall, they have a few Gods without a pantheon, or with a distant relationship to one, in the tutelary Gods section in the Companion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T18:01:45-07:00","id":1239117,"title":"","content":"Does the purview that dominates a Titan necessarily correspond to the Primordial they're tied to/that bore them? If Kronus emenates from Gaia, does that mean she's a/the Fertility Primordial, and not the Earth Primordial, for example?<br /> <br /> I'm guessing the relationship doesn't have to be that close, since Ahriman/Angra Mainyu is presumably a Titan of Deception, Darkness, or Chaos - and Ahura Mazda is a Primordial of either Sun or Order...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T02:41:56-07:00","id":1239231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1239117#post1239117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the purview that dominates a Titan necessarily correspond to the Primordial they're tied to/that bore them? If Kronus emenates from Gaia, does that mean she's a/the Fertility Primordial, and not the Earth Primordial, for example?<br /> <br /> I'm guessing the relationship doesn't have to be that close, since Ahriman/Angra Mainyu is presumably a Titan of Deception, Darkness, or Chaos - and Ahura Mazda is a Primordial of either Sun or Order...</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say no. There's probably wiggle room for a Titan to represent a Purview that's tangentially related to whatever Primordial they came from. Assuming that the Primordial in question didn't just have them and the Titan grew into a different Purview.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, Primordials can be associated with multiple Purviews. Kitchi-Manitou, of the Manitou, is a Primordial, and has Darkness, Forge, Fortune, Prosperity, Stars, and Sun associated, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T10:43:03-07:00","id":1239364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1239231#post1239231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say no. There's probably wiggle room for a Titan to represent a Purview that's tangentially related to whatever Primordial they came from. Assuming that the Primordial in question didn't just have them and the Titan grew into a different Purview.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, Primordials can be associated with multiple Purviews. Kitchi-Manitou, of the Manitou, is a Primordial, and has Darkness, Forge, Fortune, Prosperity, Stars, and Sun associated, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>He wields all of those, but I assume there\u2019s one that he is the Primordial \u201cof\u201d - my own assumption is Kitchi Manitou is how the Manitou relate to the \u201cdreams\u201d aspect of the darkness Primordial (while the Netjer for example know it as Kek and Kauket and relate to them more in terms of the absence of light than the sleep and dreams part of the purview).<br /> <br /> But I guess all of this will probably be headcanon debates until we get the God book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T11:13:46-07:00","id":1239737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1239364#post1239364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He wields all of those, but I assume there\u2019s one that he is the Primordial \u201cof\u201d - my own assumption is Kitchi Manitou is how the Manitou relate to the \u201cdreams\u201d aspect of the darkness Primordial (while the Netjer for example know it as Kek and Kauket and relate to them more in terms of the absence of light than the sleep and dreams part of the purview).<br /> <br /> But I guess all of this will probably be headcanon debates until we get the God book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Primordials are too big to be represented by just ONE Purview. Kitchi-Manitou... Here let me pull out a passage from the Hero Rough Draft-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The chief Primordial of the Manitou is Kitchi-Manitou: the Great Mystery, creator of all things, people, and Manitou. Creation began with the vision and dream within Kitchi-Manitou, sometimes known as Gitche-Manitou, other times as Chi-Manidoo. Through this dream, the Primordial had a knowing of the universe, and an experience of all it could be. Kitchi-Manitou immediately set into motion making this dream manifest, creating what we know to be the physical World. In the World, Kitchi-Manitou created and placed all the beings that would cohabitate in all ways. This included all plants, animals, fish, birds, insects, peoples, and Manitou. This is all that it did. </div> </div> </div>Kitchi-Maintou is Dream. It is potential, it is the formation of possibility and reality. Its reach and powers are more than one Purview can encompass.<br /> <br /> TITANS may be consumed by one Purview, but I'm pretty sure that Primordials are going to be several Purviews linked by a Theme<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T11:52:46-07:00","id":1239745,"title":"","content":"I have to ask; why are the Gods limited to only three Callings each? It seems arbitrary - why not just say, &quot;This God/Goddess has whatever myths say they have&quot;, and go from there? Some might have one or two, some might have five or six. It would eliminate a lot of &quot;but why doesn't deity X have Calling Y, when the myths imply they should?&quot;, and it would allow more flexibility when picking a divine parent. Again, one can do whatever you want in your own game, so it's certainly possible to customize if you want [and I would, I suspect], but I wonder why the limits were put there in the first place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T12:35:01-07:00","id":1239760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1239745#post1239745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to ask; why are the Gods limited to only three Callings each? It seems arbitrary - why not just say, &quot;This God/Goddess has whatever myths say they have&quot;, and go from there? Some might have one or two, some might have five or six. It would eliminate a lot of &quot;but why doesn't deity X have Calling Y, when the myths imply they should?&quot;, and it would allow more flexibility when picking a divine parent. Again, one can do whatever you want in your own game, so it's certainly possible to customize if you want [and I would, I suspect], but I wonder why the limits were put there in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div>Game balance?<br /> <br /> A way to call attention to the biggest roles they represented rather than go with &quot;So everyone who's ever won a fight is a Warrior yes I realize this means 80% of the Gods are now a Warrior&quot;?<br /> <br /> A method to chart the growth and change of the Legend over time, such as Loki losing the Creator Calling when he consumed Logi and took his wife and now has the Lover Calling?<br /> <br /> A way to keep distant from the 1e setup of &quot;So this one God gives you access to literally everything making them the Mechanically Objectively Superior Choice&quot; (looking at you, 1e Odin)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T12:44:21-07:00","id":1239767,"title":"","content":"Yeah the path I think there going with it isn't that God's have always had there three Callings. But that because Callings can.be changed they probably have had others but they don't have it now. Like take Zeus for example, if your talking about Zeus from the beggining of the Pantheon he was pretty much a Warrior as he declared war against the Titans. When that was done and over with, he lost that and became a Lover or something along those lines. That's probably simplifying things a bit but I think that's the reason there gonna give to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T14:02:05-07:00","id":1239794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1239745#post1239745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to ask; why are the Gods limited to only three Callings each? It seems arbitrary - why not just say, &quot;This God/Goddess has whatever myths say they have&quot;, and go from there? Some might have one or two, some might have five or six. It would eliminate a lot of &quot;but why doesn't deity X have Calling Y, when the myths imply they should?&quot;, and it would allow more flexibility when picking a divine parent. Again, one can do whatever you want in your own game, so it's certainly possible to customize if you want [and I would, I suspect], but I wonder why the limits were put there in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div>They need some degree of limitation so fighting how Fate wants to define you, and redefining yourself is an actual struggle to build stories around.<br /> <br /> If Callings are uncapped you lose that conflict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T15:36:30-07:00","id":1239816,"title":"","content":"I'm not suggesting we give everyone a Calling to reflect every time they won a fight, or seduced someone. But the heads of the Pantheons [for example] should be more flexible than their associates, so why not give Tezcatlipoca or Odin or Zeus more than three Callings? While I recognize that its' a matter of game balance, it just comes across as a bit too mechanical - in a sense, like the &quot;everything has five tribes/households/iterations&quot; limitation on standard NWoD books. Like I said, I would probably make my own changes, and maybe things will be different when we get Demigod and God down the road. But I find it a bit too limiting as a GM as it stands. Just sayin'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T15:54:57-07:00","id":1239820,"title":"","content":"\u201cRuler of Pantheon\u201d status is too ambiguous in many cases to give it special rules. It\u2019s easy to point at Zeus and Odin with their respective Pantheons, but Indra certainly shouldn\u2019t be treated with rules that place him above any of the goddesses who reflect aspects of Shakti (for example).<br /> <br /> Thankfully 2nd edition allows for gods like Zeus and Odin to be more powerful because not every viable divine parent is Legend 12 this time; so Zeus can be mightier than the rest of the Pantheon without needing more Purviews or Callings. We don\u2019t have 1st edition\u2019s problem where the number of associated powers is effectively a measure of a God\u2019s might.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T18:26:18-07:00","id":1239860,"title":"","content":"So, how is Zeus mightier, then? If he is still limited to three Callings, and there is no &quot;divine rank&quot;, how do we determine that Quetzalcoatl is a more powerful (i.e. older, more well-rounded) deity than, say, Itzlacoliuque? Or Odin over Bragi? There should be some indicator that, &quot;oh, Amaterasu is a bit higher on the celestial ladder than Uke-Mochi.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T21:05:28-07:00","id":1239891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1239860#post1239860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, how is Zeus mightier, then? If he is still limited to three Callings, and there is no &amp;quot;divine rank&amp;quot;, how do we determine that Quetzalcoatl is a more powerful (i.e. older, more well-rounded) deity than, say, Itzlacoliuque? Or Odin over Bragi? There should be some indicator that, &amp;quot;oh, Amaterasu is a bit higher on the celestial ladder than Uke-Mochi.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's called your Legend Rank. Zeus would be Legend 12, while Hestia is probably 9","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T21:53:47-07:00","id":1239897,"title":"","content":"Ah, they <i>are</i> still using Legend Rank in 2e - I wasn't clear on that. Makes sense, then. I'd probably still add extra Callings as I felt were necessary, but at least there is a rank so that one deity can be represented as stronger [so to speak] than another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T22:09:59-07:00","id":1239902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1239860#post1239860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, how is Zeus mightier, then? If he is still limited to three Callings, and there is no &quot;divine rank&quot;, how do we determine that Quetzalcoatl is a more powerful (i.e. older, more well-rounded) deity than, say, Itzlacoliuque? Or Odin over Bragi? There should be some indicator that, &quot;oh, Amaterasu is a bit higher on the celestial ladder than Uke-Mochi.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea that more Callings makes you more powerful is a fallacy... especially given the limited number of Calling dots available a theoretical God with 4 or 5 Callings would only be able to perform a trick or two related to each.<br /> <br /> In addition, Pantheons like the Deva and Manitou don't <i>have</i> a set ruling figure, so I don't see why Pantheon rulers need any special rules, unless you want to say that Zeus with 5 Callings is somehow mightier than Durga with three (though again, that is based on the idea that more Callings = more Power, which is simply not true).<br /> <br /> Finally, as already noted, there <i>is</i> a Divine Rank... it's called your Legend Score. It does the job of power level admirably, and you thankfully no longer need Legend 12 to be a viable Divine Parent and most Gods are explicitly noted as being less than 11 even. It's specified in the last paragraph pf Page 212 of the text-only Hero pdf.<br /> <br /> EDIT : Ninja'ed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 07-29-2018, 01:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T09:39:38-07:00","id":1240100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1239897#post1239897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, they <i>are</i> still using Legend Rank in 2e - I wasn't clear on that. Makes sense, then. I'd probably still add extra Callings as I felt were necessary, but at least there is a rank so that one deity can be represented as stronger [so to speak] than another.</div> </div> </div> </div>... Why wouldn't they? I mean even in the previews leading up to the Kickstarter, Neall mentioned things like &quot;Every third dot of Legend, you pick up an Omen&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T18:44:26-07:00","id":1240272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1239897#post1239897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, they <i>are</i> still using Legend Rank in 2e - I wasn't clear on that. Makes sense, then. I'd probably still add extra Callings as I felt were necessary, but at least there is a rank so that one deity can be represented as stronger [so to speak] than another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Creator/Ruling deities get a higher Legend, and among the Olympians, perhaps only Zeus, Poseidon, and Hades are Legend 12.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T18:46:38-07:00","id":1240273,"title":"","content":"Works for me. I obviously missed references to legend during the development process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T18:58:09-07:00","id":1240278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1240273#post1240273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Works for me. I obviously missed references to legend during the development process.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries! A lot changed as I plotted out how the rest of the line works. At the God tier, you have to take on a &quot;Role&quot; within your pantheon in order to have higher amounts of Legend, which means playing divine politics and maybe leading a revolt or two.<br /> <br /> Of course, you could just make your own pantheon...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T19:10:33-07:00","id":1240281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1240278#post1240278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No worries! A lot changed as I plotted out how the rest of the line works. At the God tier, you have to take on a &quot;Role&quot; within your pantheon in order to have higher amounts of Legend, which means playing divine politics and maybe leading a revolt or two.<br /> <br /> Of course, you could just make your own pantheon...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh can you tell us more about that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T16:15:31-07:00","id":1241061,"title":"","content":"Ah on the topic of legend. Do Titans also follow the same legend scale as gods? 9 to 12?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T23:10:51-07:00","id":1252681,"title":"","content":"The Hindu Pantheon seem very different in Scion. They come off as the most Anti-Titan despite numerous myths of allying or joining with demons of various stripes. It seems odd they are on the forefront as compared to the Greeks. It also felt weird that the &quot;love story&quot; of Freyr and Gerd as well as Hades and Persephone (and perhaps the discretion of the entire Greek Pantheon) got sanitized as romantic where the originals were tales of capture and threats, but The love Story of Sita and Rama got called out. It feels like the setting made them a bit of the &quot;bad guys&quot; and I was wondering how that came about and if there was a setting reason they changed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24585-princekittycat","name":"PrinceKittyCat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T05:18:23-07:00","id":1252727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceKittyCat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1252681#post1252681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hindu Pantheon seem very different in Scion. They come off as the most Anti-Titan despite numerous myths of allying or joining with demons of various stripes. It seems odd they are on the forefront as compared to the Greeks. It also felt weird that the &quot;love story&quot; of Freyr and Gerd as well as Hades and Persephone (and perhaps the discretion of the entire Greek Pantheon) got sanitized as romantic where the originals were tales of capture and threats, but The love Story of Sita and Rama got called out. It feels like the setting made them a bit of the &quot;bad guys&quot; and I was wondering how that came about and if there was a setting reason they changed?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hindu Pantheon is anti-Titan because their mythology is practically defined by their wars with the Asura and their variants... the Veda are very clear on the glory of the Gods in their battle against the thieves of Water, Light and Cattle, all Big Deals, and the latter Purana literature practically starts every chapter with 'And then, the Asura attacked...'<br /> <br /> There are, of course, multiple instances of Deva favouring Asura, but those stories kind of get grossly outnumbered by the ones where they fight them or trick them out of power... they're not even mutually exclusive, frankly, as is the case with Bali, who was tricked out of his empire by Vishnu but who is also a devoted servant of Vishnu, to the point that Vishnu gave him an entire slice of Reality to rule, in the form of Sutala, one of the Patala levels (I'd like to note here that the Patala levels are consistently portrayed as amazing places to live, with Bali's Sutala explicitly noted as being better than Indra's Heaven, so it's not like he got a raw deal)... but the fact remains that the Deva do not hesitate to stomp out any Titan activity that threatens their worshipers. It's a very strong theme throughout their literature.<br /> <br /> I'll also note that the Deva individual write-ups make it very clear that that is not a universal feeling... Ganesha explicitly is totally open to Asura alliance, and only Durga and Indra get called out as ruthlessly dedicated to Titan eradication... and of these Durga is again explicitly noted as being only dedicated and driven by defense... she doesn't start battles, she just finishes them, very, very thoroughly. Indra is the big hawk, and that completely suits his character as someone who explicitly goes out of his way to harass innocent Asura as well (never mind that he's married to a Titan, but I figure he doesn't like total about it).<br /> <br /> As for the Sita-Rama episode, I can't speak for the thoughts of the Greek or Norse writers or their stories, but the love story of Sita and Rama gets called out by Hindus all the time... pointing out how horribly Rama treats his wife after he's defeated Ravana is a very common theme in modern critics of the tale, and even ancient writers clearly didn't like it cuz there's multiple versions of the Ramayana (which has several variations) that just erase that part of the story... this ranges from scholars arguing that the Section of the Valmiki Ramayana where this was described was never an original part, to straight up re-writes like the Ramacharitmanas (the actual most popular Ramayana version, not the Valmiki Ramayana) straight up just stopping the story after the happily ever after, to the really weird stuff like the Adbhuta Ramayana where Sita turns into Kali and murders Ravana herself, and Rama is too scared stiff afterwards to ever entertain thoughts of exiling his wife... basically calling that story out is very much in theme with what actual followers of the religion have been doing for ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T10:07:21-07:00","id":1252790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceKittyCat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1252681#post1252681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hindu Pantheon seem very different in Scion. They come off as the most Anti-Titan despite numerous myths of allying or joining with demons of various stripes. It seems odd they are on the forefront as compared to the Greeks. It also felt weird that the &quot;love story&quot; of Freyr and Gerd as well as Hades and Persephone (and perhaps the discretion of the entire Greek Pantheon) got sanitized as romantic where the originals were tales of capture and threats, but The love Story of Sita and Rama got called out. It feels like the setting made them a bit of the &quot;bad guys&quot; and I was wondering how that came about and if there was a setting reason they changed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Titanomachy is backstory in Greek mythology. Their myths are defined by the petty family squabbles of the Olympians themselves, not continuing conflict with the Titans (unless you count the one myth about Typhon and the Gigantomachy, which while not literally about Titans in the original sense, probably fall under that umbrella for Scion purposes - but still are an outlier compared to \u201cZeus was horny one day and -\u201c myths).<br /> <br /> Battling Asura is CENTRAL in the Vedas as Samudra lays out above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-09-2018, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T13:12:40-07:00","id":1252834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceKittyCat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1252681#post1252681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hindu Pantheon seem very different in Scion. They come off as the most Anti-Titan despite numerous myths of allying or joining with demons of various stripes. It seems odd they are on the forefront as compared to the Greeks. It also felt weird that the &quot;love story&quot; of Freyr and Gerd as well as Hades and Persephone (and perhaps the discretion of the entire Greek Pantheon) got sanitized as romantic where the originals were tales of capture and threats, but The love Story of Sita and Rama got called out. It feels like the setting made them a bit of the &quot;bad guys&quot; and I was wondering how that came about and if there was a setting reason they changed?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the version of the Eddas I read Freyr and Gerd was more &quot;seeing her from affar and arranged marrige&quot;. And I've seen many interpretations of Hades and Persephone were Persephone was either reciprocating Hades affections, or trying to piss Demeter off and Demeter reacted with &quot;She'd never marry that jerk, he must have kidnapped her!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T13:30:12-07:00","id":1252839,"title":"","content":"I greatly prefer the version where Persephone reciprocates Hades's affections and Demeter freaks out. It's a lot more interesting than instance #3,678 of &quot;a Theoi commits a terrible sexual crime.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T14:42:47-07:00","id":1252852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1252839#post1252839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I greatly prefer the version where Persephone reciprocates Hades's affections and Demeter freaks out. It's a lot more interesting than instance #3,678 of &quot;a Theoi commits a terrible sexual crime.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. And it sets Hades apart as one of the very small number of truly decent Theoi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T18:24:29-07:00","id":1252891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1252839#post1252839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I greatly prefer the version where Persephone reciprocates Hades's affections and Demeter freaks out. It's a lot more interesting than instance #3,678 of &quot;a Theoi commits a terrible sexual crime.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So do I that's my problem.<br /> <br /> But that's not the original one and it has become very popular to romanticize it recently, but it just felt very odd. That Gerda who gets horribly threatened in all versions of the myth, and the entire Greek Pantheon get an oversight...which I prefer, no one wants to play a game with authentic Greek Gods, at least not that aspect.<br /> <br /> But Rama and Sita is supposed to be Romantic, religiously, culturally. But they get called out. If you call them out, then why does Gerda and Persephone get a rewrite?<br /> Yes, the Hindu pantheon constantly war against the demons but they also are passionately against war without proper action. Rama gives Ravana many opportunities to get out of the fight. They are all about war as a last method and giving ample opportunities to their opponents to end it peacefully.<br /> <br /> That's a big deal, pursuing every way possible to peace but being called to war as a duty when that fails. Having one god be the &quot;good god&quot; in all this makes it worse as to highlight they are bad and don't see reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24585-princekittycat","name":"PrinceKittyCat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T19:45:30-07:00","id":1252914,"title":"","content":"Part of it is the direction of the narrative. Rama treats Sita terribly AFTER the part of the story that\u2019s romanticized (rescuing her from Ravana). Persephone and Hades are traditionally seen as mutually devoted (relatively speaking) when reigning as husband and wife after the whole kidnapping thing. In both cases it\u2019s the lasting nature of the relationship that is preserved.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll leave the Deva views of war to Samudra, as they are far more knowledgeable on the subject than I am, but if I were to guess, you\u2019re probably looking at Vedic vs Puranic issue. Remember the hostile war chief always itching to blow up Asura is Indra, not Durga, Karttekya, or any of the Puranic deities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-09-2018, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T21:31:54-07:00","id":1252938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceKittyCat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1252891#post1252891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So do I that's my problem.<br /> <br /> But that's not the original one and it has become very popular to romanticize it recently, but it just felt very odd. That Gerda who gets horribly threatened in all versions of the myth, and the entire Greek Pantheon get an oversight...which I prefer, no one wants to play a game with authentic Greek Gods, at least not that aspect.<br /> <br /> But Rama and Sita is supposed to be Romantic, religiously, culturally. But they get called out. If you call them out, then why does Gerda and Persephone get a rewrite?</div> </div> </div> </div>Please explain to me the romance of a woman getting essentially slut-shamed for having been abducted by her husband, then getting exiled to the forest while pregnant by the same husband, even though the literal God og Purifying Fire Agni had already given her chastity a clean bill of health (not, again, that that should fucking matter) all because a random subject of his had doubted that she was 'pure', and then said woman preferring to literally sink into the ground rather than go back to the man just because he wants kids now.<br /> <br /> You can complain about the Persephone thing all you want, I won't stop you... but the fact remains that to the Greeks kidnapping a girl with her father's permission wouldn't have been that big a deal... the text itself makes it very clear that Rama's treatment of Sita is <i>not okay</i>, either by showing her explicitly refusing to forgive him and leaving the World permanently, or by just excising those bits altogether in embarrassment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceKittyCat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1252891#post1252891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the Hindu pantheon constantly war against the demons but they also are passionately against war without proper action. Rama gives Ravana many opportunities to get out of the fight. They are all about war as a last method and giving ample opportunities to their opponents to end it peacefully.<br /> <br /> That's a big deal, pursuing every way possible to peace but being called to war as a duty when that fails.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually no, what is warned against is not <i>improper</i> action but <i>in</i>action... the Mahabharata is absolutely full to the gills with improper and dishonorouable combat, most of it explicitly sanctioned by God (Krishna) himself, to the point that the Pandavas all end up in Naraka afterwards. Krishna goes so far as to tell Arjuna that he doesn't have to feel bad about the killing he's about to do since he's personally marked them all for killing anyway, so it was bound to happen one way or another.<br /> <br /> And again, compare this to Indra who, far from giving people chances, goes around killing peaceful ascetics and splitting apart foetuses in the womb on the off-chance that they might eventually try to overthrow him, or the hymn to Vishnu that exalts his terrifying roar which 'causes thousands of Asura women to miscarry' (It's the Narayana Kavacha, in case you're interested).<br /> <br /> It is true that Gods like Shiva and Durga give their opponents ample opportunities to retreat, but this is noted in their write-ups.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceKittyCat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1252891#post1252891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having one god be the &quot;good god&quot; in all this makes it worse as to highlight they are bad and don't see reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact, I'd contest this statement and note that it's quite the opposite... there is one 'bad' God, Indra, and he's the hostile war chief running around actively murdering innocent Asura.. none of the others do this, but again none of them are pacifists... Ganesha has more than his share of Asura blood on his hands.<br /> <br /> The Deva are defined by their battles with Asura... sometimes literally, such as Vedic Indra whose victory over Vritra is the subject of 500 odd hymns, or Durga whose most popular epithet is Mahishasuramardini (slayer of Mahishasura)... even Shiva and Vishnu are popularly called 'Slayer of the Tripura' and 'Slayer of Madhu'. Kartikkeya literally only exists because the Asura Taraka needed to be killed, Krishna has a body count higher than some professional assassins by the time he hits puberty, gentle Lakshmi kills Kolhasura and has a whole temple town dedicated to it, Parvati kills Bhandasura with her sugarcane bow, Vedic Sarasvati rides into battle against Asura on her chariot, smashing her opposition to bits... and the only reason Agni Surya or Varuna aren't on this list is because they're usually the ones getting their asses kicked... the fact that the Deva let all those Asura rampage around till things got bad enough to require intervention doesn't change the fact that their tales are pretty much defined by 'this bad guy was killed by X Deity'.<br /> <br /> The Greeks don't come close, not even remotely... they have events, wars with Titanic opposition, but it's not an everyday thing for them... It is, in fact, perfectly fitting that the Teotl and Deva see them as hobby Titanomachy participants... they kind of are, compared to those two, and it also makes the close and abiding alliance between Deva and Teotl very understandable (absolutely <i>bizarre</i> statements in the Teotl Relationships section notwithstanding).<br /> <br /> I'll just note that far from being an attempt to paint them as 'bad guys', the Deva write-up, along with the Shen and Orisha, is one of the best researched and written of all the ones in the corebook... and the Hinduisms section is arguably one of the best and most concise descriptions of the religion that I have ever seen, and I'm including ones by other Hindus in that... everything from the background to the Pantheon relationships to the style of writing the Gods is evocative of actual Hindu Myth, things Deva Scions will be dealing with everyday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T21:42:02-07:00","id":1252944,"title":"","content":"I still bet it\u2019s likely we\u2019ll see the Annuna join the Deva and Teotl as hardcore Titanomachy crusaders. The fact that they\u2019ve also got a complicated history with the Yazata probably further ingraciating Indra and Marduk as bros.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T22:00:47-07:00","id":1252948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1252938#post1252938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can complain about the Persephone thing all you want, I won't stop you... but the fact remains that to the Greeks kidnapping a girl with her father's permission wouldn't have been that big a deal... the text itself makes it very clear that Rama's treatment of Sita is <i>not okay</i>, either by showing her explicitly refusing to forgive him and leaving the World permanently, or by just excising those bits altogether in embarrassment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this gets at the heart of it. \u201cCleaning up\u201d that story would be taking liberties with a continuously living tradition. Greek and Norse myth are comparatively much fairer game for writers to play around with. While there are modern devotees, those believers are reconstructing their tradition out of stories that were already part of the collective Western canon being drawn on. This doesn\u2019t make their religions less valid, but it does mean they have less cultural ownership of said stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T04:48:25-07:00","id":1253018,"title":"","content":"Something to also keep in mind about the story of Hades and Persephone is that we don't have the 'original' tale. What we do have is multiple retelling of the story, some of which we can date and some that we can't.<br /> The truth as it pertains to Scion is that its likely that none of the stories are accurates. &quot;All myths are true&quot; but &quot;None of them are accurate&quot; is a good thing to keep in mind with Scion.<br /> <br /> To me this brings an interesting element for the storyguide. When your players accomplish an important Deed that becomes part of their Legend, it is interesting to create multiple &quot;versions&quot; of what happened being told be people and to have none of those versions be what actually happen.<br /> (Not sure it pertains much to the conversation but i thought it is something interesting to keep in mind.)<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;good gods/bad gods&quot; thing. In particular about mythologies of ancient times that these gods operated on social structures that would be almost entirely at odds with our present concepts of morality. The Tuatha De Danann are a good example of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T17:23:31-07:00","id":1253170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1252938#post1252938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please explain to me the romance of a woman getting essentially slut-shamed for having been abducted by her husband, then getting exiled to the forest while pregnant by the same husband, even though the literal God og Purifying Fire Agni had already given her chastity a clean bill of health (not, again, that that should fucking matter) all because a random subject of his had doubted that she was 'pure', and then said woman preferring to literally sink into the ground rather than go back to the man just because he wants kids now.<br /> <br /> You can complain about the Persephone thing all you want, I won't stop you... but the fact remains that to the Greeks kidnapping a girl with her father's permission wouldn't have been that big a deal... the text itself makes it very clear that Rama's treatment of Sita is <i>not okay</i>, either by showing her explicitly refusing to forgive him and leaving the World permanently, or by just excising those bits altogether in embarrassment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Actually no, what is warned against is not <i>improper</i> action but <i>in</i>action... the Mahabharata is absolutely full to the gills with improper and dishonorouable combat, most of it explicitly sanctioned by God (Krishna) himself, to the point that the Pandavas all end up in Naraka afterwards. Krishna goes so far as to tell Arjuna that he doesn't have to feel bad about the killing he's about to do since he's personally marked them all for killing anyway, so it was bound to happen one way or another.<br /> <br /> And again, compare this to Indra who, far from giving people chances, goes around killing peaceful ascetics and splitting apart foetuses in the womb on the off-chance that they might eventually try to overthrow him, or the hymn to Vishnu that exalts his terrifying roar which 'causes thousands of Asura women to miscarry' (It's the Narayana Kavacha, in case you're interested).<br /> <br /> It is true that Gods like Shiva and Durga give their opponents ample opportunities to retreat, but this is noted in their write-ups.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In fact, I'd contest this statement and note that it's quite the opposite... there is one 'bad' God, Indra, and he's the hostile war chief running around actively murdering innocent Asura.. none of the others do this, but again none of them are pacifists... Ganesha has more than his share of Asura blood on his hands.<br /> <br /> The Deva are defined by their battles with Asura... sometimes literally, such as Vedic Indra whose victory over Vritra is the subject of 500 odd hymns, or Durga whose most popular epithet is Mahishasuramardini (slayer of Mahishasura)... even Shiva and Vishnu are popularly called 'Slayer of the Tripura' and 'Slayer of Madhu'. Kartikkeya literally only exists because the Asura Taraka needed to be killed, Krishna has a body count higher than some professional assassins by the time he hits puberty, gentle Lakshmi kills Kolhasura and has a whole temple town dedicated to it, Parvati kills Bhandasura with her sugarcane bow, Vedic Sarasvati rides into battle against Asura on her chariot, smashing her opposition to bits... and the only reason Agni Surya or Varuna aren't on this list is because they're usually the ones getting their asses kicked... the fact that the Deva let all those Asura rampage around till things got bad enough to require intervention doesn't change the fact that their tales are pretty much defined by 'this bad guy was killed by X Deity'.<br /> <br /> The Greeks don't come close, not even remotely... they have events, wars with Titanic opposition, but it's not an everyday thing for them... It is, in fact, perfectly fitting that the Teotl and Deva see them as hobby Titanomachy participants... they kind of are, compared to those two, and it also makes the close and abiding alliance between Deva and Teotl very understandable (absolutely <i>bizarre</i> statements in the Teotl Relationships section notwithstanding).<br /> <br /> I'll just note that far from being an attempt to paint them as 'bad guys', the Deva write-up, along with the Shen and Orisha, is one of the best researched and written of all the ones in the corebook... and the Hinduisms section is arguably one of the best and most concise descriptions of the religion that I have ever seen, and I'm including ones by other Hindus in that... everything from the background to the Pantheon relationships to the style of writing the Gods is evocative of actual Hindu Myth, things Deva Scions will be dealing with everyday.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for your reply, I am not trying to be hostile and you are obviously more knowledgeable about it than myself, and I admit being a bit sore and worried about it to perhaps an unreasonable level. I am not Hindu but my stepfather and sister always have been very devout. We played the first edition scion together and we enjoyed it a great deal, until the companion came out and they were deeply hurt by the portrayal of the gods, to the point the campaign revolved around it and the game in general was soured.<br /> <br /> I was hoping this version would be less so, and while you are probably correct that the wider cultural analysis is more critical of the story of Sita and Rama, I always was told since I was little it was the ultimate love story. It is at least a story very dear to both of them, and I know that phrase will bother them, and to a lesser extent it bothered me. Add on my understanding of the Mahabharata and the Ramayana as lessons of always pursuing multiple avenues of peace before war or battle could be fought (except when made from hasty promises, which usually led to the lesson, of don't commit yourself lightly), it felt wrong and I was a bit ashamed I encouraged excitement about the new version if it was just going to disappoint as well.<br /> <br /> I also admit the Persephone thing is long held, and that is a larger issue of me being frustrated her myth gets often romanticized often by the same people who tend to disparage the Rama/Sita story. It's felt hypocritical, but that's aimed mostly at those who like me, were at the peripherary of the Religion and not part of it, which felt Culturally Unaware. This happily, is not the case.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, our family will probably house rule it, or make our own write ups of them if anyone wants to join in, so it is not a big issue. I fully understand a Culture is not a few groups of people, but I'd feel amiss if I didn't say anything. I do feel better knowing it sits well with other Hindus, and understand nothing can fully satisfy everybody. Thanks!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24585-princekittycat","name":"PrinceKittyCat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T19:18:42-07:00","id":1253189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceKittyCat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1253170#post1253170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Admittedly, our family will probably house rule it, or make our own write ups of them if anyone wants to join in, so it is not a big issue. I fully understand a Culture is not a few groups of people, but I'd feel amiss if I didn't say anything. I do feel better knowing it sits well with other Hindus, and understand nothing can fully satisfy everybody. Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for being very conscientious and accepting about this. Even among divine entities, feelings can shift and alter over thousands of years; and among a billion adherents of the Hinduisms, there's bound to be differences of opinion and narrative. But whatever works for your family and players, please feel free to houserule it, and I hope the new edition's version of the pantheon is more exciting to you and yours. If you or your family want to discuss this or the pantheon in more detail, please feel free to PM me here at this forum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T21:22:06-07:00","id":1253209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceKittyCat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1253170#post1253170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you for your reply, I am not trying to be hostile and you are obviously more knowledgeable about it than myself, and I admit being a bit sore and worried about it to perhaps an unreasonable level. I am not Hindu but my stepfather and sister always have been very devout. We played the first edition scion together and we enjoyed it a great deal, until the companion came out and they were deeply hurt by the portrayal of the gods, to the point the campaign revolved around it and the game in general was soured.<br /> <br /> I was hoping this version would be less so, and while you are probably correct that the wider cultural analysis is more critical of the story of Sita and Rama, I always was told since I was little it was the ultimate love story. It is at least a story very dear to both of them, and I know that phrase will bother them, and to a lesser extent it bothered me. Add on my understanding of the Mahabharata and the Ramayana as lessons of always pursuing multiple avenues of peace before war or battle could be fought (except when made from hasty promises, which usually led to the lesson, of don't commit yourself lightly), it felt wrong and I was a bit ashamed I encouraged excitement about the new version if it was just going to disappoint as well.<br /> <br /> I also admit the Persephone thing is long held, and that is a larger issue of me being frustrated her myth gets often romanticized often by the same people who tend to disparage the Rama/Sita story. It's felt hypocritical, but that's aimed mostly at those who like me, were at the peripherary of the Religion and not part of it, which felt Culturally Unaware. This happily, is not the case.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, our family will probably house rule it, or make our own write ups of them if anyone wants to join in, so it is not a big issue. I fully understand a Culture is not a few groups of people, but I'd feel amiss if I didn't say anything. I do feel better knowing it sits well with other Hindus, and understand nothing can fully satisfy everybody. Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>I also apologize if I got a bit too heated in the Deva's defense <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Trust me, after the 1e Devas Chapter in Companion, I was pretty badly turned off as well. I was pretty ecstatic when the quality of work done on the 2e Deva became apparent, and I hope that other than those two points, you enjoyed the rest of it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T21:07:15-07:00","id":1253797,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that there\u2019s an important reason for the revision of the Persephone myth that doesn\u2019t apply in Sita\u2019s case: giving Persephone agency. Sita has agency in her narrative - it\u2019s tragic, and arises from her mistreatment, but she still raises children on her own, and chooses to reject the world in her sorrow - operative word being chooses. Persephone in the traditional telling has no agency, so revising that tale to have her want to be with Hades is less about making one of the male Theoi look less bad, as it is about giving the godess of the Underworld some control of her own fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T22:01:46-07:00","id":1254095,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s no Riastadt power I\u2019m missing in the Hero text is there? Would that work by just stacking certain Epic Attribute Boons with Visage Great and Terrible, or is Demigod level Geas going to open up something more specific?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-17T20:53:37-07:00","id":1255168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1254095#post1254095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s no Riastadt power I\u2019m missing in the Hero text is there? Would that work by just stacking certain Epic Attribute Boons with Visage Great and Terrible, or is Demigod level Geas going to open up something more specific?</div> </div> </div> </div>I heard rumors about the Riastadt being a potential Cultural Knack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-17T21:17:15-07:00","id":1255169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1255168#post1255168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I heard rumors about the Riastadt being a potential Cultural Knack.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Are Cultural Knacks a thing we know to be coming in a particular book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-18T23:29:26-07:00","id":1255434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1255169#post1255169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Are Cultural Knacks a thing we know to be coming in a particular book?</div> </div> </div> </div>Neall mentioned in the Scion Discord once that the team would like to put more Knacks of both Mortal and Immortal levels, as well as Culture Specific Knacks, in Demigod.<br /> <br /> As with everything Neall says about future content I wouldn't assume this is guaranteed","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 09-19-2018, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T09:59:13-07:00","id":1256498,"title":"","content":"Ok, I'm trying to get my head around how different kinds of Scale stack.<br /> <br /> Here's what I'm pretty sure I know:<br /> <br /> 1) Scale represents a significant difference in some measure of potency; such as speed, size, numbers or divine 'weight'.<br /> 2) For Dramatic comparisons, Scale adds Enhancement based on the difference to relevant rolls.<br /> 3) Characters of a two scale disadvantage (or greater) are largely treated as trivial unless the game demands otherwise.<br /> 4) Characters cannot deal damage to targets more than two Scale above them.<br /> <br /> All makes sense to me thus far. What I'm less clear about is something like this scenario:<br /> <br /> A Band in a getaway car (Size 1, Speed 3) is hitting the tarmac after nabbing a phoenix egg from a cultist/crime boss, and her oni muscle (Size 3, Title 2 from a stolen Relic) drops into the middle of the road to block them, putting herself in the path for a violent collision.<br /> <br /> Leaving aside the expectation that plot-relevant comparisons shouldn't treated as trivial, what happens?<br /> <br /> 1a) The oni is in no way fast enough to contest the car, is treated as Trivial and easily sped past before she's able to put herself properly in the way.<br /> 1b) The car can't do anything against something that big/heavy, is treated as Trivial, smashes into the oni &amp; stops.<br /> 2) The oni has an overall +1 Scale advantage over the car, getting a +2 Enhancement bonus against them, but because the car is two scale faster, she can't do more than clip them, doing no damage to the car and limiting to non-damaging stunts (and vice versa).<br /> 3) The oni has an overall +1 Scale advantage over the car, getting a +2 Enhancement bonus against them, and the contest is rolled normally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":955,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","user":"Yue Ryong","date":". 09-22-2018, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T16:13:00-07:00","id":1256819,"title":"","content":"Scion: Origins and Scion: Hero are out. Can we maybe shift questions about them to their own threads, to make it easier to find things, and reserve Ask Neall for questions about upcoming books?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T18:50:32-07:00","id":1257061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1256819#post1256819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scion: Origins and Scion: Hero are out. Can we maybe shift questions about them to their own threads, to make it easier to find things, and reserve Ask Neall for questions about upcoming books?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they? I can't find anything on Kickstarter or Backerit about them being out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23810-redrobin","name":"RedRobin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-25T10:07:35-07:00","id":1257218,"title":"","content":"I have the first pass of the fully edited Origin, did I miss the mail on Hero?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-01T09:49:54-07:00","id":1258406,"title":"","content":"Do Titan's have Mantles? If they do, did Zeus took a mantle when he usurped Cronos and became King of the Gods and did Cronos did the same with Ouranos. If that isn't how it works its there another type of mechanic which that type of power-swapping falls under?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-01T15:47:17-07:00","id":1258438,"title":"","content":"I know I've asked this before earlier, but conversations got caught up in other trains of though, and I never got an answer (which is okay.) When you use a knack that allows you to invest legends instead of spend it on a feat of scale, how long does the legend stay imbued before the player can reclaim it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1576-mjorkk","name":"mjorkk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-02T09:22:42-07:00","id":1258547,"title":"","content":"Hi, I'm glad and liking the Scion: Origin book and rules but I have two questions about Conditions.<br /> 1) How Conditions do exactly work?<br /> 2) Will there be examples of Conditions in the book?<br /> <br /> I'm asking this because Conditions is one of the game rules that is really poorly explained in the book. It is briefly explained in page 66-67 the can apply to Complications or Enhancements, and that's it. It doesn't really explain how many Conditions a character can have, if they only work in that way, and what is really the difference between brief and permanent Conditions, and if Injury Conditions are always applied for Conditions of harmful effects or not.<br /> <br /> It seems to me this kind of rule is handwaiving and not really playtested, and that's unfortunate. I'm looking forward to tips for when to award Conditions, how many are too much, what kind of different effects it could have (examples), how to remove them (examples), and examples of Conditions in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23839-oxcelot","name":"Oxcelot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-02T10:51:28-07:00","id":1258561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oxcelot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1258547#post1258547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, I'm glad and liking the Scion: Origin book and rules but I have two questions about Conditions.<br /> 1) How Conditions do exactly work?<br /> 2) Will there be examples of Conditions in the book?<br /> <br /> I'm asking this because Conditions is one of the game rules that is really poorly explained in the book. It is briefly explained in page 66-67 the can apply to Complications or Enhancements, and that's it. It doesn't really explain how many Conditions a character can have, if they only work in that way, and what is really the difference between brief and permanent Conditions, and if Injury Conditions are always applied for Conditions of harmful effects or not.<br /> <br /> It seems to me this kind of rule is handwaiving and not really playtested, and that's unfortunate. I'm looking forward to tips for when to award Conditions, how many are too much, what kind of different effects it could have (examples), how to remove them (examples), and examples of Conditions in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not Neall but part of the thing with Conditions is that they're intentionally going to be a varied lot. There's examples of them in Hero as well.<br /> <br /> Some answers: What are Conditions like? Deliberately varied. Drunk could be a Condition. Blind could be a Condition. Fox Tail that you can't hide is a Condition.<br /> <br /> How many do you assign? As many as makes sense. If you're overloading your players, stop, but don't feel like there's a hard limit of Legend x2 Conditions a Player can suffer from.<br /> <br /> How do they resolve? It depends. &quot;Sand in the eyes&quot; may require an action to wash or rub your eyes. &quot;Eyes burned out&quot; will probably require divine magic. &quot;Drunk as a Skunk&quot; will require sleeping it off, probably &quot;Lasts until end of scene&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-05T03:55:37-07:00","id":1259042,"title":"","content":"Another question: when it says that the defense of followers is half of their rating, it never specifies whether it's round-up or round-down, and I also can't find anywhere in Origins or Hero where it gives a default assumption for the game about rounding either. Does the what't the defense of followers of 1, 3, and 5 dots respectively?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1576-mjorkk","name":"mjorkk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-05T09:59:16-07:00","id":1259093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mjorkk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1259042#post1259042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question: when it says that the defense of followers is half of their rating, it never specifies whether it's round-up or round-down, and I also can't find anywhere in Origins or Hero where it gives a default assumption for the game about rounding either. Does the what't the defense of followers of 1, 3, and 5 dots respectively?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't recall where but I thought it mentioned somewhere to round in favor of the players unless otherwise stated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-05T11:57:41-07:00","id":1259107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div c