in the art for Scion Hero as well but her stats aren't in that book either. Is this an oversight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T09:41:12-07:00","id":1263813,"title":"","content":"I'm plagiarizing myself from another thread with this question, but the more I re-read the Kami chapter the more it seems to stick out at me. To wit: why aren't Izanagi and Izanami mentioned in the cosmology subsection? I can only imagine the omission of what would probably be a whole paragraph must be a deliberate creative choice, and granted, I suppose not every primordial needs be mentioned, but they were parental options in 1e, so...I guess I'm just not sure what the criteria are for Primordials being brought up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12598-karasu-sama","name":"Karasu-sama","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T11:28:47-07:00","id":1264084,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Oops, wrong thread, meant to put this in Errata","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 11-01-2018, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T15:25:15-07:00","id":1264504,"title":"","content":"I have a question. Is it possible to customize a Purview? I'm thinking about more modern-focused gods who claim domains like Energy or Entropy. Do they just grab themes from different Purviews, or is it possible to condense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T15:50:18-07:00","id":1264507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1264504#post1264504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question. Is it possible to customize a Purview? I'm thinking about more modern-focused gods who claim domains like Energy or Entropy. Do they just grab themes from different Purviews, or is it possible to condense?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Companion is going to address custom Purviews.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T18:26:52-08:00","id":1272740,"title":"","content":"Neall. One more question about the Keepers of the World, will you they remain after they seal the gods? I mean,do they will go away too or will they stay to control the World?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 12-03-2018, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-30T02:44:54-08:00","id":1277476,"title":"","content":"I was talking about it on another thread, but I think Neal would be the best to answer it. I apologize if it has been already asked.<br /> <br /> Can multiple mantles of a god have different purviews? Or different Callings?<br /> <br /> I am asking because I just saw that in the Roman mythology she is a triple goddess with Diana/Artemis and Selene/Luna, but more in a partial aspect of Diana (Diana of the Underworld). I believe Hecate most probably would have the calling Liminal and the Death Purview, but Diana has none.<br /> <br /> Thanks for your attention and time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T19:28:02-08:00","id":1281031,"title":"","content":"I tried to click on the Q&amp;A but it didn't open for me so I got me a question. <br /> <br /> <b>Characters begin play with five Knacks from their Callings, one for each Calling dot a character begins with.</b><br /> One Knack may be swapped out for another during a minor milestone.<br /> Additional Knacks may be purchased with Experience, but a character may only have five Knacks \u201cactive\u201d at a time, corresponding to their Calling dots, until<br /> they gain more by rising in Legend.<b> Immortal Knacks are worth two Calling dots to keep active</b>; thus, a Scion with a Warrior Calling of 4 can have two Immortal Knacks, four Heroic Knacks, or two Heroic and one Immortal Knack active at a time.<br /> <br /> Bolded text is the most relevant to the question. <br /> <br /> For clarification does this mean that when I make my character and I've got 5 dots to spend on Knacks, does this mean I can get 5 knacks, regardless of weather they are Heroic or Immortal Knacks. Or is it set up that an Immortal Knack costs 2 of the starting Knack Dots whereas a Heroic Knack only costs 1 dot?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T03:02:56-08:00","id":1281069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1281031#post1281031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tried to click on the Q&amp;A but it didn't open for me so I got me a question.<br /> <br /> <b>Characters begin play with five Knacks from their Callings, one for each Calling dot a character begins with.</b><br /> One Knack may be swapped out for another during a minor milestone.<br /> Additional Knacks may be purchased with Experience, but a character may only have five Knacks \u201cactive\u201d at a time, corresponding to their Calling dots, until<br /> they gain more by rising in Legend.<b> Immortal Knacks are worth two Calling dots to keep active</b>; thus, a Scion with a Warrior Calling of 4 can have two Immortal Knacks, four Heroic Knacks, or two Heroic and one Immortal Knack active at a time.<br /> <br /> Bolded text is the most relevant to the question.<br /> <br /> For clarification does this mean that when I make my character and I've got 5 dots to spend on Knacks, does this mean I can get 5 knacks, regardless of weather they are Heroic or Immortal Knacks. Or is it set up that an Immortal Knack costs 2 of the starting Knack Dots whereas a Heroic Knack only costs 1 dot?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><i>As written</i> that is how it goes, even though Heroic and Immortal Knacks cost the same post chargen, so it's totally understandable to house rule that to five Knacks regardless of type (I do).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T03:51:24-08:00","id":1281074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1281069#post1281069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>As written</i> that is how it goes, even though Heroic and Immortal Knacks cost the same post chargen, so it's totally understandable to house rule that to five Knacks regardless of type (I do).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;As Written&quot; is the part that is confusing me. It's the whole reason for the post. So what your saying that it's like my second assumption that when purchasing them <br /> Heroic Knacks = 1 Dot to Purchase<br /> Immortal Knacks = 2 Dots to Purchase","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T05:58:02-08:00","id":1281079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ScionHero</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> For each Calling, choose a number of Heroic Knacks equal to the Calling\u2019s rating; while they can learn more, they may only have as many active as they have Calling dots. <b>Alternately, you may choose a single Immortal Knack instead of two Heroic Knacks for your character\u2019s two-dot Calling</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine. I read this to be your second assumption.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18560-saedar","name":"saedar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T09:22:33-08:00","id":1281116,"title":"","content":"Yes, that is what I was basing it off as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T10:58:18-08:00","id":1281132,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the logic at character creation seems to be \u201cyou start with enough Knacks for your Calling dots and no extras to switch out\u201d which would be fine except that Immortal Knacks cost the same experience as Heroic Knacks, so it seems more strategically sound to take all Heroic Knacks at character creation and buy Immortal Knacks in game to maximize your return.<br /> <br /> Samudra\u2019s recommendation that you start with 5 Knacks of any type, so if you take some Immortal Knacks it means some unused Heroic Knacks have to wait in reserve when you apply them, seems the most sound mechanical solution to avoid optimization at the expense of concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T13:57:17-08:00","id":1281175,"title":"","content":"Yeah my original assumption was that heroics cost one and Immortal cost 2, but then another player pointed out where it said you get 5 knacks from their calling combined with the fact that they cost the same when you're spending experience points is what kind of got me wondering","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T14:01:27-08:00","id":1281178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1281175#post1281175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah my original assumption was that heroics cost one and Immortal cost 2, but then another player pointed out where it said you get 5 knacks from their calling combined with the fact that they cost the same when you're spending experience points is what kind of got me wondering</div> </div> </div> </div>Might be clarified later, I can see the logic of both assumptions. I personally ran it so that my players got five Knacks total, which could be Heroic or Immortal, with the understanding that it's not wise to take an Immortal Knack in a Calling they only have one Dot in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T14:59:31-08:00","id":1281193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1281178#post1281178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might be clarified later, I can see the logic of both assumptions. I personally ran it so that my players got five Knacks total, which could be Heroic or Immortal, with the understanding that it's not wise to take an Immortal Knack in a Calling they only have one Dot in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, does it say you can only use &quot;slots&quot; of a calling for knacks of that calling?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T16:43:45-08:00","id":1281210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1281193#post1281193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, does it say you can only use &amp;quot;slots&amp;quot; of a calling for knacks of that calling?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it does. I'm on Mobile but I'm certain you can't slot a Trickster Knack in a Warrior Slot","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T16:54:40-08:00","id":1281212,"title":"","content":"With the exception of the 4 &quot;Any&quot; knacks that can be slotted anywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T07:30:45-08:00","id":1281506,"title":"","content":"Dear Neall,<br /> I noticed a lot of malice in the thread concerning the Cthulhu Mythos and I highly suggest that the development team consult the works of S.T Joshi on the subject. It also wouldn't be bad if you talked to Andrew Leman of The H.P Lovecraft Historical Society either. Both of these people can give up a more scholarly angle on the works and also a different view of the author himself. S.T Joshi's works for example include the most accurate biography of Lovecraft to date, the unaltered original manuscript versions of his writings, and all his personal correspondence. As a scholar in the Anthropology and Religions field whose who has studied his stories and the man from numerous angles, this is the way to go. Most people acquire information about the man from older sources which are notoriously unreliable and are responsible for the popular culture image of him. If you can't talk to them at least try to read what these men have published.<br /> Sincerely, Manannansun","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T17:15:48-08:00","id":1281845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1281193#post1281193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, does it say you can only use &quot;slots&quot; of a calling for knacks of that calling?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manannansun</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I noticed a lot of malice in the thread concerning the Cthulhu Mythos and I highly suggest that the development team consult the works of S.T Joshi on the subject. It also wouldn't be bad if you talked to Andrew Leman of The H.P Lovecraft Historical Society either. Both of these people can give up a more scholarly angle on the works and also a different view of the author himself. S.T Joshi's works for example include the most accurate biography of Lovecraft to date, the unaltered original manuscript versions of his writings, and all his personal correspondence. As a scholar in the Anthropology and Religions field whose who has studied his stories and the man from numerous angles, this is the way to go. Most people acquire information about the man from older sources which are notoriously unreliable and are responsible for the popular culture image of him. If you can't talk to them at least try to read what these men have published.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll mention it to the developer, but it's worth noting that Chris Spivey is one of gamings go-tos on the subject of the Mythos. I trust him completely to handle the complexity of these topics in the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T19:07:36-08:00","id":1281859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1281845#post1281845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'll mention it to the developer, but it's worth noting that Chris Spivey is one of gamings go-tos on the subject of the Mythos. I trust him completely to handle the complexity of these topics in the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah Spivey developing moved me from \u201cneutral\u201d to \u201ccautiously optimistic\u201d on the book!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T04:50:05-08:00","id":1282272,"title":"","content":"So, uh, have the physical copies from the Kickstarter rewards still not been sent out yet or have I somehow managed to miss that event?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T05:29:25-08:00","id":1282274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1282272#post1282272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, uh, have the physical copies from the Kickstarter rewards still not been sent out yet or have I somehow managed to miss that event?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not yet...the pdf hasn't gone out to the public yet and they tend to do that around the time PoD becomes a thing...which is a little after the backer base copy (deluxe editions take longer) is printed and/or posted.<br /> <br /> At least that has been my experience and observations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T05:39:15-08:00","id":1282275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1282272#post1282272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, uh, have the physical copies from the Kickstarter rewards still not been sent out yet or have I somehow managed to miss that event?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can check out the Monday Meeting Notes on the main site. It will have the relevant info. Currently, both books are still in the indexing phase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":