{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T12:16:41-08:00","id":1282320,"title":"","content":"Hi Neall, so just wondering and don't know if its been talked about yet.<br /> <br /> I know that there are going to be getting new boons for the new purview's in upcoming books, but are you guys going to add new boons to the old previews, particularly the pantheon previews?<br /> <br /> two per preview just seems light, especially for Demi-gods and Gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24326-jester","name":"Jester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T14:29:57-08:00","id":1282334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jester</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1282320#post1282320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> two per preview just seems light, especially for Demi-gods and Gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not Neall but I just want to note that the Boons in Hero don't stop being useful when you become a Demigod.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T19:15:38-08:00","id":1282370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jester</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1282320#post1282320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi Neall, so just wondering and don't know if its been talked about yet.<br /> <br /> I know that there are going to be getting new boons for the new purview's in upcoming books, but are you guys going to add new boons to the old previews, particularly the pantheon previews?<br /> <br /> two per preview just seems light, especially for Demi-gods and Gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neall\u2019s confirmed there will be more powerful Demigod level Boons for existing Purviews including PSPs. Keep in mind that the Boons we have now are just examples. You can and should design your own Boons within the themes of given Purviews using the mechanical guidelines for designing Marvels.<br /> <br /> For example once you have someone\u2019s True Name, perform a summoning ritual. Or a banishing one where you shatter a Shabti of them to inflict damage. Cast out your own Ba to fly invisibly as a bird wherever you want. All viable Heku Marvels and Boons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T13:48:49-08:00","id":1282504,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Boons, the you start out at two but the legend section of the hero book under one dot of legend says you should have 1? So how many boons do you get? Just one or two? <br /> <br /> Also what was the rational of linking legend directly to the number of boons you have rather than buying them experience? I assume it is so that their is more focus on callings/knacks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T14:14:41-08:00","id":1282510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1282504#post1282504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Boons, the you start out at two but the legend section of the hero book under one dot of legend says you should have 1? So how many boons do you get? Just one or two?<br /> <br /> Also what was the rational of linking legend directly to the number of boons you have rather than buying them experience? I assume it is so that their is more focus on callings/knacks?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Two, your total is equal to Legend +1. That's been confirmed as being corrected in the final text.<br /> <br /> It's in part to facilitate that Gods are not more powerful for being more diversified (as they were in 1E unfortunately). A finite number of Boons means Gods at the same Legend level are going to have the same rough level of might at their disposal, the one with fewer associated Purviews just is more focused with more Boons in the same Purview, while Monkey or Shiva have like 1 Boon in each of their Purviews.<br /> <br /> Also it emphasizes the importance of Marvels. Most miracles someone performs in myth aren't necessarily Boons. They're only likely to be Boons if they're something a figure relies on REPEATEDLY in myth. Any creative one-off miracle in their purview is probably a Marvel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-24-2019, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T14:33:29-08:00","id":1282518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1282510#post1282510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's in part to facilitate that Gods are not more powerful for being more diversified (as they were in 1E unfortunately). A finite number of Boons means Gods at the same Legend level are going to same rough level of might at their disposal, the one with fewer associated Purviews just is more focused with more Boons in the same Purview, while Monkey or Shiva have like 1 Boon in each of their Purviews.<br /> <br /> Also it emphasizes the importance of Marvels. Most miracles someone performs in myth aren't necessarily Boons. They're only likely to be Boons if they're something a figure relies on REPEATEDLY in myth. Any creative one-off miracle in their purview is probably a Marvel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never actually read Scion 1st edition because I am an egyptophile and the art they had offended me so much that I put the book down and lost interest. So I didn't know that was a issue. The rational you gave makes a lot of sense. I was just curious so thank you. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T14:39:43-08:00","id":1282520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1282518#post1282518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never actually read Scion 1st edition because I am an egyptophile and the art they had offended me so much that I put the book down and lost interest. So I didn't know that was a issue. The rational you gave makes a lot of sense. I was just curious so thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No problem!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T18:49:33-07:00","id":1296856,"title":"","content":"So the sidebar for marvels says they are free against trivial characters. Some boons also specify they are free on trivial characters. Is that a holdover and we should assume just those boons and marvels are free on trivial characters or should any boon be free as long as it only affects trivial characters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13508-necrobotany","name":"necrobotany","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T06:39:22-07:00","id":1296963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>necrobotany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1296856#post1296856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the sidebar for marvels says they are free against trivial characters. Some boons also specify they are free on trivial characters. Is that a holdover and we should assume just those boons and marvels are free on trivial characters or should any boon be free as long as it only affects trivial characters?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think anything used on trivial characters are free. Dealing with trivial is more about the story than about rules, you can punch everyone on the room in the face or you can knock them down by a single use of a marvel... booms and marvels are flash and fun...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T02:46:52-07:00","id":1301838,"title":"","content":"So, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar137_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"137\" data-vbnamecard=\"137\">Neall</a> to put the question here in writing...<br /> <br /> The Virtue Rules state that Momentum spent on actions that embrace a Virtue give one bonus die. This is the same benefit of the Virtuous Condition. Are these intended to stack? So if Kamala the Dancing Flower spends Momentum on an action that resonates with her Duty while herself in the grip of her Duty Rage Condition, would she get <i>three</i> dice from that one Momentum spent?<br /> <br /> (Given that the Momentum rules specify that you only spend one Momentum per action, this was probably intended to keep Kamala from spending three Momentum to get nine extra dice on one action)<br /> <br /> Related to that, however: Let's say that Jamie Greenleaf, daughter of the Dagda, wants to help, and her player spends a Momentum to enhance Kamala's action? Would this second Momentum benefit from Kamala's Virtuous condition? I'd wager not, as Jamie herself is (for the sake of this) not doing anything that resonates with the Virtue.<br /> <br /> And on something more specific: Flipping it around a bit. Let's say that Jamie Greenleaf, in the grips of her Honor Virtuous Condition, is trying to stand against a foe. Kamala manages to trigger the Innate power of the Yoga Purview, letting Jamie spend a point of Momentum &quot;as though they had the Virtuous Condition&quot;. So, assuming that Jamie's act aligns with her Honor virtue (+1 die for Honor, +1 die for Virtuous), would the Yoga Purview add 1 extra die? 2? Would the two stack?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T04:28:33-07:00","id":1301854,"title":"","content":"Yes, Kamala would get three dice from that one Momentum spent. The second Momentum doesn't benefit from the Virtuous Condition unless Jamie <i>also </i>has Virtuous and the action resonates with both Virtues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T16:20:11-07:00","id":1302037,"title":"","content":"How many Callings are HERO LEVEL Denizens (who aren\u2019t Scions) supposed to have? Do they get 2 Callings from the Scion list along with their Denizen status, or do they only have the one Calling and just put all their points in it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T21:42:12-07:00","id":1302457,"title":"","content":"Are you not allowed to be a scion of Raiden? Or would you only have 1 purview from him and no calling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2448-dante","name":"Dante","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T22:25:52-07:00","id":1302468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-catego