yxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1398452#post1398452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like, gaining a new Relic or Guide through story advancement? I think that's fine, yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> honestly i was thinking like, the Thor Scion would gain an enhancement to their relic, like a new dot to show connection to the Frost purview after completing a difficult task set by, say, Skadi in story. <br /> <br /> or something like that. it would become part of their legend and thus they gain access to new powers as the story advances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","name":"Grimangel53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T12:29:10-07:00","id":1398633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimangel53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1398632#post1398632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> honestly i was thinking like, the Thor Scion would gain an enhancement to their relic, like a new dot to show connection to the Frost purview after completing a difficult task set by, say, Skadi in story.<br /> <br /> or something like that. it would become part of their legend and thus they gain access to new powers as the story advances.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I can see using quests to justify adding Dots to Relics or gain new Birthrights. Like... A player goes out and kills a frost giant with their Relic, and by bathing the Relic in the giant's blood the Relic gains 2 dots and access to the Frost Purview. If this were the end to a major story, I'd probably allow them to gain the power-up, assuming that the others get similar power-ups to keep things fair. Maybe the builder on the team can get an ingredient that counts towards a Milestone or something.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T10:23:06-07:00","id":1404793,"title":"","content":"How specific does the restriction on sacred animals/dance/passion have to be? Is beasts (Aquatic Animals) specific enough? Or Artistry (Music), as opposed to, say, Beasts (Fish), or Artistry (Violin).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24323-zipdrive","name":"ZipDrive","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T13:10:53-07:00","id":1404817,"title":"","content":"If i remember right Ioskeha (one of the Orenda in the Manitou section) has Beast (diurnal animals). So it can be pretty wide ranging it seems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T14:36:22-07:00","id":1407788,"title":"","content":"According to Mysteries of the World, Specializing a Purview grants <i>access</i> to one unique Boon per tier in exchange for additional limits on the Marvels the Scion can perform with the Purview. Does that mean the Scion still needs to spend one of their normal Boon picks on the Boon they gained <i>access</i> to? If so, it seems a bit weak for the cost, but perhaps I'm just not seeing its real strength.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T14:41:56-07:00","id":1407792,"title":"","content":"I remember on the Discord server that Neal said it\u2019s supposed to mean you get a free extra Boon, but don\u2019t quote me on that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T15:58:07-07:00","id":1407808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jaerys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1407788#post1407788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to Mysteries of the World, Specializing a Purview grants <i>access</i> to one unique Boon per tier in exchange for additional limits on the Marvels the Scion can perform with the Purview. Does that mean the Scion still needs to spend one of their normal Boon picks on the Boon they gained <i>access</i> to? If so, it seems a bit weak for the cost, but perhaps I'm just not seeing its real strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>it\u2019s a bonus boon beyond what you would otherwise have. The customizable nature of boons means you shouldn\u2019t need to specialize to take a given concept with one of your slots. And yes, I do wish the Companion were clearer about this!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T20:24:52-07:00","id":1408645,"title":"","content":"Does Relic Scale (from Mysteries of the World) stack with other 'Feats of Scale', such as using a Legendary Title?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1226-gammelbraxen","name":"Gammelbraxen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T09:15:07-07:00","id":1411812,"title":"","content":"Question for Neall:<br /> <br /> Whatever happened to the Scion of Known Abilities Kickstarter rewards outside of the books and PDFs?<br /> I'm asking because I received the books, and was just thinking about the character sheet reward as well.<br /> <br /> Hope everything is going well!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","name":"Grimangel53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T12:57:49-07:00","id":1411861,"title":"","content":"Question for Neal, the Dev Team, or Anyone in the know:<br /> this might be a silly question but one I feel I need to ask since it wasn't mentioned in Titanomachy. When playing a Scion of a Titan, do you get the pantheon purview for the associated purview or 2 of your parents purviews?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T17:33:36-07:00","id":1411954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimangel53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=1411812#post1411812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question for Neall:<br /> <br /> Whatever happened to the Scion of Known Abilities Kickstarter rewards outside of the books and PDFs?<br /> I'm asking because I received the books, and was just thinking about the character sheet reward as well.<br /> <br /> Hope everything is going well!</div> </div> </div> </div>On no! Send a message to Rich on the Kickstarter page (&quot;Contact Me&quot;) - that's the surest way to get this rectified immediately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T22:26:50-07:00","id":1412221,"title":"","content":"Hey Neall looking at both titanomachy, and demigod we have seen that gods can have titanic callings. Will there be a a resource or list to let us know which gods from the core book might have titanic callings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22488-ventruestereotype","name":"VentrueStereotype","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T22:43:04-07:00","id":1412544,"title":"","content":"I'm so sorry, I know this has been answered somewhere but I can't find if;<br /> What are the Teotl Pantheon path skills? My copies of Origin and Hero still contradict one another (Athletics Culture vs Culture Empathy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T23:49:21-07:00","id":1412546,"title":"","content":"The Scion: Hero entry is probably the correct one (Culture &amp; Empathy). The general rule of thumb in the Errata pdf is to use the Hero entry for the gods instead of the Origin Appendix (for Callings and Purviews at least). Plus, the pre-made Teotl has Culture &amp; Empathy but no Athletics. I admit that the pre-made characters are bit wonky in places though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-09T12:15:18-07:00","id":1412746,"title":"","content":"To chime in and expand on what VentrueStereotype has said: Will there be a more comprehensive list of Calling changes for the Gods in Origin, Hero and the Companion to bring them up to date with the Titan Callings in Titanomachy? I know that there will be a sidebar in Demigod, but that only scratches the surface. In the same vein: will the Titans in those book get a rule overhaul? As far as I know, the errata was supposed to be a living document. I think many people would really appreciate it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":50,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/50-blacklotos","user":"BlackLotos","date":". 09-10-2020, 01:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/50-blacklotos","name":"BlackLotos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar50_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T09:41:53-07:00","id":1413387,"title":"","content":"Question for Neall. Since Dragon and Mythos will be released after Demigod, will their own book have rules for Demigod play or will it just have references for the players to adapt it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T14:48:49-07:00","id":1415238,"title":"","content":"Aside from thematic reasons and point cost, is there an actual difference from Automatic and Brutal? To me, they have the same effect, albeit worded differently (and Automatic being a mechanically worst choice, since it costs more and has drawbacks)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24400-endou_kenji","name":"endou_kenji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T02:07:41-07:00","id":1415516,"title":"","content":"Only Automatic weapons may use the &quot;Emptying the Clip&quot; Stunt. The Stunt &quot;adds a +1 Enhancement bonus <u>in addition to the Automatic Tag's usual benefits</u>&quot;. So, you're basically paying an extra point in weapon tags over Brutal to gain access to that Stunt.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b><i>That said, while the end result of the Brutal and Automatic tags are similar (when not using Emptying the Clip), Brutal's method is slightly stronger since it doesn't count toward the recommended cap on Enhancement bonuses.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3755,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","user":"Jaerys","date":". 09-27-2020, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T01:55:07-07:00","id":1416699,"title":"","content":"Question for Neall or any one of the Dev's: For Divinity Dice, it says that when they are used in Defense rolls, they automatically gain 9-again. Is this the case with all other rolls involving Divinity Dice as well, or are they just meant to be a limiting mechanic (outside of Flooding the Pool).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-28T19:30:15-07:00","id":1420745,"title":"","content":"Sorry if this has been answered and I just missed it in the previous pages, but, I have a player interested in starting with a Titan Calling, but would it be possible to see an example of a corresponding Titan knack? I believe this info is slated for release in a later book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12584-spacenerd5792","name":"spacenerd5792","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-28T19:33:06-07:00","id":1420746,"title":"","content":"Did the player say which titanic calling interest them?<br /> Also the titanic calling are in the titanomachy book which should be available on dtrpg i think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"li